clinical,care_coordination,advance_directive,advance_directive_id,advance_directive_id,Advance Directive ID,BIGINT,Y,,,,master_data,Unique surrogate identifier for the advance directive record in the lakehouse silver layer. Primary key for this entity.,
clinical,care_coordination,advance_directive,advance_clinical_order_id,advance_clinical_order_id,,BIGINT,,order.clinical_order.clinical_order_id,,,master_data,foreign_key_to,
clinical,care_coordination,advance_directive,care_site_id,care_site_id,Facility ID,BIGINT,,facility.care_site.care_site_id,,,master_data,"Reference to the healthcare facility (hospital, clinic, or outpatient center) where the advance directive was documented or verified. Supports multi-facility enterprise reporting and care transition workflows.",
clinical,care_coordination,advance_directive,claim_attachment_id,claim_attachment_id,Claim Attachment Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,claim.claim_attachment.claim_attachment_id,,,master_data,Foreign key linking to claim.claim_attachment. Business justification: Advance directives are required documentation for hospice and palliative care claims. Compliance teams must link directive to claim attachment for Medicare hospice election validation and end-of-life ,
clinical,care_coordination,advance_directive,clinical_order_id,clinical_order_id,Restricting Clinical Order Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,order.clinical_order.clinical_order_id,,,master_data,"Foreign key linking to order.clinical_order. Business justification: Advance directives constrain order placement. Real workflow: DNR status prevents code blue orders. Essential for end-of-life care compliance, CPOE decision support, ethics committee review, and regula",
clinical,care_coordination,advance_directive,clinician_id,clinician_id,Documenting Provider ID,BIGINT,,provider.clinician.clinician_id,,,master_data,Reference to the clinician or provider who documented or verified the advance directive in the Electronic Health Record (EHR). Supports audit and accountability requirements.,
clinical,care_coordination,advance_directive,compliance_policy_id,compliance_policy_id,Policy Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,compliance.compliance_policy.compliance_policy_id,,,master_data,Foreign key linking to compliance.policy. Business justification: Advance directive management is governed by organizational policies implementing state/federal regulations (Patient Self-Determination Act). Healthcare organizations must link advance directive record,
clinical,care_coordination,advance_directive,consent_record_id,consent_record_id,Consent Record Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,consent.consent_consent_record.consent_record_id,,,master_data,"Foreign key linking to consent.consent_record. Business justification: Advance directives are a specialized form of consent for end-of-life care decisions. Linking to the general consent framework ensures comprehensive consent tracking, supports POLST/MOLST workflows, an",
clinical,care_coordination,advance_directive,demographics_id,demographics_id,Patient ID,BIGINT,,patient.demographics.demographics_id,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_identifier",,master_data,Reference to the patient for whom this advance directive was documented. Links to the patient master record.,
clinical,care_coordination,advance_directive,employee_id,employee_id,,BIGINT,,workforce.employee.employee_id,"confidential,pii",,master_data,FK to workforce.employee.employee_id,
clinical,care_coordination,advance_directive,mpi_record_id,mpi_record_id,,BIGINT,,patient.mpi_record.mpi_record_id,,,master_data,description,
clinical,care_coordination,advance_directive,quality_measure_id,quality_measure_id,Quality Measure Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,quality.measure.measure_id,,,master_data,"Foreign key linking to quality.measure. Business justification: Advance directive documentation is a quality measure in MIPS, hospice quality, and palliative care programs. Direct linkage enables automated measure calculation and advance care planning quality trac",
clinical,care_coordination,advance_directive,superseded_by_directive_advance_directive_id,superseded_by_directive_advance_directive_id,Superseded By Directive ID,BIGINT,,clinical.advance_directive.advance_directive_id,,,master_data,Reference to the newer advance directive record that supersedes this one. Null if this directive has not been superseded. Enables directive version chain tracking and ensures the most current directive is applied in care decisions.,
clinical,care_coordination,advance_directive,visit_id,visit_id,Encounter ID,BIGINT,,encounter.visit.visit_id,,,master_data,Reference to the clinical encounter during which the advance directive was documented or verified. May be null if documented outside an encounter context.,
clinical,care_coordination,advance_directive,artificially_administered_nutrition,artificially_administered_nutrition,Artificially Administered Nutrition Preference,STRING,,,,Accept|Decline|Trial Period|No Preference Stated,master_data,"Patients documented preference regarding artificially administered nutrition and hydration (e.g., feeding tubes, IV fluids) as specified in the advance directive or POLST/MOLST. Critical for end-of-life care planning.",
clinical,care_coordination,advance_directive,capacity_assessment_result,capacity_assessment_result,Patient Decision-Making Capacity Assessment Result,STRING,,,,Has Capacity|Lacks Capacity|Capacity Uncertain,master_data,The result of the formal patient decision-making capacity assessment conducted at the time of advance directive documentation. Determines whether the patient could legally execute or modify the directive.,
clinical,care_coordination,advance_directive,clinical_notes,clinical_notes,Advance Directive Clinical Notes,STRING,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_health",,master_data,"Free-text clinical notes or additional instructions documented by the provider regarding the patients advance directive, including nuances, patient-expressed wishes, or contextual information not captured in structured fields.",
clinical,care_coordination,advance_directive,code_status,code_status,Code Status,STRING,,,,Full Code|DNR|DNR/DNI|Comfort Care|Limited Interventions,master_data,The patients current resuscitation code status as documented in the advance directive. Full Code = all resuscitative measures; DNR = Do Not Resuscitate; DNR/DNI = Do Not Resuscitate / Do Not Intubate; Comfort Care = palliative measures only; Limited Interventions = selective resuscitative measures as specified.,
clinical,care_coordination,advance_directive,consent_verification_method,consent_verification_method,Directive Verification Method,STRING,,,,Original Document|Scanned Copy|Verbal Confirmation|Electronic Record|Notarized Copy,master_data,The method used to verify the authenticity and currency of the advance directive. Original Document = physical original reviewed; Scanned Copy = digitized copy on file; Verbal Confirmation = patient verbally confirmed; Electronic Record = verified via Health Information Exchange (HIE); Notarized Copy = legally notarized document reviewed.,
clinical,care_coordination,advance_directive,created_timestamp,created_timestamp,Record Created Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,master_data,"The date and time when this advance directive record was first created in the lakehouse data platform. Supports data lineage, audit trail, and regulatory compliance reporting.",
clinical,care_coordination,advance_directive,directive_status,directive_status,Advance Directive Status,STRING,,,,active|revoked|superseded|expired|pending_verification,master_data,Current lifecycle status of the advance directive document. Active = currently in force; Revoked = patient has withdrawn the directive; Superseded = replaced by a newer directive; Expired = past the expiration date; Pending Verification = documented but not yet clinically verified.,
clinical,care_coordination,advance_directive,directive_type,directive_type,Advance Directive Type,STRING,,,,DNR|POLST|MOLST|Living Will|Healthcare Power of Attorney|Comfort Care Order,master_data,Classification of the advance directive document type. DNR = Do Not Resuscitate; POLST = Physician Orders for Life-Sustaining Treatment; MOLST = Medical Orders for Life-Sustaining Treatment; Living Will = written legal document; Healthcare Power of Attorney = proxy designation; Comfort Care Order = palliative/comfort-focused care order.,
clinical,care_coordination,advance_directive,document_location,document_location,Directive Document Location,STRING,,,,EHR Scanned|Patient Holds Original|Family Holds Copy|Registry|Attorney on File,master_data,Indicates where the physical or electronic copy of the advance directive document is stored or held. Supports retrieval during care transitions and emergency situations.,
clinical,care_coordination,advance_directive,documented_timestamp,documented_timestamp,Directive Documented Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,master_data,The date and time when the advance directive was first entered or documented in the Electronic Health Record (EHR). Serves as the BUSINESS_EVENT_TIMESTAMP for this records creation in the clinical system.,
clinical,care_coordination,advance_directive,effective_date,effective_date,Directive Effective Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,The date on which the advance directive becomes legally and clinically effective. Used to determine whether the directive is currently binding for care decisions.,
clinical,care_coordination,advance_directive,ethics_consult_requested,ethics_consult_requested,Ethics Consultation Requested Indicator,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,"Indicates whether an ethics committee consultation was requested in connection with this advance directive. Supports quality reporting, compliance tracking, and clinical ethics workflows.",
clinical,care_coordination,advance_directive,expiration_date,expiration_date,Directive Expiration Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,The date on which the advance directive expires and is no longer legally or clinically binding. Null if the directive has no defined expiration (open-ended). Supports automated status transitions to expired.,
clinical,care_coordination,advance_directive,fhir_consent_reference,fhir_consent_reference,Fast Healthcare Interoperability Resources (FHIR) Consent Resource ID,STRING,,,,,master_data,"The FHIR Consent resource identifier corresponding to this advance directive, enabling interoperability with Health Information Exchange (HIE) platforms and FHIR-compliant systems.",
clinical,care_coordination,advance_directive,hospice_enrolled,hospice_enrolled,Hospice Enrollment Indicator,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,Indicates whether the patient is currently enrolled in a hospice program at the time of advance directive documentation. Relevant for care plan alignment and CMS hospice benefit compliance.,
clinical,care_coordination,advance_directive,hospitalization_preference,hospitalization_preference,Hospitalization Preference,STRING,,,,Accept Hospitalization|Avoid Hospitalization|Comfort Care Only|No Preference Stated,master_data,Patients documented preference regarding hospitalization and transfer to acute care settings as specified in the POLST/MOLST. Guides care transitions and Emergency Department (ED) triage decisions.,
clinical,care_coordination,advance_directive,interpreter_used,interpreter_used,Interpreter Used Indicator,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,Indicates whether a language interpreter was used during the advance directive discussion and documentation process. Supports compliance with Title VI of the Civil Rights Act and CMS language access requirements.,
clinical,care_coordination,advance_directive,life_sustaining_treatment_preference,life_sustaining_treatment_preference,Life-Sustaining Treatment Preference,STRING,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii",Full Treatment|Selective Treatment|Comfort Measures Only,master_data,Patients documented preference regarding life-sustaining treatment as captured in the POLST/MOLST or living will. Full Treatment = all medically appropriate interventions; Selective Treatment = specific interventions as detailed; Comfort Measures Only = palliative and comfort-focused care only. Core clinical decision support field.,
clinical,care_coordination,advance_directive,mechanical_ventilation_preference,mechanical_ventilation_preference,Mechanical Ventilation Preference,STRING,,,,Accept|Decline|Trial Period|No Preference Stated,master_data,Patients documented preference regarding mechanical ventilation and intubation as specified in the advance directive or POLST/MOLST. Directly informs DNR/DNI code status decisions.,
clinical,care_coordination,advance_directive,mrn,mrn,Medical Record Number (MRN),STRING,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_identifier",,master_data,"pii_phi,pii_pii,pii_sensitive",
clinical,care_coordination,advance_directive,notarized,notarized,Directive Notarized Indicator,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,Indicates whether the advance directive document has been notarized. Some state jurisdictions require notarization for legal validity of living wills and healthcare power of attorney designations.,
clinical,care_coordination,advance_directive,organ_donation_status,organ_donation_status,Organ Donation Status,STRING,,,,Donor|Non-Donor|Donor with Restrictions|Unknown,master_data,Patients documented preference or registered status regarding organ and tissue donation as captured in the advance directive or linked registry. Supports organ procurement coordination and UNOS compliance.,
clinical,care_coordination,advance_directive,palliative_care_referral,palliative_care_referral,Palliative Care Referral Indicator,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,"Indicates whether a palliative care referral was initiated in conjunction with the advance directive documentation. Supports care coordination, population health management, and quality measure reporting.",
clinical,care_coordination,advance_directive,patient_capacity_assessed,patient_capacity_assessed,Patient Decision-Making Capacity Assessed Indicator,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,Indicates whether the patients decision-making capacity was formally assessed at the time the advance directive was documented or verified. Relevant for legal validity and ethical compliance.,
clinical,care_coordination,advance_directive,patient_education_provided,patient_education_provided,Patient Education Provided Indicator,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,Indicates whether the patient received education about advance directives and their rights under the Patient Self-Determination Act (PSDA) prior to or at the time of directive documentation.,
clinical,care_coordination,advance_directive,preferred_language,preferred_language,Patient Preferred Language,STRING,,,,"^[a-z]{2,3}(-[A-Z]{2})?$",master_data,"The patients preferred language for advance directive discussions and documentation, expressed as an ISO 639-1 or BCP-47 language code (e.g., en, es, zh-CN). Supports language access compliance and care equity reporting.",
clinical,care_coordination,advance_directive,proxy_alternate_phone,proxy_alternate_phone,Healthcare Proxy Alternate Phone Number,STRING,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_phone","^+?[0-9s-().]{7,20}$",master_data,Alternate or secondary contact phone number for the designated healthcare proxy. Used when the primary proxy phone number is unreachable during urgent care decisions.,
clinical,care_coordination,advance_directive,proxy_name,proxy_name,Healthcare Proxy Name,STRING,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_identifier",,master_data,Full name of the designated healthcare proxy or healthcare power of attorney agent authorized to make medical decisions on behalf of the patient when the patient lacks decision-making capacity.,
clinical,care_coordination,advance_directive,proxy_phone,proxy_phone,Healthcare Proxy Phone Number,STRING,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_phone","^+?[0-9s-().]{7,20}$",master_data,Primary contact phone number for the designated healthcare proxy or power of attorney agent. Used to contact the proxy when the patient is unable to make decisions.,
clinical,care_coordination,advance_directive,proxy_relationship,proxy_relationship,Healthcare Proxy Relationship,STRING,,,,,master_data,"The relationship of the designated healthcare proxy to the patient (e.g., Spouse, Parent, Child, Sibling, Friend, Legal Guardian, Attorney). Used for care coordination and next-of-kin notification workflows. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: Spouse|Parent|Child|Sibling|Friend|Legal Guardian|Attorney — 7 candidates stripped; promote to reference product]",
clinical,care_coordination,advance_directive,revocation_timestamp,revocation_timestamp,Directive Revocation Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,master_data,The date and time when the patient formally revoked the advance directive. Null if the directive has not been revoked. Triggers status transition to revoked and inactivates the directive for care decisions.,
clinical,care_coordination,advance_directive,scanned_document_url,scanned_document_url,Scanned Directive Document URL,STRING,,,dbx_confidential,,master_data,Secure URL or document management system path to the scanned or electronic copy of the advance directive document stored in the document management system or EHR. Supports retrieval for clinical review and legal reference.,
clinical,care_coordination,advance_directive,source_system,source_system,Source System,STRING,,,,Epic|Cerner|MEDITECH|Scanned Document|HIE|Manual Entry,master_data,"The originating operational system from which the advance directive record was sourced. Supports data lineage, reconciliation, and Health Information Exchange (HIE) interoperability tracking.",
clinical,care_coordination,advance_directive,source_system_directive_code,source_system_directive_code,Source System Directive ID,STRING,,,,,master_data,"The native identifier of the advance directive record in the originating operational system (e.g., Epic advance care planning record ID). Supports bidirectional traceability between the lakehouse and the source Electronic Health Record (EHR).",
clinical,care_coordination,advance_directive,state_of_execution,state_of_execution,State of Directive Execution,STRING,,,,^[A-Z]{2}$,master_data,The U.S. state (two-letter USPS abbreviation) in which the advance directive was legally executed. Determines which state-specific legal requirements and forms apply to the directives validity.,
clinical,care_coordination,advance_directive,updated_timestamp,updated_timestamp,Record Updated Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,master_data,"The date and time when this advance directive record was last modified in the lakehouse data platform. Supports change tracking, audit trail, and data quality monitoring.",
clinical,care_coordination,advance_directive,verified_timestamp,verified_timestamp,Directive Verified Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,master_data,"The date and time when the advance directive was clinically verified by a qualified provider. Verification confirms the document is current, authentic, and reflects the patients current wishes.",
clinical,care_coordination,advance_directive,witness_name,witness_name,Directive Witness Name,STRING,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_identifier",,master_data,Full name of the witness who attested to the patients execution of the advance directive document. Required by many state laws to validate the legal standing of the directive.,
clinical,care_coordination,care_plan,care_plan_id,care_plan_id,Care Plan ID,BIGINT,Y,,,,master_data,Unique surrogate identifier for the care plan record in the lakehouse Silver layer. Primary key for this entity.,
clinical,care_coordination,care_plan,activated_order_set_id,activated_order_set_id,Activated Order Set Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,order.order_order_set.order_set_id,,,master_data,"Foreign key linking to order.order_set. Business justification: Care plans activate order sets. Real workflow: CHF care plan triggers CHF admission order set. Essential for care pathway compliance tracking, order set utilization analysis, population health protoco",
clinical,care_coordination,care_plan,care_mpi_record_id,care_mpi_record_id,,BIGINT,,patient.mpi_record.mpi_record_id,,,master_data,description,
clinical,care_coordination,care_plan,care_site_id,care_site_id,Facility ID,BIGINT,,facility.care_site.care_site_id,,,master_data,"Reference to the healthcare facility or care setting (hospital, outpatient clinic, SNF, home health) where this care plan is being managed.",
clinical,care_coordination,care_plan,clinical_order_id,clinical_order_id,,BIGINT,,order.clinical_order.clinical_order_id,,,master_data,foreign_key_to,
clinical,care_coordination,care_plan,consent_record_id,consent_record_id,Consent Record Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,consent.consent_consent_record.consent_record_id,,,master_data,"Foreign key linking to consent.consent_record. Business justification: Care plans require patient consent for goals, interventions, and care team access. CMS Conditions of Participation and ACO programs mandate documented patient consent for care plan development and sha",
clinical,care_coordination,care_plan,demographics_id,demographics_id,Patient ID,BIGINT,,patient.demographics.demographics_id,,,master_data,Reference to the patient for whom this care plan was created. Links to the patient master record.,
clinical,care_coordination,care_plan,material_master_id,material_master_id,Material Master Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,supply.material_master.material_master_id,,,master_data,"Foreign key linking to supply.material_master. Business justification: Care plans specify DME, supplies, and medications required for patient management. Enables care plan-driven supply provisioning, discharge planning supply coordination, and transitions-of-care supply ",
clinical,care_coordination,care_plan,mpi_record_id,mpi_record_id,,BIGINT,,patient.mpi_record.mpi_record_id,,,master_data,FK to patient.mpi_record.mpi_record_id,
clinical,care_coordination,care_plan,payer_id,payer_id,Payer Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,insurance.payer.payer_id,,,master_data,"Foreign key linking to insurance.payer. Business justification: Care plans are often mandated by payer contracts (ACO requirements, care management programs, chronic care management billing). Payer-specific quality measures and care coordination requirements drive",
clinical,care_coordination,care_plan,primary_care_coordinator_clinician_id,primary_care_coordinator_clinician_id,Care Coordinator ID,BIGINT,,provider.clinician.clinician_id,,,master_data,"Reference to the care coordinator or case manager assigned to oversee execution of this care plan, distinct from the authoring provider. Supports ACO care coordination workflows and population health management.",
clinical,care_coordination,care_plan,primary_diagnosis_icd_code_id,primary_diagnosis_icd_code_id,,BIGINT,,reference.icd_code.icd_code_id,"restricted,pii_health",,master_data,FK to reference.icd_code.icd_code_id,
clinical,care_coordination,care_plan,quality_measure_id,quality_measure_id,Quality Measure Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,quality.measure.measure_id,,,master_data,"Foreign key linking to quality.measure. Business justification: Care plan measures (care plan documented for chronic conditions, advance care planning) require linking care plans to quality metrics. Essential for care coordination quality reporting and value-based",
clinical,care_coordination,care_plan,snomed_concept_id,snomed_concept_id,Snomed Category Code Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,reference.snomed_concept.snomed_concept_id,,,master_data,"Foreign key linking to reference.snomed_concept. Business justification: Care plan categorization for care coordination workflows, population health program assignment, and FHIR CarePlan resource generation. Care management teams use SNOMED categories to route patients to ",
clinical,care_coordination,care_plan,tertiary_care_pcp_clinician_id,tertiary_care_pcp_clinician_id,Primary Care Physician (PCP) ID,BIGINT,,provider.clinician.clinician_id,,,master_data,"Reference to the patients Primary Care Physician (PCP) who should receive care plan summary and transition communications. Supports care continuity, ACO attribution, and CMS transitions of care quality measures.",
clinical,care_coordination,care_plan,visit_id,visit_id,Encounter ID,BIGINT,,encounter.visit.visit_id,,,master_data,"Reference to the clinical encounter (inpatient admission, outpatient visit, ED visit) during which this care plan was initiated or most recently updated.",
clinical,care_coordination,care_plan,aco_attributed,aco_attributed,Accountable Care Organization (ACO) Attributed Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,"Indicates whether this care plan is associated with a patient attributed to an Accountable Care Organization (ACO) program. Drives ACO quality reporting, shared savings calculations, and population health management workflows.",
clinical,care_coordination,care_plan,advance_directive_on_file,advance_directive_on_file,Advance Directive on File Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,"Indicates whether a valid advance directive (living will, POLST, MOLST, or healthcare proxy) is on file for this patient and has been reviewed in the context of this care plan. Required for CMS Conditions of Participation and Joint Commission compliance.",
clinical,care_coordination,care_plan,authored_date,authored_date,Care Plan Authored Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,The calendar date on which the care plan was originally authored or first documented in the EHR. Distinct from the effective start date; captures the documentation event timestamp at day granularity.,
clinical,care_coordination,care_plan,behavioral_health_flag,behavioral_health_flag,Behavioral Health Care Plan Flag,BOOLEAN,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_health",,master_data,"Indicates whether this care plan addresses behavioral health, mental health, or substance use disorder conditions. Triggers enhanced privacy protections under 42 CFR Part 2 and state mental health parity laws, restricting downstream data sharing.",
clinical,care_coordination,care_plan,care_plan_description,care_plan_description,Care Plan Description,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Free-text narrative description of the overall care plan, including clinical rationale, patient-specific context, and summary of the care approach. Authored by the clinician in the EHR.",
clinical,care_coordination,care_plan,care_setting,care_setting,Care Setting,STRING,,,,,master_data,"The clinical care setting in which this care plan is being executed. Drives population health segmentation, ACO attribution, and CMS quality measure reporting. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: inpatient|outpatient|emergency|icu|home_health|snf|hospice|telehealth — promote to reference product]",
clinical,care_coordination,care_plan,cdi_review_status,cdi_review_status,Clinical Documentation Improvement (CDI) Review Status,STRING,,,,pending|in_review|completed|not_required,master_data,Status of the Clinical Documentation Improvement (CDI) review process for this care plan. CDI specialists review care plans to ensure diagnoses and clinical findings are accurately and completely documented to support appropriate DRG assignment and quality reporting.,
clinical,care_coordination,care_plan,confidentiality_level,confidentiality_level,Care Plan Confidentiality Level,STRING,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_health",normal|restricted|very_restricted,master_data,"Confidentiality classification of this care plan per HL7 v3 Confidentiality value set. restricted and very_restricted apply to sensitive conditions (e.g., behavioral health, substance use disorder, HIV) subject to 42 CFR Part 2 and state-specific privacy laws beyond standard HIPAA protections.",
clinical,care_coordination,care_plan,created_timestamp,created_timestamp,Care Plan Record Created Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,master_data,"Precise timestamp when this care plan record was first created in the source EHR system. Used for audit trail, CDI workflow tracking, and HIPAA audit log compliance.",
clinical,care_coordination,care_plan,discharge_disposition,discharge_disposition,Discharge Disposition,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Planned or actual discharge destination for the patient upon completion of this care plan. Critical for transitions of care planning, readmission risk stratification, and CMS discharge planning compliance. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: home|snf|rehab|ltac|hospice|ama|expired|other — promote to reference product]",
clinical,care_coordination,care_plan,effective_end_date,effective_end_date,Care Plan Effective End Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,The date on which this care plan is expected to conclude or was concluded. Null for open-ended chronic disease management plans. Used for LOS and transitions of care analytics.,
clinical,care_coordination,care_plan,effective_start_date,effective_start_date,Care Plan Effective Start Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,The date on which this care plan becomes or became clinically active and binding for the patients care. Used for transitions of care tracking and CMS discharge planning compliance.,
clinical,care_coordination,care_plan,external_plan_code,external_plan_code,External Care Plan Identifier,STRING,,,,,master_data,"The externally-known or source-system identifier for this care plan as assigned by the originating EHR (e.g., Epic Healthy Planet plan ID, Cerner PowerChart plan number). Supports HIE interoperability and cross-system reconciliation.",
clinical,care_coordination,care_plan,fhir_resource_reference,fhir_resource_reference,HL7 FHIR Resource ID,STRING,,,,"^[A-Za-z0-9-.]{1,64}$",master_data,"The HL7 FHIR R4 logical resource identifier for this care plan as exposed via the FHIR API. Enables interoperability with HIE partners, payer systems, and patient-facing applications under the ONC 21st Century Cures Act.",
clinical,care_coordination,care_plan,goal_count,goal_count,Care Plan Goal Count,INT,,,,,master_data,"Total number of patient goals documented within this care plan. Supports care plan completeness scoring, CDI quality metrics, and population health reporting without requiring aggregation of goal detail records.",
clinical,care_coordination,care_plan,goals_achieved_count,goals_achieved_count,Care Plan Goals Achieved Count,INT,,,,,master_data,"Number of goals within this care plan that have reached achieved status. Used for outcomes reporting, VBP performance measurement, and ACO quality scoring.",
clinical,care_coordination,care_plan,intent,intent,Care Plan Intent,STRING,,,,proposal|plan|order|option,master_data,Indicates the degree of authority and actionability of the care plan per HL7 FHIR intent value set. proposal is a suggestion; plan is an agreed-upon plan; order is a directive; option is a contingency.,
clinical,care_coordination,care_plan,last_modified_timestamp,last_modified_timestamp,Care Plan Last Modified Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,master_data,"Timestamp of the most recent modification to this care plan record in the source EHR. Supports CDI workflow, version tracking, and HIPAA audit compliance.",
clinical,care_coordination,care_plan,last_reviewed_date,last_reviewed_date,Last Care Plan Review Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,"Date on which this care plan was most recently formally reviewed and attested by a qualified clinician. Supports CDI workflow, compliance auditing, and care plan currency validation.",
clinical,care_coordination,care_plan,next_review_date,next_review_date,Next Care Plan Review Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,Scheduled date for the next formal review of this care plan by the responsible care team. Used for care management workflow queuing and overdue plan identification.,
clinical,care_coordination,care_plan,patient_consent_date,patient_consent_date,Patient Consent Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,Date on which the patient or authorized representative provided consent for this care plan. Required for HIPAA documentation and CMS regulatory compliance.,
clinical,care_coordination,care_plan,patient_consent_obtained,patient_consent_obtained,Patient Consent Obtained Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,Indicates whether the patient (or authorized representative) has provided informed consent for the care plan and its associated interventions. Required for HIPAA compliance and CMS Conditions of Participation.,
clinical,care_coordination,care_plan,plan_status,plan_status,Care Plan Status,STRING,,,,draft|active|on-hold|completed|revoked|entered-in-error,master_data,Current lifecycle state of the care plan per HL7 FHIR CarePlan status value set. draft indicates not yet activated; active is in use; on-hold is temporarily suspended; completed indicates all goals met; revoked indicates cancelled before completion.,
clinical,care_coordination,care_plan,plan_title,plan_title,Care Plan Title,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Human-readable title or name of the care plan as displayed in the EHR (e.g., Diabetes Management Plan, Post-Surgical Discharge Plan, CHF Chronic Disease Management).",
clinical,care_coordination,care_plan,plan_type,plan_type,Care Plan Type,STRING,,,,,master_data,Classification of the care plan by care setting and purpose. Drives workflow routing and regulatory reporting. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: inpatient|outpatient|chronic_disease|discharge|transitional|palliative|preventive — promote to reference product],
clinical,care_coordination,care_plan,population_health_program,population_health_program,Population Health Program Name,STRING,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii",,master_data,"Name or code of the population health management program (e.g., Diabetes Registry, CHF Disease Management, Hypertension Control, Preventive Care Outreach) under which this care plan is managed. Supports HEDIS measure attribution and ACO program reporting.",
clinical,care_coordination,care_plan,primary_diagnosis_description,primary_diagnosis_description,Primary Diagnosis Description,STRING,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_health",,master_data,"Plain-text description of the primary diagnosis or clinical problem driving this care plan, corresponding to the primary ICD-10 code. Stored for reporting and display without requiring a code lookup.",
clinical,care_coordination,care_plan,primary_icd10_code,primary_icd10_code,Primary ICD-10 Diagnosis Code,STRING,,,,"^[A-Z][0-9A-Z]{1,6}(.[0-9A-Z]{1,4})?$",master_data,"The primary ICD-10-CM diagnosis code representing the principal clinical problem or condition being addressed by this care plan. Supports DRG grouping, quality measure attribution, and population health stratification.",
clinical,care_coordination,care_plan,readmission_risk_level,readmission_risk_level,Readmission Risk Level,STRING,,,,low|medium|high|very_high,master_data,Clinician-assigned or algorithmically-derived readmission risk stratification for this patient at the time of care plan creation. Drives care management intensity and post-discharge follow-up scheduling. Supports CMS Hospital Readmissions Reduction Program (HRRP) compliance.,
clinical,care_coordination,care_plan,review_frequency,review_frequency,Care Plan Review Frequency,STRING,,,,,master_data,Prescribed frequency at which this care plan should be formally reviewed and updated by the care team. Drives scheduling of care plan review encounters and supports NCQA PCMH and CMS chronic care management billing requirements. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: daily|weekly|biweekly|monthly|quarterly|annually|as_needed — 7 candidates stripped; promote to reference product],
clinical,care_coordination,care_plan,sdoh_flag,sdoh_flag,Social Determinants of Health (SDOH) Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,"Indicates whether Social Determinants of Health (SDOH) factors (e.g., food insecurity, housing instability, transportation barriers) have been identified and incorporated into this care plan. Supports CMS SDOH screening requirements and population health management.",
clinical,care_coordination,care_plan,source_system,source_system,Source System,STRING,,,,epic_healthy_planet|cerner_powerchart|meditech_expanse|manual|other,master_data,"Identifies the originating EHR or clinical system from which this care plan record was sourced (e.g., Epic Healthy Planet, Cerner Millennium PowerChart). Supports data lineage, ETL reconciliation, and HIE interoperability tracking.",
clinical,care_coordination,care_plan,transitions_of_care_flag,transitions_of_care_flag,Transitions of Care Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,"Indicates whether this care plan was created or updated specifically to support a transition of care event (e.g., hospital discharge to home, SNF transfer, ED to inpatient admission). Supports CMS Transitions of Care quality measures and readmission reduction programs.",
clinical,care_coordination,care_plan,version_number,version_number,Care Plan Version Number,INT,,,,,master_data,"Sequential version number incremented each time the care plan is substantively revised. Supports care plan history tracking, CDI audit trails, and regulatory documentation of plan evolution.",
clinical,care_coordination,care_plan_goal,care_plan_goal_id,care_plan_goal_id,Care Plan Goal ID,BIGINT,Y,,,,transactional_data,Unique surrogate identifier for each individual clinical goal within a care plan. Primary key for this entity in the Silver Layer lakehouse.,
clinical,care_coordination,care_plan_goal,care_plan_id,care_plan_id,Care Plan ID,BIGINT,,clinical.care_plan.care_plan_id,,,transactional_data,Reference to the parent care plan under which this goal is defined. Each goal belongs to exactly one care plan.,
clinical,care_coordination,care_plan_goal,clinical_order_id,clinical_order_id,Supporting Clinical Order Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,order.clinical_order.clinical_order_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to order.clinical_order. Business justification: Care plan goals drive specific orders. Real workflow: goal to reduce A1C below 7 triggers quarterly lab orders. Essential for goal-directed care tracking, care gap closure, value-based care reporting,",
clinical,care_coordination,care_plan_goal,clinician_id,clinician_id,Responsible Provider ID,BIGINT,,provider.clinician.clinician_id,,,transactional_data,"Reference to the clinician (physician, nurse practitioner, care manager) accountable for monitoring and advancing this specific goal.",
clinical,care_coordination,care_plan_goal,consent_record_id,consent_record_id,Consent Record Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,consent.consent_consent_record.consent_record_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to consent.consent_record. Business justification: Individual goals (especially behavioral health, genetic testing, SDOH interventions) may require separate consent beyond the care plan. Patient agreement tracking and consent for goal-specific interve",
clinical,care_coordination,care_plan_goal,demographics_id,demographics_id,Patient ID,BIGINT,,patient.demographics.demographics_id,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_identifier",,transactional_data,Reference to the patient for whom this clinical goal is established. Links to the Master Patient Index (MPI) patient record.,
clinical,care_coordination,care_plan_goal,icd_code_id,icd_code_id,Icd10 Related Condition Code Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,reference.icd_code.icd_code_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to reference.icd_code. Business justification: Goal-to-condition linkage for chronic disease management, quality measure attribution, and care gap closure. Population health teams use ICD-10 codes to associate goals with specific conditions for HE",
clinical,care_coordination,care_plan_goal,imaging_order_id,imaging_order_id,Imaging Order Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,radiology.imaging_order.imaging_order_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to radiology.imaging_order. Business justification: Specific care plan goals require imaging to measure achievement (tumor reduction, fracture healing). Essential for goal progress tracking and outcome measurement in value-based care programs.",
clinical,care_coordination,care_plan_goal,laboratory_test_result_id,laboratory_test_result_id,Target Test Result Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,laboratory.laboratory_test_result.laboratory_test_result_id,,,transactional_data,Foreign key linking to laboratory.test_result. Business justification: Goal achievement measured by lab values (HbA1c<7% for diabetes control). Role prefix target_ indicates goal measurement. Essential for value-based care reporting and patient engagement dashboards.,
clinical,care_coordination,care_plan_goal,material_master_id,material_master_id,Material Master Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,supply.material_master.material_master_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to supply.material_master. Business justification: Goals may require specific DME or supplies (e.g., mobility goals → walkers, wound healing goals → wound care supplies). Enables goal-driven supply ordering and care plan supply cost tracking.",
clinical,care_coordination,care_plan_goal,problem_id,problem_id,Problem Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,clinical.problem.problem_id,,,transactional_data,Foreign key linking to clinical.problem. Business justification: Care plan goals are created to address specific problems on the patients problem list. This is a core clinical workflow: problem identified → goal created → interventions planned → outcomes measured.,
clinical,care_coordination,care_plan_goal,target_measure_loinc_code_id,target_measure_loinc_code_id,Target Measure Loinc Code Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,reference.loinc_code.loinc_code_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to reference.loinc_code. Business justification: Measurable goal definition for care plan tracking, outcome measurement, and patient engagement. Care coordinators use LOINC-coded goals to automatically track progress from lab results, vital signs, a",
clinical,care_coordination,care_plan_goal,target_observation_id,target_observation_id,Target Observation Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,clinical.observation.observation_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to clinical.observation. Business justification: Care plan goals often target specific observable measures (e.g., reduce HbA1c to <7%, maintain systolic BP <140). Linking care_plan_goal to observation allows tracking goal achievement against act",
clinical,care_coordination,care_plan_goal,visit_id,visit_id,Encounter ID,BIGINT,,encounter.visit.visit_id,,,transactional_data,Reference to the clinical encounter during which this goal was established or most recently reviewed. May be null for goals created outside a discrete encounter context.,
clinical,care_coordination,care_plan_goal,achieved_date,achieved_date,Goal Achieved Date,DATE,,,,,transactional_data,The date on which the clinical goal was documented as achieved. Populated only when goal_status is achieved. Used for outcome measurement and quality reporting.,
clinical,care_coordination,care_plan_goal,achievement_status,achievement_status,Goal Achievement Status,STRING,,,,in-progress|improving|worsening|no-change|achieved|not-achieved,transactional_data,Clinical assessment of the degree to which the patient is progressing toward or has achieved the goal. Distinct from lifecycle status — captures clinical trajectory rather than workflow state. Aligns with HL7 FHIR R4 Goal.achievementStatus.,
clinical,care_coordination,care_plan_goal,barrier_notes,barrier_notes,Goal Barrier Notes,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Free-text documentation of identified barriers preventing the patient from achieving this goal (e.g., financial constraints, transportation issues, health literacy). Supports Social Determinants of Health (SDOH) analysis and care coordination.",
clinical,care_coordination,care_plan_goal,cancellation_reason,cancellation_reason,Goal Cancellation Reason,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Clinical or administrative reason for cancelling this goal (e.g., Patient declined, Goal no longer clinically appropriate, Superseded by updated goal). Required for care plan audit and CDI workflows.",
clinical,care_coordination,care_plan_goal,cancelled_date,cancelled_date,Goal Cancelled Date,DATE,,,,,transactional_data,The date on which this clinical goal was cancelled or discontinued. Populated only when goal_status is cancelled. Supports care plan audit and quality review.,
clinical,care_coordination,care_plan_goal,care_gap_related,care_gap_related,Care Gap Related Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,"Indicates whether this goal was created in response to an identified care gap (e.g., overdue preventive screening, uncontrolled chronic condition measure). Supports HEDIS gap closure tracking and value-based care reporting.",
clinical,care_coordination,care_plan_goal,care_team_role,care_team_role,Care Team Role Responsible,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Clinical role of the care team member primarily responsible for this goal (e.g., Primary Care Physician, Care Manager, Registered Nurse, Dietitian). Supports care team coordination and workload analytics.",
clinical,care_coordination,care_plan_goal,created_timestamp,created_timestamp,Goal Record Created Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,"Timestamp when this care plan goal record was first created in the system. Used for audit trail, data lineage, and regulatory compliance with medical record retention requirements.",
clinical,care_coordination,care_plan_goal,current_value,current_value,Goal Current Measured Value,"DECIMAL(18,4)",,,,,transactional_data,"Most recently recorded value for the LOINC-coded target measure, representing the patients current status relative to the goal target. Enables real-time progress tracking and gap analysis.",
clinical,care_coordination,care_plan_goal,current_value_date,current_value_date,Goal Current Value Date,DATE,,,,,transactional_data,Date on which the current measured value was recorded. Used to assess recency of progress data and identify goals with stale measurements.,
clinical,care_coordination,care_plan_goal,expressed_by_type,expressed_by_type,Goal Expressed By Type,STRING,,,,patient|practitioner|related-person|caregiver,transactional_data,"Indicates who expressed or originated this goal — the patient themselves, a practitioner, a related person (family member), or a caregiver. Supports patient-centered care analytics and CAHPS reporting.",
clinical,care_coordination,care_plan_goal,fhir_goal_reference,fhir_goal_reference,Fast Healthcare Interoperability Resources (FHIR) Goal Resource ID,STRING,,,,"^[A-Za-z0-9-.]{1,64}$",transactional_data,"HL7 FHIR R4 logical resource ID for this goal, enabling interoperability with external systems, Health Information Exchanges (HIE), and patient-facing applications via FHIR APIs.",
clinical,care_coordination,care_plan_goal,goal_category_display,goal_category_display,Goal Category Display Name,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Human-readable display name corresponding to the SNOMED CT goal category code (e.g., Dietary Goal, Exercise Goal, Medication Adherence). Used in clinical reporting and care plan summaries.",
clinical,care_coordination,care_plan_goal,goal_category_snomed_code,goal_category_snomed_code,Goal Category SNOMED CT Code,STRING,,,,"^[0-9]{6,18}$",transactional_data,"SNOMED CT coded category classifying the clinical domain of this goal (e.g., dietary goal, exercise goal, medication adherence goal, physiological goal). Enables standardized population health analytics and HEDIS reporting.",
clinical,care_coordination,care_plan_goal,goal_description,goal_description,Goal Description,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"pii_phi,pii_pii,pii_sensitive",
clinical,care_coordination,care_plan_goal,goal_external_code,goal_external_code,Goal External Identifier,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Source system identifier for this goal as assigned by the originating Electronic Health Record (EHR) system (e.g., Epic Healthy Planet goal ID). Supports cross-system reconciliation and audit traceability.",
clinical,care_coordination,care_plan_goal,goal_status,goal_status,Goal Status,STRING,,,,proposed|accepted|in-progress|achieved|cancelled,transactional_data,Current lifecycle status of the clinical goal reflecting its progression from proposal through achievement or cancellation. Aligns with HL7 FHIR R4 Goal.lifecycleStatus value set.,
clinical,care_coordination,care_plan_goal,goal_title,goal_title,Goal Title,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Short, human-readable title summarizing the clinical goal (e.g., Reduce HbA1c to below 7%, Achieve 10,000 steps daily). Used in clinical dashboards and patient-facing care plan summaries.",
clinical,care_coordination,care_plan_goal,last_reviewed_date,last_reviewed_date,Goal Last Reviewed Date,DATE,,,,,transactional_data,"Date on which the care team last formally reviewed this goals progress. Used for care management workflows, overdue review identification, and regulatory compliance with care plan review requirements.",
clinical,care_coordination,care_plan_goal,note,note,Goal Clinical Note,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Free-text clinical annotation or progress note associated with this goal, capturing care team observations, patient feedback, or contextual information not captured in structured fields.",
clinical,care_coordination,care_plan_goal,patient_agreement,patient_agreement,Patient Goal Agreement Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,Indicates whether the patient has agreed to and accepted this clinical goal as part of their care plan. Supports shared decision-making documentation and patient engagement analytics.,
clinical,care_coordination,care_plan_goal,priority,priority,Goal Priority,STRING,,,,high-priority|medium-priority|low-priority,transactional_data,Clinical priority level assigned to this goal relative to other goals in the care plan. Guides care team focus and resource allocation. Aligns with HL7 FHIR R4 Goal.priority value set.,
clinical,care_coordination,care_plan_goal,review_frequency,review_frequency,Goal Review Frequency,STRING,,,,daily|weekly|monthly|quarterly|annually|as-needed,transactional_data,Prescribed frequency at which this goal should be reviewed by the care team. Drives care management workflow scheduling and compliance monitoring.,
clinical,care_coordination,care_plan_goal,sdoh_related,sdoh_related,Social Determinants of Health (SDOH) Related Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,"Indicates whether this goal is related to Social Determinants of Health (SDOH) factors such as food insecurity, housing instability, or transportation barriers. Enables SDOH-stratified population health reporting.",
clinical,care_coordination,care_plan_goal,source_system,source_system,Source System,STRING,,,,Epic|Cerner|MEDITECH|Manual|HIE,transactional_data,"Originating operational system from which this goal record was sourced (e.g., Epic Healthy Planet, Cerner Millennium, Health Information Exchange). Supports data lineage and ETL audit.",
clinical,care_coordination,care_plan_goal,start_date,start_date,Goal Start Date,DATE,,,,,transactional_data,The date on which work toward this clinical goal was initiated or the goal became active. Used for goal duration calculations and longitudinal care analytics.,
clinical,care_coordination,care_plan_goal,status_changed_timestamp,status_changed_timestamp,Goal Status Changed Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,"Timestamp when the goal_status was most recently changed (e.g., from proposed to accepted, or from in-progress to achieved). Enables lifecycle duration analytics and care management SLA reporting.",
clinical,care_coordination,care_plan_goal,target_date,target_date,Goal Target Date,DATE,,,,,transactional_data,"The date by which the patient is expected to achieve this clinical goal. Used for care plan timeline management, overdue goal identification, and population health reporting.",
clinical,care_coordination,care_plan_goal,target_value,target_value,Goal Target Value,"DECIMAL(18,4)",,,,,transactional_data,"Numeric target value the patient is expected to achieve for the specified LOINC-coded measure (e.g., 7.0 for HbA1c percentage, 130 for systolic blood pressure in mmHg). Used in progress tracking and outcome analytics.",
clinical,care_coordination,care_plan_goal,target_value_comparator,target_value_comparator,Goal Target Value Comparator,STRING,,,,<|<=|>=|>,transactional_data,"Relational comparator indicating the direction of the target (e.g., <= means the measured value should be less than or equal to the target). Enables precise goal evaluation logic in clinical decision support.",
clinical,care_coordination,care_plan_goal,target_value_unit,target_value_unit,Goal Target Value Unit of Measure,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Unit of measure for the numeric target value, expressed using UCUM (Unified Code for Units of Measure) notation (e.g., %, mm[Hg], kg, steps/d). Required for clinical interpretation and interoperability.",
clinical,care_coordination,care_plan_goal,updated_timestamp,updated_timestamp,Goal Record Last Updated Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,"Timestamp of the most recent modification to this care plan goal record. Used for change detection, incremental ETL processing, and audit compliance.",
clinical,care_coordination,care_plan_goal,version_number,version_number,Goal Version Number,INT,,,,,transactional_data,Sequential version number incremented each time this goal record is substantively updated. Supports audit trail requirements and longitudinal goal history tracking.,
clinical,care_coordination,care_team,care_team_id,care_team_id,Care Team ID,BIGINT,Y,,,,master_data,Unique surrogate identifier for the clinical care team record in the lakehouse silver layer.,
clinical,care_coordination,care_team,care_plan_id,care_plan_id,Care Plan ID,BIGINT,,clinical.care_plan.care_plan_id,,,master_data,"Reference to the associated care plan that this team is responsible for executing. Links care team accountability to specific clinical goals, interventions, and outcomes defined in the care plan.",
clinical,care_coordination,care_team,care_site_id,care_site_id,Facility ID,BIGINT,,facility.care_site.care_site_id,,,master_data,"Reference to the facility (hospital, clinic, outpatient center) where this care team operates. Supports multi-facility enterprise analytics and regulatory reporting by facility.",
clinical,care_coordination,care_team,improvement_initiative_id,improvement_initiative_id,Improvement Initiative Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,quality.improvement_initiative.improvement_initiative_id,,,master_data,"Foreign key linking to quality.improvement_initiative. Business justification: Quality initiatives often involve specific care teams (sepsis team, stroke team). Direct linkage enables tracking team-based initiative impact. Essential for care team performance improvement and acco",
clinical,care_coordination,care_team,mpi_record_id,mpi_record_id,Patient ID,BIGINT,,patient.mpi_record.mpi_record_id,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_health",,master_data,Reference to the patient for whom this care team is assigned. Links to the master patient record (MPI). Core PARTY_REFERENCE required by TRANSACTION_HEADER role.,
clinical,care_coordination,care_team,org_unit_id,org_unit_id,Department ID,BIGINT,,workforce.org_unit.org_unit_id,,,master_data,"Reference to the clinical department or unit (e.g., ICU, Cardiology, ED, Oncology) to which this care team is assigned. Enables department-level care coordination and staffing analytics.",
clinical,care_coordination,care_team,primary_contact_provider_clinician_id,primary_contact_provider_clinician_id,Primary Contact Provider ID,BIGINT,,provider.clinician.clinician_id,,,master_data,"Reference to the care team member designated as the primary point of contact for the patient and family. May differ from the attending provider (e.g., a care coordinator or NP may be the primary contact). Supports care coordination and patient communication workflows.",
clinical,care_coordination,care_team,tertiary_care_member_provider_clinician_id,tertiary_care_member_provider_clinician_id,Member Provider ID,BIGINT,,provider.clinician.clinician_id,,,master_data,"Reference to the provider (clinician) record for this care team member. Links to the clinician master record for NPI, credentials, and specialty information.",
clinical,care_coordination,care_team,visit_id,visit_id,Encounter ID,BIGINT,,encounter.visit.visit_id,,,master_data,"Reference to the clinical encounter (inpatient admission, outpatient visit, ED visit) with which this care team is associated. A care team may exist without a specific encounter for longitudinal/primary care contexts.",
clinical,care_coordination,care_team,aco_attributed,aco_attributed,Accountable Care Organization (ACO) Attribution Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,"Indicates whether this care team is associated with an Accountable Care Organization (ACO) attribution for the patient. Relevant for value-based care reporting, MSSP program compliance, and population health management.",
clinical,care_coordination,care_team,care_coordination_level,care_coordination_level,Care Coordination Level,STRING,,,,standard|enhanced|complex|intensive,master_data,"Classification of the intensity of care coordination required for this team, based on patient complexity and care needs. Drives resource allocation, staffing decisions, and care management program enrollment.",
clinical,care_coordination,care_team,care_setting,care_setting,Care Setting,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Clinical care setting in which the team operates. Distinct from team_type — care_setting describes the physical/virtual environment of care delivery (e.g., ED, ICU, telehealth), while team_type describes the organizational model. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: inpatient|outpatient|emergency|observation|telehealth|home_health|skilled_nursing — promote to reference product]",
clinical,care_coordination,care_team,cdi_review_flag,cdi_review_flag,Clinical Documentation Improvement (CDI) Review Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,"Indicates whether this care team record has been flagged for Clinical Documentation Improvement (CDI) review. CDI specialists use this flag to identify cases where care team documentation may require clarification to support accurate coding, DRG assignment, and reimbursement.",
clinical,care_coordination,care_team,coverage_end_timestamp,coverage_end_timestamp,Coverage End Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,master_data,Precise timestamp when this care team members coverage period ended. Used in conjunction with coverage_start_timestamp to define shift-level coverage windows and identify coverage gaps.,
clinical,care_coordination,care_team,coverage_start_timestamp,coverage_start_timestamp,Coverage Start Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,master_data,"Precise timestamp when this care team members coverage period began (e.g., start of a shift or on-call rotation). More granular than member_start_date; used for shift-level coverage gap analysis and handoff documentation.",
clinical,care_coordination,care_team,created_timestamp,created_timestamp,Record Created Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,master_data,"Timestamp when the care team record was first created in the source EHR system. Supports audit trail, data lineage, and regulatory compliance requirements. Aligns with RECORD_AUDIT_CREATED category.",
clinical,care_coordination,care_team,discharge_disposition_code,discharge_disposition_code,Discharge Disposition Code,STRING,,,,,master_data,"CMS-standard discharge disposition code indicating the patients destination upon leaving this care teams care (e.g., 01 = Home, 03 = SNF, 20 = Expired). Populated for inpatient and transitional care teams at team closure. Required for UB-04 billing and CMS quality reporting.",
clinical,care_coordination,care_team,ehr_care_team_csn,ehr_care_team_csn,Electronic Health Record (EHR) Care Team Contact Serial Number (CSN),STRING,,,,,master_data,Epic-specific Contact Serial Number (CSN) uniquely identifying the care team context within an Epic encounter. Used for cross-referencing Epic ClinDoc records during ETL and data reconciliation.,
clinical,care_coordination,care_team,hie_shared,hie_shared,Health Information Exchange (HIE) Shared Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,"Indicates whether this care team record has been shared via a Health Information Exchange (HIE) to external care partners (e.g., referring providers, ACO partners, post-acute facilities). Supports care coordination across organizational boundaries and HIE participation reporting.",
clinical,care_coordination,care_team,is_multidisciplinary,is_multidisciplinary,Multidisciplinary Team Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,"Indicates whether this care team is formally designated as a multidisciplinary team (MDT), involving providers from two or more distinct clinical disciplines. MDT designation is relevant for complex case management, oncology tumor boards, and regulatory quality reporting.",
clinical,care_coordination,care_team,is_on_call,is_on_call,On-Call Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,Indicates whether this care team member is currently designated as on-call for the patient. On-call designation determines who is contacted for urgent clinical decisions outside of normal coverage hours.,
clinical,care_coordination,care_team,is_primary_contact,is_primary_contact,Primary Contact Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,Indicates whether this care team member is designated as the primary point of contact for the patient and family within the team. Only one member per team should hold this designation at any given time.,
clinical,care_coordination,care_team,is_primary_team,is_primary_team,Primary Care Team Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,Indicates whether this is the patients primary care team (as opposed to a consulting or specialty team). A patient may have multiple concurrent care teams; this flag identifies the team with primary clinical accountability.,
clinical,care_coordination,care_team,member_end_date,member_end_date,Care Team Member Participation End Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,"Date on which this individual members participation in the care team ended (e.g., due to rotation, discharge, or reassignment). Null for currently active members. Supports member lifecycle and coverage gap analysis.",
clinical,care_coordination,care_team,member_role_code,member_role_code,Care Team Member Role Code,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Standardized role code for the care team members function within the team (e.g., SNOMED CT role codes or Epic-defined role codes such as ATT for Attending, RES for Resident, CON for Consultant). More granular than member_type.",
clinical,care_coordination,care_team,member_role_name,member_role_name,Care Team Member Role Name,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Human-readable name of the care team members role (e.g., Attending Physician, Consulting Cardiologist, Charge Nurse, Clinical Pharmacist). Complements member_role_code for display in EHR panels and reports.",
clinical,care_coordination,care_team,member_start_date,member_start_date,Care Team Member Participation Start Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,"Date on which this individual member began participating in the care team. Supports member-level assignment lifecycle tracking, transitions of care documentation, and care coordination analytics.",
clinical,care_coordination,care_team,member_status,member_status,Care Team Member Status,STRING,,,,active|inactive|on_leave|removed,master_data,"Current status of the individual care team members participation. Active indicates current participation; inactive indicates the member has left the team; on_leave indicates temporary absence (e.g., vacation, LOA); removed indicates the member was explicitly removed from the team.",
clinical,care_coordination,care_team,member_type,member_type,Care Team Member Type,STRING,,,,,master_data,Classification of the care team member by clinical role category. Physician includes MDs and DOs; NP = Nurse Practitioner; PA = Physician Assistant; RN = Registered Nurse; social_worker covers licensed clinical social workers; pharmacist covers clinical pharmacy staff; care_coordinator covers non-clinical coordination roles. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: physician|np|pa|rn|social_worker|pharmacist|care_coordinator — 7 candidates stripped; promote to reference product],
clinical,care_coordination,care_team,npi,npi,National Provider Identifier (NPI),STRING,,,,^[0-9]{10}$,master_data,"10-digit National Provider Identifier (NPI) of the care team member, as assigned by CMS. Required for billing, credentialing, and regulatory reporting. Denormalized here for care team-level queries without requiring a join to the provider master.",
clinical,care_coordination,care_team,reason_code,reason_code,Care Team Reason Code,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Coded reason for the care team assignment, expressed using SNOMED CT or ICD-10 codes (e.g., a specific diagnosis or condition driving the team composition). Supports clinical decision support and population health analytics.",
clinical,care_coordination,care_team,reason_description,reason_description,Care Team Reason Description,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Free-text or decoded description of the clinical reason for the care team assignment (e.g., Complex heart failure management, Post-surgical recovery). Complements reason_code for human-readable reporting.",
clinical,care_coordination,care_team,sdoh_flag,sdoh_flag,Social Determinants of Health (SDOH) Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,"Indicates whether this care team has been assigned to address Social Determinants of Health (SDOH) needs for the patient (e.g., housing instability, food insecurity, transportation barriers). Supports population health management and SDOH screening program reporting.",
clinical,care_coordination,care_team,source_system,source_system,Source System,STRING,,,,Epic|Cerner|MEDITECH|Manual|HIE,master_data,"Operational system of record from which this care team record was sourced (e.g., Epic ClinDoc, Cerner PowerChart). Supports data lineage, ETL audit, and multi-system reconciliation in the lakehouse.",
clinical,care_coordination,care_team,source_system_team_code,source_system_team_code,Source System Care Team ID,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Native identifier of the care team record in the originating operational system (e.g., Epic internal care team CSN or Cerner care team ID). Enables traceability back to the source EHR for reconciliation and audit.",
clinical,care_coordination,care_team,specialty_code,specialty_code,Clinical Specialty Code,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Standardized code representing the primary clinical specialty of the care team (e.g., 207R00000X for Internal Medicine per NUCC taxonomy). Enables specialty-based care coordination queries and referral management.",
clinical,care_coordination,care_team,specialty_name,specialty_name,Clinical Specialty Name,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Human-readable name of the primary clinical specialty of the care team (e.g., Cardiology, Oncology, Pediatrics). Complements specialty_code for display and reporting purposes.",
clinical,care_coordination,care_team,team_end_date,team_end_date,Care Team End Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,Date on which the care team was dissolved or the patient was discharged/transitioned out of this teams care. Null for currently active teams. Aligns with FHIR CareTeam.period.end.,
clinical,care_coordination,care_team,team_name,team_name,Care Team Name,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Human-readable name or label assigned to the care team (e.g., Cardiology Inpatient Team A, Primary Care Team — Dr. Smith). Used for display in EHR care team panels and care coordination dashboards.",
clinical,care_coordination,care_team,team_start_date,team_start_date,Care Team Start Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,Date on which the care team became active and assumed clinical accountability for the patient. Used for transitions of care documentation and care coordination reporting. Aligns with FHIR CareTeam.period.start.,
clinical,care_coordination,care_team,team_status,team_status,Care Team Status,STRING,,,,active|inactive|suspended|proposed|entered-in-error,master_data,Current lifecycle status of the care team record. Active indicates the team is currently providing care; inactive indicates the team has been dissolved or the patient discharged; proposed indicates a team pending activation; suspended indicates temporary pause; entered-in-error supports data correction workflows.,
clinical,care_coordination,care_team,team_type,team_type,Care Team Type,STRING,,,,inpatient|outpatient|primary|specialty|multidisciplinary|transitional,master_data,"Classification of the care team by care setting and organizational model. Inpatient teams are hospital-based; outpatient teams support ambulatory care; primary teams represent the patients longitudinal PCP-led team; specialty teams are disease- or organ-specific; multidisciplinary teams span disciplines; transitional teams support transitions of care (e.g., discharge to SNF).",
clinical,care_coordination,care_team,transitions_of_care_flag,transitions_of_care_flag,Transitions of Care Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,"Indicates whether this care team is specifically designated to manage a transition of care event (e.g., hospital discharge to home, SNF, or rehabilitation). Supports CMS Transitional Care Management (TCM) billing and readmission reduction programs.",
clinical,care_coordination,care_team,updated_timestamp,updated_timestamp,Record Updated Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,master_data,"Timestamp of the most recent modification to the care team record in the source EHR system. Supports change detection, incremental ETL processing, and audit trail requirements.",
clinical,care_coordination,care_team,vbp_program_code,vbp_program_code,Value-Based Purchasing (VBP) Program Code,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Code identifying the value-based purchasing or alternative payment model (APM) program under which this care team operates (e.g., MSSP, BPCI-A, CPC+). Supports VBP performance tracking and regulatory reporting to CMS.",
clinical,care_coordination,care_team_member,care_team_member_id,care_team_member_id,Care Team Member ID,BIGINT,Y,," dbx_confidential, dbx_pii",,master_data,Unique surrogate identifier for each care team member record in the silver layer lakehouse. Primary key for this entity.,
clinical,care_coordination,care_team_member,care_plan_id,care_plan_id,Care Plan ID,BIGINT,,clinical.care_plan.care_plan_id,,,master_data,"Reference to the care plan to which this care team members responsibilities are linked. Associates the members role with specific care plan goals, interventions, and outcomes.",
clinical,care_coordination,care_team_member,care_site_id,care_site_id,Facility ID,BIGINT,,facility.care_site.care_site_id,,,master_data,"Reference to the facility (hospital, clinic, outpatient center) where this care team member is providing care. Supports multi-facility enterprise care team queries and transitions of care documentation.",
clinical,care_coordination,care_team_member,employee_id,employee_id,Added By User ID,BIGINT,,workforce.employee.employee_id,"dbx_confidential, dbx_pii",,master_data,"The system user identifier of the clinician or staff member who added this provider to the care team. Used for audit trail, accountability, and CDI (Clinical Documentation Improvement) workflows.",
clinical,care_coordination,care_team_member,mpi_record_id,mpi_record_id,Patient ID,BIGINT,,patient.mpi_record.mpi_record_id,,,master_data,Reference to the patient for whom this care team membership is established. Links the care team member record to the patients Master Patient Index (MPI) record.,
clinical,care_coordination,care_team_member,org_unit_id,org_unit_id,Department ID,BIGINT,,workforce.org_unit.org_unit_id,,,master_data,"Reference to the clinical department or unit to which this care team member is assigned (e.g., ICU, ED, Cardiology, Oncology). Used for care team composition reporting and operational analytics.",
clinical,care_coordination,care_team_member,primary_care_clinician_id,primary_care_clinician_id,Provider ID,BIGINT,,provider.clinician.clinician_id,,,master_data,"Reference to the clinician or provider record for this care team member. Identifies the individual practitioner (physician, NP, PA, RN, pharmacist, social worker, care coordinator, etc.) assigned to the team.",
clinical,care_coordination,care_team_member,primary_care_team_id,primary_care_team_id,Care Team ID,BIGINT,,clinical.care_team.care_team_id,,,master_data,Reference to the parent care team to which this member belongs. Links the individual membership record to the overarching care team construct.,
clinical,care_coordination,care_team_member,visit_id,visit_id,Encounter ID,BIGINT,,encounter.visit.visit_id,,,master_data,"Reference to the clinical encounter (inpatient, outpatient, ED visit) during which this care team membership is active. Nullable for longitudinal care team assignments not tied to a single encounter.",
clinical,care_coordination,care_team_member,admission_date,admission_date,Admission Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,The date of the patients admission associated with this care team membership. Used to contextualize the care team assignment within the inpatient episode and for Length of Stay (LOS) analytics.,
clinical,care_coordination,care_team_member,care_setting,care_setting,Care Setting,STRING,,,,,master_data,"The clinical care setting in which this care team member is providing services (e.g., inpatient, outpatient, ICU, ED, telehealth). Drives care coordination workflows and transitions of care documentation. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: inpatient|outpatient|emergency|icu|surgical|telehealth|home_health|skilled_nursing — promote to reference product]",
clinical,care_coordination,care_team_member,care_team_category,care_team_category,Care Team Category,STRING,,,,longitudinal|episode|event|condition,master_data,"Classifies the care team type to which this member belongs: longitudinal (ongoing primary care), episode-based (specific inpatient stay), event-based (single procedure or visit), or condition-based (chronic disease management). Aligns with HL7 FHIR CareTeam.category.",
clinical,care_coordination,care_team_member,clinical_focus,clinical_focus,Clinical Focus,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Free-text or coded description of the specific clinical focus area or condition for which this care team member is responsible (e.g., Diabetes Management, Post-Surgical Recovery, Palliative Care). Supports population health management and care coordination analytics.",
clinical,care_coordination,care_team_member,coverage_type,coverage_type,Coverage Type,STRING,,,,scheduled|cross_coverage|locum|temporary|permanent,master_data,"Indicates whether this care team members assignment represents a scheduled/permanent role, cross-coverage arrangement, locum tenens, or temporary assignment. Used for staffing analytics and care continuity tracking.",
clinical,care_coordination,care_team_member,created_timestamp,created_timestamp,Record Created Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,master_data,"The date and time when this care team member record was first created in the source system. Used for audit trail, data lineage, and care team history analytics.",
clinical,care_coordination,care_team_member,discharge_date,discharge_date,Discharge Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,"The date of the patients discharge associated with this care team membership. Used for transitions of care documentation, Length of Stay (LOS) calculations, and post-discharge follow-up assignment.",
clinical,care_coordination,care_team_member,fte_allocation,fte_allocation,Full-Time Equivalent (FTE) Allocation,"DECIMAL(5,2)",,,,,master_data,"The proportion of this providers Full-Time Equivalent (FTE) effort allocated to this care team assignment, expressed as a decimal (e.g., 0.50 for 50% effort). Used for workforce planning, staffing analytics, and care team capacity management.",
clinical,care_coordination,care_team_member,handoff_timestamp,handoff_timestamp,Care Handoff Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,master_data,"The date and time at which clinical responsibility was formally handed off from this care team member to another provider. Supports transitions of care documentation, Joint Commission handoff communication standards, and care continuity analytics.",
clinical,care_coordination,care_team_member,is_active,is_active,Active Record Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,"Boolean flag indicating whether this care team member record is currently active and valid. Distinct from member_status in that this flag supports soft-delete and record lifecycle management at the data platform level, while member_status reflects the clinical workflow state.",
clinical,care_coordination,care_team_member,is_attending,is_attending,Attending Physician Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,"Indicates whether this care team member holds the attending physician designation for the encounter or care episode. The attending physician bears primary clinical and legal responsibility for the patients care. Critical for billing, documentation, and regulatory reporting.",
clinical,care_coordination,care_team_member,is_on_call,is_on_call,On-Call Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,Indicates whether this care team member is currently designated as on-call for the patient. Supports after-hours care coordination and urgent clinical communication routing.,
clinical,care_coordination,care_team_member,is_pcp,is_pcp,Primary Care Physician (PCP) Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,"Indicates whether this care team member is the patients designated Primary Care Physician (PCP). Used in population health management, care coordination, and payer attribution workflows.",
clinical,care_coordination,care_team_member,is_primary_contact,is_primary_contact,Primary Contact Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,Indicates whether this care team member is designated as the primary point of contact for the patient and/or family. Only one member per care team should have this flag set to true at any given time. Used in patient communication workflows and care coordination.,
clinical,care_coordination,care_team_member,member_status,member_status,Care Team Member Status,STRING,,,,active|inactive|pending|suspended|removed,master_data,Current participation status of this care team member. active indicates the member is currently responsible for the patients care; inactive or removed indicates the member has been discharged from the team. Drives care coordination queries and transitions of care documentation.,
clinical,care_coordination,care_team_member,member_type,member_type,Care Team Member Type,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Broad classification of the care team members professional discipline or role category (e.g., physician, nurse practitioner, pharmacist, social worker). Drives care coordination workflows and transitions of care documentation. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: physician|nurse_practitioner|physician_assistant|registered_nurse|pharmacist|social_worker|care_coordinator|other — promote to reference product]",
clinical,care_coordination,care_team_member,notes,notes,Care Team Member Notes,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Free-text notes or comments associated with this care team members assignment, such as specific responsibilities, coverage instructions, or care coordination context. Used by clinical staff for care team management.",
clinical,care_coordination,care_team_member,notification_preference,notification_preference,Notification Preference,STRING,,,,secure_message|pager|phone|email|in_basket,master_data,"The preferred communication channel for notifying this care team member of patient updates, critical results, or care coordination messages (e.g., secure message, pager, phone, Epic In Basket). Drives clinical communication routing.",
clinical,care_coordination,care_team_member,npi,npi,National Provider Identifier (NPI),STRING,,,,^[0-9]{10}$,master_data,"The 10-digit National Provider Identifier (NPI) assigned to this care team member by CMS. Used for billing, claims submission, and provider identity verification. Denormalized here for operational convenience in care team queries without requiring a provider join.",
clinical,care_coordination,care_team_member,provider_assignment_end_date,provider_assignment_end_date,Care Team Member Assignment End Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,The date on which this providers membership on the care team ended or is scheduled to end. Nullable for open-ended assignments. Used for historical care team queries and transitions of care documentation.,
clinical,care_coordination,care_team_member,provider_assignment_start_date,provider_assignment_start_date,Care Team Member Assignment Start Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,The date on which this providers membership on the care team became effective. Used to determine the period of clinical responsibility and for transitions of care documentation.,
clinical,care_coordination,care_team_member,provider_assignment_type,provider_assignment_type,Care Team Assignment Type,STRING,,,,primary|consulting|covering|co-managing|observing,master_data,"Classifies the nature of this providers assignment to the care team (e.g., primary responsibility, consulting, covering/cross-coverage, co-managing). Used to distinguish primary from secondary care responsibilities and for billing attribution.",
clinical,care_coordination,care_team_member,relationship_to_patient,relationship_to_patient,Provider Relationship to Patient,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Describes the clinical or care relationship between this provider and the patient (e.g., Treating Physician, Consulting Specialist, Case Manager, Discharge Planner). Used in care coordination documentation and transitions of care workflows.",
clinical,care_coordination,care_team_member,removal_reason,removal_reason,Care Team Member Removal Reason,STRING,,,,,master_data,"The reason this care team member was removed or deactivated from the care team (e.g., patient discharge, transfer, provider request, coverage end, credentialing issue). Used for care team audit trails and transitions of care documentation. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: discharge|transfer|provider_request|patient_request|coverage_end|credentialing|other — 7 candidates stripped; promote to reference product]",
clinical,care_coordination,care_team_member,role_code,role_code,Care Team Role Code,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Standardized code representing the specific functional role of this member within the care team (e.g., attending physician, consulting physician, primary nurse, case manager). Sourced from Epic or Cerner role code tables and aligned with HL7 FHIR CareTeam participant role codes.",
clinical,care_coordination,care_team_member,role_name,role_name,Care Team Role Name,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Human-readable display name for the care team members role (e.g., Attending Physician, Primary Care Nurse, Clinical Pharmacist, Discharge Planner). Used in clinical documentation and care coordination interfaces.",
clinical,care_coordination,care_team_member,sequence_number,sequence_number,Care Team Member Sequence Number,INT,,,,,master_data,Ordinal sequence number indicating the display order or priority ranking of this member within the care team. Used for care team list rendering in EHR interfaces and for determining primary vs. secondary member ordering.,
clinical,care_coordination,care_team_member,snomed_role_code,snomed_role_code,Systematized Nomenclature of Medicine Clinical Terms (SNOMED CT) Role Code,STRING,,,,,master_data,The SNOMED CT concept code representing the clinical role of this care team member. Enables semantic interoperability with FHIR-compliant systems and clinical decision support engines.,
clinical,care_coordination,care_team_member,source_system,source_system,Source System,STRING,,,,epic|cerner|meditech|manual,master_data,"Identifies the operational system of record from which this care team member record was sourced (Epic, Cerner Millennium, MEDITECH Expanse, or manually entered). Used for data lineage, reconciliation, and ETL audit purposes.",
clinical,care_coordination,care_team_member,source_system_member_code,source_system_member_code,Source System Care Team Member ID,STRING,,,"dbx_confidential, dbx_pii",,master_data,"The native identifier for this care team member record in the originating operational system (Epic ClinDoc, Cerner PowerChart, etc.). Used for data lineage, cross-system reconciliation, and ETL traceability.",
clinical,care_coordination,care_team_member,specialty_code,specialty_code,Provider Specialty Code,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Standardized code representing the clinical specialty of this care team member (e.g., internal medicine, cardiology, oncology). Sourced from the provider taxonomy code set. Used for care team composition analytics and referral management.",
clinical,care_coordination,care_team_member,specialty_name,specialty_name,Provider Specialty Name,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Human-readable display name for the clinical specialty of this care team member (e.g., Cardiology, Internal Medicine, Oncology). Used in care team displays, clinical documentation, and care coordination interfaces.",
clinical,care_coordination,care_team_member,updated_timestamp,updated_timestamp,Record Updated Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,master_data,"The date and time when this care team member record was last modified in the source system. Used for change tracking, data lineage, and incremental ETL processing.",
clinical,care_coordination,plan_care_coordination,plan_care_coordination_id,plan_care_coordination_id,Plan Care Coordination Identifier,BIGINT,Y,,,,association_data,Unique surrogate identifier for this care plan-health plan coordination record,
clinical,care_coordination,plan_care_coordination,care_plan_id,care_plan_id,Plan Care Coordination - Care Plan Id,BIGINT,,clinical.care_plan.care_plan_id,,,association_data,Foreign key linking to the patient care plan being coordinated with payer requirements,
clinical,care_coordination,plan_care_coordination,clinician_id,clinician_id,Payer Case Manager Identifier,BIGINT,,provider.clinician.clinician_id,,,association_data,Reference to the health plans case manager or care coordinator assigned to this care plan. May be different from the provider organizations care coordinator.,
clinical,care_coordination,plan_care_coordination,health_plan_id,health_plan_id,Plan Care Coordination - Health Plan Id,BIGINT,,insurance.health_plan.health_plan_id,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii",,association_data,Foreign key linking to the health insurance plan that has specific care management requirements for this care plan,
clinical,care_coordination,plan_care_coordination,authorization_date,authorization_date,Authorization Approval Date,DATE,,,,,association_data,Date when the health plan approved authorization for this care plan. Null if authorization is pending or denied.,
clinical,care_coordination,plan_care_coordination,authorization_expiration_date,authorization_expiration_date,Authorization Expiration Date,DATE,,,,,association_data,Date when the health plan authorization for this care plan expires. Triggers reauthorization workflows.,
clinical,care_coordination,plan_care_coordination,authorization_number,authorization_number,Payer Authorization Number,STRING,,,,,association_data,The authorization or reference number issued by the health plan for this care plan. Required for claims submission and payer coordination.,
clinical,care_coordination,plan_care_coordination,authorization_status,authorization_status,Payer Authorization Status,STRING,,,,,association_data,"Current authorization status from the health plan for this care plan. Values: pending, approved, denied, expired, revoked. Drives billing and service delivery authorization.",
clinical,care_coordination,plan_care_coordination,care_management_tier,care_management_tier,Care Management Tier,STRING,,,,,association_data,"The level of care management intensity required by the health plan for this care plan. Values: basic, enhanced, intensive, complex. Drives care coordinator assignment and contact frequency requirements.",
clinical,care_coordination,plan_care_coordination,coordination_end_date,coordination_end_date,Coordination End Date,DATE,,,,,association_data,Date when coordination between this care plan and health plan ended. Null if coordination is ongoing.,
clinical,care_coordination,plan_care_coordination,coordination_start_date,coordination_start_date,Coordination Start Date,DATE,,,,,association_data,Date when coordination between this care plan and health plan began. May differ from enrollment_date if coordination started before formal program enrollment.,
clinical,care_coordination,plan_care_coordination,created_timestamp,created_timestamp,Record Creation Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,association_data,Timestamp when this care plan-health plan coordination record was first created in the system.,
clinical,care_coordination,plan_care_coordination,enrollment_date,enrollment_date,Care Management Enrollment Date,DATE,,,,,association_data,Date when this care plan was enrolled in the health plans care management program. Tracks when payer-specific care coordination began.,
clinical,care_coordination,plan_care_coordination,last_modified_timestamp,last_modified_timestamp,Record Last Modified Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,association_data,"Timestamp of the most recent modification to this coordination record. Tracks changes to authorization status, program enrollment, or other coordination attributes.",
clinical,care_coordination,plan_care_coordination,last_payer_review_date,last_payer_review_date,Last Payer Review Date,DATE,,,,,association_data,Date of the most recent review or audit of this care plan by the health plan. Used for tracking payer engagement and compliance reviews.,
clinical,care_coordination,plan_care_coordination,next_payer_review_date,next_payer_review_date,Next Payer Review Date,DATE,,,,,association_data,Scheduled date for the next review of this care plan by the health plan. Drives care coordination workflow reminders.,
clinical,care_coordination,plan_care_coordination,plan_specific_goal_count,plan_specific_goal_count,Plan-Specific Goal Count,INT,,,,,association_data,Number of care plan goals that are specifically required by this health plans care management program. Subset of total care plan goals.,
clinical,care_coordination,plan_care_coordination,primary_coverage_flag,primary_coverage_flag,Primary Coverage Indicator,BOOLEAN,,,,,association_data,"Indicates whether this health plan is the primary payer for this care plan. True for primary coverage, false for secondary/tertiary. Drives coordination of benefits and billing priority.",
clinical,care_coordination,plan_care_coordination,program_enrollment_status,program_enrollment_status,Program Enrollment Status,STRING,,,,,association_data,"Current enrollment status in the health plans care management program for this care plan. Values: enrolled, active, suspended, completed, disenrolled. Tracks program participation lifecycle.",
clinical,care_coordination,plan_care_coordination,program_name,program_name,Care Management Program Name,STRING,,,,,association_data,"Name of the specific care management program within the health plan that this care plan is enrolled in (e.g., Diabetes Management, CHF Care Coordination, Transitional Care).",
clinical,care_coordination,plan_care_coordination,quality_measure_set,quality_measure_set,Quality Measure Set,STRING,,,,,association_data,"The quality measure set or HEDIS measures that this health plan requires for this care plan (e.g., HEDIS Diabetes Composite, CMS Stars Measures). Drives quality reporting requirements.",
clinical,operational_support,flowsheet_row,flowsheet_row_id,flowsheet_row_id,Flowsheet Row Identifier,BIGINT,Y,,,,master_data,Primary key for flowsheet_row,
clinical,operational_support,flowsheet_row,flowsheet_template_id,flowsheet_template_id,Flowsheet Template Id,BIGINT,,clinical.flowsheet_template.flowsheet_template_id,,,master_data,Reference to the parent flowsheet template that contains this row. Links to the flowsheet template master table.,
clinical,operational_support,flowsheet_row,parent_flowsheet_row_id,parent_flowsheet_row_id,Parent Flowsheet Row Id,BIGINT,,clinical.flowsheet_row.flowsheet_row_id,dbx_self_ref_fk,,master_data,Self-referencing FK on flowsheet_row (parent_flowsheet_row_id),
clinical,operational_support,flowsheet_row,reference_loinc_code_id,reference_loinc_code_id,,BIGINT,,reference.loinc_code.loinc_code_id,,,master_data,FK to reference.loinc_code.loinc_code_id,
clinical,operational_support,flowsheet_row,specialty_id,specialty_id,Specialty Id,BIGINT,,provider.specialty.specialty_id,,,master_data,"Reference to the medical specialty or clinical department that primarily uses this flowsheet row (e.g., Cardiology, Critical Care, Pediatrics).",
clinical,operational_support,flowsheet_row,alert_enabled,alert_enabled,Alert Enabled,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,Indicates whether automated clinical alerts are enabled when values fall outside defined thresholds for this flowsheet row.,
clinical,operational_support,flowsheet_row,alert_severity,alert_severity,Alert Severity,STRING,,,,,master_data,Severity classification for clinical alerts generated by abnormal values in this flowsheet row.,
clinical,operational_support,flowsheet_row,calculation_formula,calculation_formula,Calculation Formula,STRING,,,,,master_data,Mathematical or logical formula used to automatically calculate values for this flowsheet row from other clinical data elements.,
clinical,operational_support,flowsheet_row,clinical_notes,clinical_notes,Clinical Notes,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Additional clinical guidance, interpretation notes, or special instructions for clinicians documenting this flowsheet row.",
clinical,operational_support,flowsheet_row,consent_required,consent_required,Consent Required,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,Indicates whether specific patient consent is required before documenting or sharing data from this flowsheet row.,
clinical,operational_support,flowsheet_row,cpt_code,cpt_code,Cpt Code,STRING,,,,,master_data,CPT code associated with the clinical service or procedure represented by this flowsheet row for billing and reimbursement purposes.,
clinical,operational_support,flowsheet_row,created_timestamp,created_timestamp,Created Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,master_data,Date and time when this flowsheet row record was first created in the system.,
clinical,operational_support,flowsheet_row,critical_high_threshold,critical_high_threshold,Critical High Threshold,"DECIMAL(18,4)",,,,,master_data,Critical high threshold value that triggers immediate clinical alerts when measurements exceed this level.,
clinical,operational_support,flowsheet_row,critical_low_threshold,critical_low_threshold,Critical Low Threshold,"DECIMAL(18,4)",,,,,master_data,Critical low threshold value that triggers immediate clinical alerts when measurements fall below this level.,
clinical,operational_support,flowsheet_row,data_type,data_type,Data Type,STRING,,,,,master_data,"The data type expected for values recorded in this flowsheet row (numeric, text, date, selection list, etc.).",
clinical,operational_support,flowsheet_row,device_type,device_type,Device Type,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Type of medical device or monitoring equipment typically used to capture measurements for this flowsheet row (e.g., bedside monitor, infusion pump, ventilator).",
clinical,operational_support,flowsheet_row,display_format,display_format,Display Format,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Format specification for displaying values in clinical user interfaces (e.g., decimal precision, date format, text length).",
clinical,operational_support,flowsheet_row,display_sequence,display_sequence,Display Sequence,INT,,,,,master_data,Numeric sequence controlling the display order of flowsheet rows in clinical documentation interfaces.,
clinical,operational_support,flowsheet_row,documentation_frequency,documentation_frequency,Documentation Frequency,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Expected or required frequency for documenting this measurement in clinical workflows (e.g., hourly for critical care vital signs).",
clinical,operational_support,flowsheet_row,effective_end_date,effective_end_date,Effective End Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,Date when this flowsheet row was retired or deprecated and is no longer available for new clinical documentation. Null for currently active rows.,
clinical,operational_support,flowsheet_row,effective_start_date,effective_start_date,Effective Start Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,Date when this flowsheet row became active and available for clinical documentation.,
clinical,operational_support,flowsheet_row,flowsheet_row_description,flowsheet_row_description,Description,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Detailed description of the clinical measurement or observation captured by this flowsheet row, including clinical context and usage guidance.",
clinical,operational_support,flowsheet_row,flowsheet_row_status,flowsheet_row_status,Status,STRING,,,,,master_data,Current lifecycle status of this flowsheet row in the master reference table. Inactive or deprecated rows are no longer available for new documentation.,
clinical,operational_support,flowsheet_row,interface_code,interface_code,Interface Code,STRING,,,,,master_data,"External system interface code used for mapping this flowsheet row to medical devices, laboratory systems, or other clinical data sources.",
