clinical,operational_support,procedure_equipment_usage,charge_captured_flag,charge_captured_flag,Charge Captured Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,association_data,Indicates whether a revenue cycle charge was generated for this equipment usage. Links equipment utilization to charge capture and revenue integrity.,
clinical,operational_support,procedure_equipment_usage,documentation_timestamp,documentation_timestamp,Documentation Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,association_data,Date and time when this equipment usage record was documented in the source system. Supports audit trail and data quality assessment.,
clinical,operational_support,procedure_equipment_usage,equipment_malfunction_flag,equipment_malfunction_flag,Equipment Malfunction Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,association_data,"Indicates whether the equipment experienced a malfunction, failure, or performance issue during this procedure. Triggers biomedical engineering investigation and potential FDA Medical Device Reporting (MDR).",
clinical,operational_support,procedure_equipment_usage,implant_used,implant_used,Implant Used Indicator,BOOLEAN,,,,,association_data,"Indicates whether a medical implant or device was used during the procedure. Triggers implant log documentation requirements, FDA device tracking obligations, and supply chain charge capture. [Moved from procedure_event: The implant_used flag in procedure_event is a procedure-level aggregate indicator, but the actual implant usage is equipment-specific. A procedure may use multiple equipment assets, only some of which are implants. The implant_used_flag and udi belong in the association to track which specific equipment assets were implanted, enabling FDA traceability at the device level rather than just the procedure level.]",
clinical,operational_support,procedure_equipment_usage,implant_used_flag,implant_used_flag,Implant Used Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,association_data,Indicates whether this specific equipment asset was used as an implantable device during the procedure. Critical for FDA traceability requirements and patient implant registries.,
clinical,operational_support,procedure_equipment_usage,malfunction_description,malfunction_description,Malfunction Description,STRING,,,,,association_data,Free-text description of the equipment malfunction or performance issue if equipment_malfunction_flag is true. Used for root cause analysis and FDA reporting.,
clinical,operational_support,procedure_equipment_usage,sterilization_lot_number,sterilization_lot_number,Sterilization Lot Number,STRING,,,,,association_data,Lot or batch number from the sterilization cycle that processed this equipment prior to use in this procedure. Critical for infection control tracking and sterile processing quality assurance.,
clinical,operational_support,procedure_equipment_usage,udi,udi,Unique Device Identifier,STRING,,,,,association_data,FDA-mandated Unique Device Identifier captured at the point of use during the procedure. Required for implant traceability and device event reporting. May duplicate equipment_asset.udi but captured here for point-of-use verification.,
clinical,operational_support,procedure_equipment_usage,usage_duration_minutes,usage_duration_minutes,Usage Duration Minutes,INT,,,,,association_data,Total elapsed time in minutes that the equipment was actively used during the procedure. Derived from usage_start_timestamp and usage_end_timestamp. Supports utilization rate calculations and capacity planning.,
clinical,operational_support,procedure_equipment_usage,usage_end_timestamp,usage_end_timestamp,Usage End Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,association_data,Date and time when the equipment usage concluded and the asset was released from the procedure. Used to calculate actual usage duration and equipment turnover time.,
clinical,operational_support,procedure_equipment_usage,usage_role,usage_role,Usage Role,STRING,,,,,association_data,"Role or function of the equipment during the procedure (primary, backup, standby, ancillary). Distinguishes between primary surgical equipment and supporting devices.",
clinical,operational_support,procedure_equipment_usage,usage_start_timestamp,usage_start_timestamp,Usage Start Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,association_data,Date and time when the equipment was deployed and began being used during the procedure. Critical for utilization tracking and equipment availability management.,
