clinical,patient_documentation,cdi_query,payer_id,payer_id,Payer ID,BIGINT,,insurance.payer.payer_id,,,transactional_data,"Reference to the primary payer for the encounter associated with this CDI query. Payer type (Medicare, Medicaid, commercial) determines applicable DRG grouper, reimbursement rates, and CDI program priority.",
clinical,patient_documentation,cdi_query,procedure_event_id,procedure_event_id,Procedure Event Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,clinical.procedure_event.procedure_event_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to clinical.procedure_event. Business justification: CDI queries can target procedure documentation to clarify procedural details, approach, or complications for accurate CPT/ICD-10-PCS coding. Linking cdi_query.procedure_event_id → procedure_event.proc",
clinical,patient_documentation,cdi_query,report_id,report_id,Radiology Report Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,radiology.report.report_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to radiology.report. Business justification: CDI specialists review radiology reports to identify undocumented diagnoses from incidental findings. Critical for DRG optimization, documentation improvement programs, and ensuring clinical documenta",
clinical,patient_documentation,cdi_query,visit_id,visit_id,Encounter ID,BIGINT,,encounter.visit.visit_id,,,transactional_data,Reference to the inpatient or outpatient encounter against which this CDI query was issued. Links the query to the clinical encounter for DRG assignment and reimbursement analysis.,
