clinical,patient_documentation,cdi_query,cc_mcc_status,cc_mcc_status,Complication or Comorbidity / Major Complication or Comorbidity (CC/MCC) Status,STRING,,,,CC|MCC|none|undetermined,transactional_data,Indicates whether the diagnosis associated with this CDI query qualifies as a Complication or Comorbidity (CC) or Major Complication or Comorbidity (MCC) under CMS DRG grouping rules. CC/MCC capture is a primary driver of DRG weight and reimbursement optimization.,
clinical,patient_documentation,cdi_query,claim_appeal_support_flag,claim_appeal_support_flag,Appeal Support Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,Indicates whether this CDI query was issued or retained specifically to support a payer denial appeal or Recovery Audit Contractor (RAC) audit response. Flags queries with dual-purpose CDI and denial management utility.,
clinical,patient_documentation,cdi_query,coding_impact_flag,coding_impact_flag,Coding Impact Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,Indicates whether the resolution of this CDI query resulted in a change to the coded diagnoses or procedures on the claim. True when the query outcome led to a coding modification. Used to measure CDI program effectiveness on coding accuracy.,
clinical,patient_documentation,cdi_query,compliance_review_flag,compliance_review_flag,Compliance Review Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,"Indicates whether this CDI query has been flagged for compliance review due to potential leading query language, inappropriate query format, or OIG audit risk. Supports CDI compliance program monitoring and AHIMA/ACDIS query format auditing.",
clinical,patient_documentation,cdi_query,concurrent_review_flag,concurrent_review_flag,Concurrent Review Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,"Indicates whether this CDI query was issued during a concurrent (real-time, while patient is still admitted) review as opposed to a retrospective review after discharge. Concurrent CDI is the preferred model for maximizing documentation accuracy and DRG optimization.",
clinical,patient_documentation,cdi_query,created_timestamp,created_timestamp,Record Created Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,Timestamp when this CDI query record was first created in the source system. Satisfies RECORD_AUDIT_CREATED category for TRANSACTION_HEADER role. Used for data lineage and audit trail.,
clinical,patient_documentation,cdi_query,documentation_gap_description,documentation_gap_description,Documentation Gap Description,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Narrative description of the specific clinical documentation deficiency or opportunity identified by the CDI specialist that prompted this query. Examples include missing specificity for a diagnosis, absent linkage between conditions, or undocumented clinical indicators.",
clinical,patient_documentation,cdi_query,drg_type,drg_type,Diagnosis-Related Group (DRG) Type,STRING,,,,MS-DRG|APR-DRG|AP-DRG,transactional_data,"Indicates the DRG classification system used for this encounter (Medicare Severity DRG, All Patient Refined DRG, or All Patient DRG). Determines the applicable grouper logic and reimbursement methodology.",
clinical,patient_documentation,cdi_query,encounter_type,encounter_type,Encounter Type,STRING,,,,inpatient|observation|outpatient|ED|surgical,transactional_data,Classification of the encounter type associated with this CDI query. CDI activity is most prevalent for inpatient encounters but may extend to observation and outpatient surgical cases. Drives applicable DRG grouper and reimbursement rules.,
clinical,patient_documentation,cdi_query,expected_drg_code,expected_drg_code,Expected Diagnosis-Related Group (DRG) Code,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,The DRG code anticipated if the provider responds affirmatively and documentation is improved per the CDI query. Used to calculate expected DRG impact and projected reimbursement change.,
clinical,patient_documentation,cdi_query,expected_drg_description,expected_drg_description,Expected Diagnosis-Related Group (DRG) Description,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,Human-readable description of the expected DRG if the CDI query results in documentation improvement. Supports revenue impact analysis and CDI program ROI reporting.,
clinical,patient_documentation,cdi_query,expected_reimbursement_impact,expected_reimbursement_impact,Expected Reimbursement Impact Amount,"DECIMAL(15,2)",,,dbx_confidential,,transactional_data,Projected change in reimbursement (in USD) if the CDI query results in a DRG change. Calculated as the difference between the expected DRG payment weight and the working DRG payment weight multiplied by the applicable base rate. Satisfies MONETARY_TRIPLET / QUANTITATIVE_RESULT category for TRANSACTION_HEADER role. Critical for CDI program ROI and revenue integrity reporting.,
clinical,patient_documentation,cdi_query,final_drg_code,final_drg_code,Final Diagnosis-Related Group (DRG) Code,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,The DRG code actually assigned to the encounter after the CDI query was resolved and coding was finalized. Used to measure actual DRG change rate and realized revenue impact versus expected.,
clinical,patient_documentation,cdi_query,physician_query_method,physician_query_method,Physician Query Delivery Method,STRING,,,,electronic|verbal|written|secure_message,transactional_data,"Method by which the CDI query was delivered to the provider (electronic via EHR, verbal, written paper form, or secure message). Affects response rate tracking and compliance with AHIMA/ACDIS query format guidelines.",
clinical,patient_documentation,cdi_query,poa_indicator,poa_indicator,Present on Admission (POA) Indicator,STRING,,,,Y|N|U|W|1,transactional_data,"Indicates whether the diagnosis associated with this CDI query was present at the time of inpatient admission. POA status affects CC/MCC eligibility, HAI reporting, and value-based purchasing penalties. Standard CMS POA indicator values: Y=Yes, N=No, U=Unknown, W=Clinically undetermined, 1=Unreported/not used.",
clinical,patient_documentation,cdi_query,provider_response_text,provider_response_text,Provider Response Text,STRING,,,dbx_confidential,,transactional_data,Free-text or structured response provided by the queried physician or provider. Captures the clinical clarification or documentation addendum. Classified as confidential due to clinical content.,
clinical,patient_documentation,cdi_query,query_category,query_category,CDI Query Category,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Clinical category or topic area of the query (e.g., principal diagnosis clarification, secondary diagnosis specificity, procedure clarification, POA status, CC/MCC capture, clinical validity). Used for trend analysis and CDI program focus areas. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: principal_diagnosis|secondary_diagnosis|procedure|poa_status|cc_mcc_capture|clinical_validity|discharge_disposition|severity_of_illness — promote to reference product]",
clinical,patient_documentation,cdi_query,query_expiration_date,query_expiration_date,CDI Query Expiration Date,DATE,,,,,transactional_data,Date by which the provider must respond before the query is automatically expired per CDI program policy. Drives escalation workflows and expired query reporting.,
clinical,patient_documentation,cdi_query,query_issue_date,query_issue_date,CDI Query Issue Date,DATE,,,,,transactional_data,Calendar date on which the CDI query was formally issued to the provider. Satisfies BUSINESS_EVENT_TIMESTAMP category for TRANSACTION_HEADER role. Used to calculate response turnaround time and query aging.,
clinical,patient_documentation,cdi_query,query_number,query_number,CDI Query Number,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Externally-known alphanumeric identifier for the CDI query, as assigned by the source system (3M CDI or Epic CDI). Used for cross-system reference, audit trails, and provider communication. Satisfies BUSINESS_IDENTIFIER category for TRANSACTION_HEADER role.",
clinical,patient_documentation,cdi_query,query_opportunity_flag,query_opportunity_flag,CDI Query Opportunity Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,Indicates whether the CDI review identified a query opportunity for this encounter. True when a documentation gap with potential DRG or quality impact was identified. Used to calculate query opportunity rates and CDI program reach.,
clinical,patient_documentation,cdi_query,query_outcome,query_outcome,CDI Query Outcome,STRING,,,,agreed|disagreed|no_impact|unable_to_determine|withdrawn,transactional_data,"Final disposition of the CDI query after provider response. Indicates whether the provider agreed with the CDI specialists suggested documentation change, disagreed, or the query had no DRG impact. Drives DRG change rate and revenue impact reporting.",
clinical,patient_documentation,cdi_query,query_response_date,query_response_date,CDI Query Response Date,DATE,,,,,transactional_data,"Date on which the queried provider responded to the CDI query. Null if the query is still open, expired, or withdrawn. Used to calculate response turnaround time and provider response rate metrics.",
clinical,patient_documentation,cdi_query,query_status,query_status,CDI Query Status,STRING,,,,open|answered|expired|withdrawn|pending_review,transactional_data,"Current lifecycle state of the CDI query. Drives workflow routing, response rate calculations, and CDI program performance dashboards. Satisfies LIFECYCLE_STATUS category for TRANSACTION_HEADER role.",
clinical,patient_documentation,cdi_query,query_text,query_text,CDI Query Text,STRING,,,dbx_confidential,,transactional_data,Cleaned boilerplate phrase from attribute description,
clinical,patient_documentation,cdi_query,query_type,query_type,CDI Query Type,STRING,,,,compliant|leading|multiple_choice|yes_no|open_ended,transactional_data,Classification of the query format per ACDIS/AHIMA compliant query guidelines. Compliant queries are non-leading and clinically supported. Leading queries may introduce compliance risk. Multiple choice and yes/no formats are common structured query types. Critical for compliance auditing and OIG risk management.,
clinical,patient_documentation,cdi_query,response_turnaround_hours,response_turnaround_hours,Query Response Turnaround Hours,INT,,,,,transactional_data,"Number of hours elapsed between query issuance and provider response. Used to measure CDI program efficiency, provider engagement, and compliance with internal SLA targets for query response time.",
clinical,patient_documentation,cdi_query,retrospective_review_flag,retrospective_review_flag,Retrospective Review Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,Indicates whether this CDI query was issued during a retrospective review after the patient was discharged. Retrospective queries may have limited impact on DRG assignment if coding is already finalized but are used for denial management and appeal support.,
clinical,patient_documentation,cdi_query,risk_of_mortality_level,risk_of_mortality_level,Risk of Mortality (ROM) Level,STRING,,,,1|2|3|4,transactional_data,"APR-DRG risk of mortality subclass for the encounter at the time of CDI query issuance (1=Minor, 2=Moderate, 3=Major, 4=Extreme). Supports quality reporting, mortality review, and CDI program impact on risk-adjusted outcomes.",
clinical,patient_documentation,cdi_query,severity_of_illness_level,severity_of_illness_level,Severity of Illness (SOI) Level,STRING,,,,1|2|3|4,transactional_data,"APR-DRG severity of illness subclass for the encounter at the time of CDI query issuance (1=Minor, 2=Moderate, 3=Major, 4=Extreme). Used in APR-DRG environments to assess documentation completeness and CDI opportunity.",
clinical,patient_documentation,cdi_query,source_system,source_system,Source System,STRING,,,,3M_CDI|Epic_CDI|Cerner_CDI|MEDITECH_CDI,transactional_data,"Identifies the operational system of record from which this CDI query record was sourced (e.g., 3M Health Information Systems CDI module, Epic CDI workflows). Supports data lineage, ETL reconciliation, and multi-system CDI program integration.",
clinical,patient_documentation,cdi_query,source_system_query_code,source_system_query_code,Source System Query ID,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Native identifier of this CDI query record in the originating source system (3M CDI or Epic CDI). Enables cross-system reconciliation, ETL traceability, and support case resolution without exposing internal surrogate keys.",
clinical,patient_documentation,cdi_query,updated_timestamp,updated_timestamp,Record Updated Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,Timestamp when this CDI query record was last modified in the source system. Satisfies RECORD_AUDIT_UPDATED category for TRANSACTION_HEADER role. Used for incremental ETL processing and change tracking.,
clinical,patient_documentation,cdi_worksheet,cdi_worksheet_id,cdi_worksheet_id,Clinical Documentation Improvement (CDI) Worksheet ID,BIGINT,Y,,,,transactional_data,Unique surrogate identifier for the CDI specialist review worksheet record in the Silver layer lakehouse.,
clinical,patient_documentation,cdi_worksheet,care_site_id,care_site_id,Facility ID,BIGINT,,facility.care_site.care_site_id,,,transactional_data,Reference to the hospital or care facility where the encounter under CDI review occurred. Supports multi-facility CDI program performance benchmarking.,
clinical,patient_documentation,cdi_worksheet,claim_id,claim_id,Claim Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,claim.claim.claim_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to claim.claim. Business justification: CDI worksheets document clinical review findings that determine final claim coding and DRG. Revenue cycle operations require linking worksheet to claim for audit trail, coding validation, and measurin",
clinical,patient_documentation,cdi_worksheet,clinician_id,clinician_id,Attending Provider ID,BIGINT,,provider.clinician.clinician_id,,,transactional_data,Reference to the attending physician responsible for the encounter being reviewed. Used to route physician queries and track query response rates by provider.,
clinical,patient_documentation,cdi_worksheet,compliance_audit_id,compliance_audit_id,Compliance Audit Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,compliance.audit.audit_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to compliance.audit. Business justification: DRG validation audits and clinical documentation improvement program reviews examine CDI worksheets for compliance with CMS coding guidelines. Compliance teams audit CDI worksheet accuracy, completene",
clinical,patient_documentation,cdi_worksheet,compliance_program_id,compliance_program_id,CDI Program ID,BIGINT,,compliance.compliance_program.compliance_program_id,,,transactional_data,"Reference to the CDI program or initiative under which this worksheet was generated (e.g., inpatient CDI program, outpatient CDI program, HAC-focused program). Supports program-level performance tracking.",
clinical,patient_documentation,cdi_worksheet,drg_id,drg_id,Working Drg Code Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,reference.drg.drg_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to reference.drg. Business justification: CDI worksheet working DRG tracking for concurrent review and documentation opportunity identification. CDI specialists use working DRG attributes (relative weight, GMLOS, complication level) to assess",
clinical,patient_documentation,cdi_worksheet,employee_id,employee_id,Clinical Documentation Improvement (CDI) Specialist ID,BIGINT,,workforce.employee.employee_id,"dbx_confidential, dbx_pii",,transactional_data,Reference to the CDI specialist who performed the documentation review. Used for workload tracking and performance reporting.,
clinical,patient_documentation,cdi_worksheet,icd_code_id,icd_code_id,Principal Diagnosis Code Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,reference.icd_code.icd_code_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to reference.icd_code. Business justification: Principal diagnosis validation for DRG grouping accuracy and coding compliance. CDI specialists use ICD-10 code attributes (unacceptable principal DX flag, MDC assignment) to ensure principal diagnosi",
clinical,patient_documentation,cdi_worksheet,invoice_id,invoice_id,Invoice Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,billing.invoice.invoice_id,,,transactional_data,Foreign key linking to billing.invoice. Business justification: CDI worksheets document DRG determination and expected reimbursement for specific encounters. Revenue cycle operations require linking worksheets to invoices to reconcile expected vs. actual reimburse,
clinical,patient_documentation,cdi_worksheet,mpi_record_id,mpi_record_id,Patient ID,BIGINT,,patient.mpi_record.mpi_record_id,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_identifier",,transactional_data,Reference to the patient whose encounter is under CDI review. Protected Health Information (PHI) per HIPAA.,
clinical,patient_documentation,cdi_worksheet,visit_id,visit_id,Encounter ID,BIGINT,,encounter.visit.visit_id,,,transactional_data,Reference to the inpatient or outpatient encounter under CDI review. Links the worksheet to the clinical encounter record.,
clinical,patient_documentation,cdi_worksheet,admit_date,admit_date,Admission Date,DATE,,,,,transactional_data,The date the patient was admitted for the encounter under CDI review. Used to calculate Length of Stay (LOS) at time of review and to sequence concurrent CDI reviews.,
clinical,patient_documentation,cdi_worksheet,cc_mcc_captured,cc_mcc_captured,CC/MCC Captured Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,"Indicates whether the CDI review successfully captured a CC or MCC that was not previously documented, resulting in a DRG upgrade. Key metric for CDI program performance reporting.",
clinical,patient_documentation,cdi_worksheet,cc_mcc_status,cc_mcc_status,Complication or Comorbidity / Major Complication or Comorbidity (CC/MCC) Status,STRING,,,,none|CC|MCC,transactional_data,"Indicates whether the encounter has a captured Complication or Comorbidity (CC) or Major Complication or Comorbidity (MCC) that affects DRG assignment and reimbursement. Values: none (no CC/MCC), CC (complication or comorbidity present), MCC (major complication or comorbidity present).",
clinical,patient_documentation,cdi_worksheet,completed_timestamp,completed_timestamp,Review Completed Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,The date and time when the CDI specialist marked the worksheet review as completed. Distinct from created and updated timestamps; used to measure CDI review cycle time and productivity.,
clinical,patient_documentation,cdi_worksheet,created_timestamp,created_timestamp,Record Created Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,The date and time when the CDI worksheet record was first created in the source system. Used for audit trail and data lineage tracking per HIPAA and HITRUST requirements.,
clinical,patient_documentation,cdi_worksheet,discharge_date,discharge_date,Discharge Date,DATE,,,,,transactional_data,The date the patient was discharged from the encounter. Populated for post-discharge CDI reviews; null for concurrent reviews on active encounters.,
clinical,patient_documentation,cdi_worksheet,documentation_gap_count,documentation_gap_count,Documentation Gap Count,INT,,,,,transactional_data,"Number of distinct clinical documentation gaps identified during the CDI review (e.g., unspecified diagnoses, missing severity qualifiers, undocumented comorbidities). Supports CDI program gap analysis.",
clinical,patient_documentation,cdi_worksheet,documentation_gap_notes,documentation_gap_notes,Documentation Gap Notes,STRING,,,dbx_confidential,,transactional_data,Free-text narrative describing the specific clinical documentation gaps identified by the CDI specialist during review. Supports CDI education and physician feedback programs. Treated as confidential clinical operational data.,
clinical,patient_documentation,cdi_worksheet,drg_grouper_version,drg_grouper_version,DRG Grouper Version,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Version identifier of the DRG grouper software (e.g., CMS MS-DRG v41.0 or 3M APR-DRG v39) used to assign working and final DRG codes. Required for audit reproducibility.",
clinical,patient_documentation,cdi_worksheet,drg_weight_change,drg_weight_change,DRG Relative Weight Change,"DECIMAL(8,4)",,,,,transactional_data,The arithmetic difference between the final DRG relative weight and the working DRG relative weight (final minus working). Positive values indicate a CDI-driven DRG upgrade; negative values indicate a downgrade. Key CDI program performance metric.,
clinical,patient_documentation,cdi_worksheet,encounter_type,encounter_type,Encounter Type,STRING,,,,inpatient|observation|outpatient|ED|surgical,transactional_data,"Classification of the clinical encounter under review (e.g., inpatient admission, observation stay, outpatient, Emergency Department (ED), surgical). Determines applicable DRG grouping methodology.",
clinical,patient_documentation,cdi_worksheet,expected_reimbursement_impact,expected_reimbursement_impact,Expected Reimbursement Impact (USD),"DECIMAL(12,2)",,,dbx_confidential,,transactional_data,"Estimated dollar impact on Medicare/Medicaid reimbursement resulting from the DRG change driven by CDI review, calculated as the DRG weight change multiplied by the facilitys base payment rate. Supports Revenue Cycle Management (RCM) and revenue integrity reporting.",
clinical,patient_documentation,cdi_worksheet,facility_service_line,facility_service_line,Clinical Service Line,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"The clinical service line or specialty associated with the encounter (e.g., Cardiology, Orthopedics, Neurology, General Medicine). Used to segment CDI performance by clinical program.",
clinical,patient_documentation,cdi_worksheet,final_drg_code,final_drg_code,Final Diagnosis-Related Group (DRG) Code,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,The DRG code assigned after CDI specialist review and any physician query responses have been incorporated. Represents the post-CDI reimbursement outcome.,
clinical,patient_documentation,cdi_worksheet,final_drg_description,final_drg_description,Final Diagnosis-Related Group (DRG) Description,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Human-readable description of the final DRG code after CDI review completion, providing clinical context for the post-CDI grouping.",
clinical,patient_documentation,cdi_worksheet,final_drg_weight,final_drg_weight,Final Diagnosis-Related Group (DRG) Relative Weight,"DECIMAL(8,4)",,,,,transactional_data,The CMS-published relative weight associated with the final DRG after CDI review. Compared against working DRG weight to quantify CDI program impact on Case Mix Index (CMI).,
clinical,patient_documentation,cdi_worksheet,hac_risk_flag,hac_risk_flag,Hospital-Acquired Condition (HAC) Risk Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,Indicates whether the CDI review identified a potential Hospital-Acquired Condition (HAC) that could affect DRG payment under CMS HAC Reduction Program. Triggers compliance review workflow.,
clinical,patient_documentation,cdi_worksheet,los_at_review,los_at_review,Length of Stay (LOS) at Review (Days),INT,,,,,transactional_data,Number of inpatient days elapsed from admission to the CDI review date. Used to assess timeliness of CDI intervention relative to the encounter Length of Stay (LOS).,
clinical,patient_documentation,cdi_worksheet,mdc_code,mdc_code,Major Diagnostic Category (MDC) Code,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"The CMS Major Diagnostic Category (MDC) code derived from the principal diagnosis, representing the broad clinical grouping used in DRG assignment (e.g., MDC 05 — Diseases of the Circulatory System).",
clinical,patient_documentation,cdi_worksheet,mrn,mrn,Medical Record Number (MRN),STRING,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_identifier",,transactional_data,"The facility-assigned Medical Record Number (MRN) for the patient, used to cross-reference the CDI worksheet with the Electronic Health Record (EHR). PHI per HIPAA.",
clinical,patient_documentation,cdi_worksheet,payer_type,payer_type,Payer Type,STRING,,,,Medicare|Medicaid|commercial|self_pay|other,transactional_data,"Classification of the primary payer for the encounter under CDI review. Determines applicable DRG grouper, reimbursement methodology, and regulatory reporting requirements.",
clinical,patient_documentation,cdi_worksheet,poa_status,poa_status,Present on Admission (POA) Status,STRING,,,,Y|N|U|W|1,transactional_data,"Present on Admission (POA) indicator for the principal diagnosis as assessed during CDI review. Values follow CMS POA guidelines: Y=present on admission, N=not present, U=unknown, W=clinically undetermined, 1=exempt from POA reporting.",
clinical,patient_documentation,cdi_worksheet,query_count,query_count,Physician Query Count,INT,,,,,transactional_data,Total number of physician queries generated from this CDI worksheet review. Used to measure CDI specialist productivity and query volume per encounter.,
clinical,patient_documentation,cdi_worksheet,query_opportunity_flag,query_opportunity_flag,Physician Query Opportunity Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,"Indicates whether the CDI specialist identified a documentation gap that warrants a physician query to clarify, add, or amend a diagnosis or procedure. Drives query workflow initiation.",
clinical,patient_documentation,cdi_worksheet,query_response_status,query_response_status,Physician Query Response Status,STRING,,,,not_applicable|pending|agreed|disagreed|unable_to_determine,transactional_data,"Aggregate status of physician query responses for this worksheet: not_applicable (no query issued), pending (awaiting response), agreed (physician confirmed CDI suggestion), disagreed (physician declined), unable_to_determine (physician could not clarify).",
clinical,patient_documentation,cdi_worksheet,review_date,review_date,CDI Review Date,DATE,,,,,transactional_data,The calendar date on which the CDI specialist performed the documentation review for the encounter. Principal business event date for the worksheet.,
clinical,patient_documentation,cdi_worksheet,review_notes,review_notes,CDI Review Notes,STRING,,,dbx_confidential,,transactional_data,"Free-text clinical notes entered by the CDI specialist summarizing review findings, clinical reasoning, and recommended documentation improvements. Confidential clinical operational data used for CDI education and physician engagement.",
clinical,patient_documentation,cdi_worksheet,review_outcome,review_outcome,CDI Review Outcome,STRING,,,,no_change|drg_upgrade|drg_downgrade|cc_mcc_added|principal_dx_changed,transactional_data,"The clinical and financial outcome of the CDI review: no_change (documentation adequate), drg_upgrade (DRG moved to higher weight), drg_downgrade (DRG moved to lower weight), cc_mcc_added (CC or MCC captured), principal_dx_changed (principal diagnosis revised). [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: no_change|drg_upgrade|drg_downgrade|cc_mcc_added|principal_dx_changed|query_pending — promote to reference product]",
clinical,patient_documentation,cdi_worksheet,review_status,review_status,CDI Review Status,STRING,,,,open|in_progress|pending_query|completed|cancelled,transactional_data,"Current lifecycle state of the CDI worksheet: open (assigned, not started), in_progress (review underway), pending_query (awaiting physician query response), completed (review finalized), or cancelled.",
clinical,patient_documentation,cdi_worksheet,review_timestamp,review_timestamp,CDI Review Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,"Precise date and time when the CDI specialist initiated or completed the review session, used for audit trail and productivity measurement.",
clinical,patient_documentation,cdi_worksheet,review_type,review_type,CDI Review Type,STRING,,,,initial|concurrent|follow_up|final|post_discharge,transactional_data,"Classifies the stage of the CDI review cycle: initial (first review on admission), concurrent (ongoing during stay), follow_up (subsequent concurrent review), final (pre-discharge), or post_discharge (retrospective). Drives workflow routing in 3M CDI.",
clinical,patient_documentation,cdi_worksheet,source_system_worksheet_code,source_system_worksheet_code,Source System Worksheet ID,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"The native worksheet identifier assigned by the 3M Health Information Systems CDI source system. Preserved for data lineage, reconciliation, and audit trail back to the operational system of record.",
clinical,patient_documentation,cdi_worksheet,updated_timestamp,updated_timestamp,Record Updated Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,The date and time when the CDI worksheet record was last modified in the source system. Supports incremental ETL processing and change data capture in the Databricks Silver layer.,
clinical,patient_documentation,cdi_worksheet,worksheet_number,worksheet_number,CDI Worksheet Number,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,Externally visible alphanumeric identifier assigned to the CDI worksheet by the 3M Health Information Systems CDI module. Used for cross-referencing with source system records.,
clinical,patient_documentation,clinical_finding,clinical_finding_id,clinical_finding_id,Clinical Finding ID,BIGINT,Y,,,,transactional_data,Unique surrogate identifier for the clinical finding record in the lakehouse silver layer.,
clinical,patient_documentation,clinical_finding,care_site_id,care_site_id,Facility ID,BIGINT,,facility.care_site.care_site_id,,,transactional_data,Reference to the facility or care location where this clinical finding was documented.,
clinical,patient_documentation,clinical_finding,clinician_id,clinician_id,Documenting Provider ID,BIGINT,,provider.clinician.clinician_id,,,transactional_data,Reference to the clinician who documented or recorded this clinical finding.,
clinical,patient_documentation,clinical_finding,consent_record_id,consent_record_id,Consent Record Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,consent.consent_consent_record.consent_record_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to consent.consent_record. Business justification: Clinical findings (genetic, behavioral health, SDOH) may require consent for documentation or disclosure. Sensitive findings trigger consent verification workflows to ensure appropriate information sh",
clinical,patient_documentation,clinical_finding,demographics_id,demographics_id,Patient ID,BIGINT,,patient.demographics.demographics_id,,,transactional_data,Reference to the patient for whom this clinical finding was documented.,
clinical,patient_documentation,clinical_finding,fhir_observation_id,fhir_observation_id,FHIR (Fast Healthcare Interoperability Resources) Observation ID,BIGINT,,clinical.observation.observation_id,,,transactional_data,"FHIR Observation resource identifier assigned during FHIR-based clinical data exchange, enabling semantic interoperability with external Health Information Exchange (HIE) partners and APIs.",
clinical,patient_documentation,clinical_finding,genomic_test_result_id,genomic_test_result_id,Genomic Test Result Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,genomics.genomic_test_result.genomic_test_result_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to genomics.genomic_test_result. Business justification: Clinical findings (e.g., pharmacogenomic drug sensitivity, hereditary risk) may be directly evidenced by genomic test results. Supports pharmacogenomics-driven clinical documentation and CDS alerts.",Internal - LLM Generated Cross-Domain Link
clinical,patient_documentation,clinical_finding,laboratory_test_result_id,laboratory_test_result_id,Source Test Result Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,laboratory.laboratory_test_result.laboratory_test_result_id,,,transactional_data,Foreign key linking to laboratory.test_result. Business justification: Clinical findings often derived from/supported by lab results (finding=hyperkalemia sourced from test_result). Role prefix source_ indicates data origin. Removes denormalized lab value fields in f,
clinical,patient_documentation,clinical_finding,loinc_code_id,loinc_code_id,Loinc Code Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,reference.loinc_code.loinc_code_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to reference.loinc_code. Business justification: Finding observation type classification for result interpretation, reference range application, and interoperable data exchange. Clinical systems use LOINC codes to standardize finding observations fo",
clinical,patient_documentation,clinical_finding,note_id,note_id,Clinical Note ID,BIGINT,,clinical.note.note_id,,,transactional_data,"Reference to the clinical note from which this structured finding was extracted or with which it is associated, enabling traceability back to the source narrative documentation.",
clinical,patient_documentation,clinical_finding,quality_measure_id,quality_measure_id,Quality Measure Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,quality.measure.measure_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to quality.measure. Business justification: Clinical findings (depression diagnosis via PHQ-9, SDOH screening results) support quality measure numerator determination. Essential for automated quality measure calculation and clinical decision su",
clinical,patient_documentation,clinical_finding,snomed_concept_id,snomed_concept_id,Snomed Ct Code Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,reference.snomed_concept.snomed_concept_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to reference.snomed_concept. Business justification: Clinical finding standardization for structured documentation, clinical decision support, and quality measure calculation. SNOMED CT findings enable semantic reasoning for care pathways, risk stratifi",
clinical,patient_documentation,clinical_finding,visit_id,visit_id,Encounter ID,BIGINT,,encounter.visit.visit_id,,,transactional_data,Reference to the clinical encounter during which this finding was documented.,
clinical,patient_documentation,clinical_finding,body_site_code,body_site_code,Body Site SNOMED CT Code,STRING,,,,"^[0-9]{6,18}$",transactional_data,"SNOMED CT concept code identifying the anatomical body site to which this clinical finding applies (e.g., 368209003 for right arm). Enables structured anatomical documentation.",
clinical,patient_documentation,clinical_finding,body_site_description,body_site_description,Body Site Description,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Human-readable description of the anatomical body site corresponding to the body_site_code (e.g., Right arm, Left lower lobe of lung).",
clinical,patient_documentation,clinical_finding,care_setting,care_setting,Care Setting,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Specific care setting or unit where the finding was documented (e.g., Emergency Department (ED), Intensive Care Unit (ICU), Operating Room (OR), outpatient clinic). Supports operational and quality reporting segmentation. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: ED|ICU|OR|inpatient-ward|outpatient-clinic|telehealth|SNF|PACU|step-down — promote to reference product]",
clinical,patient_documentation,clinical_finding,cdi_query_flag,cdi_query_flag,Clinical Documentation Improvement (CDI) Query Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,"Indicates whether this clinical finding has triggered a Clinical Documentation Improvement (CDI) query to the provider for clarification or additional specificity, supporting accurate coding and reimbursement.",
clinical,patient_documentation,clinical_finding,chronic_finding_flag,chronic_finding_flag,Chronic Finding Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,Indicates whether this clinical finding represents a chronic or persistent condition rather than an acute or transient observation. Supports population health management and chronic disease registries.,
clinical,patient_documentation,clinical_finding,confidentiality_level,confidentiality_level,Confidentiality Level,STRING,,,,normal|restricted|very-restricted,transactional_data,"Confidentiality classification of this clinical finding per HIPAA and organizational policy. Restricted findings (e.g., behavioral health, substance use, HIV) require additional access controls beyond standard Protected Health Information (PHI) protections.",
clinical,patient_documentation,clinical_finding,consent_verification_status,consent_verification_status,Verification Status,STRING,,,,confirmed|provisional|refuted|entered-in-error,transactional_data,Clinical verification status indicating the degree of certainty or confirmation of the finding by the documenting provider.,
clinical,patient_documentation,clinical_finding,documentation_date,documentation_date,Documentation Date,DATE,,,,,transactional_data,Calendar date on which the clinical finding was documented by the provider in the Electronic Health Record (EHR). Used for longitudinal clinical tracking and quality measure date attribution.,
clinical,patient_documentation,clinical_finding,encounter_type,encounter_type,Encounter Type,STRING,,,,inpatient|outpatient|emergency|observation|telehealth,transactional_data,"Type of clinical encounter during which this finding was documented (e.g., inpatient, outpatient, emergency department). Supports care setting stratification in analytics.",
clinical,patient_documentation,clinical_finding,finding_category,finding_category,Clinical Finding Category,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,High-level category classifying the type of clinical finding. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: exam|symptom|history|functional|laboratory|imaging|social|vital-sign|assessment — promote to reference product],
clinical,patient_documentation,clinical_finding,finding_comment,finding_comment,Clinical Finding Comment,STRING,,,dbx_confidential,,transactional_data,Free-text narrative comment or clinical note addendum provided by the documenting provider to further qualify or contextualize the finding beyond structured coded fields.,
clinical,patient_documentation,clinical_finding,finding_status,finding_status,Clinical Finding Status,STRING,,,,present|absent|unknown|indeterminate|not-assessed,transactional_data,"Clinical assertion status indicating whether the finding is present, absent, unknown, indeterminate, or not assessed for this patient at this encounter. Core semantic qualifier per SNOMED CT post-coordination.",
clinical,patient_documentation,clinical_finding,interpretation_code,interpretation_code,Interpretation Code,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Standardized interpretation flag for the finding value relative to reference ranges (e.g., N=Normal, H=High, L=Low, HH=Critical High, LL=Critical Low, POS=Positive, NEG=Negative, IND=Indeterminate). Aligns with HL7 v2 OBX-8. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: N|A|H|L|HH|LL|POS|NEG|IND — 9 candidates stripped; promote to reference product]",
clinical,patient_documentation,clinical_finding,last_updated_timestamp,last_updated_timestamp,Last Updated Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,Date and time when the clinical finding record was most recently modified or updated in the source system.,
clinical,patient_documentation,clinical_finding,laterality,laterality,Laterality,STRING,,,,left|right|bilateral|unspecified,transactional_data,"Laterality qualifier indicating which side of the body the finding applies to (left, right, bilateral, or unspecified). Used in conjunction with body site for precise anatomical documentation.",
clinical,patient_documentation,clinical_finding,mrn,mrn,Medical Record Number (MRN),STRING,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_identifier",,transactional_data,"Medical Record Number (MRN) of the patient associated with this finding, as assigned by the facility Master Patient Index (MPI). Retained for operational cross-referencing.",
clinical,patient_documentation,clinical_finding,onset_date,onset_date,Finding Onset Date,DATE,,,,,transactional_data,"Date on which the clinical finding first appeared or was first observed, as reported by the patient or clinician. Distinct from documentation date; supports longitudinal clinical analysis.",
clinical,patient_documentation,clinical_finding,present_on_admission,present_on_admission,Present on Admission (POA) Indicator,STRING,,,,Y|N|U|W,transactional_data,"Present on Admission (POA) indicator for inpatient findings, per CMS reporting requirements. Y=Yes (present at admission), N=No (developed after admission), U=Unknown, W=Clinically undetermined. Impacts Hospital-Acquired Condition (HAC) reporting.",
clinical,patient_documentation,clinical_finding,quality_measure_flag,quality_measure_flag,Quality Measure Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,"Indicates whether this clinical finding is relevant to one or more clinical quality measures (e.g., HEDIS, CMS MIPS, Joint Commission Core Measures). Supports quality reporting workflows.",
clinical,patient_documentation,clinical_finding,recorded_timestamp,recorded_timestamp,Recorded Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,Date and time when the clinical finding was first entered into the Electronic Health Record (EHR) system. Represents the business event timestamp of initial documentation.,
clinical,patient_documentation,clinical_finding,resolution_date,resolution_date,Finding Resolution Date,DATE,,,,,transactional_data,"Date on which the clinical finding resolved or was no longer present, as documented by the provider. Null if the finding is ongoing or chronic.",
clinical,patient_documentation,clinical_finding,sdoh_flag,sdoh_flag,Social Determinants of Health (SDOH) Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,"Indicates whether this clinical finding is related to Social Determinants of Health (SDOH), such as food insecurity, housing instability, or transportation barriers. Supports population health and care management programs.",
clinical,patient_documentation,clinical_finding,sensitive_finding_type,sensitive_finding_type,Sensitive Finding Type,STRING,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_health",behavioral-health|substance-use|HIV|sexual-health|genetic|none,transactional_data,"Classifies the finding as belonging to a sensitive clinical category subject to heightened privacy protections beyond standard HIPAA PHI rules (e.g., behavioral health, substance use disorder per 42 CFR Part 2, HIV status, sexual health, genetic information). none indicates no special sensitivity.",
clinical,patient_documentation,clinical_finding,severity,severity,Finding Severity,STRING,,,,mild|moderate|severe|life-threatening,transactional_data,"Clinical severity grade of the finding as documented by the provider (e.g., mild, moderate, severe, life-threatening). Supports clinical decision support and quality reporting.",
clinical,patient_documentation,clinical_finding,source_system,source_system,Source System,STRING,,,,Epic|Cerner|MEDITECH|Manual,transactional_data,"Operational system of record from which this clinical finding was sourced (e.g., Epic ClinDoc, Cerner PowerChart).",
clinical,patient_documentation,clinical_finding,source_system_finding_code,source_system_finding_code,Source System Finding ID,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Native identifier of this clinical finding in the originating operational system (Epic or Cerner internal ID), used for lineage and reconciliation.",
clinical,patient_documentation,clinical_finding,specialty,specialty,Documenting Provider Specialty,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Clinical specialty of the provider who documented the finding (e.g., Cardiology, Internal Medicine, Emergency Medicine). Supports specialty-specific analytics and quality reporting.",
clinical,patient_documentation,clinical_finding,title,title,Clinical Finding Title,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Short, human-readable title or label for the clinical finding as displayed in the Electronic Health Record (EHR) interface (e.g., Peripheral edema, Breath sounds diminished).",
clinical,patient_documentation,clinical_finding,value_code,value_code,Finding Value Code,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Coded value for the finding when the result is expressed as a coded concept rather than a numeric quantity (e.g., a SNOMED CT code for positive, negative, or a specific coded finding result).",
clinical,patient_documentation,clinical_finding,value_string,value_string,Finding Value String,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Free-text string value for the finding when the result cannot be expressed as a numeric quantity or coded concept (e.g., Grade II/VI systolic murmur, Coarse breath sounds bilaterally).",
clinical,patient_documentation,diagnosis,diagnosis_id,diagnosis_id,Clinical Diagnosis ID,BIGINT,Y,," dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_health",,transactional_data,Unique surrogate identifier for each clinical diagnosis record in the system. Primary key for the clinical_diagnosis data product.,
clinical,patient_documentation,diagnosis,care_site_id,care_site_id,Facility ID,BIGINT,,facility.care_site.care_site_id,,,transactional_data,"Reference to the healthcare facility (hospital, clinic, outpatient center) where this diagnosis was documented. Supports multi-facility enterprise reporting, facility-level quality benchmarking, and regulatory submissions.",
clinical,patient_documentation,diagnosis,clinical_order_id,clinical_order_id,Diagnosis Clinical Order Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,order.clinical_order.clinical_order_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to order.clinical_order. Business justification: Diagnoses drive clinical order placement in real workflows. Clinician diagnoses pneumonia, orders chest X-ray and antibiotics. Essential for order appropriateness review, clinical decision support val",
clinical,patient_documentation,diagnosis,clinician_id,clinician_id,Diagnosing Provider ID,BIGINT,,provider.clinician.clinician_id,,,transactional_data,"Reference to the licensed clinician (physician, NP, PA) who documented or confirmed this diagnosis. Used for provider attribution, quality reporting, and CDI workflows.",
clinical,patient_documentation,diagnosis,demographics_id,demographics_id,Patient ID,BIGINT,,patient.demographics.demographics_id,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_health",,transactional_data,Reference to the patient for whom this diagnosis was documented. Links to the patient master record in the Master Patient Index (MPI).,
clinical,patient_documentation,diagnosis,employee_id,employee_id,Coded By User ID,BIGINT,,workforce.employee.employee_id,"dbx_confidential, dbx_pii",,transactional_data,"Reference to the HIM coder or CDI specialist who assigned or finalized the ICD-10-CM code for this diagnosis. Supports coder productivity reporting, quality audits, and RAC audit defense.",
clinical,patient_documentation,diagnosis,icd_code_id,icd_code_id,Icd10 Code Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,reference.icd_code.icd_code_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to reference.icd_code. Business justification: Diagnosis coding validation, DRG grouping, quality measure reporting, and CMS submission require authoritative ICD-10 code reference. Clinical coders validate diagnosis codes against reference tables ",
clinical,patient_documentation,diagnosis,mpi_record_id,mpi_record_id,,BIGINT,,patient.mpi_record.mpi_record_id,,,transactional_data,FK to patient.mpi_record.mpi_record_id,
clinical,patient_documentation,diagnosis,snomed_concept_id,snomed_concept_id,Snomed Code Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,reference.snomed_concept.snomed_concept_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to reference.snomed_concept. Business justification: Clinical terminology standardization for EHR interoperability, clinical decision support rules, and quality measure calculation. SNOMED CT is the required standard for USCDI and enables semantic inter",
clinical,patient_documentation,diagnosis,visit_id,visit_id,Encounter ID,BIGINT,,encounter.visit.visit_id,,,transactional_data,"Reference to the clinical encounter (visit, admission, or outpatient episode) during which this diagnosis was documented or confirmed. Supports encounter-level DRG assignment and billing.",
clinical,patient_documentation,diagnosis,admit_diagnosis_flag,admit_diagnosis_flag,Admitting Diagnosis Flag,BOOLEAN,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_health",,transactional_data,Indicates whether this diagnosis was the stated reason for inpatient admission as documented at the time of admission. The admitting diagnosis may differ from the principal discharge diagnosis and is required on UB-04 claim form field 69.,
clinical,patient_documentation,diagnosis,care_setting,care_setting,Care Setting,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"The clinical care setting in which this diagnosis was documented (e.g., ICU, ED, OR, ambulatory clinic). Supports care-setting-specific quality reporting, resource utilization analysis, and population health stratification. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: inpatient|outpatient|ED|ICU|OR|ambulatory|telehealth — promote to reference product]",
clinical,patient_documentation,diagnosis,cdi_query_flag,cdi_query_flag,Clinical Documentation Improvement (CDI) Query Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,Indicates whether a CDI specialist has issued a physician query related to this diagnosis for clarification or specificity improvement. Supports CDI workflow tracking and documentation quality metrics.,
clinical,patient_documentation,diagnosis,cdi_query_status,cdi_query_status,Clinical Documentation Improvement (CDI) Query Status,STRING,,,,pending|agreed|disagreed|no_response|withdrawn,transactional_data,Current status of the CDI physician query associated with this diagnosis. Tracks whether the provider has responded and whether the diagnosis was amended based on the query outcome.,
clinical,patient_documentation,diagnosis,chronic_condition_flag,chronic_condition_flag,Chronic Condition Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,"Indicates whether this diagnosis represents a chronic condition as defined by CMS Chronic Condition Warehouse (CCW) criteria. Used for population health management, HEDIS measure attribution, and ACO quality reporting.",
clinical,patient_documentation,diagnosis,clinical_status,clinical_status,Clinical Status,STRING,,,,active|resolved|inactive|recurrence|remission|unknown,transactional_data,Current clinical state of the diagnosis as documented by the provider. Active indicates an ongoing condition; resolved indicates the condition has been treated or cleared; chronic conditions may persist across encounters.,
clinical,patient_documentation,diagnosis,coding_date,coding_date,Coding Date,DATE,,,,,transactional_data,"The date on which the ICD-10-CM code was assigned or finalized by the HIM coder. Used for coding turnaround time reporting, revenue cycle management, and compliance audits.",
clinical,patient_documentation,diagnosis,coding_status,coding_status,Coding Status,STRING,,,,unreviewed|coded|queried|finalized|amended,transactional_data,Indicates the Health Information Management (HIM) coding workflow status for this diagnosis. Finalized diagnoses are ready for claim submission; amended diagnoses reflect post-coding corrections.,
clinical,patient_documentation,diagnosis,complication_comorbidity_flag,complication_comorbidity_flag,Complication or Comorbidity (CC/MCC) Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,Indicates whether this secondary diagnosis qualifies as a Complication (CC) or Major Complication/Comorbidity (MCC) under CMS DRG grouping logic. CC/MCC status elevates DRG weight and reimbursement.,
clinical,patient_documentation,diagnosis,consent_verification_status,consent_verification_status,Verification Status,STRING,,,,confirmed|provisional|differential|refuted|entered_in_error,transactional_data,Indicates the degree of clinical certainty for this diagnosis. Confirmed diagnoses are used for billing and DRG assignment; provisional and differential diagnoses support CDI workflows and clinical decision-making. Maps to Epic ClinDoc diagnosis certainty and Cerner PowerChart diagnosis qualifier.,
clinical,patient_documentation,diagnosis,diagnosis_date,diagnosis_date,Diagnosis Recorded Date,DATE,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_health",,transactional_data,The date on which the diagnosis was formally documented in the EHR by the clinician. Distinct from onset date (when the condition began) and encounter date. Used as the principal business event date for this transaction record.,
clinical,patient_documentation,diagnosis,diagnosis_rank,diagnosis_rank,Diagnosis Rank,INT,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_health",,transactional_data,"Numeric sequence indicating the ordering of diagnoses within an encounter (1 = principal, 2 = first secondary, etc.). Used for UB-04 claim form sequencing, DRG optimization, and CDI prioritization.",
clinical,patient_documentation,diagnosis,diagnosis_type,diagnosis_type,Diagnosis Type,STRING,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_health",principal|secondary|admitting|discharge|working|chronic_problem_list,transactional_data,Classifies the role of this diagnosis within the encounter or problem list context. Principal diagnosis drives DRG assignment; admitting diagnosis reflects the reason for admission; secondary diagnoses capture comorbidities and complications. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: principal|secondary|admitting|discharge|working|chronic_problem_list — promote to reference product],
clinical,patient_documentation,diagnosis,discharge_diagnosis_flag,discharge_diagnosis_flag,Discharge Diagnosis Flag,BOOLEAN,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_health",,transactional_data,"Indicates whether this diagnosis was finalized as a discharge diagnosis at the conclusion of the inpatient encounter. Discharge diagnoses are used for final DRG assignment, claim submission, and discharge summary documentation.",
clinical,patient_documentation,diagnosis,drg_relevant_flag,drg_relevant_flag,Diagnosis-Related Group (DRG) Relevant Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,Indicates whether this diagnosis contributes to the DRG assignment for the associated inpatient encounter. Used by the 3M grouper and revenue cycle teams to identify diagnoses that impact reimbursement.,
clinical,patient_documentation,diagnosis,encounter_diagnosis_source,encounter_diagnosis_source,Diagnosis Entry Source,STRING,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_health",physician|cdi_specialist|coder|nurse|imported,transactional_data,"Identifies the role of the person who entered or assigned this diagnosis in the EHR. Supports CDI workflow analysis, coding quality audits, and provider attribution reporting.",
clinical,patient_documentation,diagnosis,encounter_type,encounter_type,Encounter Type,STRING,,,,inpatient|outpatient|emergency|observation|telehealth,transactional_data,Classifies the type of encounter in which this diagnosis was documented. Inpatient diagnoses are subject to POA reporting and DRG grouping; outpatient diagnoses follow CMS-1500 coding guidelines. Denormalized from the encounter for direct diagnosis-level analytics.,
clinical,patient_documentation,diagnosis,external_cause_code,external_cause_code,External Cause of Injury (ICD-10-CM) Code,STRING,,,,"^[VWX][0-9A-Z]{2,6}(.[0-9A-Z]{1,4})?$|^Y[0-9A-Z]{2,6}(.[0-9A-Z]{1,4})?$",transactional_data,"ICD-10-CM external cause code (V, W, X, Y codes) documenting the mechanism, intent, and place of occurrence for injury-related diagnoses. Required for trauma registries, workers compensation claims, and injury surveillance reporting.",
clinical,patient_documentation,diagnosis,hac_flag,hac_flag,Hospital-Acquired Condition (HAC) Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,Indicates whether this diagnosis qualifies as a CMS-designated Hospital-Acquired Condition (HAC). HAC-flagged diagnoses that were not present on admission may trigger payment reductions under the HAC Reduction Program.,
clinical,patient_documentation,diagnosis,icd10_version,icd10_version,ICD-10-CM Fiscal Year Version,STRING,,,,^FY[0-9]{4}$,transactional_data,"The CMS fiscal year version of the ICD-10-CM code set used to assign this diagnosis code (e.g., FY2024). ICD-10-CM is updated annually; version tracking ensures accurate historical code interpretation and audit defense.",
clinical,patient_documentation,diagnosis,last_updated_timestamp,last_updated_timestamp,Last Updated Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,"The date and time when this diagnosis record was most recently modified in the source EHR system. Used for incremental data loads, CDI amendment tracking, and audit compliance.",
clinical,patient_documentation,diagnosis,laterality,laterality,Diagnosis Laterality,STRING,,,,left|right|bilateral|unspecified,transactional_data,"Specifies the anatomical side affected by the diagnosis where applicable (e.g., left knee fracture, right breast mass). ICD-10-CM codes often encode laterality; this field provides an explicit queryable attribute for surgical scheduling and quality reporting.",
clinical,patient_documentation,diagnosis,mcc_flag,mcc_flag,Major Complication or Comorbidity (MCC) Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,Indicates whether this diagnosis specifically qualifies as a Major Complication or Comorbidity (MCC) — the highest severity tier in CMS DRG grouping. Distinct from the general CC flag; MCC status drives the highest DRG weight tier.,
clinical,patient_documentation,diagnosis,mrn,mrn,Medical Record Number (MRN),STRING,,,"dbx_pii_identifier,dbx_restricted,pii_phi,pii_pii,pii_sensitive",,transactional_data,Added Unity Catalog tags for PHI classification.,
clinical,patient_documentation,diagnosis,note_text,note_text,Diagnosis Clinical Note,STRING,,,dbx_confidential,,transactional_data,"Free-text clinical note or comment associated with this diagnosis entry, as documented by the provider or CDI specialist. May include clinical rationale, specificity details, or query responses. Classified as confidential due to clinical content.",
clinical,patient_documentation,diagnosis,onset_date,onset_date,Diagnosis Onset Date,DATE,,,,,transactional_data,"The date on which the condition or diagnosis first began, as documented by the clinician. Used for chronic disease management, population health analytics, and longitudinal patient record construction.",
clinical,patient_documentation,diagnosis,present_on_admission,present_on_admission,Present on Admission (POA) Indicator,STRING,,,,Y|N|U|W|1,transactional_data,"CMS-required Present on Admission (POA) indicator for inpatient diagnoses. Y=present at admission, N=not present at admission, U=unknown, W=clinically undetermined, 1=unreported/not used. Affects hospital-acquired condition (HAC) payment adjustments and quality reporting.",
clinical,patient_documentation,diagnosis,principal_diagnosis_flag,principal_diagnosis_flag,Principal Diagnosis Flag,BOOLEAN,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_health",,transactional_data,Indicates whether this diagnosis is designated as the principal diagnosis for the encounter (True). The principal diagnosis is the condition established after study to be chiefly responsible for the admission and drives DRG assignment.,
clinical,patient_documentation,diagnosis,problem_list_flag,problem_list_flag,Problem List Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,Indicates whether this diagnosis is part of the patients longitudinal problem list (True) or is encounter-specific only (False). Problem list diagnoses persist across encounters and drive chronic disease management workflows.,
clinical,patient_documentation,diagnosis,quality_measure_flag,quality_measure_flag,Quality Measure Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,"Indicates whether this diagnosis is relevant to one or more quality measures (e.g., HEDIS, MIPS, VBP, TJC core measures). Used to identify patients for quality measure denominator and numerator attribution.",
clinical,patient_documentation,diagnosis,recorded_timestamp,recorded_timestamp,Diagnosis Recorded Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,"The precise date and time when this diagnosis record was first created in the source EHR system (Epic ClinDoc or Cerner PowerChart). Supports audit trails, CDI workflow timing, and data lineage.",
clinical,patient_documentation,diagnosis,resolution_date,resolution_date,Diagnosis Resolution Date,DATE,,,,,transactional_data,"The date on which the condition was resolved, cured, or no longer clinically active. Null for ongoing or chronic conditions. Used to calculate episode duration and support transitions of care.",
clinical,patient_documentation,diagnosis,sdoh_flag,sdoh_flag,Social Determinants of Health (SDOH) Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,"Indicates whether this diagnosis is classified as a Social Determinants of Health (SDOH) condition (Z55–Z65 ICD-10-CM Z-codes). Used for population health management, care coordination, and CMS SDOH reporting initiatives.",
clinical,patient_documentation,diagnosis,severity,severity,Diagnosis Severity,STRING,,,,mild|moderate|severe|critical,transactional_data,"Clinical severity level of the diagnosis as documented by the provider. Drives care intensity decisions, DRG complexity, and quality measure stratification. Aligns with SNOMED CT severity qualifiers.",
clinical,patient_documentation,diagnosis,source_system,source_system,Source System,STRING,,,,Epic_ClinDoc|Cerner_PowerChart|MEDITECH_Expanse|Manual_Entry,transactional_data,"Identifies the originating EHR or clinical information system from which this diagnosis record was sourced. Supports data lineage, reconciliation across systems, and HIE interoperability.",
clinical,patient_documentation,diagnosis,source_system_diagnosis_code,source_system_diagnosis_code,Source System Diagnosis ID,STRING,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_health",,transactional_data,"The native identifier for this diagnosis record in the originating source system (e.g., Epic diagnosis ID, Cerner diagnosis ID). Enables bidirectional traceability between the lakehouse and the operational EHR.",
clinical,patient_documentation,note,note_id,note_id,Clinical Note ID,BIGINT,Y,,"pii_phi,pii_pii,pii_sensitive",,transactional_data,"Add pii_phi, pii_pii, pii_sensitive tags",
clinical,patient_documentation,note,care_site_id,care_site_id,Facility ID,BIGINT,,facility.care_site.care_site_id,,,transactional_data,Reference to the facility or care site where the clinical note was authored. Supports multi-facility enterprise reporting and regulatory submissions.,
clinical,patient_documentation,note,clinical_order_id,clinical_order_id,Related Clinical Order Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,order.clinical_order.clinical_order_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to order.clinical_order. Business justification: Clinical notes document rationale for orders. Real workflow: progress note states ordered CBC due to fever. Essential for CDI queries, medical necessity review, audit defense, and clinical decision ",
clinical,patient_documentation,note,consent_record_id,consent_record_id,Consent Record Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,consent.consent_consent_record.consent_record_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to consent.consent_record. Business justification: Clinical notes document consent discussions, patient education, and consent status changes. EHR workflows link consent conversations to notes for regulatory audits (informed consent documentation requ",
clinical,patient_documentation,note,demographics_id,demographics_id,Patient ID,BIGINT,,patient.demographics.demographics_id,,,transactional_data,Reference to the patient who is the subject of this clinical note. Core linkage to the Master Patient Index (MPI).,
clinical,patient_documentation,note,loinc_code_id,loinc_code_id,Loinc Document Type Code Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,reference.loinc_code.loinc_code_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to reference.loinc_code. Business justification: Document type classification for C-CDA generation, HIE document exchange, and clinical document architecture compliance. Health information management uses LOINC document codes for interoperable clini",
clinical,patient_documentation,note,mpi_record_id,mpi_record_id,,BIGINT,,patient.mpi_record.mpi_record_id,,,transactional_data,FK to patient.mpi_record.mpi_record_id,
