clinical,patient_documentation,note,org_unit_id,org_unit_id,Department ID,BIGINT,,workforce.org_unit.org_unit_id,,,transactional_data,"Reference to the clinical department or unit where the note was authored (e.g., ICU, ED, Cardiology Clinic). Supports departmental productivity and documentation compliance reporting.",
clinical,patient_documentation,note,parent_note_id,parent_note_id,Parent Note ID,BIGINT,,clinical.note.note_id,,,transactional_data,Reference to the original clinical note to which this addendum or amendment is attached. Null for original notes. Enables reconstruction of the complete note history and amendment chain.,
clinical,patient_documentation,note,payer_id,payer_id,Payer Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,insurance.payer.payer_id,,,transactional_data,Foreign key linking to insurance.payer. Business justification: Clinical documentation must meet payer-specific medical necessity criteria for authorization and appeals. CDI programs review notes against payer policies. Documentation requirements vary by payer (Me,
clinical,patient_documentation,note,primary_note_attending_provider_clinician_id,primary_note_attending_provider_clinician_id,Attending Provider ID,BIGINT,,provider.clinician.clinician_id,,,transactional_data,"Reference to the attending physician of record for the encounter at the time the note was authored. May differ from the note author (e.g., resident authors, attending co-signs). Used for CMS billing attribution and quality measure assignment.",
clinical,patient_documentation,note,tertiary_note_cosigner_provider_clinician_id,tertiary_note_cosigner_provider_clinician_id,Co-signer Provider ID,BIGINT,,provider.clinician.clinician_id,,,transactional_data,Reference to the supervising or co-signing provider who attests to the note content. Required for resident/trainee notes per CMS teaching physician rules. Nullable when no co-signature is required.,
clinical,patient_documentation,note,visit_id,visit_id,Encounter ID,BIGINT,,encounter.visit.visit_id,,,transactional_data,"Reference to the clinical encounter during which this note was authored. Links the note to the patient visit context (inpatient, outpatient, ED, etc.).",
clinical,patient_documentation,note,admission_date,admission_date,Admission Date,DATE,,,,,transactional_data,"The date of inpatient admission associated with this note. Denormalized for inpatient note timeliness compliance calculations (e.g., H&P must be completed within 24 hours of admission per TJC RC.02.01.01). Null for outpatient notes.",
clinical,patient_documentation,note,amended_timestamp,amended_timestamp,Note Amended Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,The date and time when the note was last amended (corrected). Amendments replace erroneous content while preserving the original for audit purposes. Nullable for notes that have never been amended.,
clinical,patient_documentation,note,author_role,author_role,Note Author Role,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"The clinical role of the provider who authored the note. Determines co-signature requirements, billing eligibility (incident-to rules), and CDI workflow routing. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: attending|resident|fellow|nurse_practitioner|physician_assistant|registered_nurse|medical_student|clinical_pharmacist|case_manager|social_worker — promote to reference product]",
clinical,patient_documentation,note,authored_timestamp,authored_timestamp,Note Authored Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,"The date and time when the provider began authoring or first saved the clinical note in the EHR. Represents the business event timestamp for note creation. Used for timeliness compliance reporting (e.g., H&P within 24 hours of admission per TJC).",
clinical,patient_documentation,note,care_setting,care_setting,Care Setting,STRING,,,,inpatient|outpatient|emergency|observation|ambulatory_surgery|telehealth,transactional_data,"The clinical care setting in which the note was authored. Determines applicable documentation standards, billing rules (UB-04 vs CMS-1500), and regulatory requirements.",
clinical,patient_documentation,note,cdi_query_flag,cdi_query_flag,Clinical Documentation Improvement (CDI) Query Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,Indicates whether a CDI specialist has issued a physician query against this note requesting clarification or additional specificity to support accurate ICD-10 coding and DRG assignment. Core to CDI workflow management.,
clinical,patient_documentation,note,cdi_query_status,cdi_query_status,Clinical Documentation Improvement (CDI) Query Status,STRING,,,,pending|answered|withdrawn|no_query,transactional_data,"Current status of the CDI physician query associated with this note. Tracks whether the provider has responded to the query, enabling CDI team follow-up and DRG impact analysis.",
clinical,patient_documentation,note,confidentiality_level,confidentiality_level,Note Confidentiality Level,STRING,,,,normal|restricted|very_restricted,transactional_data,"The confidentiality classification of the note controlling access within the EHR. Restricted notes (e.g., behavioral health, substance abuse, HIV) require additional access controls per 42 CFR Part 2 and state mental health laws.",
clinical,patient_documentation,note,cosigned_timestamp,cosigned_timestamp,Note Co-signed Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,The date and time when the supervising provider co-signed the note. Required for resident and mid-level provider notes under CMS teaching physician and incident-to billing rules. Nullable when co-signature is not required.,
clinical,patient_documentation,note,created_timestamp,created_timestamp,Record Created Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,"The date and time when this clinical note record was first created in the lakehouse Silver layer. Represents the ETL ingestion audit timestamp, distinct from the clinical authored timestamp.",
clinical,patient_documentation,note,dictation_method,dictation_method,Note Dictation Method,STRING,,,,typed|voice_dictation|speech_recognition|scribe|imported,transactional_data,"The method by which the note content was entered into the EHR. Supports provider efficiency analytics, scribe program management, and AI-assisted documentation quality assessment.",
clinical,patient_documentation,note,discharge_date,discharge_date,Discharge Date,DATE,,,,,transactional_data,The date of patient discharge associated with this note. Used for discharge summary timeliness compliance (must be completed within 30 days of discharge per TJC). Null for non-discharge notes.,
clinical,patient_documentation,note,drg_impact_flag,drg_impact_flag,Diagnosis-Related Group (DRG) Impact Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,Indicates whether the documentation in this note has been identified as having a potential impact on the assigned DRG and associated reimbursement. Used by CDI and HIM teams to prioritize review queues.,
clinical,patient_documentation,note,encounter_type,encounter_type,Encounter Type,STRING,,,,inpatient|outpatient|emergency|observation|telehealth|surgical,transactional_data,The type of clinical encounter associated with this note. Denormalized from the encounter for note-level analytics and CDI workflow routing without requiring a join to the encounter table.,
clinical,patient_documentation,note,facility_service_date,facility_service_date,Service Date,DATE,,,,,transactional_data,The calendar date on which the clinical service or encounter event being documented occurred. Distinct from the note authoring date; used for billing date-of-service alignment and clinical timeline reconstruction.,
clinical,patient_documentation,note,facility_service_line,facility_service_line,Service Line,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"The hospital or health system service line under which the note was authored (e.g., Cardiovascular, Oncology, Womens Health, Behavioral Health). Supports service-line-level analytics and operational reporting.",
clinical,patient_documentation,note,format,format,Clinical Note Format,STRING,,,,free_text|structured|semi_structured|template_based,transactional_data,"Indicates whether the note content is unstructured free text, fully structured (discrete data elements), semi-structured (narrative with embedded structured fields), or authored from a predefined template. Drives NLP/AI processing pipelines and CDI tool integration.",
clinical,patient_documentation,note,is_addendum,is_addendum,Is Addendum Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,Indicates whether this note record is an addendum appended to a previously signed note rather than an original note. Addenda supplement but do not replace the original note content.,
clinical,patient_documentation,note,is_copy_forwarded,is_copy_forwarded,Is Copy-Forward Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,Indicates whether the note content was copied or cloned from a prior note rather than independently authored. Copy-forward documentation is an OIG audit target and a CDI quality concern affecting medical necessity and billing integrity.,
clinical,patient_documentation,note,is_late_entry,is_late_entry,Is Late Entry Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,"Indicates whether the note was authored after the standard documentation timeliness window (e.g., H&P authored more than 24 hours after admission). Late entries must be identified per TJC and CMS medical record standards.",
clinical,patient_documentation,note,mrn,mrn,Medical Record Number (MRN),STRING,,,"dbx_pii_identifier,dbx_restricted,pii_phi,pii_pii,pii_sensitive",,transactional_data,"pii_phi,pii_pii,pii_sensitive",
clinical,patient_documentation,note,note_status,note_status,Clinical Note Status,STRING,,,,draft|signed|amended|addended|retracted,transactional_data,Current workflow state of the clinical note in the EHR documentation lifecycle. Draft notes are incomplete; signed notes are legally attested; amended notes reflect corrections; addended notes have supplemental content appended; retracted notes have been withdrawn from the medical record.,
clinical,patient_documentation,note,note_text,note_text,Clinical Note Text (Protected Health Information),STRING,,,"dbx_pii_health,dbx_restricted,entity_type=Add tags pii_phi,pii_phi,pii_pii,pii_sensitive",,transactional_data,"pii_phi,pii_pii,pii_sensitive",
clinical,patient_documentation,note,note_type,note_type,Clinical Note Type,STRING,,,,History and Physical|Progress Note|Discharge Summary|Operative Note|Consult Note|Nursing Note,transactional_data,"Classification of the clinical note by its documentation purpose and clinical context. Drives CDI workflows, HIM coding queues, and regulatory reporting. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: History and Physical|Progress Note|Discharge Summary|Operative Note|Consult Note|Nursing Note|Procedure Note|Radiology Report|Pathology Report|Transfer Note|Referral Note|Telephone Encounter Note — promote to reference product]",
clinical,patient_documentation,note,principal_diagnosis_code,principal_diagnosis_code,Principal Diagnosis International Classification of Diseases 10th Revision (ICD-10) Code,STRING,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_health","^[A-Z][0-9A-Z]{1,6}(.[0-9A-Z]{1,4})?$",transactional_data,"The ICD-10-CM diagnosis code for the principal condition documented in this note, as identified by the authoring provider. Particularly relevant for discharge summaries and H&P notes. Supports HIM coding validation and CDI workflows.",
clinical,patient_documentation,note,sensitive_note_type,sensitive_note_type,Sensitive Note Type,STRING,,,,behavioral_health|substance_abuse|hiv_aids|sexual_health|domestic_violence|none,transactional_data,Identifies whether the note contains sensitive clinical content subject to heightened privacy protections beyond standard HIPAA requirements. Drives break-the-glass access controls and consent management workflows.,
clinical,patient_documentation,note,signed_timestamp,signed_timestamp,Note Signed Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,"The date and time when the author electronically signed and attested to the clinical note, making it a legally authenticated entry in the medical record. Nullable for draft notes.",
clinical,patient_documentation,note,source_system,source_system,Source System,STRING,,,,Epic_ClinDoc|Cerner_PowerChart|MEDITECH_Expanse|other,transactional_data,"The originating EHR system from which this clinical note was sourced. Supports multi-system enterprise environments and ETL lineage tracking across Epic ClinDoc, Cerner PowerChart, and MEDITECH Expanse deployments.",
clinical,patient_documentation,note,source_system_note_code,source_system_note_code,Source System Note ID,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,The native identifier of this note in the originating EHR system (Epic ClinDoc note ID or Cerner PowerChart document ID). Used for cross-system reconciliation and ETL lineage tracing.,
clinical,patient_documentation,note,specialty,specialty,Clinical Specialty,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"The medical or clinical specialty associated with the note (e.g., Cardiology, Orthopedics, Nursing, Anesthesiology). Derived from the authoring providers specialty or the ordering service. Used for specialty-specific CDI and quality reporting.",
clinical,patient_documentation,note,template_id,template_id,Note Template ID,BIGINT,,,,,transactional_data,"The identifier of the EHR documentation template used to author this note (e.g., Epic SmartText or Cerner PowerNote template ID). Supports template utilization analytics and standardization initiatives.",
clinical,patient_documentation,note,title,title,Clinical Note Title,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"The human-readable title or subject line of the clinical note as displayed in the EHR (e.g., Cardiology Consult Note, Post-Op Day 1 Progress Note). Supports note navigation and CDI workflow queuing.",
clinical,patient_documentation,note,updated_timestamp,updated_timestamp,Record Updated Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,"The date and time when this clinical note record was last modified in the lakehouse Silver layer. Supports incremental ETL processing, change data capture, and audit trail compliance.",
clinical,patient_documentation,note,version,version,Note Version Number,INT,,,,,transactional_data,"Monotonically incrementing version number for the note record, incremented with each amendment or addendum. Enables reconstruction of the complete note history and supports audit trail requirements.",
clinical,patient_documentation,note,word_count,word_count,Note Word Count,INT,,,,,transactional_data,"The total number of words in the clinical note text. Used for documentation quality metrics, CDI completeness scoring, and identifying copy-paste or cloned note patterns flagged by OIG compliance programs.",
clinical,patient_documentation,note_template,note_template_id,note_template_id,Note Template Identifier,BIGINT,Y,,"pii_phi,pii_pii,pii_sensitive",,master_data,"unity_catalog_tags: pii_phi, pii_pii, pii_sensitive; rls_predicate: ""has_access(user_id, mpi_record_id)""; delta_tblproperties: ""retention=7 years""; liquid_clustering: true",
clinical,patient_documentation,note_template,note_employee_id,note_employee_id,Created By User Identifier,BIGINT,,workforce.employee.employee_id,"confidential,pii",,master_data,Identifier of the user who created the template.,
clinical,patient_documentation,note_template,note_id,note_id,,BIGINT,,clinical.note.note_id,,,master_data,description,
