clinical,patient_documentation,note_template,template_description,template_description,Note Template Description,STRING,,,"boilerplate_description_example=Replace generic description with specific business purpose.,clinical.note_template.description=Removed boilerplate phrase,clinical.note_template=Clean boilerplate phrase from description,clinical.note_template=clean boilerplate phrase from description,clinical_note_template.description=Cleaned description without boilerplate,clinical_note_template_description=Cleaned boilerplate phrase from description,entity_type=Clean boilerplate phrase from clinical.note_template.description,entity_type=Clean boilerplate phrases from attribute descriptions.,entity_type=Cleaned boilerplate description,entity_type=Cleaned boilerplate phrase from attribute description 'clinical.note_template.description',entity_type=Cleaned boilerplate phrase from description,pii_phi,pii_pii,pii_sensitive",,master_data,"Free-text description of the note template purpose, target specialty, and intended clinical workflow context.",
clinical,patient_documentation,note_template,template_format,template_format,Template Format,STRING,,,,structured|free_text|mixed,master_data,"Indicates whether the template is fully structured, free‑text, or a hybrid.",
clinical,patient_documentation,note_template,template_type,template_type,Note Template Type,STRING,,,,progress|history|discharge|procedure|consult,master_data,"Category of clinical note the template supports (e.g., progress note, discharge summary).",
clinical,patient_documentation,note_template,uc_tag_definitions,uc_tag_definitions,,STRING,,,,,master_data,Added UC tag definitions for data classification.,
clinical,patient_documentation,note_template,updated_timestamp,updated_timestamp,Record Update Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,master_data,Timestamp of the most recent update to the template record.,
clinical,patient_documentation,note_template,version_number,version_number,Template Version Number,INT,,,,,master_data,Sequential version number of the template; increments when the template is revised.,
clinical,patient_documentation,observation,observation_id,observation_id,Observation ID,BIGINT,Y,,,,transactional_data,Unique surrogate identifier for each clinical observation record in the lakehouse silver layer. Primary key for the observation data product.,
clinical,patient_documentation,observation,care_site_id,care_site_id,Facility ID,BIGINT,,facility.care_site.care_site_id,,,transactional_data,"Reference to the healthcare facility (hospital, clinic, outpatient center) where the observation was recorded. Supports multi-facility reporting and regulatory submissions.",
clinical,patient_documentation,observation,clinical_order_id,clinical_order_id,Observation Clinical Order Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,order.clinical_order.clinical_order_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to order.clinical_order. Business justification: Observations fulfill assessment orders. Real workflow: order for fall risk assessment, nurse performs Morse scale. Essential for order completion tracking, nursing documentation compliance, quality me",
clinical,patient_documentation,observation,clinician_id,clinician_id,Clinician ID,BIGINT,,provider.clinician.clinician_id,,,transactional_data,"Reference to the licensed clinician (nurse, physician, therapist, or other credentialed provider) who documented or performed this observation. Supports accountability and Joint Commission documentation requirements.",
clinical,patient_documentation,observation,flowsheet_row_id,flowsheet_row_id,EHR Flowsheet Row ID,BIGINT,,clinical.flowsheet_row.flowsheet_row_id,,,transactional_data,"The source EHR flowsheet row or template identifier that defines the observation type in the originating system (e.g., Epic ClinDoc flowsheet row ID, Cerner PowerChart flowsheet mnemonic). Enables precise source system reconciliation and CDI workflow support.",
clinical,patient_documentation,observation,loinc_code_id,loinc_code_id,Loinc Code Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,reference.loinc_code.loinc_code_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to reference.loinc_code. Business justification: Lab result and clinical observation standardization for result interpretation, reference range application, critical value alerting, and public health reporting. Laboratory information systems use LOI",
clinical,patient_documentation,observation,mpi_record_id,mpi_record_id,Patient ID,BIGINT,,patient.mpi_record.mpi_record_id,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_health",,transactional_data,Reference to the patient for whom this clinical observation was recorded. Core party reference linking the observation to the Master Patient Index (MPI).,
clinical,patient_documentation,observation,quality_measure_id,quality_measure_id,Quality Measure Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,quality.measure.measure_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to quality.measure. Business justification: Lab-based measures (HbA1c, LDL-C) and assessment-based measures (depression screening PHQ-9) require observation data for numerator determination. Essential for automated quality measure calculation a",
clinical,patient_documentation,observation,snomed_concept_id,snomed_concept_id,Snomed Code Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,reference.snomed_concept.snomed_concept_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to reference.snomed_concept. Business justification: Clinical finding and assessment coding for structured documentation, clinical decision support, and quality measure calculation. SNOMED codes on observations enable semantic reasoning for care pathway",
clinical,patient_documentation,observation,visit_id,visit_id,Encounter ID,BIGINT,,encounter.visit.visit_id,,,transactional_data,"Reference to the clinical encounter (visit, admission, or episode of care) during which this observation was documented. Links the observation to its clinical context.",
clinical,patient_documentation,observation,amendment_reason,amendment_reason,Amendment Reason,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,Free-text or coded reason provided by the clinician for amending or correcting this observation after initial documentation. Required for CDI audit trails and HIPAA amendment compliance. Null when is_amended is false.,
clinical,patient_documentation,observation,assessment_component,assessment_component,Assessment Component Name,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"The specific sub-component or domain of a multi-part assessment tool being scored in this observation record (e.g., Sensory Perception for Braden Scale, Eye Opening for GCS, Mood for PHQ-9 item 1). Enables granular component-level analysis.",
clinical,patient_documentation,observation,assessment_score,assessment_score,Assessment Tool Score,"DECIMAL(10,2)",,,,,transactional_data,"Total composite score produced by the standardized assessment tool identified in assessment_tool (e.g., Braden Scale total score 6-23, Morse Fall Scale score 0-125, PHQ-9 score 0-27, GCS total 3-15). Drives clinical decision support thresholds and quality metric calculations.",
clinical,patient_documentation,observation,assessment_tool,assessment_tool,Clinical Assessment Tool,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Name of the standardized clinical assessment instrument or scoring tool used to generate this observation (e.g., Braden Scale, Morse Fall Scale, PHQ-9, GCS, Barthel Index, CAGE-AID, Columbia Suicide Severity Rating Scale, FIM). Supports nursing quality metrics and regulatory compliance reporting. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: Braden Scale|Morse Fall Scale|PHQ-9|GCS|Barthel Index|CAGE-AID|Columbia Suicide Severity|FIM|SDOH Screening|Discharge Readiness — promote to reference product]",
clinical,patient_documentation,observation,body_site_code,body_site_code,Body Site SNOMED CT Code,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"SNOMED CT code identifying the anatomical body site or region where the observation was performed or applies (e.g., 368209003 for right arm for blood pressure, 368209003 for wound location). Supports wound care documentation and surgical site infection (SSI) tracking.",
clinical,patient_documentation,observation,body_system,body_system,Body System,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Clinical body system or organ system to which this observation pertains (e.g., cardiovascular, respiratory, neurological, integumentary, musculoskeletal, gastrointestinal). Supports head-to-toe nursing assessment documentation and clinical analytics segmentation. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: cardiovascular|respiratory|neurological|integumentary|musculoskeletal|gastrointestinal|genitourinary|endocrine|hematologic|psychiatric — promote to reference product]",
clinical,patient_documentation,observation,care_setting,care_setting,Care Setting,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"The clinical care setting or unit type in which the observation was documented (e.g., inpatient, ED, ICU, OR, ambulatory, telehealth). Supports population health stratification, nursing quality metrics, and setting-specific regulatory reporting. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: inpatient|outpatient|ED|ICU|OR|ambulatory|telehealth|home-health — 8 candidates stripped; promote to reference product]",
clinical,patient_documentation,observation,created_datetime,created_datetime,Record Created Date and Time,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,"The date and time when this observation record was first created in the source system or ingested into the lakehouse. Supports audit trail requirements, data lineage, and HIPAA access log compliance.",
clinical,patient_documentation,observation,critical_value_notified_datetime,critical_value_notified_datetime,Critical Value Notification Date and Time,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,"Date and time when the responsible clinician was notified of a critical observation value, as required by The Joint Commission NPSG.02.03.01. Null when is_critical_value is false. Supports compliance auditing and response time measurement.",
clinical,patient_documentation,observation,data_absent_reason,data_absent_reason,Data Absent Reason,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Coded reason explaining why an expected observation value is missing or not available (e.g., patient declined, not performed, error in collection). Required for FHIR conformance and supports data quality monitoring and completeness reporting. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: unknown|asked-unknown|temp-unknown|not-asked|asked-declined|masked|not-applicable|error|not-performed — 9 candidates stripped; promote to reference product]",
clinical,patient_documentation,observation,datetime,datetime,Observation Date and Time,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,"The clinically effective date and time when the observation was made, measured, or assessed (not when it was entered into the system). This is the principal real-world event timestamp used for clinical trending, time-series analytics, and regulatory reporting.",
clinical,patient_documentation,observation,device_type,device_type,Observation Device Type,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Type of medical device or instrument used to obtain the observation (e.g., pulse oximeter, electronic thermometer, sphygmomanometer, glucometer, bedside monitor). Supports device performance tracking and FDA medical device reporting.",
clinical,patient_documentation,observation,external_observation_code,external_observation_code,External Observation ID,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Source system identifier for this observation as assigned by the originating Electronic Health Record (EHR) system (e.g., Epic ClinDoc flowsheet row ID, Cerner PowerChart result ID). Enables traceability back to the system of record.",
clinical,patient_documentation,observation,interpretation_flag,interpretation_flag,Observation Interpretation Flag,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Clinical interpretation of the observation value relative to the reference range (e.g., normal, abnormal, critical-high, critical-low). Drives clinical alerting, nursing escalation workflows, and quality metric calculations. Maps to HL7 FHIR Observation.interpretation. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: normal|abnormal|critical-high|critical-low|high|low|indeterminate — 7 candidates stripped; promote to reference product]",
clinical,patient_documentation,observation,is_amended,is_amended,Observation Amended Indicator,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,"Boolean flag indicating whether this observation record has been amended or corrected after initial documentation. Supports Clinical Documentation Improvement (CDI) workflows, audit trails, and HIPAA amendment request tracking.",
clinical,patient_documentation,observation,is_critical_value,is_critical_value,Critical Value Indicator,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,"Boolean flag indicating whether this observation result constitutes a critical (panic) value requiring immediate clinical notification per facility policy (e.g., GCS < 8, SpO2 < 85%). Drives critical value notification workflows and Joint Commission NPSG compliance.",
clinical,patient_documentation,observation,issued_datetime,issued_datetime,Observation Issued Date and Time,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,"The date and time the observation result was made available or released in the EHR system (e.g., when a nurse signed and released the flowsheet entry). Distinct from observation_datetime which captures when the measurement occurred.",
clinical,patient_documentation,observation,laterality,laterality,Laterality,STRING,,,,left|right|bilateral|midline|not-applicable,transactional_data,"Specifies the side of the body for the observation when anatomical laterality is clinically relevant (e.g., left arm blood pressure, right leg wound). Supports surgical safety, wound tracking, and clinical documentation accuracy.",
clinical,patient_documentation,observation,local_code,local_code,Local Observation Code,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Facility- or system-specific code for the observation as defined in the source EHR (e.g., Epic flowsheet row ID, Cerner mnemonic). Used for source system reconciliation when a standard LOINC code is not yet mapped.",
clinical,patient_documentation,observation,method_code,method_code,Observation Method SNOMED CT Code,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"SNOMED CT or LOINC method code describing the technique or procedure used to obtain the observation (e.g., 371911009 for auscultation, 113011001 for palpation, non-invasive vs invasive blood pressure measurement). Supports clinical accuracy and reproducibility.",
clinical,patient_documentation,observation,observation_category,observation_category,Observation Category,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"High-level clinical category classifying the type of observation per HL7 FHIR value set (e.g., vital-signs, nursing, functional, screening, exam). Drives downstream routing, analytics segmentation, and FHIR Observation.category mapping. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: vital-signs|laboratory|nursing|functional|screening|exam|social-history|imaging — 8 candidates stripped; promote to reference product]",
clinical,patient_documentation,observation,observation_status,observation_status,Observation Status,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Current workflow lifecycle status of the observation record per HL7 FHIR Observation.status value set. final indicates a verified, clinician-signed result; amended or corrected indicates post-signature modification; entered-in-error supports clinical documentation correction workflows. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: registered|preliminary|final|amended|corrected|cancelled|entered-in-error — 7 candidates stripped; promote to reference product]",
clinical,patient_documentation,observation,presence_status,presence_status,Clinical Finding Presence Status,STRING,,,,present|absent|unknown|not-applicable,transactional_data,"Indicates whether the clinical finding or condition being observed is present, absent, or unknown for this patient at the time of observation. Critical for problem list management, SNOMED CT post-coordination, and population health stratification.",
clinical,patient_documentation,observation,reference_range_high,reference_range_high,Reference Range High Value,"DECIMAL(18,6)",,,,,transactional_data,"The upper bound of the normal reference range for this observation type and patient population context (e.g., 100 for heart rate upper bound). Used to compute interpretation_flag and support clinical decision support.",
clinical,patient_documentation,observation,reference_range_low,reference_range_low,Reference Range Low Value,"DECIMAL(18,6)",,,,,transactional_data,"The lower bound of the normal reference range for this observation type and patient population context (e.g., 60 for heart rate lower bound). Used to compute interpretation_flag and support clinical decision support.",
clinical,patient_documentation,observation,sdoh_domain,sdoh_domain,Social Determinants of Health (SDOH) Domain,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"For SDOH screening observations, identifies the specific Social Determinants of Health (SDOH) domain being assessed (e.g., food insecurity, housing instability, transportation barriers). Supports population health management, ACO quality reporting, and CMS SDOH initiatives. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: food-insecurity|housing-instability|transportation|social-isolation|financial-strain|education|not-applicable — 7 candidates stripped; promote to reference product]",
clinical,patient_documentation,observation,severity,severity,Clinical Severity,STRING,,,,mild|moderate|severe|life-threatening|not-applicable,transactional_data,"Clinician-assessed severity of the finding or symptom documented in this observation (e.g., mild pain, severe dyspnea). Used in symptom documentation, behavioral health screenings, and clinical acuity stratification.",
clinical,patient_documentation,observation,source_system,source_system,Source System,STRING,,,,Epic-ClinDoc|Cerner-PowerChart|MEDITECH-Expanse|Manual-Entry|HL7-Interface|FHIR-API,transactional_data,"Identifies the originating operational system or integration channel from which this observation record was sourced (e.g., Epic ClinDoc flowsheet, Cerner PowerChart, HL7 interface). Supports data lineage, ETL reconciliation, and audit trail requirements.",
clinical,patient_documentation,observation,subcategory,subcategory,Observation Subcategory,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Finer-grained clinical classification within the observation_category (e.g., fall-risk, pressure-injury, neurological, wound, intake-output, behavioral-health, sdoh, discharge-readiness). Supports nursing quality metrics and Joint Commission compliance reporting. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: fall-risk|pressure-injury|neurological|wound|intake-output|behavioral-health|sdoh|discharge-readiness|pain|functional-status — promote to reference product]",
clinical,patient_documentation,observation,updated_datetime,updated_datetime,Record Last Updated Date and Time,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,"The date and time when this observation record was most recently modified in the source system or updated in the lakehouse silver layer. Supports incremental ETL processing, CDI workflows, and audit trail requirements.",
clinical,patient_documentation,observation,value_coded,value_coded,Coded Observation Value,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"The coded result value when the observation is expressed as a standardized code (e.g., SNOMED CT code 260385009 for negative, 10828004 for positive, or a LOINC answer list code). Used for coded clinical findings, presence/absence, and assessment scale responses.",
clinical,patient_documentation,observation,value_coded_system,value_coded_system,Coded Observation Value Coding System,STRING,,,,SNOMED-CT|LOINC|ICD-10|CPT|LOCAL,transactional_data,"The coding system used for the coded observation value when the result is expressed as a code rather than a number (e.g., SNOMED-CT for clinical findings, LOINC answer lists). Null when value_numeric or value_text is used.",
clinical,patient_documentation,observation,value_numeric,value_numeric,Numeric Observation Value,"DECIMAL(18,6)",,,,,transactional_data,"The quantitative measured value of the observation when the result is numeric (e.g., 98.6 for temperature, 120 for systolic blood pressure, 7 for GCS eye response score, 15 for Braden Scale total). Null when the observation result is coded or free-text.",
clinical,patient_documentation,observation,value_text,value_text,Free-Text Observation Value,STRING,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_health",,transactional_data,"Free-text narrative value for observations that cannot be expressed numerically or as a coded value (e.g., wound description, clinical impression, nursing note excerpt). Contains Protected Health Information (PHI) and must be handled per HIPAA requirements.",
clinical,patient_documentation,observation,value_unit,value_unit,Observation Value Unit of Measure,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"The unit of measure for the numeric observation value using UCUM (Unified Code for Units of Measure) notation (e.g., degF, mm[Hg], kg, /min, %, mL). Required when value_numeric is populated.",
clinical,patient_documentation,problem,problem_id,problem_id,Problem ID,BIGINT,Y,,,,master_data,Unique surrogate identifier for the patient problem list entry in the lakehouse silver layer. Primary key for this entity.,
clinical,patient_documentation,problem,care_plan_id,care_plan_id,Care Plan ID,BIGINT,,clinical.care_plan.care_plan_id,,,master_data,Reference to the care plan that addresses or manages this problem. Links the problem list entry to the patients longitudinal care plan for population health management and care coordination.,
clinical,patient_documentation,problem,care_site_id,care_site_id,Facility ID,BIGINT,,facility.care_site.care_site_id,,,master_data,"Reference to the healthcare facility (hospital, clinic, outpatient center) where this problem was documented. Supports multi-facility enterprise analytics and population health segmentation.",
clinical,patient_documentation,problem,clinical_order_id,clinical_order_id,Triggering Clinical Order Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,order.clinical_order.clinical_order_id,,,master_data,"Foreign key linking to order.clinical_order. Business justification: Active problems trigger standing and recurring orders. Real workflow: diabetes problem triggers quarterly A1C orders. Essential for chronic disease management protocols, population health order compli",
clinical,patient_documentation,problem,consent_record_id,consent_record_id,Consent Record Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,consent.consent_consent_record.consent_record_id,,,master_data,"Foreign key linking to consent.consent_record. Business justification: Chronic/sensitive problems (substance use disorder, mental health, HIV) trigger consent verification workflows. Problem list maintenance requires consent for disclosure to care team members. 42 CFR Pa",
clinical,patient_documentation,problem,icd_code_id,icd_code_id,Icd10 Code Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,reference.icd_code.icd_code_id,,,master_data,"Foreign key linking to reference.icd_code. Business justification: Problem-to-diagnosis mapping for HCC risk adjustment, quality measure attribution, and chronic condition reporting. Risk adjustment teams use ICD-10 codes on problem lists to calculate RAF scores and ",
clinical,patient_documentation,problem,primary_problem_added_by_provider_clinician_id,primary_problem_added_by_provider_clinician_id,Added By Provider ID,BIGINT,,provider.clinician.clinician_id,,,master_data,Reference to the clinician who originally added this problem to the patients problem list. Distinct from ordering_provider_id which reflects the current responsible provider. Supports audit and CDI workflows.,
clinical,patient_documentation,problem,problem_mpi_record_id,problem_mpi_record_id,Patient ID,BIGINT,,patient.mpi_record.mpi_record_id,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_health",,master_data,Reference to the patient whose longitudinal problem list this entry belongs to. Links to the master patient record.,
clinical,patient_documentation,problem,problem_onset_encounter_visit_id,problem_onset_encounter_visit_id,,BIGINT,,encounter.visit.visit_id,,,master_data,FK to encounter.visit.visit_id,
clinical,patient_documentation,problem,problem_patient_mpi_record_id,problem_patient_mpi_record_id,,BIGINT,,patient.mpi_record.mpi_record_id,,,master_data,description,
clinical,patient_documentation,problem,problem_visit_id,problem_visit_id,Encounter ID,BIGINT,,encounter.visit.visit_id,,,master_data,Reference to the clinical encounter during which this problem was first identified or most recently updated. Nullable — problems may exist independent of a specific encounter on the longitudinal problem list.,
clinical,patient_documentation,problem,snomed_concept_id,snomed_concept_id,Snomed Ct Code Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,reference.snomed_concept.snomed_concept_id,,,master_data,"Foreign key linking to reference.snomed_concept. Business justification: Problem list standardization for care coordination, clinical decision support, and USCDI compliance. SNOMED CT problem codes enable semantic matching for care gaps, drug-disease interactions, and popu",
clinical,patient_documentation,problem,tertiary_problem_last_updated_by_provider_clinician_id,tertiary_problem_last_updated_by_provider_clinician_id,Last Updated By Provider ID,BIGINT,,provider.clinician.clinician_id,,,master_data,Reference to the clinician who most recently modified this problem record. Supports Clinical Documentation Improvement (CDI) audit trails and accountability tracking.,
clinical,patient_documentation,problem,body_site_code,body_site_code,Body Site Code,STRING,,,,,master_data,"SNOMED CT code identifying the anatomical body site associated with this problem (e.g., 368209003 = Right arm). Supports surgical planning, radiology ordering, and clinical specificity in documentation.",
clinical,patient_documentation,problem,body_site_description,body_site_description,Body Site Description,STRING,,,,,master_data,Human-readable description of the anatomical body site corresponding to body_site_code. Stored for reporting and display purposes.,
clinical,patient_documentation,problem,care_setting,care_setting,Care Setting,STRING,,,,inpatient|outpatient|emergency|ambulatory|telehealth,master_data,"The clinical care setting in which this problem was documented or is being managed. Supports population health stratification and care coordination analytics across inpatient, outpatient, Emergency Department (ED), and telehealth settings.",
clinical,patient_documentation,problem,cdi_query_flag,cdi_query_flag,Clinical Documentation Improvement (CDI) Query Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,"Indicates whether a Clinical Documentation Improvement (CDI) query has been raised against this problem entry, requesting clarification or specificity from the treating physician to support accurate coding and reimbursement.",
clinical,patient_documentation,problem,cdi_query_status,cdi_query_status,Clinical Documentation Improvement (CDI) Query Status,STRING,,,,pending|answered|withdrawn|no-query,master_data,"Current status of the Clinical Documentation Improvement (CDI) query associated with this problem, if applicable. Tracks whether the physician has responded to the CDI query for coding specificity.",
clinical,patient_documentation,problem,chronic_condition_flag,chronic_condition_flag,Chronic Condition Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,"Indicates whether this problem is classified as a chronic condition for the purposes of population health management, care management program enrollment, and CMS Hierarchical Condition Category (HCC) risk adjustment. True = chronic condition.",
clinical,patient_documentation,problem,confidential_flag,confidential_flag,Confidential Problem Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,"Indicates whether this problem has been marked as confidential in the Electronic Health Record (EHR), restricting access to authorized users only. Commonly applied to sensitive diagnoses such as HIV/AIDS, substance use disorders, and psychiatric conditions per 42 CFR Part 2 and state privacy laws.",
clinical,patient_documentation,problem,consent_verification_status,consent_verification_status,Verification Status,STRING,,,,confirmed|unconfirmed|provisional|differential|refuted,master_data,Clinical verification status indicating the degree of certainty that the problem exists for this patient. Aligns with HL7 FHIR Condition.verificationStatus. confirmed indicates a definitive diagnosis; provisional or differential indicates a working diagnosis under evaluation.,
clinical,patient_documentation,problem,created_timestamp,created_timestamp,Record Created Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,master_data,The date and time when this problem record was first created in the source Electronic Health Record (EHR) system. Establishes the audit trail origin for the problem list entry.,
clinical,patient_documentation,problem,fhir_condition_reference,fhir_condition_reference,HL7 FHIR Condition Resource ID,STRING,,,,,master_data,"The HL7 Fast Healthcare Interoperability Resources (FHIR) Condition resource identifier for this problem, used in Health Information Exchange (HIE) and interoperability workflows. Supports CMS Interoperability and Patient Access Rule compliance.",
clinical,patient_documentation,problem,hcc_category_code,hcc_category_code,Hierarchical Condition Category (HCC) Code,STRING,,,,,master_data,"CMS Hierarchical Condition Category (HCC) code mapped to this problem. Used for Medicare Advantage risk adjustment, capitation payment calculations, and population health risk stratification.",
clinical,patient_documentation,problem,is_encounter_diagnosis,is_encounter_diagnosis,Is Encounter Diagnosis Flag,BOOLEAN,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_health",,master_data,Indicates whether this problem list entry was also used as an encounter-level diagnosis for billing and claims purposes. Distinguishes longitudinal problem list entries from encounter-specific diagnoses used in revenue cycle management.,
clinical,patient_documentation,problem,last_reviewed_date,last_reviewed_date,Last Reviewed Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,The most recent date on which a clinician reviewed and affirmed or updated this problem on the patients problem list. Supports Clinical Documentation Improvement (CDI) workflows and problem list hygiene audits.,
clinical,patient_documentation,problem,last_updated_timestamp,last_updated_timestamp,Last Updated Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,master_data,"The date and time when this problem record was most recently modified in the source Electronic Health Record (EHR) system. Used for change detection, audit trails, and incremental ETL processing.",
clinical,patient_documentation,problem,laterality,laterality,Laterality,STRING,,,,left|right|bilateral|unspecified,master_data,"Anatomical laterality qualifier for the problem where applicable (e.g., left knee osteoarthritis, right breast mass). Supports precise ICD-10-CM coding specificity and surgical planning.",
clinical,patient_documentation,problem,list_display_order,list_display_order,Problem List Display Order,INT,,,,,master_data,Numeric sequence indicating the display order of this problem on the patients problem list as configured in the Electronic Health Record (EHR). Lower numbers appear first. Supports clinical workflow and provider-defined prioritization.,
clinical,patient_documentation,problem,mrn,mrn,Medical Record Number (MRN),STRING,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_identifier",,master_data,The Medical Record Number (MRN) assigned to the patient by the facility. Denormalized here for operational reporting and audit purposes without requiring a join to the patient master.,
clinical,patient_documentation,problem,noted_date,noted_date,Problem Noted Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,The date on which the problem was first documented or noted in the Electronic Health Record (EHR) problem list by a clinician. May differ from onset_date if the condition predates the current care relationship.,
clinical,patient_documentation,problem,onset_age_years,onset_age_years,Onset Age in Years,INT,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_health",,master_data,"Patients age in years at the time of problem onset, as documented or calculated. Useful for population health stratification and epidemiological analytics when exact onset date is unavailable or approximate.",
clinical,patient_documentation,problem,onset_date,onset_date,Problem Onset Date,DATE,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_health",,master_data,"The date on which the patients problem or condition first began, as documented by the clinician. May be approximate (e.g., year only) for historical conditions. Used in longitudinal care management, population health analytics, and chronic disease registries.",
clinical,patient_documentation,problem,principal_problem_flag,principal_problem_flag,Principal Problem Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,Indicates whether this problem is designated as the principal or primary problem driving the current episode of care or encounter. Used in Diagnosis-Related Group (DRG) assignment and revenue cycle workflows.,
clinical,patient_documentation,problem,priority,priority,Problem Priority,STRING,,,,high|medium|low|routine,master_data,Clinical priority assigned to this problem indicating its relative importance in the patients care plan. high priority problems typically drive care plan goals and quality measure attribution.,
clinical,patient_documentation,problem,problem_comment,problem_comment,Problem Comment,STRING,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_health",,master_data,"Free-text clinical comment or note associated with this problem list entry, as entered by the clinician in the Electronic Health Record (EHR). May include clinical context, treatment notes, or documentation improvement remarks.",
clinical,patient_documentation,problem,problem_status,problem_status,Problem Status,STRING,,,,active|inactive|resolved|deleted|entered-in-error,master_data,Current clinical lifecycle status of the problem on the patients longitudinal problem list. active indicates an ongoing condition; resolved indicates the condition has been addressed; inactive indicates the condition is not currently being managed; deleted or entered-in-error indicates administrative correction.,
clinical,patient_documentation,problem,problem_type,problem_type,Problem Type,STRING,,,,chronic|acute|historical|social|surgical|psychiatric,master_data,Clinical classification of the problem by its temporal and clinical nature. chronic indicates a long-standing condition; acute indicates a short-term condition; historical indicates a past condition no longer active; social indicates a social determinant of health (SDOH); surgical indicates a surgical history item; psychiatric indicates a behavioral health condition. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: chronic|acute|historical|social|surgical|psychiatric|functional|genetic — promote to reference product],
clinical,patient_documentation,problem,resolution_date,resolution_date,Problem Resolution Date,DATE,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_health",,master_data,The date on which the problem was clinically resolved or marked as resolved/inactive on the patients problem list. Null for active or chronic conditions. Used to calculate problem duration and track care outcomes.,
clinical,patient_documentation,problem,sdoh_flag,sdoh_flag,Social Determinants of Health (SDOH) Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,"Indicates whether this problem represents a Social Determinant of Health (SDOH) condition (e.g., food insecurity, housing instability, transportation barriers). Supports population health management and CMS SDOH reporting requirements.",
clinical,patient_documentation,problem,severity,severity,Problem Severity,STRING,,,,mild|moderate|severe|unspecified,master_data,"Clinical severity classification of the problem as documented by the treating clinician. Supports risk stratification, care management triage, and quality reporting.",
clinical,patient_documentation,problem,source_system,source_system,Source System,STRING,,,,Epic|Cerner|MEDITECH|Manual,master_data,"Identifies the originating Electronic Health Record (EHR) or clinical system from which this problem record was sourced (e.g., Epic, Cerner Millennium, MEDITECH Expanse).",
clinical,patient_documentation,problem,source_system_problem_code,source_system_problem_code,Source System Problem ID,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Native identifier for this problem record in the originating Electronic Health Record (EHR) system (e.g., Epic problem list ID or Cerner problem instance ID). Used for lineage tracing and reconciliation during ETL.",
clinical,patient_documentation,problem,stage_code,stage_code,Problem Stage Code,STRING,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_health",,master_data,"Clinical staging code for the problem where applicable (e.g., cancer TNM staging, chronic kidney disease stage, heart failure NYHA class). Supports oncology registries, chronic disease management, and quality reporting.",
clinical,patient_documentation,problem,stage_description,stage_description,Problem Stage Description,STRING,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_health",,master_data,"Human-readable description of the clinical stage corresponding to stage_code (e.g., Stage III Non-Small Cell Lung Cancer, CKD Stage 4). Stored for reporting clarity.",
clinical,patient_documentation,problem,title,title,Problem Title,STRING,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_health",,master_data,"Human-readable clinical name or title of the problem as displayed in the Electronic Health Record (EHR) problem list (e.g., Type 2 Diabetes Mellitus, Essential Hypertension). May be the SNOMED CT preferred term or a clinician-entered free-text label.",
