clinical,patient_documentation,procedure_event,visit_id,visit_id,Encounter ID,BIGINT,,encounter.visit.visit_id,,,transactional_data,"Reference to the clinical encounter (inpatient, outpatient, ED, surgical) during which this procedure was performed. Links procedure to the broader care episode for revenue cycle and quality reporting.",
clinical,patient_documentation,procedure_event,anesthesia_type,anesthesia_type,Anesthesia Type,STRING,,,,general|regional|local|monitored_anesthesia_care|none,transactional_data,"Type of anesthesia administered during the procedure. Drives anesthesia billing (ASA base units + time units), OR scheduling requirements, and pre-operative assessment workflows.",
clinical,patient_documentation,procedure_event,approach,approach,Surgical Approach,STRING,,,,open|laparoscopic|robotic|endoscopic|percutaneous|transcatheter,transactional_data,"Technique or access method used to perform the procedure (e.g., open, laparoscopic, robotic-assisted, endoscopic). Captured in ICD-10-PCS character 5 and used for surgical quality benchmarking and OR resource planning.",
clinical,patient_documentation,procedure_event,asa_classification,asa_classification,American Society of Anesthesiologists (ASA) Physical Status Classification,STRING,,,,I|II|III|IV|V|VI,transactional_data,"ASA Physical Status Classification (I–VI) assigned by the anesthesiologist to assess patient pre-operative risk. Required for anesthesia billing, surgical risk stratification, and quality benchmarking (ACS NSQIP).",
clinical,patient_documentation,procedure_event,body_site,body_site,Procedure Body Site,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Anatomical body site or region where the procedure was performed, coded using SNOMED CT body structure hierarchy. Supports surgical safety, clinical documentation completeness, and CDI workflows.",
clinical,patient_documentation,procedure_event,cancellation_reason,cancellation_reason,Procedure Cancellation Reason,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Coded reason for procedure cancellation when procedure_status is cancelled or not-done. Used for OR cancellation rate reporting, patient safety analysis, and operational improvement initiatives. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: patient_refusal|medical_contraindication|equipment_failure|scheduling_error|insurance_denial|no_show|provider_unavailable — promote to reference product]",
clinical,patient_documentation,procedure_event,cdm_code,cdm_code,Charge Description Master (CDM) Code,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,Internal facility CDM (Charge Description Master) code identifying the specific charge item for this procedure. Links clinical documentation to the revenue cycle charge capture process.,
clinical,patient_documentation,procedure_event,charge_amount,charge_amount,Procedure Charge Amount,"DECIMAL(12,2)",,,dbx_confidential,,transactional_data,"Gross charge amount in USD posted to the patient account for this procedure, sourced from the CDM (Charge Description Master). Represents the facilitys list price before contractual adjustments. Used for revenue cycle charge capture reconciliation.",
clinical,patient_documentation,procedure_event,consent_obtained,consent_obtained,Informed Consent Obtained Indicator,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,"Indicates whether documented informed consent was obtained from the patient or authorized representative prior to the procedure. Required for regulatory compliance, medical-legal documentation, and The Joint Commission RI.01.03.01.",
clinical,patient_documentation,procedure_event,cpt_modifier_1,cpt_modifier_1,CPT Modifier 1,STRING,,,,^[A-Z0-9]{2}$,transactional_data,"Primary AMA CPT modifier appended to the procedure code to indicate special circumstances (e.g., 22=Increased Procedural Services, 50=Bilateral, 51=Multiple Procedures, 59=Distinct Procedural Service). Required for accurate claim adjudication.",
clinical,patient_documentation,procedure_event,cpt_modifier_2,cpt_modifier_2,CPT Modifier 2,STRING,,,,^[A-Z0-9]{2}$,transactional_data,"Secondary AMA CPT modifier when multiple modifiers are required for the procedure code. Supports complex claim scenarios such as assistant surgeon (80), teaching physician (GC), or anesthesia qualifiers.",
clinical,patient_documentation,procedure_event,created_timestamp,created_timestamp,Record Created Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,"Timestamp when this procedure event record was first created in the source EHR system. Serves as the RECORD_AUDIT_CREATED field for data governance, audit trail, and HIPAA audit log requirements.",
clinical,patient_documentation,procedure_event,duration_minutes,duration_minutes,Procedure Duration (Minutes),INT,,,,,transactional_data,"Total elapsed time in minutes from procedure start to procedure end. Derived from start and end timestamps at source and stored for OR utilization analytics, anesthesia billing, and surgical quality benchmarking.",
clinical,patient_documentation,procedure_event,estimated_blood_loss_ml,estimated_blood_loss_ml,Estimated Blood Loss (EBL) in Milliliters,INT,,,,,transactional_data,"Estimated blood loss in milliliters recorded by the surgical team during the procedure. Used for post-operative care planning, transfusion trigger assessment, and surgical quality benchmarking (ACS NSQIP).",
clinical,patient_documentation,procedure_event,facility_service_line,facility_service_line,Clinical Service Line,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Hospital or health system service line under which the procedure is classified (e.g., Cardiovascular, Orthopedics, Neurosurgery, Oncology). Used for service-line P&L reporting, CMI analysis, and strategic planning. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: cardiovascular|orthopedics|neurosurgery|oncology|general_surgery|obstetrics|urology|gastroenterology — promote to reference product]",
clinical,patient_documentation,procedure_event,icd10_pcs_code,icd10_pcs_code,International Classification of Diseases 10th Revision Procedure Coding System (ICD-10-PCS) Code,STRING,,,,^[A-Z0-9]{7}$,transactional_data,"ICD-10-PCS code for inpatient procedures, used on UB-04 institutional claims for DRG grouping and inpatient quality reporting. Required for CMS inpatient prospective payment system (IPPS) reimbursement.",
clinical,patient_documentation,procedure_event,laterality,laterality,Procedure Laterality,STRING,,,,left|right|bilateral|unilateral|not_applicable,transactional_data,"Body side on which the procedure was performed. Required for surgical safety verification (Universal Protocol), correct-site surgery compliance, and ICD-10-PCS/CPT modifier application.",
clinical,patient_documentation,procedure_event,primary_diagnosis_code,primary_diagnosis_code,Primary Diagnosis ICD-10 Code,STRING,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_health","^[A-Z][0-9]{2}(.[A-Z0-9]{1,4})?$",transactional_data,"ICD-10-CM diagnosis code representing the primary indication for the procedure. Required for medical necessity validation, DRG grouping, and claim adjudication by payers.",
clinical,patient_documentation,procedure_event,priority,priority,Procedure Priority,STRING,,,,elective|urgent|emergent|stat,transactional_data,"Clinical urgency classification of the procedure at time of scheduling or ordering. Drives OR scheduling queue prioritization, resource allocation, and EMTALA compliance tracking for emergent cases.",
clinical,patient_documentation,procedure_event,procedure_category,procedure_category,Procedure Category,STRING,,,,surgical|diagnostic|therapeutic|preventive|rehabilitative|palliative,transactional_data,"High-level clinical category classifying the nature of the procedure. Used for service-line analytics, OR scheduling resource allocation, and population health stratification.",
clinical,patient_documentation,procedure_event,procedure_date,procedure_date,Procedure Date,DATE,,,,,transactional_data,"Calendar date on which the procedure was performed. Used as the primary date dimension for reporting, HEDIS measure denominator logic, and claim date-of-service on CMS-1500 and UB-04 forms.",
clinical,patient_documentation,procedure_event,procedure_end_datetime,procedure_end_datetime,Procedure End Date and Time,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,"Date and time when the procedure was completed (wound closure for surgical cases, or final intervention for non-surgical). Used with start time to calculate procedure duration for OR scheduling, staffing, and quality metrics.",
clinical,patient_documentation,procedure_event,procedure_number,procedure_number,Procedure Event Number,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Externally visible, human-readable business identifier for this procedure event, assigned by the source EHR system (e.g., Epic OpTime case number or Cerner SurgiNet procedure ID). Used for cross-system reconciliation and charge capture reference.",
clinical,patient_documentation,procedure_event,procedure_start_datetime,procedure_start_datetime,Procedure Start Date and Time,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,"Date and time when the procedure was initiated (knife-to-skin for surgical cases, or first intervention for non-surgical). Principal BUSINESS_EVENT_TIMESTAMP for this transaction. Used for OR utilization, LOS calculation, and quality measure timing.",
clinical,patient_documentation,procedure_event,procedure_status,procedure_status,Procedure Status,STRING,,,,performed|in-progress|cancelled|not-done|on-hold|entered-in-error,transactional_data,Current lifecycle state of the procedure event per HL7 FHIR Procedure.status value set. Drives revenue cycle charge capture eligibility and quality measure inclusion/exclusion logic. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: performed|in-progress|cancelled|not-done|on-hold|entered-in-error — promote to reference product],
clinical,patient_documentation,procedure_event,procedure_type,procedure_type,Procedure Type,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Operational classification of the procedure within the facilitys CDM (Charge Description Master), such as OR Case, Bedside Procedure, Interventional Radiology, Endoscopy, Cardiac Cath. Drives charge routing and scheduling resource assignment. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: or_case|bedside|interventional_radiology|endoscopy|cardiac_cath|ambulatory_surgery|labor_delivery — promote to reference product]",
clinical,patient_documentation,procedure_event,rvu_work,rvu_work,Relative Value Unit (RVU) — Work Component,"DECIMAL(8,2)",,,,,transactional_data,"CMS physician work Relative Value Unit (RVU) assigned to the CPT code for this procedure. Used for provider productivity measurement, compensation modeling, and MIPS performance reporting.",
clinical,patient_documentation,procedure_event,scheduled_start_datetime,scheduled_start_datetime,Scheduled Procedure Start Date and Time,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,"Originally scheduled date and time for the procedure. Compared against actual start time to measure on-time starts, OR schedule adherence, and first-case delay metrics.",
clinical,patient_documentation,procedure_event,snomed_ct_code,snomed_ct_code,Systematized Nomenclature of Medicine Clinical Terms (SNOMED CT) Procedure Code,STRING,,,,"^[0-9]{6,18}$",transactional_data,"SNOMED CT concept code representing the clinical procedure. Supports interoperability via HL7 FHIR and HIE exchange, and enables clinical decision support and population health analytics beyond billing code sets.",
clinical,patient_documentation,procedure_event,source_system,source_system,Source System,STRING,,,,epic_optime|epic_clindoc|cerner_surginet|cerner_powerchart|meditech_expanse,transactional_data,"Identifies the operational system of record from which this procedure event record was sourced. Used for data lineage, ETL reconciliation, and audit trail in the Silver Layer lakehouse.",
clinical,patient_documentation,procedure_event,source_system_record_code,source_system_record_code,Source System Record ID,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Native primary key or unique identifier of this procedure record in the originating source system (e.g., Epic OpTime case ID, Cerner SurgiNet procedure ID). Enables bidirectional traceability between the lakehouse Silver Layer and the operational EHR.",
clinical,patient_documentation,procedure_event,specimen_collected,specimen_collected,Specimen Collected Indicator,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,Indicates whether a tissue specimen or pathology sample was collected during the procedure. Triggers downstream laboratory/pathology order workflow and chain-of-custody documentation.,
clinical,patient_documentation,procedure_event,timeout_performed,timeout_performed,Surgical Time-Out Performed Indicator,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,"Indicates whether the pre-procedure surgical time-out (Universal Protocol) was completed and documented. Mandatory for Joint Commission accreditation and CMS Conditions of Participation to prevent wrong-site, wrong-procedure, wrong-patient events.",
clinical,patient_documentation,procedure_event,udi,udi,Unique Device Identifier (UDI),STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"FDA-assigned Unique Device Identifier (UDI) for the primary implant or medical device used during the procedure. Required for FDA device tracking, recall management, and 21st Century Cures Act compliance.",
clinical,patient_documentation,procedure_event,updated_timestamp,updated_timestamp,Record Updated Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,"Timestamp of the most recent modification to this procedure event record in the source EHR system. Serves as the RECORD_AUDIT_UPDATED field for change data capture (CDC), data quality monitoring, and HIPAA audit trail compliance.",
clinical,patient_documentation,procedure_event,wound_classification,wound_classification,Surgical Wound Classification,STRING,,,,clean|clean_contaminated|contaminated|dirty_infected,transactional_data,"CDC/ACS wound classification (Clean, Clean-Contaminated, Contaminated, Dirty/Infected) assigned at time of procedure. Used for SSI (Surgical Site Infection) surveillance, HAI reporting, and infection control quality metrics.",
clinical,preventive_health,allergy,allergy_id,allergy_id,Allergy Record ID,BIGINT,Y,,,,master_data,Unique surrogate identifier for each patient allergy or adverse reaction record in the clinical data product. Primary key for the allergy entity in the Silver Layer lakehouse.,
clinical,preventive_health,allergy,alert_triggering_cpoe_alert_id,alert_triggering_cpoe_alert_id,Alert Triggering Cpoe Alert Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,order.cpoe_alert.cpoe_alert_id,,,master_data,"Foreign key linking to order.cpoe_alert. Business justification: Allergies trigger CPOE alerts for contraindicated orders. Real workflow: penicillin allergy fires alert when ordering amoxicillin. Critical for patient safety event investigation, alert override analy",
clinical,preventive_health,allergy,allergen_drug_master_id,allergen_drug_master_id,Allergen Drug Master Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,pharmacy.drug_master.drug_master_id,,,master_data,Foreign key linking to pharmacy.drug_master. Business justification: Allergy checking against ordered/dispensed medications is critical patient safety function. Every CPOE and pharmacy system implements drug-allergy interaction screening. Required for meaningful use an,
clinical,preventive_health,allergy,care_site_id,care_site_id,Facility ID,BIGINT,,facility.care_site.care_site_id,,,master_data,"Reference to the healthcare facility (hospital, clinic, outpatient center) where this allergy was documented. Supports multi-facility enterprise reporting and population health analytics.",
clinical,preventive_health,allergy,demographics_id,demographics_id,Patient ID,BIGINT,,patient.demographics.demographics_id,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_health",,master_data,Reference to the patient for whom this allergy or adverse reaction is documented. Links to the patient master record in the Patient domain.,
clinical,preventive_health,allergy,laboratory_test_result_id,laboratory_test_result_id,Confirmatory Test Result Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,laboratory.laboratory_test_result.laboratory_test_result_id,,,master_data,"Foreign key linking to laboratory.test_result. Business justification: Drug/food allergies confirmed via lab testing (specific IgE panels, tryptase levels). Role prefix confirmatory_ indicates diagnostic purpose. Important for allergy verification and de-labeling initi",
clinical,preventive_health,allergy,material_master_id,material_master_id,Material Master Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,supply.material_master.material_master_id,,,master_data,"Foreign key linking to supply.material_master. Business justification: Drug/material allergies prevent ordering of specific supplies/medications. Enables allergy-based supply contraindication checking, patient safety alerts, and formulary restriction enforcement in CPOE ",
clinical,preventive_health,allergy,ndc_drug_id,ndc_drug_id,Ndc Code Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,reference.ndc_drug.ndc_drug_id,,,master_data,"Foreign key linking to reference.ndc_drug. Business justification: Drug allergy identification for medication reconciliation, e-prescribing safety checks, and formulary management. Pharmacy systems use NDC codes to link allergies to specific drug products and active ",
clinical,preventive_health,allergy,primary_allergy_clinician_id,primary_allergy_clinician_id,Documenting Provider ID,BIGINT,,provider.clinician.clinician_id,,,master_data,"Reference to the clinician (physician, nurse, pharmacist) who documented or entered this allergy record into the Electronic Health Record (EHR). Supports audit and Clinical Documentation Improvement (CDI) workflows.",
clinical,preventive_health,allergy,snomed_concept_id,snomed_concept_id,Allergen Snomed Code Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,reference.snomed_concept.snomed_concept_id,,,master_data,"Foreign key linking to reference.snomed_concept. Business justification: Allergen standardization for clinical decision support, drug-allergy interaction checking, and allergy reconciliation across care settings. Pharmacy and clinical systems use SNOMED allergen codes to t",
clinical,preventive_health,allergy,visit_id,visit_id,Encounter ID,BIGINT,,encounter.visit.visit_id,,,master_data,Reference to the clinical encounter during which this allergy was first documented or most recently updated. May be null if the allergy was entered outside of a specific encounter context.,
clinical,preventive_health,allergy,alert_override_reason,alert_override_reason,Allergy Alert Override Reason,STRING,,,,,master_data,Clinical justification documented when a provider overrides a drug allergy alert during Computerized Physician Order Entry (CPOE). Required for regulatory compliance and medication safety audits. Null if no override has occurred.,
clinical,preventive_health,allergy,allergen_name,allergen_name,Allergen Name,STRING,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_health",,master_data,"pii_phi,pii_pii,pii_sensitive",
clinical,preventive_health,allergy,allergen_type,allergen_type,Allergen Type,STRING,,,,,master_data,Classification of the allergen category. Drives clinical decision support rules and patient safety alerts. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: drug|food|environmental|contrast_media|latex|insect_venom|other — promote to reference product],
clinical,preventive_health,allergy,allergy_category,allergy_category,Allergy Category Type,STRING,,,,allergy|intolerance|side_effect,master_data,"Distinguishes between a true immunological allergy, a non-immunological intolerance (e.g., GI upset from NSAIDs), and a documented side effect. Critical for appropriate clinical decision support alert configuration and pharmacy dispensing rules.",
clinical,preventive_health,allergy,care_setting,care_setting,Care Setting,STRING,,,,inpatient|outpatient|emergency|ambulatory|telehealth|other,master_data,"The clinical care setting in which this allergy was documented (e.g., inpatient, outpatient, Emergency Department (ED), ambulatory). Supports population health segmentation and quality reporting.",
clinical,preventive_health,allergy,clinical_status,clinical_status,Allergy Clinical Status,STRING,,,,active|inactive|resolved,master_data,"Current clinical status of the allergy indicating whether it is currently active, has become inactive, or has been resolved. Active allergies trigger clinical decision support alerts during order entry (CPOE).",
clinical,preventive_health,allergy,consent_verification_status,consent_verification_status,Allergy Verification Status,STRING,,,,confirmed|unconfirmed|refuted|entered_in_error,master_data,Clinical verification status of the allergy record indicating the confidence level of the allergy documentation. Entered-in-error records are retained for audit purposes per Health Information Management (HIM) standards.,
clinical,preventive_health,allergy,criticality,criticality,Allergy Criticality,STRING,,,,low|high|unable_to_assess,master_data,Assessment of the potential clinical risk if the patient is re-exposed to the allergen. High indicates risk of life-threatening reaction. Distinct from severity (which describes the past reaction); criticality predicts future risk. Aligns with HL7 FHIR AllergyIntolerance.criticality.,
clinical,preventive_health,allergy,data_quality_flag,data_quality_flag,Data Quality Flag,STRING,,,,clean|suspect|duplicate|incomplete,master_data,Indicates the data quality assessment status of this allergy record as determined during ETL processing into the Silver Layer. Supports data stewardship workflows and Clinical Documentation Improvement (CDI) initiatives.,
clinical,preventive_health,allergy,deleted_timestamp,deleted_timestamp,Record Deletion Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,master_data,The date and timestamp when this allergy record was soft-deleted in the source EHR system. Null if the record has not been deleted. Supports audit trail requirements under HIPAA and HIM standards.,
clinical,preventive_health,allergy,fhir_resource_reference,fhir_resource_reference,HL7 FHIR Resource ID,STRING,,,,,master_data,"The HL7 Fast Healthcare Interoperability Resources (FHIR) AllergyIntolerance resource identifier. Enables interoperability with Health Information Exchanges (HIE), patient portals, and external clinical systems via FHIR APIs.",
clinical,preventive_health,allergy,information_source,information_source,Allergy Information Source,STRING,,,,patient|caregiver|provider|medical_record|pharmacy|other,master_data,"Identifies who provided the allergy information (e.g., patient self-report, caregiver, prior medical record, pharmacy records). Affects the confidence level and verification workflow for the allergy record.",
clinical,preventive_health,allergy,is_deleted,is_deleted,Soft Delete Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,Indicates whether this allergy record has been soft-deleted in the source EHR system. Soft-deleted records are retained in the Silver Layer for audit and Health Information Management (HIM) compliance purposes rather than being physically removed.,
clinical,preventive_health,allergy,is_no_known_allergy,is_no_known_allergy,No Known Allergy (NKA) Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,"Indicates that the patient has been explicitly assessed and confirmed to have No Known Allergies (NKA). Distinct from an empty allergy list, which may indicate incomplete documentation. Critical for patient safety and Joint Commission compliance.",
clinical,preventive_health,allergy,is_no_known_drug_allergy,is_no_known_drug_allergy,No Known Drug Allergy (NKDA) Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,Indicates that the patient has been explicitly assessed and confirmed to have No Known Drug Allergies (NKDA). Specifically scoped to drug allergens to support pharmacy safety checks and CPOE alert configuration.,
clinical,preventive_health,allergy,last_updated_timestamp,last_updated_timestamp,Allergy Last Updated Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,master_data,The date and timestamp when this allergy record was most recently modified in the source EHR system. Supports change detection in ETL pipelines and audit compliance.,
clinical,preventive_health,allergy,mrn,mrn,Medical Record Number (MRN),STRING,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_identifier",,master_data,The Medical Record Number (MRN) assigned to the patient by the facilitys Master Patient Index (MPI). Included here as a denormalized identifier to support direct patient safety lookups without joining to the patient master.,
clinical,preventive_health,allergy,ndf_rt_code,ndf_rt_code,National Drug File Reference Terminology (NDF-RT) Code,STRING,,,,,master_data,"The National Drug File – Reference Terminology (NDF-RT) code for drug allergens, enabling pharmacological class-level allergy checking (e.g., all penicillin-class antibiotics). Used in drug allergy cross-sensitivity analysis.",
clinical,preventive_health,allergy,note,note,Allergy Clinical Note,STRING,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_health",,master_data,"Free-text clinical notes or additional comments documented by the clinician regarding this allergy record (e.g., details about the reaction, treatment administered, cross-sensitivity concerns). Supports Clinical Documentation Improvement (CDI) workflows.",
clinical,preventive_health,allergy,onset_date,onset_date,Allergy Onset Date,DATE,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_health",,master_data,The date on which the allergic reaction was first observed or reported by the patient. May be approximate (year only) for historical allergies. Supports longitudinal patient safety tracking.,
clinical,preventive_health,allergy,override_timestamp,override_timestamp,Alert Override Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,master_data,Date and time when the allergy alert was overridden by the provider during CPOE. Supports medication safety audit trails. Null if no override has occurred.,
clinical,preventive_health,allergy,phi_access_restricted,phi_access_restricted,Protected Health Information (PHI) Access Restricted Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,"Indicates whether access to this allergy record is subject to additional Protected Health Information (PHI) access restrictions (e.g., VIP patient, sensitive condition). When true, row-level security controls are applied per HIPAA Privacy Rule requirements.",
clinical,preventive_health,allergy,reaction_description,reaction_description,Reaction Description,STRING,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_health",,master_data,"Free-text clinical description of the adverse reaction observed or reported by the patient (e.g., hives and facial swelling, anaphylactic shock requiring epinephrine). Captured from clinical documentation in Epic ClinDoc or Cerner PowerChart.",
clinical,preventive_health,allergy,reaction_route,reaction_route,Reaction Exposure Route,STRING,,,,,master_data,"The route of exposure through which the allergic reaction occurred (e.g., oral ingestion, intravenous administration, topical contact). Informs clinical decision support rules for route-specific allergy alerts. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: oral|intravenous|topical|inhalation|subcutaneous|intramuscular|other — promote to reference product]",
clinical,preventive_health,allergy,reaction_snomed_code,reaction_snomed_code,Reaction SNOMED CT Code,STRING,,,,"^[0-9]{6,18}$",master_data,"The SNOMED CT concept code representing the clinical manifestation of the allergic reaction (e.g., urticaria, anaphylaxis, angioedema). Enables structured clinical reporting and interoperability via HL7 FHIR.",
clinical,preventive_health,allergy,reconciliation_date,reconciliation_date,Allergy Reconciliation Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,The date on which this allergy record was last reviewed and reconciled as part of a medication reconciliation process. Supports compliance with The Joint Commission NPSG.03.06.01 and CMS discharge planning requirements.,
clinical,preventive_health,allergy,reconciliation_status,reconciliation_status,Allergy Reconciliation Status,STRING,,,,reconciled|not_reconciled|pending,master_data,"Indicates whether this allergy has been reviewed and reconciled during a medication reconciliation process (e.g., at admission, discharge, or care transitions). Supports Transitions of Care compliance and The Joint Commission NPSG requirements.",
clinical,preventive_health,allergy,recorded_date,recorded_date,Allergy Recorded Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,master_data,The date and timestamp when this allergy record was first entered into the Electronic Health Record (EHR) system. Represents the RECORD_AUDIT_CREATED canonical category for this entity. Used for audit trails and Clinical Documentation Improvement (CDI) workflows.,
clinical,preventive_health,allergy,severity,severity,Reaction Severity,STRING,,,,mild|moderate|severe|life_threatening,master_data,Clinical severity classification of the allergic reaction. Drives clinical decision support alert levels and patient safety protocols. Values align with HL7 FHIR AllergyIntolerance severity coding.,
clinical,preventive_health,allergy,source_system,source_system,Source System,STRING,,,,epic|cerner|meditech|manual|other,master_data,"Identifies the operational system of record from which this allergy record was sourced (e.g., Epic EHR, Cerner Millennium, MEDITECH Expanse). Supports data lineage tracking and multi-system reconciliation in the lakehouse.",
clinical,preventive_health,allergy,source_system_allergy_code,source_system_allergy_code,Source System Allergy ID,STRING,,,,,master_data,"The native identifier for this allergy record in the originating operational system (e.g., Epic allergy ID, Cerner allergy ID). Enables traceability back to the system of record for reconciliation and audit.",
clinical,preventive_health,functional_status,functional_status_id,functional_status_id,Functional Status Assessment ID,BIGINT,Y,,,,transactional_data,Unique surrogate identifier for each functional status assessment record in the clinical data product. Primary key for the functional_status table in the Databricks Silver Layer.,
clinical,preventive_health,functional_status,care_plan_id,care_plan_id,Care Plan Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,clinical.care_plan.care_plan_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to clinical.care_plan. Business justification: Functional status assessments (ADL, IADL, mobility, cognitive assessments) directly inform care plan creation and updates. Linking functional_status.care_plan_id → care_plan.care_plan_id establishes t",
clinical,preventive_health,functional_status,consent_record_id,consent_record_id,Consent Record Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,consent.consent_consent_record.consent_record_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to consent.consent_record. Business justification: Functional assessments (SDOH screenings, mental health assessments, substance use screenings) require consent for data collection and sharing. CMS quality programs and state SDOH initiatives mandate c",
clinical,preventive_health,functional_status,demographics_id,demographics_id,Patient ID,BIGINT,,patient.demographics.demographics_id,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_health",,transactional_data,Reference to the patient for whom this functional status assessment was performed. Links to the master patient record in the Patient domain.,
clinical,preventive_health,functional_status,icd_code_id,icd_code_id,Icd10 Code Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,reference.icd_code.icd_code_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to reference.icd_code. Business justification: Functional impairment diagnosis coding for HCC risk adjustment, disability determination, and post-acute care reimbursement. Coding and case management teams use ICD-10 codes for functional impairment",
clinical,preventive_health,functional_status,laboratory_test_result_id,laboratory_test_result_id,Supporting Test Result Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,laboratory.laboratory_test_result.laboratory_test_result_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to laboratory.test_result. Business justification: Functional assessments incorporate lab data (albumin for nutritional status, hemoglobin for fatigue). Role prefix supporting_ indicates assessment basis. Important for rehabilitation planning and di",
clinical,preventive_health,functional_status,loinc_code_id,loinc_code_id,Loinc Code Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,reference.loinc_code.loinc_code_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to reference.loinc_code. Business justification: Functional assessment standardization for post-acute care planning, IRF/SNF admission criteria, and quality measure reporting. Case management and therapy teams use LOINC codes for functional assessme",
clinical,preventive_health,functional_status,material_master_id,material_master_id,Material Master Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,supply.material_master.material_master_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to supply.material_master. Business justification: Functional assessments drive DME orders (ADL scores → assistive devices, mobility scores → wheelchairs). Enables functional assessment-based DME provisioning, discharge planning, and post-acute care s",
clinical,preventive_health,functional_status,medication_therapy_mgmt_id,medication_therapy_mgmt_id,Medication Therapy Mgmt Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,pharmacy.medication_therapy_mgmt.medication_therapy_mgmt_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to pharmacy.medication_therapy_mgmt. Business justification: Functional assessments (ADL scores, fall risk, cognitive status) inform MTM interventions for medication optimization in elderly and complex patients. Required for comprehensive medication reviews and",
clinical,preventive_health,functional_status,primary_functional_clinician_id,primary_functional_clinician_id,Assessing Clinician ID,BIGINT,,provider.clinician.clinician_id,,,transactional_data,"Reference to the licensed clinician (nurse, therapist, physician, social worker) who performed and documented the functional status assessment. Supports accountability and care team attribution.",
clinical,preventive_health,functional_status,prom_response_id,prom_response_id,Prom Response Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,digital_health.prom_response.prom_response_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to digital_health.prom_response. Business justification: Functional status assessments (PHQ-9, PROMIS scores) are derived from patient-reported outcome measure responses. CMS quality reporting and value-based care programs require linking the clinical asses",Internal - LLM Generated Cross-Domain Link
clinical,preventive_health,functional_status,quality_measure_id,quality_measure_id,Quality Measure Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,quality.measure.measure_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to quality.measure. Business justification: Functional status measures (ADL assessment post-discharge, functional improvement) require functional assessment data. Essential for post-acute care quality reporting and rehabilitation program evalua",
clinical,preventive_health,functional_status,snomed_concept_id,snomed_concept_id,Snomed Code Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,reference.snomed_concept.snomed_concept_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to reference.snomed_concept. Business justification: Functional status coding for care planning, rehabilitation goal setting, and outcome tracking. Therapy and care coordination teams use SNOMED codes to document functional limitations and track improve",
clinical,preventive_health,functional_status,visit_id,visit_id,Encounter ID,BIGINT,,encounter.visit.visit_id,,,transactional_data,"Reference to the clinical encounter (inpatient admission, outpatient visit, ED visit) during which this functional status assessment was conducted. Supports contextualizing assessment within care episode.",
clinical,preventive_health,functional_status,adl_score,adl_score,Activities of Daily Living (ADL) Score,"DECIMAL(5,2)",,,,,transactional_data,"Sub-score measuring the patients ability to perform basic Activities of Daily Living (ADL) including bathing, dressing, grooming, toileting, transferring, and feeding. Core component of Barthel Index, Katz ADL, and FIM assessments.",
clinical,preventive_health,functional_status,advance_directive_on_file,advance_directive_on_file,Advance Directive on File,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,"Indicates whether a valid advance directive (living will, healthcare proxy, POLST/MOLST) is documented in the patients medical record. Required documentation element under the Patient Self-Determination Act and CMS Conditions of Participation.",
clinical,preventive_health,functional_status,assessing_discipline,assessing_discipline,Assessing Clinical Discipline,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Clinical discipline of the licensed professional who performed the functional status assessment. Determines scope of practice, assessment tool applicability, and care plan ownership. Required for interdisciplinary team documentation. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: nursing|physical_therapy|occupational_therapy|speech_therapy|social_work|physician|psychology — 7 candidates stripped; promote to reference product]",
clinical,preventive_health,functional_status,assessment_date,assessment_date,Assessment Date,DATE,,,,,transactional_data,Calendar date on which the functional status assessment was administered to the patient. Used for trending functional decline or improvement over time and for discharge planning timelines.,
clinical,preventive_health,functional_status,assessment_duration_minutes,assessment_duration_minutes,Assessment Duration (Minutes),INT,,,,,transactional_data,"Total time in minutes required to complete the functional status assessment. Used for therapy billing (timed CPT codes), productivity reporting, and staffing analysis. Required for Medicare Part B therapy billing documentation.",
clinical,preventive_health,functional_status,assessment_location,assessment_location,Assessment Location,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Physical or virtual location where the functional status assessment was conducted (e.g., bedside, therapy gym, outpatient clinic, telehealth). Supports operational reporting and care setting analytics.",
clinical,preventive_health,functional_status,assessment_status,assessment_status,Assessment Status,STRING,,,,completed|in_progress|cancelled|amended|entered_in_error,transactional_data,"Current workflow status of the functional status assessment record. Completed indicates a finalized, signed assessment; amended indicates a correction was made post-completion; entered_in_error supports clinical data quality management.",
clinical,preventive_health,functional_status,assessment_timestamp,assessment_timestamp,Assessment Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,Precise date and time at which the functional status assessment was completed and documented in the EHR. Supports clinical workflow sequencing and audit trail requirements.,
clinical,preventive_health,functional_status,assessment_tool,assessment_tool,Functional Assessment Tool,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Standardized clinical instrument used to evaluate the patients functional status. Common tools include Barthel Index, Functional Independence Measure (FIM), PHQ-9 (depression), CAGE-AID (substance use), Katz ADL Scale, Lawton IADL Scale, Mini-Mental State Examination (MMSE), Montreal Cognitive Assessment (MoCA), and SDOH screening tools. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: Barthel Index|FIM|PHQ-9|CAGE-AID|Katz ADL|Lawton IADL|MMSE|MoCA|SDOH Screening|Berg Balance Scale|Braden Scale|Morse Fall Scale — promote to reference product]",
clinical,preventive_health,functional_status,assessment_type,assessment_type,Assessment Type,STRING,,,,admission|discharge|interim|annual|follow_up|referral,transactional_data,Classification of when in the care continuum the assessment was performed. Admission assessments establish baseline; discharge assessments support post-acute placement; interim assessments track progress; annual assessments support population health programs.,
clinical,preventive_health,functional_status,cage_aid_score,cage_aid_score,CAGE-AID Substance Use Screening Score,INT,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_health",,transactional_data,"Total score from the CAGE-AID (Cut down, Annoyed, Guilty, Eye-opener — Adapted to Include Drugs) substance use disorder screening tool, ranging from 0 to 4. A score of 2 or higher is considered a positive screen for alcohol or drug use disorder.",
clinical,preventive_health,functional_status,care_setting,care_setting,Care Setting,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Clinical care setting in which the functional status assessment was performed. Drives assessment tool selection, regulatory reporting requirements (MDS for SNF, OASIS for home health), and post-acute care placement decisions. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: inpatient|outpatient|ed|icu|snf|home_health|hospice|rehabilitation — 8 candidates stripped; promote to reference product]",
clinical,preventive_health,functional_status,caregiver_support_available,caregiver_support_available,Caregiver Support Available,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,"Indicates whether the patient has an identified informal caregiver (family member, friend, or unpaid caregiver) available to assist with post-discharge care needs. Critical factor in discharge planning and community care placement decisions.",
clinical,preventive_health,functional_status,clinical_notes,clinical_notes,Clinical Assessment Notes,STRING,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_health",,transactional_data,"Free-text narrative documentation by the assessing clinician providing qualitative context, clinical observations, and nuanced findings beyond the structured scoring fields. Contains Protected Health Information (PHI) and is subject to HIPAA minimum necessary standards.",
clinical,preventive_health,functional_status,cognitive_score,cognitive_score,Cognitive Function Score,"DECIMAL(5,2)",,,,,transactional_data,"Sub-score measuring cognitive function including orientation, memory, attention, language, and executive function. Derived from MMSE (0–30), MoCA (0–30), FIM cognitive subscale, or BIMS (Brief Interview for Mental Status). Supports dementia screening and care planning.",
clinical,preventive_health,functional_status,communication_status,communication_status,Communication Status,STRING,,,,intact|impaired|nonverbal|requires_interpreter|unknown,transactional_data,"Assessment of the patients ability to communicate effectively, including speech, language, hearing, and vision. Impacts assessment validity, informed consent processes, and care plan communication. Triggers speech-language pathology referrals.",
clinical,preventive_health,functional_status,created_timestamp,created_timestamp,Record Created Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,Timestamp when this functional status assessment record was first created in the source EHR system. Supports audit trail requirements under HIPAA Security Rule and data lineage tracking in the lakehouse.,
clinical,preventive_health,functional_status,discharge_disposition_recommended,discharge_disposition_recommended,Recommended Discharge Disposition,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Clinician-recommended post-discharge care setting based on functional status assessment findings. Drives discharge planning workflows, post-acute care referrals, and transitions of care coordination. Supports CMS Discharge Planning Rule compliance. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: home|home_with_services|snf|inpatient_rehab|ltach|hospice|assisted_living — 7 candidates stripped; promote to reference product]",
clinical,preventive_health,functional_status,fall_risk_level,fall_risk_level,Fall Risk Level,STRING,,,,low|moderate|high,transactional_data,"Clinician-assigned fall risk stratification based on Morse Fall Scale, Hendrich II, or equivalent validated tool. Drives fall prevention care plan interventions and is a required safety metric under TJC National Patient Safety Goals (NPSG.09.02.01).",
clinical,preventive_health,functional_status,iadl_score,iadl_score,Instrumental Activities of Daily Living (IADL) Score,"DECIMAL(5,2)",,,,,transactional_data,"Sub-score measuring the patients ability to perform Instrumental Activities of Daily Living (IADL) such as managing medications, finances, transportation, meal preparation, and housekeeping. Assessed via Lawton IADL Scale. Critical for community discharge planning.",
clinical,preventive_health,functional_status,is_baseline_assessment,is_baseline_assessment,Baseline Assessment Indicator,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,Indicates whether this assessment represents the initial baseline functional status evaluation for the patient within the current episode of care. Baseline assessments anchor longitudinal functional trajectory analysis and rehabilitation goal-setting.,
clinical,preventive_health,functional_status,mobility_score,mobility_score,Mobility Score,"DECIMAL(5,2)",,,,,transactional_data,"Sub-score quantifying the patients mobility status including ambulation, transfers, stair climbing, and wheelchair use. Derived from FIM motor subscale, Barthel mobility items, or Berg Balance Scale. Informs physical therapy referrals and fall risk management.",
clinical,preventive_health,functional_status,mobility_status,mobility_status,Mobility Status,STRING,,,,independent|supervision|limited_assistance|extensive_assistance|total_dependence|activity_did_not_occur,transactional_data,"Categorical classification of the patients overall mobility level using CMS MDS-aligned coding. Supports post-acute care placement criteria, physical therapy orders, and fall prevention protocols.",
clinical,preventive_health,functional_status,mrn,mrn,Medical Record Number (MRN),STRING,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_identifier",,transactional_data,"pii_phi,pii_pii,pii_sensitive",
clinical,preventive_health,functional_status,nutritional_status,nutritional_status,Nutritional Status,STRING,,,,adequate|at_risk|malnourished|unknown,transactional_data,"Clinician-assessed nutritional status of the patient as determined during functional assessment. Malnutrition directly impacts functional recovery, wound healing, and rehabilitation outcomes. Supports dietitian referrals and care plan development.",
clinical,preventive_health,functional_status,pain_level,pain_level,Pain Level Score,INT,,,,,transactional_data,"Patient-reported pain intensity score on a standardized numeric rating scale (NRS 0–10) or equivalent validated tool (Wong-Baker FACES, FLACC). Functional pain assessment is integral to ADL performance and mobility evaluation. Required by TJC pain management standards.",
clinical,preventive_health,functional_status,phq9_score,phq9_score,Patient Health Questionnaire-9 (PHQ-9) Score,INT,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_health",,transactional_data,"Total score from the Patient Health Questionnaire-9 (PHQ-9) depression screening tool, ranging from 0 to 27. Scores of 5, 10, 15, and 20 represent mild, moderate, moderately severe, and severe depression thresholds respectively. Required for HEDIS MDD measures and CMS quality reporting.",
clinical,preventive_health,functional_status,pressure_injury_risk,pressure_injury_risk,Pressure Injury Risk Level,STRING,,,,no_risk|at_risk|high_risk|very_high_risk,transactional_data,Risk stratification for pressure injury (decubitus ulcer) development based on Braden Scale or Norton Scale score. Supports wound prevention care planning and is tracked as a Hospital-Acquired Condition (HAC) under CMS quality programs.,
clinical,preventive_health,functional_status,prior_level_of_function,prior_level_of_function,Prior Level of Function (PLOF),STRING,,,,independent|modified_independent|supervised|assisted|dependent|unknown,transactional_data,"Patients functional status prior to the current illness, injury, or hospitalization as reported by patient, family, or prior care records. Establishes rehabilitation goals and discharge planning targets. Standard component of physical and occupational therapy evaluations.",
clinical,preventive_health,functional_status,rehabilitation_potential,rehabilitation_potential,Rehabilitation Potential,STRING,,,,good|fair|poor|not_applicable,transactional_data,"Clinicians assessment of the patients potential to improve functional status through rehabilitation services. Influences therapy authorization, post-acute care placement, and Medicare skilled care eligibility determinations.",
clinical,preventive_health,functional_status,score_interpretation,score_interpretation,Score Interpretation,STRING,,,,normal|mild_impairment|moderate_impairment|severe_impairment|total_dependence,transactional_data,"Clinically validated categorical interpretation of the total assessment score based on the tools published scoring bands. Supports rapid clinical triage, care plan development, and post-acute care placement decisions.",
clinical,preventive_health,functional_status,sdoh_domain_flags,sdoh_domain_flags,Social Determinants of Health (SDOH) Domain Flags,STRING,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_health",,transactional_data,"Pipe-delimited list of specific SDOH domains where unmet needs were identified (e.g., food_insecurity|housing_instability|transportation). Supports targeted community resource referrals and population health stratification under CMS SDOH initiatives.",
clinical,preventive_health,functional_status,sdoh_screening_result,sdoh_screening_result,Social Determinants of Health (SDOH) Screening Result,STRING,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_health",no_needs_identified|needs_identified|patient_declined|not_screened,transactional_data,"Overall result of the Social Determinants of Health (SDOH) screening indicating whether unmet social needs (food insecurity, housing instability, transportation barriers, financial strain, social isolation) were identified. Supports population health management and care coordination referrals.",
clinical,preventive_health,functional_status,source_system,source_system,Source System,STRING,,,,epic_clindoc|cerner_powerchart|meditech_expanse|manual_entry,transactional_data,"Operational system of record from which this functional status assessment record was sourced. Supports data lineage tracking, ETL audit, and multi-system reconciliation in the Databricks Silver Layer.",
clinical,preventive_health,functional_status,source_system_record_code,source_system_record_code,Source System Record ID,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Native record identifier from the originating operational system (e.g., Epic ClinDoc SmartForm instance ID, Cerner PowerChart assessment ID). Enables traceability from the Silver Layer back to the source EHR record for data quality investigations.",
clinical,preventive_health,functional_status,total_score,total_score,Total Assessment Score,"DECIMAL(6,2)",,,,,transactional_data,"Composite numeric score derived from the assessment tools scoring algorithm. Score range and interpretation vary by tool (e.g., Barthel Index 0–100; PHQ-9 0–27; FIM 18–126). Used for clinical decision-making, discharge planning, and population health stratification.",
clinical,preventive_health,functional_status,updated_timestamp,updated_timestamp,Record Updated Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,"Timestamp of the most recent modification to this functional status assessment record, including amendments, corrections, or status changes. Required for change data capture (CDC) processing in the Silver Layer ETL pipeline.",
clinical,preventive_health,hai_event,hai_event_id,hai_event_id,Healthcare-Associated Infection (HAI) Event ID,BIGINT,Y,,,,transactional_data,Unique surrogate identifier for each Healthcare-Associated Infection (HAI) surveillance event record in the silver layer lakehouse. Primary key for this entity.,
clinical,preventive_health,hai_event,bed_id,bed_id,Bed Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,facility.bed.bed_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to facility.bed. Business justification: Hospital-acquired infections (CLABSI, CAUTI, SSI) are attributed to specific bed locations for infection control surveillance, outbreak investigation, unit-level infection rate tracking, and NHSN repo",
clinical,preventive_health,hai_event,care_site_id,care_site_id,Facility ID,BIGINT,,facility.care_site.care_site_id,,,transactional_data,"Reference to the healthcare facility (hospital, campus, or care site) where the HAI event occurred. Required for facility-level NHSN reporting and CMS Value-Based Purchasing (VBP) penalty calculations.",
clinical,preventive_health,hai_event,clinical_ai_patient_risk_score_id,clinical_ai_patient_risk_score_id,Predicted Risk Score Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,clinical_ai.clinical_ai_patient_risk_score.clinical_ai_patient_risk_score_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to clinical_ai.patient_risk_score. Business justification: HAI prediction model validation requires linking actual infection events to prior risk predictions. Enables model performance monitoring, calibration assessment, and infection prevention program evalu",Internal - LLM Generated Cross-Domain Link
clinical,preventive_health,hai_event,clinical_order_id,clinical_order_id,Response Clinical Order Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,order.clinical_order.clinical_order_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to order.clinical_order. Business justification: HAI events trigger response orders. Real workflow: CLABSI identified, orders placed for line removal and antibiotics. Essential for infection control tracking, HAI response protocol compliance, NHSN r",
clinical,preventive_health,hai_event,clinician_id,clinician_id,Infection Preventionist ID,BIGINT,,provider.clinician.clinician_id,,,transactional_data,"Reference to the infection preventionist (IP) clinician responsible for reviewing, confirming, and submitting this HAI event to NHSN. Required for audit trail and regulatory accountability.",
clinical,preventive_health,hai_event,corrective_action_id,corrective_action_id,Corrective Action Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,quality.corrective_action.corrective_action_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to quality.corrective_action. Business justification: HAI events trigger corrective actions (process improvements, staff education). Direct linkage enables tracking corrective action effectiveness. Essential for infection prevention quality improvement a",
clinical,preventive_health,hai_event,cost_center_id,cost_center_id,Cost Center Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,finance.cost_center.cost_center_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to finance.cost_center. Business justification: HAI events trigger VBP penalties and increased treatment costs. Finance tracks HAI-related costs by department/cost center for penalty attribution, cost containment initiatives, and quality program RO",
clinical,preventive_health,hai_event,diagnosis_id,diagnosis_id,Diagnosis Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,clinical.diagnosis.diagnosis_id,"restricted,pii_health",,transactional_data,Foreign key linking to clinical.diagnosis. Business justification: Healthcare-Associated Infection (HAI) surveillance events result in infection diagnoses being documented in the patient record. Linking hai_event.diagnosis_id → diagnosis.diagnosis_id connects the inf,
clinical,preventive_health,hai_event,imaging_order_id,imaging_order_id,Imaging Order Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,radiology.imaging_order.imaging_order_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to radiology.imaging_order. Business justification: Healthcare-associated infections require imaging to assess extent/complications (CLABSI with endocarditis, VAP with infiltrate). Required for infection control investigations and HAC penalty avoidance",
clinical,preventive_health,hai_event,improvement_initiative_id,improvement_initiative_id,Improvement Initiative Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,quality.improvement_initiative.improvement_initiative_id,,,transactional_data,Foreign key linking to quality.improvement_initiative. Business justification: HAI reduction is a primary quality improvement focus. Initiatives link to specific HAI events for root cause analysis and intervention tracking. Essential for infection prevention quality improvement ,
clinical,preventive_health,hai_event,interoperability_public_health_report_id,interoperability_public_health_report_id,,BIGINT,,interoperability.public_health_report.public_health_report_id,"restricted,pii",,transactional_data,FK to interoperability.public_health_report.public_health_report_id,
clinical,preventive_health,hai_event,linked_procedure_procedure_event_id,linked_procedure_procedure_event_id,Linked Procedure ID,BIGINT,,clinical.procedure_event.procedure_event_id,,,transactional_data,"Reference to the surgical or invasive procedure associated with this HAI event. Mandatory for Surgical Site Infection (SSI) events per NHSN SSI protocol; nullable for device-associated infections (CLABSI, CAUTI, VAP).",
clinical,preventive_health,hai_event,material_master_id,material_master_id,Material Master Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,supply.material_master.material_master_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to supply.material_master. Business justification: HAIs linked to specific devices/supplies for root cause analysis, NHSN reporting, and regulatory compliance. Enables infection control supply tracking, device-associated infection surveillance, and qu",
clinical,preventive_health,hai_event,microbiology_culture_id,microbiology_culture_id,Diagnostic Culture Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,laboratory.microbiology_culture.microbiology_culture_id,,,transactional_data,Foreign key linking to laboratory.microbiology_culture. Business justification: HAI events identified/confirmed by positive cultures - infection control core process. Role prefix diagnostic_ indicates event confirmation. Required for NHSN reporting and outbreak investigation. R,
clinical,preventive_health,hai_event,mpi_record_id,mpi_record_id,Patient ID,BIGINT,,patient.mpi_record.mpi_record_id,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_health",,transactional_data,Reference to the patient who experienced the Healthcare-Associated Infection (HAI) event. Links to the master patient record for demographic and clinical context.,
clinical,preventive_health,hai_event,outbreak_id,outbreak_id,Outbreak Investigation ID,BIGINT,,clinical.outbreak.outbreak_id,,,transactional_data,Identifier linking this HAI event to a specific outbreak investigation record when outbreak_flag is True. Enables grouping of related HAI events for epidemiological analysis and root cause investigation.,
clinical,preventive_health,hai_event,patient_safety_event_id,patient_safety_event_id,Patient Safety Event Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,quality.patient_safety_event.patient_safety_event_id,,,transactional_data,Foreign key linking to quality.patient_safety_event. Business justification: HAI events are a subset of patient safety events. Many organizations track HAIs within their safety event system for unified reporting and root cause analysis. Essential for integrated safety reportin,
clinical,preventive_health,hai_event,susceptibility_result_id,susceptibility_result_id,Susceptibility Result Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,laboratory.susceptibility_result.susceptibility_result_id,,,transactional_data,Foreign key linking to laboratory.susceptibility_result. Business justification: Antibiotic selection for HAI treatment based on susceptibility results. Essential for antibiotic stewardship and MDRO tracking. Removes denormalized resistance profile data in favor of proper FK relat,
clinical,preventive_health,hai_event,treatment_drug_master_id,treatment_drug_master_id,Treatment Drug Master Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,pharmacy.drug_master.drug_master_id,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii",,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to pharmacy.drug_master. Business justification: Healthcare-acquired infections treated with specific antimicrobials. Antibiotic stewardship programs track drug-bug relationships, resistance patterns, and treatment outcomes. Required for NHSN report",
clinical,preventive_health,hai_event,visit_id,visit_id,Encounter ID,BIGINT,,encounter.visit.visit_id,,,transactional_data,"Reference to the inpatient encounter during which the HAI event was identified. Used to correlate infection events with admission, discharge, and clinical documentation.",
clinical,preventive_health,hai_event,attributed_los_days,attributed_los_days,Attributed Length of Stay (LOS) Days,INT,,,,,transactional_data,"Number of additional inpatient days clinically attributed to this HAI event beyond the expected Length of Stay (LOS). Used for cost-of-infection analysis, quality improvement, and VBP impact assessments. Distinct from total encounter LOS.",
clinical,preventive_health,hai_event,consent_event_date,consent_event_date,HAI Event Date,DATE,,,,,transactional_data,"The date on which the Healthcare-Associated Infection (HAI) event was identified or the infection onset date as defined by NHSN criteria. This is the principal real-world event date used for NHSN reporting, rate calculations, and CMS submission windows.",
clinical,preventive_health,hai_event,consent_event_status,consent_event_status,HAI Event Status,STRING,,,,pending_review|confirmed|rejected|submitted|amended,transactional_data,"Current workflow lifecycle status of the HAI event record. Tracks progression from initial identification through infection preventionist review, NHSN submission, and any subsequent amendments. Drives quality and compliance dashboards.",
clinical,preventive_health,hai_event,created_timestamp,created_timestamp,Record Created Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,"Timestamp when this HAI event record was first created in the system of record or ingested into the lakehouse silver layer. Supports audit trail, data lineage, and NHSN submission timeliness tracking.",
clinical,preventive_health,hai_event,device_days,device_days,Device Days,INT,,,,,transactional_data,"Total number of device-days (central line days, catheter days, or ventilator days) for the patient during the relevant surveillance period. Used as the denominator in NHSN device-associated infection rate calculations (infections per 1,000 device days).",
clinical,preventive_health,hai_event,device_type,device_type,Invasive Device Type,STRING,,,,central_line|urinary_catheter|ventilator|none|other,transactional_data,"Type of invasive device associated with the HAI event. Applicable for device-associated infections: central line (CLABSI), urinary catheter (CAUTI), mechanical ventilator (VAP). Set to none for non-device-associated infections such as SSI, MRSA bacteremia, or CDI.",
clinical,preventive_health,hai_event,hac_flag,hac_flag,Hospital-Acquired Condition (HAC) Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,"Indicates whether this HAI event qualifies as a Hospital-Acquired Condition (HAC) under CMS payment policy, potentially triggering a payment reduction or penalty. True = qualifies as HAC; False = does not meet HAC criteria.",
clinical,preventive_health,hai_event,infection_onset_setting,infection_onset_setting,Infection Onset Setting,STRING,,,,inpatient|outpatient|community|ltcf|unknown,transactional_data,"Clinical setting in which the infection is determined to have originated: inpatient (hospital-acquired), outpatient, community-acquired, long-term care facility (LTCF), or unknown. Supports NHSN attribution rules and population health analysis.",
clinical,preventive_health,hai_event,infection_type,infection_type,Healthcare-Associated Infection (HAI) Type,STRING,,,,CLABSI|CAUTI|SSI|MRSA|CDI|VAP,transactional_data,"Classification of the HAI event per NHSN definitions: Central Line-Associated Bloodstream Infection (CLABSI), Catheter-Associated Urinary Tract Infection (CAUTI), Surgical Site Infection (SSI), Methicillin-Resistant Staphylococcus aureus (MRSA) bacteremia, Clostridioides difficile Infection (CDI), or Ventilator-Associated Pneumonia (VAP). Drives NHSN module routing and CMS VBP penalty calculations.",
clinical,preventive_health,hai_event,ip_review_date,ip_review_date,Infection Preventionist (IP) Review Date,DATE,,,,,transactional_data,"Date on which the infection preventionist completed their clinical review of this HAI event. Used for workflow tracking, timeliness metrics, and audit trail documentation.",
clinical,preventive_health,hai_event,ip_review_notes,ip_review_notes,Infection Preventionist (IP) Review Notes,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Free-text clinical notes entered by the infection preventionist during review of this HAI event. May include rationale for confirmation, rejection, or amendment of the event classification. Supports CDI and quality review workflows.",
clinical,preventive_health,hai_event,ip_review_status,ip_review_status,Infection Preventionist (IP) Review Status,STRING,,,,not_reviewed|in_review|reviewed|approved|disputed,transactional_data,"Status of the infection preventionists clinical review of this HAI event. Tracks whether the IP has reviewed, approved, or disputed the event classification prior to NHSN submission. Required for regulatory audit trails.",
clinical,preventive_health,hai_event,last_updated_timestamp,last_updated_timestamp,Record Last Updated Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,"Timestamp of the most recent modification to this HAI event record, including status changes, IP review updates, NHSN submission updates, or clinical amendments. Required for change data capture (CDC) and audit compliance.",
clinical,preventive_health,hai_event,mrn,mrn,Medical Record Number (MRN),STRING,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_identifier",,transactional_data,Medical Record Number (MRN) of the patient associated with this HAI event. Denormalized from the patient record to support infection surveillance workflows and NHSN submission without requiring a join.,
clinical,preventive_health,hai_event,nhsn_definition_met,nhsn_definition_met,National Healthcare Safety Network (NHSN) Definition Criteria Met,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,Indicates whether this event meets the CDC NHSN surveillance definition criteria for the specified infection type. True = confirmed HAI per NHSN criteria; False = under review or criteria not fully met. Determines reportability to CMS and state health departments.,
clinical,preventive_health,hai_event,nhsn_event_number,nhsn_event_number,National Healthcare Safety Network (NHSN) Event Number,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Unique event number assigned by the CDC National Healthcare Safety Network (NHSN) upon submission of this HAI event. Used for regulatory tracking, CMS reporting reconciliation, and state mandatory reporting.",
clinical,preventive_health,hai_event,nhsn_procedure_code,nhsn_procedure_code,National Healthcare Safety Network (NHSN) Procedure Code,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"NHSN-specific procedure category code for the operative procedure linked to an SSI event (e.g., COLO for colon surgery, HPRO for hip prosthesis). Distinct from CPT codes; used specifically for NHSN SSI risk index calculation and benchmarking.",
clinical,preventive_health,hai_event,nhsn_reporting_status,nhsn_reporting_status,National Healthcare Safety Network (NHSN) Reporting Status,STRING,,,,not_reported|reported|accepted|rejected_by_nhsn,transactional_data,"Indicates the submission and acceptance status of this HAI event with the CDC National Healthcare Safety Network (NHSN). Tracks whether the event has been reported, accepted, or rejected by NHSN. Critical for CMS HAI reporting compliance and VBP penalty avoidance.",
clinical,preventive_health,hai_event,nhsn_submission_date,nhsn_submission_date,National Healthcare Safety Network (NHSN) Submission Date,DATE,,,,,transactional_data,Date on which this HAI event was submitted to the CDC National Healthcare Safety Network (NHSN). Used to verify timely reporting compliance with CMS and state mandatory reporting deadlines.,
clinical,preventive_health,hai_event,outbreak_flag,outbreak_flag,Outbreak Association Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,Indicates whether this HAI event has been associated with a declared infection outbreak investigation at the facility. True = linked to an active or closed outbreak; False = sporadic/isolated event. Supports epidemiological cluster analysis.,
clinical,preventive_health,hai_event,patient_days,patient_days,Patient Days,INT,,,,,transactional_data,"Total number of patient-days in the unit or facility during the surveillance period associated with this HAI event. Used as the denominator for non-device-associated infection rates (e.g., CDI, MRSA per 10,000 patient days) per NHSN methodology.",
clinical,preventive_health,hai_event,patient_outcome,patient_outcome,Patient Outcome,STRING,,,,recovered|transferred|expired|unknown,transactional_data,"Clinical outcome of the patient attributed to or associated with this HAI event: recovered, transferred to higher level of care, expired, or unknown. Used for mortality analysis, quality reporting, and NHSN outcome tracking.",
clinical,preventive_health,hai_event,present_on_admission,present_on_admission,Present on Admission (POA) Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,Indicates whether the infection was present at the time of hospital admission (True) or developed after admission (False). HAI events by definition should be False (post-admission onset). Used for HAC (Hospital-Acquired Condition) determination and CMS payment adjustments.,
clinical,preventive_health,hai_event,secondary_infection_type,secondary_infection_type,Secondary Healthcare-Associated Infection (HAI) Type,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Secondary or co-occurring HAI type when a patient experiences more than one concurrent infection event (e.g., a patient with both CLABSI and CAUTI). Nullable; populated only when a secondary infection is clinically documented and meets NHSN criteria.",
clinical,preventive_health,hai_event,source_system,source_system,Source System,STRING,,,,Epic|Theradoc|ICNet|Cerner|MEDITECH|Manual,transactional_data,"Operational system of record from which this HAI event was sourced. Supports data lineage and ETL reconciliation. Common sources include Epic infection control modules, Theradoc, and ICNet surveillance platforms.",
clinical,preventive_health,hai_event,source_system_event_code,source_system_event_code,Source System Event ID,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Native identifier of this HAI event in the originating source system (e.g., Epic infection control record ID, Theradoc case number). Enables bidirectional traceability between the lakehouse and the system of record.",
clinical,preventive_health,hai_event,ssi_depth,ssi_depth,Surgical Site Infection (SSI) Depth,STRING,,,,superficial_incisional|deep_incisional|organ_space,transactional_data,"NHSN classification of the depth/anatomical level of the Surgical Site Infection (SSI): Superficial Incisional, Deep Incisional, or Organ/Space. Applicable only when infection_type = SSI. Determines NHSN SSI category and CMS reporting classification.",
clinical,preventive_health,hai_event,ssi_wound_class,ssi_wound_class,Surgical Site Infection (SSI) Wound Classification,STRING,,,,clean|clean_contaminated|contaminated|dirty_infected,transactional_data,"NHSN wound classification for Surgical Site Infection (SSI) events: Clean, Clean-Contaminated, Contaminated, or Dirty/Infected. Applicable only when infection_type = SSI. Used for SSI risk stratification and NHSN SSI rate calculations.",
clinical,preventive_health,hai_event,state_report_date,state_report_date,State Report Date,DATE,,,,,transactional_data,"Date on which this HAI event was reported to the state health department, when state_reportable_flag is True. Used to verify compliance with state mandatory reporting timelines.",
clinical,preventive_health,hai_event,state_reportable_flag,state_reportable_flag,State Mandatory Reporting Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,Indicates whether this HAI event is subject to mandatory reporting to the state health department under applicable state law. True = state reporting required; False = not subject to state mandatory reporting. Varies by infection type and state jurisdiction.,
clinical,preventive_health,hai_event,unit_location_code,unit_location_code,Unit Location Code,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"NHSN-mapped location code identifying the patient care unit or ward where the HAI event occurred (e.g., ICU, medical-surgical, step-down). Used for unit-level infection rate calculations, benchmarking, and targeted prevention interventions.",
clinical,preventive_health,hai_event,unit_location_description,unit_location_description,Unit Location Description,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Human-readable description of the patient care unit or ward where the HAI event occurred (e.g., Medical ICU, Surgical Step-Down Unit). Complements the NHSN location code for reporting and operational dashboards.",
clinical,preventive_health,hai_event,vbp_penalty_flag,vbp_penalty_flag,Value-Based Purchasing (VBP) Penalty Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,Indicates whether this HAI event contributes to a CMS Value-Based Purchasing (VBP) HAI domain penalty calculation for the facility. True = event is included in VBP HAI scoring; False = excluded from VBP calculation.,
clinical,preventive_health,immunization,immunization_id,immunization_id,Immunization ID,BIGINT,Y,,,,transactional_data,Unique surrogate identifier for each immunization administration record in the lakehouse silver layer. Primary key for this data product.,
clinical,preventive_health,immunization,claim_id,claim_id,Claim Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,claim.claim.claim_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to claim.claim. Business justification: Immunizations are billable services that generate claims with CPT/CVX codes. Revenue cycle requires linking immunization event to claim for charge capture validation, VFC program billing, and reimburs",
clinical,preventive_health,immunization,clinical_order_id,clinical_order_id,Immunization Clinical Order Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,order.clinical_order.clinical_order_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to order.clinical_order. Business justification: Immunizations fulfill vaccine orders. Real workflow: provider orders flu vaccine, nurse administers. Essential for vaccine order-to-administration tracking, VFC program compliance, immunization regist",
clinical,preventive_health,immunization,consent_record_id,consent_record_id,Consent Record Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,consent.consent_consent_record.consent_record_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to consent.consent_record. Business justification: Immunizations require documented consent, especially for minors, research vaccines, or religious exemptions. VIS presentation and consent documentation are CDC and state-mandated. Links immunization e",
clinical,preventive_health,immunization,cpt_code_id,cpt_code_id,Cpt Code Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,reference.cpt_code.cpt_code_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to reference.cpt_code. Business justification: Immunization billing for vaccine administration charges, counseling services, and combination vaccine coding. Revenue cycle teams use CPT codes for vaccine administration to generate accurate claims a",
clinical,preventive_health,immunization,hedis_measure_id,hedis_measure_id,Hedis Measure Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,quality.hedis_measure.hedis_measure_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to quality.hedis_measure. Business justification: HEDIS immunization measures (childhood vaccines, flu shots, pneumococcal) directly reference immunization records for numerator compliance. Essential for HEDIS reporting and health plan quality rating",
clinical,preventive_health,immunization,immunization_administered_location_care_site_id,immunization_administered_location_care_site_id,,BIGINT,,facility.care_site.care_site_id,,,transactional_data,FK to facility.care_site.care_site_id,
clinical,preventive_health,immunization,immunization_care_site_id,immunization_care_site_id,Facility ID,BIGINT,,facility.care_site.care_site_id,,,transactional_data,Reference to the facility or clinic location where the immunization was administered. Supports public health reporting by site.,
clinical,preventive_health,immunization,immunization_material_master_id,immunization_material_master_id,Material Master Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,supply.material_master.material_master_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to supply.material_master. Business justification: Vaccines are inventory items with lot tracking, expiration management, and recall requirements. Enables vaccine inventory management, VFC program compliance, and immunization registry reporting. Remov",
clinical,preventive_health,immunization,immunization_supply_lot_number_material_master_id,immunization_supply_lot_number_material_master_id,,BIGINT,,supply.material_master.material_master_id,,,transactional_data,FK to supply.material_master.material_master_id,
clinical,preventive_health,immunization,mpi_record_id,mpi_record_id,Patient ID,BIGINT,,patient.mpi_record.mpi_record_id,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_identifier",,transactional_data,Reference to the patient who received the immunization. Links to the Master Patient Index (MPI) patient record.,
clinical,preventive_health,immunization,ndc_drug_id,ndc_drug_id,Ndc Code Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,reference.ndc_drug.ndc_drug_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to reference.ndc_drug. Business justification: Vaccine product identification for inventory management, lot tracking, recall management, and VFC program compliance. Pharmacy and immunization registries use NDC codes to track specific vaccine produ",
clinical,preventive_health,immunization,primary_care_physician_clinician_id,primary_care_physician_clinician_id,Primary Care Physician (PCP) ID,BIGINT,,provider.clinician.clinician_id,,,transactional_data,"Reference to the patients Primary Care Physician (PCP) at the time of immunization. Supports care coordination, preventive care gap closure, and HEDIS reporting for immunization measures.",
clinical,preventive_health,immunization,tertiary_immunization_ordering_provider_clinician_id,tertiary_immunization_ordering_provider_clinician_id,Ordering Provider ID,BIGINT,,provider.clinician.clinician_id,,,transactional_data,"Reference to the provider who ordered or authorized the immunization, which may differ from the administering provider. Supports Computerized Physician Order Entry (CPOE) traceability.",
clinical,preventive_health,immunization,vaccine_drug_master_id,vaccine_drug_master_id,Vaccine Drug Master Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,pharmacy.drug_master.drug_master_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to pharmacy.drug_master. Business justification: Immunizations are pharmaceutical products tracked in inventory and formulary systems. Vaccine administration requires drug master reference for lot tracking, expiration management, recall notification",
clinical,preventive_health,immunization,visit_id,visit_id,Encounter ID,BIGINT,,encounter.visit.visit_id,,,transactional_data,Reference to the clinical encounter during which the immunization was administered. Supports linkage to Admit-Discharge-Transfer (ADT) and clinical encounter context.,
clinical,preventive_health,immunization,administration_route_code,administration_route_code,Administration Route Code,STRING,,,,IM|SC|ID|PO|IN|IV,transactional_data,"The coded route by which the vaccine was administered (e.g., IM for intramuscular, SC for subcutaneous, PO for oral, IN for intranasal). Follows NCI Thesaurus / HL7 route of administration codes.",
clinical,preventive_health,immunization,administration_site_code,administration_site_code,Administration Site Code,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Coded anatomical site where the vaccine was injected or administered (e.g., LA for left arm deltoid, RT for right thigh). Uses HL7 v2 or SNOMED CT body site codes. Required for adverse event documentation. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: LA|RA|LT|RT|LG|RG|ABD|NASAL|ORAL — promote to reference product]",
clinical,preventive_health,immunization,administration_status,administration_status,Immunization Administration Status,STRING,,,,completed|entered-in-error|not-done,transactional_data,"Current lifecycle status of the immunization record indicating whether the vaccine was successfully administered, not given, or entered in error. Aligns with HL7 FHIR Immunization.status value set.",
clinical,preventive_health,immunization,administration_timestamp,administration_timestamp,Immunization Administration Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,The exact date and time the vaccine was administered to the patient. This is the principal real-world event timestamp for the immunization record. Sourced from Epic or Cerner immunization module.,
clinical,preventive_health,immunization,clinical_note,clinical_note,Immunization Clinical Note,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Free-text clinical notes or comments documented by the administering provider regarding the immunization event, patient response, or special circumstances. Supports Clinical Documentation Improvement (CDI) workflows.",
clinical,preventive_health,immunization,consent_obtained,consent_obtained,Immunization Consent Obtained Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,Indicates whether informed consent was obtained from the patient or legal guardian prior to vaccine administration. Supports NCVIA compliance and risk management documentation.,
clinical,preventive_health,immunization,created_timestamp,created_timestamp,Record Created Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,"The date and time this immunization record was first created or entered into the source system. Supports audit trail, data lineage, and HIPAA compliance documentation.",
clinical,preventive_health,immunization,dose_number_in_series,dose_number_in_series,Dose Number in Series,INT,,,,,transactional_data,"The sequential dose number within the immunization series (e.g., 1 for first dose, 2 for second dose, 3 for booster). Used to track series completion and determine next dose eligibility.",
clinical,preventive_health,immunization,dose_quantity,dose_quantity,Vaccine Dose Quantity,"DECIMAL(10,4)",,,,,transactional_data,"The numeric quantity of vaccine administered in the specified dose unit of measure (e.g., 0.5 mL). Supports clinical documentation and adverse event investigation.",
clinical,preventive_health,immunization,dose_unit,dose_unit,Vaccine Dose Unit of Measure,STRING,,,,mL|mg|mcg|units,transactional_data,"The unit of measure for the administered vaccine dose quantity (e.g., mL, mg). Follows UCUM (Unified Code for Units of Measure) standards as used in HL7 FHIR.",
clinical,preventive_health,immunization,expiration_date,expiration_date,Vaccine Expiration Date,DATE,,,,,transactional_data,"The manufacturer-assigned expiration date of the vaccine lot administered. Required for quality assurance, regulatory compliance, and to flag potential administration of expired product.",
clinical,preventive_health,immunization,funding_source_code,funding_source_code,Vaccine Funding Source Code,STRING,,,,VFC|317|STATE|PRIVATE|OTHER,transactional_data,Code identifying the funding source for the administered vaccine. VFC indicates Vaccines for Children program eligibility; 317 indicates CDC Section 317 public health grant funding. Required for state IIS reporting and VFC program compliance.,
clinical,preventive_health,immunization,iis_reported,iis_reported,Immunization Information System (IIS) Reported Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,Indicates whether this immunization record has been successfully reported to the state Immunization Information System (IIS) / immunization registry. Supports public health reporting compliance tracking.,
clinical,preventive_health,immunization,iis_reported_timestamp,iis_reported_timestamp,Immunization Information System (IIS) Reported Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,The date and time this immunization record was transmitted to the state Immunization Information System (IIS). Supports audit trail for public health reporting obligations.,
clinical,preventive_health,immunization,lot_number,lot_number,Vaccine Lot Number,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"The manufacturer-assigned lot number for the specific vaccine vial or unit administered. Critical for adverse event tracking, FDA recall management, and Vaccine Adverse Event Reporting System (VAERS) reporting.",
clinical,preventive_health,immunization,mrn,mrn,Medical Record Number (MRN),STRING,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_identifier",,transactional_data,The Medical Record Number (MRN) assigned to the patient by the healthcare organization. Used for cross-system patient identification and immunization registry reporting.,
clinical,preventive_health,immunization,not_given_reason_code,not_given_reason_code,Immunization Not Given Reason Code,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Coded reason why the immunization was not administered when administration_status is not-done. Examples include patient refusal, contraindication, or vaccine unavailability. SNOMED CT coded.",
clinical,preventive_health,immunization,reaction_detail,reaction_detail,Adverse Reaction Detail,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,Free-text or coded description of the adverse reaction observed following vaccine administration. Supports VAERS reporting and clinical documentation. SNOMED CT coded when structured.,
clinical,preventive_health,immunization,reaction_observed,reaction_observed,Adverse Reaction Observed Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,"Indicates whether an adverse reaction or side effect was observed following vaccine administration. When true, triggers adverse event documentation workflow and potential VAERS reporting.",
clinical,preventive_health,immunization,series_completion_status,series_completion_status,Immunization Series Completion Status,STRING,,,,complete|in-progress|not-started|overdue,transactional_data,"Indicates the patients current completion status for the immunization series as of this administration event. Supports population health management, HEDIS measure reporting, and preventive care outreach.",
clinical,preventive_health,immunization,series_doses_required,series_doses_required,Series Total Doses Required,INT,,,,,transactional_data,"The total number of doses required to complete the immunization series as defined by the CDC Advisory Committee on Immunization Practices (ACIP) schedule (e.g., 2 for Hepatitis B, 3 for HPV).",
clinical,preventive_health,immunization,series_name,series_name,Immunization Series Name,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"The name of the immunization series or protocol to which this dose belongs (e.g., COVID-19 Primary Series, Hepatitis B 3-Dose Series, Childhood Immunization Schedule). Supports series completion tracking.",
clinical,preventive_health,immunization,source_system,source_system,Source System,STRING,,,,EPIC|CERNER|MEDITECH|MANUAL|EXTERNAL,transactional_data,"Identifies the originating operational system from which this immunization record was sourced (e.g., EPIC for Epic EHR immunization module, CERNER for Cerner Millennium immunization module). Supports data lineage and reconciliation.",
clinical,preventive_health,immunization,source_system_record_code,source_system_record_code,Source System Record ID,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"The native record identifier from the originating operational system (Epic, Cerner, etc.) for this immunization administration event. Enables traceability back to the system of record for audit and reconciliation.",
clinical,preventive_health,immunization,updated_timestamp,updated_timestamp,Record Updated Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,"The date and time this immunization record was last modified or updated in the source system. Supports change tracking, audit trail, and data quality monitoring.",
clinical,preventive_health,immunization,vaers_reported,vaers_reported,Vaccine Adverse Event Reporting System (VAERS) Reported Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,Indicates whether an adverse event following this immunization was reported to the FDA/CDC Vaccine Adverse Event Reporting System (VAERS). Required for pharmacovigilance and regulatory compliance.,
clinical,preventive_health,immunization,vfc_eligibility_code,vfc_eligibility_code,Vaccines for Children (VFC) Eligibility Code,STRING,,,,V01|V02|V03|V04|V05|V06,transactional_data,"CDC-assigned Vaccines for Children (VFC) eligibility category code for the patient at time of administration (e.g., V01=Medicaid eligible, V02=Uninsured, V03=American Indian/Alaska Native, V04=Underinsured). Required for VFC program billing and compliance reporting.",
clinical,preventive_health,immunization,vis_document_type,vis_document_type,Vaccine Information Statement (VIS) Document Type,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"The type or name of the CDC Vaccine Information Statement (VIS) provided to the patient or guardian prior to administration (e.g., Influenza VIS, COVID-19 mRNA VIS). Required by the National Childhood Vaccine Injury Act (NCVIA).",
clinical,preventive_health,immunization,vis_presentation_date,vis_presentation_date,Vaccine Information Statement (VIS) Presentation Date,DATE,,,,,transactional_data,The date the Vaccine Information Statement (VIS) was presented to the patient or legal guardian. Documents informed consent compliance per NCVIA requirements.,
clinical,preventive_health,immunization,vis_publication_date,vis_publication_date,Vaccine Information Statement (VIS) Publication Date,DATE,,,,,transactional_data,The CDC publication date of the Vaccine Information Statement (VIS) provided to the patient. Required for NCVIA compliance documentation and immunization registry reporting.,
clinical,preventive_health,nursing_assessment,nursing_assessment_id,nursing_assessment_id,Nursing Assessment ID,BIGINT,Y,,,,transactional_data,Unique surrogate identifier for each nursing assessment record in the lakehouse silver layer. Primary key for this data product.,
clinical,preventive_health,nursing_assessment,bed_id,bed_id,Bed Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,facility.bed.bed_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to facility.bed. Business justification: Nursing assessments are performed at specific bedsides. Linking enables bed-level acuity tracking for staffing ratios, fall risk heat maps by bed location, pressure injury prevention tied to bed assig",
clinical,preventive_health,nursing_assessment,care_plan_id,care_plan_id,Care Plan Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,clinical.care_plan.care_plan_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to clinical.care_plan. Business justification: Nursing assessments (admission assessments, shift assessments, discharge assessments) inform care plan development and updates. Linking nursing_assessment.care_plan_id → care_plan.care_plan_id establi",
clinical,preventive_health,nursing_assessment,care_site_id,care_site_id,Facility ID,BIGINT,,facility.care_site.care_site_id,,,transactional_data,"Reference to the healthcare facility (hospital, clinic, or outpatient center) where this nursing assessment was conducted.",
clinical,preventive_health,nursing_assessment,clinical_order_id,clinical_order_id,,BIGINT,,order.clinical_order.clinical_order_id,,,transactional_data,foreign_key_to,
clinical,preventive_health,nursing_assessment,consent_record_id,consent_record_id,Consent Record Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,consent.consent_consent_record.consent_record_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to consent.consent_record. Business justification: Nursing assessments include sensitive data (restraint use, mental status, fall risk) requiring documented consent for interventions. Joint Commission standards mandate consent for restraints; mental h",
clinical,preventive_health,nursing_assessment,laboratory_test_result_id,laboratory_test_result_id,Reviewed Test Result Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,laboratory.laboratory_test_result.laboratory_test_result_id,,,transactional_data,Foreign key linking to laboratory.test_result. Business justification: Nursing assessments review recent lab results for care planning (potassium levels→cardiac monitoring). Role prefix reviewed_ indicates assessment input. Essential for nursing flowsheet integration a,
clinical,preventive_health,nursing_assessment,mar_record_id,mar_record_id,Mar Record Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,pharmacy.mar_record.mar_record_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to pharmacy.mar_record. Business justification: Nursing assessments (pain, respiratory status, skin integrity) documented alongside medication administration for clinical correlation. Required for nursing documentation standards and medication admi",
clinical,preventive_health,nursing_assessment,mpi_record_id,mpi_record_id,Patient ID,BIGINT,,patient.mpi_record.mpi_record_id,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_identifier",,transactional_data,Reference to the patient who is the subject of this nursing assessment. Links to the master patient record.,
clinical,preventive_health,nursing_assessment,patient_safety_event_id,patient_safety_event_id,Patient Safety Event Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,quality.patient_safety_event.patient_safety_event_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to quality.patient_safety_event. Business justification: Safety events (falls, pressure injuries) trigger review of nursing assessments to identify missed risk factors. Root cause analysis requires linking events to prior assessments. Essential for safety e",
clinical,preventive_health,nursing_assessment,primary_nursing_clinician_id,primary_nursing_clinician_id,Assessing Nurse Provider ID,BIGINT,,provider.clinician.clinician_id,,,transactional_data,"Reference to the licensed nurse (RN or LPN) who completed and signed this nursing assessment. Used for accountability, staffing analytics, and Joint Commission compliance.",
clinical,preventive_health,nursing_assessment,resulting_diet_order_id,resulting_diet_order_id,Resulting Diet Order Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,order.diet_order.diet_order_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to order.diet_order. Business justification: Nursing assessments drive diet orders. Real workflow: swallow assessment shows aspiration risk, triggers pureed diet order. Essential for nutrition care compliance, aspiration prevention protocols, sp",
clinical,preventive_health,nursing_assessment,visit_id,visit_id,Encounter ID,BIGINT,,encounter.visit.visit_id,,,transactional_data,"Reference to the clinical encounter (inpatient admission, ED visit, or outpatient visit) during which this nursing assessment was performed.",
clinical,preventive_health,nursing_assessment,assessment_interval_hours,assessment_interval_hours,Assessment Interval Hours,INT,,,,,transactional_data,"The required reassessment interval in hours as defined by the care setting protocol and assessment type (e.g., every 4 hours for ICU, every 8 hours for medical-surgical). Used to monitor reassessment compliance and timeliness.",
clinical,preventive_health,nursing_assessment,assessment_notes,assessment_notes,Assessment Clinical Notes,STRING,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_health",,transactional_data,"Free-text narrative clinical notes entered by the assessing nurse to supplement structured assessment findings. May include abnormal findings, patient responses, and clinical reasoning. Contains Protected Health Information (PHI).",
clinical,preventive_health,nursing_assessment,assessment_status,assessment_status,Nursing Assessment Status,STRING,,,,In Progress|Completed|Amended|Cosigned|Voided,transactional_data,"Current workflow status of the nursing assessment record. Indicates whether the assessment is actively being documented, finalized, amended after completion, or voided. Supports Joint Commission compliance audits.",
clinical,preventive_health,nursing_assessment,assessment_timestamp,assessment_timestamp,Assessment Date and Time,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,The date and time at which the nursing assessment was clinically performed (real-world event time). Distinct from documentation or record creation timestamps. Critical for shift-based quality metrics and regulatory reporting.,
clinical,preventive_health,nursing_assessment,assessment_type,assessment_type,Nursing Assessment Type,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Classification of the nursing assessment by its clinical purpose and timing. Drives workflow routing, documentation requirements, and quality metric calculations. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: Admission|Shift Change|Discharge|Head-to-Toe|Fall Risk|Skin Integrity|Restraint|Pressure Injury|Discharge Readiness|Pain — promote to reference product]",
clinical,preventive_health,nursing_assessment,braden_score,braden_score,Braden Scale Score,INT,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_health",,transactional_data,Numeric pressure injury risk score calculated using the Braden Scale (range 6–23). Lower scores indicate higher risk. Required for pressure injury prevention protocol activation and CMS HAC reporting.,
clinical,preventive_health,nursing_assessment,cardiovascular_status,cardiovascular_status,Cardiovascular Status,STRING,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_health",Regular Rate and Rhythm|Irregular|Tachycardic|Bradycardic|Absent,transactional_data,Documented cardiovascular assessment findings including heart rate regularity and rhythm. Core component of the head-to-toe nursing assessment and cardiac monitoring documentation.,
clinical,preventive_health,nursing_assessment,care_recommendations,care_recommendations,Care Recommendations,STRING,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_health",,transactional_data,"Nursing care recommendations and planned interventions documented as part of the assessment (e.g., reposition every 2 hours, initiate fall prevention bundle, consult wound care). Feeds into the nursing care plan.",
clinical,preventive_health,nursing_assessment,care_setting,care_setting,Care Setting,STRING,,,,Inpatient|ICU|ED|Outpatient|Surgical|Observation,transactional_data,"The clinical care setting in which the nursing assessment was performed (e.g., Inpatient, Intensive Care Unit (ICU), Emergency Department (ED), Outpatient). Drives assessment template selection and quality metric stratification.",
clinical,preventive_health,nursing_assessment,completed_timestamp,completed_timestamp,Assessment Completed Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,The date and time at which the nurse finalized and signed the nursing assessment in the EHR. Used to measure documentation timeliness and compliance with shift-completion requirements.,
clinical,preventive_health,nursing_assessment,continence_status,continence_status,Continence Status,STRING,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_health",Continent|Incontinent|Catheter|Ostomy|Unknown,transactional_data,Patients urinary and bowel continence status as documented in the nursing assessment. Relevant to Catheter-Associated Urinary Tract Infection (CAUTI) prevention protocols and skin integrity management.,
clinical,preventive_health,nursing_assessment,created_timestamp,created_timestamp,Record Created Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,The date and time when this nursing assessment record was first created in the source system. Supports audit trail and data lineage requirements.,
clinical,preventive_health,nursing_assessment,discharge_barriers,discharge_barriers,Discharge Barriers,STRING,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_health",,transactional_data,"Free-text or structured documentation of identified barriers to patient discharge (e.g., awaiting placement, transportation, caregiver availability, Social Determinants of Health (SDOH) factors). Supports care coordination and discharge planning workflows.",
clinical,preventive_health,nursing_assessment,discharge_readiness_score,discharge_readiness_score,Discharge Readiness Score,INT,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_health",,transactional_data,"Numeric score from a validated discharge readiness assessment tool (e.g., Readiness for Hospital Discharge Scale) indicating the patients preparedness for discharge. Supports discharge planning, Length of Stay (LOS) management, and readmission reduction initiatives.",
clinical,preventive_health,nursing_assessment,fall_risk_category,fall_risk_category,Fall Risk Category,STRING,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_health",Low|Moderate|High,transactional_data,"Categorical fall risk classification derived from the fall risk score (Low, Moderate, High). Drives nursing care plan interventions, bed alarm activation, and fall prevention bundle compliance reporting.",
clinical,preventive_health,nursing_assessment,fall_risk_score,fall_risk_score,Fall Risk Score,INT,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_health",,transactional_data,"Numeric fall risk score calculated from the validated fall risk assessment tool (e.g., Morse Fall Scale, Hendrich II). Drives fall prevention protocol activation and care plan interventions. Required for Joint Commission NPSG.09.02.01.",
clinical,preventive_health,nursing_assessment,fall_risk_tool,fall_risk_tool,Fall Risk Assessment Tool,STRING,,,,Morse Fall Scale|Hendrich II|STRATIFY|Johns Hopkins,transactional_data,"The validated fall risk assessment instrument used to calculate the fall risk score (e.g., Morse Fall Scale, Hendrich II Fall Risk Model). Ensures comparability of scores across units and facilities.",
clinical,preventive_health,nursing_assessment,iv_access_type,iv_access_type,Intravenous (IV) Access Type,STRING,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_health",Peripheral IV|Central Line|PICC|Port|None,transactional_data,"Type of intravenous access device present and assessed during the nursing assessment (Peripheral IV, Central Line, PICC, Port, or None). Critical for Central Line-Associated Bloodstream Infection (CLABSI) prevention bundle compliance and HAI reporting.",
clinical,preventive_health,nursing_assessment,iv_site_condition,iv_site_condition,Intravenous (IV) Site Condition,STRING,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_health",Patent|Infiltrated|Phlebitis|Occluded|Removed,transactional_data,"Condition of the intravenous access site as assessed by the nurse (Patent, Infiltrated, Phlebitis, Occluded, Removed). Drives IV site care interventions and CLABSI prevention bundle documentation.",
clinical,preventive_health,nursing_assessment,joint_commission_compliant,joint_commission_compliant,Joint Commission Compliance Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,"Indicates whether this nursing assessment meets all applicable Joint Commission documentation requirements for the assessment type (e.g., all required fields completed, completed within required timeframe). Used for quality reporting and survey readiness.",
clinical,preventive_health,nursing_assessment,last_updated_timestamp,last_updated_timestamp,Record Last Updated Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,"The date and time when this nursing assessment record was most recently modified in the source system. Supports change detection, incremental ETL loads, and audit compliance.",
clinical,preventive_health,nursing_assessment,mobility_status,mobility_status,Mobility Status,STRING,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_health",Independent|Assisted|Dependent|Bedrest|Ambulating,transactional_data,"Patients functional mobility level as assessed by the nurse (Independent, Assisted, Dependent, Bedrest, Ambulating). Informs fall prevention, pressure injury prevention, and physical therapy referral decisions.",
clinical,preventive_health,nursing_assessment,mrn,mrn,Medical Record Number (MRN),STRING,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_identifier",,transactional_data,The Medical Record Number (MRN) assigned to the patient by the facilitys Master Patient Index (MPI). Provides a human-readable patient identifier for clinical staff and HIM workflows.,
clinical,preventive_health,nursing_assessment,neurological_status,neurological_status,Neurological Status,STRING,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_health",Alert and Oriented|Confused|Lethargic|Obtunded|Stuporous|Comatose,transactional_data,"Documented neurological status of the patient at the time of assessment, reflecting level of consciousness and orientation. Core component of head-to-toe nursing assessment and change-of-condition monitoring.",
clinical,preventive_health,nursing_assessment,nursing_unit,nursing_unit,Nursing Unit,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"The specific nursing unit or department (e.g., 4 North Medical-Surgical, MICU, PACU) where the patient was located at the time of the assessment. Used for unit-level quality benchmarking and staffing analysis.",
clinical,preventive_health,nursing_assessment,nutrition_status,nutrition_status,Nutrition Status,STRING,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_health",Adequate|At Risk|Malnourished|NPO|Tube Feeding,transactional_data,Nursing assessment of the patients nutritional status and feeding method. Drives dietary consult referrals and nutrition care plan interventions. Supports malnutrition quality reporting.,
clinical,preventive_health,nursing_assessment,orientation_level,orientation_level,Orientation Level,STRING,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_health",x1|x2|x3|x4,transactional_data,"Patient orientation level documented during neurological assessment: x1 (person), x2 (person and place), x3 (person, place, and time), x4 (person, place, time, and event). Standard clinical notation used in nursing documentation.",
clinical,preventive_health,nursing_assessment,pain_scale_type,pain_scale_type,Pain Scale Type,STRING,,,,NRS|FLACC|CPOT|Wong-Baker|VAS,transactional_data,"The validated pain assessment scale used to obtain the pain score (e.g., Numeric Rating Scale (NRS), FLACC for pediatric/non-verbal patients, Critical Care Pain Observation Tool (CPOT)). Required for clinical interpretation of pain scores.",
clinical,preventive_health,nursing_assessment,pain_score,pain_score,Pain Score,INT,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_health",,transactional_data,"Numeric pain intensity score documented by the nurse using a validated pain scale (e.g., Numeric Rating Scale 0–10, FLACC, CPOT). Required by The Joint Commission for all patient assessments. Drives pain management interventions.",
clinical,preventive_health,nursing_assessment,patient_education_provided,patient_education_provided,Patient Education Provided Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,Indicates whether patient and/or family education was provided during this nursing assessment encounter. Required documentation for Joint Commission and CMS patient education standards.,
clinical,preventive_health,nursing_assessment,pressure_injury_location,pressure_injury_location,Pressure Injury Location,STRING,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_health",,transactional_data,"Anatomical body site location of the identified pressure injury (e.g., sacrum, coccyx, heel, occiput). Documented using standardized anatomical terminology. Required for wound care documentation and HAC reporting.",
clinical,preventive_health,nursing_assessment,pressure_injury_stage,pressure_injury_stage,Pressure Injury Stage,STRING,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_health",Stage 1|Stage 2|Stage 3|Stage 4|Unstageable|Deep Tissue,transactional_data,"National Pressure Injury Advisory Panel (NPIAP) staging classification for any identified pressure injury (Stage 1 through Stage 4, Unstageable, or Deep Tissue Pressure Injury). Required for CMS Hospital-Acquired Condition (HAC) reporting and quality metrics.",
clinical,preventive_health,nursing_assessment,respiratory_status,respiratory_status,Respiratory Status,STRING,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_health",Regular|Labored|Shallow|Absent|Assisted,transactional_data,Documented respiratory status of the patient including breathing pattern and effort. Part of the head-to-toe body system assessment. Triggers escalation protocols when abnormal.,
clinical,preventive_health,nursing_assessment,restraint_indication,restraint_indication,Restraint Clinical Indication,STRING,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_health",,transactional_data,"Clinical justification documented by the nurse for restraint application (e.g., risk of self-harm, removal of life-sustaining devices, violent behavior). Required by CMS and Joint Commission for every restraint episode.",
clinical,preventive_health,nursing_assessment,restraint_type,restraint_type,Restraint Type,STRING,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_health",Physical|Chemical|Soft Limb|Vest|Mitts|None,transactional_data,"Type of restraint applied to the patient as documented in the restraint assessment (Physical, Chemical, Soft Limb, Vest, Mitts, or None). Required for CMS Conditions of Participation restraint documentation and Joint Commission compliance.",
clinical,preventive_health,nursing_assessment,safety_check_completed,safety_check_completed,Safety Check Completed Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,"Indicates whether the nursing safety check (e.g., bed in lowest position, call light within reach, side rails up, ID band verified) was completed and documented as part of this assessment. Supports Joint Commission National Patient Safety Goal compliance.",
clinical,preventive_health,nursing_assessment,skin_integrity_status,skin_integrity_status,Skin Integrity Status,STRING,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_health",Intact|Impaired|Wound Present|Pressure Injury,transactional_data,Overall skin integrity assessment finding indicating whether the patients skin is intact or compromised. Triggers wound care protocols and pressure injury prevention bundles. Required for HAI reporting.,
clinical,preventive_health,nursing_assessment,source_system,source_system,Source System,STRING,,,,Epic ClinDoc|Cerner PowerChart|MEDITECH Expanse|Manual Entry,transactional_data,"The operational system of record from which this nursing assessment was sourced (e.g., Epic ClinDoc, Cerner PowerChart). Supports data lineage and ETL traceability.",
clinical,preventive_health,nursing_assessment,source_system_assessment_code,source_system_assessment_code,Source System Assessment ID,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"The native identifier of this nursing assessment record in the originating Electronic Health Record (EHR) system (e.g., Epic ClinDoc flowsheet row ID or Cerner PowerChart documentation ID). Supports data lineage and reconciliation.",
