clinical,preventive_health,vital_sign,vital_sign_id,vital_sign_id,Vital Sign ID,BIGINT,Y,,,,transactional_data,Unique surrogate identifier for each vital sign measurement record in the lakehouse silver layer. Primary key for the vital_sign data product.,
clinical,preventive_health,vital_sign,care_site_id,care_site_id,Facility ID,BIGINT,,facility.care_site.care_site_id,,,transactional_data,"Reference to the healthcare facility (hospital, clinic, outpatient center) where the vital sign measurement was taken. Supports multi-facility analytics, population health management, and facility-level quality reporting.",
clinical,preventive_health,vital_sign,clinical_order_id,clinical_order_id,Vital Sign Clinical Order Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,order.clinical_order.clinical_order_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to order.clinical_order. Business justification: Vital signs fulfill monitoring orders. Real workflow: order for q4h vitals, nurse documents BP/HR. Essential for order compliance tracking, nursing workload analysis, sepsis protocol adherence, and re",
clinical,preventive_health,vital_sign,clinician_id,clinician_id,Clinician ID,BIGINT,,provider.clinician.clinician_id,,,transactional_data,"Reference to the clinician (nurse, physician, or allied health professional) who recorded or validated the vital sign measurement. Supports accountability and CDI workflows.",
clinical,preventive_health,vital_sign,loinc_code_id,loinc_code_id,Loinc Code Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,reference.loinc_code.loinc_code_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to reference.loinc_code. Business justification: Vital sign observation standardization for clinical surveillance, early warning scores, quality measure calculation, and interoperable data exchange. Clinical systems use LOINC codes to aggregate vita",
clinical,preventive_health,vital_sign,mar_record_id,mar_record_id,Mar Record Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,pharmacy.mar_record.mar_record_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to pharmacy.mar_record. Business justification: Vital signs documented at medication administration time for high-risk medications (BP before antihypertensives, HR before beta-blockers, glucose before insulin). Required for safe medication administ",
clinical,preventive_health,vital_sign,mpi_record_id,mpi_record_id,Patient ID,BIGINT,,patient.mpi_record.mpi_record_id,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_health",,transactional_data,Reference to the patient for whom the vital sign measurement was recorded. Links to the master patient record in the Patient domain.,
clinical,preventive_health,vital_sign,nursing_assessment_id,nursing_assessment_id,,BIGINT,,clinical.nursing_assessment.nursing_assessment_id,,,transactional_data,description,
clinical,preventive_health,vital_sign,previous_vital_sign_id,previous_vital_sign_id,Previous Vital Sign Record ID,BIGINT,,clinical.vital_sign.vital_sign_id,,,transactional_data,Reference to the prior version of this vital sign record when observation_status is amended or corrected. Enables amendment chain traceability and supports audit requirements for clinical documentation integrity.,
clinical,preventive_health,vital_sign,primary_vital_device_equipment_asset_id,primary_vital_device_equipment_asset_id,,BIGINT,,facility.equipment_asset.equipment_asset_id,,,transactional_data,FK to facility.equipment_asset.equipment_asset_id,
clinical,preventive_health,vital_sign,quality_measure_id,quality_measure_id,Quality Measure Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,quality.measure.measure_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to quality.measure. Business justification: Many quality measures have vital sign thresholds (BP control in hypertension, BMI documentation). Direct linkage supports automated measure calculation and clinical decision support for quality improv",
clinical,preventive_health,vital_sign,visit_id,visit_id,Encounter ID,BIGINT,,encounter.visit.visit_id,,,transactional_data,"Reference to the clinical encounter (inpatient admission, ED visit, outpatient visit) during which the vital sign was measured. Supports encounter-level trending and early warning score calculations.",
clinical,preventive_health,vital_sign,abnormal_flag,abnormal_flag,Vital Sign Abnormal Flag,STRING,,,,normal|low|high|critical_low|critical_high|abnormal,transactional_data,"Interpretation flag indicating whether the measured value falls within, below, or above the reference range. critical_low and critical_high trigger immediate clinical notification per facility policy. Supports sepsis screening, EWS alerting, and clinical deterioration detection workflows.",
clinical,preventive_health,vital_sign,amended_reason,amended_reason,Vital Sign Amendment Reason,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"The clinical or administrative reason provided when a vital sign record is amended, corrected, or marked as entered-in-error (e.g., transcription error, wrong patient, device malfunction, duplicate entry). Populated only when observation_status is amended, corrected, or entered-in-error. Supports CDI audit trails and data quality governance.",
clinical,preventive_health,vital_sign,body_site,body_site,Vital Sign Body Site,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"The anatomical body site where the measurement was taken (e.g., left arm, right arm, finger, ear, forehead, toe). Encoded using SNOMED CT body structure codes. Relevant for blood pressure laterality, temperature site, and SpO2 probe placement. Affects clinical interpretation.",
clinical,preventive_health,vital_sign,care_unit,care_unit,Care Unit,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"The clinical care unit or department where the patient was located when the vital sign was measured (e.g., ICU, ED, Medical/Surgical, OR, PACU, Step-Down). Supports unit-level benchmarking, staffing analytics, and HAI surveillance.",
clinical,preventive_health,vital_sign,clinical_note,clinical_note,Vital Sign Clinical Note,STRING,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_health",,transactional_data,"Free-text clinical annotation or comment entered by the recording clinician to provide context for the vital sign measurement (e.g., patient anxious during measurement, cuff size large, post-exercise reading). Supports CDI workflows and clinical interpretation.",
clinical,preventive_health,vital_sign,created_timestamp,created_timestamp,Record Created Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,"The date and time when this vital sign record was first created in the lakehouse silver layer. Represents the ETL ingestion audit timestamp, distinct from measurement_timestamp (when the vital was taken) and documented_timestamp (when it was entered in the EHR). Format: yyyy-MM-ddTHH:mm:ss.SSSXXX.",
clinical,preventive_health,vital_sign,documented_timestamp,documented_timestamp,Vital Sign Documentation Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,The date and time when the vital sign measurement was entered or finalized in the EHR system (Epic ClinDoc flowsheet or Cerner PowerChart). May differ from measurement_timestamp when documentation is retrospective. Used for CDI audit trails and documentation timeliness reporting.,
clinical,preventive_health,vital_sign,ews_score_contribution,ews_score_contribution,Early Warning Score (EWS) Component Score,INT,,,,,transactional_data,"The numeric score contribution of this individual vital sign measurement to the composite Early Warning Score (EWS), Modified Early Warning Score (MEWS), or National Early Warning Score (NEWS/NEWS2). Scored 0–3 per parameter per NEWS2 methodology. Supports real-time clinical deterioration detection and rapid response team activation.",
clinical,preventive_health,vital_sign,ews_score_type,ews_score_type,Early Warning Score (EWS) Type,STRING,,,,NEWS2|MEWS|EWS|PEWS|custom,transactional_data,"Identifies the specific early warning scoring system used to derive the ews_score_contribution for this vital sign (e.g., NEWS2 for adult inpatients, PEWS for pediatric patients, MEWS for general ward use). Allows multi-system EWS coexistence in the same dataset.",
clinical,preventive_health,vital_sign,flowsheet_row_code,flowsheet_row_code,EHR Flowsheet Row Identifier,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"The source system flowsheet row identifier from Epic ClinDoc or Cerner PowerChart that uniquely identifies the flowsheet template row from which this vital sign was extracted. Supports ETL lineage, source system reconciliation, and re-ingestion deduplication.",
clinical,preventive_health,vital_sign,gcs_component,gcs_component,Glasgow Coma Scale (GCS) Component,STRING,,,,eye_opening|verbal_response|motor_response|total,transactional_data,"Identifies which component of the Glasgow Coma Scale (GCS) is represented when observation_type is gcs_total or a GCS sub-score (Eye Opening E1-E4, Verbal Response V1-V5, Motor Response M1-M6, or Total 3-15). Null for non-GCS vital sign observations. Supports neurological assessment trending and ICU severity scoring.",
clinical,preventive_health,vital_sign,is_patient_reported,is_patient_reported,Patient Reported Indicator,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,"Indicates whether the vital sign value was self-reported by the patient (True), such as home blood pressure readings, pain scores, or weight from a patient portal or remote monitoring program. Distinguishes patient-generated health data (PGHD) from clinician-measured values for analytics and clinical decision support.",
clinical,preventive_health,vital_sign,is_telemetry_derived,is_telemetry_derived,Telemetry Derived Indicator,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,Indicates whether the vital sign measurement was automatically captured from a continuous bedside telemetry or patient monitoring device (True) versus manually entered by a clinician (False). Supports differentiation of high-frequency device-generated data from manually documented assessments in time-series analytics.,
clinical,preventive_health,vital_sign,measurement_method,measurement_method,Vital Sign Measurement Method,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"The clinical method used to obtain the vital sign measurement (e.g., auscultation for BP, pulse oximetry for SpO2, tympanic or oral or rectal or axillary for temperature, Doppler for BP). Encoded using SNOMED CT method codes where applicable. Affects clinical interpretation and normal range thresholds.",
clinical,preventive_health,vital_sign,measurement_timestamp,measurement_timestamp,Vital Sign Measurement Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_health",,transactional_data,"The precise date and time when the vital sign measurement was physically taken from the patient. This is the principal clinical event time, distinct from the documentation timestamp. Critical for time-series trending, EWS/MEWS/NEWS calculations, and sepsis screening time-to-treatment metrics. Format: yyyy-MM-ddTHH:mm:ss.SSSXXX.",
clinical,preventive_health,vital_sign,mrn,mrn,Medical Record Number (MRN),STRING,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_identifier",,transactional_data,"pii_phi,pii_pii,pii_sensitive",
clinical,preventive_health,vital_sign,numeric_value,numeric_value,Vital Sign Numeric Value,"DECIMAL(10,4)",,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_health",,transactional_data,"The principal quantitative measured value of the vital sign observation (e.g., 120 for systolic BP in mmHg, 98.6 for temperature in °F, 98 for SpO2 in %). Stored as a decimal to accommodate fractional values such as temperature and BMI. Null when the observation is non-numeric (e.g., qualitative pain descriptors).",
clinical,preventive_health,vital_sign,observation_status,observation_status,Vital Sign Observation Status,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,Current lifecycle status of the vital sign observation record per HL7 FHIR Observation status value set. final indicates a verified measurement; amended or corrected indicates a post-documentation change; entered-in-error flags records to be excluded from clinical calculations. Supports data quality filtering for EWS and sepsis screening. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: registered|preliminary|final|amended|corrected|cancelled|entered-in-error — 7 candidates stripped; promote to reference product],
clinical,preventive_health,vital_sign,observation_type,observation_type,Vital Sign Observation Type,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Standardized enumeration of the vital sign observation category captured in this record. Each row represents a single atomic observation. Supports time-series analytics, EWS/MEWS/NEWS scoring, and sepsis screening. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: blood_pressure_systolic|blood_pressure_diastolic|heart_rate|respiratory_rate|temperature|spo2|height|weight|bmi|pain_score|gcs_total — promote to reference product]",
clinical,preventive_health,vital_sign,oxygen_delivery_method,oxygen_delivery_method,Oxygen Delivery Method,STRING,,,,room_air|nasal_cannula|simple_mask|non_rebreather|high_flow_nasal|mechanical_ventilator,transactional_data,"The supplemental oxygen delivery method in use at the time of SpO2 or respiratory rate measurement (e.g., room air, nasal cannula, simple mask, non-rebreather mask, high-flow nasal cannula, mechanical ventilator). Null for non-respiratory vital signs. Critical context for SpO2 interpretation and NEWS2 scoring (Scale 1 vs Scale 2).",
clinical,preventive_health,vital_sign,pain_scale_type,pain_scale_type,Pain Assessment Scale Type,STRING,,,,numeric_rating|visual_analog|faces|flacc|cpot|behavioral,transactional_data,"The specific pain assessment scale used when observation_type is pain_score (e.g., Numeric Rating Scale 0-10, Visual Analog Scale, Wong-Baker FACES, FLACC for pediatric/non-verbal, CPOT for critically ill). Null for non-pain vital sign observations. Required for accurate pain score interpretation per Joint Commission pain management standards.",
clinical,preventive_health,vital_sign,patient_position,patient_position,Patient Position During Measurement,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"The patients body position at the time of the vital sign measurement (e.g., sitting, standing, supine). Particularly relevant for blood pressure and orthostatic vital sign assessments. Encoded using SNOMED CT observable entity codes. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: sitting|standing|supine|prone|left_lateral|right_lateral|semi-recumbent — 7 candidates stripped; promote to reference product]",
clinical,preventive_health,vital_sign,reference_range_high,reference_range_high,Vital Sign Reference Range High,"DECIMAL(10,4)",,,,,transactional_data,"The upper bound of the normal reference range for this vital sign observation type, in the same unit of measure as numeric_value. Used for clinical alerting, EWS/MEWS/NEWS scoring, and out-of-range flagging.",
clinical,preventive_health,vital_sign,reference_range_low,reference_range_low,Vital Sign Reference Range Low,"DECIMAL(10,4)",,,,,transactional_data,"The lower bound of the normal reference range for this vital sign observation type, in the same unit of measure as numeric_value. Used for clinical alerting, EWS/MEWS/NEWS scoring, and out-of-range flagging. Age- and condition-adjusted ranges may differ from population norms.",
clinical,preventive_health,vital_sign,snomed_finding_code,snomed_finding_code,Systematized Nomenclature of Medicine Clinical Terms (SNOMED CT) Finding Code,STRING,,,,"^[0-9]{6,18}$",transactional_data,"SNOMED CT clinical finding code representing the clinical interpretation of the vital sign result (e.g., 38341003 Hypertensive disorder, 44054006 Diabetes mellitus type 2 context). Supports semantic interoperability, clinical decision support, and FHIR-based HIE exchange.",
clinical,preventive_health,vital_sign,source_system,source_system,Source System,STRING,,,,epic_clindoc|cerner_powerchart|meditech_expanse|bedside_monitor|wearable_device|manual_entry,transactional_data,"Identifies the operational system of record from which this vital sign measurement was ingested (e.g., Epic ClinDoc flowsheet, Cerner PowerChart, MEDITECH Expanse, bedside monitoring device integration, wearable device feed). Supports data lineage, ETL audit, and multi-source reconciliation.",
clinical,preventive_health,vital_sign,source_system_record_code,source_system_record_code,Source System Record Identifier,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"The native primary key or observation identifier from the originating source system (Epic, Cerner, MEDITECH, or device integration platform). Enables bidirectional traceability between the lakehouse silver layer record and the operational EHR record for reconciliation and audit.",
clinical,preventive_health,vital_sign,supplemental_oxygen_flow_rate,supplemental_oxygen_flow_rate,Supplemental Oxygen Flow Rate (L/min),"DECIMAL(5,2)",,,,,transactional_data,The flow rate of supplemental oxygen in liters per minute (L/min) being administered to the patient at the time of the SpO2 or respiratory vital sign measurement. Null when oxygen_delivery_method is room_air or for non-respiratory observations. Supports NEWS2 Scale 2 scoring and respiratory therapy documentation.,
clinical,preventive_health,vital_sign,text_value,text_value,Vital Sign Text Value,"DECIMAL(18,2)",,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_health",,transactional_data,"Free-text or coded string value for vital sign observations that are qualitative or semi-quantitative (e.g., pain descriptor mild, moderate, severe; GCS verbal response oriented; SpO2 trend improving). Null when numeric_value is populated.",
clinical,preventive_health,vital_sign,unit_of_measure,unit_of_measure,Unit of Measure,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"The unit of measure for the numeric vital sign value using UCUM (Unified Code for Units of Measure) notation (e.g., mm[Hg] for blood pressure, /min for heart/respiratory rate, Cel or [degF] for temperature, % for SpO2, cm or [in_i] for height, kg or [lb_av] for weight, kg/m2 for BMI, {score} for pain/GCS).",
clinical,preventive_health,vital_sign,updated_timestamp,updated_timestamp,Record Updated Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,"The date and time when this vital sign record was last modified in the lakehouse silver layer (e.g., due to an amendment, correction, or status change propagated from the source EHR). Format: yyyy-MM-ddTHH:mm:ss.SSSXXX.",
consent,authorization_management,consent_form_template,consent_form_template_id,consent_form_template_id,Consent Form Template Identifier (ID),BIGINT,Y,,,,master_data,Unique identifier for the consent form template record. Primary key.,
consent,authorization_management,consent_form_template,compliance_policy_id,compliance_policy_id,Compliance Policy Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,compliance.compliance_policy.compliance_policy_id,,,master_data,"Foreign key linking to compliance.policy. Business justification: Templates are governed by compliance policies defining required elements, approval workflows, and regulatory requirements. Essential for policy enforcement, version control, and demonstrating that con",
consent,authorization_management,consent_form_template,consent_policy_id,consent_policy_id,Consent Policy Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,consent.consent_policy.consent_policy_id,,,master_data,"Foreign key linking to consent.consent_policy. Business justification: Consent form templates implement and enforce consent policies. Each template should reference the policy it supports. Adding consent_policy_id FK links template design to governing policy, enabling po",
consent,authorization_management,consent_form_template,exchange_standard_id,exchange_standard_id,Exchange Standard Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,interoperability.exchange_standard.exchange_standard_id,,,master_data,"Foreign key linking to interoperability.exchange_standard. Business justification: Consent form templates must conform to specific exchange standards (C-CDA Consent Directive template 2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.64, FHIR Consent resource profiles). Required for interoperability des",
consent,authorization_management,consent_form_template,superseded_by_template_form_template_consent_form_template_id,superseded_by_template_form_template_consent_form_template_id,Superseded By Template Identifier (ID),BIGINT,,consent.consent_form_template.consent_form_template_id,,,master_data,Reference to the consent_form_template_id of the newer version that supersedes this template. Null if this is the current active version.,
consent,authorization_management,consent_form_template,applicable_facility_types,applicable_facility_types,Applicable Facility Types,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Comma-separated list or description of facility types where this consent form template is applicable (e.g., inpatient hospital, outpatient clinic, emergency department, ambulatory surgery center, telehealth platform).",
consent,authorization_management,consent_form_template,applicable_service_lines,applicable_service_lines,Applicable Service Lines,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Comma-separated list or description of clinical service lines or departments where this consent form template is used (e.g., cardiology, oncology, behavioral health, radiology, laboratory).",
consent,authorization_management,consent_form_template,approval_authority,approval_authority,Approval Authority,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Name or title of the individual, committee, or department that approved this consent form template for use (e.g., Chief Compliance Officer, Legal Department, Privacy Officer, IRB Chair).",
consent,authorization_management,consent_form_template,approval_date,approval_date,Approval Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,Date when the consent form template was officially approved by the designated authority for deployment and use.,
consent,authorization_management,consent_form_template,consent_category,consent_category,Consent Category,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Primary category of consent this form template addresses: treatment (general medical treatment), surgical (procedure-specific), research (clinical trials and studies), hipaa_authorization (PHI disclosure), hie_opt_in_out (Health Information Exchange participation), telehealth (virtual care consent), data_sharing (third-party data use). [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: treatment|surgical|research|hipaa_authorization|hie_opt_in_out|telehealth|data_sharing — 7 candidates stripped; promote to reference product]",
consent,authorization_management,consent_form_template,consent_subcategory,consent_subcategory,Consent Subcategory,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Optional subcategory or specialization within the primary consent category (e.g., anesthesia, blood transfusion, genetic testing, marketing communications).",
consent,authorization_management,consent_form_template,created_by_user,created_by_user,Created By User,STRING,,,,,master_data,Username or identifier of the system user who created this consent form template record.,
consent,authorization_management,consent_form_template,created_timestamp,created_timestamp,Created Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,master_data,Timestamp when this consent form template record was first created in the system.,
consent,authorization_management,consent_form_template,effective_date,effective_date,Effective Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,Date when this consent form template version becomes valid and available for use in patient consent workflows.,
consent,authorization_management,consent_form_template,electronic_signature_enabled_flag,electronic_signature_enabled_flag,Electronic Signature Enabled Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,"Indicates whether this consent form template supports electronic signature capture in compliance with ESIGN Act and state electronic signature laws. True if electronic signature is enabled, False if wet signature is required.",
consent,authorization_management,consent_form_template,expiration_date,expiration_date,Expiration Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,Date when this consent form template version is no longer valid for new consent collection. Nullable for forms without predetermined expiration.,
consent,authorization_management,consent_form_template,form_checksum,form_checksum,Form Checksum,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Cryptographic hash (e.g., SHA-256) of the form document file to ensure integrity and detect unauthorized modifications. Used for audit and compliance verification.",
consent,authorization_management,consent_form_template,form_code,form_code,Form Code,STRING,,,,"^[A-Z0-9_-]{3,20}$",master_data,"Unique business identifier code for the consent form template used for reference across systems (e.g., HIPAA_AUTH_2024, SURG_CONSENT_V3).",
consent,authorization_management,consent_form_template,form_document_url,form_document_url,Form Document Uniform Resource Locator (URL),STRING,,,,,master_data,"URL or file path to the digital master copy of the consent form template document (PDF, Word, or other format) stored in the document management system.",
