consent,lifecycle_operations,expiration_alert,alert_generation_date,alert_generation_date,Alert Generation Date,DATE,,,,,transactional_data,The date on which this expiration alert was generated by the consent monitoring system. Establishes alert creation timeline for SLA tracking.,
consent,lifecycle_operations,expiration_alert,alert_generation_timestamp,alert_generation_timestamp,Alert Generation Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,Precise date and time when the alert was created by the automated consent expiration monitoring process. Used for audit trail and alert latency analysis.,
consent,lifecycle_operations,expiration_alert,alert_number,alert_number,Alert Number,STRING,,,,^CEA-[0-9]{10}$,transactional_data,Human-readable business identifier for the consent expiration alert. Format: CEA-XXXXXXXXXX where X is a digit. Used for tracking and reference in workflows and communications.,
consent,lifecycle_operations,expiration_alert,alert_priority,alert_priority,Alert Priority,STRING,,,,low|medium|high|urgent,transactional_data,"Business priority level assigned to the alert based on consent type, patient care impact, and time to expiration. Drives workflow routing and staff assignment.",
consent,lifecycle_operations,expiration_alert,alert_status,alert_status,Alert Status,STRING,,,,open|acknowledged|in_progress|resolved|escalated|cancelled,transactional_data,Current lifecycle status of the consent expiration alert. Open indicates new alert requiring attention; acknowledged indicates staff awareness; in progress indicates renewal workflow initiated; resolved indicates consent renewed or issue addressed; escalated indicates elevated priority; cancelled indicates alert no longer applicable.,
consent,lifecycle_operations,expiration_alert,alert_type,alert_type,Alert Type,STRING,,,,approaching_expiration|expired|renewal_required|grace_period|critical,transactional_data,Classification of the expiration alert based on urgency and timing. Approaching expiration indicates consent nearing end date; expired indicates consent has lapsed; renewal required indicates proactive action needed; grace period indicates post-expiration window; critical indicates immediate action required to prevent care disruption.,
consent,lifecycle_operations,expiration_alert,auto_renewal_eligible_flag,auto_renewal_eligible_flag,Auto-Renewal Eligible Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,Indicates whether the consent is eligible for automatic renewal without patient re-signature based on consent type and organizational policy. True if auto-renewal allowed; false if patient action required.,
consent,lifecycle_operations,expiration_alert,care_impact_flag,care_impact_flag,Care Impact Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,"Indicates whether the expiring consent has direct impact on patient care delivery. True if consent expiration would delay or prevent scheduled treatment, procedures, or services; false if administrative only.",
consent,lifecycle_operations,expiration_alert,consent_expiration_date,consent_expiration_date,Consent Expiration Date,DATE,,,,,transactional_data,The date on which the referenced consent record expires or expired. Denormalized from consent record for alert processing efficiency and historical tracking.,
consent,lifecycle_operations,expiration_alert,consent_scope,consent_scope,Consent Scope,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"The scope or coverage of the expiring consent. Denormalized from consent record to inform renewal urgency. Examples: General Treatment, Specific Procedure, Research Study Participation, Broad Data Sharing, Limited Disclosure.",
consent,lifecycle_operations,expiration_alert,consent_type,consent_type,Consent Type,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"The category of consent that is expiring. Denormalized from consent record for alert filtering and prioritization. Examples: Treatment Consent, Research Consent, HIPAA Authorization, HIE Opt-In, Telehealth Consent, Data Sharing Authorization.",
consent,lifecycle_operations,expiration_alert,created_timestamp,created_timestamp,Created Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,Date and time when this alert record was first created in the data platform. Used for audit trail and data lineage tracking.,
consent,lifecycle_operations,expiration_alert,days_until_expiration,days_until_expiration,Days Until Expiration,INT,,,,,transactional_data,Number of days remaining until consent expiration at the time of alert generation. Negative values indicate days since expiration. Used for alert prioritization and workflow routing.,
consent,lifecycle_operations,expiration_alert,escalation_date,escalation_date,Escalation Date,DATE,,,,,transactional_data,The date on which the alert was escalated. Null if no escalation occurred.,
consent,lifecycle_operations,expiration_alert,escalation_flag,escalation_flag,Escalation Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,"Indicates whether this alert has been escalated to higher authority or management due to unresolved status, patient unreachability, or care impact. True if escalated; false if standard workflow.",
consent,lifecycle_operations,expiration_alert,escalation_reason,escalation_reason,Escalation Reason,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"The reason or justification for escalating the alert. Examples: Patient unreachable after multiple attempts, consent critical for scheduled procedure, regulatory compliance risk, patient dispute.",
consent,lifecycle_operations,expiration_alert,last_reminder_date,last_reminder_date,Last Reminder Date,DATE,,,,,transactional_data,The date of the most recent reminder notification sent for this alert. Used to schedule follow-up reminders and assess communication frequency.,
consent,lifecycle_operations,expiration_alert,last_updated_timestamp,last_updated_timestamp,Last Updated Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,Date and time when this alert record was most recently modified. Tracks alert lifecycle changes and status updates.,
consent,lifecycle_operations,expiration_alert,next_action_due_date,next_action_due_date,Next Action Due Date,DATE,,,,,transactional_data,"The target date by which the next action (patient contact, escalation, resolution) should be completed. Drives workflow task scheduling and SLA monitoring.",
consent,lifecycle_operations,expiration_alert,notification_channel,notification_channel,Notification Channel,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Primary communication channel used to deliver the expiration alert notification. Patient portal for patient-facing alerts; staff worklist for clinical team alerts; EHR alert for in-system notifications; email, SMS, phone, mail for direct outreach; none if alert is internal only. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: patient_portal|staff_worklist|ehr_alert|email|sms|phone|mail|none — 8 candidates stripped; promote to reference product]",
consent,lifecycle_operations,expiration_alert,notification_delivery_status,notification_delivery_status,Notification Delivery Status,STRING,,,,pending|sent|delivered|failed|bounced|read,transactional_data,Detailed status of notification delivery attempt. Pending indicates queued; sent indicates transmitted; delivered indicates confirmed receipt; failed indicates delivery error; bounced indicates invalid recipient; read indicates recipient opened notification.,
consent,lifecycle_operations,expiration_alert,notification_sent_flag,notification_sent_flag,Notification Sent Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,Indicates whether an alert notification has been successfully sent through the designated channel. True if notification delivered; false if pending or failed.,
consent,lifecycle_operations,expiration_alert,notification_sent_timestamp,notification_sent_timestamp,Notification Sent Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,Date and time when the alert notification was successfully delivered to the recipient. Null if notification not yet sent or failed.,
consent,lifecycle_operations,expiration_alert,patient_contact_attempted_flag,patient_contact_attempted_flag,Patient Contact Attempted Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,Indicates whether staff have attempted to contact the patient regarding consent renewal. True if outreach initiated; false if no contact attempt made.,
consent,lifecycle_operations,expiration_alert,patient_contact_date,patient_contact_date,Patient Contact Date,DATE,,,,,transactional_data,The date on which staff successfully contacted the patient regarding the expiring consent. Null if contact not yet made or unsuccessful.,
consent,lifecycle_operations,expiration_alert,patient_response,patient_response,Patient Response,STRING,,,,agreed_to_renew|declined_renewal|requested_modification|no_response|unreachable,transactional_data,The patients response to the consent renewal request. Agreed to renew indicates patient consent to continue; declined renewal indicates patient wishes to revoke or not extend; requested modification indicates patient wants changes; no response indicates patient has not replied; unreachable indicates contact attempts failed.,
consent,lifecycle_operations,expiration_alert,regulatory_compliance_flag,regulatory_compliance_flag,Regulatory Compliance Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,"Indicates whether the expiring consent is required for regulatory compliance (HIPAA, research IRB, state law). True if regulatory mandate; false if organizational policy only.",
consent,lifecycle_operations,expiration_alert,reminder_count,reminder_count,Reminder Count,INT,,,,,transactional_data,The number of reminder notifications sent to patient or staff regarding this expiring consent. Used to track outreach intensity and prevent notification fatigue.,
consent,lifecycle_operations,expiration_alert,renewal_method,renewal_method,Renewal Method,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,The method or channel through which consent renewal should be obtained. In-person for clinic visit; patient portal for electronic signature; telehealth for virtual visit; mail for postal forms; phone for verbal consent; email for electronic forms; not applicable if renewal not required. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: in_person|patient_portal|telehealth|mail|phone|email|not_applicable — 7 candidates stripped; promote to reference product],
consent,lifecycle_operations,expiration_alert,renewal_required_flag,renewal_required_flag,Renewal Required Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,Indicates whether the expiring consent requires active patient re-consent or renewal action. True if patient signature or new authorization needed; false if consent can be administratively extended or is not renewable.,
consent,lifecycle_operations,expiration_alert,resolution_date,resolution_date,Resolution Date,DATE,,,,,transactional_data,The date on which the consent expiration alert was resolved or closed. Null if alert remains open.,
consent,lifecycle_operations,expiration_alert,resolution_notes,resolution_notes,Resolution Notes,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Free-text notes documenting the actions taken to resolve the alert, patient interactions, barriers encountered, and final outcome. Supports audit trail and quality improvement.",
consent,lifecycle_operations,expiration_alert,resolution_status,resolution_status,Resolution Status,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,The outcome or resolution of the consent expiration alert. Pending indicates unresolved; consent renewed indicates patient re-consented; consent revoked indicates patient declined continuation; consent expired indicates lapsed without renewal; administrative extension indicates organizational extension granted; patient unreachable indicates contact failure; no action required indicates alert cancelled or superseded. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: pending|consent_renewed|consent_revoked|consent_expired|administrative_extension|patient_unreachable|no_action_required — 7 candidates stripped; promote to reference product],
consent,lifecycle_operations,expiration_alert,resolution_timestamp,resolution_timestamp,Resolution Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,Precise date and time when the alert was resolved or closed. Used for alert resolution time analysis and Service Level Agreement (SLA) compliance tracking.,
consent,lifecycle_operations,expiration_alert,responsible_staff_role,responsible_staff_role,Responsible Staff Role,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"The functional role or job title of the staff member assigned to this alert. Examples: Consent Coordinator, Case Manager, Primary Care Physician (PCP), Nurse Navigator, Health Information Management (HIM) Specialist.",
consent,lifecycle_operations,expiration_alert,scheduled_procedure_date,scheduled_procedure_date,Scheduled Procedure Date,DATE,,,,,transactional_data,The date of a scheduled procedure or service that requires the expiring consent. Used to assess urgency and care impact of unresolved alert.,
consent,lifecycle_operations,expiration_alert,sla_breach_flag,sla_breach_flag,Service Level Agreement (SLA) Breach Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,Indicates whether the alert resolution exceeded the SLA target resolution time. True if SLA breached; false if resolved within target.,
consent,lifecycle_operations,expiration_alert,sla_target_resolution_hours,sla_target_resolution_hours,Service Level Agreement (SLA) Target Resolution Hours,INT,,,,,transactional_data,The number of hours within which this alert should be resolved per organizational Service Level Agreement (SLA). Based on alert priority and consent type.,
consent,lifecycle_operations,expiration_alert,source_system,source_system,Source System,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"The name of the system or application that generated this consent expiration alert. Examples: Epic EHR Consent Module, Cerner Consent Management, Custom Consent Monitoring Service.",
consent,lifecycle_operations,revocation,revocation_id,revocation_id,Consent Revocation Identifier (ID),BIGINT,Y,,,,transactional_data,Unique identifier for the consent revocation record. Primary key for the consent revocation entity.,
