encounter,clinical_documentation,drg_assignment,actual_los,actual_los,Actual Length of Stay (LOS),"DECIMAL(6,2)",,,,,transactional_data,"The actual number of days the patient was hospitalized for this encounter, calculated from admission to discharge. Compared against geometric and arithmetic mean LOS for efficiency and outlier analysis.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,drg_assignment,admit_source_code,admit_source_code,Admission Source Code,STRING,,,,"^[0-9]{1,2}$",transactional_data,"The UB-04 admission source code indicating how the patient was admitted (e.g., 1=Physician Referral, 4=Transfer from Hospital, 7=Emergency Room). Influences DRG grouping logic for certain MDCs.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,drg_assignment,arithmetic_mean_los,arithmetic_mean_los,Arithmetic Mean Length of Stay (LOS),"DECIMAL(6,2)",,,,,transactional_data,"The arithmetic mean length of stay in days for the assigned DRG, published by CMS. Used alongside geometric mean LOS for outlier threshold determination and payer contract benchmarking.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,drg_assignment,base_payment_rate,base_payment_rate,DRG Base Payment Rate,"DECIMAL(12,2)",,,dbx_confidential,,transactional_data,The hospital-specific or payer-contracted base payment rate (in USD) applied to the DRG weight to calculate expected reimbursement. Reflects IPPS standardized amount or negotiated payer contract rate.,
encounter,clinical_documentation,drg_assignment,cc_mcc_flag,cc_mcc_flag,Complication and Comorbidity / Major Complication and Comorbidity (CC/MCC) Flag,STRING,,,,MCC|CC|None,transactional_data,"Indicates whether the encounter qualifies for a Complication and Comorbidity (CC) or Major Complication and Comorbidity (MCC) designation, which elevates the DRG tier and associated reimbursement weight. Critical CDI target for revenue optimization.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,drg_assignment,cdi_query_count,cdi_query_count,Clinical Documentation Improvement (CDI) Query Count,INT,,,,,transactional_data,The number of CDI queries issued to the attending physician for this encounter to clarify or improve clinical documentation supporting the DRG assignment. Key CDI productivity and impact metric.,
encounter,clinical_documentation,drg_assignment,cdi_query_response_flag,cdi_query_response_flag,Clinical Documentation Improvement (CDI) Query Response Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,Indicates whether at least one CDI query for this encounter received a physician response that resulted in a documentation change affecting the DRG assignment. Measures CDI program effectiveness.,
encounter,clinical_documentation,drg_assignment,claim_appeal_status,claim_appeal_status,DRG Appeal Status,STRING,,,,not_appealed|pending|upheld|overturned|withdrawn,transactional_data,Current status of any payer or RAC appeal related to this DRG assignment. Tracks the outcome of reimbursement disputes through the appeals process.,
encounter,clinical_documentation,drg_assignment,created_timestamp,created_timestamp,Record Created Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,The date and time when this DRG assignment record was first created in the system. Supports audit trail requirements and data lineage tracking.,
encounter,clinical_documentation,drg_assignment,discharge_status_code,discharge_status_code,Patient Discharge Status Code,STRING,,,,^[0-9]{2}$,transactional_data,"The UB-04 patient discharge status code (01–99) indicating the disposition of the patient at discharge (e.g., 01=Home, 02=SNF, 20=Expired). Affects DRG payment under post-acute care transfer rules.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,drg_assignment,drg_changed_flag,drg_changed_flag,DRG Changed Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,"Indicates whether the DRG code was changed from the initial working DRG to the final assigned DRG, typically as a result of CDI query responses or coding review. Tracks CDI program impact on reimbursement.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,drg_assignment,drg_description,drg_description,Diagnosis-Related Group (DRG) Description,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Full text description of the assigned DRG code (e.g., SIMPLE PNEUMONIA AND PLEURISY W MCC). Used in clinical documentation improvement workflows and reimbursement reporting.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,drg_assignment,drg_version,drg_version,Diagnosis-Related Group (DRG) Version,STRING,,,,MS-DRG|APR-DRG|IR-DRG,transactional_data,"The DRG classification system version used for grouping: MS-DRG (Medicare Severity), APR-DRG (All Patient Refined), or IR-DRG (International Refined). Determines the applicable reimbursement methodology and payer contract.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,drg_assignment,drg_version_number,drg_version_number,Diagnosis-Related Group (DRG) Version Number,STRING,,,,"^v?[0-9]{1,2}(.[0-9]{1,2})?$",transactional_data,"The specific fiscal year or release version of the DRG grouper applied (e.g., v41 for MS-DRG Version 41). Required for audit trails and reimbursement reconciliation across fiscal year transitions.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,drg_assignment,drg_weight,drg_weight,Diagnosis-Related Group (DRG) Relative Weight,"DECIMAL(10,4)",,,,,transactional_data,"The relative weight assigned to the DRG, reflecting the average resource intensity of cases in that group relative to the average Medicare case. Used to calculate CMI and expected reimbursement from the base payment rate.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,drg_assignment,expected_reimbursement,expected_reimbursement,Expected DRG Reimbursement Amount,"DECIMAL(12,2)",,,dbx_confidential,,transactional_data,"The calculated expected reimbursement amount (in USD) derived from DRG weight multiplied by the base payment rate, before outlier adjustments. Used for revenue forecasting and variance analysis against actual payments.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,drg_assignment,finalized_timestamp,finalized_timestamp,DRG Finalized Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,"The date and time when the DRG assignment was finalized by the coding team, triggering claim submission eligibility. Key milestone in the revenue cycle management workflow.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,drg_assignment,geometric_mean_los,geometric_mean_los,Geometric Mean Length of Stay (LOS),"DECIMAL(6,2)",,,,,transactional_data,"The geometric mean length of stay in days for the assigned DRG, published by CMS. Used as a benchmark for LOS efficiency analysis and outlier payment threshold calculations.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,drg_assignment,grouper_software,grouper_software,Grouper Software Name,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Name of the DRG grouper software used to assign the DRG (e.g., 3M Grouper Plus, OptumInsight Encoder). Required for audit trails and reimbursement dispute resolution.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,drg_assignment,grouper_software_version,grouper_software_version,Grouper Software Version,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"The specific release version of the grouper software applied (e.g., 3M Grouper Plus v32.1). Critical for audit compliance and reimbursement reconciliation when grouper logic changes between versions.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,drg_assignment,grouping_date,grouping_date,DRG Grouping Date,DATE,,,,,transactional_data,The calendar date on which the DRG grouper software was executed and the DRG code was assigned. Used for tracking CDI workflow timelines and coding productivity.,
encounter,clinical_documentation,drg_assignment,initial_drg_code,initial_drg_code,Initial Working Diagnosis-Related Group (DRG) Code,STRING,,,,^[0-9]{3}$,transactional_data,"The DRG code assigned at the initial working grouping (typically at admission or during the stay), before final coding and CDI review. Compared against the final DRG to measure CDI program impact and reimbursement uplift.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,drg_assignment,initial_drg_weight,initial_drg_weight,Initial Working Diagnosis-Related Group (DRG) Relative Weight,"DECIMAL(10,4)",,,,,transactional_data,The DRG relative weight associated with the initial working DRG code. Used to calculate the reimbursement uplift achieved through CDI and coding optimization.,
encounter,clinical_documentation,drg_assignment,is_outlier,is_outlier,Cost Outlier Indicator,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,"Indicates whether this encounter qualifies as a cost outlier under CMS IPPS policy, triggering additional outlier payment beyond the standard DRG payment. True when actual costs exceed the fixed-loss threshold.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,drg_assignment,mdc_code,mdc_code,Major Diagnostic Category (MDC) Code,STRING,,,,"^(P[RR]E|[0-9]{1,2})$",transactional_data,The Major Diagnostic Category code (01–25 plus PRE for pre-MDC) that serves as the primary clinical grouping tier above the DRG. Derived from the principal diagnosis and used for service-line analytics and CMI benchmarking.,
encounter,clinical_documentation,drg_assignment,mdc_description,mdc_description,Major Diagnostic Category (MDC) Description,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Full text description of the MDC (e.g., Diseases and Disorders of the Respiratory System). Supports service-line reporting and clinical program analytics.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,drg_assignment,outlier_payment,outlier_payment,Outlier Payment Amount,"DECIMAL(12,2)",,,dbx_confidential,,transactional_data,Additional payment amount (in USD) approved for high-cost outlier cases where actual costs exceed the fixed-loss outlier threshold. Applicable under CMS IPPS cost outlier policy.,
encounter,clinical_documentation,drg_assignment,patient_type,patient_type,Patient Type,STRING,,,,inpatient|observation|short_stay,transactional_data,"Classifies the encounter type for DRG assignment purposes: inpatient (full admission), observation (outpatient observation status), or short_stay. Determines DRG applicability and reimbursement methodology.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,drg_assignment,principal_diagnosis_code,principal_diagnosis_code,Principal Diagnosis ICD-10-CM Code,STRING,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_health","^[A-Z][0-9A-Z]{2,6}(.[0-9A-Z]{1,4})?$",transactional_data,The ICD-10-CM code for the principal diagnosis — the condition established after study to be chiefly responsible for the admission. Drives DRG grouping logic and is a key CDI target for reimbursement optimization.,
encounter,clinical_documentation,drg_assignment,principal_diagnosis_description,principal_diagnosis_description,Principal Diagnosis Description,STRING,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_health",,transactional_data,"Full text description of the principal ICD-10-CM diagnosis code. Supports CDI workflow review, clinical documentation audits, and payer communication.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,drg_assignment,principal_procedure_code,principal_procedure_code,Principal Procedure ICD-10-PCS Code,STRING,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_health",^[0-9A-Z]{7}$,transactional_data,The ICD-10-PCS code for the principal procedure performed during the encounter. Surgical procedures are the primary driver of DRG partition assignment (surgical vs. medical) and reimbursement weight.,
encounter,clinical_documentation,drg_assignment,procedure_count,procedure_count,Procedure Code Count,INT,,,,,transactional_data,"The total number of ICD-10-PCS procedure codes submitted on the claim. Surgical procedures drive DRG assignment into surgical partitions, significantly affecting reimbursement weight.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,drg_assignment,provider_assignment_status,provider_assignment_status,DRG Assignment Status,STRING,,,,preliminary|final|amended|voided,transactional_data,"Current workflow status of the DRG assignment record: preliminary (initial grouping), final (coding complete and validated), amended (revised after CDI query or audit), or voided (invalidated). Drives revenue cycle workflow routing.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,drg_assignment,provider_assignment_type,provider_assignment_type,DRG Assignment Type,STRING,,,,initial|working|final|appeal|rac_review,transactional_data,"Classifies the nature of the DRG assignment: initial (first grouping at admission), working (interim CDI grouping), final (post-discharge coding), appeal (payer dispute), or rac_review (Recovery Audit Contractor review). [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: initial|working|final|appeal|rac_review — promote to reference product]",
encounter,clinical_documentation,drg_assignment,rac_review_flag,rac_review_flag,Recovery Audit Contractor (RAC) Review Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,Indicates whether this DRG assignment has been selected for review by a Recovery Audit Contractor (RAC) under the CMS RAC program. Triggers additional documentation retention and appeal workflow.,
encounter,clinical_documentation,drg_assignment,secondary_diagnosis_count,secondary_diagnosis_count,Secondary Diagnosis Count,INT,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_health",,transactional_data,The total number of secondary (additional) ICD-10-CM diagnosis codes submitted on the claim. Influences CC/MCC determination and DRG tier assignment; a key CDI metric for documentation completeness.,
encounter,clinical_documentation,drg_assignment,source_system,source_system,Source System,STRING,,,,Epic_Resolute_HB|Cerner_Revenue_Cycle|3M_Grouper|MEDITECH_Expanse,transactional_data,"The operational system of record from which this DRG assignment record was sourced (e.g., Epic Resolute HB, 3M Grouper Plus). Required for data lineage, reconciliation, and ETL audit purposes.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,drg_assignment,transfer_case_flag,transfer_case_flag,Transfer Case Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,"Indicates whether this encounter is a transfer case subject to the post-acute care transfer (PACT) policy, which may reduce DRG payment when the patient is transferred to a post-acute care setting before the geometric mean LOS.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,drg_assignment,updated_timestamp,updated_timestamp,Record Updated Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,"The date and time when this DRG assignment record was last modified. Tracks amendments from CDI queries, coding audits, or payer appeals.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,triage_assessment,triage_assessment_id,triage_assessment_id,Triage Assessment ID,BIGINT,Y,,,,transactional_data,Unique surrogate identifier for the triage assessment record in the Silver layer lakehouse. Primary key for this entity.,
encounter,clinical_documentation,triage_assessment,care_site_id,care_site_id,Facility ID,BIGINT,,facility.care_site.care_site_id,,,transactional_data,Reference to the facility (ED or urgent care location) where the triage assessment was conducted. Supports multi-site throughput and capacity analytics.,
encounter,clinical_documentation,triage_assessment,clinical_order_id,clinical_order_id,,BIGINT,,order.clinical_order.clinical_order_id,,,transactional_data,foreign_key_to,
encounter,clinical_documentation,triage_assessment,clinician_id,clinician_id,Triage Nurse Provider ID,BIGINT,,provider.clinician.clinician_id,,,transactional_data,"Reference to the licensed nurse or clinician who performed the triage assessment. Used for accountability, staffing analytics, and EMTALA compliance tracking.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,triage_assessment,employee_id,employee_id,Triage Nurse Employee Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,workforce.employee.employee_id,"dbx_confidential, dbx_pii",,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to workforce.employee. Business justification: Triage nurses are often RNs tracked in workforce (not provider domain). Required for ED staffing models, competency validation (ESI certification), and labor productivity. Complements existing clinici",
encounter,clinical_documentation,triage_assessment,mpi_record_id,mpi_record_id,Patient ID,BIGINT,,patient.mpi_record.mpi_record_id,,,transactional_data,Reference to the patient who was triaged. Core party reference linking the triage assessment to the Master Patient Index (MPI).,
encounter,clinical_documentation,triage_assessment,osha_exposure_incident_id,osha_exposure_incident_id,Osha Exposure Incident Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,compliance.osha_exposure_incident.osha_exposure_incident_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to compliance.osha_exposure_incident. Business justification: Exposure incidents in ED/triage settings (needlesticks, blood/body fluid exposure) require linkage to the triage encounter for root cause analysis, source patient testing coordination, and OSHA 300 lo",
encounter,clinical_documentation,triage_assessment,prior_triage_assessment_id,prior_triage_assessment_id,Prior Triage Assessment ID,BIGINT,,encounter.triage_assessment.triage_assessment_id,,,transactional_data,Reference to the original triage assessment record when this record is a reassessment. Enables linkage of reassessment chains for acuity escalation tracking and waiting room safety analytics.,
encounter,clinical_documentation,triage_assessment,snomed_concept_id,snomed_concept_id,,BIGINT,,reference.snomed_concept.snomed_concept_id,,,transactional_data,FK to reference.snomed_concept.snomed_concept_id,
encounter,clinical_documentation,triage_assessment,visit_id,visit_id,Encounter ID,BIGINT,,encounter.visit.visit_id,,,transactional_data,Reference to the parent Emergency Department (ED) or urgent care encounter for which this triage assessment was performed. Links triage to the broader encounter lifecycle.,
encounter,clinical_documentation,triage_assessment,acuity_change_reason,acuity_change_reason,Acuity Change Reason,STRING,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_health",,transactional_data,Free-text or structured reason documented by the triage nurse when the ESI acuity level is changed during a reassessment. PHI under HIPAA. Used for clinical quality review and patient safety event analysis.,
encounter,clinical_documentation,triage_assessment,ama_flag,ama_flag,Against Medical Advice (AMA) Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,"Indicates whether the patient left the ED Against Medical Advice (AMA) after triage but before completing the full ED visit. Distinct from LWBS — AMA occurs after provider contact. Used for risk management, quality reporting, and EMTALA compliance.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,triage_assessment,arrival_mode,arrival_mode,Mode of Arrival,STRING,,,,ambulance|walk_in|helicopter|police|private_vehicle|transfer,transactional_data,"Method by which the patient arrived at the ED or urgent care facility. Includes ground ambulance, air transport (helicopter), walk-in, police transport, private vehicle, or inter-facility transfer. Used for EMTALA compliance, acuity benchmarking, and EMS coordination analytics.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,triage_assessment,chief_complaint,chief_complaint,Chief Complaint,STRING,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_health",,transactional_data,"Free-text or structured description of the patients primary reason for presenting to the ED or urgent care, as stated by the patient or documented by the triage nurse. Protected Health Information (PHI) under HIPAA. Used for clinical documentation, coding, and population health analytics.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,triage_assessment,chief_complaint_code,chief_complaint_code,Chief Complaint SNOMED CT Code,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Standardized SNOMED CT (Systematized Nomenclature of Medicine Clinical Terms) code representing the chief complaint. Enables structured clinical analytics, interoperability, and population health reporting across systems.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,triage_assessment,consent_record_created_timestamp,consent_record_created_timestamp,Record Created Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,"Date and time when this triage assessment record was first created in the source system. Used for audit trail, data lineage, and Silver layer ingestion tracking.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,triage_assessment,consent_record_updated_timestamp,consent_record_updated_timestamp,Record Last Updated Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,"Date and time when this triage assessment record was most recently modified in the source system. Used for change detection, incremental ETL processing, and audit compliance.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,triage_assessment,diastolic_bp_mmhg,diastolic_bp_mmhg,Diastolic Blood Pressure (BP) in mmHg,INT,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_health",,transactional_data,"Diastolic blood pressure measurement recorded at triage, expressed in millimeters of mercury (mmHg). Used alongside systolic BP for hemodynamic assessment and ESI acuity scoring. PHI under HIPAA.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,triage_assessment,door_arrival_timestamp,door_arrival_timestamp,Door Arrival Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,Date and time the patient physically arrived at the ED or urgent care facility (door time). Used as the baseline for door-to-triage and door-to-provider time quality measures reported to CMS.,
encounter,clinical_documentation,triage_assessment,esi_level,esi_level,Emergency Severity Index (ESI) Level,INT,,,,,transactional_data,"Emergency Severity Index (ESI) triage acuity score assigned by the triage nurse, ranging from 1 (most critical/immediate) to 5 (least urgent/non-urgent). Drives resource allocation, bed assignment priority, and ED throughput analytics. Defined by AHRQ ESI Triage Algorithm.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,triage_assessment,glasgow_coma_score,glasgow_coma_score,Glasgow Coma Scale (GCS) Score,INT,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_health",,transactional_data,"Total Glasgow Coma Scale (GCS) score assessed at triage, ranging from 3 (deep unconsciousness) to 15 (fully alert). Used for neurological status assessment, ESI acuity determination, and trauma triage protocols. PHI under HIPAA.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,triage_assessment,heart_rate_bpm,heart_rate_bpm,Heart Rate (HR) in Beats Per Minute (BPM),INT,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_health",,transactional_data,"Heart rate (pulse) measured at triage, expressed in beats per minute (BPM). Key vital sign for ESI acuity determination and identification of hemodynamic instability. PHI under HIPAA.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,triage_assessment,interpreter_language,interpreter_language,Interpreter Language,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Primary language for which interpretation services are required, using ISO 639-1 two-letter language codes (e.g., es for Spanish, zh for Chinese). Supports LEP compliance reporting and interpreter resource planning.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,triage_assessment,interpreter_required_flag,interpreter_required_flag,Interpreter Required Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,Indicates whether the patient requires language interpretation services during the triage assessment. Supports compliance with Title VI of the Civil Rights Act and CMS Limited English Proficiency (LEP) requirements.,
encounter,clinical_documentation,triage_assessment,isolation_required_flag,isolation_required_flag,Isolation Required Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,"Indicates whether the patient requires isolation precautions at triage (e.g., airborne, droplet, contact, or neutropenic precautions). Drives bed assignment workflows, infection control protocols, and Healthcare-Associated Infection (HAI) prevention measures.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,triage_assessment,isolation_type,isolation_type,Isolation Precaution Type,STRING,,,,airborne|droplet|contact|neutropenic|standard,transactional_data,"Type of isolation precaution required for the patient as determined at triage. Drives room assignment, personal protective equipment (PPE) requirements, and infection control workflows.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,triage_assessment,lwbs_flag,lwbs_flag,Left Without Being Seen (LWBS) Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,Indicates whether the patient left the ED without being seen by a provider after triage (LWBS). Key ED throughput quality metric reported to CMS and used for EMTALA compliance monitoring and operational improvement initiatives.,
encounter,clinical_documentation,triage_assessment,lwbs_timestamp,lwbs_timestamp,Left Without Being Seen (LWBS) Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,"Date and time the patient departed the ED without being seen by a provider, when the LWBS flag is true. Used to calculate time-to-LWBS and identify peak demand periods contributing to patient walkouts.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,triage_assessment,mental_health_flag,mental_health_flag,Mental Health Presentation Flag,BOOLEAN,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii",,transactional_data,"Indicates whether the patients chief complaint or triage assessment involves a primary mental health or behavioral health concern. Used for ED behavioral health throughput analytics, psychiatric bed management, and EMTALA psychiatric screening compliance.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,triage_assessment,pain_scale_type,pain_scale_type,Pain Assessment Scale Type,STRING,,,,numeric|faces|flacc|verbal|behavioral,transactional_data,"Type of validated pain assessment scale used to obtain the pain score at triage. Distinguishes between numeric rating scale (NRS), Wong-Baker FACES (pediatric), FLACC (non-verbal), verbal descriptor, or behavioral observation scales.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,triage_assessment,pain_score,pain_score,Pain Score,INT,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_health",,transactional_data,"Patient-reported pain intensity score at triage, typically on a 0–10 numeric rating scale (NRS) or equivalent validated scale (e.g., Wong-Baker FACES for pediatric patients). Used for ESI acuity determination and Joint Commission pain management compliance. PHI under HIPAA.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,triage_assessment,respiratory_rate_bpm,respiratory_rate_bpm,Respiratory Rate (RR) in Breaths Per Minute,INT,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_health",,transactional_data,"Respiratory rate measured at triage, expressed in breaths per minute. Used for ESI acuity scoring and identification of respiratory distress. PHI under HIPAA.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,triage_assessment,sepsis_alert_flag,sepsis_alert_flag,Sepsis Alert Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,"Indicates whether a sepsis screening alert was triggered at triage based on vital signs and clinical criteria (e.g., SIRS criteria, qSOFA). Supports SEP-1 bundle compliance reporting to CMS and Joint Commission sepsis quality measures.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,triage_assessment,source_system,source_system,Source System,STRING,,,,epic_clindoc|cerner_powerchart|meditech_expanse|manual,transactional_data,"Operational system of record from which this triage assessment record was sourced. Supports data lineage, ETL audit, and multi-system reconciliation in the Silver layer lakehouse.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,triage_assessment,source_system_record_code,source_system_record_code,Source System Record ID,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,Native record identifier from the originating operational system (Epic ClinDoc or Cerner PowerChart ED) for this triage assessment. Enables cross-system traceability and supports Health Information Exchange (HIE) reconciliation.,
encounter,clinical_documentation,triage_assessment,spo2_percent,spo2_percent,Oxygen Saturation (SpO2) Percentage,"DECIMAL(4,1)",,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_health",,transactional_data,"Peripheral oxygen saturation (SpO2) measured by pulse oximetry at triage, expressed as a percentage. Critical indicator for respiratory status and ESI acuity level assignment. PHI under HIPAA.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,triage_assessment,stroke_alert_flag,stroke_alert_flag,Stroke Alert Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,"Indicates whether a stroke alert protocol was activated at triage based on presenting symptoms (e.g., FAST criteria). Supports door-to-CT and door-to-needle time quality measures for stroke care reported to The Joint Commission and CMS.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,triage_assessment,systolic_bp_mmhg,systolic_bp_mmhg,Systolic Blood Pressure (BP) in mmHg,INT,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_health",,transactional_data,"Systolic blood pressure measurement recorded at triage, expressed in millimeters of mercury (mmHg). Critical vital sign for ESI acuity determination and clinical decision support. PHI under HIPAA.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,triage_assessment,temperature_celsius,temperature_celsius,Body Temperature in Degrees Celsius,"DECIMAL(4,1)",,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_health",,transactional_data,"Body temperature measured at triage, expressed in degrees Celsius. Used for ESI acuity determination, sepsis screening, and infection surveillance. PHI under HIPAA.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,triage_assessment,temperature_route,temperature_route,Temperature Measurement Route,STRING,,,,oral|rectal|axillary|tympanic|temporal,transactional_data,"Anatomical route used to obtain the body temperature measurement at triage (e.g., oral, rectal, axillary, tympanic, temporal). Affects clinical interpretation of temperature values.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,triage_assessment,trauma_activation_flag,trauma_activation_flag,Trauma Activation Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,"Indicates whether a trauma team activation was initiated at or following triage. Used for trauma registry reporting, ACS trauma center verification, and ED resource utilization analytics.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,triage_assessment,trauma_level,trauma_level,Trauma Activation Level,STRING,,,,level_1|level_2|level_3,transactional_data,"Level of trauma team activation triggered at triage (Level 1 = full activation for most critical injuries, Level 2 = partial activation, Level 3 = consult/standby). Drives resource deployment and trauma registry classification.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,triage_assessment,triage_category,triage_category,Triage Category,STRING,,,,emergent|urgent|semi_urgent|non_urgent|immediate,transactional_data,"Categorical classification of triage acuity corresponding to the ESI level. Supports ED throughput reporting, staffing models, and payer analytics. Values align with standard ED triage nomenclature.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,triage_assessment,triage_completed_timestamp,triage_completed_timestamp,Triage Completion Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,Date and time when the triage assessment was fully documented and completed by the triage nurse. Used to calculate triage duration and nurse productivity metrics.,
encounter,clinical_documentation,triage_assessment,triage_number,triage_number,Triage Assessment Number,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Externally visible, human-readable identifier for the triage assessment record as assigned by the source system (Epic ClinDoc or Cerner PowerChart ED). Used for cross-system reconciliation and audit trails.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,triage_assessment,triage_nurse_npi,triage_nurse_npi,Triage Nurse National Provider Identifier (NPI),STRING,,,,^[0-9]{10}$,transactional_data,National Provider Identifier (NPI) of the licensed nurse or clinician who performed the triage assessment. Required for EMTALA compliance documentation and provider-level quality reporting. Sourced from Epic ClinDoc or Cerner PowerChart ED.,
encounter,clinical_documentation,triage_assessment,triage_reassessment_flag,triage_reassessment_flag,Triage Reassessment Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,"Indicates whether this triage record represents a reassessment of a previously triaged patient (e.g., patient condition changed while waiting). Supports tracking of acuity escalation events and waiting room safety monitoring.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,triage_assessment,triage_status,triage_status,Triage Assessment Status,STRING,,,,in_progress|completed|amended|voided,transactional_data,"Current workflow state of the triage assessment record. Indicates whether triage documentation is in progress, finalized, subsequently amended, or voided.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,triage_assessment,triage_timestamp,triage_timestamp,Triage Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,Date and time when the triage assessment was initiated by the triage nurse. This is the principal business event timestamp used to calculate door-to-triage time and ED throughput quality measures.,
encounter,clinical_documentation,triage_assessment,weight_kg,weight_kg,Patient Weight in Kilograms,"DECIMAL(5,1)",,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_health",,transactional_data,"Patient weight measured or reported at triage, expressed in kilograms. Used for medication dosing calculations, pediatric weight-based protocols, and clinical decision support. PHI under HIPAA.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,visit_diagnosis,visit_diagnosis_id,visit_diagnosis_id,Visit Diagnosis ID,BIGINT,Y,," dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_health",,transactional_data,Unique surrogate identifier for each visit diagnosis record in the Silver layer lakehouse. Primary key for this encounter-level diagnosis entity. Role: TRANSACTION_LINE — this record is a line-level diagnosis attached to a parent encounter/visit header.,
encounter,clinical_documentation,visit_diagnosis,clinician_id,clinician_id,Attending Provider ID,BIGINT,,provider.clinician.clinician_id,,,transactional_data,"Reference to the attending physician responsible for the patients care during this encounter, as associated with this diagnosis. Used for provider-level quality reporting, MIPS attribution, and UB-04 claim form population. Aligns with PARTY_REFERENCE canonical category.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,visit_diagnosis,cost_center_id,cost_center_id,Cost Center Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,finance.cost_center.cost_center_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to finance.cost_center. Business justification: Diagnosis coding drives reimbursement and HCC risk adjustment. Linking to cost centers enables service-line profitability analysis, clinical program financial performance, and diagnosis-related cost b",
encounter,clinical_documentation,visit_diagnosis,icd_code_id,icd_code_id,Icd Code Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,reference.icd_code.icd_code_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to reference.icd_code. Business justification: Core clinical coding workflow—every diagnosis on a visit must reference the official ICD-10 code set for billing compliance, quality reporting, HCC risk adjustment, and clinical documentation integrit",
encounter,clinical_documentation,visit_diagnosis,material_master_id,material_master_id,Material Master Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,supply.material_master.material_master_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to supply.material_master. Business justification: Diagnoses often require specific medications or supplies (diabetes→insulin, wounds→dressings). Formulary management, clinical pathway optimization, and diagnosis-related supply cost analysis depend on",
encounter,clinical_documentation,visit_diagnosis,mpi_record_id,mpi_record_id,Patient ID,BIGINT,,patient.mpi_record.mpi_record_id,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_health",,transactional_data,"Reference to the patient associated with this visit diagnosis. Supports patient-level longitudinal diagnosis history, population health analytics, and risk adjustment. Classified as restricted PHI per HIPAA.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,visit_diagnosis,note_id,note_id,Clinical Note ID,BIGINT,,clinical.note.note_id,,,transactional_data,"Reference to the clinical note or documentation that supports this diagnosis. Links the coded diagnosis back to the source clinical documentation for CDI, audit, and RAC defense purposes. Sourced from Epic ClinDoc.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,visit_diagnosis,research_study_id,research_study_id,Research Study Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,research.research_study.research_study_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to research.research_study. Business justification: Research protocols require tracking diagnoses occurring during study participation for safety monitoring, endpoint assessment, and adverse event reporting. Clinical research operations need to identif",
encounter,clinical_documentation,visit_diagnosis,snomed_concept_id,snomed_concept_id,Snomed Concept Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,reference.snomed_concept.snomed_concept_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to reference.snomed_concept. Business justification: Clinical terminology mapping—SNOMED codes on diagnoses must reference the official SNOMED CT concept for interoperability, clinical decision support, quality measure reporting, and data exchange with ",
encounter,clinical_documentation,visit_diagnosis,visit_id,visit_id,Encounter ID,BIGINT,,encounter.visit.visit_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key reference to the parent encounter/visit record. Establishes the HEADER_REFERENCE relationship linking this diagnosis line to its owning visit. Central to DRG grouping, quality reporting, and revenue cycle processing.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,visit_diagnosis,bill_indicator,bill_indicator,Billable Diagnosis Indicator,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,"Indicates whether this diagnosis code is included on the claim submitted to the payer. True = included on the claim. Some diagnoses may be documented clinically but excluded from billing (e.g., working diagnoses, non-billable codes). Drives UB-04 and CMS-1500 claim form population.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,visit_diagnosis,cc_mcc_indicator,cc_mcc_indicator,Complication/Comorbidity (CC) / Major Complication/Comorbidity (MCC) Indicator,STRING,,,,CC|MCC|HAC|none,transactional_data,"Classifies this diagnosis as a Complication/Comorbidity (CC), Major Complication/Comorbidity (MCC), Hospital-Acquired Condition (HAC), or none. Directly impacts MS-DRG assignment and inpatient reimbursement under IPPS. Sourced from 3M HIS grouper output and CMS CC/MCC exclusion lists.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,visit_diagnosis,chronic_condition_flag,chronic_condition_flag,Chronic Condition Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,"Indicates whether this diagnosis represents a chronic condition as defined by CMS Chronic Condition Warehouse (CCW) or clinical classification standards. True = chronic condition. Supports population health management, care management program enrollment, HEDIS chronic disease measure attribution, and SDOH analysis.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,visit_diagnosis,coded_date,coded_date,Diagnosis Coded Date,DATE,,,,,transactional_data,"The date on which the ICD-10-CM code was assigned to this diagnosis by the HIM coding team. Used for coding productivity tracking, CDI program metrics, and revenue cycle timeliness reporting. Sourced from 3M HIS and Epic Resolute coding workflows.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,visit_diagnosis,coding_provider_npi,coding_provider_npi,Coding Provider National Provider Identifier (NPI),STRING,,,,^[0-9]{10}$,transactional_data,"The 10-digit National Provider Identifier (NPI) of the clinician or coder who assigned or attested this diagnosis code. Used for audit trails, CDI accountability, RAC audit defense, and provider-level coding quality reporting. Sourced from 3M HIS and Epic ClinDoc coding workflows.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,visit_diagnosis,coding_status,coding_status,Coding Status,STRING,,,,pending|coded|validated|queried|amended|final,transactional_data,Current workflow status of this diagnosis record within the HIM/CDI coding lifecycle. pending indicates awaiting coder review; coded indicates initial code assignment; validated indicates coder-confirmed; queried indicates a CDI query has been issued; amended indicates a post-bill correction; final indicates billing-ready. Drives revenue cycle workflow and CDI query management in 3M HIS and Epic Resolute.,
encounter,clinical_documentation,visit_diagnosis,created_timestamp,created_timestamp,Record Created Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,"The timestamp when this visit diagnosis record was first created in the source system or ingested into the Silver layer. Supports audit trail, data lineage, and RECORD_AUDIT_CREATED canonical category requirement.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,visit_diagnosis,diagnosis_rank,diagnosis_rank,Diagnosis Rank,INT,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_health",,transactional_data,"Clinical ranking of this diagnosis by severity or clinical significance within the encounter, as assigned by the coding team or clinical documentation system. Distinct from diagnosis_seq_num (billing sequence); this rank reflects clinical priority for care management and quality reporting purposes.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,visit_diagnosis,diagnosis_seq_num,diagnosis_seq_num,Diagnosis Sequence Number,INT,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_health",,transactional_data,"Ordinal position of this diagnosis within the encounters diagnosis list. Sequence 1 typically denotes the principal diagnosis. Used for claim form ordering (UB-04 diagnosis fields), DRG grouping logic, and quality measure attribution. Aligns with LINE_SEQUENCE canonical category.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,visit_diagnosis,diagnosis_source,diagnosis_source,Diagnosis Source,STRING,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_health",physician|coder|cdi_specialist|system|imported,transactional_data,Identifies who or what originated this diagnosis record. physician = entered by the treating clinician; coder = assigned by HIM coding staff; cdi_specialist = added via CDI query resolution; system = auto-populated by clinical decision support; imported = received via HIE or external system. Supports audit trail and coding accountability.,
encounter,clinical_documentation,visit_diagnosis,diagnosis_type,diagnosis_type,Diagnosis Type,STRING,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_health",admitting|principal|secondary|discharge|working|final,transactional_data,Classification of the diagnosis role within the encounter. admitting is the reason for admission; principal is the condition chiefly responsible for the stay after study; secondary are comorbidities and complications; discharge is the final coded diagnosis at discharge; working is a provisional diagnosis during the encounter; final is the confirmed diagnosis post-workup. Drives DRG assignment and UB-04/CMS-1500 claim form population.,
encounter,clinical_documentation,visit_diagnosis,drg_code,drg_code,Diagnosis-Related Group (DRG) Code,STRING,,,,^[0-9]{3}$,transactional_data,The MS-DRG or APR-DRG code assigned to the encounter as influenced by this diagnosis. Populated after DRG grouping by 3M HIS or CMS grouper. Central to inpatient reimbursement under IPPS and case mix index (CMI) calculation.,
encounter,clinical_documentation,visit_diagnosis,drg_relevance_flag,drg_relevance_flag,Diagnosis-Related Group (DRG) Relevance Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,Indicates whether this diagnosis code contributes to the DRG assignment for this encounter. True = this diagnosis is a complication/comorbidity (CC) or major complication/comorbidity (MCC) that affects DRG grouping and reimbursement. Critical for revenue cycle optimization and CDI program targeting.,
encounter,clinical_documentation,visit_diagnosis,drg_type,drg_type,Diagnosis-Related Group (DRG) Type,STRING,,,,MS-DRG|APR-DRG|IR-DRG,transactional_data,"Specifies the DRG classification system used: MS-DRG (Medicare Severity DRG, CMS), APR-DRG (All Patient Refined DRG, 3M), or IR-DRG (International Refined DRG). Determines the reimbursement methodology and payer applicability.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,visit_diagnosis,encounter_diagnosis_comment,encounter_diagnosis_comment,Encounter Diagnosis Comment,STRING,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_health",,transactional_data,"Free-text clinical comment or qualifier associated with this diagnosis record, as entered by the coding team or clinician. May include specificity notes, CDI query resolution rationale, or coding clarifications. Classified as restricted PHI per HIPAA.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,visit_diagnosis,encounter_diagnosis_source_code,encounter_diagnosis_source_code,Encounter Diagnosis Source System ID,STRING,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_health",,transactional_data,"The native identifier for this diagnosis record in the source operational system (e.g., Epic ClinDoc diagnosis ID or Cerner PowerChart diagnosis ID). Supports ETL lineage, data reconciliation, and source system audit trails in the Silver layer.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,visit_diagnosis,external_cause_code,external_cause_code,External Cause of Injury (ICD-10-CM) Code,STRING,,,,"^[VWX][0-9A-Z]{2,6}(.[0-9A-Z]{1,4})?$|^Y[0-9A-Z]{2,6}(.[0-9A-Z]{1,4})?$",transactional_data,"ICD-10-CM external cause code (V, W, X, Y codes) documenting the cause, place of occurrence, activity, and status for injury and poisoning diagnoses. Required for trauma registries, injury surveillance, workers compensation claims, and public health reporting.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,visit_diagnosis,hai_flag,hai_flag,Healthcare-Associated Infection (HAI) Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,"Indicates whether this diagnosis represents a healthcare-associated infection (HAI) such as CLABSI, CAUTI, or SSI. True = HAI diagnosis. Triggers HAI surveillance workflows, CMS HAC Reduction Program payment adjustments, and TJC infection control reporting.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,visit_diagnosis,hcc_category_code,hcc_category_code,Hierarchical Condition Category (HCC) Category Code,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"The specific CMS HCC category code to which this ICD-10-CM diagnosis maps. Populated only when hcc_flag is True. Used for risk score calculation in Medicare Advantage, ACO, and MIPS/APM programs. Sourced from CMS HCC mapping crosswalk tables.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,visit_diagnosis,hcc_flag,hcc_flag,Hierarchical Condition Category (HCC) Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,"Indicates whether this ICD-10-CM diagnosis code maps to a CMS Hierarchical Condition Category (HCC) used for risk adjustment in Medicare Advantage and ACO programs. True = this diagnosis contributes to the patients HCC risk score. Critical for population health management, value-based care contracting, and capitation payment accuracy.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,visit_diagnosis,icd10_code,icd10_code,International Classification of Diseases 10th Revision (ICD-10) Code,STRING,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_health","^[A-Z][0-9A-Z]{1,6}(.[0-9A-Z]{1,4})?$",transactional_data,"The ICD-10-CM diagnosis code assigned to this visit. Drives DRG grouping, quality measure attribution, risk adjustment (HCC mapping), and medical billing. Sourced from Epic ClinDoc and validated through 3M HIS coding workflows. Conforms to WHO ICD-10-CM code format.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,visit_diagnosis,icd10_description,icd10_description,International Classification of Diseases 10th Revision (ICD-10) Diagnosis Description,STRING,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_health",,transactional_data,"Full clinical description of the ICD-10-CM diagnosis code as defined by the WHO/CMS code set. Provides human-readable context for the coded diagnosis. Used in clinical documentation, reporting, and CDI workflows.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,visit_diagnosis,icd10_version,icd10_version,ICD-10-CM Fiscal Year Version,STRING,,,,^FY[0-9]{4}$,transactional_data,"The fiscal year version of the ICD-10-CM code set used to assign this diagnosis code (e.g., FY2024). ICD-10-CM is updated annually by CMS/CDC. Ensures accurate code interpretation across fiscal year transitions and supports historical data analysis.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,visit_diagnosis,mental_health_flag,mental_health_flag,Mental Health Diagnosis Flag,BOOLEAN,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii",,transactional_data,"Indicates whether this diagnosis is classified as a mental health or behavioral health condition per ICD-10-CM Chapter 5 (F-codes). True = mental/behavioral health diagnosis. Supports behavioral health program management, parity compliance reporting, and population health segmentation.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,visit_diagnosis,onset_date,onset_date,Diagnosis Onset Date,DATE,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_health",,transactional_data,"The date on which the diagnosed condition first manifested or was first identified, as documented in the clinical record. Supports longitudinal disease tracking, chronic condition management, POA determination, and population health analytics. Aligns with BUSINESS_EVENT_TIMESTAMP canonical category.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,visit_diagnosis,poa_indicator,poa_indicator,Present on Admission (POA) Indicator,STRING,,,,Y|N|U|W|1,transactional_data,"Indicates whether the diagnosis condition was present at the time of inpatient admission. Values: Y=Yes (present on admission), N=No (not present on admission), U=Unknown, W=Clinically undetermined, 1=Exempt from POA reporting. Required by CMS for inpatient claims on UB-04. Impacts HAI reporting, VBP penalties, and hospital-acquired condition (HAC) payment adjustments.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,visit_diagnosis,primary_diagnosis_flag,primary_diagnosis_flag,Primary Diagnosis Flag,BOOLEAN,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_health",,transactional_data,Indicates whether this diagnosis is designated as the primary/principal diagnosis for the encounter. True = primary diagnosis. Provides a quick boolean filter for analytics and reporting without requiring sequence number logic. Complements diagnosis_seq_num and diagnosis_type.,
encounter,clinical_documentation,visit_diagnosis,quality_measure_flag,quality_measure_flag,Quality Measure Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,"Indicates whether this diagnosis contributes to one or more quality measure denominators or numerators (e.g., HEDIS, MIPS, VBP, TJC core measures). True = this diagnosis is relevant to at least one active quality measure. Supports quality reporting, MIPS scoring, and VBP program management.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,visit_diagnosis,reportable_condition_flag,reportable_condition_flag,Reportable Condition Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,"Indicates whether this diagnosis is a notifiable/reportable condition requiring mandatory reporting to public health authorities (e.g., state health departments, CDC). True = reportable. Supports public health surveillance, regulatory compliance, and HIE reporting obligations.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,visit_diagnosis,resolved_date,resolved_date,Diagnosis Resolved Date,DATE,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_health",,transactional_data,"The date on which the diagnosed condition was resolved, abated, or no longer active, as documented in the clinical record. Null if the condition is ongoing. Used for chronic disease management, care plan updates, and longitudinal patient health tracking.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,visit_diagnosis,sdoh_flag,sdoh_flag,Social Determinants of Health (SDOH) Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,"Indicates whether this diagnosis code represents a Social Determinants of Health (SDOH) factor (e.g., Z-codes for housing instability, food insecurity, transportation barriers). True = SDOH-related diagnosis. Supports population health management, care coordination, and CMS SDOH reporting initiatives.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,visit_diagnosis,snomed_code,snomed_code,Systematized Nomenclature of Medicine Clinical Terms (SNOMED CT) Code,STRING,,,,"^[0-9]{6,18}$",transactional_data,"The SNOMED CT concept identifier mapped to this ICD-10-CM diagnosis code. Supports clinical interoperability, HL7 FHIR-based HIE data exchange, and clinical decision support. Populated via ICD-10 to SNOMED CT crosswalk. Used in FHIR Condition resources for interoperability.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,visit_diagnosis,source_system,source_system,Source System,STRING,,,,Epic|Cerner|MEDITECH|3M_HIS|imported,transactional_data,"Identifies the operational system of record from which this visit diagnosis record was sourced. Supports data lineage, ETL audit, and multi-system reconciliation in the Silver lakehouse layer.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,visit_diagnosis,substance_use_flag,substance_use_flag,Substance Use Disorder (SUD) Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,"Indicates whether this diagnosis represents a substance use disorder (SUD) per ICD-10-CM codes. True = substance use disorder diagnosis. Supports SUD program management, 42 CFR Part 2 confidentiality compliance, and population health analytics.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,visit_diagnosis,updated_timestamp,updated_timestamp,Record Updated Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,"The timestamp when this visit diagnosis record was last modified in the source system or Silver layer. Supports change data capture, audit trail, and RECORD_AUDIT_UPDATED canonical category requirement.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,visit_procedure,visit_procedure_id,visit_procedure_id,Visit Procedure ID,BIGINT,Y,,,,transactional_data,Unique surrogate identifier for each procedure record performed during a patient visit. Primary key for the visit_procedure data product in the encounter domain.,
encounter,clinical_documentation,visit_procedure,cost_center_id,cost_center_id,Cost Center Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,finance.cost_center.cost_center_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to finance.cost_center. Business justification: Procedures are performed in specific departments/cost centers. Essential for activity-based costing, OR suite profitability analysis, procedural revenue tracking, and CPT-based cost allocation for dep",
encounter,clinical_documentation,visit_procedure,cpt_code_id,cpt_code_id,Cpt Code Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,reference.cpt_code.cpt_code_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to reference.cpt_code. Business justification: Essential procedure coding workflow—every CPT code on a visit procedure must validate against the official CPT reference for claims submission, reimbursement calculation, RVU assignment, and NCCI edit",
encounter,clinical_documentation,visit_procedure,hcpcs_code_id,hcpcs_code_id,Hcpcs Code Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,reference.hcpcs_code.hcpcs_code_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to reference.hcpcs_code. Business justification: Required for HCPCS procedure coding—DME, supplies, drugs, and non-physician services must reference official HCPCS codes for billing, coverage determination, and reimbursement. Critical for outpatient",
encounter,clinical_documentation,visit_procedure,icd_code_id,icd_code_id,Icd10 Pcs Code Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,reference.icd_code.icd_code_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to reference.icd_code. Business justification: Inpatient procedure coding workflow—ICD-10-PCS codes must validate against the official ICD-10 code set for inpatient claims submission, DRG grouping, and quality measure reporting. Required for hospi",
encounter,clinical_documentation,visit_procedure,interventional_procedure_id,interventional_procedure_id,Interventional Procedure Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,radiology.interventional_procedure.interventional_procedure_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to radiology.interventional_procedure. Business justification: Interventional radiology procedures (biopsies, drainages, embolizations) are billable encounter procedures requiring linkage for charge capture, procedural documentation, and outcomes tracking. IR pro",
encounter,clinical_documentation,visit_procedure,material_master_id,material_master_id,Material Master Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,supply.material_master.material_master_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to supply.material_master. Business justification: Procedures consume specific supplies, devices, and implants that must be documented for billing (CDM charge codes), regulatory compliance (UDI tracking for implantables), and procedure cost analysis. ",
encounter,clinical_documentation,visit_procedure,mpi_record_id,mpi_record_id,Patient ID,BIGINT,,patient.mpi_record.mpi_record_id,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_identifier",,transactional_data,"Reference to the patient on whom the procedure was performed. Supports patient-level procedure history, quality measurement, and population health analytics.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,visit_procedure,or_suite_id,or_suite_id,Operating Room (OR) / Procedure Room ID,BIGINT,,facility.or_suite.or_suite_id,,,transactional_data,"Reference to the operating room or procedure room where the procedure was performed. Supports OR utilization reporting, room turnover analysis, and facility capacity planning.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,visit_procedure,primary_visit_clinician_id,primary_visit_clinician_id,Performing Provider ID,BIGINT,,provider.clinician.clinician_id,,,transactional_data,"Reference to the clinician who performed the procedure. Used for provider-level quality reporting, credentialing validation, and RVU attribution.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,visit_procedure,privileging_id,privileging_id,Privileging Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,provider.privileging.privileging_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to provider.privileging. Business justification: Enables retrospective verification that performing clinician held valid privileges for the specific procedure at the facility on the procedure date. Required for peer review, quality assurance audits,",
encounter,clinical_documentation,visit_procedure,research_study_id,research_study_id,Research Study Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,research.research_study.research_study_id,,,transactional_data,Foreign key linking to research.research_study. Business justification: Research billing requires distinguishing study-mandated procedures from standard-of-care for coverage analysis and sponsor billing. Protocol compliance monitoring needs to verify required procedures w,
encounter,clinical_documentation,visit_procedure,snomed_concept_id,snomed_concept_id,Snomed Concept Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,reference.snomed_concept.snomed_concept_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to reference.snomed_concept. Business justification: Procedure terminology mapping—SNOMED codes on procedures must reference official SNOMED CT for clinical documentation, interoperability, and data exchange with external systems. Required for USCDI com",
encounter,clinical_documentation,visit_procedure,visit_id,visit_id,Encounter ID,BIGINT,,encounter.visit.visit_id,,,transactional_data,"Reference to the parent encounter/visit during which this procedure was performed. Links the procedure to the ADT event, visit type, and associated clinical and billing context.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,visit_procedure,anesthesia_type,anesthesia_type,Anesthesia Type,STRING,,,,general|regional|local|monitored_anesthesia_care|none,transactional_data,"Type of anesthesia administered during the procedure. Drives anesthesia CPT code selection, anesthesia time unit billing, ASA physical status documentation, and OR case complexity classification.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,visit_procedure,asa_class,asa_class,American Society of Anesthesiologists (ASA) Physical Status Classification,STRING,,,,I|II|III|IV|V|VI,transactional_data,"ASA physical status classification assigned by the anesthesiologist prior to the procedure, reflecting the patients overall health status. Used for anesthesia risk stratification, surgical case complexity scoring, and outcomes risk adjustment.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,visit_procedure,body_site,body_site,Procedure Body Site,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Anatomical location or body site where the procedure was performed, coded using SNOMED CT body structure concepts. Supports surgical safety documentation, quality measure stratification, and clinical analytics.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,visit_procedure,cancellation_reason,cancellation_reason,Procedure Cancellation Reason,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Reason code or description explaining why a scheduled procedure was cancelled (e.g., patient not ready, equipment unavailable, surgeon unavailable, insurance denial). Populated only when is_cancelled is true. Supports root cause analysis and OR efficiency improvement.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,visit_procedure,charge_amount,charge_amount,Procedure Charge Amount,"DECIMAL(18,2)",,,dbx_confidential,,transactional_data,"Gross charge amount posted to the patient account for this procedure based on the CDM. Represents the billed amount before contractual adjustments, payer discounts, or patient responsibility. Used in revenue cycle management and financial reporting.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,visit_procedure,charge_code,charge_code,Charge Description Master (CDM) Charge Code,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Internal charge code from the Charge Description Master (CDM) mapped to this procedure. Links the clinical procedure to the revenue cycle for charge capture, pricing, and claim generation in Epic Resolute or Cerner Revenue Cycle.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,visit_procedure,complication_description,complication_description,Procedure Complication Description,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Free-text or coded description of the complication that occurred during or after the procedure. Populated only when complication_flag is true. Used for clinical documentation, quality review, and risk management reporting.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,visit_procedure,complication_flag,complication_flag,Procedure Complication Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,"Indicates whether a complication was documented as occurring during or immediately following the procedure. Triggers CDI query workflow, quality event review, and HAI/PSI surveillance reporting.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,visit_procedure,consent_obtained_flag,consent_obtained_flag,Informed Consent Obtained Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,"Indicates whether informed consent was documented as obtained from the patient or legal guardian prior to the procedure. Required for regulatory compliance, malpractice risk management, and The Joint Commission accreditation standards.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,visit_procedure,cpt_code,cpt_code,Current Procedural Terminology (CPT) Code,STRING,,,,^[0-9]{4}[0-9A-Z]$,transactional_data,"AMA CPT code identifying the procedure for professional billing, charge capture, and payer adjudication. Required on CMS-1500 claims. Drives RVU calculation and reimbursement.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,visit_procedure,cpt_modifier_1,cpt_modifier_1,CPT Modifier 1,STRING,,,,^[A-Z0-9]{2}$,transactional_data,"Primary CPT modifier appended to the procedure code to indicate special circumstances (e.g., 50=bilateral, LT=left side, RT=right side, 22=increased procedural services, 59=distinct procedural service). Required for accurate claim adjudication.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,visit_procedure,cpt_modifier_2,cpt_modifier_2,CPT Modifier 2,STRING,,,,^[A-Z0-9]{2}$,transactional_data,Secondary CPT modifier providing additional claim specificity when a single modifier is insufficient. Used in conjunction with cpt_modifier_1 for complex billing scenarios per CMS Correct Coding Initiative.,
encounter,clinical_documentation,visit_procedure,created_timestamp,created_timestamp,Record Created Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,"Timestamp when this procedure record was first created in the source system. Used for audit trail, data lineage, and regulatory compliance documentation per HIPAA and The Joint Commission medical record requirements.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,visit_procedure,drg_relevant_flag,drg_relevant_flag,Diagnosis-Related Group (DRG) Relevant Procedure Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,Indicates whether this procedure influences the DRG assignment for the inpatient encounter. Flagged by the 3M grouper or equivalent DRG grouping engine. Critical for inpatient revenue integrity and CDI prioritization.,
encounter,clinical_documentation,visit_procedure,hcpcs_code,hcpcs_code,Healthcare Common Procedure Coding System (HCPCS) Code,STRING,,,,^[A-Z][0-9]{4}$,transactional_data,"HCPCS Level II code used when a CPT code is not applicable, primarily for supplies, durable medical equipment, and non-physician services billed to Medicare/Medicaid. Complements CPT on UB-04 and CMS-1500 claims.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,visit_procedure,icd10_pcs_code,icd10_pcs_code,ICD-10 Procedure Coding System (ICD-10-PCS) Code,STRING,,,,^[0-9A-HJ-NP-Z]{7}$,transactional_data,"ICD-10-PCS code assigned for inpatient procedures. Required for inpatient DRG grouping, UB-04 institutional claims, and CMS inpatient prospective payment system (IPPS) reimbursement. Not applicable for outpatient encounters.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,visit_procedure,implant_flag,implant_flag,Implant Used Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,Indicates whether a medical device or implant was used during the procedure. Triggers UDI (Unique Device Identifier) documentation requirements per FDA regulations and supply chain charge capture workflows.,
encounter,clinical_documentation,visit_procedure,is_cancelled,is_cancelled,Procedure Cancelled Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,"Indicates whether a scheduled procedure was cancelled before execution. Used for OR cancellation rate reporting, scheduling efficiency analysis, and revenue impact assessment.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,visit_procedure,is_elective,is_elective,Elective Procedure Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,"Indicates whether the procedure was scheduled as elective (non-urgent) versus emergent or urgent. Supports surgical scheduling analytics, OR block time management, and payer prior authorization workflows.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,visit_procedure,is_principal_procedure,is_principal_procedure,Principal Procedure Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,"Indicates whether this is the principal procedure performed for the encounter, as defined by the Uniform Hospital Discharge Data Set (UHDDS). The principal procedure is the one most closely related to the principal diagnosis and drives DRG assignment for inpatient cases.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,visit_procedure,laterality,laterality,Procedure Laterality,STRING,,,,left|right|bilateral|unilateral|not_applicable,transactional_data,"Body side on which the procedure was performed. Required for correct CPT modifier assignment (RT/LT/50), surgical safety checklists, and wrong-site surgery prevention per The Joint Commission Universal Protocol.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,visit_procedure,performing_provider_npi,performing_provider_npi,Performing Provider National Provider Identifier (NPI),STRING,,,,^[0-9]{10}$,transactional_data,"10-digit NPI of the performing provider as required on CMS-1500 and UB-04 claims. Stored denormalized here for claim generation and audit purposes, as the NPI is a regulatory billing requirement independent of the provider master record.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,visit_procedure,procedure_date,procedure_date,Procedure Date,DATE,,,,,transactional_data,"Calendar date on which the procedure was performed. Used for charge capture date-of-service, quality measure denominator identification, and surgical case scheduling analytics.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,visit_procedure,procedure_description,procedure_description,Procedure Description,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Full clinical description of the procedure as documented in the source system (Epic ClinDoc, OpTime, or Cerner SurgiNet). Provides human-readable context for the CPT/HCPCS/ICD-10-PCS code.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,visit_procedure,procedure_end_timestamp,procedure_end_timestamp,Procedure End Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,"Date and time when the procedure was completed (closure for surgical cases, or final clinical action for non-surgical). Combined with start timestamp to derive procedure duration for OR utilization and case costing.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,visit_procedure,procedure_number,procedure_number,Procedure Number,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Externally visible, human-readable identifier assigned to this procedure record within the source system (e.g., Epic OpTime case number or Cerner SurgiNet procedure order number). Used for cross-system reconciliation and audit.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,visit_procedure,procedure_start_timestamp,procedure_start_timestamp,Procedure Start Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,"Date and time when the procedure began (knife-to-skin for surgical cases, or first clinical action for non-surgical). Used for OR utilization analysis, case duration calculation, and scheduling efficiency reporting.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,visit_procedure,procedure_status,procedure_status,Procedure Status,STRING,,,,completed|in-progress|not-done|entered-in-error|unknown,transactional_data,"Current workflow status of the procedure record per HL7 FHIR Procedure.status value set. Drives charge capture eligibility, quality measure inclusion/exclusion, and CDI workflow routing.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,visit_procedure,procedure_type,procedure_type,Procedure Type,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"High-level classification of the procedure category. Supports operational reporting, OR scheduling, charge master (CDM) mapping, and departmental cost allocation. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: surgical|diagnostic|therapeutic|anesthesia|radiology|laboratory|nursing|other — promote to reference product]",
encounter,clinical_documentation,visit_procedure,quantity,quantity,Procedure Quantity,INT,,,,,transactional_data,"Number of times this procedure was performed or units billed within the encounter. Used for charge capture accuracy, claim line quantity reporting, and utilization analysis.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,visit_procedure,rvu_total,rvu_total,Relative Value Unit (RVU) — Total,"DECIMAL(10,4)",,,,,transactional_data,"Total RVU for the procedure, comprising work RVU, practice expense RVU, and malpractice RVU components per the CMS Physician Fee Schedule. Used for overall provider productivity benchmarking and reimbursement modeling.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,visit_procedure,rvu_work,rvu_work,Relative Value Unit (RVU) — Work Component,"DECIMAL(10,4)",,,,,transactional_data,"Physician work RVU assigned to this procedure per the CMS Physician Fee Schedule. Represents the time, skill, and intensity of the physicians work. Used for provider productivity measurement, compensation modeling, and MIPS performance reporting.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,visit_procedure,sequence_number,sequence_number,Procedure Sequence Number,INT,,,,,transactional_data,"Ordinal position of this procedure within the encounter, used to distinguish principal from secondary procedures on claims. Sequence 1 typically denotes the principal procedure for DRG grouping and IPPS reimbursement.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,visit_procedure,snomed_code,snomed_code,Systematized Nomenclature of Medicine Clinical Terms (SNOMED CT) Procedure Code,STRING,,,,"^[0-9]{6,18}$",transactional_data,"SNOMED CT concept identifier for the procedure, providing a clinically precise, interoperable representation beyond CPT/ICD-10-PCS. Supports HIE data exchange, FHIR-based interoperability, and clinical decision support.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,visit_procedure,source_system,source_system,Source System,STRING,,,,epic_optime|epic_clindoc|cerner_surginet|cerner_powerchart|meditech|manual,transactional_data,"Identifies the operational system of record from which this procedure record was sourced. Supports data lineage, ETL reconciliation, and audit traceability across Epic OpTime, Epic ClinDoc, Cerner SurgiNet, and other source systems.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,visit_procedure,source_system_procedure_code,source_system_procedure_code,Source System Procedure ID,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Native identifier of this procedure record in the originating source system (e.g., Epic OpTime case ID, Cerner SurgiNet order ID). Enables bidirectional traceability between the lakehouse silver layer and the operational EHR system.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,visit_procedure,surgical_approach,surgical_approach,Surgical Approach,STRING,,,,open|laparoscopic|robotic|endoscopic|percutaneous|other,transactional_data,"Method or technique used to access the operative site. Drives ICD-10-PCS character 5 (approach) coding, surgical case complexity classification, and outcomes benchmarking.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,visit_procedure,timeout_performed_flag,timeout_performed_flag,Surgical Time-Out Performed Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,"Indicates whether the pre-procedure surgical time-out (Universal Protocol) was performed and documented, confirming correct patient, site, and procedure. Required by The Joint Commission Universal Protocol for preventing wrong-site surgery.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,visit_procedure,udi,udi,Unique Device Identifier (UDI),STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"FDA-assigned Unique Device Identifier for any medical device or implant used during the procedure. Required for FDA MDR (Medical Device Reporting), recall management, and supply chain traceability. Populated only when implant_flag is true.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,visit_procedure,updated_timestamp,updated_timestamp,Record Updated Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,"Timestamp of the most recent modification to this procedure record in the source system. Supports incremental ETL processing, change data capture, and audit trail requirements for medical record integrity.",
encounter,clinical_documentation,visit_procedure,wound_class,wound_class,Wound Classification,STRING,,,,clean|clean_contaminated|contaminated|dirty_infected,transactional_data,"CDC wound classification assigned at the time of surgery, indicating the degree of microbial contamination. Used for SSI (Surgical Site Infection) risk stratification, HAI surveillance, and quality reporting to NHSN.",
encounter,coverage_authorization,encounter_authorization,encounter_authorization_id,encounter_authorization_id,Encounter Authorization ID,BIGINT,Y,,,,transactional_data,Unique surrogate primary key for the prior authorization and concurrent review record within the encounter domain. Assigned by the lakehouse Silver layer upon ingestion.,
encounter,coverage_authorization,encounter_authorization,clinician_id,clinician_id,Requesting Provider ID,BIGINT,,provider.clinician.clinician_id,,,transactional_data,Reference to the clinician or provider who submitted the prior authorization request to the payer. Used for provider-level utilization management reporting.,
encounter,coverage_authorization,encounter_authorization,cost_center_id,cost_center_id,Cost Center Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,finance.cost_center.cost_center_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to finance.cost_center. Business justification: Prior authorizations for services tie to the cost center delivering care. Needed for denied-service cost tracking, authorization yield financial analysis, and payer contract performance evaluation at ",
encounter,coverage_authorization,encounter_authorization,cpt_code_id,cpt_code_id,Cpt Code Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,reference.cpt_code.cpt_code_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to reference.cpt_code. Business justification: Prior authorization workflow—requested procedures must reference official CPT codes for payer review, medical necessity determination, and authorization approval. Required for utilization management a",
encounter,coverage_authorization,encounter_authorization,demographics_id,demographics_id,Patient ID,BIGINT,,patient.demographics.demographics_id,,,transactional_data,Reference to the patient for whom the authorization was requested. Supports patient-level denial management and utilization management analytics.,
encounter,coverage_authorization,encounter_authorization,drg_id,drg_id,Drg Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,reference.drg.drg_id,,,transactional_data,Foreign key linking to reference.drg. Business justification: Inpatient authorization workflow—DRG-based authorizations must reference official DRG definitions for expected payment calculation and length-of-stay approval. Required for inpatient utilization manag,
encounter,coverage_authorization,encounter_authorization,employee_id,employee_id,Authorization Coordinator Employee Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,workforce.employee.employee_id,"dbx_confidential, dbx_pii",,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to workforce.employee. Business justification: Utilization review coordinators process authorization requests. Required for audit trails, denial appeal preparation, productivity tracking, and compliance with payer submission timelines. Distinct fr",
encounter,coverage_authorization,encounter_authorization,hcpcs_code_id,hcpcs_code_id,Hcpcs Code Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,reference.hcpcs_code.hcpcs_code_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to reference.hcpcs_code. Business justification: Prior authorization for HCPCS services—DME, supplies, and drug authorizations must reference official HCPCS codes for payer review and approval. Required for utilization management of non-physician se",
encounter,coverage_authorization,encounter_authorization,icd_code_id,icd_code_id,Icd10 Diagnosis Code Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,reference.icd_code.icd_code_id,,,transactional_data,Foreign key linking to reference.icd_code. Business justification: Medical necessity validation—authorization diagnosis codes must reference official ICD-10 for clinical justification and payer approval. Required for utilization management to validate that requested ,
encounter,coverage_authorization,encounter_authorization,insurance_coverage_policy_id,insurance_coverage_policy_id,Coverage Policy Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,insurance.insurance_coverage_policy.insurance_coverage_policy_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to insurance.coverage_policy. Business justification: Authorizations are approved or denied based on specific coverage policies. Tracking which policy was applied enables denial management, appeals preparation, and policy effectiveness analysis—critical ",
encounter,coverage_authorization,encounter_authorization,interface_channel_id,interface_channel_id,Interface Channel Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,interoperability.interface_channel.interface_channel_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to interoperability.interface_channel. Business justification: Authorization requests/responses are transmitted via specific payer interface channels. Tracking which channel processed each authorization enables SLA monitoring, payer-specific error analysis, routi",
encounter,coverage_authorization,encounter_authorization,material_master_id,material_master_id,Material Master Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,supply.material_master.material_master_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to supply.material_master. Business justification: Prior authorizations frequently specify approved devices, medications, or supplies by item number. Payer contract compliance and authorization workflow systems require tracking which specific material",
encounter,coverage_authorization,encounter_authorization,payer_id,payer_id,Payer ID,BIGINT,,insurance.payer.payer_id,,,transactional_data,Reference to the insurance payer or health plan responsible for adjudicating the authorization request. Drives payer contract compliance and denial trend analysis.,
encounter,coverage_authorization,encounter_authorization,prior_auth_rule_id,prior_auth_rule_id,Prior Auth Rule Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,insurance.prior_auth_rule.prior_auth_rule_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to insurance.prior_auth_rule. Business justification: Each authorization decision applies specific prior auth rules defined by payer. Direct link enables compliance tracking, rule effectiveness analysis, and appeals documentation—essential for utilizatio",
encounter,coverage_authorization,encounter_authorization,research_study_id,research_study_id,Research Study Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,research.research_study.research_study_id,,,transactional_data,Foreign key linking to research.research_study. Business justification: Prior authorizations for research-related services must reference the study protocol for proper coverage determination under Medicare NCD 310.1 and commercial clinical trial policies. Research billing,
encounter,coverage_authorization,encounter_authorization,authorization_number,authorization_number,Authorization Number,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,Externally assigned authorization reference number issued by the payer upon approval or acknowledgment of the prior authorization request. Required on claims submission to validate covered services. Sourced from Epic Resolute HB payer portal integration.,
encounter,coverage_authorization,encounter_authorization,authorization_status,authorization_status,Authorization Status,STRING,,,,approved|denied|pending|appealed|retro_authorized|cancelled,transactional_data,"Current workflow state of the prior authorization request. Drives revenue cycle integrity, denial management workflows, and utilization management escalation. Key values: approved (payer approved services), denied (payer denied services), pending (awaiting payer decision), appealed (denial under appeal), retro_authorized (authorization obtained after service delivery), cancelled (request withdrawn).",
encounter,coverage_authorization,encounter_authorization,authorization_type,authorization_type,Authorization Type,STRING,,,,prior|concurrent|retrospective|expedited,transactional_data,Classification of the authorization request by timing relative to service delivery. Prior: requested before service; Concurrent: requested during ongoing inpatient stay (utilization review); Retrospective: requested after service delivery; Expedited: urgent/emergent prior authorization with accelerated payer review timeline.,
encounter,coverage_authorization,encounter_authorization,authorized_amount,authorized_amount,Authorized Amount,"DECIMAL(18,2)",,,dbx_confidential,,transactional_data,"Dollar amount of services approved by the payer under this authorization. Used for revenue cycle forecasting, expected reimbursement calculation, and payer contract compliance monitoring.",
encounter,coverage_authorization,encounter_authorization,authorized_days,authorized_days,Authorized Days,INT,,,,,transactional_data,"Number of inpatient days or service days approved by the payer for the authorized admission or ongoing care episode. Critical for concurrent review, length-of-stay management, and discharge planning. Distinct from authorized_units which applies to discrete service counts.",
encounter,coverage_authorization,encounter_authorization,authorized_units,authorized_units,Authorized Units,INT,,,,,transactional_data,"Number of service units (e.g., therapy visits, procedure units, infusion doses) approved by the payer for the authorized service. Used for utilization tracking against approved quantities and denial prevention.",
encounter,coverage_authorization,encounter_authorization,claim_appeal_decision,claim_appeal_decision,Appeal Decision,STRING,,,,upheld|overturned|partial|pending,transactional_data,"Outcome of the payer appeal review. Upheld: original denial maintained; Overturned: denial reversed, services approved; Partial: partial approval granted on appeal; Pending: appeal under review. Drives denial overturn rate KPI reporting.",
encounter,coverage_authorization,encounter_authorization,claim_appeal_submitted_date,claim_appeal_submitted_date,Appeal Submitted Date,DATE,,,,,transactional_data,Date on which a formal appeal of the payer denial was submitted. Populated when authorization_status is appealed. Used to track appeal filing deadlines and payer response timelines.,
encounter,coverage_authorization,encounter_authorization,claim_denial_reason_code,claim_denial_reason_code,Denial Reason Code,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Payer-issued standardized code identifying the reason for authorization denial (e.g., not medically necessary, experimental/investigational, out-of-network, missing documentation, benefit exclusion). Used for denial management root cause analysis and appeal strategy. Populated only when authorization_status is denied or appealed.",
encounter,coverage_authorization,encounter_authorization,claim_denial_reason_description,claim_denial_reason_description,Denial Reason Description,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,Free-text or payer-provided narrative description of the denial rationale. Supplements the denial_reason_code with additional clinical or administrative context. Used by CDI and RCM teams for appeal letter preparation.,
encounter,coverage_authorization,encounter_authorization,clinical_indication,clinical_indication,Clinical Indication,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Narrative description of the medical necessity justification submitted to the payer supporting the authorization request. Documents the clinical rationale, patient condition, and treatment plan context. Used by CDI teams for documentation improvement and appeal preparation.",
encounter,coverage_authorization,encounter_authorization,cpt_code,cpt_code,Current Procedural Terminology (CPT) Code,STRING,,,,^[0-9]{4}[0-9A-Z]$,transactional_data,"AMA Current Procedural Terminology code identifying the specific procedure or service for which authorization is requested. Used for claims matching, denial root cause analysis, and payer contract compliance validation.",
encounter,coverage_authorization,encounter_authorization,created_timestamp,created_timestamp,Record Created Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,Date and time the authorization record was first created in the source system (Epic Resolute HB or payer portal integration). Audit trail field for data lineage and compliance.,
encounter,coverage_authorization,encounter_authorization,days_used,days_used,Days Used,INT,,,,,transactional_data,"Number of authorized inpatient days actually consumed against this authorization. Compared against authorized_days for concurrent review, length-of-stay management, and proactive extension request triggering.",
encounter,coverage_authorization,encounter_authorization,end_date,end_date,Authorization End Date,DATE,,,,,transactional_data,Last date on which authorized services may be rendered under this authorization. Services delivered after this date require re-authorization. Used for authorization expiration monitoring and proactive renewal workflows.,
encounter,coverage_authorization,encounter_authorization,extension_authorization_number,extension_authorization_number,Extension Authorization Number,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,Payer-issued authorization number for an approved extension of the original authorization period or unit count. Links the extension approval to the parent authorization record for complete authorization chain tracking.,
encounter,coverage_authorization,encounter_authorization,extension_requested_flag,extension_requested_flag,Authorization Extension Requested Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,Indicates whether an extension of the original authorization (additional days or units) has been requested from the payer. True = extension request submitted. Supports concurrent review workflow management and LOS management reporting.,
encounter,coverage_authorization,encounter_authorization,facility_service_type,facility_service_type,Authorized Service Type,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Category of clinical service or care setting for which authorization is being requested (e.g., inpatient admission, outpatient surgery, skilled nursing facility, home health, durable medical equipment, specialty referral, imaging, infusion therapy). Sourced from payer-specific service type codes. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: inpatient|outpatient_surgery|skilled_nursing|home_health|dme|specialty_referral|imaging|infusion|behavioral_health|physical_therapy — promote to reference product]",
encounter,coverage_authorization,encounter_authorization,facility_type,facility_type,Authorized Facility Type,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,Type of care setting or facility for which the authorization was requested. Inpatient: acute hospital admission; Outpatient: ambulatory services; ED: emergency department; Observation: observation status; SNF: skilled nursing facility; Home Health: home-based services; Telehealth: virtual care services. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: inpatient|outpatient|ed|observation|snf|home_health|telehealth — 7 candidates stripped; promote to reference product],
encounter,coverage_authorization,encounter_authorization,hcpcs_code,hcpcs_code,Healthcare Common Procedure Coding System (HCPCS) Code,STRING,,,,^[A-Z][0-9]{4}$,transactional_data,"HCPCS Level II code for services, supplies, or equipment not covered by CPT codes (e.g., durable medical equipment, ambulance services, drugs). Complements CPT code for comprehensive service identification on authorization requests.",
encounter,coverage_authorization,encounter_authorization,icd10_diagnosis_code,icd10_diagnosis_code,International Classification of Diseases 10th Revision (ICD-10) Diagnosis Code,STRING,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_health","^[A-Z][0-9]{2}(.[0-9A-Z]{1,4})?$",transactional_data,Primary ICD-10-CM diagnosis code submitted as clinical indication supporting the medical necessity of the requested service. Required by most payers for authorization adjudication. Sourced from Epic ClinDoc clinical documentation.,
encounter,coverage_authorization,encounter_authorization,notes,notes,Authorization Notes,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Free-text field capturing additional clinical, administrative, or payer-specific notes related to the authorization request or decision. Used by RCM and utilization management staff to document follow-up actions, payer communications, and special circumstances.",
encounter,coverage_authorization,encounter_authorization,payer_authorization_reference,payer_authorization_reference,Payer Authorization Reference Number,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Payer-assigned internal tracking or case reference number for the authorization request, distinct from the final authorization_number. Used for payer portal follow-up, status inquiries, and audit trail documentation during the pending review period.",
encounter,coverage_authorization,encounter_authorization,payer_decision_timestamp,payer_decision_timestamp,Payer Decision Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,"Date and time the payer issued its authorization decision (approval, denial, or partial approval). Used to calculate payer turnaround time, measure compliance with CMS prior authorization timelines, and support denial management workflows.",
encounter,coverage_authorization,encounter_authorization,payer_reviewer_name,payer_reviewer_name,Payer Reviewer Name,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Name of the payer clinical reviewer or medical director who adjudicated the authorization request. Used for peer-to-peer review scheduling, appeal escalation, and payer relationship management.",
encounter,coverage_authorization,encounter_authorization,payer_reviewer_npi,payer_reviewer_npi,Payer Reviewer National Provider Identifier (NPI),STRING,,,,^[0-9]{10}$,transactional_data,National Provider Identifier of the payer medical director or clinical reviewer who adjudicated the authorization. Required for peer-to-peer review documentation and regulatory audit trails.,
encounter,coverage_authorization,encounter_authorization,peer_to_peer_outcome,peer_to_peer_outcome,Peer-to-Peer (P2P) Review Outcome,STRING,,,,approved|denied|partial|pending,transactional_data,Result of the peer-to-peer clinical review with the payer medical director. Approved: payer reversed denial after P2P; Denied: payer upheld denial after P2P; Partial: partial approval granted; Pending: outcome not yet determined.,
encounter,coverage_authorization,encounter_authorization,peer_to_peer_review_date,peer_to_peer_review_date,Peer-to-Peer (P2P) Review Date,DATE,,,,,transactional_data,Date on which the peer-to-peer clinical review between the requesting provider and payer medical director was conducted. Populated when peer_to_peer_review_flag is True.,
encounter,coverage_authorization,encounter_authorization,peer_to_peer_review_flag,peer_to_peer_review_flag,Peer-to-Peer (P2P) Review Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,Indicates whether a peer-to-peer clinical review was requested or conducted between the requesting provider and the payer medical director to contest a denial or support authorization. True = P2P review requested/completed. Key metric for utilization management and denial overturn tracking.,
encounter,coverage_authorization,encounter_authorization,request_submitted_timestamp,request_submitted_timestamp,Authorization Request Submitted Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,Date and time the prior authorization request was formally submitted to the payer. Principal business event timestamp for the authorization lifecycle. Used for turnaround time measurement and payer SLA compliance tracking.,
encounter,coverage_authorization,encounter_authorization,retro_authorization_reason,retro_authorization_reason,Retrospective Authorization Reason,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Documented reason why authorization was obtained retrospectively after service delivery (e.g., emergency admission, system downtime, payer portal unavailability, clinical urgency). Required for retro-authorization requests and RAC audit defense. Populated when authorization_type is retrospective.",
encounter,coverage_authorization,encounter_authorization,source_system,source_system,Source System,STRING,,,,epic_resolute_hb|cerner_revenue_cycle|payer_portal|meditech|manual,transactional_data,"Operational system of record from which this authorization record was sourced. Supports data lineage, ETL audit, and multi-system reconciliation. Primary source is Epic Resolute HB with supplemental payer portal integrations.",
encounter,coverage_authorization,encounter_authorization,source_system_auth_code,source_system_auth_code,Source System Authorization ID,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Native authorization record identifier from the originating source system (e.g., Epic Resolute HB authorization ID or payer portal case ID). Enables cross-system reconciliation, ETL traceability, and audit trail back to the system of record.",
encounter,coverage_authorization,encounter_authorization,start_date,start_date,Authorization Start Date,DATE,,,,,transactional_data,First date on which the authorized services may be rendered under this authorization. Services delivered before this date are not covered and may result in claim denial. Sourced from payer authorization response.,
encounter,coverage_authorization,encounter_authorization,submission_method,submission_method,Authorization Submission Method,STRING,,,,electronic|phone|fax|portal|edi,transactional_data,Channel through which the prior authorization request was submitted to the payer. Electronic: automated EDI 278 transaction; Phone: verbal submission via payer call center; Fax: paper-based fax submission; Portal: payer web portal submission; EDI: direct EDI integration. Used for operational efficiency analysis and automation opportunity identification.,
encounter,coverage_authorization,encounter_authorization,units_used,units_used,Units Used,INT,,,,,transactional_data,"Number of authorized service units actually consumed against this authorization. Compared against authorized_units to monitor utilization, prevent over-utilization, and trigger re-authorization workflows when approaching the authorized limit.",
encounter,coverage_authorization,encounter_authorization,updated_timestamp,updated_timestamp,Record Updated Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,"Date and time the authorization record was most recently modified in the source system. Tracks status changes, unit updates, and appeal outcomes throughout the authorization lifecycle.",
encounter,coverage_authorization,encounter_authorization,urgency_level,urgency_level,Authorization Urgency Level,STRING,,,,routine|urgent|emergent|expedited,transactional_data,Clinical urgency classification of the authorization request. Routine: standard processing timeline; Urgent: accelerated review required within 72 hours; Emergent: immediate review required; Expedited: CMS-defined expedited review for life-threatening conditions. Drives payer SLA requirements and processing priority.,
encounter,coverage_authorization,visit_coverage,visit_coverage_id,visit_coverage_id,Visit Coverage - Visit Coverage Id,BIGINT,Y,,,,association_data,Primary key for the visit_coverage association,
encounter,coverage_authorization,visit_coverage,payer_id,payer_id,Visit Coverage - Payer Id,BIGINT,,insurance.payer.payer_id,,,association_data,Foreign key linking to the insurance payer providing coverage for this visit,
encounter,coverage_authorization,visit_coverage,visit_id,visit_id,Visit Coverage - Visit Id,BIGINT,,encounter.visit.visit_id,,,association_data,Foreign key linking to the patient visit record that this coverage applies to,
encounter,coverage_authorization,visit_coverage,authorization_number,authorization_number,Prior Authorization Number,STRING,,,,,association_data,Unique authorization or referral number issued by the payer approving coverage for this specific visit. Required on claim submission for services requiring prior authorization. Obtained during pre-registration or admission process and specific to this visit-payer combination.,
encounter,coverage_authorization,visit_coverage,authorization_status,authorization_status,Authorization Status,STRING,,,,,association_data,Current status of prior authorization for this visit-payer combination. Approved indicates payer has authorized coverage for the planned services. Not Required indicates payer does not require authorization for this visit type or service category. Drives admission clearance and claim submission readiness.,
encounter,coverage_authorization,visit_coverage,copay_amount,copay_amount,Patient Copayment Amount,"DECIMAL(10,2)",,,,,association_data,Fixed dollar amount the patient owes at time of service per the benefit plan for this payer. Collected at registration or discharge. Amount is specific to this visit-payer combination and varies by payer contract and patient benefit plan.,
encounter,coverage_authorization,visit_coverage,coverage_effective_date,coverage_effective_date,Coverage Effective Date,DATE,,,,,association_data,Date on which the patients coverage with this payer became active. Retrieved from eligibility verification. Used to validate that coverage was active on the date of service for this visit.,
encounter,coverage_authorization,visit_coverage,coverage_sequence,coverage_sequence,Coverage Sequence,STRING,,,,,association_data,"Indicates the order of financial responsibility when multiple payers cover a single visit. Primary payer is billed first, secondary covers remaining balance per coordination of benefits rules, tertiary covers after secondary. Critical for claim submission sequencing and coordination of benefits processing.",
encounter,coverage_authorization,visit_coverage,coverage_termination_date,coverage_termination_date,Coverage Termination Date,DATE,,,,,association_data,Date on which the patients coverage with this payer ends or ended. Retrieved from eligibility verification. Null for active open-ended coverage. Used to validate coverage was active on date of service and to flag potential coverage gaps.,
encounter,coverage_authorization,visit_coverage,deductible_met_amount,deductible_met_amount,Deductible Met Amount,"DECIMAL(10,2)",,,,,association_data,Dollar amount of the annual deductible the patient has already satisfied with this payer at the time of visit registration. Retrieved from eligibility verification response. Used to calculate patient financial responsibility and estimate out-of-pocket costs for this visit.,
encounter,coverage_authorization,visit_coverage,eligibility_status,eligibility_status,Eligibility Verification Status,STRING,,,,,association_data,"Status of real-time eligibility verification performed at visit registration or admission. Verified indicates active coverage confirmed via EDI 270/271 transaction or payer portal. Drives financial counseling, authorization requirements, and registration workflow completion.",
encounter,coverage_authorization,visit_coverage,eligibility_verification_timestamp,eligibility_verification_timestamp,Eligibility Verification Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,association_data,Date and time when real-time eligibility verification was performed with this payer for this visit. Documents when coverage was confirmed and provides audit trail for registration compliance and claim denial prevention.,
encounter,coverage_authorization,visit_coverage,network_status,network_status,Network Participation Status,STRING,,,,,association_data,"Indicates whether the facility or attending provider is in-network or out-of-network for this specific payer. Determines reimbursement rates, patient cost-sharing levels, and claim adjudication rules. Retrieved during eligibility verification and specific to this visit-payer relationship.",
encounter,coverage_authorization,visit_coverage,subscriber_relationship,subscriber_relationship,Subscriber Relationship,STRING,,,,,association_data,Relationship of the patient to the insurance subscriber (policyholder) for this payer. Self indicates patient is the policyholder. Required for claim submission and coordination of benefits processing. Specific to this visit-payer combination as patient may have different relationships with different payers.,
encounter,coverage_authorization,visit_insurance,visit_insurance_id,visit_insurance_id,Visit Insurance ID,BIGINT,Y,,,,transactional_data,Unique surrogate identifier for the visit insurance record. Primary key for the visit_insurance data product within the encounter domain.,
encounter,coverage_authorization,visit_insurance,health_plan_id,health_plan_id,Health Plan Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,insurance.health_plan.health_plan_id,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii",,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to insurance.health_plan. Business justification: Visit insurance records denormalize plan_name and plan_type but lack FK to health_plan. Direct link is essential for benefit determination, claims adjudication, and cost-sharing calculation—core reven",
encounter,coverage_authorization,visit_insurance,insurance_coverage_id,insurance_coverage_id,Insurance Coverage ID,BIGINT,,patient.insurance_coverage.insurance_coverage_id,,,transactional_data,"Reference to the patients insurance coverage record in the patient domain (patient.insurance_coverage), representing the standing policy used for this visit.",
encounter,coverage_authorization,visit_insurance,payer_contract_id,payer_contract_id,Payer Contract ID,BIGINT,,insurance.payer_contract.payer_contract_id,,,transactional_data,Identifier of the payer contract or fee schedule agreement under which services for this visit will be reimbursed. Used in contract management and expected reimbursement calculation.,
encounter,coverage_authorization,visit_insurance,payer_id,payer_id,Payer ID,BIGINT,,insurance.payer.payer_id,,,transactional_data,Reference to the payer (insurance company or government program) responsible for reimbursement for this visit. Links to the payer reference entity.,
encounter,coverage_authorization,visit_insurance,primary_mpi_record_id,primary_mpi_record_id,Patient ID,BIGINT,,patient.mpi_record.mpi_record_id,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_identifier",,transactional_data,Reference to the patient whose insurance coverage is being captured for this visit. Links to the Master Patient Index (MPI) in the patient domain.,
encounter,coverage_authorization,visit_insurance,subscriber_id,subscriber_id,Subscriber ID,BIGINT,,insurance.subscriber.subscriber_id,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_identifier",,transactional_data,Unique identifier of the primary policyholder (subscriber) as assigned by the payer. May differ from the patients member ID when the patient is a dependent.,
encounter,coverage_authorization,visit_insurance,visit_id,visit_id,Visit ID,BIGINT,,encounter.visit.visit_id,,,transactional_data,Reference to the patient visit or encounter to which this insurance coverage record is associated. Core linkage to the encounter domain.,
encounter,coverage_authorization,visit_insurance,visit_mpi_record_id,visit_mpi_record_id,Member ID,BIGINT,,patient.mpi_record.mpi_record_id,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_identifier",,transactional_data,Unique member identification number assigned by the payer to identify the insured individual on the insurance card and in payer systems. Required for eligibility verification and claims submission.,
encounter,coverage_authorization,visit_insurance,authorization_effective_date,authorization_effective_date,Authorization Effective Date,DATE,,,,,transactional_data,Start date of the approved prior authorization period. Services rendered before this date may not be covered under the authorization.,
encounter,coverage_authorization,visit_insurance,authorization_expiration_date,authorization_expiration_date,Authorization Expiration Date,DATE,,,,,transactional_data,End date of the approved prior authorization period. Services rendered after this date require a new authorization. Critical for revenue cycle management to prevent claim denials.,
encounter,coverage_authorization,visit_insurance,authorization_number,authorization_number,Prior Authorization Number,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,Pre-authorization or prior authorization number issued by the payer approving the services rendered during this visit. Required for claims submission for services that mandate prior authorization.,
encounter,coverage_authorization,visit_insurance,authorization_status,authorization_status,Prior Authorization Status,STRING,,,,APPROVED|PENDING|DENIED|NOT_REQUIRED|EXPIRED,transactional_data,Current status of the prior authorization request for services associated with this visit. APPROVED = payer approved; PENDING = awaiting payer decision; DENIED = payer denied; NOT_REQUIRED = service does not require auth; EXPIRED = auth obtained but expired.,
encounter,coverage_authorization,visit_insurance,billing_npi,billing_npi,Billing National Provider Identifier (NPI),STRING,,,,^[0-9]{10}$,transactional_data,National Provider Identifier (NPI) of the billing provider or organization submitted to the payer for this visit. Required on CMS-1500 and UB-04 claim forms.,
encounter,coverage_authorization,visit_insurance,claim_form_type,claim_form_type,Claim Form Type,STRING,,,,CMS_1500|UB_04|ELECTRONIC_837P|ELECTRONIC_837I,transactional_data,Type of claim form used to bill the payer for this visit. CMS_1500 = professional/physician claims; UB_04 = institutional/facility claims; ELECTRONIC_837P = electronic professional claim; ELECTRONIC_837I = electronic institutional claim.,
encounter,coverage_authorization,visit_insurance,cob_notes,cob_notes,Coordination of Benefits (COB) Notes,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Free-text notes related to coordination of benefits (COB) for this visit, capturing special instructions, payer-specific COB rules, or manual overrides documented by revenue cycle staff.",
encounter,coverage_authorization,visit_insurance,coinsurance_rate,coinsurance_rate,Coinsurance Rate,"DECIMAL(5,4)",,,,,transactional_data,"Patients coinsurance percentage (expressed as a decimal, e.g., 0.20 = 20%) representing the share of covered service costs the patient is responsible for after the deductible is met.",
encounter,coverage_authorization,visit_insurance,copay_amount,copay_amount,Copay Amount,"DECIMAL(12,2)",,,"dbx_confidential, dbx_pii_financial",,transactional_data,Fixed dollar amount the patient is responsible for paying at the time of service as defined by the insurance plan for this visit type. Used in patient financial counseling and billing.,
encounter,coverage_authorization,visit_insurance,coverage_effective_date,coverage_effective_date,Coverage Effective Date,DATE,,,,,transactional_data,Date on which the patients insurance coverage under this plan became effective. Used to confirm coverage was active at the time of the visit.,
encounter,coverage_authorization,visit_insurance,coverage_sequence,coverage_sequence,Coverage Sequence (Coordination of Benefits),INT,,,,,transactional_data,"Coordination of Benefits (COB) sequence number indicating the order in which payers are billed. 1 = primary, 2 = secondary, 3 = tertiary. Governs payer billing priority per COB rules.",
encounter,coverage_authorization,visit_insurance,coverage_termination_date,coverage_termination_date,Coverage Termination Date,DATE,,,,,transactional_data,Date on which the patients insurance coverage under this plan ends or was terminated. Null if coverage is open-ended or still active. Used to validate coverage at time of service.,
encounter,coverage_authorization,visit_insurance,coverage_type,coverage_type,Coverage Type,STRING,,,,MEDICAL|DENTAL|VISION|BEHAVIORAL_HEALTH|PHARMACY,transactional_data,Type of insurance coverage applicable to this visit. Determines which benefit category applies for claims adjudication. MEDICAL = general medical/surgical; DENTAL; VISION; BEHAVIORAL_HEALTH = mental health/substance use; PHARMACY.,
encounter,coverage_authorization,visit_insurance,created_timestamp,created_timestamp,Record Created Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,Timestamp when this visit insurance record was first created in the system. Supports audit trail and data lineage tracking per HIPAA and internal data governance requirements.,
encounter,coverage_authorization,visit_insurance,deductible_amount,deductible_amount,Deductible Amount,"DECIMAL(12,2)",,,"dbx_confidential, dbx_pii_financial",,transactional_data,Annual deductible amount the patient must meet before the insurance plan begins paying for covered services. Sourced from eligibility verification response for patient financial counseling.,
encounter,coverage_authorization,visit_insurance,deductible_met_amount,deductible_met_amount,Deductible Met Amount,"DECIMAL(12,2)",,,"dbx_confidential, dbx_pii_financial",,transactional_data,Dollar amount of the patients annual deductible that has already been satisfied as of the date of this visit. Used to estimate patient financial responsibility.,
encounter,coverage_authorization,visit_insurance,eligibility_status,eligibility_status,Eligibility Verification Status,STRING,,,,VERIFIED|PENDING|INACTIVE|UNABLE_TO_VERIFY|NOT_ELIGIBLE,transactional_data,Current status of the insurance eligibility verification for this visit. Indicates whether the patients coverage has been confirmed active with the payer at the time of service.,
encounter,coverage_authorization,visit_insurance,eligibility_verification_method,eligibility_verification_method,Eligibility Verification Method,STRING,,,,ELECTRONIC|PHONE|PORTAL|MANUAL|REAL_TIME,transactional_data,Method used to verify the patients insurance eligibility. ELECTRONIC = automated 270/271 transaction; PHONE = staff called payer; PORTAL = payer web portal; MANUAL = paper/fax; REAL_TIME = real-time API query.,
encounter,coverage_authorization,visit_insurance,eligibility_verified_date,eligibility_verified_date,Eligibility Verified Date,DATE,,,,,transactional_data,Date on which the patients insurance eligibility was last verified with the payer for this visit. Used to confirm coverage was active at the time of service.,
encounter,coverage_authorization,visit_insurance,financial_class,financial_class,Financial Class,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Financial classification assigned to the visit based on the primary payer, used for revenue cycle management (RCM), billing workflow routing, and financial reporting. Examples: Commercial, Medicare, Medicaid, Self-Pay, Workers Comp, Charity Care. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: COMMERCIAL|MEDICARE|MEDICAID|SELF_PAY|WORKERS_COMP|CHARITY_CARE|TRICARE|MANAGED_CARE — promote to reference product]",
encounter,coverage_authorization,visit_insurance,group_number,group_number,Insurance Group Number,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,Group policy number assigned by the payer to identify the employer group or association under which the patients insurance plan is issued. Used in claims submission and eligibility verification.,
encounter,coverage_authorization,visit_insurance,insurance_type_code,insurance_type_code,Insurance Type Code,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Standardized payer-assigned or industry-standard code identifying the type of insurance (e.g., Medicare Part A, Medicare Part B, Medicaid, CHAMPUS/TRICARE, FECA Black Lung, Group Health Plan). Corresponds to Box 1 on CMS-1500.",
encounter,coverage_authorization,visit_insurance,insurance_verification_source,insurance_verification_source,Insurance Verification Source System,STRING,,,,EPIC|CERNER|CHANGE_HEALTHCARE|AVAILITY|MANUAL|PAYER_PORTAL,transactional_data,Source system or clearinghouse used to perform the insurance eligibility verification for this visit. Supports audit trail and troubleshooting of eligibility discrepancies.,
encounter,coverage_authorization,visit_insurance,network_status,network_status,Network Status,STRING,,,,IN_NETWORK|OUT_OF_NETWORK|UNKNOWN,transactional_data,Indicates whether the rendering provider and/or facility is in-network or out-of-network with the patients insurance plan for this visit. Affects patient cost-sharing and reimbursement rates.,
encounter,coverage_authorization,visit_insurance,out_of_pocket_max,out_of_pocket_max,Out-of-Pocket Maximum,"DECIMAL(12,2)",,,"dbx_confidential, dbx_pii_financial",,transactional_data,"Maximum annual dollar amount the patient is required to pay out-of-pocket for covered services under the insurance plan. Once met, the plan covers 100% of covered services.",
encounter,coverage_authorization,visit_insurance,out_of_pocket_met_amount,out_of_pocket_met_amount,Out-of-Pocket Met Amount,"DECIMAL(12,2)",,,"dbx_confidential, dbx_pii_financial",,transactional_data,Dollar amount of the patients annual out-of-pocket maximum that has already been satisfied as of the date of this visit. Used to determine remaining patient financial liability.,
encounter,coverage_authorization,visit_insurance,payer_phone,payer_phone,Payer Phone Number,STRING,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_phone","^+?[0-9-s().]{7,20}$",transactional_data,Primary contact phone number for the insurance payers provider services or claims department. Used by revenue cycle staff for eligibility verification and claims follow-up.,
encounter,coverage_authorization,visit_insurance,preauth_required,preauth_required,Pre-Authorization Required Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,Indicates whether the payer requires prior authorization for the services rendered during this visit. True = pre-authorization is required; False = no pre-authorization needed.,
encounter,coverage_authorization,visit_insurance,referral_number,referral_number,Referral Number,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,Referral authorization number issued by the patients Primary Care Physician (PCP) or gatekeeper for HMO/POS plans requiring referrals for specialist or facility services during this visit.,
encounter,coverage_authorization,visit_insurance,reimbursement_method,reimbursement_method,Expected Reimbursement Method,STRING,,,,FFS|CAPITATION|BUNDLED|VBP|DRG|PER_DIEM,transactional_data,Expected payment methodology under which the payer will reimburse the provider for this visit. FFS = Fee-For-Service; CAPITATION = per-member per-month; BUNDLED = bundled payment; VBP = Value-Based Purchasing; DRG = Diagnosis-Related Group; PER_DIEM = daily rate.,
encounter,coverage_authorization,visit_insurance,source_system,source_system,Source System,STRING,,,,EPIC_RESOLUTE_HB|CERNER_REVENUE_CYCLE|MEDITECH|MANUAL,transactional_data,"Operational system of record from which this visit insurance record was sourced. Supports data lineage, reconciliation, and ETL audit in the Databricks Silver lakehouse layer.",
encounter,coverage_authorization,visit_insurance,subscriber_dob,subscriber_dob,Subscriber Date of Birth,DATE,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_identifier",,transactional_data,Date of birth of the primary policyholder (subscriber). Used for eligibility verification and claims adjudication when the patient is a dependent.,
encounter,coverage_authorization,visit_insurance,subscriber_relationship,subscriber_relationship,Subscriber Relationship,STRING,,,,SELF|SPOUSE|CHILD|OTHER,transactional_data,"Relationship of the patient to the primary policyholder (subscriber). Determines dependent eligibility and COB rules. Values: SELF (patient is the subscriber), SPOUSE, CHILD, OTHER. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: SELF|SPOUSE|CHILD|DOMESTIC_PARTNER|WARD|EMPLOYEE|UNKNOWN|OTHER — promote to reference product]",
encounter,coverage_authorization,visit_insurance,updated_timestamp,updated_timestamp,Record Updated Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,"Timestamp when this visit insurance record was last modified. Used for change data capture (CDC), audit trail, and downstream ETL processing in the Databricks Silver layer.",
encounter,coverage_authorization,visit_recall_impact,visit_recall_impact_id,visit_recall_impact_id,Visit Recall Impact - Visit Recall Impact Id,BIGINT,Y,,,,association_data,Primary key for the visit_recall_impact association,
encounter,coverage_authorization,visit_recall_impact,assigned_to_clinician_id,assigned_to_clinician_id,Assigned Clinician ID,BIGINT,,provider.clinician.clinician_id,,,association_data,Reference to the clinician assigned to conduct the clinical review and patient notification for this visit-recall combination. Supports patient safety workflow assignment and accountability.,
encounter,coverage_authorization,visit_recall_impact,recall_notice_id,recall_notice_id,Visit Recall Impact - Recall Notice Id,BIGINT,,supply.recall_notice.recall_notice_id,,,association_data,Foreign key linking to the recall notice that potentially affects this visit based on supply usage during the encounter.,
encounter,coverage_authorization,visit_recall_impact,visit_id,visit_id,Visit Recall Impact - Visit Id,BIGINT,,encounter.visit.visit_id,,,association_data,"Foreign key linking to the patient visit that may have been exposed to the recalled medical supply, device, or implant during the encounter.",
encounter,coverage_authorization,visit_recall_impact,clinical_review_completed,clinical_review_completed,Clinical Review Completed Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,association_data,Indicates whether a clinical review has been completed to assess the actual patient impact for this specific visit-recall combination. Clinical review determines if the recalled product was actually used on this patient and what clinical follow-up is required.,
encounter,coverage_authorization,visit_recall_impact,clinical_review_date,clinical_review_date,Clinical Review Date,DATE,,,,,association_data,Date on which the clinical review was completed for this visit-recall combination. Used to track compliance with patient safety investigation timelines.,
encounter,coverage_authorization,visit_recall_impact,created_timestamp,created_timestamp,Record Created Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,association_data,"Timestamp when this visit-recall impact record was created in the system, typically when the recall was matched to potentially affected visits through supply chain traceability analysis.",
encounter,coverage_authorization,visit_recall_impact,follow_up_due_date,follow_up_due_date,Follow-Up Due Date,DATE,,,,,association_data,Target date by which clinical follow-up should be completed for this visit-recall combination. Used for patient safety task management and compliance tracking.,
encounter,coverage_authorization,visit_recall_impact,follow_up_required,follow_up_required,Follow-Up Required Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,association_data,Indicates whether ongoing clinical follow-up is required for this patient based on the recall impact assessment. Drives care coordination and patient safety monitoring workflows.,
encounter,coverage_authorization,visit_recall_impact,last_updated_timestamp,last_updated_timestamp,Record Last Updated Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,association_data,"Timestamp of the most recent update to this visit-recall impact record, tracking the progression of the patient safety investigation and notification workflow.",
encounter,coverage_authorization,visit_recall_impact,lot_serial_match_confirmed,lot_serial_match_confirmed,Lot/Serial Match Confirmed Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,association_data,Indicates whether the specific lot number or serial number of the product used in this visit matches the affected lot/serial range specified in the recall notice. Critical for determining actual patient exposure.,
encounter,coverage_authorization,visit_recall_impact,notification_date,notification_date,Patient Notification Date,DATE,,,dbx_phi,,association_data,Date on which the patient associated with this visit was formally notified of potential exposure to the recalled product. Used for regulatory compliance tracking and patient safety audit trails.,
encounter,coverage_authorization,visit_recall_impact,patient_impact_assessment,patient_impact_assessment,Patient Impact Assessment,STRING,,,,,association_data,Clinical assessment of the actual or potential impact of the recalled product on this specific patient during this visit. Categorizes risk level and drives notification urgency and remediation priority.,
encounter,coverage_authorization,visit_recall_impact,patient_notification_status,patient_notification_status,Patient Notification Status,STRING,,,dbx_phi,,association_data,"Current status of the patient notification workflow for this visit-recall combination. Tracks whether the patient has been notified of potential exposure to the recalled product, supporting FDA MedWatch and patient safety regulatory requirements.",
encounter,coverage_authorization,visit_recall_impact,product_actually_used,product_actually_used,Product Actually Used Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,association_data,"Indicates whether the recalled product was definitively confirmed to have been used on this patient during this visit. Determined through supply chain traceability, clinical documentation review, and UDI tracking.",
encounter,coverage_authorization,visit_recall_impact,remediation_action_taken,remediation_action_taken,Remediation Action Taken,STRING,,,,,association_data,Specific remediation action taken for this visit-recall combination based on clinical review findings. Documents the healthcare organizations response to the recall for this specific patient encounter.,
encounter,coverage_authorization,visit_recall_impact,remediation_date,remediation_date,Remediation Action Date,DATE,,,,,association_data,Date on which the remediation action was completed for this visit-recall combination. Used for regulatory compliance tracking and patient safety audit trails.,
encounter,operational_logistics,bed_assignment,bed_assignment_id,bed_assignment_id,Bed Assignment ID,BIGINT,Y,,,,transactional_data,Unique surrogate identifier for each bed assignment record in the lakehouse Silver layer. Primary key for the bed_assignment data product.,
encounter,operational_logistics,bed_assignment,care_site_id,care_site_id,Facility ID,BIGINT,,facility.care_site.care_site_id,,,transactional_data,Reference to the facility (hospital or care site) where the bed is located. Supports multi-facility capacity planning and reporting.,
encounter,operational_logistics,bed_assignment,clinician_id,clinician_id,Assigned Provider ID,BIGINT,,provider.clinician.clinician_id,,,transactional_data,Reference to the attending or admitting provider responsible for the patient at the time of bed assignment. Used for provider-level capacity and workload reporting.,
encounter,operational_logistics,bed_assignment,employee_id,employee_id,Assigning Nurse Employee Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,workforce.employee.employee_id,"dbx_confidential, dbx_pii",,transactional_data,"Rename generic employee_id columns to role‑specific names (e.g., assigning_nurse_employee_id -> assigning_nurse_id).",
encounter,operational_logistics,bed_assignment,inventory_location_id,inventory_location_id,Inventory Location Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,supply.inventory_location.inventory_location_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to supply.inventory_location. Business justification: Patient beds are spatially co-located with PAR locations and ADC machines. Bedside supply replenishment, nursing workflow optimization, and inventory par level management depend on linking bed assignm",
encounter,operational_logistics,bed_assignment,mpi_record_id,mpi_record_id,Patient ID,BIGINT,,patient.mpi_record.mpi_record_id,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_identifier",,transactional_data,Reference to the patient assigned to this bed. Supports patient-level bed utilization tracking and HAI (Healthcare-Associated Infection) isolation compliance.,
encounter,operational_logistics,bed_assignment,primary_bed_id,primary_bed_id,Bed ID,BIGINT,,facility.bed.bed_id,,,transactional_data,"Unique identifier of the physical bed as defined in the facilitys bed management system (Epic ADT or Cerner Bed Board). Used to track individual bed utilization, turnover, and HAI (Healthcare-Associated Infection) events.",
encounter,operational_logistics,bed_assignment,visit_id,visit_id,Encounter ID,BIGINT,,encounter.visit.visit_id,,,transactional_data,Reference to the patient encounter (visit) associated with this bed assignment. Links the bed assignment to the core encounter record for the patient visit.,
encounter,operational_logistics,bed_assignment,admission_date,admission_date,Admission Date,DATE,,,,,transactional_data,"Calendar date of the patients hospital admission associated with this bed assignment. Used for LOS (Length of Stay) calculation, DRG (Diagnosis-Related Group) assignment, and CMS reporting.",
encounter,operational_logistics,bed_assignment,admission_source_code,admission_source_code,Admission Source Code,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Standardized CMS admission source code indicating how the patient arrived for this admission (e.g., 1 = physician referral, 4 = transfer from hospital, 7 = emergency room). Required for UB-04 billing and CMS quality reporting. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: 1|2|3|4|5|6|7|8|9|D|E|F — promote to reference product]",
encounter,operational_logistics,bed_assignment,adt_event_type,adt_event_type,"ADT (Admit, Discharge, Transfer) Event Type",STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"HL7 ADT (Admit, Discharge, Transfer) event type code that triggered this bed assignment record. A01 = admit; A02 = transfer; A03 = discharge; A04 = register outpatient; A08 = update patient info; A11 = cancel admit; A12 = cancel transfer; A13 = cancel discharge. Supports HL7 FHIR interoperability and HIE (Health Information Exchange) event processing. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: A01|A02|A03|A04|A08|A11|A12|A13 — 8 candidates stripped; promote to reference product]",
encounter,operational_logistics,bed_assignment,bed_class,bed_class,Bed Class,STRING,,,,inpatient|outpatient|observation|emergency|behavioral_health|rehabilitation,transactional_data,Regulatory classification of the bed for CMS (Centers for Medicare and Medicaid Services) reporting and reimbursement purposes. Determines whether the bed counts toward licensed inpatient capacity or outpatient/observation capacity. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: inpatient|outpatient|observation|emergency|behavioral_health|rehabilitation|long_term_care|skilled_nursing — promote to reference product],
encounter,operational_logistics,bed_assignment,bed_gender_designation,bed_gender_designation,Bed Gender Designation,STRING,,,"dbx_confidential, dbx_pii",male|female|any,transactional_data,Gender designation of the bed for patient placement purposes. male = designated for male patients; female = designated for female patients; any = no gender restriction. Used for bed placement rules and patient privacy compliance.,
encounter,operational_logistics,bed_assignment,bed_hold_reason,bed_hold_reason,Bed Hold Reason,STRING,,,,procedure|imaging|therapy|family_request|clinical_hold|none,transactional_data,"Reason the bed is being held for a patient who is temporarily off the unit (e.g., for a procedure, imaging, or therapy). none indicates no hold is in effect. Used for bed availability accuracy and capacity management.",
encounter,operational_logistics,bed_assignment,bed_label,bed_label,Bed Label,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Human-readable label or name of the bed as displayed in the ADT system (e.g., 4B-12A). Used by nursing staff and bed coordinators for operational identification.",
encounter,operational_logistics,bed_assignment,bed_request_source,bed_request_source,Bed Request Source,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,Origin point from which the bed request was initiated. ed = Emergency Department; or = Operating Room post-procedure; icu = ICU step-down; direct_admit = direct admission from clinic or physician office; transfer_center = inter-facility transfer; observation = conversion from observation status; pacu = Post-Anesthesia Care Unit. Used for bed flow analysis and throughput optimization. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: ed|or|icu|direct_admit|transfer_center|observation|pacu — 7 candidates stripped; promote to reference product],
encounter,operational_logistics,bed_assignment,bed_type,bed_type,Bed Type,STRING,,,,icu|telemetry|med_surg|isolation|observation|step_down,transactional_data,"Clinical classification of the bed based on care intensity and equipment capability. icu = Intensive Care Unit bed; telemetry = cardiac monitoring bed; med_surg = medical-surgical bed; isolation = negative pressure or contact precaution bed; observation = short-stay observation bed; step_down = intermediate care bed. Drives staffing ratios, reimbursement, and HAI (Healthcare-Associated Infection) tracking.",
encounter,operational_logistics,bed_assignment,created_timestamp,created_timestamp,Record Created Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,Date and time when this bed assignment record was first created in the source ADT system. Supports audit trail and data lineage requirements.,
encounter,operational_logistics,bed_assignment,discharge_date,discharge_date,Discharge Date,DATE,,,,,transactional_data,Calendar date of the patients discharge from the facility associated with this bed assignment. Null if the patient is still admitted. Used for ALOS (Average Length of Stay) reporting and DRG (Diagnosis-Related Group) reimbursement.,
encounter,operational_logistics,bed_assignment,discharge_disposition_code,discharge_disposition_code,Discharge Disposition Code,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Standardized CMS discharge disposition code indicating where the patient went upon leaving this bed assignment (e.g., 01 = home, 02 = short-term hospital, 03 = SNF, 20 = expired). Required for UB-04 billing and CMS quality reporting. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: 01|02|03|04|05|06|07|20|21|30|43|50|51|61|62|63|64|65|66|69|70|71|72|81|82|83|84|85|86|87|88|89|90|91|92|93|94|95|96|97|98|99 — promote to reference product]",
encounter,operational_logistics,bed_assignment,expected_discharge_date,expected_discharge_date,Expected Discharge Date,DATE,,,,,transactional_data,"Clinician-estimated date of patient discharge from this bed assignment. Used for discharge planning, bed availability forecasting, and ALOS (Average Length of Stay) management. Sourced from Epic Discharge Planning or Cerner Millennium care management workflows.",
encounter,operational_logistics,bed_assignment,floor_number,floor_number,Floor Number,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Physical floor or level of the facility building where the bed is located. Used for facility management, emergency evacuation planning, and environmental services routing.",
encounter,operational_logistics,bed_assignment,housekeeping_status_at_assignment,housekeeping_status_at_assignment,Housekeeping Status at Assignment,STRING,,,,clean|dirty|in_progress|inspected|out_of_service,transactional_data,Environmental services (EVS) status of the bed at the moment of patient assignment. clean = bed was verified clean and ready; dirty = bed had not yet been cleaned (emergency placement); in_progress = cleaning was underway; inspected = cleaning completed and inspected; out_of_service = bed was flagged as unavailable. Critical for HAI (Healthcare-Associated Infection) prevention audits and EVS performance measurement.,
encounter,operational_logistics,bed_assignment,is_isolation_bed,is_isolation_bed,Is Isolation Bed Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,Indicates whether this bed is designated as a negative pressure or isolation room capable of supporting infection control precautions. True = isolation-capable bed; False = standard bed. Used for capacity planning of isolation-capable beds and HAI (Healthcare-Associated Infection) compliance reporting.,
encounter,operational_logistics,bed_assignment,is_observation_status,is_observation_status,Is Observation Status Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,"Indicates whether the patient is under CMS observation status (rather than formal inpatient admission) during this bed assignment. True = observation status; False = inpatient or other status. Critical for CMS Two-Midnight Rule compliance, Medicare Part A vs. Part B billing, and patient financial counseling obligations under the NOTICE Act.",
encounter,operational_logistics,bed_assignment,is_private_room,is_private_room,Is Private Room Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,"Indicates whether the bed is located in a private single-occupancy room. True = private room; False = semi-private or multi-bed room. Relevant for infection control, patient satisfaction (CAHPS), and revenue for private room upgrades.",
encounter,operational_logistics,bed_assignment,is_telemetry_monitored,is_telemetry_monitored,Is Telemetry Monitored Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,Indicates whether the patient in this bed assignment is connected to continuous cardiac telemetry monitoring. True = telemetry active; False = no telemetry. Used for telemetry capacity management and nursing workload planning.,
encounter,operational_logistics,bed_assignment,isolation_type,isolation_type,Isolation Type,STRING,,,,contact|droplet|airborne|protective|none,transactional_data,"Type of infection control isolation precaution in effect for this bed assignment. contact = contact precautions (e.g., MRSA, C. diff); droplet = droplet precautions (e.g., influenza); airborne = airborne precautions (e.g., TB, COVID-19); protective = reverse isolation for immunocompromised patients; none = no isolation required. Critical for HAI (Healthcare-Associated Infection) tracking including CLABSI, CAUTI, and SSI prevention.",
encounter,operational_logistics,bed_assignment,los_days,los_days,Length of Stay (LOS) Days,"DECIMAL(6,2)",,,,,transactional_data,"Number of days the patient occupied this specific bed assignment, calculated as the difference between assignment end and start timestamps expressed in fractional days. Supports ALOS (Average Length of Stay) benchmarking, CMI (Case Mix Index) analysis, and capacity planning. Note: this is bed-level LOS, not encounter-level LOS.",
encounter,operational_logistics,bed_assignment,nursing_station_code,nursing_station_code,Nursing Station Code,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Code identifying the nursing station responsible for this bed. Used for nursing assignment, medication administration routing (MAR), and staffing ratio compliance reporting.",
encounter,operational_logistics,bed_assignment,patient_class,patient_class,Patient Class,STRING,,,,inpatient|outpatient|observation|emergency|recurring|preadmit,transactional_data,"CMS-defined patient classification status at the time of this bed assignment. Determines reimbursement pathway (inpatient DRG vs. outpatient APC), two-midnight rule applicability, and Medicare Part A vs. Part B billing. observation status has significant patient financial implications under CMS rules.",
encounter,operational_logistics,bed_assignment,provider_assignment_end_timestamp,provider_assignment_end_timestamp,Bed Assignment End Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,"Date and time when the patient vacated the assigned bed, either through discharge, transfer, or death. Null if the assignment is still active. Used to compute bed occupancy duration.",
encounter,operational_logistics,bed_assignment,provider_assignment_number,provider_assignment_number,Bed Assignment Number,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Externally visible, human-readable identifier for this bed assignment event as generated by the ADT (Admit, Discharge, Transfer) system. Used for operational tracking and audit trails.",
encounter,operational_logistics,bed_assignment,provider_assignment_reason,provider_assignment_reason,Bed Assignment Reason,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,Clinical or operational reason for this specific bed assignment event. admission = initial placement upon admission; transfer = moved from another bed/unit; upgrade = moved to higher acuity bed; downgrade = moved to lower acuity bed; isolation_precaution = placed for infection control; overflow = placed due to capacity constraints; elective = planned placement. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: admission|transfer|upgrade|downgrade|isolation_precaution|overflow|elective|post_procedure|observation_conversion — promote to reference product],
encounter,operational_logistics,bed_assignment,provider_assignment_start_timestamp,provider_assignment_start_timestamp,Bed Assignment Start Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,Date and time when the patient was physically placed in the assigned bed. Principal business event timestamp for the bed assignment lifecycle. Used for LOS (Length of Stay) calculation and capacity analytics.,
encounter,operational_logistics,bed_assignment,provider_assignment_status,provider_assignment_status,Bed Assignment Status,STRING,,,,pending|active|completed|cancelled|transferred,transactional_data,Current lifecycle state of the bed assignment. pending indicates a bed request has been made but not yet fulfilled; active indicates the patient is currently occupying the bed; completed indicates the patient has vacated; cancelled indicates the assignment was voided; transferred indicates the patient moved to another bed.,
encounter,operational_logistics,bed_assignment,request_timestamp,request_timestamp,Bed Request Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,"Date and time when the bed request was initiated by the clinical team or bed coordinator. Used to calculate bed request-to-assignment elapsed time, a key operational KPI (Key Performance Indicator) for bed management efficiency.",
encounter,operational_logistics,bed_assignment,request_to_assignment_minutes,request_to_assignment_minutes,Bed Request to Assignment Elapsed Time (Minutes),INT,,,,,transactional_data,Elapsed time in minutes between the bed request timestamp and the assignment start timestamp. Key operational KPI (Key Performance Indicator) for bed management throughput and ED (Emergency Department) boarding reduction. Sourced from Epic ADT or Cerner Bed Board workflow timestamps.,
encounter,operational_logistics,bed_assignment,room_number,room_number,Room Number,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Room number within the unit or ward where the bed is located. Used for wayfinding, nursing assignments, and infection control zone tracking.",
encounter,operational_logistics,bed_assignment,sequence,sequence,Bed Assignment Sequence Number,INT,,,,,transactional_data,"Sequential ordinal number of this bed assignment within the patients encounter, starting at 1 for the first bed assignment. Used to reconstruct the patients bed movement history throughout a visit and calculate total number of transfers.",
encounter,operational_logistics,bed_assignment,source_system,source_system,Source System,STRING,,,,epic_adt|cerner_millennium|meditech_expanse,transactional_data,"Identifies the operational system of record from which this bed assignment record was sourced. epic_adt = Epic ADT Bed Management module; cerner_millennium = Cerner Millennium Bed Board; meditech_expanse = MEDITECH Expanse ADT. Required for data lineage, ETL (Extract, Transform, Load) reconciliation, and multi-system environments.",
encounter,operational_logistics,bed_assignment,source_system_assignment_code,source_system_assignment_code,Source System Assignment ID,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Native identifier of this bed assignment record in the originating operational system (Epic ADT, Cerner Millennium, or MEDITECH Expanse). Used for cross-system reconciliation, data lineage tracing, and support of HIE (Health Information Exchange) integrations.",
encounter,operational_logistics,bed_assignment,unit_code,unit_code,Unit Code,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,Standardized alphanumeric code identifying the clinical unit or ward in the facilitys master data. Used for cross-system reporting and integration with billing and staffing systems.,
encounter,operational_logistics,bed_assignment,unit_name,unit_name,Unit Name,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Name of the clinical unit or ward where the bed is located (e.g., Medical ICU, 4 North Med-Surg, ED Observation). Used for unit-level capacity planning and staffing analytics.",
encounter,operational_logistics,bed_assignment,updated_timestamp,updated_timestamp,Record Updated Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,"Date and time when this bed assignment record was last modified in the source ADT system. Supports change tracking and incremental ETL (Extract, Transform, Load) processing.",
encounter,operational_logistics,bed_assignment,wing_or_pod,wing_or_pod,Wing or Pod,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Sub-unit designation within a nursing unit identifying the wing, pod, or cluster where the bed is located (e.g., North Wing, Pod A). Used for nursing assignment optimization and infection control zone management.",
encounter,operational_logistics,readmission,readmission_id,readmission_id,Readmission ID,BIGINT,Y,,,,transactional_data,Unique surrogate identifier for the readmission tracking record linking an index encounter to a subsequent readmission encounter.,
encounter,operational_logistics,readmission,care_site_id,care_site_id,Facility ID,BIGINT,,facility.care_site.care_site_id,,,transactional_data,Foreign key reference to the facility where the readmission encounter occurred. Supports facility-level HRRP penalty calculation and Joint Commission reporting.,
encounter,operational_logistics,readmission,clinical_ai_patient_risk_score_id,clinical_ai_patient_risk_score_id,Patient Risk Score Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,clinical_ai.clinical_ai_patient_risk_score.clinical_ai_patient_risk_score_id,,,transactional_data,Foreign key linking to clinical_ai.patient_risk_score. Business justification: CMS HRRP penalty calculations require linking readmission events to the predictive risk score that was active at index discharge. Enables root-cause analysis of whether risk stratification models corr,Internal - LLM Generated Cross-Domain Link
encounter,operational_logistics,readmission,clinician_id,clinician_id,Attending Provider ID,BIGINT,,provider.clinician.clinician_id,,,transactional_data,Foreign key reference to the attending physician responsible for the readmission encounter. Used for provider-level quality reporting and MIPS performance attribution.,
encounter,operational_logistics,readmission,compliance_regulatory_submission_id,compliance_regulatory_submission_id,Regulatory Submission Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,compliance.compliance_regulatory_submission.compliance_regulatory_submission_id,,,transactional_data,Foreign key linking to compliance.regulatory_submission. Business justification: Readmission data is directly submitted to CMS for Hospital Readmissions Reduction Program (HRRP) penalty calculation. Specific readmission records are referenced in regulatory submissions. Core CMS qu,
encounter,operational_logistics,readmission,demographics_id,demographics_id,Patient ID,BIGINT,,patient.demographics.demographics_id,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_identifier",,transactional_data,Foreign key reference to the patient record. Links the readmission pair to the Master Patient Index (MPI) for population health analytics and care management targeting.,
encounter,operational_logistics,readmission,index_drg_id,index_drg_id,Index Drg Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,reference.drg.drg_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to reference.drg. Business justification: Readmission tracking—index admission DRG must reference official DRG definition for HRRP penalty calculation, excess readmission ratio reporting, and quality measure validation. Required for CMS readm",
encounter,operational_logistics,readmission,mpi_record_id,mpi_record_id,,BIGINT,,patient.mpi_record.mpi_record_id,,,transactional_data,description,
encounter,operational_logistics,readmission,payer_id,payer_id,Payer ID,BIGINT,,insurance.payer.payer_id,,,transactional_data,Foreign key reference to the payer (insurance plan) responsible for the index encounter. Used to segment readmission rates by payer for value-based contract performance reporting and ACO/HMO/PPO analytics.,
encounter,operational_logistics,readmission,post_acute_episode_id,post_acute_episode_id,Post Acute Episode Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,post_acute_care.post_acute_episode.post_acute_episode_id,,,transactional_data,Foreign key linking to post_acute_care.post_acute_episode. Business justification: HRRP penalty calculations require linking readmissions to preceding PAC episodes. Quality teams analyze whether PAC failures caused readmission. CMS bundled payment models track this relationship for ,Internal - LLM Generated Cross-Domain Link
encounter,operational_logistics,readmission,primary_readmission_encounter_visit_id,primary_readmission_encounter_visit_id,Readmission Encounter ID,BIGINT,,encounter.visit.visit_id,,,transactional_data,Foreign key reference to the subsequent encounter that qualifies as a readmission within the defined time window following the index discharge.,
encounter,operational_logistics,readmission,readmission_original_visit_id,readmission_original_visit_id,,BIGINT,,encounter.visit.visit_id,,,transactional_data,FK to encounter.visit.visit_id,
encounter,operational_logistics,readmission,readmission_readmit_visit_id,readmission_readmit_visit_id,,BIGINT,,encounter.visit.visit_id,,,transactional_data,FK to encounter.visit.visit_id,
encounter,operational_logistics,readmission,aco_attributed,aco_attributed,Accountable Care Organization (ACO) Attributed Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,Indicates whether the patient was attributed to an Accountable Care Organization (ACO) at the time of the index encounter. ACO-attributed readmissions have direct financial implications under shared savings and risk-based contracts.,
encounter,operational_logistics,readmission,admission_date,admission_date,Readmission Admission Date,DATE,,,,,transactional_data,"Date the patient was admitted for the readmission encounter. Used to calculate days between discharge and readmission and to determine which time-window cohort (7, 30, 90 days) the readmission falls into.",
encounter,operational_logistics,readmission,admit_source,admit_source,Readmission Admission Source,STRING,,,,ed|physician_referral|transfer|direct_admit|other,transactional_data,"Source through which the patient was admitted for the readmission encounter (e.g., Emergency Department, physician referral, transfer from another facility). Supports analysis of care transition failure points.",
encounter,operational_logistics,readmission,care_gap_identified,care_gap_identified,Care Gap Identified,STRING,,,,no_follow_up_appointment|medication_reconciliation_gap|no_discharge_instructions|no_post_acute_referral|no_care_gap,transactional_data,Specific care gap identified during readmission review that contributed to the readmission event. Used to drive post-discharge intervention program design and care management outreach. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: no_follow_up_appointment|medication_reconciliation_gap|no_discharge_instructions|no_post_acute_referral|no_care_gap — promote to reference product],
encounter,operational_logistics,readmission,created_timestamp,created_timestamp,Record Created Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,"Timestamp when this readmission tracking record was first created in the system, typically triggered by the ADT discharge event or quality review workflow initiation.",
encounter,operational_logistics,readmission,days_to_readmission,days_to_readmission,Days to Readmission,INT,,,,,transactional_data,Number of calendar days elapsed between the index discharge date and the readmission admission date. Core metric for HRRP cohort assignment and post-discharge intervention effectiveness analysis.,
encounter,operational_logistics,readmission,drg_code,drg_code,Readmission Diagnosis-Related Group (DRG) Code,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,MS-DRG code assigned to the readmission encounter by the grouper. Used for financial impact analysis of readmissions on reimbursement and for HRRP penalty cost modeling.,
encounter,operational_logistics,readmission,estimated_penalty_amount,estimated_penalty_amount,Estimated HRRP Penalty Amount,"DECIMAL(12,2)",,,dbx_confidential,,transactional_data,Estimated financial penalty amount (in USD) attributable to this readmission under the CMS Hospital Readmissions Reduction Program. Used for revenue cycle impact analysis and CFO-level financial reporting. Confidential business financial data.,
encounter,operational_logistics,readmission,follow_up_appointment_date,follow_up_appointment_date,Post-Discharge Follow-Up Appointment Date,DATE,,,,,transactional_data,Scheduled date of the first post-discharge follow-up appointment after the index encounter. Used to assess timeliness of follow-up care and its correlation with readmission prevention.,
encounter,operational_logistics,readmission,follow_up_appointment_scheduled,follow_up_appointment_scheduled,Post-Discharge Follow-Up Appointment Scheduled Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,Indicates whether a follow-up outpatient appointment was scheduled prior to or at the time of index discharge. A key care gap indicator; absence is associated with higher 30-day readmission risk.,
encounter,operational_logistics,readmission,hrrp_excess_readmission_ratio,hrrp_excess_readmission_ratio,Hospital Readmissions Reduction Program (HRRP) Excess Readmission Ratio,"DECIMAL(8,4)",,,,,transactional_data,CMS-calculated ratio of predicted to expected readmissions for the applicable HRRP measure category. A ratio greater than 1.0 indicates excess readmissions subject to payment penalty. Sourced from CMS IPPS final rule calculations.,
encounter,operational_logistics,readmission,hrrp_measure_category,hrrp_measure_category,Hospital Readmissions Reduction Program (HRRP) Measure Category,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"CMS HRRP condition-specific measure category assigned to the readmission. AMI=Acute Myocardial Infarction, HF=Heart Failure, PN=Pneumonia, COPD=Chronic Obstructive Pulmonary Disease, THA_TKA=Total Hip/Knee Arthroplasty, CABG=Coronary Artery Bypass Graft, other=does not fall under a specific HRRP measure. Drives CMS penalty calculation and quality reporting. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: AMI|HF|PN|COPD|THA_TKA|CABG|other — promote to reference product]",
encounter,operational_logistics,readmission,index_discharge_date,index_discharge_date,Index Discharge Date,DATE,,,,,transactional_data,Date the patient was discharged from the index (original) inpatient encounter. Serves as the start of the readmission measurement window per CMS HRRP methodology.,
encounter,operational_logistics,readmission,index_discharge_disposition,index_discharge_disposition,Index Discharge Disposition,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Discharge disposition code from the index encounter indicating where the patient was discharged to. Critical for identifying post-acute care failures as a readmission root cause and for HRRP exclusion logic (e.g., AMA, expired). [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: home|home_health|snf|ltach|rehab|hospice|ama|expired — promote to reference product]",
encounter,operational_logistics,readmission,index_los_days,index_los_days,Index Length of Stay (LOS) Days,INT,,,,,transactional_data,Number of inpatient days for the index encounter. Used in readmission risk stratification and to assess whether short LOS contributed to the readmission.,
encounter,operational_logistics,readmission,index_primary_icd10_code,index_primary_icd10_code,Index Primary International Classification of Diseases 10th Revision (ICD-10) Diagnosis Code,STRING,,,,"^[A-Z][0-9A-Z]{1,6}$",transactional_data,Primary ICD-10-CM diagnosis code from the index encounter. Used to determine HRRP measure category eligibility and to analyze clinical patterns driving readmissions.,
encounter,operational_logistics,readmission,is_hrrp_applicable,is_hrrp_applicable,Hospital Readmissions Reduction Program (HRRP) Applicable Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,"Indicates whether this readmission is subject to CMS HRRP penalty calculation. False when the readmission meets CMS exclusion criteria (e.g., planned readmission, transfer, AMA discharge, death during index stay).",
encounter,operational_logistics,readmission,is_related_to_index,is_related_to_index,Clinically Related to Index Encounter Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,"Indicates whether the readmission diagnosis is clinically related to the index encounters principal diagnosis, as determined by clinical documentation review or CDI query outcome. Supports root cause analysis and preventability assessment.",
encounter,operational_logistics,readmission,los_days,los_days,Readmission Length of Stay (LOS) Days,INT,,,,,transactional_data,Number of inpatient days for the readmission encounter. Used for financial impact analysis and to assess severity of the readmission event.,
encounter,operational_logistics,readmission,medication_reconciliation_completed,medication_reconciliation_completed,Medication Reconciliation Completed Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,Indicates whether medication reconciliation was completed at the time of index discharge. Medication discrepancies are a leading cause of preventable readmissions; this flag supports MAR audit and quality reporting.,
encounter,operational_logistics,readmission,payer_type,payer_type,Payer Type,STRING,,,,medicare|medicaid|commercial|self_pay|other,transactional_data,"Classification of the payer for the index encounter. Medicare is the primary payer subject to CMS HRRP penalties. Segmentation by payer type enables value-based contract performance analysis across HMO, PPO, ACO, and government programs.",
encounter,operational_logistics,readmission,preventability_assessment,preventability_assessment,Readmission Preventability Assessment,STRING,,,,potentially_preventable|not_preventable|undetermined,transactional_data,"Clinical determination of whether the readmission was potentially preventable through improved care coordination, discharge planning, or post-discharge follow-up. Drives care management program targeting and quality improvement initiatives.",
encounter,operational_logistics,readmission,primary_icd10_code,primary_icd10_code,Readmission Primary International Classification of Diseases 10th Revision (ICD-10) Diagnosis Code,STRING,,,,"^[A-Z][0-9A-Z]{1,6}$",transactional_data,Primary ICD-10-CM diagnosis code assigned at the readmission encounter. Core field for determining whether the readmission is related to the index condition and for CMS HRRP measure attribution.,
encounter,operational_logistics,readmission,readmission_status,readmission_status,Readmission Status,STRING,,,,pending_review|confirmed|excluded|appealed|closed,transactional_data,Current workflow status of the readmission record within the quality review and HRRP adjudication process. pending_review indicates awaiting clinical validation; confirmed indicates validated readmission; excluded indicates meets CMS exclusion criteria; appealed indicates under payer or CMS appeal; closed indicates final disposition reached.,
encounter,operational_logistics,readmission,readmission_type,readmission_type,Readmission Type,STRING,,,,planned|unplanned,transactional_data,"Classification of the readmission as planned or unplanned per CMS HRRP methodology. Planned readmissions (e.g., scheduled chemotherapy, elective procedures) are excluded from HRRP penalty calculations. Unplanned readmissions are subject to CMS penalty assessment.",
encounter,operational_logistics,readmission,review_completed_date,review_completed_date,Readmission Review Completed Date,DATE,,,,,transactional_data,Date on which the clinical quality review of this readmission record was completed by the quality or CDI team. Supports workflow management and regulatory reporting timeliness tracking.,
encounter,operational_logistics,readmission,reviewer_notes,reviewer_notes,Readmission Reviewer Notes,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Free-text clinical notes entered by the quality reviewer documenting the rationale for preventability assessment, root cause determination, and any care gaps identified during the readmission review process.",
encounter,operational_logistics,readmission,risk_score,risk_score,Readmission Risk Score,"DECIMAL(5,2)",,,,,transactional_data,"Numeric risk score assigned to the patient at the time of index discharge predicting likelihood of 30-day readmission (e.g., LACE score, HOSPITAL score, Epic readmission risk model output). Used for care management program targeting and post-discharge intervention prioritization.",
encounter,operational_logistics,readmission,risk_score_model,risk_score_model,Readmission Risk Score Model,STRING,,,,LACE|HOSPITAL|BOOST|epic_model|custom,transactional_data,"Name of the validated risk stratification model used to generate the readmission risk score. LACE=Length of stay, Acuity, Comorbidities, ED visits; HOSPITAL=Hemoglobin, Oncology, Sodium, Procedure, Index admission type, Type of admission, number of Admissions, Length of stay.",
encounter,operational_logistics,readmission,root_cause_category,root_cause_category,Readmission Root Cause Category,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,Categorized root cause of the readmission as identified through clinical review. Supports targeted quality improvement interventions and population health management. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: medication_issue|care_coordination_gap|patient_non_compliance|inadequate_discharge_planning|disease_progression|social_determinants|post_acute_care_failure — promote to reference product],
encounter,operational_logistics,readmission,sdoh_flag,sdoh_flag,Social Determinants of Health (SDOH) Contributing Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,"Indicates whether Social Determinants of Health (SDOH) factors (e.g., housing instability, food insecurity, transportation barriers) were identified as contributing to the readmission. Supports population health management and care management program targeting.",
encounter,operational_logistics,readmission,tracking_number,tracking_number,Readmission Tracking Number,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Externally visible business identifier for this readmission record, used in care management workflows, quality reporting submissions, and cross-system reconciliation (e.g., Epic Healthy Planet case reference).",
encounter,operational_logistics,readmission,transition_of_care_completed,transition_of_care_completed,Transition of Care Completed Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,"Indicates whether a formal transition of care communication (e.g., discharge summary transmitted to PCP, care transition call completed) was documented following the index discharge. Supports HEDIS Transitions of Care measure compliance.",
encounter,operational_logistics,readmission,updated_timestamp,updated_timestamp,Record Updated Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,"Timestamp when this readmission tracking record was last modified, such as when a review is completed, status changes, or preventability assessment is updated.",
encounter,operational_logistics,readmission,window,window,Readmission Time Window,STRING,,,,7_day|30_day|90_day,transactional_data,Defined time window within which the readmission occurred relative to the index discharge. 7_day supports high-acuity post-discharge monitoring; 30_day is the primary CMS HRRP measurement window; 90_day supports extended care management program targeting.,
encounter,operational_logistics,transfer_request,transfer_request_id,transfer_request_id,Transfer Request Identifier (ID),BIGINT,Y,,,,transactional_data,Unique identifier for the patient transfer request record. Primary key for the transfer_request product.,
