encounter,operational_logistics,transfer_request,destination_bed_id,destination_bed_id,Destination Bed Identifier (ID),BIGINT,,facility.bed.bed_id,,,transactional_data,Reference to the specific bed assigned to the patient at the destination facility.,
encounter,operational_logistics,transfer_request,destination_facility_care_site_id,destination_facility_care_site_id,Destination Facility Identifier (ID),BIGINT,,facility.care_site.care_site_id,,,transactional_data,Reference to the facility to which the patient is being transferred.,
encounter,operational_logistics,transfer_request,employee_id,employee_id,Approved By User Identifier (ID),BIGINT,,workforce.employee.employee_id,"dbx_confidential, dbx_pii",,transactional_data,"Reference to the user (administrator, physician, or case manager) who approved the transfer request.",
encounter,operational_logistics,transfer_request,mpi_record_id,mpi_record_id,Patient Identifier (ID),BIGINT,,patient.mpi_record.mpi_record_id,,,transactional_data,Reference to the patient being transferred.,
encounter,operational_logistics,transfer_request,origin_bed_id,origin_bed_id,Origin Bed Identifier (ID),BIGINT,,facility.bed.bed_id,,,transactional_data,Reference to the specific bed the patient is being transferred from.,
encounter,operational_logistics,transfer_request,origin_cost_center_id,origin_cost_center_id,Origin Cost Center Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,finance.cost_center.cost_center_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to finance.cost_center. Business justification: Inter-unit transfers move cost responsibility between cost centers. Required for accurate departmental cost accounting, transfer pricing between units, and cost allocation during multi-department epis",
encounter,operational_logistics,transfer_request,original_transfer_request_id,original_transfer_request_id,Original Transfer Request Id,BIGINT,,encounter.transfer_request.transfer_request_id,dbx_self_ref_fk,,transactional_data,Self-referencing FK on transfer_request (original_transfer_request_id),
encounter,operational_logistics,transfer_request,post_acute_location_id,post_acute_location_id,Post Acute Location Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,post_acute_care.post_acute_location.post_acute_location_id,,,transactional_data,Foreign key linking to post_acute_care.post_acute_location. Business justification: Inter-facility transfers to SNFs/rehab/LTACH require referencing the PAC destination. EMTALA and CMS transfer regulations mandate documenting receiving facility. Supports bed management and transfer c,Internal - LLM Generated Cross-Domain Link
encounter,operational_logistics,transfer_request,primary_transfer_care_site_id,primary_transfer_care_site_id,Origin Facility Identifier (ID),BIGINT,,facility.care_site.care_site_id,,,transactional_data,Reference to the facility from which the patient is being transferred.,
encounter,operational_logistics,transfer_request,primary_transfer_clinician_id,primary_transfer_clinician_id,Requesting Provider Identifier (ID),BIGINT,,provider.clinician.clinician_id,,,transactional_data,Reference to the provider who initiated the transfer request.,
encounter,operational_logistics,transfer_request,visit_id,visit_id,Encounter Identifier (ID),BIGINT,,encounter.visit.visit_id,,,transactional_data,Reference to the encounter (visit) for which the transfer is being requested.,
encounter,operational_logistics,transfer_request,accepting_provider_npi,accepting_provider_npi,Accepting Provider National Provider Identifier (NPI),STRING,,,,,transactional_data,National Provider Identifier of the physician or clinician accepting the patient at the destination facility.,
encounter,operational_logistics,transfer_request,actual_transfer_timestamp,actual_transfer_timestamp,Actual Transfer Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,Actual date and time when the patient transfer was completed and the patient arrived at the destination.,
encounter,operational_logistics,transfer_request,acuity_level,acuity_level,Patient Acuity Level,STRING,,,,critical|acute|stable|routine,transactional_data,"Clinical acuity classification of the patient at the time of transfer request, indicating urgency and level of care required.",
encounter,operational_logistics,transfer_request,approval_required,approval_required,Approval Required Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,Indicates whether the transfer request requires administrative or clinical approval before proceeding.,
encounter,operational_logistics,transfer_request,approval_timestamp,approval_timestamp,Approval Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,Date and time when the transfer request was approved.,
encounter,operational_logistics,transfer_request,bed_availability_confirmed,bed_availability_confirmed,Bed Availability Confirmed Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,Indicates whether the destination facility has confirmed availability of an appropriate bed for the patient.,
encounter,operational_logistics,transfer_request,cancellation_reason,cancellation_reason,Cancellation Reason,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,Explanation for why the transfer request was cancelled after initial approval.,
encounter,operational_logistics,transfer_request,claim_denial_reason,claim_denial_reason,Denial Reason,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Explanation for why the transfer request was denied, if applicable.",
encounter,operational_logistics,transfer_request,clinical_indication,clinical_indication,Clinical Indication,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Detailed clinical justification for the transfer, including diagnosis, condition severity, and required interventions not available at the origin facility.",
encounter,operational_logistics,transfer_request,created_timestamp,created_timestamp,Record Created Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,Date and time when this transfer request record was first created in the system.,
encounter,operational_logistics,transfer_request,destination_unit_code,destination_unit_code,Destination Unit Code,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,Department or unit code at the destination facility where the patient will be admitted.,
encounter,operational_logistics,transfer_request,emtala_certification_completed,emtala_certification_completed,Emergency Medical Treatment and Labor Act (EMTALA) Certification Completed Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,"Indicates whether the required EMTALA physician certification form has been completed, documenting that medical benefits of transfer outweigh risks.",
encounter,operational_logistics,transfer_request,emtala_certification_timestamp,emtala_certification_timestamp,Emergency Medical Treatment and Labor Act (EMTALA) Certification Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,Date and time when the EMTALA physician certification was signed.,
encounter,operational_logistics,transfer_request,emtala_compliant,emtala_compliant,Emergency Medical Treatment and Labor Act (EMTALA) Compliant Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,"Indicates whether the transfer request meets EMTALA requirements for appropriate transfer, including medical screening, stabilization, and informed consent.",
encounter,operational_logistics,transfer_request,isolation_required,isolation_required,Isolation Required Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,Indicates whether the patient requires isolation precautions during and after transfer due to infectious disease or other clinical reasons.,
encounter,operational_logistics,transfer_request,isolation_type,isolation_type,Isolation Type,STRING,,,,contact|droplet|airborne|protective|none,transactional_data,"Type of isolation precautions required for the patient (e.g., contact, droplet, airborne, protective).",
encounter,operational_logistics,transfer_request,level_of_care_required,level_of_care_required,Level of Care Required,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Specific level of care needed at the destination facility (e.g., ICU, step-down, telemetry, general medical-surgical).",
encounter,operational_logistics,transfer_request,medical_records_sent,medical_records_sent,Medical Records Sent Flag,BOOLEAN,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii",,transactional_data,"Indicates whether copies of medical records, imaging, and test results have been sent to the accepting facility.",
encounter,operational_logistics,transfer_request,medical_records_sent_timestamp,medical_records_sent_timestamp,Medical Records Sent Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii",,transactional_data,Date and time when medical records were transmitted to the destination facility.,
encounter,operational_logistics,transfer_request,mrn,mrn,Medical Record Number (MRN),STRING,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_identifier",,transactional_data,The patients medical record number at the originating facility.,
encounter,operational_logistics,transfer_request,origin_unit_code,origin_unit_code,Origin Unit Code,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,Department or unit code at the origin facility where the patient is currently located.,
encounter,operational_logistics,transfer_request,patient_consent_obtained,patient_consent_obtained,Patient Consent Obtained Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,Indicates whether informed consent for the transfer has been obtained from the patient or their legal representative.,
encounter,operational_logistics,transfer_request,patient_consent_timestamp,patient_consent_timestamp,Patient Consent Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,Date and time when patient or representative consent for transfer was documented.,
encounter,operational_logistics,transfer_request,patient_stability_score,patient_stability_score,Patient Stability Score,INT,,,,,transactional_data,"Numeric score representing the patients clinical stability at the time of transfer, used to assess transfer risk.",
encounter,operational_logistics,transfer_request,primary_diagnosis_code,primary_diagnosis_code,Primary Diagnosis Code (ICD-10),STRING,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_health",,transactional_data,ICD-10 diagnosis code representing the primary condition necessitating the transfer.,
encounter,operational_logistics,transfer_request,primary_diagnosis_description,primary_diagnosis_description,Primary Diagnosis Description,STRING,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_health",,transactional_data,Human-readable description of the primary diagnosis associated with the transfer request.,
encounter,operational_logistics,transfer_request,request_timestamp,request_timestamp,Transfer Request Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,Date and time when the transfer request was initiated. This is the principal business event timestamp for the transfer request transaction.,
encounter,operational_logistics,transfer_request,requested_transfer_timestamp,requested_transfer_timestamp,Requested Transfer Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,"Desired date and time for the patient transfer to occur, as specified by the requesting provider.",
encounter,operational_logistics,transfer_request,requesting_provider_npi,requesting_provider_npi,Requesting Provider National Provider Identifier (NPI),STRING,,,,,transactional_data,National Provider Identifier of the physician or clinician requesting the transfer.,
encounter,operational_logistics,transfer_request,source_system,source_system,Source System,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Name of the operational system from which this transfer request record originated (e.g., Epic, Cerner, MEDITECH).",
encounter,operational_logistics,transfer_request,source_system_record_code,source_system_record_code,Source System Record Identifier (ID),STRING,,,,,transactional_data,Unique identifier for this transfer request in the source operational system.,
encounter,operational_logistics,transfer_request,specialty_service_required,specialty_service_required,Specialty Service Required,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Specialized medical service or capability required at the destination facility (e.g., neurosurgery, cardiac catheterization, burn unit, neonatal intensive care).",
encounter,operational_logistics,transfer_request,transfer_reason,transfer_reason,Transfer Reason,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,Clinical or operational reason for the transfer request. Free-text description of why the patient needs to be transferred.,
encounter,operational_logistics,transfer_request,transfer_reason_code,transfer_reason_code,Transfer Reason Code,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Standardized code representing the reason for transfer (e.g., higher level of care, specialty service unavailable, patient request, capacity constraints).",
encounter,operational_logistics,transfer_request,transfer_request_number,transfer_request_number,Transfer Request Number,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Business identifier for the transfer request, used for tracking and communication between facilities.",
encounter,operational_logistics,transfer_request,transfer_status,transfer_status,Transfer Request Status,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,Current lifecycle status of the transfer request. Tracks the request from initial submission through completion or cancellation. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: requested|pending_approval|approved|in_progress|completed|cancelled|denied — 7 candidates stripped; promote to reference product],
encounter,operational_logistics,transfer_request,transfer_type,transfer_type,Transfer Type,STRING,,,,inter_facility|intra_facility|emergency|elective|specialty_care|higher_level_of_care,transactional_data,"Classification of the transfer request based on scope and urgency. Inter-facility transfers occur between different healthcare organizations, intra-facility transfers occur within the same organization.",
encounter,operational_logistics,transfer_request,transport_mode,transport_mode,Transport Mode,STRING,,,,ambulance|air_ambulance|wheelchair_van|private_vehicle|walk,transactional_data,Method of transportation used or planned for the patient transfer.,
encounter,operational_logistics,transfer_request,transport_provider,transport_provider,Transport Provider,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Name of the ambulance service, air transport company, or other transportation provider responsible for the transfer.",
encounter,operational_logistics,transfer_request,updated_timestamp,updated_timestamp,Record Updated Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,Date and time when this transfer request record was last modified.,
encounter,patient_visit,adt_event,adt_event_id,adt_event_id,Admit Discharge Transfer (ADT) Event ID,BIGINT,Y,,,,transactional_data,Unique surrogate identifier for each ADT event record in the silver layer. Primary key for the adt_event data product. Role: TRANSACTION_HEADER.,
encounter,patient_visit,adt_event,clinician_id,clinician_id,Responsible Provider ID,BIGINT,,provider.clinician.clinician_id,,,transactional_data,"Reference to the attending or responsible provider at the time of this ADT event. Captures the clinician accountable for the patient at the moment of admit, transfer, or discharge.",
encounter,patient_visit,adt_event,demographics_id,demographics_id,Patient ID,BIGINT,,patient.demographics.demographics_id,,,transactional_data,"Reference to the patient associated with this ADT event. Serves as the PARTY_REFERENCE for this TRANSACTION_HEADER, linking the event to the Master Patient Index (MPI).",
encounter,patient_visit,adt_event,drg_id,drg_id,Drg Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,reference.drg.drg_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to reference.drg. Business justification: ADT event tracking—DRG codes captured during patient movement events must reference official DRG definitions for real-time case management, bed utilization analysis, and revenue cycle monitoring. Requ",
encounter,patient_visit,adt_event,employee_id,employee_id,Transporting Employee Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,workforce.employee.employee_id,"dbx_confidential, dbx_pii",,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to workforce.employee. Business justification: Patient transport events require accountability tracking for safety incidents, OSHA reporting, and labor cost allocation. Transport staff (orderlies, techs) are workforce employees whose activity must",
encounter,patient_visit,adt_event,message_log_id,message_log_id,Health Level Seven (HL7) Message ID,BIGINT,,interoperability.message_log.message_log_id,,,transactional_data,"Unique identifier of the originating HL7 ADT message from the source system (Epic or Cerner). Used for message traceability, deduplication, and reconciliation with upstream ADT feeds. Corresponds to MSH-10 in HL7 v2.x.",
encounter,patient_visit,adt_event,prior_event_adt_event_id,prior_event_adt_event_id,Prior ADT Event ID,BIGINT,,encounter.adt_event.adt_event_id,,,transactional_data,Reference to the immediately preceding ADT event in the same encounters event chain. Enables reconstruction of the full ADT event sequence and care pathway for LOS milestone tracking and transitions-of-care analysis.,
encounter,patient_visit,adt_event,visit_id,visit_id,Encounter ID,BIGINT,,encounter.visit.visit_id,,,transactional_data,"Reference to the parent encounter (visit) to which this ADT event belongs. Links the ADT event to the broader encounter context including patient, provider, and billing information.",
encounter,patient_visit,adt_event,accepting_provider_npi,accepting_provider_npi,Accepting Provider National Provider Identifier (NPI),STRING,,,,^[0-9]{10}$,transactional_data,10-digit National Provider Identifier (NPI) of the provider accepting responsibility for the patient at the destination care setting during a transfer event. Required for EMTALA transfer compliance documentation and inter-facility transfer records.,
encounter,patient_visit,adt_event,admission_source_code,admission_source_code,Admission Source Code,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Standardized code indicating the source from which the patient was admitted (e.g., physician referral, emergency room, transfer from another facility, birth). Corresponds to PV1-14 (Admit Source) in HL7 v2.x and UB-04 field 15. Used for DRG grouping and regulatory reporting. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: 1|2|3|4|5|6|7|8|9 — promote to reference product per UB-04 Admit Source codes]",
encounter,patient_visit,adt_event,ama_flag,ama_flag,Against Medical Advice (AMA) Discharge Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,"Indicates whether the patient was discharged Against Medical Advice (AMA). Populated for discharge events (A03). Relevant for discharge disposition coding, liability documentation, and readmission risk analysis.",
encounter,patient_visit,adt_event,bed_assigned_timestamp,bed_assigned_timestamp,Bed Assigned Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,Date and time a specific bed was assigned to the patient as part of this ADT event. Used to calculate bed assignment turnaround time and support capacity management analytics.,
encounter,patient_visit,adt_event,bed_request_timestamp,bed_request_timestamp,Bed Request Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,Date and time a bed was requested for the patient as part of this ADT event. Used to calculate bed placement turnaround time and support real-time bed management KPIs.,
encounter,patient_visit,adt_event,cancel_reason,cancel_reason,ADT Event Cancellation Reason,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Free-text or coded reason for cancellation when event_status is cancelled. Captures clinical or administrative rationale for reversing an ADT event (e.g., Patient not admitted, Duplicate registration). Corresponds to EVN-4 in HL7 v2.x.",
encounter,patient_visit,adt_event,clinical_reason_for_transfer,clinical_reason_for_transfer,Clinical Reason for Transfer,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Free-text or coded clinical justification for a patient transfer event (e.g., Requires ICU-level monitoring, Specialist not available at sending facility). Populated for transfer and inter-facility transition events. Supports EMTALA compliance documentation and care transitions analysis.",
encounter,patient_visit,adt_event,consent_event_recorded_timestamp,consent_event_recorded_timestamp,ADT Event Recorded Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,The date and time the ADT event was recorded or entered into the source system (Epic or Cerner). May differ from event_timestamp when events are back-entered. Corresponds to EVN-4 (Event Recorded Date/Time) in HL7 v2.x.,
encounter,patient_visit,adt_event,consent_event_status,consent_event_status,ADT Event Status,STRING,,,,active|cancelled|corrected|pending,transactional_data,"Current lifecycle status of the ADT event record. active indicates a valid, confirmed event; cancelled indicates the event was reversed (e.g., A11 Cancel Admit); corrected indicates the event was amended; pending indicates the event is pre-registered or pre-admitted but not yet confirmed.",
encounter,patient_visit,adt_event,consent_event_timestamp,consent_event_timestamp,ADT Event Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,"The precise date and time the ADT event occurred in the real world (e.g., when the patient was physically admitted, transferred, or discharged). This is the BUSINESS_EVENT_TIMESTAMP — distinct from record audit timestamps. Corresponds to EVN-2 in HL7 v2.x.",
encounter,patient_visit,adt_event,consent_event_type_code,consent_event_type_code,ADT Event Type Code,STRING,,,,A01|A02|A03|A04|A05|A06,transactional_data,"HL7 ADT event type code identifying the nature of the ADT transaction. Standard HL7 v2.x event codes include A01 (Admit), A02 (Transfer), A03 (Discharge), A04 (Register Outpatient), A05 (Pre-Admit), A06 (Change Outpatient to Inpatient), A07 (Change Inpatient to Outpatient), A08 (Update Patient Info), A11 (Cancel Admit), A12 (Cancel Transfer), A13 (Cancel Discharge), A21 (Patient Goes on Leave of Absence), A22 (Patient Returns from Leave of Absence), among others. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: A01|A02|A03|A04|A05|A06|A07|A08|A09|A10|A11|A12|A13|A21|A22 — promote to reference product]",
encounter,patient_visit,adt_event,consent_event_type_description,consent_event_type_description,ADT Event Type Description,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Human-readable description of the ADT event type corresponding to the event_type_code (e.g., Admit a Patient, Transfer a Patient, Discharge/End Visit). Sourced from HL7 ADT event type table.",
encounter,patient_visit,adt_event,created_timestamp,created_timestamp,Record Created Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,Date and time this ADT event record was first created in the silver layer data product. Serves as the RECORD_AUDIT_CREATED timestamp for data lineage and audit trail purposes.,
encounter,patient_visit,adt_event,discharge_disposition_code,discharge_disposition_code,Discharge Disposition Code,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Standardized code indicating the patients status or destination at discharge (e.g., home, skilled nursing facility, expired, AMA). Corresponds to PV1-36 (Discharge Disposition) in HL7 v2.x and UB-04 field 17. Required for DRG assignment, readmission risk, and CMS quality reporting. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: 01|02|03|04|05|06|07|20|30|43|50|51|61|62|63|64|65|66|69|70|71|72 — promote to reference product per NUBC Patient Discharge Status codes]",
encounter,patient_visit,adt_event,drg_type,drg_type,Diagnosis-Related Group (DRG) Type,STRING,,,,MS-DRG|APR-DRG|IR-DRG,transactional_data,Classification of the DRG methodology used for grouping. MS-DRG (Medicare Severity DRG) is used for Medicare/Medicaid; APR-DRG (All Patient Refined DRG) is used for commercial and Medicaid managed care; IR-DRG (International Refined DRG) for international payers.,
encounter,patient_visit,adt_event,emtala_compliant,emtala_compliant,Emergency Medical Treatment and Labor Act (EMTALA) Transfer Compliance Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,"Indicates whether the transfer event meets all EMTALA (Emergency Medical Treatment and Labor Act) compliance requirements, including medical screening examination, stabilization, and appropriate transfer documentation. Applicable to inter-facility transfer events from emergency settings.",
encounter,patient_visit,adt_event,emtala_transfer_form_completed,emtala_transfer_form_completed,EMTALA Transfer Form Completed Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,Indicates whether the required EMTALA transfer certification form was completed and signed by the responsible physician prior to inter-facility transfer. Supports OIG audit readiness and EMTALA compliance tracking.,
encounter,patient_visit,adt_event,from_bed_code,from_bed_code,From Bed Code,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,Specific bed identifier from which the patient is being transferred or discharged. Supports real-time bed management and occupancy tracking. Corresponds to PV1-3 (Prior Patient Location) bed component in HL7 v2.x.,
encounter,patient_visit,adt_event,from_unit_code,from_unit_code,From Unit Code,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Code identifying the nursing unit, care area, or department from which the patient is being transferred or discharged. For admission events, this represents the originating unit (e.g., ED). Corresponds to PV1-3 prior location in HL7 v2.x.",
encounter,patient_visit,adt_event,isolation_flag,isolation_flag,Patient Isolation Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,"Indicates whether the patient requires isolation precautions at the time of this ADT event (e.g., contact, droplet, airborne precautions). Drives bed assignment logic, infection control workflows, and HAI prevention protocols.",
encounter,patient_visit,adt_event,isolation_type,isolation_type,Isolation Type,STRING,,,,contact|droplet|airborne|protective|none,transactional_data,"Type of isolation precaution required for the patient at the time of this ADT event. Values: contact, droplet, airborne, protective (reverse isolation), none. Populated when isolation_flag is true. Supports infection control and bed management workflows.",
encounter,patient_visit,adt_event,leave_of_absence_reason,leave_of_absence_reason,Leave of Absence Reason,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Reason for a patient leave of absence event (HL7 A21). Captures the clinical or administrative justification when a patient temporarily leaves the facility (e.g., therapeutic pass, family visit). Null for non-leave events.",
encounter,patient_visit,adt_event,level_of_care_code,level_of_care_code,Level of Care Code,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Code representing the clinical level of care at the destination unit for this ADT event. Values: ICU (Intensive Care Unit), PCU (Progressive Care Unit), MED_SURG (Medical-Surgical), ED (Emergency Department), OR (Operating Room), PACU (Post-Anesthesia Care Unit), OBS (Observation), TELE (Telemetry), NICU (Neonatal ICU), PICU (Pediatric ICU). Supports LOS milestone tracking and level-of-care transition analysis. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: ICU|PCU|MED_SURG|ED|OR|PACU|OBS|TELE|NICU|PICU — 10 candidates stripped; promote to reference product]",
encounter,patient_visit,adt_event,patient_class_code,patient_class_code,Patient Class Code,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"HL7 patient class code indicating the care setting type at the time of this ADT event. Values: I=Inpatient, O=Outpatient, E=Emergency, B=Obstetrics, C=Commercial Account, N=Not Applicable, R=Recurring Patient, U=Unknown. Corresponds to PV1-2 in HL7 v2.x. Drives billing, regulatory reporting, and LOS calculations. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: I|O|E|B|C|N|R|U — 8 candidates stripped; promote to reference product]",
encounter,patient_visit,adt_event,patient_stability_score,patient_stability_score,Patient Stability Score at Transfer,STRING,,,,stable|guarded|critical|unstable,transactional_data,"Clinical assessment of patient stability at the time of a transfer event. Values: stable, guarded, critical, unstable. Required for EMTALA transfer compliance documentation and supports risk stratification for inter-facility transfers.",
encounter,patient_visit,adt_event,readmission_risk_flag,readmission_risk_flag,Readmission Risk Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,Indicates whether the patient has been flagged as high-risk for readmission at the time of this discharge ADT event. Populated by predictive risk models or clinical decision support tools. Supports CMS Hospital Readmissions Reduction Program (HRRP) compliance and care transitions planning.,
encounter,patient_visit,adt_event,sending_application,sending_application,Sending Application,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Name of the source application that generated the HL7 ADT message (e.g., EPIC, CERNER). Corresponds to MSH-3 (Sending Application) in HL7 v2.x. Supports source system traceability and ETL lineage.",
encounter,patient_visit,adt_event,sending_facility,sending_facility,Sending Facility,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,Name or identifier of the facility or system that originated the HL7 ADT message. Corresponds to MSH-4 (Sending Facility) in HL7 v2.x. Used for multi-facility environments and HIE routing.,
encounter,patient_visit,adt_event,sequence_number,sequence_number,ADT Event Sequence Number,INT,,,,,transactional_data,"Ordinal sequence number of this ADT event within the encounters event chain. Enables chronological ordering of all ADT events for a given encounter when timestamps alone are insufficient (e.g., same-second events).",
encounter,patient_visit,adt_event,source_system_event_code,source_system_event_code,Source System ADT Event ID,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Native identifier of this ADT event in the originating source system (Epic or Cerner). Used for ETL reconciliation, deduplication, and bi-directional traceability between the lakehouse silver layer and the operational EHR system.",
encounter,patient_visit,adt_event,source_system_name,source_system_name,Source System Name,STRING,,,,EPIC|CERNER|MEDITECH,transactional_data,"Name of the operational EHR system that is the authoritative source for this ADT event record. Values: EPIC (Epic EHR ADT), CERNER (Cerner Millennium ADT), MEDITECH (MEDITECH Expanse). Supports multi-system environments and data lineage.",
encounter,patient_visit,adt_event,to_bed_code,to_bed_code,To Bed Code,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Specific bed identifier to which the patient is being admitted or transferred. Supports real-time bed management, housekeeping workflows, and infection control tracking. Corresponds to PV1-3 assigned bed component in HL7 v2.x.",
encounter,patient_visit,adt_event,to_room_code,to_room_code,To Room Code,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,Room identifier within the destination unit to which the patient is assigned. Complements to_bed_code for full location resolution. Corresponds to PV1-3 room component in HL7 v2.x.,
encounter,patient_visit,adt_event,to_unit_code,to_unit_code,To Unit Code,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Code identifying the nursing unit, care area, or department to which the patient is being admitted or transferred. Corresponds to PV1-3 (Assigned Patient Location) in HL7 v2.x. Central to real-time bed management and capacity planning.",
encounter,patient_visit,adt_event,transition_type,transition_type,Care Transition Type,STRING,,,,inter_unit|level_of_care_change|inter_facility|internal_transfer|external_transfer,transactional_data,"Classification of the care setting transition for transfer events. Values: inter_unit (within same facility, same level of care), level_of_care_change (e.g., floor to ICU), inter_facility (between different facilities), internal_transfer, external_transfer. Null for non-transfer events. Supports transitions-of-care quality measures.",
encounter,patient_visit,adt_event,transport_mode,transport_mode,Transport Mode,STRING,,,,ambulance|helicopter|wheelchair|stretcher|ambulatory|private_vehicle,transactional_data,"Mode of transport used for patient transfer between care settings or facilities. Applicable for transfer and discharge events. Values include ambulance, helicopter, wheelchair, stretcher, ambulatory, private_vehicle. Null for non-transfer events.",
encounter,patient_visit,adt_event,updated_timestamp,updated_timestamp,Record Updated Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,"Date and time this ADT event record was last modified in the silver layer data product. Serves as the RECORD_AUDIT_UPDATED timestamp. Updated when corrections, cancellations, or amendments are applied to the event.",
encounter,patient_visit,adt_event,visit_type_code,visit_type_code,Visit Type Code,STRING,,,,inpatient|outpatient|emergency|observation|telehealth|ambulatory,transactional_data,"Classification of the visit type associated with this ADT event (e.g., inpatient, outpatient, emergency, observation, telehealth, ambulatory). Complements patient_class_code with business-level visit categorization used in analytics and reporting.",
encounter,patient_visit,visit,visit_id,visit_id,Visit ID,BIGINT,Y,,"pii_phi,pii_pii,pii_sensitive",,master_data,Add PII/PHI classification tags,
encounter,patient_visit,visit,cost_center_id,cost_center_id,Cost Center Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,finance.cost_center.cost_center_id,,,master_data,"Foreign key linking to finance.cost_center. Business justification: Every visit incurs costs tracked to a specific cost center for departmental P&L, variance analysis, Medicare cost reporting, and service-line profitability. Core operational link in healthcare financi",
