encounter,patient_visit,visit,admission_source,admission_source,Admission Source,STRING,,,,emergency_department|direct_admission|transfer|referral|birth,master_data,"Indicates the origin point from which the patient entered the facility for this visit. Required for UB-04 billing, readmission analysis, and care transition reporting. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: emergency_department|direct_admission|transfer|referral|birth|court_law|information_not_available — promote to reference product]",
encounter,patient_visit,visit,admission_timestamp,admission_timestamp,Admission Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,master_data,"Date and time the patient was formally admitted to the facility or the visit began. Principal business event timestamp for the encounter lifecycle. Used for LOS calculation, throughput analytics, and regulatory reporting.",
encounter,patient_visit,visit,admission_type,admission_type,Admission Type,STRING,,,,elective|urgent|emergent|newborn|trauma,master_data,Characterizes the clinical urgency and circumstance under which the patient was admitted. Required for UB-04 billing and DRG grouping. Sourced from Epic ADT or Cerner PowerChart admission workflow.,
encounter,patient_visit,visit,admitting_diagnosis_code,admitting_diagnosis_code,Admitting Diagnosis ICD-10 Code,STRING,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_health","^[A-Z][0-9A-Z]{1,6}(.[0-9A-Z]{1,4})?$",master_data,"ICD-10-CM code representing the condition documented at the time of admission, before full workup. May differ from the principal discharge diagnosis. Required on UB-04 for inpatient claims.",
encounter,patient_visit,visit,care_setting,care_setting,Care Setting,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Specific clinical environment within the facility where the patient received care during this visit. More granular than visit type; used for staffing, capacity management, and HAI surveillance. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: inpatient_ward|icu|ed|or|observation_unit|outpatient_clinic|telehealth|labor_delivery|nicu|step_down — promote to reference product]",
encounter,patient_visit,visit,care_transition_plan_completed,care_transition_plan_completed,Care Transition Plan Completed Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,Indicates whether a formal care transition plan was completed and communicated to the receiving provider or care setting at discharge. Required for CMS Transitional Care Management billing and TJC accreditation.,
encounter,patient_visit,visit,consent_obtained,consent_obtained,Informed Consent Obtained Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,Indicates whether informed consent for treatment was obtained and documented at the time of admission or prior to procedure. Required for TJC accreditation and HIPAA compliance.,
encounter,patient_visit,visit,converted_to_inpatient,converted_to_inpatient,Converted to Inpatient Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,Indicates whether an observation encounter was subsequently converted to a formal inpatient admission. Triggers billing reclassification and DRG assignment workflows.,
encounter,patient_visit,visit,created_timestamp,created_timestamp,Record Created Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,master_data,"Date and time the visit record was first created in the source EHR system. Used for audit trail, data lineage, and ETL processing. Sourced from Epic or Cerner encounter creation event.",
encounter,patient_visit,visit,discharge_disposition,discharge_disposition,Discharge Disposition,STRING,,,,home|snf|rehab|ama|expired|hospice,master_data,"Standardized code describing where the patient went or what occurred at the conclusion of the visit. Required for UB-04 billing, DRG grouping, readmission risk stratification, and CMS quality reporting. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: home|snf|rehab|ama|expired|hospice|transfer_acute|transfer_other|home_health|left_without_being_seen — promote to reference product]",
encounter,patient_visit,visit,discharge_instructions_issued,discharge_instructions_issued,Discharge Instructions Issued Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,"Indicates whether written discharge instructions were provided to the patient or caregiver at the time of discharge. Required for TJC accreditation, HCAHPS scoring, and CMS Conditions of Participation.",
encounter,patient_visit,visit,discharge_timestamp,discharge_timestamp,Discharge Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,master_data,"Date and time the patient was formally discharged or the visit concluded. Used for LOS calculation, bed management, and revenue cycle close-out. Null for visits still in progress.",
encounter,patient_visit,visit,drg_type,drg_type,Diagnosis-Related Group (DRG) Type,STRING,,,,MS-DRG|APR-DRG|AP-DRG,master_data,"Identifies the DRG classification system used for this encounter (Medicare Severity DRG, All Patient Refined DRG, or All Patient DRG). Determines reimbursement methodology and payer applicability.",
encounter,patient_visit,visit,drg_weight,drg_weight,Diagnosis-Related Group (DRG) Relative Weight,"DECIMAL(8,4)",,,,,master_data,"Numeric relative weight assigned to the DRG, reflecting the average resource intensity of cases in that group. Used to calculate expected reimbursement and Case Mix Index (CMI) contribution for the facility.",
encounter,patient_visit,visit,emtala_compliant,emtala_compliant,Emergency Medical Treatment and Labor Act (EMTALA) Compliance Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,"Indicates whether EMTALA obligations were assessed and met for this visit, including medical screening examination and stabilization requirements. Critical for ED visits and transfer scenarios. Required for OIG compliance audits.",
encounter,patient_visit,visit,encounter_number,encounter_number,Encounter Number,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Human-readable, externally-known visit or encounter number assigned by the source EHR system (e.g., Epic CSN — Contact Serial Number, or Cerner FIN — Financial Identification Number). Used in billing, claims, and patient communications.",
encounter,patient_visit,visit,expected_los_days,expected_los_days,Expected Length of Stay (LOS) in Days,"DECIMAL(6,2)",,,,,master_data,"DRG-based or risk-adjusted expected length of stay for this encounter, used to benchmark actual LOS against peer performance and identify outlier cases for CDI and utilization management review.",
encounter,patient_visit,visit,financial_class,financial_class,Financial Class,STRING,,,,commercial|medicare|medicaid|self_pay|workers_comp,master_data,"Payer category assigned at the time of visit registration, used to route the encounter through the appropriate revenue cycle workflow. Drives charge capture, claim form selection (UB-04 vs CMS-1500), and reimbursement expectations. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: commercial|medicare|medicaid|self_pay|workers_comp|tricare|charity|other_government — promote to reference product]",
encounter,patient_visit,visit,follow_up_scheduled,follow_up_scheduled,Follow-Up Appointment Scheduled Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,"Indicates whether a follow-up appointment was scheduled prior to or at the time of discharge. Used for care transition quality metrics, readmission prevention programs, and HEDIS measure compliance.",
encounter,patient_visit,visit,inpatient_conversion_timestamp,inpatient_conversion_timestamp,Inpatient Conversion Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,master_data,"Date and time an observation status encounter was formally converted to inpatient admission. Used for LOS recalculation, billing reclassification, and two-midnight rule compliance documentation.",
encounter,patient_visit,visit,length_of_stay_days,length_of_stay_days,Length of Stay (LOS) in Days,INT,,,,,master_data,"Total number of inpatient days from admission to discharge, calculated as discharge date minus admission date. Key operational and financial metric used for ALOS benchmarking, CMI analysis, and VBP performance.",
encounter,patient_visit,visit,moon_delivered_timestamp,moon_delivered_timestamp,Medicare Outpatient Observation Notice (MOON) Delivery Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,master_data,"Date and time the Medicare Outpatient Observation Notice (MOON) was delivered to the patient, as required by the NOTICE Act for Medicare beneficiaries receiving observation services exceeding 24 hours.",
encounter,patient_visit,visit,mrn,mrn,Medical Record Number (MRN),STRING,,,"dbx_pii_identifier,dbx_restricted,pii_phi,pii_pii,pii_sensitive",,master_data,"pii_phi,pii_pii,pii_sensitive",
encounter,patient_visit,visit,observation_hours,observation_hours,Total Observation Hours,"DECIMAL(6,2)",,,,,master_data,"Total number of hours the patient spent under outpatient observation status during this visit. Used for two-midnight rule compliance assessment, MOON trigger evaluation, and Medicare billing.",
encounter,patient_visit,visit,observation_status,observation_status,Observation Status Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,"Indicates whether the patient is classified under outpatient observation status rather than formal inpatient admission. Drives MOON delivery requirement, two-midnight rule assessment, and Medicare Part A vs Part B billing determination.",
encounter,patient_visit,visit,point_of_service_code,point_of_service_code,Place of Service (POS) Code,STRING,,,,,master_data,CMS two-digit Place of Service code indicating the setting where the professional service was rendered. Required on CMS-1500 professional claims for correct reimbursement routing.,
encounter,patient_visit,visit,principal_icd10_diagnosis_code,principal_icd10_diagnosis_code,Principal ICD-10 Diagnosis Code,STRING,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_health","^[A-Z][0-9A-Z]{1,6}(.[0-9A-Z]{1,4})?$",master_data,"ICD-10-CM code for the principal diagnosis — the condition established after study to be chiefly responsible for the admission. Required for DRG grouping, claims submission, and quality reporting.",
encounter,patient_visit,visit,readmission_flag,readmission_flag,Readmission Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,Indicates whether this visit is classified as an unplanned readmission within 30 days of a prior discharge. Used for CMS Hospital Readmissions Reduction Program (HRRP) reporting and VBP performance measurement.,
encounter,patient_visit,visit,readmission_risk_score,readmission_risk_score,Readmission Risk Score,"DECIMAL(5,2)",,,,,master_data,"Numeric risk score (e.g., LACE, HOSPITAL score) predicting the probability of unplanned 30-day readmission. Used by care management teams to prioritize post-discharge follow-up and care transition interventions.",
encounter,patient_visit,visit,source_encounter_code,source_encounter_code,Source System Encounter ID,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Native encounter identifier from the originating EHR system (e.g., Epic CSN, Cerner Encounter ID). Preserved for cross-system reconciliation, HIE interoperability, and FHIR API mapping.",
encounter,patient_visit,visit,source_system,source_system,Source System,STRING,,,,Epic|Cerner|MEDITECH|Allscripts|Other,master_data,"Identifies the operational EHR or source system from which this visit record was extracted (e.g., Epic, Cerner Millennium, MEDITECH Expanse). Required for data lineage, multi-system reconciliation, and ETL audit.",
encounter,patient_visit,visit,telehealth_connection_quality,telehealth_connection_quality,Telehealth Connection Quality,STRING,,,,excellent|good|fair|poor|failed,master_data,"Assessed quality of the audio/video connection during a telehealth visit. Used for patient experience reporting, platform SLA monitoring, and identifying visits that may require follow-up due to technical issues.",
encounter,patient_visit,visit,telehealth_platform,telehealth_platform,Telehealth Platform,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Name of the telehealth technology platform used to conduct the virtual visit (e.g., Epic MyChart Video, Zoom for Healthcare, Teladoc). Required for telehealth billing modifier application and platform performance reporting.",
encounter,patient_visit,visit,two_midnight_compliant,two_midnight_compliant,Two-Midnight Rule Compliance Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,"Indicates whether the inpatient admission meets CMS two-midnight rule criteria, requiring the admitting physician to expect the patient to require hospital care spanning at least two midnights. Critical for Medicare inpatient billing compliance and RAC audit defense.",
encounter,patient_visit,visit,updated_timestamp,updated_timestamp,Record Last Updated Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,master_data,"Date and time the visit record was most recently modified in the source EHR system or the lakehouse silver layer. Used for incremental ETL processing, change data capture, and audit compliance.",
encounter,patient_visit,visit,visit_status,visit_status,Visit Status,STRING,,,,scheduled|arrived|in_progress|discharged|cancelled|no_show,master_data,"Current lifecycle state of the visit from scheduling through discharge. Drives ADT event processing, bed management, and revenue cycle workflows in Epic ADT and Cerner PowerChart.",
encounter,patient_visit,visit,visit_type,visit_type,Visit Type,STRING,,,,inpatient|outpatient|emergency|observation|telehealth|ambulatory,master_data,"Classification of the patient-provider interaction by care setting and service modality. Drives billing rules, regulatory requirements, and clinical workflow routing. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: inpatient|outpatient|emergency|observation|telehealth|ambulatory|surgical|preventive — promote to reference product]",
encounter,patient_visit,visit_provider,visit_provider_id,visit_provider_id,Visit Provider ID,BIGINT,Y,,,,association_data,Unique surrogate identifier for each visit-provider association record in the Silver layer lakehouse. Primary key for this junction entity linking a provider to a specific patient visit with a defined role.,
encounter,patient_visit,visit_provider,cost_center_id,cost_center_id,Cost Center Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,finance.cost_center.cost_center_id,,,association_data,"Foreign key linking to finance.cost_center. Business justification: Provider assignments drive RVU-based compensation and cost allocation models. Linking to cost centers enables provider productivity analysis, departmental expense tracking, and physician compensation ",
encounter,patient_visit,visit_provider,employee_id,employee_id,Supervising Nurse Employee Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,workforce.employee.employee_id,"dbx_confidential, dbx_pii",,association_data,"Foreign key linking to workforce.employee. Business justification: Advanced practice providers (NPs, PAs) require documented nurse supervision in many states and for credentialing. Tracks supervisory relationships for compliance, privileging, and malpractice coverage",
encounter,patient_visit,visit_provider,insurance_network_participation_id,insurance_network_participation_id,Network Participation Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,insurance.insurance_network_participation.insurance_network_participation_id,,,association_data,"Foreign key linking to insurance.network_participation. Business justification: Determines in-network vs out-of-network status for each provider on a visit, directly impacting reimbursement rates and patient cost-sharing. Critical for claims processing, payment accuracy, and pati",
encounter,patient_visit,visit_provider,network_affiliation_id,network_affiliation_id,Network Affiliation Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,provider.network_affiliation.network_affiliation_id,,,association_data,"Foreign key linking to provider.network_affiliation. Business justification: Links provider assignment to specific network participation record for the visits payer. Essential for determining in-network vs out-of-network status, calculating patient cost-sharing, and supportin",
encounter,patient_visit,visit_provider,payer_id,payer_id,Payer ID,BIGINT,,insurance.payer.payer_id,,,association_data,"Reference to the primary payer (insurance plan) associated with this visit at the time of provider assignment. Used for payer-specific provider network validation, credentialing verification, and RCM (Revenue Cycle Management) analytics.",
encounter,patient_visit,visit_provider,primary_visit_clinician_id,primary_visit_clinician_id,Provider ID,BIGINT,,provider.clinician.clinician_id,,,association_data,Reference to the clinician or provider record assigned to this visit. Links to the provider domain clinician master record.,
encounter,patient_visit,visit_provider,provider_payer_enrollment_id,provider_payer_enrollment_id,Payer Enrollment Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,provider.provider_payer_enrollment.provider_payer_enrollment_id,,,association_data,"Foreign key linking to provider.payer_enrollment. Business justification: Validates that the assigned clinician is enrolled with the patients payer at time of service. Critical for billing compliance, claims adjudication, and preventing denials due to provider enrollment g",
encounter,patient_visit,visit_provider,referral_order_id,referral_order_id,Consult Request ID,BIGINT,,order.referral_order.referral_order_id,,,association_data,Reference to the formal consultation order or request that triggered this providers assignment to the visit. Applicable when assignment_type is consult_request. Links to the order management domain.,
encounter,patient_visit,visit_provider,stark_arrangement_id,stark_arrangement_id,Stark Arrangement Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,compliance.stark_arrangement.stark_arrangement_id,,,association_data,Foreign key linking to compliance.stark_arrangement. Business justification: Stark Law compliance monitoring requires tracking which physicians provided designated health services under which financial arrangements. Referral volume tracking and FMV validation depend on linking,
encounter,patient_visit,visit_provider,tertiary_visit_supervising_provider_clinician_id,tertiary_visit_supervising_provider_clinician_id,Supervising Provider ID,BIGINT,,provider.clinician.clinician_id,,,association_data,"Reference to the supervising or attending physician responsible for overseeing this providers participation in the visit. Required for resident, student, and mid-level provider assignments per CMS teaching physician billing guidelines.",
encounter,patient_visit,visit_provider,visit_id,visit_id,Visit ID,BIGINT,,encounter.visit.visit_id,,,association_data,"Reference to the patient visit or encounter to which this provider is assigned. Links to the encounter domain visit record representing the ADT (Admit, Discharge, Transfer) event.",
encounter,patient_visit,visit_provider,admission_source_role,admission_source_role,Admission Source Role,STRING,,,,admitting|referring|transferring|none,association_data,"Indicates whether this provider served as the admitting, referring, or transferring physician at the time of patient admission. Relevant for ADT (Admit, Discharge, Transfer) event documentation and CMS admission source reporting.",
encounter,patient_visit,visit_provider,billing_provider_npi,billing_provider_npi,Billing Provider National Provider Identifier (NPI),STRING,,,,^[0-9]{10}$,association_data,The NPI (National Provider Identifier) used specifically for billing and claims submission for services rendered by this provider during this visit. May differ from the rendering provider NPI when billing under a group practice or supervising physician.,
encounter,patient_visit,visit_provider,care_setting,care_setting,Care Setting,STRING,,,,,association_data,"The clinical care setting in which the provider is participating for this visit (e.g., inpatient, outpatient, ED (Emergency Department), observation, telehealth, surgical, ICU (Intensive Care Unit)). Supports care setting-specific analytics and regulatory reporting. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: inpatient|outpatient|ed|observation|telehealth|surgical|icu — 7 candidates stripped; promote to reference product]",
encounter,patient_visit,visit_provider,care_team_sequence,care_team_sequence,Care Team Sequence,INT,,,,,association_data,Ordinal sequence number indicating the order in which this provider was added to the visit care team. Used to reconstruct care team composition history and identify primary vs. secondary team members in chronological order.,
encounter,patient_visit,visit_provider,comments,comments,Assignment Comments,STRING,,,,,association_data,"Free-text comments or notes entered by clinical staff regarding this providers assignment to the visit. May include coverage rationale, special instructions, or handoff context not captured in structured fields.",
encounter,patient_visit,visit_provider,cosignature_required,cosignature_required,Co-Signature Required Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,association_data,"Indicates whether the providers clinical documentation for this visit requires co-signature by a supervising physician (e.g., resident or student notes requiring attending co-signature). Supports CDI (Clinical Documentation Improvement) workflow and compliance.",
encounter,patient_visit,visit_provider,created_timestamp,created_timestamp,Record Created Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,association_data,"Date and time when this visit-provider association record was first created in the data platform. Supports audit trail, data lineage, and compliance with HIPAA record retention requirements.",
encounter,patient_visit,visit_provider,credentialing_verified_flag,credentialing_verified_flag,Credentialing Verified Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,association_data,Indicates whether the providers credentials and privileges were verified as current and active at the time of this visit assignment. Supports Joint Commission credentialing compliance and risk management.,
encounter,patient_visit,visit_provider,drg_attribution_flag,drg_attribution_flag,Diagnosis-Related Group (DRG) Attribution Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,association_data,Indicates whether this providers assignment is attributed to the DRG (Diagnosis-Related Group) assignment for inpatient billing purposes. The attending of records DRG attribution drives inpatient reimbursement under CMS IPPS.,
encounter,patient_visit,visit_provider,effective_date,effective_date,Effective Date,DATE,,,,,association_data,"Calendar date on which this provider assignment became effective for the visit. Used for date-level scheduling, staffing reports, and daily census attribution distinct from the precise assignment_start_timestamp.",
encounter,patient_visit,visit_provider,handoff_reference,handoff_reference,Handoff Documentation Reference,STRING,,,,,association_data,"Reference identifier or note key pointing to the handoff documentation record created when this provider transferred care responsibility to another provider. Supports care continuity, patient safety, and Joint Commission handoff communication standards.",
encounter,patient_visit,visit_provider,is_attending_of_record,is_attending_of_record,Attending of Record Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,association_data,Indicates whether this provider is designated as the attending physician of record for the visit. The attending of record bears overall clinical and legal responsibility for the patients care and is reported on all billing claims.,
encounter,patient_visit,visit_provider,is_primary_provider,is_primary_provider,Primary Provider Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,association_data,"Indicates whether this provider holds primary clinical and billing responsibility for the visit. Only one provider per visit should have this flag set to True. Drives attending physician attribution on claims, UB-04, and CMS-1500 forms.",
encounter,patient_visit,visit_provider,locum_tenens_flag,locum_tenens_flag,Locum Tenens Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,association_data,Indicates whether the provider is serving in a locum tenens (temporary substitute) capacity for this visit. Locum tenens billing has specific CMS rules requiring the Q6 modifier on claims.,
encounter,patient_visit,visit_provider,mips_eligible_flag,mips_eligible_flag,Merit-based Incentive Payment System (MIPS) Eligible Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,association_data,Indicates whether this providers participation in this visit is eligible for MIPS (Merit-based Incentive Payment System) performance measurement under MACRA (Medicare Access and CHIP Reauthorization Act). Drives quality measure attribution.,
encounter,patient_visit,visit_provider,note_count,note_count,Clinical Note Count,INT,,,,,association_data,Number of clinical notes authored or co-signed by this provider for this visit. Supports CDI (Clinical Documentation Improvement) completeness tracking and provider documentation compliance reporting.,
encounter,patient_visit,visit_provider,npi,npi,National Provider Identifier (NPI),STRING,,,,^[0-9]{10}$,association_data,"The 10-digit National Provider Identifier (NPI) of the assigned provider as issued by CMS. Captured at time of assignment to support billing, claims adjudication, and RVU (Relative Value Unit) attribution independent of provider master record changes.",
encounter,patient_visit,visit_provider,on_call_flag,on_call_flag,On-Call Assignment Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,association_data,Indicates whether this provider was assigned to the visit as part of an on-call coverage rotation rather than a scheduled or direct assignment. Supports on-call scheduling analytics and EMTALA (Emergency Medical Treatment and Labor Act) compliance tracking.,
encounter,patient_visit,visit_provider,order_count,order_count,Order Count,INT,,,,,association_data,"Number of clinical orders (lab, radiology, pharmacy, procedures) placed by this provider via CPOE (Computerized Physician Order Entry) for this visit. Supports provider ordering pattern analytics and CPOE adoption reporting.",
encounter,patient_visit,visit_provider,participation_duration_minutes,participation_duration_minutes,Provider Participation Duration (Minutes),INT,,,,,association_data,"Total number of minutes the provider was actively engaged in this visit, calculated from assignment_start_timestamp to assignment_end_timestamp. Used for time-based billing (e.g., anesthesia, critical care), provider productivity reporting, and staffing analytics.",
encounter,patient_visit,visit_provider,place_of_service_code,place_of_service_code,Place of Service (POS) Code,STRING,,,,^[0-9]{2}$,association_data,"Two-digit CMS Place of Service (POS) code indicating the setting where the provider rendered services during this visit (e.g., 11=Office, 21=Inpatient Hospital, 23=Emergency Room, 02=Telehealth). Required on CMS-1500 professional claims.",
encounter,patient_visit,visit_provider,privilege_type,privilege_type,Clinical Privilege Type,STRING,,,,full|provisional|temporary|locum_tenens|telemedicine,association_data,"The type of clinical privileges held by the provider at the facility for this visit assignment (e.g., full, provisional, temporary, locum tenens, telemedicine). Determines scope of permissible clinical activities.",
encounter,patient_visit,visit_provider,provider_assignment_end_timestamp,provider_assignment_end_timestamp,Provider Assignment End Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,association_data,"Date and time when the providers active participation in this visit ended. Null if the provider is still actively assigned. Used for LOS (Length of Stay) attribution, handoff documentation, and coverage gap analysis.",
encounter,patient_visit,visit_provider,provider_assignment_start_timestamp,provider_assignment_start_timestamp,Provider Assignment Start Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,association_data,"Date and time when the providers active participation in this visit began. Used for time-bounded care team tracking, shift coverage analysis, and provider performance analytics per encounter.",
encounter,patient_visit,visit_provider,provider_assignment_status,provider_assignment_status,Provider Assignment Status,STRING,,,,active|inactive|pending|cancelled|transferred,association_data,Current lifecycle status of the providers assignment to this visit. active indicates current participation; transferred indicates a handoff to another provider has occurred; cancelled indicates the assignment was voided.,
encounter,patient_visit,visit_provider,provider_assignment_type,provider_assignment_type,Provider Assignment Type,STRING,,,,scheduled|unscheduled|emergency|coverage|consult_request,association_data,"Indicates how the provider came to be assigned to this visit — whether through scheduled care, unscheduled walk-in, emergency response, on-call coverage, or formal consult request. Supports operational staffing and care coordination analytics.",
encounter,patient_visit,visit_provider,provider_role,provider_role,Provider Role,STRING,,,,,association_data,"Clinical role of the provider for this specific visit assignment (e.g., attending, consulting, admitting, covering, resident, hospitalist, surgeon, anesthesiologist, PCP). Determines care team hierarchy, billing responsibility, and RVU attribution. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: attending|consulting|admitting|covering|resident|hospitalist|surgeon|anesthesiologist|pcp|co_surgeon|scrub_tech|circulating_nurse|care_coordinator — promote to reference product]",
encounter,patient_visit,visit_provider,provider_type,provider_type,Provider Type,STRING,,,,,association_data,"Classification of the providers credential type for this assignment (e.g., physician, NP (Nurse Practitioner), PA (Physician Assistant), resident, fellow, student, RN, CRNA). Determines billing rules, supervision requirements, and scope of practice. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: physician|np|pa|resident|fellow|student|rn|crna|other — 9 candidates stripped; promote to reference product]",
encounter,patient_visit,visit_provider,rendering_provider_npi,rendering_provider_npi,Rendering Provider National Provider Identifier (NPI),STRING,,,,^[0-9]{10}$,association_data,The NPI (National Provider Identifier) of the individual clinician who actually rendered the service during this visit. Distinct from billing_provider_npi when services are billed under a group or supervising provider.,
encounter,patient_visit,visit_provider,rvu_credit_flag,rvu_credit_flag,Relative Value Unit (RVU) Credit Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,association_data,"Indicates whether this provider assignment is eligible to receive RVU (Relative Value Unit) credit for services rendered during this visit. Used in provider productivity reporting, compensation modeling, and MIPS (Merit-based Incentive Payment System) performance tracking.",
encounter,patient_visit,visit_provider,rvu_work_units,rvu_work_units,Relative Value Unit (RVU) Work Units,"DECIMAL(10,4)",,,,,association_data,The physician work RVU (wRVU) value attributed to this provider for services rendered during this visit assignment. Sourced from CMS RBRVS fee schedule and used for provider productivity measurement and compensation calculations.,
encounter,patient_visit,visit_provider,source_system,source_system,Source System,STRING,,,,epic_clindoc|cerner_powerchart|meditech|manual|other,association_data,"Identifies the operational system of record from which this provider assignment record was sourced (e.g., Epic ClinDoc, Cerner PowerChart, MEDITECH). Supports data lineage, ETL (Extract, Transform, Load) audit, and reconciliation.",
encounter,patient_visit,visit_provider,source_system_record_code,source_system_record_code,Source System Record ID,STRING,,,,,association_data,"The native identifier of this provider assignment record in the originating operational system (e.g., Epic ClinDoc provider assignment ID, Cerner care team member ID). Enables traceability back to the system of record for reconciliation and audit.",
encounter,patient_visit,visit_provider,specialty_at_assignment,specialty_at_assignment,Provider Specialty at Assignment,STRING,,,,,association_data,"The clinical specialty of the provider at the time of this visit assignment, captured as a point-in-time snapshot. Supports specialty-based care team analytics and quality reporting independent of provider master record updates.",
encounter,patient_visit,visit_provider,telehealth_flag,telehealth_flag,Telehealth Encounter Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,association_data,"Indicates whether the providers participation in this visit was conducted via telehealth modality. Affects billing modifier requirements, place of service codes, and state telehealth licensure compliance.",
encounter,patient_visit,visit_provider,updated_timestamp,updated_timestamp,Record Updated Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,association_data,"Date and time when this visit-provider association record was last modified in the data platform. Supports change tracking, SCD (Slowly Changing Dimension) processing, and audit compliance.",
encounter,patient_visit,visit_status_history,visit_status_history_id,visit_status_history_id,Visit Status History ID,BIGINT,Y,,,,transactional_data,Unique surrogate identifier for each visit status history record. Primary key for the visit_status_history data product in the encounter domain.,
encounter,patient_visit,visit_status_history,bed_id,bed_id,Bed ID,BIGINT,,facility.bed.bed_id,,,transactional_data,"Reference to the specific bed assigned to the patient at the time of this status change. Supports bed management, occupancy tracking, and throughput analysis.",
encounter,patient_visit,visit_status_history,clinician_id,clinician_id,Attending Provider ID,BIGINT,,provider.clinician.clinician_id,,,transactional_data,Reference to the attending physician responsible for the patient at the time of this status change. Supports provider-level throughput and LOS analysis.,
encounter,patient_visit,visit_status_history,demographics_id,demographics_id,Patient ID,BIGINT,,patient.demographics.demographics_id,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_identifier",,transactional_data,Reference to the patient associated with the visit. Enables patient-level throughput and LOS milestone analysis without requiring a join to the visit table.,
encounter,patient_visit,visit_status_history,employee_id,employee_id,Changed By User ID,BIGINT,,workforce.employee.employee_id,"dbx_confidential, dbx_pii",,transactional_data,"Reference to the system user (clinician, registrar, or automated process) who initiated or recorded the status change. Used for workflow auditing and accountability tracking.",
encounter,patient_visit,visit_status_history,message_log_id,message_log_id,HL7 Message Control ID,BIGINT,,interoperability.message_log.message_log_id,,,transactional_data,The HL7 message control ID (MSH-10) from the ADT message that triggered this status change. Enables traceability back to the originating HL7 ADT message for interface troubleshooting and audit.,
encounter,patient_visit,visit_status_history,org_unit_id,org_unit_id,Department ID,BIGINT,,workforce.org_unit.org_unit_id,,,transactional_data,"Reference to the clinical department or unit associated with this status change event (e.g., ED, ICU, Med-Surg). Supports department-level throughput and capacity analysis.",
encounter,patient_visit,visit_status_history,primary_visit_care_site_id,primary_visit_care_site_id,Facility ID,BIGINT,,facility.care_site.care_site_id,,,transactional_data,Reference to the facility or hospital where the visit status change occurred. Enables multi-facility throughput comparison and operational reporting.,
encounter,patient_visit,visit_status_history,visit_id,visit_id,Visit ID,BIGINT,,encounter.visit.visit_id,,,transactional_data,Reference to the parent visit/encounter record for which this status change event is recorded. Links the status history to the core encounter.,
encounter,patient_visit,visit_status_history,admission_source_code,admission_source_code,Admission Source Code,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Standardized code indicating the source from which the patient was admitted at the time of an admission status event (e.g., emergency room, physician referral, transfer from another facility). Relevant for admit-type status transitions. Aligns with UB-04 FL-15.",
encounter,patient_visit,visit_status_history,adt_event_reason_code,adt_event_reason_code,Admit Discharge Transfer (ADT) Event Reason Code,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Coded reason for the ADT event or status change as defined by the source system or HL7 standard (e.g., elective admission, emergency, transfer for higher level of care). Supports root-cause analysis of status transitions.",
encounter,patient_visit,visit_status_history,adt_event_type,adt_event_type,Admit Discharge Transfer (ADT) Event Type,STRING,,,,A01|A02|A03|A04|A05|A06,transactional_data,"HL7 ADT event type code that triggered this status change (e.g., A01=Admit, A02=Transfer, A03=Discharge, A04=Register Outpatient, A05=Pre-Admit, A06=Change Outpatient to Inpatient). Enables HL7-aligned event classification. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: A01|A02|A03|A04|A05|A06|A07|A08|A09|A10|A11|A12|A13|A21|A22|A38|A40 — promote to reference product]",
encounter,patient_visit,visit_status_history,care_setting,care_setting,Care Setting,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Physical or virtual care setting where the patient was located at the time of this status change (e.g., ED, ICU, OR, inpatient unit, outpatient clinic, observation unit, telehealth). Supports care setting transition analysis. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: ED|ICU|OR|inpatient_unit|outpatient_clinic|observation_unit|telehealth — 7 candidates stripped; promote to reference product]",
encounter,patient_visit,visit_status_history,changed_by_role,changed_by_role,Changed By User Role,STRING,,,,physician|nurse|registrar|care_coordinator|system|other,transactional_data,"Functional role of the user who performed the status change (e.g., physician, nurse, registrar, care coordinator, system). Enables role-based throughput and workflow analysis.",
encounter,patient_visit,visit_status_history,changed_by_user_name,changed_by_user_name,Changed By User Name,STRING,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_identifier",,transactional_data,Display name of the user who initiated the status change. Carried on the record to support audit reporting without requiring a join to the user directory.,
encounter,patient_visit,visit_status_history,created_timestamp,created_timestamp,Record Created Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,Timestamp when this visit status history record was first created in the data platform. Distinct from status_change_timestamp which reflects the real-world event time. Used for audit trail and ETL lineage.,
encounter,patient_visit,visit_status_history,department_name,department_name,Department Name,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,Name of the clinical department or unit at the time of the status change. Carried on the record to support reporting without requiring a join to the department reference table.,
encounter,patient_visit,visit_status_history,discharge_disposition_code,discharge_disposition_code,Discharge Disposition Code,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Standardized code indicating the patients disposition at the time of a discharge status event (e.g., home, skilled nursing facility, expired, AMA). Aligns with UB-04 FL-17 and CMS discharge disposition codes. Relevant for discharge-type status transitions.",
encounter,patient_visit,visit_status_history,duration_in_status_minutes,duration_in_status_minutes,Duration in Status (Minutes),INT,,,,,transactional_data,Number of minutes the visit remained in the previous status before transitioning to the new status. Calculated at ingestion time from consecutive status_change_timestamps. Supports LOS milestone tracking and throughput bottleneck analysis.,
encounter,patient_visit,visit_status_history,effective_date,effective_date,Effective Date,DATE,,,,,transactional_data,"Calendar date on which the status change became effective. Derived from status_change_timestamp for date-level partitioning, daily census reporting, and operational dashboards.",
encounter,patient_visit,visit_status_history,encounter_number,encounter_number,Encounter Number,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Human-readable, externally visible encounter or visit number assigned by the source system (e.g., Epic CSN or Cerner FIN). Used for cross-system reconciliation and operational reporting.",
encounter,patient_visit,visit_status_history,financial_class,financial_class,Financial Class,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Financial class or payer category of the visit at the time of this status change (e.g., Medicare, Medicaid, Commercial, Self-Pay). Supports payer-stratified throughput and LOS analysis.",
encounter,patient_visit,visit_status_history,is_corrected,is_corrected,Is Corrected Record Indicator,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,Indicates whether this status history record is a correction of a previously entered status change. True if this record supersedes an erroneous prior entry. Supports data quality auditing and HIM correction workflows.,
encounter,patient_visit,visit_status_history,is_current_status,is_current_status,Is Current Status Indicator,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,Indicates whether this record represents the most recent (current) status of the visit. True for the latest status record; False for all prior status records. Enables efficient current-state queries without window functions.,
encounter,patient_visit,visit_status_history,is_system_generated,is_system_generated,Is System Generated Indicator,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,"Indicates whether this status change was automatically generated by the source system (e.g., automated bed assignment, scheduled discharge trigger) rather than manually entered by a user. Supports audit quality and workflow automation analysis.",
encounter,patient_visit,visit_status_history,los_at_event_hours,los_at_event_hours,Length of Stay at Event (Hours),"DECIMAL(10,2)",,,,,transactional_data,Cumulative length of stay in hours from the initial admission or arrival timestamp to the time of this status change event. Supports LOS milestone tracking and throughput benchmarking at each status transition point.,
encounter,patient_visit,visit_status_history,mrn,mrn,Medical Record Number (MRN),STRING,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_identifier",,transactional_data,Medical Record Number assigned to the patient by the facility. Carried on the status history record to support operational auditing and patient-level throughput reporting without requiring upstream joins.,
encounter,patient_visit,visit_status_history,new_status,new_status,New Visit Status,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,The visit status assigned as a result of this status change event. Represents the current state of the visit at the time of this record. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: scheduled|pre-registered|arrived|admitted|in-progress|observation|transferred|discharged|cancelled|no-show|left-without-being-seen — promote to reference product],
encounter,patient_visit,visit_status_history,notes,notes,Status Change Notes,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Free-text notes or comments entered by the user at the time of the status change. May include clinical context, operational instructions, or escalation notes. Supports workflow auditing and care coordination.",
encounter,patient_visit,visit_status_history,previous_status,previous_status,Previous Visit Status,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,The visit status immediately before this status change event occurred. Null for the initial status record. Used to reconstruct the full status transition chain. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: scheduled|pre-registered|arrived|admitted|in-progress|observation|transferred|discharged|cancelled|no-show|left-without-being-seen — promote to reference product],
encounter,patient_visit,visit_status_history,room_number,room_number,Room Number,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Room number assigned to the patient at the time of this status change. Relevant for bed assignment, transfer, and discharge events. Supports bed management and capacity planning.",
encounter,patient_visit,visit_status_history,sequence_number,sequence_number,Status Sequence Number,INT,,,,,transactional_data,"Ordinal sequence number of this status change event within the visit lifecycle, starting at 1. Enables chronological ordering of status transitions for a given visit without relying solely on timestamps.",
encounter,patient_visit,visit_status_history,source_system,source_system,Source System,STRING,,,,Epic|Cerner|MEDITECH|manual|interface,transactional_data,"Identifies the operational system of record that originated this status change event (e.g., Epic ADT, Cerner Millennium ADT, MEDITECH Expanse, manual entry, HL7 interface). Supports data lineage and reconciliation.",
encounter,patient_visit,visit_status_history,source_system_event_code,source_system_event_code,Source System Event ID,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"The native event or transaction identifier from the originating source system (e.g., Epic ADT event ID, Cerner Millennium event ID). Used for cross-system reconciliation, deduplication, and ETL lineage tracking.",
encounter,patient_visit,visit_status_history,status_change_reason,status_change_reason,Status Change Reason,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Free-text or coded narrative reason entered by the user or system explaining why the visit status was changed (e.g., Patient arrived at ED triage, Bed assigned in ICU, Patient left without being seen). Supports operational workflow auditing.",
encounter,patient_visit,visit_status_history,status_change_timestamp,status_change_timestamp,Status Change Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,"The precise date and time when the visit status transition occurred. Principal event timestamp for this record. Used for LOS milestone tracking, throughput analysis, and ADT event sequencing.",
encounter,patient_visit,visit_status_history,updated_timestamp,updated_timestamp,Record Updated Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,"Timestamp when this visit status history record was last modified in the data platform. Used for incremental ETL processing, change detection, and audit trail maintenance.",
