facility,equipment_maintenance,maintenance_order,maintenance_employee_id,maintenance_employee_id,Assigned Technician Identifier (ID),BIGINT,,workforce.employee.employee_id,"dbx_confidential, dbx_pii",,transactional_data,Reference to the facilities or biomedical engineering technician assigned to execute this maintenance work order. Links to workforce/employee master data.,
facility,equipment_maintenance,maintenance_order,pm_schedule_id,pm_schedule_id,Preventive Maintenance (PM) Schedule Identifier (ID),BIGINT,,facility.pm_schedule.pm_schedule_id,,,transactional_data,"Reference to the preventive maintenance schedule definition that generated this work order. Null for corrective, emergency, or ad-hoc work orders. Links to the PM schedule template for compliance tracking.",
facility,equipment_maintenance,maintenance_order,tertiary_employee_id,tertiary_employee_id,Approved By Identifier (ID),BIGINT,,workforce.employee.employee_id,"dbx_confidential, dbx_pii",,transactional_data,Reference to the manager or approver who authorized the maintenance work order. Null if no approval was required or if work order is pending approval.,
facility,equipment_maintenance,maintenance_order,vendor_id,vendor_id,Vendor Identifier (ID),BIGINT,,supply.vendor.vendor_id,,,transactional_data,Reference to the external vendor or contractor who performed the maintenance work. Null for work performed by internal staff. Links to vendor master data.,
facility,equipment_maintenance,maintenance_order,actual_completion_datetime,actual_completion_datetime,Actual Completion Date and Time,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,Actual date and time when the maintenance work was completed and the asset or location was returned to service. Used for calculating actual labor duration and PM compliance rates.,
facility,equipment_maintenance,maintenance_order,actual_start_datetime,actual_start_datetime,Actual Start Date and Time,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,Actual date and time when the technician began work on the maintenance order. Captured by technician check-in or mobile work order system.,
facility,equipment_maintenance,maintenance_order,approval_datetime,approval_datetime,Approval Date and Time,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,Date and time when the maintenance work order was approved. Used for tracking approval cycle time and work order lifecycle metrics.,
facility,equipment_maintenance,maintenance_order,approval_required_flag,approval_required_flag,Approval Required Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,Indicates whether this maintenance work order requires management or budget approval before work can commence. Typically true for high-cost repairs or capital improvements.,
facility,equipment_maintenance,maintenance_order,completion_notes,completion_notes,Completion Notes,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Detailed narrative notes entered by the technician upon work order completion, documenting work performed, parts replaced, findings, and any follow-up recommendations.",
facility,equipment_maintenance,maintenance_order,created_timestamp,created_timestamp,Record Created Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,System timestamp when this maintenance order record was first created in the data platform. Used for data lineage and audit trail purposes.,
facility,equipment_maintenance,maintenance_order,downtime_minutes,downtime_minutes,Equipment Downtime Minutes,INT,,,,,transactional_data,Total duration in minutes that the asset or location was out of service due to this maintenance activity. Used for calculating equipment availability and operational impact metrics.,
facility,equipment_maintenance,maintenance_order,failure_code,failure_code,Equipment Failure Code,STRING,,,,"^[A-Z0-9]{2,10}$",transactional_data,"Standardized code classifying the type of equipment failure or maintenance issue. Used for failure mode analysis, trend reporting, and root cause analysis. Follows facility-specific or manufacturer failure taxonomy.",
facility,equipment_maintenance,maintenance_order,labor_cost,labor_cost,Labor Cost,"DECIMAL(12,2)",,,,,transactional_data,"Total labor cost for the maintenance work order, calculated from labor hours and technician hourly rates. Used for total cost of ownership analysis and budget tracking.",
facility,equipment_maintenance,maintenance_order,labor_hours,labor_hours,Labor Hours,"DECIMAL(8,2)",,,,,transactional_data,"Total labor hours expended by technicians to complete the maintenance work order. Used for cost calculation, productivity analysis, and PM schedule estimation.",
facility,equipment_maintenance,maintenance_order,order_status,order_status,Maintenance Order Status,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Current lifecycle status of the maintenance work order. Tracks progression from creation through assignment, execution, completion, and closure. On-hold indicates temporary suspension pending parts or access. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: created|assigned|in_progress|on_hold|completed|cancelled|closed — 7 candidates stripped; promote to reference product]",
facility,equipment_maintenance,maintenance_order,order_type,order_type,Maintenance Order Type,STRING,,,,preventive|corrective|emergency|inspection|recall,transactional_data,"Classification of the maintenance work order by its purpose: preventive (scheduled routine maintenance), corrective (repair of identified failure), emergency (urgent unplanned repair), inspection (regulatory or safety inspection), or recall (manufacturer-driven equipment recall).",
facility,equipment_maintenance,maintenance_order,parts_cost,parts_cost,Parts Cost,"DECIMAL(12,2)",,,,,transactional_data,"Total cost of parts, materials, and consumables used in the maintenance work order. Aggregated from parts consumption records linked to this work order.",
facility,equipment_maintenance,maintenance_order,priority_level,priority_level,Maintenance Priority Level,STRING,,,,critical|urgent|routine|scheduled,transactional_data,Business priority classification indicating the urgency and criticality of the maintenance work order. Critical indicates immediate patient safety or facility operations impact; urgent requires same-day response; routine is standard priority; scheduled is planned preventive maintenance.,
facility,equipment_maintenance,maintenance_order,problem_description,problem_description,Problem Description,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"pii_phi,pii_pii,pii_sensitive",
facility,equipment_maintenance,maintenance_order,purchase_order_number,purchase_order_number,Purchase Order (PO) Number,STRING,,,,"^[A-Z0-9]{8,20}$",transactional_data,Purchase order number associated with vendor-performed maintenance work or parts procurement for this work order. Used for financial reconciliation and vendor payment processing.,
facility,equipment_maintenance,maintenance_order,regulatory_driver,regulatory_driver,Regulatory Driver,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Identification of the regulatory requirement, accreditation standard, or compliance framework that mandates this maintenance activity. Examples include TJC EC.02.04.01 (environment of care), CMS conditions of participation, NFPA 99 (healthcare facilities code), NFPA 101 (life safety code), or state department of health regulations.",
facility,equipment_maintenance,maintenance_order,request_datetime,request_datetime,Request Date and Time,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,Date and time when the maintenance work order was originally requested or created in the system. Used for calculating response time and work order aging metrics.,
facility,equipment_maintenance,maintenance_order,risk_assessment_score,risk_assessment_score,Risk Assessment Score,INT,,,,,transactional_data,Quantitative risk score assigned to the asset or maintenance activity based on risk-based assessment methodology such as Alternative Equipment Maintenance (AEM) or Authority Having Jurisdiction (AHJ) criteria. Higher scores indicate greater patient safety or operational risk.,
facility,equipment_maintenance,maintenance_order,safety_incident_flag,safety_incident_flag,Safety Incident Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,"Indicates whether this maintenance work order was triggered by or resulted in a safety incident, patient safety event, or environmental hazard. Used for safety reporting and root cause analysis.",
facility,equipment_maintenance,maintenance_order,scheduled_end_datetime,scheduled_end_datetime,Scheduled End Date and Time,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,Planned date and time when the maintenance work is scheduled to be completed. Used for resource planning and downtime coordination with clinical operations.,
facility,equipment_maintenance,maintenance_order,scheduled_start_datetime,scheduled_start_datetime,Scheduled Start Date and Time,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,"Planned date and time when the maintenance work is scheduled to begin. For preventive maintenance, this is calculated from the PM schedule frequency and last completion date.",
facility,equipment_maintenance,maintenance_order,total_cost,total_cost,Total Maintenance Cost,"DECIMAL(12,2)",,,,,transactional_data,"Total cost of the maintenance work order, including labor cost, parts cost, and any additional charges (contractor fees, disposal fees). Used for asset lifecycle cost analysis and facilities management KPIs.",
facility,equipment_maintenance,maintenance_order,trade_type,trade_type,Trade Type,STRING,,,,biomedical|electrical|plumbing|hvac|carpentry|fire_protection,transactional_data,Classification of the skilled trade or technical specialty required to perform the maintenance work. Biomedical covers medical equipment; other trades cover facility infrastructure systems.,
facility,equipment_maintenance,maintenance_order,updated_timestamp,updated_timestamp,Record Updated Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,"System timestamp when this maintenance order record was last modified in the data platform. Used for data lineage, change tracking, and audit trail purposes.",
facility,equipment_maintenance,maintenance_order,vendor_service_flag,vendor_service_flag,Vendor Service Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,Indicates whether this maintenance work order was performed by an external vendor or contractor rather than internal facilities staff. Used for cost allocation and vendor performance tracking.,
facility,equipment_maintenance,maintenance_order,warranty_claim_flag,warranty_claim_flag,Warranty Claim Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,Indicates whether this maintenance work order is eligible for warranty claim or manufacturer reimbursement. Used for tracking warranty utilization and cost recovery.,
facility,equipment_maintenance,maintenance_order,work_order_number,work_order_number,Work Order Number,STRING,,,,"^[A-Z0-9]{8,20}$",transactional_data,"Externally-known unique business identifier for the maintenance work order, used for tracking and reference across systems and by technicians.",
facility,equipment_maintenance,pm_schedule,pm_schedule_id,pm_schedule_id,Preventive Maintenance (PM) Schedule ID,BIGINT,Y,,,,master_data,Unique identifier for the preventive maintenance schedule record.,
