facility,equipment_maintenance,pm_schedule,notification_required,notification_required,Notification Required Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,Boolean flag indicating whether stakeholder notification is required when work orders are generated or when maintenance is due.,
facility,equipment_maintenance,pm_schedule,parts_required,parts_required,Parts Required,STRING,,,,,master_data,"List or description of spare parts, consumables, or materials required to complete the preventive maintenance task.",
facility,equipment_maintenance,pm_schedule,planner_group,planner_group,Planner Group,STRING,,,,,master_data,Maintenance planning group responsible for scheduling and coordinating this preventive maintenance activity.,
facility,equipment_maintenance,pm_schedule,priority,priority,Maintenance Priority,STRING,,,,critical|high|medium|low,master_data,"Priority level of the preventive maintenance schedule, indicating urgency and impact on patient safety and facility operations.",
facility,equipment_maintenance,pm_schedule,regulatory_citation,regulatory_citation,Regulatory Citation,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Specific regulatory standard, code section, or citation that mandates this preventive maintenance requirement.",
facility,equipment_maintenance,pm_schedule,regulatory_driver,regulatory_driver,Regulatory Driver,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Regulatory body or standard requiring this preventive maintenance activity (e.g., The Joint Commission (TJC), Centers for Medicare and Medicaid Services (CMS), National Fire Protection Association (NFPA), state Department of Health (DOH), Food and Drug Administration (FDA)).",
facility,equipment_maintenance,pm_schedule,required_trade,required_trade,Required Trade or Skill,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Specific trade, skill, or certification required to perform the maintenance task (e.g., biomedical engineer, HVAC technician, electrician, plumber).",
facility,equipment_maintenance,pm_schedule,safety_precautions,safety_precautions,Safety Precautions,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Required safety precautions, personal protective equipment (PPE), lockout/tagout procedures, or infection control measures that must be followed during maintenance.",
facility,equipment_maintenance,pm_schedule,schedule_code,schedule_code,Preventive Maintenance (PM) Schedule Code,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Unique business identifier or code for the preventive maintenance schedule, often used for integration with SAP PM and work order systems.",
facility,equipment_maintenance,pm_schedule,schedule_end_date,schedule_end_date,Schedule End Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,Date when this preventive maintenance schedule expires or is no longer active. Null indicates an ongoing schedule.,
