facility,site_management,bed,visit_id,visit_id,Visit Identifier (ID),BIGINT,,encounter.visit.visit_id,,,master_data,Reference to the current inpatient visit or encounter associated with the bed assignment. Null when bed is unoccupied. Used for linking bed utilization to clinical and billing events.,
facility,site_management,bed,age_restriction,age_restriction,Age Restriction,STRING,,,,adult|pediatric|neonatal|any,master_data,"Age-based restriction for patient assignment to this bed, driven by clinical care model and equipment. Values: adult (18+ years), pediatric (0-17 years), neonatal (newborn to 28 days), any (no restriction).",
facility,site_management,bed,asset_tag,asset_tag,Bed Asset Tag,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Physical asset tag or serial number affixed to the bed frame for equipment tracking, preventive maintenance scheduling, and biomedical engineering inventory management.",
facility,site_management,bed,bed_category,bed_category,Bed Category,STRING,,,,medical|surgical|pediatric|maternity|psychiatric|rehabilitation,master_data,"Clinical service line or specialty category of the bed. Used for capacity planning by service line, regulatory reporting, and patient placement algorithms. Values: medical, surgical, pediatric, maternity, psychiatric, rehabilitation.",
facility,site_management,bed,bed_status,bed_status,Bed Status,STRING,,,,available|occupied|dirty|blocked|out_of_service|housekeeping,master_data,"Current operational status of the bed. Core field for real-time bed management and ADT (Admit, Discharge, Transfer) operations. Values: available (ready for patient assignment), occupied (patient currently assigned), dirty (patient discharged, awaiting environmental services cleaning), blocked (administratively held), out_of_service (maintenance or repair required), housekeeping (cleaning in progress).",
facility,site_management,bed,bed_type,bed_type,Bed Type,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Classification of the bed based on clinical care level and purpose. Determines staffing ratios, reimbursement categories, and capacity reporting. Values: acute (general medical-surgical), icu (intensive care unit), observation (short-stay monitoring), ed (emergency department), or_table (operating room table), procedure (procedure room bed), bariatric (high weight capacity), low_bed (fall prevention), bassinet (neonatal/pediatric). [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: acute|icu|observation|ed|or_table|procedure|bariatric|low_bed|bassinet — 9 candidates stripped; promote to reference product]",
facility,site_management,bed,blocked_reason,blocked_reason,Blocked Reason,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Free-text explanation for why the bed is administratively blocked from patient assignment (e.g., construction, equipment failure, infection control hold, staffing shortage). Populated only when bed_status is blocked.",
facility,site_management,bed,created_timestamp,created_timestamp,Record Created Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,master_data,Date and time when this bed record was first created in the system. Audit field for data lineage and record lifecycle tracking.,
facility,site_management,bed,discharge_ready_timestamp,discharge_ready_timestamp,Discharge Ready Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,master_data,"Date and time when the clinical team marked the patient as medically ready for discharge. Used to calculate discharge delays, bed turnover bottlenecks, and length of stay (LOS) optimization metrics.",
facility,site_management,bed,effective_end_date,effective_end_date,Effective End Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,Date when the bed was permanently removed from service or decommissioned. Null for active beds. Used for historical capacity reporting and facility planning analysis.,
facility,site_management,bed,effective_start_date,effective_start_date,Effective Start Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,Date when the bed was first placed into service or added to the facility inventory. Used for bed lifecycle tracking and historical capacity analysis.,
facility,site_management,bed,expected_available_timestamp,expected_available_timestamp,Expected Available Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,master_data,"Estimated date and time when a currently unavailable bed (dirty, blocked, out_of_service, housekeeping) is expected to become available for patient assignment. Used for bed demand forecasting and patient placement planning.",
facility,site_management,bed,floor_number,floor_number,Floor Number,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Physical floor or level within the facility where the bed is located (e.g., 1, 2, 3, B1 for basement, G for ground). Used for wayfinding, emergency response, and facility planning.",
facility,site_management,bed,gender_restriction,gender_restriction,Gender Restriction,STRING,,,"dbx_confidential, dbx_pii",male|female|any,master_data,"Gender restriction for patient assignment to this bed, typically driven by shared room configurations or unit policies. Values: male (male patients only), female (female patients only), any (no restriction).",
facility,site_management,bed,is_active,is_active,Active Bed Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,"Indicates whether the bed record is currently active in the system. Inactive beds are permanently removed from inventory (e.g., facility closure, unit reconfiguration). Used for historical reporting and capacity trend analysis.",
facility,site_management,bed,is_air_fluidized,is_air_fluidized,Air Fluidized Bed Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,Indicates whether the bed is an air-fluidized therapy bed used for severe pressure ulcer treatment and prevention. Specialized equipment requiring clinical justification and authorization.,
facility,site_management,bed,is_bariatric_capable,is_bariatric_capable,Bariatric Capable Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,Indicates whether the bed is equipped to safely accommodate bariatric patients (typically weight capacity 350+ lbs). Impacts patient placement decisions and equipment requirements.,
facility,site_management,bed,is_isolation_capable,is_isolation_capable,Isolation Capable Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,"Indicates whether the bed is in a room suitable for isolation precautions (contact, droplet, or airborne). Supports infection control protocols and patient placement decisions.",
facility,site_management,bed,is_licensed,is_licensed,Licensed Bed Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,"Indicates whether the bed is included in the facilitys licensed bed count as approved by state health department. Impacts regulatory reporting, reimbursement, and capacity planning.",
facility,site_management,bed,is_low_bed,is_low_bed,Low Bed Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,"Indicates whether the bed is a low-height bed designed for fall prevention, typically used for high-risk patients (elderly, confused, post-operative). Supports patient safety protocols.",
facility,site_management,bed,is_negative_pressure_room,is_negative_pressure_room,Negative Pressure Room Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,"Indicates whether the bed is located in a negative pressure isolation room designed for airborne infection control (e.g., tuberculosis, COVID-19, measles). Critical for infection prevention and control.",
facility,site_management,bed,is_private_room,is_private_room,Private Room Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,"Indicates whether the bed is in a private (single-occupancy) room. Impacts patient satisfaction, infection control, and room charge billing.",
facility,site_management,bed,is_staffed,is_staffed,Staffed Bed Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,Indicates whether the bed is currently staffed and operationally available for patient assignment. A bed may be licensed but not staffed due to nursing shortages or seasonal demand fluctuations.,
facility,site_management,bed,is_telemetry_capable,is_telemetry_capable,Telemetry Capable Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,Indicates whether the bed location is equipped with continuous cardiac telemetry monitoring capability. Determines appropriate placement for patients requiring cardiac monitoring.,
facility,site_management,bed,label,label,Bed Label,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Human-readable identifier for the bed, typically including unit, room, and bed position (e.g., 4-West-201-A, ICU-12-B, ED-Bay-3). Used for operational communication and bed board displays.",
facility,site_management,bed,last_cleaned_timestamp,last_cleaned_timestamp,Last Cleaned Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,master_data,"Date and time when environmental services completed cleaning and disinfection of the bed and room. Critical for infection control, bed turnover tracking, and housekeeping performance metrics.",
