interoperability,standards_governance,fhir_resource_log,fhir_resource_identifier,fhir_resource_identifier,Fast Healthcare Interoperability Resources (FHIR) Resource ID,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"The logical identifier of the specific FHIR resource instance being accessed (e.g., Patient/12345, Observation/67890). Empty for search or create operations that do not target a specific resource instance.",
interoperability,standards_governance,fhir_resource_log,fhir_resource_type,fhir_resource_type,Fast Healthcare Interoperability Resources (FHIR) Resource Type,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"The type of FHIR resource being accessed or manipulated (e.g., Patient, Observation, Condition, MedicationRequest). Defines the clinical or administrative entity subject to the operation. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: Patient|Observation|Condition|MedicationRequest|Procedure|Encounter|AllergyIntolerance|DiagnosticReport|Immunization|CarePlan|DocumentReference|Practitioner|Organization|Location|Device|Appointment|ServiceRequest|Coverage|Claim|ExplanationOfBenefit|CareTeam|Goal|Medication|Substance|Specimen|Task|Communication|Consent|Provenance|AuditEvent|Bundle — promote to reference product]",
interoperability,standards_governance,fhir_resource_log,fhir_version_code,fhir_version_code,Fast Healthcare Interoperability Resources (FHIR) Version ID,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,The version identifier of the FHIR resource instance accessed via vread or returned in response. Supports resource versioning and history tracking per FHIR specification.,
interoperability,standards_governance,fhir_resource_log,hie_transaction_code,hie_transaction_code,Health Information Exchange (HIE) Transaction ID,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,Correlation identifier linking this FHIR operation to a broader Health Information Exchange (HIE) transaction or query. Used to trace data flows across organizational boundaries.,
interoperability,standards_governance,fhir_resource_log,http_status_code,http_status_code,Hypertext Transfer Protocol (HTTP) Status Code,INT,,,,,transactional_data,"The HTTP response status code returned by the FHIR server (e.g., 200 for success, 404 for not found, 401 for unauthorized, 500 for server error). Indicates the outcome of the API operation.",
interoperability,standards_governance,fhir_resource_log,modified_timestamp,modified_timestamp,Record Modified Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,The date and time when this log record was last modified or updated in the data warehouse. Supports change tracking and data quality monitoring.,
interoperability,standards_governance,fhir_resource_log,operation_outcome,operation_outcome,Operation Outcome,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"High-level categorization of the operation result (success, client_error, server_error, not_found, unauthorized, forbidden, validation_error). Derived from HTTP status code for simplified reporting and alerting. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: success|client_error|server_error|not_found|unauthorized|forbidden|validation_error — 7 candidates stripped; promote to reference product]",
interoperability,standards_governance,fhir_resource_log,operation_type,operation_type,FHIR Operation Type,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"The RESTful interaction type performed on the FHIR resource (read, vread, update, patch, delete, create, search-type, history-instance, history-type, or custom $operation). Aligns with FHIR RESTful API interaction definitions. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: read|vread|update|patch|delete|create|search-type|history-instance|history-type|operation — 10 candidates stripped; promote to reference product]",
interoperability,standards_governance,fhir_resource_log,request_body_size_bytes,request_body_size_bytes,Request Body Size in Bytes,INT,,,,,transactional_data,The size of the HTTP request body payload in bytes. Used for bandwidth monitoring and identifying large resource submissions.,
interoperability,standards_governance,fhir_resource_log,request_method,request_method,Hypertext Transfer Protocol (HTTP) Request Method,STRING,,,,GET|POST|PUT|PATCH|DELETE,transactional_data,"The HTTP method used for the FHIR API request (GET, POST, PUT, PATCH, DELETE). Indicates the type of RESTful operation performed.",
interoperability,standards_governance,fhir_resource_log,request_timestamp,request_timestamp,Request Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,The date and time when the FHIR API request was received by the server. Represents the business event time for the operation and is used for audit trail and performance analysis.,
interoperability,standards_governance,fhir_resource_log,request_url,request_url,Request Uniform Resource Locator (URL),STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"The full URL path of the FHIR API request, including query parameters for search operations. Captures the exact API endpoint and parameters used for detailed audit and debugging.",
interoperability,standards_governance,fhir_resource_log,requesting_application_code,requesting_application_code,Requesting Application ID,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Identifier of the client application or system that initiated the FHIR API request (e.g., mobile app, EHR module, third-party application). Used for access tracking and application-level analytics.",
interoperability,standards_governance,fhir_resource_log,requesting_client_code,requesting_client_code,Requesting Client ID,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,OAuth 2.0 client identifier or API key associated with the requesting application. Supports authentication audit and client-level access control.,
interoperability,standards_governance,fhir_resource_log,response_body_size_bytes,response_body_size_bytes,Response Body Size in Bytes,INT,,,,,transactional_data,The size of the HTTP response body payload in bytes. Used for bandwidth monitoring and identifying large resource retrievals.,
interoperability,standards_governance,fhir_resource_log,response_time_ms,response_time_ms,Response Time in Milliseconds,INT,,,,,transactional_data,The elapsed time in milliseconds between request receipt and response transmission. Key performance indicator for FHIR API latency and service level agreement (SLA) monitoring.,
interoperability,standards_governance,fhir_resource_log,response_timestamp,response_timestamp,Response Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,The date and time when the FHIR API response was sent back to the client. Used to calculate response time and monitor API performance.,
interoperability,standards_governance,fhir_resource_log,search_parameters,search_parameters,FHIR Search Parameters,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"The query string parameters used in FHIR search operations (e.g., _id, _lastUpdated, patient, code). Captured for search pattern analysis and optimization.",
interoperability,standards_governance,fhir_resource_log,search_result_count,search_result_count,Search Result Count,INT,,,,,transactional_data,The number of FHIR resources returned in response to a search operation. Used to analyze search effectiveness and identify overly broad queries.,
interoperability,standards_governance,fhir_resource_log,source_ip_address,source_ip_address,Source Internet Protocol (IP) Address,STRING,,,"dbx_confidential, dbx_pii_ip",,transactional_data,"The IP address of the client that originated the FHIR API request. Used for security monitoring, access control, and geographic analysis. May be considered personally identifiable information (PII) in some jurisdictions.",
interoperability,standards_governance,fhir_resource_log,user_agent,user_agent,User Agent String,STRING,,,"dbx_internal, dbx_pii",,transactional_data,"The HTTP User-Agent header value identifying the client software, operating system, and device type. Used for client compatibility analysis and troubleshooting.",
interoperability,standards_governance,fhir_resource_log,validation_errors,validation_errors,Validation Errors,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,Detailed error messages or codes returned by the FHIR validator when conformance validation fails. Used for troubleshooting and data quality improvement.,
