laboratory,instrument_quality,instrument,clia_certificate_id,clia_certificate_id,Clia Certificate Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,laboratory.clia_certificate.clia_certificate_id,,,master_data,Foreign key linking to laboratory.clia_certificate. Business justification: Instruments operate under CLIA certificates. Currently instrument has clia_certificate_number (string) but no FK. Business reality: instruments are certified under CLIA for specific testing. Adding cl,
laboratory,instrument_quality,instrument,compliance_program_id,compliance_program_id,Compliance Program Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,compliance.compliance_program.compliance_program_id,,,master_data,"Foreign key linking to compliance.compliance_program. Business justification: Instruments must operate under compliance programs (CLIA quality systems, proficiency testing). Required for tracking regulatory obligations, audit scope, and quality control program alignment per CLI",
laboratory,instrument_quality,instrument,cost_center_id,cost_center_id,Cost Center Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,finance.cost_center.cost_center_id,,,master_data,"Foreign key linking to finance.cost_center. Business justification: Instruments must be assigned to cost centers for depreciation expense allocation, maintenance cost tracking, and departmental asset accountability. Essential for cost allocation and capital equipment ",
laboratory,instrument_quality,instrument,employee_id,employee_id,Responsible Technician ID,BIGINT,,workforce.employee.employee_id,"dbx_confidential, dbx_pii",,master_data,Identifier of the laboratory technician or biomedical engineer assigned primary responsibility for this instruments operation and maintenance.,
laboratory,instrument_quality,instrument,fixed_asset_id,fixed_asset_id,Fixed Asset Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,finance.fixed_asset.fixed_asset_id,,,master_data,"Foreign key linking to finance.fixed_asset. Business justification: Lab instruments meeting capitalization thresholds must be tracked as fixed assets for depreciation, asset management, insurance coverage, and financial statement reporting. Required for GAAP complianc",
laboratory,instrument_quality,instrument,osha_safety_program_id,osha_safety_program_id,Osha Safety Program Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,compliance.osha_safety_program.osha_safety_program_id,,,master_data,"Foreign key linking to compliance.osha_safety_program. Business justification: Laboratory instruments (analyzers, centrifuges) covered by OSHA safety programs for equipment safety, lockout/tagout, and hazard communication. Linking instruments to programs enables compliance track",
laboratory,instrument_quality,instrument,purchase_order_id,purchase_order_id,Purchase Order Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,supply.purchase_order.purchase_order_id,,,master_data,"Foreign key linking to supply.purchase_order. Business justification: Laboratory instruments are capital equipment acquired via purchase orders. Tracking the originating PO supports asset lifecycle management, warranty validation, depreciation calculation, and capital b",
laboratory,instrument_quality,instrument,room_id,room_id,Room Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,facility.room.room_id,,,master_data,"Foreign key linking to facility.room. Business justification: Laboratory instruments are fixed assets installed in specific rooms. CLIA/CAP accreditation requires documented physical location for inspections, preventive maintenance scheduling, and operational pl",
laboratory,instrument_quality,instrument,training_id,training_id,Training Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,compliance.training.training_id,,,master_data,Foreign key linking to compliance.training. Business justification: Instrument operation requires documented competency training before independent testing per CLIA. Linking instruments to training programs enables tracking of required competencies and audit verificat,
laboratory,instrument_quality,instrument,vendor_id,vendor_id,Vendor Id,BIGINT,,supply.vendor.vendor_id,dbx_internal,,master_data,FK to supply.vendor,
laboratory,instrument_quality,instrument,acquisition_cost,acquisition_cost,Acquisition Cost,"DECIMAL(15,2)",,,dbx_confidential,,master_data,"Total cost paid to acquire the instrument, including purchase price, shipping, installation, and initial setup fees. Expressed in USD.",
laboratory,instrument_quality,instrument,asset_tag,asset_tag,Asset Tag Number,STRING,,,,,master_data,Internal asset tracking identifier assigned by the healthcare organization for inventory and fixed asset management.,
laboratory,instrument_quality,instrument,calibration_frequency,calibration_frequency,Calibration Frequency,STRING,,,,daily|weekly|monthly|quarterly|semi_annual|annual,master_data,"Required frequency for calibration verification or full calibration per manufacturer specifications, CLIA requirements, or laboratory policy.",
laboratory,instrument_quality,instrument,created_timestamp,created_timestamp,Record Created Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,master_data,Timestamp when this instrument record was first created in the system.,
laboratory,instrument_quality,instrument,decommission_date,decommission_date,Decommission Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,Date when the instrument was permanently removed from service and decommissioned.,
laboratory,instrument_quality,instrument,decommission_reason,decommission_reason,Decommission Reason,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Business or technical justification for decommissioning the instrument (e.g., end of life, obsolescence, replacement, irreparable failure).",
laboratory,instrument_quality,instrument,facility_service_contract_expiration_date,facility_service_contract_expiration_date,Service Contract Expiration Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,Date when the current service or maintenance contract for the instrument expires.,
laboratory,instrument_quality,instrument,facility_service_contract_number,facility_service_contract_number,Service Contract Number,STRING,,,,,master_data,Identifier for the active maintenance or service contract covering this instrument.,
laboratory,instrument_quality,instrument,installation_date,installation_date,Installation Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,Date when the instrument was installed and commissioned for use in the laboratory.,
laboratory,instrument_quality,instrument,instrument_name,instrument_name,Instrument Name,STRING,,,,,master_data,Human-readable name or designation of the laboratory instrument as known to laboratory staff.,
laboratory,instrument_quality,instrument,instrument_type,instrument_type,Instrument Type,STRING,,,,analyzer|centrifuge|microscope|incubator|spectrophotometer|other,master_data,Classification of the instrument by its primary analytical or operational function within the laboratory.,
laboratory,instrument_quality,instrument,lab_section,lab_section,Laboratory Section,STRING,,,,chemistry|hematology|microbiology|immunology|blood_bank|molecular,master_data,"The laboratory department or section to which this instrument is assigned (e.g., Chemistry, Hematology, Microbiology).",
laboratory,instrument_quality,instrument,last_calibration_date,last_calibration_date,Last Calibration Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,Date when the instrument was last calibrated to ensure measurement accuracy and precision.,
laboratory,instrument_quality,instrument,last_calibration_result,last_calibration_result,Last Calibration Result,STRING,,,,pass|fail|conditional,master_data,Outcome of the most recent calibration verification indicating whether the instrument met accuracy and precision specifications.,
laboratory,instrument_quality,instrument,last_corrective_maintenance_date,last_corrective_maintenance_date,Last Corrective Maintenance Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,Date when the most recent unscheduled corrective maintenance or repair was performed on the instrument.,
laboratory,instrument_quality,instrument,last_preventive_maintenance_date,last_preventive_maintenance_date,Last Preventive Maintenance Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,Date when the most recent scheduled preventive maintenance was performed on the instrument.,
laboratory,instrument_quality,instrument,last_quality_control_date,last_quality_control_date,Last Quality Control (QC) Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,Date when the most recent quality control testing was performed on the instrument.,
laboratory,instrument_quality,instrument,last_quality_control_result,last_quality_control_result,Last Quality Control (QC) Result,STRING,,,,pass|fail|conditional,master_data,Outcome of the most recent quality control testing indicating whether the instrument met performance specifications.,
laboratory,instrument_quality,instrument,last_updated_timestamp,last_updated_timestamp,Record Last Updated Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,master_data,Timestamp when this instrument record was most recently modified.,
laboratory,instrument_quality,instrument,lis_connectivity_status,lis_connectivity_status,Laboratory Information System (LIS) Connectivity Status,STRING,,,,connected|disconnected|error|not_applicable,master_data,Current status of the bidirectional interface connection between the instrument and the Laboratory Information System.,
laboratory,instrument_quality,instrument,lis_interface_code,lis_interface_code,Laboratory Information System (LIS) Interface ID,STRING,,,,,master_data,Unique identifier used by the Laboratory Information System to communicate with and receive results from this instrument.,
laboratory,instrument_quality,instrument,manufacturer,manufacturer,Manufacturer Name,STRING,,,,,master_data,Name of the company that manufactured the laboratory instrument.,
laboratory,instrument_quality,instrument,model_number,model_number,Model Number,STRING,,,,,master_data,Manufacturer-assigned model number or designation for the instrument type.,
laboratory,instrument_quality,instrument,next_calibration_date,next_calibration_date,Next Calibration Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,Scheduled date for the next calibration verification or full calibration of the instrument.,
laboratory,instrument_quality,instrument,next_preventive_maintenance_date,next_preventive_maintenance_date,Next Preventive Maintenance Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,Scheduled date for the next preventive maintenance service on the instrument.,
laboratory,instrument_quality,instrument,notes,notes,Instrument Notes,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Free-text field for additional notes, special handling instructions, known issues, or operational considerations for the instrument.",
laboratory,instrument_quality,instrument,operational_status,operational_status,Operational Status,STRING,,,,active|down|maintenance|decommissioned|pending_installation|calibration,master_data,Current operational state of the instrument indicating its availability for testing and analysis.,
laboratory,instrument_quality,instrument,preventive_maintenance_frequency,preventive_maintenance_frequency,Preventive Maintenance Frequency,STRING,,,,daily|weekly|monthly|quarterly|semi_annual|annual,master_data,Scheduled frequency at which preventive maintenance must be performed on the instrument per manufacturer specifications or laboratory policy.,
laboratory,instrument_quality,instrument,quality_control_frequency,quality_control_frequency,Quality Control (QC) Frequency,STRING,,,,per_shift|daily|weekly|per_run,master_data,Required frequency for running quality control samples on the instrument to verify ongoing analytical performance.,
laboratory,instrument_quality,instrument,serial_number,serial_number,Serial Number,STRING,,,,,master_data,Unique serial number assigned by the manufacturer to this specific instrument unit.,
laboratory,instrument_quality,instrument,total_downtime_hours,total_downtime_hours,Total Downtime Hours,"DECIMAL(10,2)",,,,,master_data,"Cumulative hours the instrument has been non-operational due to maintenance, repair, or malfunction since installation or last reset period.",
laboratory,instrument_quality,instrument,warranty_expiration_date,warranty_expiration_date,Warranty Expiration Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,Date when the manufacturer warranty coverage for the instrument expires.,
laboratory,instrument_quality,instrument_policy_compliance,instrument_policy_compliance_id,instrument_policy_compliance_id,Instrument Policy Compliance Identifier,BIGINT,Y,,,,association_data,Unique identifier for this instrument-policy compliance record. Primary key.,
laboratory,instrument_quality,instrument_policy_compliance,compliance_policy_id,compliance_policy_id,Instrument Policy Compliance - Policy Id,BIGINT,,compliance.compliance_policy.compliance_policy_id,,,association_data,Foreign key linking to the organizational policy that applies to the instrument,
laboratory,instrument_quality,instrument_policy_compliance,employee_id,employee_id,Assessor Employee Identifier,BIGINT,,workforce.employee.employee_id,"dbx_confidential, dbx_pii",,association_data,Identifier of the compliance officer or quality assurance staff member who conducted the most recent compliance assessment for this instrument-policy pairing.,
laboratory,instrument_quality,instrument_policy_compliance,instrument_id,instrument_id,Instrument Policy Compliance - Instrument Id,BIGINT,,laboratory.instrument.instrument_id,,,association_data,Foreign key linking to the laboratory instrument being governed by the policy,
laboratory,instrument_quality,instrument_policy_compliance,attestation_status,attestation_status,Attestation Status,STRING,,,,,association_data,Status of staff attestation that they have read and will comply with this policy for this instrument. Attested indicates current valid attestation; not_attested indicates no attestation on record; pending indicates attestation requested but not completed; expired indicates attestation has passed its validity period.,
laboratory,instrument_quality,instrument_policy_compliance,compliance_status,compliance_status,Compliance Status,STRING,,,,,association_data,Current compliance status of this instrument with respect to this policy. Compliant indicates full adherence; non_compliant indicates violations or gaps; pending_review indicates assessment in progress; not_applicable indicates policy does not apply to this instrument; waived indicates formal exception granted.,
laboratory,instrument_quality,instrument_policy_compliance,effective_date,effective_date,Policy Effective Date for Instrument,DATE,,,,,association_data,Date when this policy became applicable to this specific instrument. May differ from the policys general effective date if the instrument was acquired later or the policy scope changed.,
laboratory,instrument_quality,instrument_policy_compliance,last_assessment_date,last_assessment_date,Last Compliance Assessment Date,DATE,,,,,association_data,Date when compliance with this policy was most recently assessed for this instrument. Used to track assessment currency and schedule next reviews.,
laboratory,instrument_quality,instrument_policy_compliance,next_review_date,next_review_date,Next Compliance Review Date,DATE,,,,,association_data,Scheduled date for the next compliance review of this instrument against this policy. Calculated based on policy review cycle and last assessment date.,
laboratory,instrument_quality,instrument_policy_compliance,non_compliance_notes,non_compliance_notes,Non-Compliance Notes,STRING,,,,,association_data,"Detailed notes documenting any non-compliance findings, corrective actions required, or remediation plans for this instrument-policy combination. Nullable when compliance_status is compliant.",
laboratory,instrument_quality,instrument_policy_compliance,waiver_expiration_date,waiver_expiration_date,Waiver Expiration Date,DATE,,,,,association_data,Date when the compliance waiver expires and full compliance is required. Nullable unless compliance_status is waived.,
laboratory,instrument_quality,instrument_policy_compliance,waiver_justification,waiver_justification,Waiver Justification,STRING,,,,,association_data,Business or technical justification for granting a compliance waiver or exception for this instrument-policy pairing. Nullable unless compliance_status is waived.,
laboratory,instrument_quality,qc_run,qc_run_id,qc_run_id,Quality Control (QC) Run Identifier (ID),BIGINT,Y,,,,transactional_data,Unique identifier for the quality control run record. Primary key for the qc_run product.,
laboratory,instrument_quality,qc_run,accreditation_survey_id,accreditation_survey_id,Accreditation Survey Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,quality.accreditation_survey.accreditation_survey_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to quality.accreditation_survey. Business justification: QC documentation is reviewed during laboratory accreditation surveys. Surveyors verify QC compliance with CLIA/CAP standards (daily QC, proficiency testing, corrective actions) as part of laboratory q",
laboratory,instrument_quality,qc_run,cost_center_id,cost_center_id,Cost Center Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,finance.cost_center.cost_center_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to finance.cost_center. Business justification: Quality control costs must be allocated to the performing lab sections cost center for QC cost analysis, regulatory compliance cost tracking, and budget management. Required for CLIA compliance cost ",
laboratory,instrument_quality,qc_run,employee_id,employee_id,Performing Technologist Identifier (ID),BIGINT,,workforce.employee.employee_id,"dbx_confidential, dbx_pii",,transactional_data,"Reference to the laboratory technologist or medical laboratory scientist who performed the quality control run. Links to workforce or provider master data for technologist name, credentials, and competency records.",
laboratory,instrument_quality,qc_run,instrument_id,instrument_id,Laboratory Instrument Identifier (ID),BIGINT,,laboratory.instrument.instrument_id,,,transactional_data,"Reference to the laboratory instrument or analyzer on which the quality control run was performed. Links to the laboratory instrument master data for instrument identification, model, serial number, and location.",
laboratory,instrument_quality,qc_run,reagent_lot_id,reagent_lot_id,Reagent Lot Id,BIGINT,,laboratory.reagent_lot.reagent_lot_id,dbx_internal,,transactional_data,FK to laboratory.reagent_lot,
laboratory,instrument_quality,qc_run,test_catalog_id,test_catalog_id,Test Catalog Id,BIGINT,,laboratory.test_catalog.test_catalog_id,dbx_internal,,transactional_data,FK to laboratory.test_catalog,
laboratory,instrument_quality,qc_run,training_id,training_id,Training Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,compliance.training.training_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to compliance.training. Business justification: QC procedures require documented competency training per CLIA. Linking QC runs to training records enables verification that only trained personnel performed quality control, required for regulatory c",
laboratory,instrument_quality,qc_run,comments,comments,Quality Control (QC) Comments,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Free-text comments or notes related to the quality control run. May include technologist observations, unusual circumstances, instrument issues, or additional context for QC results. Used for quality investigations and troubleshooting.",
laboratory,instrument_quality,qc_run,corrective_action_taken,corrective_action_taken,Corrective Action Taken,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Detailed description of corrective action taken in response to failed quality control. Examples include recalibration performed, reagent lot changed, instrument maintenance completed, repeat QC passed, patient results reviewed and reissued. Required documentation for CLIA compliance when QC fails.",
laboratory,instrument_quality,qc_run,corrective_action_timestamp,corrective_action_timestamp,Corrective Action Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,Date and time when corrective action was completed. Documents when the laboratory resolved the quality control failure and resumed patient testing. Required for CLIA compliance and quality management.,
laboratory,instrument_quality,qc_run,created_timestamp,created_timestamp,Record Created Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,Date and time when this quality control run record was first created in the laboratory information system. Audit trail timestamp for record creation.,
laboratory,instrument_quality,qc_run,expected_mean,expected_mean,Expected Mean Value,"DECIMAL(18,4)",,,,,transactional_data,Manufacturer-assigned or laboratory-established mean value for the quality control material at this level. This is the target value against which observed results are compared. Used in Westgard rule evaluation and statistical quality control.,
laboratory,instrument_quality,qc_run,expected_standard_deviation,expected_standard_deviation,Expected Standard Deviation (SD),"DECIMAL(18,4)",,,,,transactional_data,"Manufacturer-assigned or laboratory-established standard deviation for the quality control material at this level. Defines the acceptable range of variation. Used to calculate control limits (e.g., mean ± 2SD, mean ± 3SD) for Westgard rule evaluation.",
laboratory,instrument_quality,qc_run,last_updated_timestamp,last_updated_timestamp,Record Last Updated Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,"Date and time when this quality control run record was last modified in the laboratory information system. Audit trail timestamp for record updates. Updated when QC status changes, review is completed, or corrective actions are documented.",
laboratory,instrument_quality,qc_run,observed_result,observed_result,Observed Quality Control (QC) Result,"DECIMAL(18,4)",,,,,transactional_data,Actual measured value obtained from the quality control run. This is the raw result produced by the instrument or test method. Compared against expected mean and standard deviation to determine pass/fail status.,
laboratory,instrument_quality,qc_run,pass_fail_indicator,pass_fail_indicator,Pass or Fail Indicator,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,Boolean indicator of whether the quality control run met acceptance criteria. True indicates QC passed and patient testing may proceed. False indicates QC failed and corrective action is required before patient testing can resume.,
laboratory,instrument_quality,qc_run,pt_attestation_date,pt_attestation_date,Proficiency Testing (PT) Attestation Date,DATE,,,,,transactional_data,"Date when the laboratory director or designee attested that proficiency testing was performed in the same manner as patient testing, without interlaboratory communication or use of reference materials. Required attestation for CLIA compliance.",
laboratory,instrument_quality,qc_run,pt_corrective_action_plan,pt_corrective_action_plan,Proficiency Testing (PT) Corrective Action Plan,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Detailed corrective action plan documented in response to unacceptable proficiency testing result. Must include root cause analysis, immediate corrective actions, long-term preventive actions, and timeline for implementation. Required by CLIA for PT failures.",
laboratory,instrument_quality,qc_run,pt_event_code,pt_event_code,Proficiency Testing (PT) Event Code,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Unique identifier for the proficiency testing event or survey cycle. Typically includes year and survey number (e.g., CAP-2024-A, AAFP-2024-Q1). Used to track PT participation and results over time.",
laboratory,instrument_quality,qc_run,pt_graded_result,pt_graded_result,Proficiency Testing (PT) Graded Result,STRING,,,,acceptable|unacceptable|pending|not_graded,transactional_data,Grading outcome assigned by the proficiency testing program. Acceptable indicates the laboratory result met PT acceptance criteria. Unacceptable indicates the laboratory result failed PT criteria and triggers regulatory action. Pending indicates grading is not yet complete. Not graded indicates the sample was educational only.,
laboratory,instrument_quality,qc_run,pt_peer_group_mean,pt_peer_group_mean,Proficiency Testing (PT) Peer Group Mean,"DECIMAL(18,4)",,,,,transactional_data,Mean value of all laboratories in the peer group for this proficiency testing sample. Peer groups are defined by test method or instrument type. Used to evaluate laboratory performance relative to peers.,
laboratory,instrument_quality,qc_run,pt_peer_group_standard_deviation,pt_peer_group_standard_deviation,Proficiency Testing (PT) Peer Group Standard Deviation (SD),"DECIMAL(18,4)",,,,,transactional_data,Standard deviation of all laboratories in the peer group for this proficiency testing sample. Measures the variability of peer group results. Used to calculate z-score and evaluate laboratory performance.,
laboratory,instrument_quality,qc_run,pt_program_name,pt_program_name,Proficiency Testing (PT) Program Name,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Name of the external proficiency testing program or provider. Examples include CAP (College of American Pathologists), AAFP (American Academy of Family Physicians), COLA (Commission on Office Laboratory Accreditation), Wisconsin State Laboratory of Hygiene. Applicable only when qc_type is proficiency_testing.",
laboratory,instrument_quality,qc_run,pt_sample_number,pt_sample_number,Proficiency Testing (PT) Sample Number,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Unique identifier for the specific proficiency testing sample within the event. PT programs typically send multiple samples per event (e.g., Sample 1, Sample 2, Sample 3). Used to track individual sample results.",
laboratory,instrument_quality,qc_run,pt_submitted_result,pt_submitted_result,Proficiency Testing (PT) Submitted Result,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,Result value submitted by the laboratory to the proficiency testing program. This is the laboratorys answer for the PT sample. Stored as string to accommodate both quantitative and qualitative results.,
laboratory,instrument_quality,qc_run,pt_z_score,pt_z_score,Proficiency Testing (PT) Z-Score,"DECIMAL(10,4)",,,,,transactional_data,Statistical measure of how many standard deviations the laboratory result differs from the peer group mean. Calculated as (submitted result - peer group mean) / peer group SD. Z-scores within ±2 are typically acceptable. Z-scores beyond ±3 indicate significant deviation.,
laboratory,instrument_quality,qc_run,qc_level,qc_level,Quality Control (QC) Level,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Concentration level of the quality control material. Low, normal, and high levels span the reportable range of the test. Level 1, 2, 3 are alternative designations. Abnormal low and abnormal high represent pathological ranges. Multiple levels ensure accuracy across the entire measurement range. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: low|normal|high|level_1|level_2|level_3|abnormal_low|abnormal_high — 8 candidates stripped; promote to reference product]",
laboratory,instrument_quality,qc_run,qc_material_lot_number,qc_material_lot_number,Quality Control (QC) Material Lot Number,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Manufacturer lot number of the quality control material used in this run. For internal QC, this is the control material lot. For proficiency testing, this is the PT sample lot or shipment identifier. Critical for traceability and lot-to-result investigations.",
laboratory,instrument_quality,qc_run,qc_run_status,qc_run_status,Quality Control (QC) Run Status,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Current lifecycle status of the quality control run. Pending indicates QC is scheduled but not yet performed, in progress indicates QC is actively being executed, passed indicates QC met acceptance criteria, failed indicates QC did not meet acceptance criteria and requires investigation, reviewed indicates QC results have been reviewed by supervisor, corrective action required indicates failed QC requires documented corrective action before patient testing can resume, and cancelled indicates QC run was voided. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: pending|in_progress|passed|failed|reviewed|corrective_action_required|cancelled — 7 candidates stripped; promote to reference product]",
laboratory,instrument_quality,qc_run,qc_run_timestamp,qc_run_timestamp,Quality Control (QC) Run Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,Date and time when the quality control run was performed. This is the principal business event timestamp representing when the QC material was analyzed or when the proficiency testing sample was tested.,
laboratory,instrument_quality,qc_run,qc_type,qc_type,Quality Control (QC) Type,STRING,,,,internal_qc|proficiency_testing|reagent_lot_validation|calibration_verification|instrument_maintenance_qc|competency_assessment,transactional_data,"Type of quality control activity performed. Internal QC validates daily instrument performance, proficiency testing evaluates laboratory competency against external standards, reagent lot validation ensures new reagent lots meet specifications, calibration verification confirms instrument calibration accuracy, instrument maintenance QC verifies post-maintenance performance, and competency assessment validates technologist proficiency.",
laboratory,instrument_quality,qc_run,reagent_storage_temperature,reagent_storage_temperature,Reagent Storage Temperature,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Required storage temperature or temperature range for the reagent or consumable. Examples include 2-8°C (refrigerated), -20°C (frozen), 15-30°C (room temperature). Proper storage is critical for reagent stability and performance.",
laboratory,instrument_quality,qc_run,result_unit_of_measure,result_unit_of_measure,Result Unit of Measure,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Unit of measure for the observed quality control result. Examples include mg/dL, mmol/L, g/dL, IU/L, seconds, cells/uL. Must match the unit of measure for the expected mean and standard deviation.",
laboratory,instrument_quality,qc_run,reviewed_timestamp,reviewed_timestamp,Reviewed Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,Date and time when the quality control results were reviewed by a supervisor or technical consultant. Required for failed QC runs and periodic supervisory review per CLIA regulations.,
laboratory,instrument_quality,qc_run,test_code,test_code,Laboratory Test Code,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Laboratory test or analyte code for which quality control was performed. Typically corresponds to LOINC code or internal laboratory test catalog code. For proficiency testing, this is the surveyed analyte or test method.",
laboratory,instrument_quality,qc_run,westgard_rule_evaluation,westgard_rule_evaluation,Westgard Rule Evaluation,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Outcome of Westgard multirule quality control evaluation. Pass indicates result is within acceptable limits. 1_2s_warning indicates one control exceeds 2SD (warning, not rejection). 1_3s_reject indicates one control exceeds 3SD (reject run). 2_2s_reject indicates two consecutive controls exceed 2SD on same side of mean (reject run). r_4s_reject indicates range between two controls exceeds 4SD (reject run). 4_1s_reject indicates four consecutive controls exceed 1SD on same side (reject run). 10_x_reject indicates ten consecutive controls on same side of mean (reject run). Not applicable for non-quantitative QC. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: pass|1_2s_warning|1_3s_reject|2_2s_reject|r_4s_reject|4_1s_reject|10_x_reject|not_applicable — 8 candidates stripped; promote to reference product]",
laboratory,instrument_quality,reagent_lot,reagent_lot_id,reagent_lot_id,Reagent Lot Identifier (ID),BIGINT,Y,,,,master_data,Unique identifier for the reagent lot record. Primary key for the reagent_lot product.,
laboratory,instrument_quality,reagent_lot,assigned_instrument_id,assigned_instrument_id,Assigned Instrument Identifier (ID),BIGINT,,laboratory.instrument.instrument_id,,,master_data,The identifier of the laboratory instrument or analyzer to which this reagent lot is assigned or dedicated.,
laboratory,instrument_quality,reagent_lot,cost_center_id,cost_center_id,Cost Center Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,finance.cost_center.cost_center_id,,,master_data,"Foreign key linking to finance.cost_center. Business justification: Reagent inventory must be tracked by cost center for consumption analysis, budget variance reporting, and cost-per-test calculations. Critical for laboratory supply cost management and inventory valua",
laboratory,instrument_quality,reagent_lot,employee_id,employee_id,Quality Control (QC) Validated By Technologist Identifier (ID),BIGINT,,workforce.employee.employee_id,"dbx_confidential, dbx_pii",,master_data,The identifier of the laboratory technologist or staff member who performed and validated the QC testing for this reagent lot.,
laboratory,instrument_quality,reagent_lot,material_master_id,material_master_id,Material Master Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,supply.material_master.material_master_id,,,master_data,"Foreign key linking to supply.material_master. Business justification: Reagent lots are instances of material master items. This is the fundamental product-to-lot relationship for inventory management, enabling lot tracking, expiration management, recall handling, and in",
