laboratory,order_processing,lab_order,primary_lab_clinician_id,primary_lab_clinician_id,Ordering Provider ID,BIGINT,,provider.clinician.clinician_id,,,transactional_data,"Unique identifier for the healthcare provider (physician, nurse practitioner, physician assistant) who ordered the laboratory test via CPOE (Computerized Physician Order Entry).",
laboratory,order_processing,lab_order,quality_measure_id,quality_measure_id,Quality Measure Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,quality.measure.measure_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to quality.measure. Business justification: Lab orders trigger quality measure opportunities (ordering appropriate screening tests like colonoscopy prep labs, pre-op testing). Quality gap closure workflows track which measures are addressed by ",
laboratory,order_processing,lab_order,research_study_id,research_study_id,Research Study Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,research.research_study.research_study_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to research.research_study. Business justification: Lab orders generated for research protocols must link to originating study for protocol compliance tracking, coverage analysis (standard-of-care vs research), regulatory reporting, and research billin",
laboratory,order_processing,lab_order,tertiary_lab_cancelled_by_provider_clinician_id,tertiary_lab_cancelled_by_provider_clinician_id,Cancelled By Provider ID,BIGINT,,provider.clinician.clinician_id,,,transactional_data,Unique identifier for the healthcare provider who cancelled or discontinued the laboratory order. Used for audit trail and accountability.,
laboratory,order_processing,lab_order,test_catalog_id,test_catalog_id,Test Catalog Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,laboratory.test_catalog.test_catalog_id,,,transactional_data,Foreign key linking to laboratory.test_catalog. Business justification: Lab orders request specific catalog tests. Currently lab_order has test_code/test_name/test_category but no FK. Business reality: orders reference catalog tests for what to perform. Adding test_catalo,
laboratory,order_processing,lab_order,visit_id,visit_id,Encounter ID,BIGINT,,encounter.visit.visit_id,,,transactional_data,Unique identifier for the clinical encounter or visit during which the laboratory order was placed. Links to the visit/encounter record.,
laboratory,order_processing,lab_order,authorization_number,authorization_number,Prior Authorization Number,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,Authorization or pre-certification number obtained from the insurance payer approving coverage for this laboratory test. Required for claim submission when authorization_required is True.,
laboratory,order_processing,lab_order,authorization_required,authorization_required,Prior Authorization Required Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,Boolean flag indicating whether payer prior authorization is required before performing this laboratory test. True for high-cost or specialized tests that require pre-approval for reimbursement.,
laboratory,order_processing,lab_order,billing_code,billing_code,CPT (Current Procedural Terminology) Billing Code,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,CPT or HCPCS (Healthcare Common Procedure Coding System) code used for billing and reimbursement of the laboratory test. Links laboratory orders to revenue cycle and supports charge capture.,
laboratory,order_processing,lab_order,cancellation_reason,cancellation_reason,Order Cancellation Reason,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Free-text or coded reason why the laboratory order was cancelled. Examples: duplicate order, ordered in error, patient refused, specimen quality insufficient, test no longer clinically indicated. Used for quality improvement and utilization review.",
laboratory,order_processing,lab_order,cancelled_timestamp,cancelled_timestamp,Order Cancelled Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,Date and time when the laboratory order was cancelled or discontinued. Populated only when order_status is cancelled or discontinued.,
laboratory,order_processing,lab_order,clinical_indication,clinical_indication,Clinical Indication,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Free-text clinical reason or diagnosis justifying the laboratory order. Provides context for medical necessity, supports appropriate utilization, and may be required for insurance authorization and reimbursement.",
laboratory,order_processing,lab_order,collection_date,collection_date,Specimen Collection Date,DATE,,,,,transactional_data,Calendar date when the specimen was collected from the patient. May differ from order date for scheduled or delayed collections.,
laboratory,order_processing,lab_order,collection_method,collection_method,Specimen Collection Method,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Technique or procedure used to collect the specimen. Examples: venipuncture, capillary stick, clean catch, catheterized, biopsy. Affects specimen quality and test validity.",
laboratory,order_processing,lab_order,collection_timestamp,collection_timestamp,Specimen Collection Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,Precise date and time when the specimen was collected from the patient. Critical for time-sensitive tests and stability calculations. Used as the start point for laboratory turnaround time measurement.,
laboratory,order_processing,lab_order,created_timestamp,created_timestamp,Record Created Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,Date and time when this laboratory order record was first created in the data lakehouse. Audit field for data lineage and record lifecycle tracking.,
laboratory,order_processing,lab_order,diagnosis_code,diagnosis_code,ICD-10 (International Classification of Diseases 10th Revision) Diagnosis Code,STRING,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_health",,transactional_data,"ICD-10 diagnosis code associated with the laboratory order, documenting the clinical condition being investigated or monitored. Required for claims processing and medical necessity validation.",
laboratory,order_processing,lab_order,expected_turnaround_time_hours,expected_turnaround_time_hours,Expected Turnaround Time Hours,INT,,,,,transactional_data,"Expected number of hours from specimen collection to result availability, based on test type and performing laboratory. Used for result expectation management and delay identification. For send-out orders, includes shipping and reference lab processing time.",
laboratory,order_processing,lab_order,fasting_required,fasting_required,Fasting Required Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,"Boolean flag indicating whether the patient must fast prior to specimen collection for accurate test results. True for tests such as fasting glucose, lipid panel. Used for patient preparation instructions.",
laboratory,order_processing,lab_order,is_send_out,is_send_out,Is Send-Out Order Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,Boolean flag indicating whether this laboratory order is sent to an external reference laboratory for testing (True) or performed internally (False). Send-out orders require additional tracking for shipping and result receipt.,
laboratory,order_processing,lab_order,order_date,order_date,Laboratory Order Date,DATE,,,,,transactional_data,Calendar date when the laboratory order was placed by the ordering provider via CPOE (Computerized Physician Order Entry). Used for turnaround time calculations and operational metrics.,
laboratory,order_processing,lab_order,order_number,order_number,Laboratory Order Number,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,The externally-known unique order number or accession number assigned to this laboratory order by the LIS (Laboratory Information System) such as Epic Beaker or Cerner PathNet. Used for tracking and reference across systems.,
laboratory,order_processing,lab_order,order_priority,order_priority,Laboratory Order Priority,STRING,,,,STAT|routine|ASAP|timed|urgent,transactional_data,"Clinical priority level assigned to the laboratory order. STAT indicates immediate/emergency processing, routine for standard turnaround, ASAP for expedited but not emergency, timed for specific collection time requirements, urgent for high-priority processing.",
laboratory,order_processing,lab_order,order_set_name,order_set_name,Order Set Name,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Name of the clinical order set or protocol from which this laboratory order was generated. Order sets bundle commonly-ordered tests for specific clinical scenarios (admission panels, pre-operative workup, sepsis workup).",
laboratory,order_processing,lab_order,order_status,order_status,Laboratory Order Status,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Current lifecycle status of the laboratory order. Tracks progression from order placement through specimen collection, processing, and result delivery. For send-out orders, includes sent_out status when specimen is shipped to reference laboratory. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: ordered|collected|in_process|sent_out|resulted|cancelled|discontinued|on_hold — 8 candidates stripped; promote to reference product]",
laboratory,order_processing,lab_order,order_timestamp,order_timestamp,Laboratory Order Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,Precise date and time when the laboratory order was electronically placed in the system. The principal business event timestamp for this transaction. Critical for STAT order tracking and turnaround time analysis.,
laboratory,order_processing,lab_order,performing_lab_location,performing_lab_location,Performing Laboratory Location,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Name or identifier of the laboratory facility or department performing the test. For internal orders: hospital lab, clinic lab, point-of-care. For send-outs: reference laboratory name.",
laboratory,order_processing,lab_order,point_of_care_test,point_of_care_test,Point-of-Care Test Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,"Boolean flag indicating whether this is a point-of-care test performed at or near the patient location (bedside, clinic exam room, emergency department) rather than in the central laboratory. Examples: glucose meter, rapid strep test, blood gas analyzer.",
laboratory,order_processing,lab_order,reference_lab_accession_number,reference_lab_accession_number,Reference Laboratory Accession Number,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,Unique accession or tracking number assigned by the external reference laboratory to this specimen. Used for result reconciliation and inquiry. Populated only for send-out orders.,
laboratory,order_processing,lab_order,reference_lab_name,reference_lab_name,Reference Laboratory Name,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Name of the external reference laboratory to which the specimen is sent for testing. Populated only for send-out orders. Examples: Quest Diagnostics, LabCorp, Mayo Clinic Laboratories, ARUP Laboratories.",
laboratory,order_processing,lab_order,result_integration_status,result_integration_status,Result Integration Status,STRING,,,,pending|integrated|failed|manual_entry_required,transactional_data,Status of electronic result integration from the reference laboratory into the internal LIS and EHR (Electronic Health Record). Tracks whether results were successfully auto-imported or require manual intervention. Populated only for send-out orders.,
laboratory,order_processing,lab_order,result_received_timestamp,result_received_timestamp,Result Received Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,Date and time when the laboratory result was received back from the reference laboratory and integrated into the LIS (Laboratory Information System). Populated only for send-out orders. Marks completion of the send-out order lifecycle.,
laboratory,order_processing,lab_order,shipping_carrier,shipping_carrier,Shipping Carrier,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Name of the courier or shipping service used to transport the specimen to the reference laboratory. Examples: FedEx, UPS, DHL, courier service. Populated only for send-out orders.",
laboratory,order_processing,lab_order,shipping_tracking_number,shipping_tracking_number,Shipping Tracking Number,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,Carrier-provided tracking number for the specimen shipment. Enables real-time tracking of specimen in transit and confirmation of delivery to reference laboratory. Populated only for send-out orders.,
laboratory,order_processing,lab_order,source_system,source_system,Source System,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Name of the source operational system from which this laboratory order record originated. Examples: Epic Beaker, Cerner PathNet, MEDITECH Laboratory. Used for data lineage and troubleshooting.",
laboratory,order_processing,lab_order,source_system_order_number,source_system_order_number,Source System Order ID,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Unique identifier for this laboratory order in the source operational system (Epic Beaker, Cerner PathNet). Used for cross-system reconciliation and drill-back to source records.",
laboratory,order_processing,lab_order,specimen_shipped_timestamp,specimen_shipped_timestamp,Specimen Shipped Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,Date and time when the specimen was shipped or dispatched to the external reference laboratory. Used to track send-out order logistics and calculate total turnaround time. Populated only for send-out orders.,
laboratory,order_processing,lab_order,specimen_source,specimen_source,Specimen Source,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Anatomical site or body location from which the specimen was collected. Examples: left arm venipuncture, throat swab, wound site, right knee joint. Important for pathology and microbiology orders.",
laboratory,order_processing,lab_order,specimen_type,specimen_type,Specimen Type,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Type of biological specimen collected for the laboratory test. Examples: blood, serum, plasma, urine, tissue, swab, cerebrospinal fluid. Determines handling and processing requirements.",
laboratory,order_processing,lab_order,standing_order,standing_order,Standing Order Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,"Boolean flag indicating whether this order is part of a standing order protocol (recurring orders based on clinical protocol or care plan) rather than a one-time order. Examples: daily morning labs for ICU patients, weekly monitoring for chronic conditions.",
laboratory,order_processing,lab_order,updated_timestamp,updated_timestamp,Record Updated Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,Date and time when this laboratory order record was last modified in the data lakehouse. Audit field for change tracking and data freshness monitoring.,
laboratory,order_processing,laboratory_test_result,laboratory_test_result_id,laboratory_test_result_id,Test Result Identifier (ID),BIGINT,Y,,,,transactional_data,Unique identifier for the laboratory test result record. Primary key for the test result entity.,
