laboratory,order_processing,reference_range,loinc_code_id,loinc_code_id,Loinc Code Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,reference.loinc_code.loinc_code_id,,,reference_data,"Foreign key linking to reference.loinc_code. Business justification: Reference ranges are LOINC-specific and vary by test methodology. Structured linkage enables proper result interpretation across systems, supports automated abnormal flag generation, and ensures clini",
laboratory,order_processing,reference_range,test_catalog_id,test_catalog_id,Test Catalog Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,laboratory.test_catalog.test_catalog_id,,,reference_data,Foreign key linking to laboratory.test_catalog. Business justification: Reference ranges are defined FOR specific tests in the catalog. Currently reference_range has test_code/test_name but no FK to test_catalog. Business reality: reference ranges are test-specific and sh,
laboratory,order_processing,reference_range,age_group,age_group,Patient Age Group,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"Age group or age range for which this reference range applies (e.g., Neonate, Infant, Child, Adolescent, Adult, Geriatric, or specific age ranges like 0-1 years, 1-12 years, 18-65 years). Reference ranges are age-dependent for many tests.",
laboratory,order_processing,reference_range,alert_priority,alert_priority,Alert Priority Level,STRING,,,,routine|urgent|critical|stat,reference_data,Priority level for clinical alerts triggered when results fall outside this reference range. Critical priority requires immediate notification within minutes; urgent within hours; routine for next business day review.,
laboratory,order_processing,reference_range,alert_trigger_flag,alert_trigger_flag,Alert Trigger Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,reference_data,Indicates whether results outside this reference range should trigger automated clinical alerts or notifications. True for critical value ranges requiring immediate provider notification per Joint Commission requirements.,
laboratory,order_processing,reference_range,clinical_significance,clinical_significance,Clinical Significance,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"Clinical interpretation guidance describing the significance of values outside this reference range. Provides context for clinicians interpreting abnormal results (e.g., elevated values may indicate infection, dehydration, or malignancy).",
laboratory,order_processing,reference_range,created_timestamp,created_timestamp,Record Created Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,reference_data,Timestamp when this reference range record was first created in the system. Supports audit trail and data lineage tracking.,
laboratory,order_processing,reference_range,critical_high_threshold,critical_high_threshold,Critical High Threshold,"DECIMAL(18,6)",,,,,reference_data,The critical high value threshold (panic value) above which immediate clinical notification is required. Represents life-threatening high values requiring urgent intervention.,
laboratory,order_processing,reference_range,critical_low_threshold,critical_low_threshold,Critical Low Threshold,"DECIMAL(18,6)",,,,,reference_data,The critical low value threshold (panic value) below which immediate clinical notification is required. Represents life-threatening low values requiring urgent intervention.,
laboratory,order_processing,reference_range,effective_end_date,effective_end_date,Effective End Date,DATE,,,,,reference_data,The date through which this reference range remains valid. Null indicates the range is currently active with no planned end date. Supports historical tracking and periodic review requirements.,
laboratory,order_processing,reference_range,effective_start_date,effective_start_date,Effective Start Date,DATE,,,,,reference_data,The date from which this reference range becomes valid and should be used for result interpretation. Supports versioning of reference ranges over time.,
laboratory,order_processing,reference_range,instrument_platform,instrument_platform,Instrument Platform,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"Specific laboratory instrument or analyzer platform for which this reference range is validated (e.g., Roche Cobas, Abbott Architect, Siemens Atellica). Different platforms may require different reference ranges.",
laboratory,order_processing,reference_range,interpretation_code,interpretation_code,Interpretation Code,STRING,,,,normal|low|high|critical_low|critical_high|abnormal,reference_data,Standardized code used by result interpretation logic to assign abnormal flags when test results fall outside this reference range. Maps to HL7 observation interpretation codes.,
laboratory,order_processing,reference_range,last_review_date,last_review_date,Last Review Date,DATE,,,,,reference_data,Date when this reference range was last reviewed and validated by the laboratory medical director or quality team. CLIA and CAP require periodic review of reference ranges at least annually or when methodology changes.,
laboratory,order_processing,reference_range,last_updated_timestamp,last_updated_timestamp,Record Last Updated Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,reference_data,Timestamp when this reference range record was last modified. Supports change tracking and audit compliance.,
laboratory,order_processing,reference_range,lis_system_code,lis_system_code,Laboratory Information System (LIS) System Code,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"Internal system code or identifier used by the Laboratory Information System (Epic Beaker, Cerner PathNet) to reference this range in result interpretation logic and reporting.",
laboratory,order_processing,reference_range,lower_normal_limit,lower_normal_limit,Lower Normal Limit,"DECIMAL(18,6)",,,,,reference_data,The lower boundary of the normal reference range. Values below this threshold are typically flagged as low or abnormal.,
laboratory,order_processing,reference_range,medical_director_override_flag,medical_director_override_flag,Medical Director Override Flag,BOOLEAN,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii",,reference_data,Indicates whether this reference range represents an institutional medical director override of standard published ranges. True if the laboratory medical director has approved a deviation from manufacturer or published ranges based on local population characteristics.,
laboratory,order_processing,reference_range,methodology,methodology,Laboratory Test Methodology,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"The analytical method or instrument platform used to establish this reference range (e.g., Spectrophotometry, Immunoassay, Mass Spectrometry, PCR). Reference ranges may vary by methodology for the same test.",
laboratory,order_processing,reference_range,next_review_date,next_review_date,Next Scheduled Review Date,DATE,,,,,reference_data,Scheduled date for the next periodic review of this reference range. Supports compliance with CLIA and CAP requirements for annual review and documentation.,
laboratory,order_processing,reference_range,notes,notes,Reference Range Notes,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"Additional notes, comments, or special instructions related to this reference range. May include information about interfering substances, pre-analytical requirements, or special patient populations.",
laboratory,order_processing,reference_range,override_justification,override_justification,Override Justification,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"Clinical justification and documentation for medical director override of standard reference ranges. Required when medical_director_override_flag is true. Includes rationale, supporting data, and approval documentation.",
laboratory,order_processing,reference_range,population_basis,population_basis,Reference Population Basis,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"Description of the reference population used to establish this range (e.g., healthy adult volunteers, local patient population, manufacturer validation study). Documents the basis for the reference interval per CLSI guidelines.",
laboratory,order_processing,reference_range,pregnancy_status,pregnancy_status,Pregnancy Status,STRING,,,,pregnant|not_pregnant|not_applicable|unknown,reference_data,"Pregnancy status for which this reference range applies. Certain laboratory values have distinct reference ranges during pregnancy (e.g., thyroid function tests, hemoglobin).",
laboratory,order_processing,reference_range,race_ethnicity,race_ethnicity,Race and Ethnicity,STRING,,,"dbx_confidential, dbx_pii",,reference_data,"Race or ethnicity group for which this reference range applies, when clinically validated differences exist (e.g., creatinine clearance adjustments for African American patients). Only populated when evidence-based clinical guidelines support race-specific ranges.",
laboratory,order_processing,reference_range,review_status,review_status,Review Status,STRING,,,,current|pending_review|under_revision|retired,reference_data,Current review and approval status of this reference range. Tracks lifecycle state for quality management and compliance purposes.,
laboratory,order_processing,reference_range,sample_size,sample_size,Reference Population Sample Size,INT,,,,,reference_data,Number of individuals in the reference population used to establish this range. CLSI recommends minimum 120 samples for robust reference intervals. Documents statistical validity of the range.,
laboratory,order_processing,reference_range,sex,sex,Patient Sex,STRING,,,,male|female|all|unknown,reference_data,"Biological sex for which this reference range applies. Many laboratory tests have sex-specific reference ranges (e.g., hemoglobin, creatinine).",
laboratory,order_processing,reference_range,source_citation,source_citation,Source Citation,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"Detailed citation or reference to the authoritative source document (e.g., CAP guideline version, manufacturer package insert identifier, peer-reviewed journal article, institutional policy document). Required for CLIA compliance and periodic review.",
laboratory,order_processing,reference_range,source_type,source_type,Reference Range Source Type,STRING,,,,cap|clia|manufacturer|institutional|peer_reviewed,reference_data,The type of authoritative source from which this reference range was derived. CLIA requires documentation of reference range sources.,
laboratory,order_processing,reference_range,statistical_method,statistical_method,Statistical Method,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"Statistical method used to calculate the reference interval (e.g., parametric 95% confidence interval, non-parametric percentile method, robust method). Documents the analytical approach per CLSI standards.",
laboratory,order_processing,reference_range,unit_of_measure,unit_of_measure,Unit of Measure (UOM),STRING,,,,,reference_data,"The standardized unit of measure for the reference range values (e.g., mg/dL, mmol/L, g/dL, cells/mcL, IU/L). Must match the unit used in test results for proper interpretation.",
laboratory,order_processing,reference_range,upper_normal_limit,upper_normal_limit,Upper Normal Limit,"DECIMAL(18,6)",,,,,reference_data,The upper boundary of the normal reference range. Values above this threshold are typically flagged as high or abnormal.,
