laboratory,order_processing,specimen,employee_id,employee_id,Collector Identifier,BIGINT,,workforce.employee.employee_id,"dbx_confidential, dbx_pii",,master_data,Identifier of the healthcare provider or phlebotomist who collected the specimen. Supports chain of custody and quality tracking.,
laboratory,order_processing,specimen,lab_order_id,lab_order_id,Order Identifier,BIGINT,,laboratory.lab_order.lab_order_id,,,master_data,Identifier of the clinical order that requested the laboratory tests for which this specimen was collected. Links specimen to ordering workflow.,
laboratory,order_processing,specimen,mpi_record_id,mpi_record_id,Patient Identifier,BIGINT,,patient.mpi_record.mpi_record_id,,,master_data,Unique identifier of the patient from whom the specimen was collected. Links specimen to patient master record.,
laboratory,order_processing,specimen,parent_specimen_id,parent_specimen_id,Parent Specimen Identifier,BIGINT,,laboratory.specimen.specimen_id,,,master_data,Identifier of the parent specimen if this specimen is an aliquot or derivative. Supports specimen lineage tracking.,
laboratory,order_processing,specimen,scheduling_appointment_id,scheduling_appointment_id,Scheduling Appointment Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,scheduling.scheduling_appointment.scheduling_appointment_id,,,master_data,"Foreign key linking to scheduling.scheduling_appointment. Business justification: Specimens collected during scheduled appointments require linkage for workflow tracking, collection verification, and no-show reconciliation. Critical for outpatient phlebotomy operations where patien",
laboratory,order_processing,specimen,training_id,training_id,Training Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,compliance.training.training_id,,,master_data,Foreign key linking to compliance.training. Business justification: Specimen collection and handling requires documented competency training per CLIA. Healthcare operations link specimens to training records for quality investigations and competency verification durin,
laboratory,order_processing,specimen,visit_id,visit_id,Visit Identifier,BIGINT,,encounter.visit.visit_id,,,master_data,Identifier of the clinical encounter or visit during which the specimen was collected. Provides clinical context and billing linkage.,
laboratory,order_processing,specimen,accession_datetime,accession_datetime,Accession Date and Time,TIMESTAMP,,,,,master_data,Date and time when the specimen was received and accessioned into the Laboratory Information System (LIS). Marks the beginning of laboratory custody and processing.,
laboratory,order_processing,specimen,accession_number,accession_number,Accession Number,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Laboratory Information System (LIS) assigned unique work-unit identifier for the specimen. This is the operational identity in Epic Beaker and Cerner PathNet, used to track the specimen through the laboratory workflow from receipt through testing and disposal.",
laboratory,order_processing,specimen,accession_status,accession_status,Accession Status,STRING,,,,received|processing|resulted|archived|rejected,master_data,Current lifecycle status of the specimen in the laboratory workflow. Tracks progression from receipt through testing to final disposition.,
laboratory,order_processing,specimen,biohazard_level,biohazard_level,Biohazard Level,STRING,,,,standard|high_risk|unknown,master_data,Biohazard risk classification of the specimen based on known or suspected infectious agents. Determines safety precautions and handling protocols.,
laboratory,order_processing,specimen,chain_of_custody_status,chain_of_custody_status,Chain of Custody Status,STRING,,,,intact|broken|not_applicable,master_data,"Indicates whether the chain of custody has been maintained throughout specimen handling. Critical for forensic, toxicology, and legal specimens.",
laboratory,order_processing,specimen,collection_datetime,collection_datetime,Collection Date and Time,TIMESTAMP,,,,,master_data,Date and time when the specimen was collected from the patient. Critical for time-sensitive tests and stability assessments.,
laboratory,order_processing,specimen,collection_duration_minutes,collection_duration_minutes,Collection Duration (Minutes),INT,,,,,master_data,Duration of specimen collection in minutes. Relevant for timed collections such as 24-hour urine or glucose tolerance tests.,
laboratory,order_processing,specimen,collection_method,collection_method,Collection Method,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Technique or procedure used to collect the specimen (e.g., venipuncture, clean catch, biopsy, swab). Critical for quality assessment and result interpretation.",
laboratory,order_processing,specimen,collector_role,collector_role,Collector Role,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Professional role or title of the person who collected the specimen (e.g., phlebotomist, registered nurse, physician). Provides context for collection quality and training requirements.",
laboratory,order_processing,specimen,comments,comments,Specimen Comments,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Free-text comments or notes about the specimen, collection circumstances, or quality observations. Provides additional context for laboratory staff and clinicians.",
laboratory,order_processing,specimen,condition_at_receipt,condition_at_receipt,Condition at Receipt,STRING,,,,acceptable|hemolyzed|clotted|insufficient|contaminated|unlabeled,master_data,Assessment of specimen quality and integrity upon receipt at the laboratory. Documents any pre-analytical issues that may affect test results.,
laboratory,order_processing,specimen,container_type,container_type,Container Type,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Type of collection container or tube used (e.g., red top, lavender top EDTA, sterile cup). Determines appropriate tests and handling requirements.",
laboratory,order_processing,specimen,created_datetime,created_datetime,Record Created Date and Time,TIMESTAMP,,,,,master_data,Date and time when this specimen record was first created in the system. Supports audit trail and data lineage tracking.,
