laboratory,order_processing,test_catalog,last_updated_timestamp,last_updated_timestamp,Last Updated Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,reference_data,Timestamp when this test catalog entry was last modified. Supports audit trail and change tracking for regulatory compliance.,
laboratory,order_processing,test_catalog,methodology,methodology,Laboratory Test Methodology,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"Analytical method or technology used to perform the test (e.g., immunoassay, PCR, mass spectrometry, flow cytometry, enzymatic assay, culture). Important for result interpretation and quality control.",
laboratory,order_processing,test_catalog,minimum_volume,minimum_volume,Minimum Specimen Volume,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"Minimum volume of specimen required to perform the test, typically expressed with units (e.g., 2 mL, 5 mL, 0.5 mL). Critical for specimen adequacy assessment.",
laboratory,order_processing,test_catalog,orderable_flag,orderable_flag,Orderable Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,reference_data,"Indicates whether this test is currently available for ordering by clinicians through CPOE (Computerized Physician Order Entry) systems. False for retired, suspended, or component-only tests.",
laboratory,order_processing,test_catalog,orderable_status,orderable_status,Orderable Status,STRING,,,,active|inactive|suspended|retired|pending_validation,reference_data,Current lifecycle status of the test in the catalog. Active tests are available for ordering; inactive/retired tests are no longer available; suspended tests are temporarily unavailable; pending validation tests are under review.,
laboratory,order_processing,test_catalog,ordering_instructions,ordering_instructions,Ordering Instructions,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"Special instructions or requirements for ordering this test, including patient preparation (e.g., fasting required, medication restrictions), timing considerations, or authorization requirements.",
laboratory,order_processing,test_catalog,panic_value_flag,panic_value_flag,Panic Value Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,reference_data,Indicates whether this test can produce panic or critical values requiring immediate clinical notification and documentation of provider acknowledgment.,
laboratory,order_processing,test_catalog,patient_preparation,patient_preparation,Patient Preparation Requirements,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"Specific patient preparation requirements prior to specimen collection (e.g., 8-hour fast, discontinue medications, timed collection, dietary restrictions). Critical for accurate test results.",
laboratory,order_processing,test_catalog,performing_lab_location,performing_lab_location,Performing Laboratory Location,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"Name or identifier of the laboratory location or section that performs this test (e.g., Main Hospital Lab - Chemistry, Regional Reference Lab, Point of Care Testing). Indicates internal vs external testing.",
laboratory,order_processing,test_catalog,preferred_volume,preferred_volume,Preferred Specimen Volume,STRING,,,,,reference_data,Preferred or optimal volume of specimen for best test performance and to allow for repeat testing if needed.,
laboratory,order_processing,test_catalog,reference_lab_code,reference_lab_code,Reference Laboratory Test Code,STRING,,,,,reference_data,Test code used by the external reference laboratory for ordering and tracking. Used for send-out test routing and result reconciliation.,
