laboratory,order_processing,test_catalog,result_type,result_type,Laboratory Result Type,STRING,,,,quantitative|qualitative|semi_quantitative|narrative|culture|microscopic,reference_data,"Type of result produced by the test: quantitative (numeric with units), qualitative (positive/negative/detected), semi-quantitative (titers, grades), narrative (free text interpretation), culture results, or microscopic findings.",
laboratory,order_processing,test_catalog,specimen_container,specimen_container,Specimen Container Type,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"Type of collection container or tube required (e.g., red top, lavender top EDTA, green top heparin, yellow top ACD, sterile container). Includes tube color and additive information.",
laboratory,order_processing,test_catalog,specimen_stability,specimen_stability,Specimen Stability Duration,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"Duration for which the specimen remains stable under specified storage conditions before testing must be performed (e.g., 24 hours at room temperature, 7 days refrigerated).",
laboratory,order_processing,test_catalog,specimen_type,specimen_type,Specimen Type,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"Type of biological specimen required for the test (e.g., blood, serum, plasma, urine, CSF, tissue, swab). Critical for specimen collection and handling.",
laboratory,order_processing,test_catalog,storage_temperature,storage_temperature,Specimen Storage Temperature,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"Required storage temperature for the specimen prior to testing (e.g., room temperature, refrigerated 2-8°C, frozen -20°C, frozen -80°C). Critical for specimen stability.",
laboratory,order_processing,test_catalog,test_abbreviation,test_abbreviation,Laboratory Test Abbreviation,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"Short abbreviation or mnemonic for the test used in clinical documentation and reporting (e.g., CBC, BMP, CMP, TSH).",
laboratory,order_processing,test_catalog,test_category,test_category,Laboratory Test Category,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"High-level classification of the test by laboratory discipline or department (e.g., chemistry, hematology, microbiology, immunology, molecular diagnostics, anatomic pathology). [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: chemistry|hematology|microbiology|immunology|molecular|pathology|blood_bank|coagulation|toxicology|urinalysis — 10 candidates stripped; promote to reference product]",
laboratory,order_processing,test_catalog,test_code,test_code,Laboratory Test Code,STRING,,,,,reference_data,Internal laboratory test code used for ordering and identification within the Laboratory Information System (LIS). Unique business identifier for the test or panel.,
laboratory,order_processing,test_catalog,test_name,test_name,Laboratory Test Name,STRING,,,,,reference_data,Full descriptive name of the laboratory test or panel as displayed to clinicians and in order entry systems.,
laboratory,order_processing,test_catalog,test_type,test_type,Laboratory Test Type,STRING,,,,individual_test|panel|profile|reflex_test|add_on_test,reference_data,"Indicates whether this catalog entry represents an individual test, a panel (group of related tests), a profile, a reflex test (automatically triggered based on results), or an add-on test.",
laboratory,order_processing,test_catalog,transport_conditions,transport_conditions,Specimen Transport Conditions,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"Special transport requirements for the specimen (e.g., transport on ice, ambient temperature, protect from light, transport immediately). Ensures specimen integrity during transport.",
laboratory,order_processing,test_catalog,turnaround_time_routine,turnaround_time_routine,Routine Turnaround Time (TAT),STRING,,,,,reference_data,"Expected turnaround time for routine test orders from specimen receipt to result availability, typically expressed in hours or days (e.g., 4 hours, 24 hours, 3-5 days).",
laboratory,order_processing,test_catalog,turnaround_time_stat,turnaround_time_stat,STAT Turnaround Time (TAT),STRING,,,,,reference_data,"Expected turnaround time for STAT (urgent) test orders requiring expedited processing, typically expressed in minutes or hours (e.g., 30 minutes, 1 hour, 2 hours).",
laboratory,order_processing,test_catalog,unit_of_measure,unit_of_measure,Unit of Measure,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"Standard unit of measure for quantitative test results (e.g., mg/dL, mmol/L, IU/mL, cells/mcL, %). Aligned with UCUM (Unified Code for Units of Measure) standards.",
laboratory,order_processing,test_coverage_policy,test_coverage_policy_id,test_coverage_policy_id,Test Coverage Policy Identifier,BIGINT,Y,,,,association_data,Unique identifier for this test-policy coverage determination record. Primary key.,
