order,fulfillment_routing,referral_order,disposition_notes,disposition_notes,Referral Disposition Notes,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Free-text notes from the receiving provider or care coordinator documenting the reason for the referral disposition, particularly for declined or cancelled referrals. Supports clinical documentation improvement (CDI) and care coordination workflows.",
order,fulfillment_routing,referral_order,effective_date,effective_date,Referral Effective Date,DATE,,,,,transactional_data,The date on which the referral authorization becomes valid and the patient may begin receiving referred services. Typically the date the authorization was approved by the payer.,
order,fulfillment_routing,referral_order,expiration_date,expiration_date,Referral Expiration Date,DATE,,,,,transactional_data,The date after which the referral authorization is no longer valid and services cannot be rendered under this referral. Triggers re-authorization workflows and patient outreach when approaching expiry.,
order,fulfillment_routing,referral_order,first_available_date,first_available_date,Specialist First Available Appointment Date,DATE,,,,,transactional_data,The earliest available appointment date offered by the receiving provider at the time the referral was processed. Used to measure access to specialty care and network adequacy.,
order,fulfillment_routing,referral_order,is_stat_order,is_stat_order,STAT Order Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,Indicates whether the referral order was placed as a STAT (immediate/urgent) order requiring expedited processing and scheduling. Distinct from urgency_level as this is the operational flag used by scheduling and authorization workflows.,
order,fulfillment_routing,referral_order,loop_closed_date,loop_closed_date,Referral Loop Closed Date,DATE,,,,,transactional_data,"The date on which the referral communication loop was closed, meaning the referring provider received the specialists consultation report or outcome documentation.",
order,fulfillment_routing,referral_order,mrn,mrn,Medical Record Number (MRN),STRING,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_identifier",,transactional_data,The patients Medical Record Number (MRN) as assigned by the facilitys Master Patient Index (MPI). Included on the referral for cross-system patient identification and payer submission.,
order,fulfillment_routing,referral_order,order_placed_timestamp,order_placed_timestamp,Referral Order Placed Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,The date and time when the referring provider placed the referral order via Computerized Physician Order Entry (CPOE) in the Electronic Health Record (EHR). This is the principal business event timestamp for the referral lifecycle.,
order,fulfillment_routing,referral_order,order_source_system,order_source_system,Order Source System,STRING,,,,Epic|Cerner|MEDITECH|Salesforce|manual,transactional_data,"The operational system of record from which the referral order was originated or ingested into the lakehouse. Supports data lineage, reconciliation, and multi-system integration auditing.",
order,fulfillment_routing,referral_order,order_status,order_status,Referral Order Status,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,Current workflow lifecycle state of the referral order. Drives downstream processing in Salesforce Health Cloud and Epic Orders. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: pending|active|accepted|declined|completed|cancelled|expired — promote to reference product],
order,fulfillment_routing,referral_order,plan_type,plan_type,Health Plan Type,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,The type of health insurance plan governing the referral authorization requirements. HMO and POS plans typically require referrals; PPO plans may not. Drives authorization workflow logic. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: HMO|PPO|POS|EPO|Medicare|Medicaid|self_pay — 7 candidates stripped; promote to reference product],
order,fulfillment_routing,referral_order,receiving_facility_name,receiving_facility_name,Receiving Facility Name,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,Name of the external facility or organization where the referred services will be rendered. Captured when the receiving provider is affiliated with an external organization not in the internal provider master.,
order,fulfillment_routing,referral_order,receiving_provider_npi,receiving_provider_npi,Receiving Provider National Provider Identifier (NPI),STRING,,,,^[0-9]{10}$,transactional_data,The 10-digit National Provider Identifier (NPI) of the specialist or receiving provider to whom the patient is referred. Required for payer authorization and claims adjudication.,
order,fulfillment_routing,referral_order,referral_disposition,referral_disposition,Referral Disposition,STRING,,,,pending|accepted|declined|completed|cancelled|no_show,transactional_data,"The outcome or final disposition of the referral as reported by the receiving provider. Indicates whether the specialist accepted, declined, completed, or the patient did not attend. Used for referral loop closure tracking and quality reporting.",
order,fulfillment_routing,referral_order,referral_loop_closed,referral_loop_closed,Referral Loop Closed Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,"Indicates whether the referring provider has received and acknowledged the specialists consultation report, closing the referral communication loop. A key quality metric for NCQA HEDIS and PCMH accreditation.",
order,fulfillment_routing,referral_order,referral_number,referral_number,Referral Order Number,STRING,,,,^REF-[0-9]{10}$,transactional_data,"Externally visible, human-readable business identifier for the referral order. Used in payer communications, patient correspondence, and cross-system tracking (e.g., Salesforce Health Cloud, Epic Orders). Format: REF- followed by 10 digits.",
order,fulfillment_routing,referral_order,referral_reason_description,referral_reason_description,Referral Reason Description,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Free-text clinical narrative describing the reason for the referral, supplementing the ICD-10 code. Captures clinical context not fully expressed by the diagnosis code, such as symptom progression, treatment failure, or specific clinical question for the specialist.",
order,fulfillment_routing,referral_order,referral_source,referral_source,Referral Source,STRING,,,,PCP|ED|inpatient|specialist|self|care_program,transactional_data,"The clinical setting or care context from which the referral originated. Indicates whether the referral was initiated by a Primary Care Physician (PCP), Emergency Department (ED), inpatient unit, specialist, patient self-referral, or care program enrollment.",
order,fulfillment_routing,referral_order,referral_type,referral_type,Referral Type,STRING,,,,specialist|external_provider|care_program|second_opinion|diagnostic,transactional_data,"Categorizes the nature of the referral: to a specialist, external provider, care program, second opinion, or for a specific diagnostic workup. Used for operational routing and analytics segmentation.",
order,fulfillment_routing,referral_order,referring_provider_npi,referring_provider_npi,Referring Provider National Provider Identifier (NPI),STRING,,,,^[0-9]{10}$,transactional_data,The 10-digit National Provider Identifier (NPI) of the referring provider as registered with CMS. Required on CMS-1500 and UB-04 claim forms and payer authorization requests.,
order,fulfillment_routing,referral_order,scheduled_appointment_date,scheduled_appointment_date,Referred Appointment Scheduled Date,DATE,,,,,transactional_data,The date on which the patients appointment with the receiving specialist or provider has been scheduled. Used to measure time-to-appointment and referral fulfillment timeliness.,
order,fulfillment_routing,referral_order,updated_timestamp,updated_timestamp,Record Last Updated Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,Timestamp when the referral order record was last modified in the lakehouse Silver layer. Supports change detection and incremental processing.,
order,fulfillment_routing,referral_order,urgency_level,urgency_level,Referral Urgency Level,STRING,,,,routine|urgent|stat|emergent,transactional_data,"Clinical priority level assigned to the referral order by the referring provider. Drives scheduling priority at the receiving provider and payer authorization turnaround time requirements. Values: routine, urgent, stat, emergent.",
order,fulfillment_routing,referral_order,visits_used,visits_used,Referral Visits Used,INT,,,,,transactional_data,The number of authorized visits that have been consumed against this referral to date. Compared against authorized_visits to determine remaining utilization and trigger re-authorization alerts.,
