order,fulfillment_routing,therapy_order,laterality,laterality,Laterality,STRING,,,,left|right|bilateral,Master,"Indicates whether the therapy is focused on the left side, right side, or both sides of the body.",
order,fulfillment_routing,therapy_order,order_datetime,order_datetime,Order Date and Time,TIMESTAMP,,,,,Master,The date and time when the therapy order was placed by the ordering provider. Principal business event timestamp.,
order,fulfillment_routing,therapy_order,order_mode,order_mode,Order Mode,STRING,,,,inpatient|outpatient|home_health|telehealth,Master,"The care setting or mode in which the therapy service will be delivered (e.g., inpatient, outpatient, home health, telehealth).",
order,fulfillment_routing,therapy_order,order_number,order_number,Therapy Order Number,STRING,,,,,Master,"Externally-known unique business identifier for the therapy order, used for tracking and communication across systems.",
order,fulfillment_routing,therapy_order,order_status,order_status,Therapy Order Status,STRING,,,,draft|active|on-hold|completed|cancelled|discontinued,Master,Current lifecycle status of the therapy order indicating its workflow state.,
order,fulfillment_routing,therapy_order,ordering_provider_npi,ordering_provider_npi,Ordering Provider National Provider Identifier (NPI),STRING,,,,,Master,National Provider Identifier of the provider who ordered the therapy service.,
order,fulfillment_routing,therapy_order,patient_instructions,patient_instructions,Patient Instructions,STRING,,,,,Master,"Instructions or guidance to be provided to the patient regarding the therapy service, such as preparation steps or what to expect.",
order,fulfillment_routing,therapy_order,priority,priority,Order Priority,STRING,,,,routine|urgent|stat|asap,Master,The urgency level of the therapy order indicating how quickly the service should be initiated.,
order,fulfillment_routing,therapy_order,sessions_completed,sessions_completed,Sessions Completed,INT,,,,,Master,The number of therapy sessions that have been completed to date.,
order,fulfillment_routing,therapy_order,sessions_remaining,sessions_remaining,Sessions Remaining,INT,,,,,Master,The number of therapy sessions remaining from the total authorized sessions.,
order,fulfillment_routing,therapy_order,source_system,source_system,Source System,STRING,,,,,Master,"The name or identifier of the source system from which the therapy order originated (e.g., Epic Orders, Cerner PowerChart).",
order,fulfillment_routing,therapy_order,source_system_order_reference,source_system_order_reference,Source System Order Identifier (ID),STRING,,,,,Master,"The unique identifier for this therapy order in the source system, used for traceability and reconciliation.",
order,fulfillment_routing,therapy_order,special_instructions,special_instructions,Special Instructions,STRING,,,,,Master,"Additional instructions or notes from the ordering provider regarding the therapy service delivery, precautions, or patient-specific considerations.",
order,fulfillment_routing,therapy_order,start_date,start_date,Therapy Start Date,DATE,,,,,Master,The date when the therapy service is scheduled to begin or when treatment should commence.,
order,fulfillment_routing,therapy_order,therapy_service_code,therapy_service_code,Therapy Service Code,STRING,,,,,Master,"Standardized code representing the specific therapy service ordered, typically from a clinical terminology system.",
order,fulfillment_routing,therapy_order,therapy_service_description,therapy_service_description,Therapy Service Description,STRING,,,,,Master,Human-readable description of the therapy service being ordered.,
order,fulfillment_routing,therapy_order,therapy_type,therapy_type,Therapy Type,STRING,,,,physical_therapy|occupational_therapy|speech_therapy|respiratory_therapy,Master,"The type of therapy service ordered: physical therapy, occupational therapy, speech therapy, or respiratory therapy.",
order,fulfillment_routing,therapy_order,total_sessions_ordered,total_sessions_ordered,Total Sessions Ordered,INT,,,,,Master,The total number of therapy sessions authorized or ordered for this treatment plan.,
order,fulfillment_routing,therapy_order,treatment_goal,treatment_goal,Treatment Goal,STRING,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii",,Master,"The intended therapeutic outcome or goal for the therapy service, such as improving mobility, restoring function, or enhancing communication.",
order,fulfillment_routing,therapy_order,updated_timestamp,updated_timestamp,Updated Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,Master,The date and time when this therapy order record was last modified or updated in the data platform.,
order,protocol_configuration,alert_rule,alert_rule_id,alert_rule_id,Alert Rule Identifier,BIGINT,Y,,,,master_data,Primary key for alert_rule,
order,protocol_configuration,alert_rule,alert_employee_id,alert_employee_id,Approved By User Employee Id,BIGINT,,workforce.employee.employee_id,"confidential,pii",,master_data,Identifier of the clinical or administrative user who approved this alert rule for production use.,
order,protocol_configuration,alert_rule,clinical_order_id,clinical_order_id,,BIGINT,,order.clinical_order.clinical_order_id,,,master_data,description,
order,protocol_configuration,alert_rule,parent_alert_rule_id,parent_alert_rule_id,Parent Alert Rule Id,BIGINT,,order.alert_rule.alert_rule_id,dbx_self_ref_fk,,master_data,Self-referencing FK on alert_rule (parent_alert_rule_id),
order,protocol_configuration,alert_rule,primary_employee_id,primary_employee_id,Employee Id,BIGINT,,workforce.employee.employee_id,"confidential,pii",,master_data,Identifier of the user or system account that created this alert rule record.,
order,protocol_configuration,alert_rule,alert_fatigue_risk_score,alert_fatigue_risk_score,Alert Fatigue Risk Score,"DECIMAL(5,2)",,,,,master_data,Calculated risk score (0-100) indicating likelihood this alert contributes to clinician alert fatigue based on fire frequency and override rate.,
order,protocol_configuration,alert_rule,alert_message_template,alert_message_template,Alert Message Template,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Standardized message text template displayed to clinicians when the alert fires, may include placeholders for dynamic values.",
order,protocol_configuration,alert_rule,approved_timestamp,approved_timestamp,Approved Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,master_data,Date and time when this alert rule was approved for activation in production systems.,
order,protocol_configuration,alert_rule,auto_dismiss_seconds,auto_dismiss_seconds,Auto Dismiss Seconds,INT,,,,,master_data,Number of seconds after which the alert automatically dismisses if not acknowledged. Null means no auto-dismiss.,
order,protocol_configuration,alert_rule,clinical_specialty_scope,clinical_specialty_scope,Clinical Specialty Scope,STRING,,,,,master_data,Comma-separated list of clinical specialties or departments where this rule is active. Empty means applies to all specialties.,
order,protocol_configuration,alert_rule,created_timestamp,created_timestamp,Created Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,master_data,Date and time when this alert rule record was first created in the system.,
order,protocol_configuration,alert_rule,display_priority,display_priority,Display Priority,INT,,,,,master_data,Numeric ranking used to determine display order when multiple alerts fire simultaneously. Lower numbers indicate higher priority.,
order,protocol_configuration,alert_rule,effective_end_date,effective_end_date,Effective End Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,Date when this alert rule is scheduled to be retired or deactivated. Null indicates no planned end date.,
order,protocol_configuration,alert_rule,effective_start_date,effective_start_date,Effective Start Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,Date when this alert rule becomes active and begins firing in production systems.,
order,protocol_configuration,alert_rule,evidence_source,evidence_source,Evidence Source,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Citation or reference to the clinical evidence, guideline, or regulatory requirement that justifies this alert rule.",
order,protocol_configuration,alert_rule,evidence_strength_level,evidence_strength_level,Evidence Strength Level,STRING,,,,,master_data,Classification of the strength of clinical evidence supporting this alert rule based on evidence-based medicine hierarchy.,
order,protocol_configuration,alert_rule,external_rule_code,external_rule_code,External Rule Code,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Identifier for this alert rule in the source operational system, used for system integration and reconciliation.",
order,protocol_configuration,alert_rule,fire_count_total,fire_count_total,Fire Count Total,BIGINT,,,,,master_data,"Cumulative number of times this alert rule has fired since activation, used for alert fatigue analysis.",
order,protocol_configuration,alert_rule,hard_stop_flag,hard_stop_flag,Hard Stop Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,Indicates whether this alert prevents order completion until resolved (hard stop) or is advisory only (soft stop).,
order,protocol_configuration,alert_rule,integration_system_code,integration_system_code,Integration System Code,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Code identifying the source clinical system where this alert rule is configured (e.g., Epic, Beaker, Radiant, Willow).",
order,protocol_configuration,alert_rule,last_modified_timestamp,last_modified_timestamp,Last Modified Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,master_data,Date and time when this alert rule record was last updated in the system.,
order,protocol_configuration,alert_rule,last_review_date,last_review_date,Last Review Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,Date when this alert rule was last reviewed for clinical accuracy and operational effectiveness.,
order,protocol_configuration,alert_rule,next_review_date,next_review_date,Next Review Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,Scheduled date for the next periodic review of this alert rule to ensure continued clinical relevance.,
order,protocol_configuration,alert_rule,notes,notes,Notes,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Free-text field for additional operational notes, implementation guidance, or historical context about this alert rule.",
order,protocol_configuration,alert_rule,order_type_scope,order_type_scope,Order Type Scope,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Comma-separated list of order types this rule applies to (e.g., medication, lab, radiology, procedure). Empty means applies to all order types.",
order,protocol_configuration,alert_rule,override_allowed_flag,override_allowed_flag,Override Allowed Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,Indicates whether clinicians are permitted to override or dismiss this alert without taking action.,
order,protocol_configuration,alert_rule,override_count_total,override_count_total,Override Count Total,BIGINT,,,,,master_data,"Cumulative number of times clinicians have overridden this alert, used to assess alert appropriateness.",
order,protocol_configuration,alert_rule,override_rate_percent,override_rate_percent,Override Rate Percent,"DECIMAL(5,2)",,,,,master_data,"Percentage of alert fires that resulted in clinician override, calculated as (override_count / fire_count) * 100.",
order,protocol_configuration,alert_rule,override_reason_required_flag,override_reason_required_flag,Override Reason Required Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,Indicates whether a documented reason is mandatory when a clinician overrides this alert.,
order,protocol_configuration,alert_rule,patient_population_filter,patient_population_filter,Patient Population Filter,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Criteria defining which patient populations this rule applies to (e.g., age range, gender, diagnosis codes). Empty means applies to all patients.",
order,protocol_configuration,alert_rule,recommended_action,recommended_action,Recommended Action,STRING,,,,,master_data,Clinical guidance or recommended action for the clinician to take when this alert is triggered.,
order,protocol_configuration,alert_rule,regulatory_requirement_flag,regulatory_requirement_flag,Regulatory Requirement Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,Indicates whether this alert rule is mandated by regulatory or accreditation requirements and cannot be disabled.,
order,protocol_configuration,alert_rule,review_frequency_months,review_frequency_months,Review Frequency Months,INT,,,,,master_data,Number of months between scheduled reviews of this alert rule for clinical and operational validation.,
order,protocol_configuration,alert_rule,rule_category,rule_category,Rule Category,STRING,,,,,master_data,Classification of the alert rule by clinical domain or purpose.,
order,protocol_configuration,alert_rule,rule_code,rule_code,Rule Code,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Unique business identifier code for the alert rule, used for external reference and system integration.",
order,protocol_configuration,alert_rule,rule_description,rule_description,Rule Description,STRING,,,,,master_data,Detailed clinical and operational description of what the alert rule detects and why it is important for patient safety.,
order,protocol_configuration,alert_rule,rule_name,rule_name,Rule Name,STRING,,,,,master_data,Human-readable name of the alert rule displayed to clinicians and administrators.,
order,protocol_configuration,alert_rule,rule_status,rule_status,Rule Status,STRING,,,,,master_data,Current lifecycle status of the alert rule indicating whether it is actively firing in production systems.,
order,protocol_configuration,alert_rule,severity_level,severity_level,Severity Level,STRING,,,,,master_data,Severity classification indicating the clinical urgency and required response level for the alert.,
order,protocol_configuration,alert_rule,trigger_condition,trigger_condition,Trigger Condition,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Business logic expression or criteria that must be met for the alert to fire, expressed in human-readable format.",
order,protocol_configuration,alert_rule,version_number,version_number,Version Number,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Semantic version number of this alert rule configuration, incremented with each modification.",
order,protocol_configuration,order_order_set,order_set_id,order_set_id,Order Set ID,BIGINT,Y,,,,,Unique surrogate identifier for the order set record in the lakehouse Silver layer. Primary key for the order_set data product.,
order,protocol_configuration,order_order_set,care_site_id,care_site_id,Facility ID,BIGINT,,facility.care_site.care_site_id,,,,Identifier of the healthcare facility or campus where this order set is deployed and available for use. Supports multi-facility health system deployments where order sets may be facility-specific or enterprise-wide.,
order,protocol_configuration,order_order_set,clinical_order_id,clinical_order_id,,BIGINT,,order.clinical_order.clinical_order_id,,,,description,
order,protocol_configuration,order_order_set,cms_measure_id,cms_measure_id,Centers for Medicare and Medicaid Services (CMS) Measure ID,BIGINT,,quality.measure.measure_id,,,,"CMS quality measure identifier associated with this order set when is_cms_core_measure is True (e.g., SEP-1, VTE-1, STK-1). Enables direct linkage to regulatory reporting requirements and Value-Based Purchasing (VBP) program metrics.",
order,protocol_configuration,order_order_set,compliance_policy_id,compliance_policy_id,Policy Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,compliance.compliance_policy.compliance_policy_id,,,,"Foreign key linking to compliance.policy. Business justification: Order sets implement clinical policies (antibiotic stewardship policy, opioid prescribing policy). Direct policy-to-protocol relationship ensures order sets enforce organizational standards and regula",
order,protocol_configuration,order_order_set,compliance_program_id,compliance_program_id,Compliance Program Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,compliance.compliance_program.compliance_program_id,,,,"Foreign key linking to compliance.compliance_program. Business justification: Order sets implement evidence-based protocols satisfying specific compliance programs (sepsis bundles for CMS SEP-1, VTE prophylaxis for Joint Commission). Direct link between clinical protocols and r",
order,protocol_configuration,order_order_set,consent_form_template_id,consent_form_template_id,Consent Form Template Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,consent.consent_form_template.consent_form_template_id,,,,"Foreign key linking to consent.consent_form_template. Business justification: Clinical order sets (surgical protocols, chemotherapy regimens) specify required consent forms. Protocol-driven consent management ensures correct consent template is presented when order set is activ",
order,protocol_configuration,order_order_set,default_appointment_type_id,default_appointment_type_id,Default Appointment Type Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,scheduling.appointment_type.appointment_type_id,,,,"Foreign key linking to scheduling.appointment_type. Business justification: Order sets designed for specific appointment types (annual wellness visit order set, pre-operative order set) standardize care delivery. Linking order sets to appointment types enables protocol-driven",
order,protocol_configuration,order_order_set,drg_id,drg_id,Drg Code Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,reference.drg.drg_id,,,,"Foreign key linking to reference.drg. Business justification: DRG-based order sets support case management, utilization review, and cost containment initiatives. Links protocol to DRG master for expected LOS management, resource utilization tracking, and bundled",
order,protocol_configuration,order_order_set,health_plan_id,health_plan_id,Health Plan Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,insurance.health_plan.health_plan_id,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii",,,"Foreign key linking to insurance.health_plan. Business justification: Health systems create plan-specific order sets for value-based care contracts, formulary compliance, and coverage optimization. Real-world process: clinical informatics teams build order sets aligned ",
order,protocol_configuration,order_order_set,icd_code_id,icd_code_id,Icd10 Trigger Code Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,reference.icd_code.icd_code_id,,,,"Foreign key linking to reference.icd_code. Business justification: Order set activation logic depends on diagnosis-driven protocol triggering. Links to ICD-10 master enables automated clinical pathway initiation, evidence-based care delivery, and quality measure comp",
order,protocol_configuration,order_order_set,primary_order_set_approved_by_provider_clinician_id,primary_order_set_approved_by_provider_clinician_id,Approved By Provider ID,BIGINT,,provider.clinician.clinician_id,,,,Identifier of the physician or clinical leader who formally approved the order set on behalf of the approving committee. Supports governance accountability and regulatory audit requirements.,
order,protocol_configuration,order_order_set,research_study_id,research_study_id,Research Study Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,research.research_study.research_study_id,,,,"Foreign key linking to research.research_study. Business justification: Research protocols often define standardized order sets for study visits (baseline labs, imaging sequences, assessments). Linking order_set to research_study supports protocol adherence, study-specifi",
order,protocol_configuration,order_order_set,specialty_id,specialty_id,Specialty Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,provider.specialty.specialty_id,,,,"Foreign key linking to provider.specialty. Business justification: Order sets are specialty-specific clinical protocols (cardiology admission order sets, oncology treatment pathways). Healthcare organizations maintain specialty-based order set libraries, track specia",
order,protocol_configuration,order_order_set,approval_date,approval_date,Order Set Approval Date,DATE,,,,,,Date on which the approving clinical committee formally approved the current version of the order set. Establishes the official governance record for audit and regulatory reporting purposes.,
order,protocol_configuration,order_order_set,approval_status,approval_status,Order Set Approval Status,STRING,,,,draft|pending_review|approved|retired|suspended,,Current approval workflow status of the order set within the clinical governance process. Drives whether the order set is available for provider use in CPOE. draft = under development; pending_review = submitted to approving committee; approved = active and available; retired = superseded; suspended = temporarily withdrawn.,
order,protocol_configuration,order_order_set,approving_committee,approving_committee,Approving Clinical Committee,STRING,,,,,,"Name of the clinical governance committee or body responsible for reviewing and approving the order set (e.g., Pharmacy and Therapeutics Committee, Medical Executive Committee, Clinical Quality Council). Required for Joint Commission accreditation and CMS Conditions of Participation compliance.",
order,protocol_configuration,order_order_set,care_pathway_name,care_pathway_name,Associated Care Pathway Name,STRING,,,,,,"Name of the clinical care pathway or protocol bundle with which this order set is associated (e.g., Sepsis Care Pathway, Hip Replacement Enhanced Recovery After Surgery (ERAS) Pathway). Links the executable order bundle to the broader clinical protocol framework.",
order,protocol_configuration,order_order_set,care_setting,care_setting,Applicable Care Setting,STRING,,,,inpatient|outpatient|emergency|icu|surgical|observation,,Clinical care setting in which the order set is intended to be used. Restricts order set availability to appropriate clinical contexts within the EHR. inpatient = admitted patients; outpatient = clinic/ambulatory; emergency = Emergency Department (ED); icu = Intensive Care Unit (ICU); surgical = Operating Room (OR)/perioperative; observation = observation status.,
order,protocol_configuration,order_order_set,clinical_indication,clinical_indication,Clinical Indication,STRING,,,,,,"Free-text or structured description of the clinical condition, diagnosis, or scenario that triggers activation of this order set (e.g., Suspected sepsis with organ dysfunction, Acute ST-elevation myocardial infarction). Complements the ICD-10 trigger code.",
order,protocol_configuration,order_order_set,compliance_rate_pct,compliance_rate_pct,Order Set Compliance Rate Percentage,"DECIMAL(5,2)",,,,,,"Percentage of triggered clinical scenarios where the order set was activated by providers, as reported by the EHR analytics module. Sourced from Epic reporting or Cerner analytics — not computed in the lakehouse. Supports HEDIS, MIPS, and VBP quality measure reporting.",
order,protocol_configuration,order_order_set,created_timestamp,created_timestamp,Record Created Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,,"Timestamp when the order set record was first created in the source system or lakehouse. Supports audit trail requirements per HIPAA Security Rule, Joint Commission, and HIM governance policies.",
order,protocol_configuration,order_order_set,effective_date,effective_date,Order Set Effective Date,DATE,,,,,,Date on which the order set version becomes clinically effective and available for provider use in CPOE. Aligns with the approved go-live date established by the governing clinical committee.,
order,protocol_configuration,order_order_set,evidence_level,evidence_level,Evidence Level,STRING,,,,A|B|C|D|expert_consensus,,"Strength of clinical evidence supporting the order set, using standard evidence grading. A = strong evidence from multiple randomized controlled trials; B = moderate evidence; C = limited evidence; D = very limited evidence; expert_consensus = based on expert opinion in absence of trials. Supports quality measurement and regulatory reporting.",
order,protocol_configuration,order_order_set,expiration_date,expiration_date,Order Set Expiration Date,DATE,,,,,,Date on which the order set version expires and is no longer valid for clinical use. Null indicates no scheduled expiration. Triggers mandatory review workflow when approaching expiration per clinical governance policy.,
order,protocol_configuration,order_order_set,fhir_plan_definition_reference,fhir_plan_definition_reference,Fast Healthcare Interoperability Resources (FHIR) PlanDefinition ID,STRING,,,,,,"HL7 FHIR PlanDefinition resource identifier corresponding to this order set, enabling interoperability with Health Information Exchange (HIE) platforms and external clinical decision support systems. Aligns with HL7 FHIR R4 PlanDefinition resource.",
order,protocol_configuration,order_order_set,governance_level,governance_level,Protocol Governance Level,STRING,,,,guideline|consensus|regulatory_mandate,,"Classification of the governance authority underpinning the order set protocol. guideline = based on published clinical practice guidelines; consensus = based on institutional expert consensus without external guideline; regulatory_mandate = required by CMS, Joint Commission, or other regulatory body (e.g., CMS Core Measures, EMTALA requirements).",
order,protocol_configuration,order_order_set,guideline_reference,guideline_reference,Evidence-Based Guideline Reference,STRING,,,,,,"Citation or reference to the external clinical practice guideline, systematic review, or regulatory mandate that underpins the order set (e.g., Surviving Sepsis Campaign 2021 Guidelines, AHA/ACC STEMI Management Guidelines 2023, CMS Sepsis Core Measure SEP-1). Supports clinical documentation improvement (CDI) and regulatory compliance.",
order,protocol_configuration,order_order_set,includes_lab_orders,includes_lab_orders,Includes Laboratory Orders Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,,Indicates whether the order set bundle contains laboratory orders routed to Beaker (LIS) or equivalent Laboratory Information System (LIS). True = lab orders present; False = no lab orders included.,
order,protocol_configuration,order_order_set,includes_pharmacy_orders,includes_pharmacy_orders,Includes Pharmacy Orders Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,,Indicates whether the order set bundle contains medication orders routed to Willow (pharmacy) or equivalent pharmacy system. True = pharmacy/medication orders present; False = no pharmacy orders included. Relevant for DEA controlled substance tracking.,
order,protocol_configuration,order_order_set,includes_radiology_orders,includes_radiology_orders,Includes Radiology Orders Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,,Indicates whether the order set bundle contains radiology/imaging orders routed to Radiant (RIS) or equivalent Radiology Information System (RIS). True = radiology orders present; False = no radiology orders included.,
order,protocol_configuration,order_order_set,includes_referral_orders,includes_referral_orders,Includes Referral Orders Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,,Indicates whether the order set bundle contains referral orders to specialists or ancillary services. True = referral orders present; False = no referral orders included. Supports care coordination and transitions of care workflows.,
order,protocol_configuration,order_order_set,is_active,is_active,Order Set Active Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,,Indicates whether the order set is currently active and available for selection in the CPOE workflow. True = active and selectable by providers; False = inactive and hidden from the order entry interface. Distinct from approval_status — an approved order set may be temporarily deactivated without retiring it.,
order,protocol_configuration,order_order_set,is_cms_core_measure,is_cms_core_measure,Centers for Medicare and Medicaid Services (CMS) Core Measure Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,,"Indicates whether this order set is directly associated with a CMS Core Measure or quality reporting requirement (e.g., SEP-1 Sepsis Bundle, VTE Prophylaxis). True = linked to a CMS Core Measure; False = not a CMS Core Measure order set. Supports quality measurement and regulatory reporting.",
order,protocol_configuration,order_order_set,is_hipaa_sensitive,is_hipaa_sensitive,Health Insurance Portability and Accountability Act (HIPAA) Sensitive Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,,"Indicates whether the order set is associated with HIPAA-sensitive clinical categories requiring enhanced access controls (e.g., behavioral health, substance use disorder, HIV/AIDS, reproductive health). True = sensitive category requiring additional PHI protections; False = standard clinical order set.",
order,protocol_configuration,order_order_set,last_review_date,last_review_date,Last Clinical Review Date,DATE,,,,,,"Date of the most recent clinical review of the order set, regardless of whether a version change resulted. Supports mandatory periodic review cycles (typically annual) required by Joint Commission and institutional policy.",
order,protocol_configuration,order_order_set,next_review_date,next_review_date,Next Scheduled Review Date,DATE,,,,,,Date by which the next mandatory clinical review of the order set must be completed. Drives governance workflow alerts and ensures compliance with periodic review requirements per Joint Commission and institutional policy.,
order,protocol_configuration,order_order_set,order_count,order_count,Order Count,INT,,,,,,"Total number of individual clinical orders (lab, radiology, pharmacy, nursing, referral) included in the order set bundle. Provides a quick indicator of order set complexity and scope for provider review.",
order,protocol_configuration,order_order_set,order_set_code,order_set_code,Order Set Code,STRING,,,,,,"Externally-known alphanumeric code uniquely identifying the order set within the source system (e.g., Epic Orders catalog ID or Cerner Millennium order set mnemonic). Used for cross-system referencing and integration with Beaker (LIS), Radiant (RIS), and Willow (pharmacy).",
order,protocol_configuration,order_order_set,order_set_description,order_set_description,Order Set Description,STRING,,,,,,"Detailed narrative description of the order sets clinical purpose, intended patient population, and scope of included orders. Supports clinical documentation improvement (CDI) and provider education.",
order,protocol_configuration,order_order_set,order_set_name,order_set_name,Order Set Name,STRING,,,,,,"Human-readable name of the pre-defined, evidence-based order set bundle as displayed in the Computerized Physician Order Entry (CPOE) interface (e.g., Sepsis Bundle — Adult ICU, Community-Acquired Pneumonia Admission Orders).",
order,protocol_configuration,order_order_set,order_set_type,order_set_type,Order Set Type,STRING,,,,admission|discharge|procedure|condition|preventive|transition,,Classification of the order set by its clinical purpose in the care continuum. admission = admission orders bundle; discharge = discharge planning orders; procedure = pre/intra/post-procedure orders; condition = condition-specific management bundle; preventive = preventive care protocol; transition = transitions of care orders.,
order,protocol_configuration,order_order_set,owning_department,owning_department,Owning Clinical Department,STRING,,,,,,"Name of the clinical department or service line that owns and is responsible for maintaining the order set (e.g., Department of Cardiology, Emergency Medicine, Pharmacy). Establishes accountability for content governance and periodic review.",
order,protocol_configuration,order_order_set,population_age_group,population_age_group,Target Population Age Group,STRING,,,,pediatric|adult|geriatric|neonatal|all,,Target patient age group for which the order set is clinically appropriate. Restricts order set availability to appropriate patient populations in CPOE. pediatric = patients under 18; adult = 18-64; geriatric = 65+; neonatal = newborns; all = all age groups.,
order,protocol_configuration,order_order_set,renal_adjustment_required,renal_adjustment_required,Renal Dose Adjustment Required Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,,"Indicates whether the order set contains medications requiring renal function-based dose adjustments (e.g., creatinine clearance-based dosing). True = renal adjustment logic embedded; False = no renal adjustment required. Supports clinical decision support (CDS) alerts in CPOE.",
order,protocol_configuration,order_order_set,source_system,source_system,Source System,STRING,,,,epic|cerner|meditech|manual,,Operational system of record from which the order set was sourced. epic = Epic Orders/CPOE; cerner = Cerner Millennium PowerChart; meditech = MEDITECH Expanse; manual = manually entered outside a standard EHR system.,
order,protocol_configuration,order_order_set,source_system_code,source_system_code,Source System Order Set ID,STRING,,,,,,"Native identifier of the order set in the originating operational system (e.g., Epic Orders internal record ID, Cerner Millennium order set catalog ID). Supports ETL lineage tracking and cross-system reconciliation.",
order,protocol_configuration,order_order_set,updated_timestamp,updated_timestamp,Record Last Updated Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,,"Timestamp of the most recent modification to the order set record in the source system or lakehouse. Supports change tracking, audit trail requirements, and ETL incremental load processing.",
order,protocol_configuration,order_order_set,usage_count,usage_count,Order Set Usage Count,INT,,,,,,"Cumulative count of the number of times this order set version has been activated by providers in CPOE. Supports utilization analytics, adoption tracking, and clinical quality improvement initiatives. Not a calculated aggregate — sourced directly from the EHR order set activation log.",
order,protocol_configuration,order_order_set,version_number,version_number,Order Set Version Number,STRING,,,,^d+.d+(.d+)?$,,"Semantic version number of the order set (e.g., 1.0, 2.3, 3.1.2). Incremented upon each approved revision to support version control, audit trails, and rollback capabilities per Health Information Management (HIM) governance requirements.",
