pharmacy,dispensing_operations,prescription,prescription_timestamp,prescription_timestamp,Prescription Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_health",,transactional_data,The precise date and time when the prescription was written and entered into the system. Used for audit trails and CPOE (Computerized Physician Order Entry) compliance.,
pharmacy,dispensing_operations,prescription,prescription_type,prescription_type,Prescription Type,STRING,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_health",new|refill|renewal|transfer-in|transfer-out|change,transactional_data,Classifies the prescription transaction type. New indicates first-time prescription; refill indicates subsequent fill of existing prescription; renewal indicates new prescription for same medication after previous expired; transfer indicates prescription moved between pharmacies; change indicates modification to existing prescription.,
pharmacy,dispensing_operations,prescription,prior_authorization_number,prior_authorization_number,Prior Authorization Number,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,The authorization number issued by the insurance payer approving coverage for this prescription. Null if no prior authorization was required or obtained.,
pharmacy,dispensing_operations,prescription,prior_authorization_required_flag,prior_authorization_required_flag,Prior Authorization Required Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,Indicates whether insurance prior authorization is required before this prescription can be filled. True if prior auth is needed; false otherwise.,
pharmacy,dispensing_operations,prescription,quantity_prescribed,quantity_prescribed,Quantity Prescribed,"DECIMAL(10,2)",,,,,transactional_data,"The total quantity of medication prescribed, expressed in the unit appropriate to the dosage form (e.g., number of tablets, milliliters of liquid).",
pharmacy,dispensing_operations,prescription,quantity_unit,quantity_unit,Quantity Unit of Measure,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"The unit of measure for the prescribed quantity (e.g., tablets, capsules, mL, grams).",
pharmacy,dispensing_operations,prescription,refills_authorized,refills_authorized,Refills Authorized,INT,,,,,transactional_data,The number of refills authorized by the prescriber. Zero indicates no refills allowed. Controlled substances have regulatory limits on refill counts.,
pharmacy,dispensing_operations,prescription,refills_remaining,refills_remaining,Refills Remaining,INT,,,,,transactional_data,The number of refills remaining on this prescription. Decremented each time the prescription is filled.,
pharmacy,dispensing_operations,prescription,route_of_administration,route_of_administration,Route of Administration,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"The path by which the medication is administered to the patient (e.g., oral, intravenous, topical). [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: oral|intravenous|intramuscular|subcutaneous|topical|inhalation|rectal|transdermal|sublingual|ophthalmic|otic|nasal — 12 candidates stripped; promote to reference product]",
pharmacy,dispensing_operations,prescription,sig,sig,Sig (Directions for Use),STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"The prescribers instructions to the patient on how to take the medication. Free-text field containing dosing frequency, timing, and special instructions (e.g., Take 1 tablet by mouth twice daily with food).",
