post_acute_care,skilled_nursing,snf_data,snf_data_id,snf_data_id,snf_data Identifier,BIGINT,Y,,,,,Primary key for snf_data,
post_acute_care,skilled_nursing,snf_data,post_acute_episode_id,post_acute_episode_id,Post Acute Episode Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,post_acute_care.post_acute_episode.post_acute_episode_id,,,,Foreign key linking to post_acute_care.post_acute_episode. Business justification: SNF data stub should link to the master episode for data integration.,Internal - LLM Generated Cross-Domain Link
post_acute_care,skilled_nursing,snf_data,post_acute_location_id,post_acute_location_id,Post Acute Location Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,post_acute_care.post_acute_location.post_acute_location_id,,,,Foreign key linking to post_acute_care.post_acute_location. Business justification: SNF data should reference the location where the SNF services are provided.,Internal - LLM Generated Cross-Domain Link
post_acute_care,skilled_nursing,snf_data,snf_id,snf_id,Snf Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,post_acute_care.snf.snf_id,,,,Foreign key linking to post_acute_care.snf. Business justification: SNF data records belong to a specific SNF facility. Direct linkage enables facility-level data aggregation and reporting.,Internal - LLM Generated Cross-Domain Link
post_acute_care,skilled_nursing,snf_encounter,snf_encounter_id,snf_encounter_id,snf_encounter Identifier,BIGINT,Y,,,,,Primary key for snf_encounter,
post_acute_care,skilled_nursing,snf_encounter,post_acute_episode_id,post_acute_episode_id,Post Acute Episode Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,post_acute_care.post_acute_episode.post_acute_episode_id,,,,Foreign key linking to post_acute_care.post_acute_episode. Business justification: SNF encounters occur within a post-acute episode. Linking connects encounter-level data to the master episode.,Internal - LLM Generated Cross-Domain Link
post_acute_care,skilled_nursing,snf_encounter,post_acute_location_id,post_acute_location_id,Post Acute Location Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,post_acute_care.post_acute_location.post_acute_location_id,,,,Foreign key linking to post_acute_care.post_acute_location. Business justification: SNF encounters occur at a specific location. Linking to post_acute_location identifies the facility.,Internal - LLM Generated Cross-Domain Link
post_acute_care,skilled_nursing,snf_encounter,snf_id,snf_id,Snf Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,post_acute_care.snf.snf_id,,,,"Foreign key linking to post_acute_care.snf. Business justification: An SNF encounter occurs at a specific SNF. While snf_encounter has post_acute_location_id, a direct link to the SNF entity provides clearer facility-level attribution.",Internal - LLM Generated Cross-Domain Link
post_acute_care,skilled_nursing,snf_stay,snf_stay_id,snf_stay_id,snf_stay Identifier,BIGINT,Y,,,,,Primary key for snf_stay,
post_acute_care,skilled_nursing,snf_stay,mpi_record_id,mpi_record_id,,BIGINT,,patient.mpi_record.mpi_record_id,,,,description,
post_acute_care,skilled_nursing,snf_stay,post_acute_episode_id,post_acute_episode_id,Post Acute Episode Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,post_acute_care.post_acute_episode.post_acute_episode_id,,,,Foreign key linking to post_acute_care.post_acute_episode. Business justification: SNF stay is a type of post-acute episode. Linking to the master episode record connects this legacy stub table to the normalized model.,Internal - LLM Generated Cross-Domain Link
post_acute_care,skilled_nursing,snf_stay,post_acute_location_id,post_acute_location_id,Post Acute Location Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,post_acute_care.post_acute_location.post_acute_location_id,,,,Foreign key linking to post_acute_care.post_acute_location. Business justification: A SNF stay occurs at a specific post-acute location. This enables location-level analytics for SNF stays including capacity planning and quality metrics.,Internal - LLM Generated Cross-Domain Link
post_acute_care,skilled_nursing,snf_stay,snf_id,snf_id,Snf Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,post_acute_care.snf.snf_id,,,,Foreign key linking to post_acute_care.snf. Business justification: A SNF stay occurs at a specific skilled nursing facility. This links the stay record to the facility where care was provided.,Internal - LLM Generated Cross-Domain Link
radiology,interpretation_reporting,critical_result,critical_result_id,critical_result_id,Critical Result Identifier,BIGINT,Y,,,,transactional_data,Primary key for critical_result,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,critical_result,care_site_id,care_site_id,Facility ID,BIGINT,,facility.care_site.care_site_id,,,transactional_data,Reference to the facility or imaging center where the study was performed and the critical finding was identified. Supports multi-facility enterprise reporting and TJC accreditation tracking at the facility level.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,critical_result,clinical_order_id,clinical_order_id,Clinical Order Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,order.clinical_order.clinical_order_id,,,transactional_data,Foreign key linking to order.clinical_order. Business justification: Critical findings require closed-loop communication linking back to originating clinical orders. Joint Commission critical results notification standards require tracking from order placement through ,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,critical_result,cpt_code_id,cpt_code_id,Cpt Code Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,reference.cpt_code.cpt_code_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to reference.cpt_code. Business justification: Critical findings are associated with procedure codes for quality tracking, Joint Commission compliance reporting, and critical result rate benchmarking by exam type. Supports patient safety analytics",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,critical_result,demographics_id,demographics_id,Patient ID,BIGINT,,patient.demographics.demographics_id,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_identifier",,transactional_data,Reference to the patient associated with the imaging study containing the critical finding. Links to the enterprise Master Patient Index (MPI) record.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,critical_result,employee_id,employee_id,Radiologist Provider ID,BIGINT,,workforce.employee.employee_id,"dbx_confidential, dbx_pii",,transactional_data,Reference to the radiologist who identified and reported the critical finding. Links to the provider/clinician master record for NPI resolution and accountability tracking.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,critical_result,imaging_order_id,imaging_order_id,Imaging Order ID,BIGINT,,radiology.imaging_order.imaging_order_id,,,transactional_data,Reference to the radiology imaging order that generated the critical finding. Links to the originating order in the RIS (Epic Radiant / Cerner RadNet).,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,critical_result,message_log_id,message_log_id,Message Log Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,interoperability.message_log.message_log_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to interoperability.message_log. Business justification: Critical radiology findings trigger mandatory HL7 ORU result messages to ordering providers and EHR systems for TJC compliance and patient safety. Message_log tracks notification delivery, acknowledgm",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,critical_result,org_unit_id,org_unit_id,Radiology Department ID,BIGINT,,workforce.org_unit.org_unit_id,,,transactional_data,"Reference to the radiology department or imaging section (e.g., neuroradiology, body imaging, emergency radiology) responsible for the study. Supports departmental quality reporting and workload analytics.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,critical_result,primary_critical_clinician_id,primary_critical_clinician_id,Notified Provider ID,BIGINT,,provider.clinician.clinician_id,,,transactional_data,Reference to the ordering or responsible provider who received the critical result notification. Required for TJC NPSG.02.03.01 compliance documentation of the notification recipient.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,critical_result,report_id,report_id,Radiology Report ID,BIGINT,,radiology.report.report_id,,,transactional_data,Reference to the formal radiology report (final or preliminary) in which the critical finding was documented. Links to the radiology report data product for full diagnostic context and PACS/RIS integration.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,critical_result,subject_enrollment_id,subject_enrollment_id,Subject Enrollment Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,research.subject_enrollment.subject_enrollment_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to research.subject_enrollment. Business justification: Critical imaging findings in research subjects trigger adverse event reporting workflows to IRBs, sponsors, and data safety monitoring boards. Direct linkage enables automated AE capture, safety signa",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,critical_result,tertiary_critical_ordering_provider_clinician_id,tertiary_critical_ordering_provider_clinician_id,Ordering Provider ID,BIGINT,,provider.clinician.clinician_id,,,transactional_data,Reference to the provider who placed the original imaging order. May differ from the notified provider if the ordering provider is unavailable. Used for accountability tracking and notification workflow routing.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,critical_result,visit_id,visit_id,Visit ID,BIGINT,,encounter.visit.visit_id,,,transactional_data,Reference to the patient encounter or visit during which the imaging study was performed and the critical finding was identified. Supports EMTALA compliance tracking and care coordination.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,critical_result,accession_number,accession_number,Radiology Accession Number,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,The RIS-assigned accession number uniquely identifying the imaging order or study that produced the critical finding. Serves as the primary business identifier linking this notification to the originating radiology order in Epic Radiant or Cerner RadNet.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,critical_result,acknowledgment_datetime,acknowledgment_datetime,Acknowledgment Datetime,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,The date and time when the notified provider acknowledged receipt and understanding of the critical finding. Required for TJC NPSG.02.03.01 closed-loop communication compliance. Null if acknowledgment has not yet been received.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,critical_result,acknowledgment_method,acknowledgment_method,Acknowledgment Method,STRING,,,,phone|secure_message|ehr_alert|pager|in_person|fax,transactional_data,The communication channel through which the notified provider acknowledged the critical finding. Required for TJC NPSG.02.03.01 closed-loop verification documentation. May differ from the notification method.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,critical_result,acknowledgment_turnaround_minutes,acknowledgment_turnaround_minutes,Acknowledgment Turnaround Time (Minutes),INT,,,,,transactional_data,The elapsed time in minutes between notification_datetime and acknowledgment_datetime. Measures provider responsiveness to critical finding notifications. Used for TJC NPSG.02.03.01 compliance measurement and provider performance analytics. Null if acknowledgment has not been received.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,critical_result,body_part_examined,body_part_examined,Body Part Examined,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"The anatomical body part or region examined in the imaging study that produced the critical finding. Aligns with DICOM Tag (0018,0015) and SNOMED CT anatomical site codes. Supports clinical analytics and quality reporting.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,critical_result,created_timestamp,created_timestamp,Record Created Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,"The date and time when this critical finding notification record was first created in the data platform. Supports audit trail, data lineage, and Silver layer ingestion tracking per HIPAA audit control requirements.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,critical_result,dicom_study_uid,dicom_study_uid,DICOM Study Instance Unique Identifier (UID),STRING,,,"pii_phi,pii_pii,pii_sensitive",,transactional_data,"The globally unique DICOM Study Instance UID (0020,000D) identifying the imaging study in the PACS (Picture Archiving and Communication System). Enables direct linkage to DICOM images for clinical review and audit purposes.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,critical_result,emtala_applicable,emtala_applicable,Emergency Medical Treatment and Labor Act (EMTALA) Applicable Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,"Indicates whether EMTALA obligations apply to this critical finding notification, typically when the patient presented through the Emergency Department. True = EMTALA applies; False = EMTALA not applicable. Supports EMTALA compliance documentation and legal risk management.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,critical_result,escalation_datetime,escalation_datetime,Escalation Datetime,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,The date and time when the escalation process was initiated for this critical finding notification. Populated only when escalation_flag is True. Used to measure escalation response times and compliance with institutional escalation policies.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,critical_result,escalation_flag,escalation_flag,Escalation Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,Indicates whether the critical finding notification required escalation due to failure to reach the primary responsible provider within the defined response time threshold. True = escalation was triggered; False = no escalation required. Supports TJC NPSG.02.03.01 compliance and patient safety event tracking.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,critical_result,escalation_reason,escalation_reason,Escalation Reason,STRING,,,,no_response|provider_unavailable|wrong_contact|system_failure|other,transactional_data,"The reason escalation was triggered for this critical finding notification: no_response (provider did not respond within threshold), provider_unavailable (provider not reachable), wrong_contact (incorrect contact information), system_failure (notification system failure), other. Supports root cause analysis and process improvement.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,critical_result,finding_category,finding_category,Finding Category,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Clinical category of the critical finding (e.g., pulmonary embolism, intracranial hemorrhage, pneumothorax, aortic dissection, malignancy, fracture). Supports population health analytics, quality reporting, and pattern analysis. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: pulmonary_embolism|intracranial_hemorrhage|pneumothorax|aortic_dissection|malignancy|fracture|other — promote to reference product]",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,critical_result,finding_datetime,finding_datetime,Finding Identified Datetime,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,The date and time when the radiologist identified and documented the critical finding during image interpretation. This is the principal business event timestamp representing when the critical result was discovered. Critical for measuring notification turnaround time against TJC NPSG.02.03.01 compliance thresholds.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,critical_result,finding_description,finding_description,Critical Finding Description,STRING,,,"dbx_pii_health,dbx_restricted,pii_phi,pii_pii,pii_sensitive",,transactional_data,Free-text clinical description of the critical or significant radiology finding requiring immediate action. Captured from the radiologists report or preliminary read in the RIS/PACS. Constitutes Protected Health Information (PHI) under HIPAA.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,critical_result,finding_severity,finding_severity,Finding Severity Level,STRING,,,,critical|significant|incidental,transactional_data,"Severity classification of the radiology finding: critical (life-threatening, requires immediate action), significant (clinically important, requires timely action), or incidental (unexpected finding not directly related to the primary indication). Drives notification urgency and escalation workflows per TJC NPSG.02.03.01.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,critical_result,modality,modality,Imaging Modality,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"The imaging modality used for the study that produced the critical finding (e.g., CT=Computed Tomography, MRI=Magnetic Resonance Imaging, XR=X-Ray, US=Ultrasound, PET=Positron Emission Tomography, NM=Nuclear Medicine, MG=Mammography, FL=Fluoroscopy). Aligns with DICOM modality codes. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: CT|MRI|XR|US|PET|NM|MG|FL — 8 candidates stripped; promote to reference product]",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,critical_result,mrn,mrn,Medical Record Number (MRN),STRING,,,"dbx_pii_identifier,dbx_restricted,pii_phi,pii_pii,pii_sensitive",,transactional_data,The facility-assigned Medical Record Number (MRN) for the patient associated with the critical finding. Used for cross-system patient identification and audit trail in compliance with HIPAA PHI requirements.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,critical_result,notification_attempt_count,notification_attempt_count,Notification Attempt Count,INT,,,,,transactional_data,The total number of notification attempts made before successful delivery or escalation. Tracks communication persistence and supports root cause analysis for notification failures and escalation triggers.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,critical_result,notification_datetime,notification_datetime,Notification Datetime,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,The date and time when the critical finding notification was transmitted to the responsible provider. Used to calculate notification turnaround time (finding_datetime to notification_datetime) for TJC NPSG.02.03.01 compliance measurement.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,critical_result,notification_method,notification_method,Notification Method,STRING,,,,phone|secure_message|ehr_alert|pager|in_person|fax,transactional_data,"The communication channel used to deliver the critical finding notification to the responsible provider (e.g., phone=direct telephone call, secure_message=encrypted messaging platform, ehr_alert=EHR in-basket alert, pager=numeric/alphanumeric pager, in_person=face-to-face, fax=facsimile). Aligns with HL7 FHIR CommunicationRequest.medium.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,critical_result,notification_status,notification_status,Notification Status,STRING,,,,pending|notified|acknowledged|escalated|failed|cancelled,transactional_data,"Current workflow status of the critical finding notification lifecycle: pending (finding identified, notification not yet sent), notified (notification sent, awaiting acknowledgment), acknowledged (provider confirmed receipt), escalated (escalation triggered due to non-response), failed (notification delivery failed), cancelled (notification voided). Drives workflow management and compliance dashboards.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,critical_result,notification_turnaround_minutes,notification_turnaround_minutes,Notification Turnaround Time (Minutes),INT,,,,,transactional_data,"The elapsed time in minutes between finding_datetime and notification_datetime. Represents the raw operational measurement of how quickly the critical finding was communicated after identification. Used for TJC NPSG.02.03.01 compliance measurement and quality dashboards. Note: this is a stored operational metric captured at notification time, not a real-time calculation.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,critical_result,notified_provider_npi,notified_provider_npi,Notified Provider National Provider Identifier (NPI),STRING,,,"pii_phi,pii_pii,pii_sensitive",^[0-9]{10}$,transactional_data,The 10-digit National Provider Identifier (NPI) of the provider who received the critical result notification. Directly supports TJC NPSG.02.03.01 documentation requirements for the receiving clinician.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,critical_result,pacs_system_name,pacs_system_name,Picture Archiving and Communication System (PACS) Name,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"The name or identifier of the PACS system where the imaging study is archived (e.g., vendor name, system instance). Supports multi-PACS enterprise environments and image retrieval workflows.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,critical_result,patient_care_setting,patient_care_setting,Patient Care Setting,STRING,,,,inpatient|outpatient|emergency|observation|ambulatory,transactional_data,"The care setting classification of the patient at the time of the critical finding notification: inpatient, outpatient, emergency (Emergency Department), observation, or ambulatory. Influences notification protocols, escalation pathways, and regulatory reporting requirements.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,critical_result,patient_location_at_notification,patient_location_at_notification,Patient Location at Notification,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"The patients care location (unit, department, or facility) at the time the critical finding notification was issued (e.g., ED, ICU, outpatient clinic, inpatient floor). Supports EMTALA compliance, care coordination, and patient safety event analysis.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,critical_result,patient_safety_event_flag,patient_safety_event_flag,Patient Safety Event Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,"Indicates whether this critical finding notification has been associated with a formal patient safety event report (e.g., near-miss, adverse event). True = linked to a patient safety event; False = no patient safety event association. Supports OIG compliance, TJC accreditation, and AHRQ patient safety reporting.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,critical_result,radiologist_npi,radiologist_npi,Radiologist National Provider Identifier (NPI),STRING,,,"pii_phi,pii_pii,pii_sensitive",^[0-9]{10}$,transactional_data,The 10-digit National Provider Identifier (NPI) of the radiologist who identified the critical finding. Required for regulatory reporting and provider accountability under CMS and TJC standards.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,critical_result,read_back_notes,read_back_notes,Read-Back Documentation Notes,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Free-text documentation of the read-back communication, including any discrepancies noted during the read-back process. Populated when read_back_performed is True. Supports TJC NPSG.02.03.01 closed-loop communication audit trail.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,critical_result,read_back_performed,read_back_performed,Read-Back Performed Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,"Indicates whether the notified provider performed a verbal read-back of the critical finding to confirm accurate communication, as required by TJC NPSG.02.03.01 for verbal/telephone notifications. True = read-back was performed and documented; False = read-back not performed or not applicable.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,critical_result,report_status_at_notification,report_status_at_notification,Report Status at Notification,STRING,,,,preliminary|final|addendum,transactional_data,"The status of the radiology report at the time the critical finding notification was issued: preliminary (initial read, not yet finalized), final (attending radiologist signed report), addendum (correction or addition to a finalized report). Important for clinical decision-making context and liability documentation.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,critical_result,source_system,source_system,Source System,STRING,,,,epic_radiant|cerner_radnet|meditech|other,transactional_data,"The operational system of record from which this critical finding notification record was sourced (e.g., epic_radiant, cerner_radnet, meditech). Supports data lineage, ETL audit, and multi-system enterprise integration.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,critical_result,tjc_compliance_status,tjc_compliance_status,The Joint Commission (TJC) Compliance Status,STRING,,,,compliant|non_compliant|pending_review|exception_granted,transactional_data,"Indicates whether this critical finding notification meets The Joint Commission (TJC) National Patient Safety Goal NPSG.02.03.01 requirements for critical result communication: compliant (all requirements met), non_compliant (requirements not met, e.g., acknowledgment not received within threshold), pending_review (under quality review), exception_granted (documented exception approved). Directly supports TJC accreditation reporting.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,critical_result,updated_timestamp,updated_timestamp,Record Updated Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,"The date and time when this critical finding notification record was last modified in the data platform. Supports change tracking, audit trail, and incremental ETL processing per HIPAA audit control requirements.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,follow_up,follow_up_id,follow_up_id,Follow Up Identifier,BIGINT,Y,,,,transactional_data,Primary key for follow_up,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,follow_up,audit_finding_id,audit_finding_id,Audit Finding Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,compliance.audit_finding.audit_finding_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to compliance.audit_finding. Business justification: Follow-up recommendation tracking is audited for patient safety and standard-of-care compliance. Compliance monitors follow-up closure rates, patient notification, and lost-to-follow-up rates; deficie",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,follow_up,clinical_order_id,clinical_order_id,Clinical Order Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,order.clinical_order.clinical_order_id,,,transactional_data,Foreign key linking to order.clinical_order. Business justification: Follow-up recommendations generate new clinical orders. Care gap closure tracking requires linking recommendations to original orders for longitudinal care coordination. Population health management t,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,follow_up,cpt_code_id,cpt_code_id,Cpt Code Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,reference.cpt_code.cpt_code_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to reference.cpt_code. Business justification: Follow-up recommendations specify CPT codes for recommended procedures to enable automated order entry, care gap closure tracking, and ACR appropriateness criteria validation. Supports population heal",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,follow_up,demographics_id,demographics_id,Patient ID,BIGINT,,patient.demographics.demographics_id,,,transactional_data,Reference to the patient for whom this follow-up recommendation was issued. Core party reference linking the recommendation to the Master Patient Index (MPI).,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,follow_up,employee_id,employee_id,Care Coordinator Employee Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,workforce.employee.employee_id,"dbx_confidential, dbx_pii",,transactional_data,Foreign key linking to workforce.employee. Business justification: Follow-up recommendation tracking programs use care coordinators (nurses/navigators) to ensure patient compliance with recommended imaging. Required for population health management and quality measur,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,follow_up,icd10_finding_icd_code_id,icd10_finding_icd_code_id,Icd10 Finding Icd Code Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,reference.icd_code.icd_code_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to reference.icd_code. Business justification: Follow-up recommendations reference diagnosis codes for medical necessity justification, care gap identification, and quality measure reporting. Links support diagnosis-driven follow-up compliance tra",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,follow_up,imaging_order_id,imaging_order_id,Imaging Order ID,BIGINT,,radiology.imaging_order.imaging_order_id,,,transactional_data,Reference to the original imaging order that produced the study from which this follow-up recommendation was derived.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,follow_up,primary_follow_clinician_id,primary_follow_clinician_id,Ordering Provider ID,BIGINT,,provider.clinician.clinician_id,,,transactional_data,Reference to the clinician who placed the original imaging order. Used for provider notification workflows and accountability tracking.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,follow_up,prior_auth_rule_id,prior_auth_rule_id,Prior Auth Rule Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,insurance.prior_auth_rule.prior_auth_rule_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to insurance.prior_auth_rule. Business justification: Follow-up imaging recommendations frequently require prior authorization. Linking to applicable PA rule enables automated requirement flagging, patient notification of coverage prerequisites, scheduli",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,follow_up,report_id,report_id,Radiology Report ID,BIGINT,,radiology.report.report_id,,,transactional_data,Reference to the radiology report from which this follow-up recommendation was generated. Links the recommendation to its source diagnostic interpretation.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,follow_up,visit_id,visit_id,Encounter ID,BIGINT,,encounter.visit.visit_id,,,transactional_data,Reference to the clinical encounter associated with the original imaging study that generated this follow-up recommendation.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,follow_up,acr_category_code,acr_category_code,ACR (American College of Radiology) Category Code,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Structured ACR category or risk stratification code assigned to the finding per applicable ACR reporting system (e.g., Lung-RADS 4A, LI-RADS LR-4, TI-RADS 4). Drives follow-up urgency and recommended action.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,follow_up,acr_guideline_reference,acr_guideline_reference,ACR (American College of Radiology) Incidental Findings Guideline Reference,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Specific ACR (American College of Radiology) incidental findings guideline or white paper that governs this recommendation (e.g., ACR Lung-RADS 2022, ACR Incidental Thyroid Findings 2023). Enables automated guideline compliance validation.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,follow_up,care_gap_flag,care_gap_flag,Care Gap Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,Indicates whether this follow-up recommendation represents an open care gap in population health management workflows. True when the recommended action has not been completed within the guideline-specified timeframe. Drives HEDIS (Healthcare Effectiveness Data and Information Set) and MIPS care gap closure programs.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,follow_up,cms_quality_measure_flag,cms_quality_measure_flag,CMS (Centers for Medicare and Medicaid Services) Quality Measure Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,Indicates whether this follow-up recommendation is attributable to a CMS (Centers for Medicare and Medicaid Services) quality measure or MIPS (Merit-based Incentive Payment System) performance measure. True when the recommendation contributes to a reportable quality metric.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,follow_up,completed_date,completed_date,Follow-Up Completed Date,DATE,,,,,transactional_data,Date on which the follow-up action was completed. Populated when recommendation_status transitions to completed. Used to calculate compliance with recommended timeframes and CMS quality measures.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,follow_up,created_timestamp,created_timestamp,Record Created Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,Date and time when this follow-up recommendation record was first created in the data platform. Supports audit trail and data lineage requirements.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,follow_up,declined_reason,declined_reason,Declined or Cancelled Reason,STRING,,,,patient_refused|provider_cancelled|clinically_inappropriate|duplicate_recommendation|other,transactional_data,Reason code explaining why the follow-up recommendation was declined or cancelled. Populated when recommendation_status is declined or cancelled. Supports quality reporting and exception documentation.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,follow_up,escalation_flag,escalation_flag,Escalation Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,"Indicates whether this follow-up recommendation has been escalated due to non-compliance, overdue status, or high-risk finding. True when escalation has been triggered; drives escalation workflow and management reporting.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,follow_up,escalation_reason,escalation_reason,Escalation Reason,STRING,,,,overdue|high_risk_finding|patient_no_show|provider_non_response|critical_result,transactional_data,Reason code explaining why this follow-up recommendation was escalated. Supports root cause analysis and quality improvement programs.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,follow_up,escalation_timestamp,escalation_timestamp,Escalation Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,Date and time when this follow-up recommendation was escalated. Populated only when escalation_flag is True. Supports escalation audit trail and response time measurement.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,follow_up,finding_body_region,finding_body_region,Finding Body Region,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Anatomical body region or organ system where the actionable finding was identified (e.g., lung, liver, adrenal gland, thyroid). Supports ACR guideline-based routing and population health cohort analysis.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,follow_up,finding_category_code,finding_category_code,Finding Category Code,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Standardized code classifying the type of incidental finding per ACR or SNOMED CT terminology (e.g., pulmonary nodule, renal cyst, hepatic lesion). Enables structured tracking and guideline-based workflow routing.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,follow_up,finding_description,finding_description,Incidental Finding Description,STRING,,,"dbx_pii_health,dbx_restricted,pii_phi,pii_pii,pii_sensitive",,transactional_data,"Description of the incidental or actionable finding that triggered this follow-up recommendation. Captures the clinical observation (e.g., pulmonary nodule, adrenal mass) as documented in the radiology report.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,follow_up,lost_to_follow_up_date,lost_to_follow_up_date,Lost to Follow-Up Date,DATE,,,,,transactional_data,"Date on which the recommendation was classified as lost-to-follow-up, indicating the patient did not complete the recommended action within the acceptable timeframe despite outreach efforts.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,follow_up,ordering_provider_notification_status,ordering_provider_notification_status,Ordering Provider Notification Status,STRING,,,,not_notified|notified|acknowledged|action_taken,transactional_data,Current status of notification to the ordering provider regarding this follow-up recommendation. Tracks whether the referring clinician has been informed and has acknowledged or acted on the recommendation.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,follow_up,ordering_provider_notification_timestamp,ordering_provider_notification_timestamp,Ordering Provider Notification Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,Date and time when the ordering provider was first notified of this follow-up recommendation. Supports closed-loop communication compliance and provider accountability tracking.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,follow_up,pacs_study_instance_uid,pacs_study_instance_uid,PACS (Picture Archiving and Communication System) Study Instance UID,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,DICOM Study Instance Unique Identifier (UID) for the imaging study from which this follow-up recommendation was generated. Enables direct linkage to the source images in the PACS (Picture Archiving and Communication System).,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,follow_up,patient_notification_method,patient_notification_method,Patient Notification Method,STRING,,,,portal_message|phone_call|letter|in_person|secure_email,transactional_data,"Channel or method used to notify the patient of the follow-up recommendation (e.g., patient portal message, phone call, letter). Supports communication preference compliance and outreach effectiveness analysis.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,follow_up,patient_notification_status,patient_notification_status,Patient Notification Status,STRING,,,,not_notified|notified|acknowledged|declined_notification,transactional_data,"Current status of patient notification regarding this follow-up recommendation. Tracks whether the patient has been informed, acknowledged receipt, or declined notification. Supports HIPAA patient communication compliance.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,follow_up,patient_notification_timestamp,patient_notification_timestamp,Patient Notification Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,Date and time when the patient was first notified of this follow-up recommendation. Supports compliance documentation and patient communication audit trails.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,follow_up,population_health_cohort,population_health_cohort,Population Health Cohort,STRING,,,"dbx_pii,dbx_restricted,pii_phi,pii_pii,pii_sensitive",,transactional_data,"Population health management cohort or program to which this follow-up recommendation is attributed (e.g., Lung Cancer Screening Program, Incidental Pulmonary Nodule Registry, Adrenal Incidentaloma Program). Supports ACO and population health analytics.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,follow_up,priority_level,priority_level,Follow-Up Priority Level,STRING,,,,routine|urgent|emergent|critical,transactional_data,"Clinical urgency classification of the follow-up recommendation indicating how quickly action must be taken. Drives escalation workflows, patient notification timelines, and provider alert routing.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,follow_up,recommendation_date,recommendation_date,Recommendation Issue Date and Time,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,Date and time when the follow-up recommendation was formally issued by the radiologist in the finalized report. Serves as the principal business event timestamp for lifecycle and compliance tracking.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,follow_up,recommendation_number,recommendation_number,Follow-Up Recommendation Number,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Externally visible business identifier for this follow-up recommendation, used in patient communications, provider notifications, and tracking workflows. Format: FU-YYYYMMDD-NNNNNN.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,follow_up,recommendation_status,recommendation_status,Follow-Up Recommendation Status,STRING,,,,pending|scheduled|completed|declined|lost_to_follow_up|cancelled,transactional_data,Current workflow state of the follow-up recommendation. Drives population health management dashboards and CMS quality measure reporting.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,follow_up,recommendation_text,recommendation_text,Follow-Up Recommendation Text,STRING,,,"dbx_pii_health,dbx_restricted,pii_phi,pii_pii,pii_sensitive",,transactional_data,Free-text narrative of the follow-up recommendation as authored by the radiologist in the report. Contains Protected Health Information (PHI) and clinical detail supporting the recommended action.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,follow_up,recommendation_type,recommendation_type,Follow-Up Recommendation Type,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Category of action recommended by the radiologist. Classifies the nature of the follow-up required (e.g., repeat imaging, biopsy, specialist referral). [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: repeat_imaging|biopsy|clinical_correlation|specialist_referral|lab_workup|clinical_follow_up|surveillance — promote to reference product]",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,follow_up,recommended_due_date,recommended_due_date,Recommended Follow-Up Due Date,DATE,,,,,transactional_data,"Calculated target date by which the follow-up action should be completed, derived from the recommendation date plus the recommended timeframe. Used for overdue tracking, escalation triggers, and patient outreach scheduling.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,follow_up,recommended_modality,recommended_modality,Recommended Imaging Modality,STRING,,,,CT|MRI|ultrasound|PET|X-ray|mammography,transactional_data,"Imaging modality recommended for the follow-up study (e.g., CT, MRI, ultrasound). Used for scheduling, resource planning, and modality-specific workflow routing. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: CT|MRI|ultrasound|PET|X-ray|mammography|fluoroscopy|nuclear_medicine — promote to reference product if additional modalities are needed]",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,follow_up,recommended_timeframe_days,recommended_timeframe_days,Recommended Follow-Up Timeframe (Days),INT,,,,,transactional_data,"Number of days within which the follow-up action should be completed, as specified by the radiologist or derived from ACR incidental finding guidelines (e.g., 90 days for a 6–8 mm pulmonary nodule). Drives escalation and overdue tracking.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,follow_up,report_finalized_timestamp,report_finalized_timestamp,Radiology Report Finalized Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,Date and time when the radiology report containing this recommendation was finalized and signed by the interpreting radiologist. Used for turnaround time measurement and compliance reporting.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,follow_up,ris_recommendation_code,ris_recommendation_code,Radiology Information System (RIS) Recommendation ID,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,Native identifier for this follow-up recommendation as assigned by the source Radiology Information System (RIS) such as Epic Radiant or Cerner RadNet. Supports system-of-record traceability and cross-system reconciliation.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,follow_up,scheduled_date,scheduled_date,Follow-Up Scheduled Date,DATE,,,,,transactional_data,"Date on which the follow-up action (imaging, biopsy, referral appointment) has been scheduled. Populated when recommendation_status transitions to scheduled. Used for compliance gap analysis.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,follow_up,source_system,source_system,Source System,STRING,,,,Epic_Radiant|Cerner_RadNet|MEDITECH|manual_entry,transactional_data,"Operational system of record from which this follow-up recommendation was sourced (e.g., Epic Radiant, Cerner RadNet). Supports data lineage, ETL audit, and multi-system reconciliation in the lakehouse.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,follow_up,specialist_referral_type,specialist_referral_type,Specialist Referral Type,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Specialty or service to which the patient is referred when recommendation_type is specialist_referral (e.g., pulmonology, oncology, endocrinology, interventional radiology). Supports referral management and care coordination workflows.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,follow_up,updated_timestamp,updated_timestamp,Record Last Updated Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,"Date and time when this follow-up recommendation record was most recently modified. Supports change tracking, audit compliance, and incremental data pipeline processing.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,radiology_finding,radiology_finding_id,radiology_finding_id,Finding Identifier,BIGINT,Y,,,,transactional_data,Primary key for finding,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,radiology_finding,clinical_ai_model_inference_log_id,clinical_ai_model_inference_log_id,Model Inference Log Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,clinical_ai.clinical_ai_model_inference_log.clinical_ai_model_inference_log_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to clinical_ai.model_inference_log. Business justification: AI-detected radiology findings (incidental nodules, PE, fractures) must trace to the specific inference run for FDA SaMD audit trail, bias monitoring, model performance tracking, and regulatory post-m",Internal - LLM Generated Cross-Domain Link
radiology,interpretation_reporting,radiology_finding,clinician_id,clinician_id,Interpreting Radiologist ID,BIGINT,,provider.clinician.clinician_id,,,transactional_data,"Reference to the radiologist (provider) who interpreted the imaging study and identified or confirmed this finding. Used for quality measurement, MIPS reporting, and RVU attribution.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,radiology_finding,demographics_id,demographics_id,Patient ID,BIGINT,,patient.demographics.demographics_id,,,transactional_data,Reference to the patient associated with this imaging finding. Core PARTY_REFERENCE linking the finding to the patient master record for population health and care coordination.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,radiology_finding,icd10_finding_icd_code_id,icd10_finding_icd_code_id,Icd10 Finding Icd Code Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,reference.icd_code.icd_code_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to reference.icd_code. Business justification: Findings may be mapped to ICD-10 codes for billing support, incidental finding tracking, and diagnosis-based population health cohort identification. Links enable finding-to-diagnosis crosswalks for a",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,radiology_finding,imaging_order_id,imaging_order_id,Imaging Order ID,BIGINT,,radiology.imaging_order.imaging_order_id,,,transactional_data,Reference to the imaging order (CPOE order) that initiated the study producing this finding. Supports order-to-finding traceability and RCM workflows.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,radiology_finding,report_id,report_id,Radiology Report ID,BIGINT,,radiology.report.report_id,,,transactional_data,Reference to the parent radiology report from which this finding was extracted or coded. Links the finding to its source narrative report for audit and traceability.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,radiology_finding,research_study_id,research_study_id,Research Study Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,research.research_study.research_study_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to research.research_study. Business justification: Structured imaging findings are extracted for research endpoint adjudication, efficacy assessments, and safety monitoring. Direct linkage enables automated endpoint capture, independent imaging review",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,radiology_finding,snomed_concept_id,snomed_concept_id,Finding Snomed Concept Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,reference.snomed_concept.snomed_concept_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to reference.snomed_concept. Business justification: Findings are coded using SNOMED CT for structured clinical documentation, NLP-extracted finding validation, and interoperable clinical data exchange. Supports radiology reporting quality measures and ",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,radiology_finding,visit_id,visit_id,Encounter ID,BIGINT,,encounter.visit.visit_id,,,transactional_data,Reference to the clinical encounter (visit) during which the imaging study was performed and this finding was identified. Supports encounter-level analytics and care episode linkage.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,radiology_finding,accession_number,accession_number,Radiology Accession Number,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,Externally-known unique identifier assigned by the Radiology Information System (RIS) to the imaging order/study from which this finding was extracted. Used as the primary cross-system business key linking findings to their parent imaging study in Epic Radiant and Cerner RadNet.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,radiology_finding,acr_score_type,acr_score_type,ACR Standardized Scoring System Type,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Identifies the ACR (American College of Radiology) standardized scoring system applied to this finding. LUNG_RADS for lung nodules, BI_RADS for breast imaging, TI_RADS for thyroid nodules, LI_RADS for liver observations, PI_RADS for prostate, C_RADS for colon. NONE if no ACR scoring system applies. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: LUNG_RADS|BI_RADS|TI_RADS|LI_RADS|PI_RADS|C_RADS|NONE — 7 candidates stripped; promote to reference product]",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,radiology_finding,acr_score_value,acr_score_value,ACR Standardized Score Value,"DECIMAL(18,2)",,,,,transactional_data,"The specific score or category value assigned under the applicable ACR scoring system (e.g., 3 for Lung-RADS 3, 4B for BI-RADS 4B, M for LI-RADS M). Stored as STRING to accommodate alphanumeric category designations across different ACR systems.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,radiology_finding,body_site_code,body_site_code,Body Site Code (SNOMED CT),STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"SNOMED CT code identifying the anatomical body site or region where the finding is located (e.g., SNOMED CT 368209003 for right arm). Enables structured anatomical querying and population health analytics.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,radiology_finding,body_site_description,body_site_description,Body Site Description,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Human-readable description of the anatomical location of the finding (e.g., Right upper lobe of lung, Left breast upper outer quadrant). Complements the coded body_site_code for display and reporting.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,radiology_finding,code_system,code_system,Finding Code System,STRING,,,,SNOMED_CT|RADLEX|ICD10|LOINC|LOCAL,transactional_data,"Identifies the coding system used for the finding_code (e.g., SNOMED_CT, RADLEX, ICD10, LOINC, LOCAL). Required for correct semantic interpretation of the code value.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,radiology_finding,created_timestamp,created_timestamp,Record Created Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,"Date and time when this radiology finding record was first created in the data platform. Supports audit trail, data lineage, and SLA compliance tracking.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,radiology_finding,data_source_method,data_source_method,Finding Data Source Method,STRING,,,,NLP_EXTRACTED|RADIOLOGIST_CODED|STRUCTURED_TEMPLATE|MANUAL_ENTRY,transactional_data,"Indicates how this structured finding was captured: NLP_EXTRACTED = derived via natural language processing from free-text report; RADIOLOGIST_CODED = directly coded by the radiologist using structured reporting tools; STRUCTURED_TEMPLATE = populated via a structured reporting template (e.g., Epic Radiant SmartForms); MANUAL_ENTRY = manually entered by HIM or CDI staff.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,radiology_finding,dicom_series_uid,dicom_series_uid,DICOM Series Instance UID,STRING,,,"pii_phi,pii_pii,pii_sensitive",,transactional_data,DICOM Series Instance UID identifying the specific image series within the PACS (Picture Archiving and Communication System) where this finding was identified. Enables direct PACS image retrieval and viewer deep-linking for clinical review.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,radiology_finding,dicom_sop_instance_uid,dicom_sop_instance_uid,DICOM SOP Instance UID,STRING,,,"pii_phi,pii_pii,pii_sensitive",,transactional_data,DICOM SOP Instance UID identifying the specific image instance (slice/frame) within the PACS where this finding is most prominently visualized. Supports precise image-level annotation and AI/ML training data linkage.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,radiology_finding,escalation_status,escalation_status,Finding Escalation Status,STRING,,,,NOT_ESCALATED|ESCALATED|ESCALATION_RESOLVED,transactional_data,"Indicates whether this finding has been escalated beyond standard notification workflows (e.g., escalated to department chief, patient safety officer, or risk management). Supports critical finding management and patient safety reporting.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,radiology_finding,escalation_timestamp,escalation_timestamp,Escalation Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,Date and time when this finding was escalated. Populated when escalation_status transitions to ESCALATED. Supports patient safety audit trails and risk management workflows.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,radiology_finding,finding_category,finding_category,Finding Category,STRING,,,,PRIMARY|INCIDENTAL|FOLLOW_UP_RECOMMENDED|CRITICAL|NORMAL,transactional_data,Clinical classification of the findings significance and origin within the study context. PRIMARY = the primary indication finding; INCIDENTAL = found outside the primary indication; FOLLOW_UP_RECOMMENDED = requires further workup; CRITICAL = requires immediate communication; NORMAL = no abnormality detected.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,radiology_finding,finding_description,finding_description,Finding Description,STRING,,,"pii_phi,pii_pii,pii_sensitive",,transactional_data,"Human-readable clinical description of the discrete finding as documented or extracted from the radiology report (e.g., Solitary pulmonary nodule, right upper lobe, 8mm). Supports clinical review, CDI workflows, and NLP validation.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,radiology_finding,finding_status,finding_status,Finding Status,STRING,,,,ACTIVE|RESOLVED|SUPERSEDED|ENTERED_IN_ERROR,transactional_data,Current lifecycle status of the radiology finding record. ACTIVE = current and actionable; RESOLVED = finding addressed or no longer present; SUPERSEDED = replaced by an amended or addended finding; ENTERED_IN_ERROR = incorrectly created. Aligns with HL7 FHIR Observation.status.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,radiology_finding,follow_up_completed_date,follow_up_completed_date,Follow-Up Completed Date,DATE,,,,,transactional_data,Date on which the recommended follow-up action was completed. Populated when follow_up_status transitions to COMPLETED. Used for compliance reporting and outcome tracking.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,radiology_finding,follow_up_due_date,follow_up_due_date,Follow-Up Due Date,DATE,,,,,transactional_data,Calculated or specified date by which the recommended follow-up action should be completed. Derived from study_date plus follow_up_timeframe_days or explicitly set by the radiologist. Drives follow-up tracking dashboards and patient outreach workflows.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,radiology_finding,follow_up_modality,follow_up_modality,Follow-Up Recommended Imaging Modality,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Specific imaging modality recommended for follow-up when follow_up_type is IMAGING (e.g., CT Chest with contrast, MRI Brain without contrast, PET/CT). Free-text or coded value per ACR guidelines.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,radiology_finding,follow_up_recommended,follow_up_recommended,Follow-Up Recommended Indicator,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,"Indicates whether the radiologist has recommended follow-up action for this finding. When TRUE, the follow-up recommendation fields are expected to be populated. Supports ACR incidental finding tracking and CMS quality measures.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,radiology_finding,follow_up_status,follow_up_status,Follow-Up Tracking Status,STRING,,,,PENDING|SCHEDULED|COMPLETED|OVERDUE|CANCELLED|NOT_REQUIRED,transactional_data,Current status of the follow-up recommendation lifecycle. PENDING = not yet acted upon; SCHEDULED = follow-up appointment or order placed; COMPLETED = follow-up performed; OVERDUE = past due date without completion; CANCELLED = follow-up cancelled; NOT_REQUIRED = no follow-up needed.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,radiology_finding,follow_up_timeframe_days,follow_up_timeframe_days,Follow-Up Recommended Timeframe (Days),INT,,,,,transactional_data,"Recommended timeframe in days within which the follow-up action should be completed, as specified by the radiologist or derived from ACR guidelines (e.g., 90 days for Lung-RADS 3, 30 days for Lung-RADS 4A). Used for follow-up scheduling and compliance tracking.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,radiology_finding,follow_up_type,follow_up_type,Follow-Up Recommendation Type,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,Type of follow-up action recommended by the radiologist for this finding. IMAGING = repeat or additional imaging; BIOPSY = tissue sampling; CLINICAL_EVALUATION = provider assessment; LABORATORY = lab workup; REFERRAL = specialist referral; NO_ACTION = no further action needed. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: IMAGING|BIOPSY|CLINICAL_EVALUATION|LABORATORY|REFERRAL|NO_ACTION|OTHER — 7 candidates stripped; promote to reference product],
radiology,interpretation_reporting,radiology_finding,imaging_modality,imaging_modality,Imaging Modality,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"The imaging modality used to produce the study from which this finding was identified (e.g., CT, MRI, XRAY, ULTRASOUND, PET). Supports modality-specific analytics, ACR scoring applicability, and scheduling workflows. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: CT|MRI|XRAY|ULTRASOUND|PET|PET_CT|MAMMOGRAPHY|FLUOROSCOPY|NUCLEAR_MED|DEXA|ANGIO|OTHER — promote to reference product]",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,radiology_finding,is_critical_result,is_critical_result,Critical Result Indicator,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,Indicates whether this finding meets the organizations criteria for a critical/urgent result requiring immediate communication to the ordering provider. Drives critical result notification workflows per TJC NPSG.02.03.01.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,radiology_finding,is_incidental_finding,is_incidental_finding,Incidental Finding Indicator,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,Indicates whether this finding was identified incidentally (outside the primary clinical indication for the imaging study). Drives ACR incidental finding management workflows and population health tracking.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,radiology_finding,laterality,laterality,Laterality,STRING,,,,LEFT|RIGHT|BILATERAL|MIDLINE|NOT_APPLICABLE,transactional_data,"Indicates the side of the body where the finding is located. Critical for surgical planning, follow-up tracking, and preventing wrong-site errors. Aligns with SNOMED CT laterality qualifiers.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,radiology_finding,measurement_unit,measurement_unit,Finding Measurement Unit,STRING,,,,mm|cm|mL|SUV|HU|OTHER,transactional_data,"Unit of measure for the measurement_value (e.g., mm for nodule diameter, HU for Hounsfield units on CT, SUV for PET standardized uptake value). Follows UCUM (Unified Code for Units of Measure) standards.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,radiology_finding,measurement_value,measurement_value,Finding Measurement Value,"DECIMAL(10,4)",,,,,transactional_data,"Principal quantitative measurement associated with the finding (e.g., nodule size in mm, lesion diameter, SUV max for PET findings). The unit is specified in measurement_unit. Supports size-based ACR scoring, trending, and growth rate analytics.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,radiology_finding,nlp_confidence_score,nlp_confidence_score,NLP Confidence Score,"DECIMAL(5,4)",,,,,transactional_data,"Confidence score (0.0000–1.0000) assigned by the NLP engine when data_source_method is NLP_EXTRACTED. Indicates the models certainty in the extracted finding. Used for quality filtering, human review routing, and AI/ML model validation.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,radiology_finding,patient_notification_timestamp,patient_notification_timestamp,Patient Notification Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,"Date and time when the patient was notified of this finding (e.g., via patient portal, phone, or letter). Supports 21st Century Cures Act compliance and patient engagement analytics.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,radiology_finding,patient_notified,patient_notified,Patient Notified Indicator,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,"Indicates whether the patient has been notified of this finding and any associated follow-up recommendations. Supports patient engagement, portal communication tracking, and regulatory compliance.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,radiology_finding,provider_notification_timestamp,provider_notification_timestamp,Provider Notification Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,Date and time when the ordering or responsible provider was notified of this finding. Supports critical result communication audit trails and TJC compliance documentation.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,radiology_finding,provider_notified,provider_notified,Ordering Provider Notified Indicator,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,Indicates whether the ordering or responsible provider has been notified of this finding and its follow-up recommendation. Required for critical result communication compliance per TJC NPSG.02.03.01.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,radiology_finding,report_finalized_timestamp,report_finalized_timestamp,Report Finalized Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,"Date and time when the radiology report containing this finding was finalized (signed/attested) by the interpreting radiologist. Used for turnaround time measurement, SLA compliance, and MIPS quality reporting.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,radiology_finding,severity,severity,Finding Severity,STRING,,,,MILD|MODERATE|SEVERE|CRITICAL|INDETERMINATE,transactional_data,"Clinical severity classification of the finding as assessed by the interpreting radiologist. Drives escalation workflows, follow-up urgency, and critical result notification processes.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,radiology_finding,source_system,source_system,Source System,STRING,,,,EPIC_RADIANT|CERNER_RADNET|MEDITECH|MANUAL|OTHER,transactional_data,"Identifies the operational system of record from which this finding record originated (e.g., EPIC_RADIANT, CERNER_RADNET, MEDITECH). Supports data lineage, ETL audit, and multi-system reconciliation in the lakehouse.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,radiology_finding,source_system_finding_code,source_system_finding_code,Source System Finding ID,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"The native identifier of this finding record in the originating operational system (e.g., Epic Radiant finding ID, Cerner RadNet observation ID). Supports ETL reconciliation, deduplication, and cross-system traceability.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,radiology_finding,study_date,study_date,Imaging Study Date,DATE,,,,,transactional_data,"The calendar date on which the imaging study was performed. Principal business event date for the finding. Used for follow-up interval calculation, trending, and population health reporting.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,radiology_finding,updated_timestamp,updated_timestamp,Record Updated Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,"Date and time when this radiology finding record was last modified in the data platform. Supports change detection, incremental ETL processing, and audit compliance.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,reader_assignment,reader_assignment_id,reader_assignment_id,Reader Assignment Identifier,BIGINT,Y,,,,transactional_data,Primary key for reader_assignment,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,reader_assignment,care_site_id,care_site_id,Facility ID,BIGINT,,facility.care_site.care_site_id,,,transactional_data,"Reference to the facility (hospital, imaging center, outpatient clinic) where the imaging study was performed. Used for facility-level TAT reporting, worklist segmentation, and operational analytics.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,reader_assignment,cpt_code_id,cpt_code_id,Cpt Code Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,reference.cpt_code.cpt_code_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to reference.cpt_code. Business justification: Radiologist assignments track CPT codes for workload balancing by procedure complexity, RVU-based productivity measurement, and subspecialty matching. Essential for radiologist compensation and staffi",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,reader_assignment,primary_reader_clinician_id,primary_reader_clinician_id,Radiologist Provider ID,BIGINT,,provider.clinician.clinician_id,,,transactional_data,Reference to the radiologist or reading provider assigned to interpret the imaging study. May reference an internal clinician or a teleradiology vendor reader.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,reader_assignment,prior_reader_assignment_id,prior_reader_assignment_id,Prior Assignment ID,BIGINT,,radiology.reader_assignment.reader_assignment_id,,,transactional_data,Reference to the previous reader_assignment record when this record represents a reassignment or second read. Enables chaining of assignment history for a single imaging study to support audit trails and TAT analysis.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,reader_assignment,radiology_study_id,radiology_study_id,Imaging Study ID,BIGINT,,radiology.radiology_study.radiology_study_id,,,transactional_data,Reference to the imaging study (accession) to which this reader assignment applies. Links the assignment to the specific diagnostic imaging order and PACS study.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,reader_assignment,report_id,report_id,Radiology Report ID,BIGINT,,radiology.report.report_id,,,transactional_data,Reference to the finalized radiology report generated as the output of this reader assignment. Links the assignment record to the report document in the RIS/PACS or clinical documentation system.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,reader_assignment,stark_arrangement_id,stark_arrangement_id,Stark Arrangement Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,compliance.stark_arrangement.stark_arrangement_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to compliance.stark_arrangement. Business justification: Radiologist reading assignments, especially teleradiology and overread arrangements, may involve Stark-regulated compensation. Compliance monitors whether assignment-based compensation meets fair mark",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,reader_assignment,visit_id,visit_id,Encounter ID,BIGINT,,encounter.visit.visit_id,,,transactional_data,Reference to the patient encounter (visit) associated with the imaging study being assigned for interpretation. Supports linkage to ADT and clinical context.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,reader_assignment,accession_number,accession_number,Radiology Accession Number,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"The RIS-assigned accession number uniquely identifying the imaging study within the radiology information system. Used as the primary business identifier for the study in Epic Radiant, Cerner RadNet, and PACS/DICOM workflows.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,reader_assignment,addendum_flag,addendum_flag,Report Addendum Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,Indicates whether an addendum was appended to the original radiology report after initial signing. True if an addendum exists; False otherwise. Supports HIM audit trails and clinical documentation integrity.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,reader_assignment,addendum_timestamp,addendum_timestamp,Report Addendum Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,Date and time when the most recent addendum was added to the radiology report. Populated only when addendum_flag is True. Used for HIM documentation tracking and clinical audit.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,reader_assignment,assigned_timestamp,assigned_timestamp,Assignment Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,Date and time when the radiologist was formally assigned to the imaging study. Serves as the start of the turnaround time (TAT) clock for SLA measurement. Stored in ISO 8601 format with timezone offset.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,reader_assignment,assignment_effective_date,assignment_effective_date,,DATE,,,"pii_phi,pii_pii,pii_sensitive",,transactional_data,description,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,reader_assignment,assignment_source,assignment_source,Assignment Source Method,STRING,,,,worklist_auto|manual|teleradiology_vendor|ai_routing|escalation,transactional_data,"Mechanism by which the radiologist was assigned to the study. Values: worklist_auto (RIS auto-assignment algorithm), manual (dispatcher or radiologist self-assignment), teleradiology_vendor (routed to external vendor), ai_routing (AI-assisted worklist routing), escalation (escalated from prior assignment). [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: worklist_auto|manual|teleradiology_vendor|ai_routing|escalation|stat_escalation|protocol_override — promote to reference product if values expand]",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,reader_assignment,assignment_status,assignment_status,Assignment Status,STRING,,,,assigned|in_progress|completed|cancelled|reassigned|pending,transactional_data,"Current lifecycle state of the reader assignment. Values: assigned (radiologist notified, not yet started), in_progress (read actively underway), completed (report finalized), cancelled (assignment voided), reassigned (transferred to another reader), pending (awaiting routing confirmation).",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,reader_assignment,assignment_type,assignment_type,Reader Assignment Type,STRING,,,,primary_read|second_read|peer_review|overread|teleradiology,transactional_data,"Classification of the reader assignment indicating the role of the radiologist relative to the study. Values: primary_read (initial interpretation), second_read (confirmatory read), peer_review (quality/audit read), overread (supervisory review), teleradiology (remote vendor read).",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,reader_assignment,body_part,body_part,Body Part Examined,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Anatomical body part or region examined in the imaging study, as coded in the RIS/PACS. Used for subspecialty routing, worklist filtering, and subspecialty match validation. Aligns with SNOMED CT anatomical site codes.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,reader_assignment,contrast_used,contrast_used,Contrast Administration Indicator,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,"Indicates whether contrast agent was administered during the imaging study. True if contrast was used; False for non-contrast studies. Relevant for CPT code selection, billing, and clinical interpretation context.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,reader_assignment,created_timestamp,created_timestamp,Record Created Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,Date and time when the reader assignment record was first created in the RIS or data platform. Serves as the audit trail creation timestamp per HIPAA and TJC record-keeping requirements.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,reader_assignment,critical_finding_flag,critical_finding_flag,Critical Finding Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,Indicates whether the radiologist identified a critical or urgent finding during interpretation that requires immediate clinical communication per ACR and TJC standards. True if a critical finding was flagged; False otherwise. Drives critical result notification workflows.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,reader_assignment,critical_finding_notified_timestamp,critical_finding_notified_timestamp,Critical Finding Notification Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,Date and time when the radiologist or RIS system notified the ordering provider of a critical imaging finding. Required for TJC and ACR compliance documentation. Populated only when critical_finding_flag is True.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,reader_assignment,dictation_method,dictation_method,Dictation Method,STRING,,,,voice_recognition|manual_transcription|structured_reporting|template,transactional_data,"Method used by the radiologist to generate the report for this assignment. Values: voice_recognition (real-time speech-to-text, e.g., Nuance PowerScribe), manual_transcription (transcriptionist-assisted), structured_reporting (form-based structured data entry), template (pre-built report template).",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,reader_assignment,image_count,image_count,DICOM Image Count,INT,,,,,transactional_data,Total number of DICOM image instances in the imaging study at the time of assignment. Used as a proxy for study complexity in radiologist workload and productivity analysis.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,reader_assignment,is_teleradiology,is_teleradiology,Teleradiology Assignment Indicator,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,Indicates whether this assignment was routed to an external teleradiology vendor rather than an internal radiologist. True for teleradiology assignments; False for internal reads. Drives vendor SLA tracking and billing differentiation.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,reader_assignment,modality,modality,Imaging Modality,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"The imaging modality of the study being assigned for interpretation. Standard DICOM modality codes: CT (Computed Tomography), MRI (Magnetic Resonance Imaging), XR/DX/CR (X-ray), US (Ultrasound), PET (Positron Emission Tomography), NM (Nuclear Medicine), MG (Mammography), FL (Fluoroscopy). [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: CT|MRI|XR|US|PET|NM|MG|FL|DX|CR|DEXA|OT — promote to reference product]",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,reader_assignment,pacs_study_uid,pacs_study_uid,Picture Archiving and Communication System (PACS) Study Instance UID,STRING,,,"pii_phi,pii_pii,pii_sensitive",^[0-9]+(.[0-9]+)+$,transactional_data,The globally unique DICOM Study Instance UID used to identify and retrieve the imaging study in the PACS. Enables direct linkage between the RIS assignment record and the PACS image archive for worklist integration and image retrieval.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,reader_assignment,peer_review_category,peer_review_category,Peer Review Discrepancy Category,STRING,,,,agree|minor_discrepancy|significant_discrepancy|major_discrepancy,transactional_data,Categorical classification of the peer review outcome indicating the level of agreement or discrepancy between the primary read and the peer reviewers interpretation. Supports quality improvement programs and radiologist performance monitoring.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,reader_assignment,peer_review_score,peer_review_score,Peer Review Score,STRING,,,,1|2|3|4|5,transactional_data,"Radiologist peer review quality score assigned during a peer review or overread assignment. Typically uses the ACR RADPEER scoring scale (1=agree, 2=minor discrepancy, 3=significant discrepancy, 4=major discrepancy). Populated only for peer_review and overread assignment types.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,reader_assignment,priority,priority,Study Read Priority,STRING,,,,stat|urgent|routine|scheduled,transactional_data,"Clinical priority level assigned to the imaging study read, driving worklist ordering and SLA target selection. Values: stat (immediate, life-threatening), urgent (expedited, clinically time-sensitive), routine (standard queue), scheduled (pre-planned elective read).",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,reader_assignment,radiation_dose_dlp,radiation_dose_dlp,Radiation Dose Length Product (DLP) mGy·cm,"DECIMAL(10,2)",,,,,transactional_data,"Dose Length Product (DLP) in mGy·cm recorded for CT studies, representing the total radiation dose delivered during the imaging acquisition. Used for radiation dose tracking, ACR Dose Index Registry reporting, and patient safety compliance.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,reader_assignment,read_complete_timestamp,read_complete_timestamp,Read Completion Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,Date and time when the radiologist completed the interpretation and the report was finalized or signed. Used as the end point for TAT SLA calculation.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,reader_assignment,read_start_timestamp,read_start_timestamp,Read Start Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,Date and time when the radiologist opened and began actively interpreting the imaging study in PACS or the RIS worklist. Used to measure time-to-read and radiologist productivity.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,reader_assignment,reading_site,reading_site,Reading Site Location,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Physical or virtual location from which the radiologist performed the interpretation (e.g., on-site reading room, remote home workstation, teleradiology hub). Distinct from the imaging facility; captures where the read occurred.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,reader_assignment,reassignment_reason,reassignment_reason,Reassignment Reason,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Free-text or coded reason why the study was reassigned from the originally assigned radiologist to another reader. Examples include radiologist unavailability, subspecialty escalation, conflict of interest, or workload rebalancing. Populated only when assignment_status is reassigned.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,reader_assignment,report_signed_timestamp,report_signed_timestamp,Report Signed Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,Date and time when the radiologist electronically signed and authenticated the final radiology report. Distinct from read_complete_timestamp as signing may occur after dictation/transcription. Supports HIM and compliance audit requirements.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,reader_assignment,rvu_value,rvu_value,Relative Value Unit (RVU) Value,"DECIMAL(8,4)",,,,,transactional_data,"The total Relative Value Unit (RVU) assigned to the CPT code for this interpretation, sourced from the CMS Physician Fee Schedule. Used for radiologist productivity measurement, compensation modeling, and departmental workload reporting.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,reader_assignment,sla_met,sla_met,Service Level Agreement (SLA) Met Indicator,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,Indicates whether the reader assignment was completed within the applicable SLA target turnaround time. True if tat_minutes is less than or equal to sla_target_minutes; False otherwise. Supports SLA compliance dashboards and vendor performance management.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,reader_assignment,sla_target_minutes,sla_target_minutes,Service Level Agreement (SLA) Target Minutes,INT,,,,,transactional_data,"The contractual or operational SLA target turnaround time in minutes applicable to this assignment, based on study priority, modality, and assignment type. Sourced from the applicable SLA contract or internal policy at time of assignment.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,reader_assignment,subspecialty_match,subspecialty_match,Subspecialty Match Indicator,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,"Indicates whether the assigned radiologists subspecialty certification matches the subspecialty required for the imaging study. True if matched; False if assigned outside subspecialty (e.g., general radiologist reading a neuroradiology study). Supports quality and credentialing compliance reporting.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,reader_assignment,subspecialty_required,subspecialty_required,Required Radiologist Subspecialty,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"The radiologist subspecialty required to interpret this imaging study (e.g., neuroradiology, musculoskeletal, breast imaging, interventional, nuclear medicine). Drives subspecialty-based worklist routing and teleradiology vendor selection.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,reader_assignment,tat_minutes,tat_minutes,Turnaround Time (TAT) Minutes,INT,,,,,transactional_data,Calculated turnaround time in minutes from study assignment to report completion. Stored as a pre-computed operational field (not a KPI aggregate) to support SLA compliance monitoring and worklist management without requiring real-time computation.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,reader_assignment,teleradiology_routing_reason,teleradiology_routing_reason,Teleradiology Routing Reason,STRING,,,,after_hours|subspecialty_gap|volume_overflow|coverage_gap|stat_backup,transactional_data,"Business reason why the study was routed to a teleradiology vendor rather than read internally. Values: after_hours (no internal radiologist available), subspecialty_gap (required subspecialty not available internally), volume_overflow (worklist capacity exceeded), coverage_gap (scheduled radiologist absent), stat_backup (emergency backup coverage).",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,reader_assignment,teleradiology_vendor_name,teleradiology_vendor_name,Teleradiology Vendor Name,STRING,,,"dbx_confidential,pii_phi,pii_pii,pii_sensitive",,transactional_data,Name of the external teleradiology vendor to whom the study was routed for interpretation. Populated only when is_teleradiology is True. Used for vendor performance management and contract SLA tracking.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,reader_assignment,updated_timestamp,updated_timestamp,Record Updated Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,Date and time when the reader assignment record was most recently modified. Supports change data capture (CDC) in the Databricks Silver Layer ETL pipeline and audit trail requirements.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,reader_assignment,vendor_accession_number,vendor_accession_number,Vendor Accession Number,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,The accession number assigned by the teleradiology vendors RIS to the study. Used for cross-referencing the internal RIS accession number with the vendors system for report reconciliation and image retrieval.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,reader_assignment,worklist_code,worklist_code,RIS Worklist ID,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,Identifier of the RIS worklist queue from which this assignment was generated or pulled. Used to trace the assignment back to its originating worklist configuration for routing audit and performance analysis.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,report,report_id,report_id,Report Identifier,BIGINT,Y,,,,transactional_data,Primary key for report,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,report,audit_finding_id,audit_finding_id,Audit Finding Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,compliance.audit_finding.audit_finding_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to compliance.audit_finding. Business justification: Radiology reports are audited for completeness, critical result communication timeliness, and documentation standards. TJC, state medical boards, and internal compliance programs audit reports for reg",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,report,clinical_order_id,clinical_order_id,Clinical Order Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,order.clinical_order.clinical_order_id,,,transactional_data,Foreign key linking to order.clinical_order. Business justification: Radiology reports document findings from ordered studies. Providers review results in context of original orders. Quality metrics track order-to-report turnaround times. Regulatory requirements for re,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,report,cost_center_id,cost_center_id,Cost Center Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,finance.cost_center.cost_center_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to finance.cost_center. Business justification: Radiology reports represent professional component work that must be allocated to radiologist cost centers for productivity-based costing, professional fee allocation, and departmental P&L. Critical f",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,report,cpt_code_id,cpt_code_id,Cpt Code Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,reference.cpt_code.cpt_code_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to reference.cpt_code. Business justification: Reports reference CPT codes for billing reconciliation between RIS and revenue cycle systems, support professional fee coding, and enable radiologist productivity tracking by procedure complexity and ",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,report,icd10_primary_icd_code_id,icd10_primary_icd_code_id,Icd10 Primary Icd Code Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,reference.icd_code.icd_code_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to reference.icd_code. Business justification: Reports document ICD-10 codes for clinical documentation integrity, support diagnosis-based quality measures, and enable population health analytics linking imaging findings to disease prevalence.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,report,imaging_order_id,imaging_order_id,Imaging Order ID,BIGINT,,radiology.imaging_order.imaging_order_id,,,transactional_data,Reference to the parent imaging order that triggered this radiology report. Links the report back to the order management workflow in the radiology domain.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,report,message_log_id,message_log_id,Health Level Seven (HL7) Observation Result Unsolicited (ORU) Message ID,BIGINT,,interoperability.message_log.message_log_id,,,transactional_data,"Unique identifier of the HL7 ORU^R01 message used to transmit the finalized radiology report to downstream clinical systems (EHR, ordering provider). Enables message traceability, deduplication, and integration audit. Sourced from the HL7 interface engine.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,report,primary_report_addendum_author_clinician_id,primary_report_addendum_author_clinician_id,Addendum Author ID,BIGINT,,provider.clinician.clinician_id,,,transactional_data,Reference to the provider who authored the addendum or amendment. May differ from the original signing radiologist. Null for the original report.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,report,radiology_study_id,radiology_study_id,Imaging Study Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,radiology.radiology_study.radiology_study_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to radiology.study. Business justification: report currently has imaging_order_id FK but no imaging_study_id FK. Radiology reports interpret STUDIES (the actual acquired images), not orders. One order can result in multiple studies (e.g., repea",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,report,report_care_site_id,report_care_site_id,Facility ID,BIGINT,,facility.care_site.care_site_id,,,transactional_data,"Reference to the facility (hospital, imaging center, outpatient clinic) where the imaging study was performed. Used for operational reporting, capacity management, and multi-site analytics.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,report,report_employee_id,report_employee_id,,BIGINT,,workforce.employee.employee_id,"confidential,pii",,transactional_data,FK to workforce.employee.employee_id,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,report,report_mpi_record_id,report_mpi_record_id,Patient ID,BIGINT,,patient.mpi_record.mpi_record_id,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_identifier",,transactional_data,Reference to the patient who is the subject of the imaging study and this report. Protected Health Information (PHI) under HIPAA. Links to the Master Patient Index (MPI).,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,report,report_performing_facility_care_site_id,report_performing_facility_care_site_id,,BIGINT,,facility.care_site.care_site_id,,,transactional_data,FK to facility.care_site.care_site_id,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,report,report_transcriptionist_employee_id,report_transcriptionist_employee_id,Transcriptionist Employee Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,workforce.employee.employee_id,"dbx_confidential, dbx_pii",,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to workforce.employee. Business justification: Radiology reports often dictated and transcribed by medical transcriptionists. Tracking needed for quality assurance, productivity monitoring, and error investigation when voice recognition not used.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,report,research_study_id,research_study_id,Research Study Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,research.research_study.research_study_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to research.research_study. Business justification: Radiology reports for research subjects require linkage for endpoint adjudication, independent imaging review, safety monitoring, and regulatory submissions. Reports may be blinded for trial integrity",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,report,tertiary_report_reading_radiologist_clinician_id,tertiary_report_reading_radiologist_clinician_id,Reading Radiologist ID,BIGINT,,provider.clinician.clinician_id,,,transactional_data,"Reference to the radiologist who performed the primary interpretation of the imaging study. May differ from the signing radiologist in teaching or supervisory contexts (e.g., resident reads, attending signs). Used for productivity tracking and RVU attribution.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,report,visit_id,visit_id,Encounter ID,BIGINT,,encounter.visit.visit_id,,,transactional_data,Reference to the clinical encounter (visit) during which the imaging study was ordered and performed. Enables linkage to the patient visit context for clinical and revenue cycle workflows.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,report,accession_number,accession_number,Accession Number,STRING,,,"pii_phi,pii_pii,pii_sensitive",,transactional_data,"Externally-known unique identifier assigned by the Radiology Information System (RIS) to the imaging order and its associated report. Used as the primary cross-system business key linking the report to the imaging order, PACS, and billing systems. Sourced from Epic Radiant and Cerner RadNet.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,report,addendum_sequence,addendum_sequence,Addendum Sequence Number,INT,,,,,transactional_data,Sequential number identifying the addendum within the reports amendment history. Null for the original report. Increments with each addendum or amendment added post-finalization. Used to order and display the full report amendment history.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,report,addendum_text,addendum_text,Addendum Text,STRING,,,"dbx_pii_health,dbx_restricted,pii_phi,pii_pii,pii_sensitive",,transactional_data,Full text content of the addendum or amendment added to the report post-finalization. Contains Protected Health Information (PHI). Null for the original report. Preserves the complete amendment history as versioned child records.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,report,addendum_timestamp,addendum_timestamp,Addendum Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,Date and time when the addendum or amendment was authored and signed. Null for the original report. Used to track the timeline of post-final modifications.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,report,addendum_type,addendum_type,Addendum Type,STRING,,,,addendum|amendment|correction|retraction,transactional_data,Classifies the type of post-final modification to the report. Addendum adds new information without changing the original; amendment modifies existing content; correction fixes a factual error; retraction withdraws the report. Null for the original report.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,report,attestation_timestamp,attestation_timestamp,Attestation Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,"Date and time when the signing radiologist attested and finalized the report, transitioning it to final status. This is the principal business event timestamp for the report lifecycle. Required for billing, legal, and compliance purposes.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,report,body_part,body_part,Body Part Examined,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Anatomical region or body part that was the subject of the imaging study (e.g., CHEST, ABDOMEN, BRAIN, KNEE). Sourced from DICOM tag (0018,0015) and RIS order. Used for clinical classification and CPT code validation.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,report,contrast_administered_flag,contrast_administered_flag,Contrast Administered Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,"Indicates whether contrast agent was administered during the imaging study. Relevant for CPT code selection, billing accuracy, radiation safety, and clinical documentation of contrast reactions.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,report,contrast_agent_name,contrast_agent_name,Contrast Agent Name,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Name of the contrast agent administered during the imaging study (e.g., Gadolinium, Iohexol, Gadobutrol). Null if no contrast was administered. Used for adverse event tracking, pharmacy reconciliation, and clinical documentation.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,report,created_timestamp,created_timestamp,Record Created Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,"Date and time when the radiology report record was first created in the source system. Represents the audit creation timestamp for the report entity. Used for data lineage, audit trails, and compliance reporting.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,report,critical_finding_communicated_flag,critical_finding_communicated_flag,Critical Finding Communicated Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,Indicates whether the critical finding has been communicated to the ordering or responsible provider. Required for Joint Commission compliance. Only applicable when critical_finding_flag is True.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,report,critical_finding_communicated_timestamp,critical_finding_communicated_timestamp,Critical Finding Communication Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,Date and time when the critical finding was communicated to the ordering or responsible provider. Used to measure turnaround time compliance with Joint Commission and ACR critical results communication standards.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,report,critical_finding_flag,critical_finding_flag,Critical Finding Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,"Indicates whether the report contains a critical or urgent finding that requires immediate communication to the ordering provider per ACR and Joint Commission guidelines. When True, triggers a critical results notification workflow. Supports patient safety and regulatory compliance.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,report,dicom_study_instance_uid,dicom_study_instance_uid,DICOM Study Instance Unique Identifier (UID),STRING,,,"pii_phi,pii_pii,pii_sensitive",,transactional_data,"Globally unique DICOM Study Instance UID linking this report to the corresponding image set in the Picture Archiving and Communication System (PACS). Enables direct navigation from the report to the source images. Sourced from DICOM tag (0020,000D).",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,report,dictation_timestamp,dictation_timestamp,Dictation Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,Date and time when the radiologist began dictating the report. Used to measure report turnaround time (TAT) from study completion to dictation. Sourced from Epic Radiant or Cerner RadNet workflow timestamps.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,report,findings_text,findings_text,Findings Narrative Text,STRING,,,"dbx_pii_health,dbx_restricted,pii_phi,pii_pii,pii_sensitive",,transactional_data,"Full narrative text of the radiologists findings section of the report, describing the imaging observations in detail. Contains Protected Health Information (PHI). This is the primary clinical content of the report and the source of truth for diagnostic observations. Sourced from Epic ClinDoc or Cerner PowerChart dictation/transcription.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,report,follow_up_recommendation,follow_up_recommendation,Follow-Up Recommendation,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Structured follow-up recommendation from the radiologists impression, indicating the recommended next action (e.g., Follow-up CT in 3 months, Biopsy recommended, No follow-up needed). Used for care coordination, population health management, and closing the loop on incidental findings.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,report,impression_text,impression_text,Impression Text,STRING,,,"dbx_pii_health,dbx_restricted,pii_phi,pii_pii,pii_sensitive",,transactional_data,"Radiologists summary impression or conclusion section of the report, providing the diagnostic interpretation and clinical recommendations. Contains Protected Health Information (PHI). This is the most clinically actionable section of the report and is used for clinical decision support, CDI, and quality measurement.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,report,laterality,laterality,Laterality,STRING,,,,left|right|bilateral|unspecified,transactional_data,"Indicates the side of the body examined when applicable (left, right, bilateral, or unspecified). Critical for surgical safety, billing accuracy, and clinical documentation. Sourced from DICOM tag (0020,0060) and RIS.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,report,modality_code,modality_code,Imaging Modality Code,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"DICOM-standard code identifying the imaging modality used for the study (e.g., CT = Computed Tomography, MR = Magnetic Resonance Imaging, XR/DX/CR = X-Ray, US = Ultrasound, PT = Positron Emission Tomography, NM = Nuclear Medicine, MG = Mammography, FL = Fluoroscopy). Sourced from DICOM tag (0008,0060). [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: CT|MR|XR|US|PT|NM|MG|FL|DX|CR — 10 candidates stripped; promote to reference product]",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,report,preliminary_timestamp,preliminary_timestamp,Preliminary Report Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,"Date and time when the report was first released in preliminary status, making it available to ordering providers before final attestation. Key lifecycle event for TAT measurement and clinical workflow.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,report,radiation_dose_ctdi,radiation_dose_ctdi,Radiation Dose CT Dose Index Volume (CTDIvol) mGy,"DECIMAL(10,4)",,,,,transactional_data,CT Dose Index Volume (CTDIvol) in mGy representing the average radiation dose per unit length for CT studies. Null for non-CT modalities. Used alongside DLP for comprehensive radiation dose monitoring and ACR Dose Index Registry reporting.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,report,radiation_dose_dlp,radiation_dose_dlp,Radiation Dose Dose Length Product (DLP) mGy·cm,"DECIMAL(10,4)",,,,,transactional_data,"Dose Length Product (DLP) in mGy·cm representing the total radiation dose delivered during the CT or fluoroscopy study. Null for non-ionizing modalities (MRI, Ultrasound). Used for radiation dose monitoring, ACR Dose Index Registry reporting, and patient safety compliance.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,report,rads_category,rads_category,Reporting and Data System (RADS) Category,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Standardized ACR Reporting and Data System (RADS) assessment category assigned in the impression (e.g., BI-RADS 0-6 for mammography, LI-RADS 1-5 for liver, TI-RADS 1-5 for thyroid, Lung-RADS 1-4). Drives follow-up recommendations and quality measurement. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: BI-RADS 0|BI-RADS 1|BI-RADS 2|BI-RADS 3|BI-RADS 4|BI-RADS 5|BI-RADS 6|LI-RADS 1|LI-RADS 2|LI-RADS 3|LI-RADS 4|LI-RADS 5|TI-RADS 1|TI-RADS 2|TI-RADS 3|TI-RADS 4|TI-RADS 5|Lung-RADS 1|Lung-RADS 2|Lung-RADS 3|Lung-RADS 4 — promote to reference product]",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,report,report_status,report_status,Report Status,STRING,,,,preliminary|final|addendum|amended|corrected|cancelled,transactional_data,"Current workflow state of the radiology report. Drives clinical decision-making and downstream notification workflows. Preliminary indicates a draft interpretation; final indicates the signed, attested report; addendum and amended indicate post-final modifications. Aligns with HL7 FHIR DiagnosticReport.status.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,report,ris_report_code,ris_report_code,Radiology Information System (RIS) Report ID,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Native report identifier from the source Radiology Information System (RIS), such as Epic Radiant or Cerner RadNet. Used for cross-system reconciliation, ETL lineage tracking, and source system audit.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,report,signing_radiologist_npi,signing_radiologist_npi,Signing Radiologist National Provider Identifier (NPI),STRING,,,"pii_phi,pii_pii,pii_sensitive",^[0-9]{10}$,transactional_data,"10-digit National Provider Identifier (NPI) of the radiologist who signed and attested the final report. Required for CMS billing, claims submission, and provider credentialing validation. Sourced from the NPPES registry.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,report,stat_priority_flag,stat_priority_flag,STAT Priority Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,"Indicates whether the imaging order and report were designated as STAT (immediate/urgent priority), requiring expedited turnaround time. Drives workflow prioritization in the RIS and radiologist worklist. Used for TAT compliance monitoring.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,report,study_datetime,study_datetime,Study Date and Time,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,"Date and time when the imaging study was performed (image acquisition). This is the principal real-world event time for the report. Sourced from DICOM tag (0008,0020)/(0008,0030) and RIS. Used as the primary temporal anchor for TAT calculations and clinical timelines.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,report,study_description,study_description,Study Description,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Human-readable description of the imaging study protocol or procedure performed (e.g., CT Chest with Contrast, MRI Brain without Contrast). Sourced from the RIS order and DICOM tag (0008,1030). Used for report titling and clinical context.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,report,template_code,template_code,Report Template ID,BIGINT,,,,,transactional_data,"Reference to the structured reporting template used to generate the report (e.g., ACR-standardized templates, site-specific templates). Supports structured reporting initiatives, quality measurement, and AI-assisted reporting workflows.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,report,transcription_timestamp,transcription_timestamp,Transcription Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,Date and time when the report transcription was completed (if applicable). Relevant for facilities using human transcription services rather than voice recognition. Used in TAT measurement.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,report,updated_timestamp,updated_timestamp,Record Updated Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,"Date and time when the radiology report record was last modified in the source system. Used for incremental data loading, change data capture (CDC), and audit trail maintenance.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,report,version,version,Report Version Number,INT,,,,,transactional_data,"Sequential version number of the report, starting at 1 for the initial report and incrementing with each amendment or addendum. Enables tracking of the full amendment history and identification of the current authoritative version.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,report_addendum,report_addendum_id,report_addendum_id,Report Addendum ID,BIGINT,Y,,,,transactional_data,Unique surrogate identifier for each radiology report addendum record in the Silver Layer lakehouse. Primary key for this entity.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,report_addendum,audit_finding_id,audit_finding_id,Audit Finding Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,compliance.audit_finding.audit_finding_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to compliance.audit_finding. Business justification: Report addenda are audited for timeliness, appropriateness, and medical record integrity. Compliance monitors addendum practices to ensure proper documentation standards and regulatory compliance.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,report_addendum,care_site_id,care_site_id,Facility ID,BIGINT,,facility.care_site.care_site_id,,,transactional_data,"Reference to the healthcare facility (hospital, imaging center, outpatient clinic) where the original imaging study was performed and the addendum was issued. Supports multi-facility enterprise reporting and regulatory submissions.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,report_addendum,cda_document_id,cda_document_id,Cda Document Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,interoperability.cda_document.cda_document_id,,,transactional_data,Foreign key linking to interoperability.cda_document. Business justification: Report addenda generate separate CDA document versions (replacement or addendum document types) for HIE transmission. Required for regulatory compliance and ensuring downstream systems receive correct,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,report_addendum,cdi_query_id,cdi_query_id,Clinical Documentation Improvement (CDI) Query ID,BIGINT,,clinical.cdi_query.cdi_query_id,,,transactional_data,"Reference to the CDI (Clinical Documentation Improvement) query that prompted this addendum, if applicable. Links the addendum to the CDI workflow for documentation quality tracking and DRG (Diagnosis-Related Group) impact analysis.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,report_addendum,cpt_code_id,cpt_code_id,Cpt Code Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,reference.cpt_code.cpt_code_id,,,transactional_data,Foreign key linking to reference.cpt_code. Business justification: Addenda may reference procedure codes when clarifying exam scope or correcting billing. Supports revenue integrity audits and ensures addendum changes are reflected in charge capture systems.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,report_addendum,icd10_icd_code_id,icd10_icd_code_id,Icd10 Icd Code Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,reference.icd_code.icd_code_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to reference.icd_code. Business justification: Addenda may update or clarify diagnosis codes for CDI queries, DRG impact analysis, and billing corrections. Links support amendment tracking and diagnosis code change auditing for compliance.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,report_addendum,message_log_id,message_log_id,HL7 Message ID,BIGINT,,interoperability.message_log.message_log_id,,,transactional_data,"Unique identifier of the HL7 (Health Level Seven) ORU or MDM message used to transmit this addendum between systems (e.g., from RIS to EHR via HL7 v2.x or FHIR). Supports interoperability audit and HIE (Health Information Exchange) traceability.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,report_addendum,mpi_record_id,mpi_record_id,Patient ID,BIGINT,,patient.mpi_record.mpi_record_id,,,transactional_data,Reference to the patient whose imaging study and original report are being amended. Required for PHI (Protected Health Information) audit trails and HIM (Health Information Management) compliance.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,report_addendum,org_unit_id,org_unit_id,Radiology Department ID,BIGINT,,workforce.org_unit.org_unit_id,,,transactional_data,Reference to the radiology department or imaging section within the facility where the addendum was issued. Supports departmental performance analytics and CDI program management.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,report_addendum,primary_report_clinician_id,primary_report_clinician_id,Addendum Author Provider ID,BIGINT,,provider.clinician.clinician_id,,,transactional_data,Internal provider identifier for the radiologist or clinician who authored this addendum. Complements author_npi for internal system linkage to the provider master.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,report_addendum,report_id,report_id,Original Radiology Report ID,BIGINT,,radiology.report.report_id,,,transactional_data,Reference to the finalized radiology report to which this addendum is appended. Links the addendum to its parent report for audit and CDI (Clinical Documentation Improvement) traceability.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,report_addendum,tertiary_report_ordering_provider_clinician_id,tertiary_report_ordering_provider_clinician_id,Ordering Provider ID,BIGINT,,provider.clinician.clinician_id,,,transactional_data,"Internal provider identifier for the clinician who placed the original imaging order. Required to determine notification obligations when an addendum is issued, per ACR communication guidelines.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,report_addendum,visit_id,visit_id,Encounter ID,BIGINT,,encounter.visit.visit_id,,,transactional_data,Reference to the patient encounter (visit) during which the original imaging study was ordered. Supports clinical context linkage for CDI and quality reporting.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,report_addendum,accession_number,accession_number,Accession Number,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,RIS (Radiology Information System)-assigned accession number of the imaging order associated with the original report. Used to correlate the addendum back to the imaging study in Epic Radiant or Cerner RadNet.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,report_addendum,acknowledgment_datetime,acknowledgment_datetime,Provider Acknowledgment Date and Time,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,Date and time when the ordering provider acknowledged receipt of the addendum notification. Nullable until acknowledged. Critical for closed-loop communication compliance per ACR and TJC standards.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,report_addendum,addendum_datetime,addendum_datetime,Addendum Date and Time,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,Date and time when the addendum was authored and entered into the RIS/EHR system. Represents the principal business event timestamp for this transaction. Stored in ISO 8601 format (yyyy-MM-ddTHH:mm:ss.SSSXXX).,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,report_addendum,addendum_sequence_number,addendum_sequence_number,Addendum Sequence Number,INT,,,,,transactional_data,"Sequential integer indicating the order of this addendum relative to other addenda on the same original report (e.g., 1 = first addendum, 2 = second addendum). Supports multi-addendum tracking and version ordering.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,report_addendum,addendum_status,addendum_status,Addendum Status,STRING,,,,draft|pending_review|finalized|retracted,transactional_data,Current workflow lifecycle state of the addendum. draft = authored but not yet signed; pending_review = awaiting co-signature or peer review; finalized = signed and locked; retracted = addendum itself has been withdrawn.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,report_addendum,addendum_text,addendum_text,Addendum Text,STRING,,,"dbx_pii_health,dbx_restricted,pii_phi,pii_pii,pii_sensitive",,transactional_data,Full narrative text of the addendum as authored by the radiologist. Contains PHI (Protected Health Information) and clinical findings. Supports CDI (Clinical Documentation Improvement) workflows and HIM audit requirements.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,report_addendum,addendum_type,addendum_type,Addendum Type,STRING,,,,correction|clarification|clinical_update|addendum|retraction,transactional_data,Categorical classification of the addendum indicating its clinical purpose. correction = factual error corrected; clarification = ambiguous language clarified; clinical_update = new clinical information incorporated; addendum = supplemental information added; retraction = prior finding retracted. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: correction|clarification|clinical_update|addendum|retraction — promote to reference product if additional types emerge],
radiology,interpretation_reporting,report_addendum,addendum_word_count,addendum_word_count,Addendum Word Count,INT,,,,,transactional_data,"Number of words in the addendum text. Used for documentation completeness analytics, CDI program metrics, and radiologist productivity reporting. Derived at ingestion time from addendum_text.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,report_addendum,amendment_reason,amendment_reason,Amendment Reason,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Free-text or structured explanation of why the original report required amendment. Documents the clinical or administrative rationale (e.g., Transcription error in laterality, New clinical history provided by ordering physician). Required for HIM audit and OIG (Office of Inspector General) compliance.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,report_addendum,amendment_reason_code,amendment_reason_code,Amendment Reason Code,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Standardized code categorizing the reason for amendment, enabling structured reporting and quality analytics. Complements the free-text amendment_reason field. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: transcription_error|laterality_error|clinical_history_update|measurement_correction|impression_revision|additional_finding|provider_request|other — promote to reference product]",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,report_addendum,author_npi,author_npi,Addendum Author National Provider Identifier (NPI),STRING,,,"dbx_confidential,pii_phi,pii_pii,pii_sensitive",^[0-9]{10}$,transactional_data,"10-digit NPI (National Provider Identifier) of the radiologist or clinician who authored this addendum. Required for provider attribution, credentialing validation, and CMS (Centers for Medicare and Medicaid Services) billing compliance.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,report_addendum,body_part,body_part,Body Part Examined,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Anatomical body part or region examined in the original imaging study (e.g., CHEST, ABDOMEN, BRAIN, SPINE). Derived from DICOM tag (0018,0015) BodyPartExamined. Supports anatomical-level quality and utilization analytics.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,report_addendum,created_timestamp,created_timestamp,Record Created Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,System timestamp when this addendum record was first created in the data platform. Used for audit trail and data lineage tracking per HIPAA and HIM requirements.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,report_addendum,critical_finding_flag,critical_finding_flag,Critical Finding Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,"Indicates whether this addendum contains or introduces a critical or urgent finding requiring immediate clinical action. When True, triggers expedited notification workflows per ACR and TJC critical results communication standards.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,report_addendum,dicom_study_instance_uid,dicom_study_instance_uid,DICOM Study Instance UID,STRING,,,,^[0-9]+(.[0-9]+)+$,transactional_data,Globally unique DICOM (Digital Imaging and Communications in Medicine) Study Instance UID of the imaging study associated with the original report. Enables direct linkage to PACS (Picture Archiving and Communication System) for image retrieval and addendum context.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,report_addendum,drg_impact_flag,drg_impact_flag,Diagnosis-Related Group (DRG) Impact Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,"Indicates whether this addendum has the potential to change the DRG (Diagnosis-Related Group) assignment for the associated inpatient encounter, affecting reimbursement. True = DRG may be affected; False = no DRG impact anticipated. Supports RCM (Revenue Cycle Management) and CDI analytics.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,report_addendum,finalized_datetime,finalized_datetime,Addendum Finalized Date and Time,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,Date and time when the addendum was electronically signed and finalized by the authoring radiologist. Distinct from addendum_datetime (authoring time) — captures the attestation event for HIM audit and legal record purposes.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,report_addendum,him_review_datetime,him_review_datetime,Health Information Management (HIM) Review Date and Time,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,Date and time when the HIM department completed its review of this addendum. Nullable until HIM review is performed. Supports HIM audit trail and CDI workflow tracking.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,report_addendum,him_review_flag,him_review_flag,Health Information Management (HIM) Review Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,"Indicates whether this addendum has been flagged for review by the HIM (Health Information Management) department for coding accuracy, documentation integrity, or compliance purposes.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,report_addendum,impression_changed_flag,impression_changed_flag,Impression Changed Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,Indicates whether the addendum materially changes the clinical impression or diagnosis of the original report. True = impression revised; False = addendum is supplemental or administrative only. Key metric for CDI quality analytics and RAC (Recovery Audit Contractor) review.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,report_addendum,laterality,laterality,Laterality,STRING,,,,left|right|bilateral|not_applicable,transactional_data,"Laterality of the anatomical region examined (left, right, bilateral, or not applicable). Frequently the subject of addenda when laterality errors are identified in the original report. Supports patient safety and HIM audit workflows.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,report_addendum,modality,modality,Imaging Modality,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Imaging modality of the original study being amended (e.g., CT = Computed Tomography, MRI = Magnetic Resonance Imaging, XR = X-Ray, US = Ultrasound, PET = Positron Emission Tomography). Supports modality-level quality analytics and ACR benchmarking. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: CT|MRI|XR|US|PET|NM|MG|FL|DX|other — promote to reference product]",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,report_addendum,notification_datetime,notification_datetime,Ordering Provider Notification Date and Time,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,Date and time when the notification of this addendum was dispatched to the ordering provider. Nullable when notification_status is not_required. Supports ACR communication audit trail.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,report_addendum,notification_method,notification_method,Notification Method,STRING,,,,in_basket|secure_message|phone|fax|ehr_alert|email,transactional_data,"Channel or method used to notify the ordering provider of the addendum (e.g., Epic In Basket message, secure message, phone call, fax). Supports communication audit and ACR compliance documentation.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,report_addendum,notification_status,notification_status,Ordering Provider Notification Status,STRING,,,,not_required|pending|sent|acknowledged|failed,transactional_data,Status of notification sent to the ordering provider regarding this addendum. not_required = no notification needed per policy; pending = notification queued; sent = notification dispatched; acknowledged = provider confirmed receipt; failed = notification delivery failed. Supports ACR communication compliance.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,report_addendum,original_report_finalized_datetime,original_report_finalized_datetime,Original Report Finalized Date and Time,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,"Date and time when the original radiology report was finalized prior to this addendum. Used to calculate turnaround time between original finalization and addendum, supporting quality metrics and ACR (American College of Radiology) benchmarking.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,report_addendum,peer_review_flag,peer_review_flag,Peer Review Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,"Indicates whether this addendum was generated as a result of a formal peer review process (e.g., ACR RADPEER, internal quality review). True = peer review initiated; False = standard clinical addendum. Supports quality program analytics.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,report_addendum,peer_review_score,peer_review_score,Peer Review Score,STRING,,,,1|2a|2b|3a|3b|4,transactional_data,"ACR RADPEER concordance score assigned during peer review, if applicable. Scale: 1 = agree with interpretation; 2a/2b = minor discrepancy; 3a/3b = significant discrepancy; 4 = major discrepancy. Nullable when peer_review_flag is False.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,report_addendum,source_system,source_system,Source System,STRING,,,,epic_radiant|cerner_radnet|meditech|other,transactional_data,"Operational system of record from which this addendum record was sourced (e.g., Epic Radiant, Cerner RadNet, MEDITECH Expanse). Supports data lineage and ETL (Extract Transform Load) provenance tracking in the Silver Layer.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,report_addendum,source_system_addendum_code,source_system_addendum_code,Source System Addendum ID,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Native identifier of this addendum record in the originating operational system (e.g., Epic Radiant internal addendum ID, Cerner RadNet addendum key). Enables reconciliation between the lakehouse Silver Layer and the source RIS/EHR.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,report_addendum,updated_timestamp,updated_timestamp,Record Updated Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,System timestamp when this addendum record was last modified in the data platform. Supports change detection and incremental ETL (Extract Transform Load) processing.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,report_addendum,voice_recognition_flag,voice_recognition_flag,Voice Recognition Dictation Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,"Indicates whether this addendum was authored using voice recognition / speech-to-text dictation software (e.g., Nuance PowerScribe, Nuance DAX). True = voice recognition used; False = manually typed. Supports transcription error root cause analysis.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,report_distribution,report_distribution_id,report_distribution_id,Report Distribution - Report Distribution Id,BIGINT,Y,,,,association_data,Primary key for the report_distribution association,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,report_distribution,message_log_id,message_log_id,Message ID,BIGINT,,interoperability.message_log.message_log_id,,,association_data,"Unique identifier for the HL7/FHIR message sent to this trading partner for this report. Used for message tracking, troubleshooting, and correlation with partner acknowledgments.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,report_distribution,report_id,report_id,Report Distribution - Radiology Report Id,BIGINT,,radiology.report.report_id,,,association_data,Foreign key linking to the radiology report being distributed to external partners,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,report_distribution,trading_partner_id,trading_partner_id,Report Distribution - Trading Partner Id,BIGINT,,interoperability.trading_partner.trading_partner_id,,,association_data,Foreign key linking to the external trading partner receiving the report,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,report_distribution,acknowledgment_code,acknowledgment_code,Acknowledgment Code,STRING,,,,,association_data,"HL7 acknowledgment code returned by the trading partner (AA=Application Accept, AE=Application Error, AR=Application Reject). Used for troubleshooting failed transmissions and partner-specific delivery issues.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,report_distribution,delivered_timestamp,delivered_timestamp,Delivered Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,association_data,Date and time when the trading partner acknowledged successful receipt and processing of the report. Null if not yet acknowledged. Used to calculate end-to-end delivery time.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,report_distribution,delivery_status,delivery_status,Delivery Status,STRING,,,,,association_data,"Current status of the report delivery to this trading partner. Tracks the lifecycle from initial transmission through acknowledgment or failure. Values: pending, transmitted, acknowledged, failed, retrying, delivered.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,report_distribution,document_format,document_format,Document Format,STRING,,,,,association_data,"Interoperability standard format used to transmit the report to this specific trading partner. Different partners may receive the same report in different formats based on their capabilities and data sharing agreements. Values: CDA, HL7v2, FHIR, Direct, PDF.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,report_distribution,error_message,error_message,Error Message,STRING,,,,,association_data,Detailed error message returned by the trading partner or interface engine if delivery failed. Used for troubleshooting and partner support escalation.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,report_distribution,retry_count,retry_count,Retry Count,INT,,,,,association_data,Number of transmission retry attempts for this specific report-partner distribution. Used to identify problematic partner connections and trigger escalation workflows after threshold exceeded.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,report_distribution,sla_compliance_flag,sla_compliance_flag,SLA Compliance Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,association_data,Indicates whether the report was delivered to this trading partner within the contractual SLA timeframe specified in the data sharing agreement. Used for partner performance monitoring and contract compliance reporting.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,report_distribution,transmission_timestamp,transmission_timestamp,Transmission Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,association_data,Date and time when the radiology report was transmitted to this specific trading partner. Critical for SLA tracking and audit trail of when each partner received the report.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,teleradiology_case,teleradiology_case_id,teleradiology_case_id,Teleradiology Case ID,BIGINT,Y,,,,transactional_data,Unique surrogate identifier for the teleradiology case record in the lakehouse silver layer. Primary key for this entity.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,teleradiology_case,ap_invoice_id,ap_invoice_id,Ap Invoice Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,finance.ap_invoice.ap_invoice_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to finance.ap_invoice. Business justification: Teleradiology vendor professional reading services generate accounts payable invoices that must be matched to specific cases for three-way matching (case/contract/invoice), vendor payment processing, ",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,teleradiology_case,business_associate_agreement_id,business_associate_agreement_id,Business Associate Agreement Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,compliance.business_associate_agreement.business_associate_agreement_id,,,transactional_data,Foreign key linking to compliance.business_associate_agreement. Business justification: Teleradiology vendors are HIPAA business associates requiring executed BAAs. Compliance tracks which BAA governs each vendor relationship; teleradiology cases must reference the governing BAA for audi,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,teleradiology_case,care_site_id,care_site_id,Originating Facility ID,BIGINT,,facility.care_site.care_site_id,,,transactional_data,"Reference to the facility (hospital, clinic, or imaging center) from which the imaging study was transmitted to the teleradiology vendor. Used for facility-level SLA reporting and volume analytics.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,teleradiology_case,clinician_id,clinician_id,Ordering Provider ID,BIGINT,,provider.clinician.clinician_id,,,transactional_data,Reference to the clinician who placed the imaging order that triggered this teleradiology case. Used for provider-level utilization reporting and clinical communication of results.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,teleradiology_case,cpt_code_id,cpt_code_id,Cpt Code Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,reference.cpt_code.cpt_code_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to reference.cpt_code. Business justification: Teleradiology cases are billed using CPT codes for vendor invoicing reconciliation, professional component billing, and contract compliance verification. Essential for teleradiology financial manageme",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,teleradiology_case,demographics_id,demographics_id,Patient ID,BIGINT,,patient.demographics.demographics_id,,,transactional_data,Reference to the patient whose imaging study is being interpreted via teleradiology. Supports patient-level reporting and PHI governance.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,teleradiology_case,employee_id,employee_id,Case Coordinator Employee Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,workforce.employee.employee_id,"dbx_confidential, dbx_pii",,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to workforce.employee. Business justification: Teleradiology cases require internal coordinators to manage vendor handoffs, image transmission, report reconciliation, and escalation. Distinct operational role from interpreting radiologist.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,teleradiology_case,imaging_order_id,imaging_order_id,Imaging Order ID,BIGINT,,radiology.imaging_order.imaging_order_id,,,transactional_data,Reference to the originating radiology order that triggered this teleradiology routing. Links the teleradiology case to the parent imaging order in the RIS.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,teleradiology_case,message_log_id,message_log_id,Message Log Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,interoperability.message_log.message_log_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to interoperability.message_log. Business justification: Teleradiology DICOM transmissions (study send/receive) and HL7 result messages are logged for vendor SLA tracking, transmission success monitoring, and billing reconciliation. Message_log provides aud",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,teleradiology_case,payer_contract_id,payer_contract_id,Payer Contract Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,insurance.payer_contract.payer_contract_id,,,transactional_data,Foreign key linking to insurance.payer_contract. Business justification: Teleradiology professional component billing responsibility and reimbursement rates are governed by specific payer contracts. Vendor_contract_id covers vendor relationship; payer_contract_id needed fo,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,teleradiology_case,stark_arrangement_id,stark_arrangement_id,Stark Arrangement Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,compliance.stark_arrangement.stark_arrangement_id,,,transactional_data,Foreign key linking to compliance.stark_arrangement. Business justification: Teleradiology contracts often involve Stark-regulated physician compensation arrangements. Compliance reviews teleradiology case volume and compensation to ensure arrangements meet fair market value a,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,teleradiology_case,vendor_contract_id,vendor_contract_id,Vendor Contract ID,BIGINT,,supply.vendor_contract.vendor_contract_id,dbx_confidential,,transactional_data,"The contract or agreement identifier governing the teleradiology services provided by the vendor for this case. Used to associate the case with specific SLA terms, pricing schedules, and billing responsibility clauses.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,teleradiology_case,vendor_id,vendor_id,Teleradiology Vendor ID,BIGINT,,supply.vendor.vendor_id,,,transactional_data,Reference to the teleradiology vendor or remote reading group to whom this study was routed. Links to the vendor master for contract and SLA management.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,teleradiology_case,visit_id,visit_id,Visit ID,BIGINT,,encounter.visit.visit_id,,,transactional_data,Reference to the patient encounter or visit associated with this imaging study. Supports linkage to encounter-level clinical and billing context.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,teleradiology_case,accession_number,accession_number,Accession Number,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,The RIS-assigned accession number that uniquely identifies the imaging study within the originating facility. Used to correlate the teleradiology case back to the local RIS/PACS order.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,teleradiology_case,actual_tat_minutes,actual_tat_minutes,Actual Turnaround Time (TAT) in Minutes,INT,,,,,transactional_data,The measured turnaround time in minutes from study transmission datetime to final report received datetime. Compared against expected_tat_minutes to determine SLA compliance status.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,teleradiology_case,billing_responsibility,billing_responsibility,Professional Component Billing Responsibility,STRING,,,,vendor|facility|shared|not_applicable,transactional_data,"Designates which party owns the professional component (PC) billing responsibility for the radiology interpretation: the teleradiology vendor, the originating facility, or a shared arrangement. Critical for revenue cycle management and claim submission.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,teleradiology_case,body_part,body_part,Body Part Examined,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"The anatomical region or body part that is the subject of the imaging study, as coded in the DICOM header or RIS order. Used for subspecialty routing and procedure-level reporting.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,teleradiology_case,case_status,case_status,Teleradiology Case Status,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Current workflow status of the teleradiology case, tracking progression from transmission through final report reconciliation. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: transmitted|received|in_interpretation|preliminary_reported|final_reported|reconciled|cancelled — promote to reference product]",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,teleradiology_case,clinical_indication,clinical_indication,Clinical Indication,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,Free-text or coded clinical indication or reason for the imaging study as documented in the radiology order. Provides clinical context to the remote radiologist and supports appropriateness criteria evaluation.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,teleradiology_case,created_timestamp,created_timestamp,Record Created Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,"The date and time at which this teleradiology case record was first created in the system, typically coinciding with the routing decision. Audit trail field for data governance and lineage.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,teleradiology_case,critical_finding_flag,critical_finding_flag,Critical Finding Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,Boolean flag indicating whether the teleradiology report contains a critical or urgent finding requiring immediate clinical notification per ACR and Joint Commission communication standards. Triggers critical results notification workflows.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,teleradiology_case,critical_finding_notified_datetime,critical_finding_notified_datetime,Critical Finding Notification Datetime,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,The date and time at which the ordering provider or clinical team was notified of a critical imaging finding. Required for Joint Commission NPSG compliance documentation. Null when critical_finding_flag is False.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,teleradiology_case,dicom_study_uid,dicom_study_uid,DICOM Study Instance Unique Identifier (UID),STRING,,,"pii_phi,pii_pii,pii_sensitive",,transactional_data,"The globally unique DICOM Study Instance UID (0020,000D) that identifies the imaging study across PACS systems. Used for PACS-to-PACS transmission tracking and image retrieval reconciliation.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,teleradiology_case,discrepancy_category,discrepancy_category,Discrepancy Category,STRING,,,,major|minor|none,transactional_data,Classification of the reconciliation discrepancy severity when reconciliation_discrepancy_flag is True. Major discrepancies represent clinically significant differences that may affect patient management; minor discrepancies are interpretive differences without clinical impact.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,teleradiology_case,expected_tat_minutes,expected_tat_minutes,Expected Turnaround Time (TAT) in Minutes,INT,,,,,transactional_data,"The contractually agreed or SLA-defined turnaround time (TAT) in minutes from study transmission to final report delivery, as specified in the vendor contract for the applicable priority level and modality.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,teleradiology_case,final_report_datetime,final_report_datetime,Final Report Received Datetime,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,"The date and time at which the final, authenticated radiology report was received from the teleradiology vendor. Used to measure final TAT compliance and trigger report reconciliation workflows.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,teleradiology_case,final_report_text,final_report_text,Final Report Text,STRING,,,"dbx_pii_health,dbx_restricted,pii_phi,pii_pii,pii_sensitive",,transactional_data,"The verbatim text of the final, authenticated radiology report received from the teleradiology vendor. Contains PHI and the definitive radiological interpretation. Used for clinical decision-making, reconciliation, and medical record documentation.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,teleradiology_case,interpretation_start_datetime,interpretation_start_datetime,Interpretation Start Datetime,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,The date and time at which the remote radiologist began active interpretation of the imaging study. Used to measure reading time and identify workflow bottlenecks in vendor SLA performance.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,teleradiology_case,interpreting_radiologist_name,interpreting_radiologist_name,Interpreting Radiologist Name,STRING,,,"dbx_confidential,pii_phi,pii_pii,pii_sensitive",,transactional_data,"Full name of the remote radiologist who performed the teleradiology interpretation. Retained for report attribution, credentialing verification, and regulatory reporting purposes.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,teleradiology_case,interpreting_radiologist_npi,interpreting_radiologist_npi,Interpreting Radiologist National Provider Identifier (NPI),STRING,,,"pii_phi,pii_pii,pii_sensitive",^[0-9]{10}$,transactional_data,The 10-digit National Provider Identifier (NPI) of the remote radiologist who interpreted the imaging study on behalf of the teleradiology vendor. Required for professional component billing and credentialing verification.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,teleradiology_case,modality_code,modality_code,Imaging Modality Code,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"DICOM-standard modality code identifying the imaging technology used to acquire the study (e.g., CT, MR, XR, US, PT). Drives subspecialty routing logic and SLA tier assignment. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: CT|MR|XR|US|PT|NM|MG|FL|DX|CR — 10 candidates stripped; promote to reference product]",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,teleradiology_case,mrn,mrn,Medical Record Number (MRN),STRING,,,"dbx_pii_identifier,dbx_restricted,pii_phi,pii_pii,pii_sensitive",,transactional_data,The facility-assigned Medical Record Number (MRN) for the patient associated with this teleradiology case. Retained on the case record to support report reconciliation and audit without requiring a join to the patient master.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,teleradiology_case,number_of_images,number_of_images,Number of Images,INT,,,,,transactional_data,Total count of DICOM image instances included in the transmitted imaging study. Used to verify transmission completeness and assess study complexity for vendor workload management.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,teleradiology_case,number_of_series,number_of_series,Number of Series,INT,,,,,transactional_data,"Total count of DICOM series included in the transmitted imaging study. Alongside number_of_images, used to assess study complexity and verify transmission completeness.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,teleradiology_case,order_routing_reason,order_routing_reason,Routing Reason,STRING,,,,after_hours|subspecialty|overflow|stat_coverage|disaster_recovery|other,transactional_data,The business reason this imaging study was routed to a teleradiology vendor rather than interpreted by an on-site radiologist. Drives SLA tier selection and vendor performance analytics. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: after_hours|subspecialty|overflow|stat_coverage|disaster_recovery|other — promote to reference product if additional values are needed],
radiology,interpretation_reporting,teleradiology_case,preliminary_report_datetime,preliminary_report_datetime,Preliminary Report Received Datetime,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,The date and time at which the preliminary (wet read) radiology report was received from the teleradiology vendor. Used to measure preliminary TAT compliance against SLA thresholds.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,teleradiology_case,preliminary_report_text,preliminary_report_text,Preliminary Report Text,STRING,,,"dbx_pii_health,dbx_restricted,pii_phi,pii_pii,pii_sensitive",,transactional_data,The verbatim text of the preliminary (wet read) radiology report received from the teleradiology vendor. Contains PHI and clinical findings. Used for reconciliation comparison and clinical communication prior to final report availability.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,teleradiology_case,priority_level,priority_level,Study Priority Level,STRING,,,,stat|urgent|routine|elective,transactional_data,"Clinical priority assigned to the imaging study, which determines the applicable turnaround time (TAT) SLA tier for the teleradiology vendor. STAT studies require the shortest TAT.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,teleradiology_case,professional_component_billed,professional_component_billed,Professional Component Billed Indicator,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,Boolean flag indicating whether the professional component (PC) of the radiology interpretation has been billed to the payer. Used to track billing completion and prevent duplicate claim submission.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,teleradiology_case,reconciliation_datetime,reconciliation_datetime,Report Reconciliation Datetime,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,The date and time at which the report reconciliation process was completed by the on-site or supervising radiologist. Null if reconciliation is still pending.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,teleradiology_case,reconciliation_discrepancy_flag,reconciliation_discrepancy_flag,Reconciliation Discrepancy Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,Boolean flag indicating whether a clinically significant discrepancy was identified between the teleradiology vendors interpretation and the on-site radiologists reconciliation review. Triggers quality review workflows when True.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,teleradiology_case,report_reconciliation_status,report_reconciliation_status,Report Reconciliation Status,STRING,,,,pending|in_review|reconciled|discrepancy_identified|escalated|waived,transactional_data,Status of the reconciliation process between the teleradiology vendors preliminary/final report and the on-site radiologists review. Tracks whether discrepancies between preliminary and final interpretations have been identified and resolved.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,teleradiology_case,retransmission_count,retransmission_count,Retransmission Count,INT,,,,,transactional_data,Number of times the imaging study was retransmitted to the teleradiology vendor due to transmission failures or incomplete transfers. Used for infrastructure reliability monitoring and SLA dispute resolution.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,teleradiology_case,sla_met,sla_met,SLA Met Indicator,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,Boolean flag indicating whether the teleradiology vendor met the contractual turnaround time (TAT) SLA for this case. True when actual_tat_minutes is less than or equal to expected_tat_minutes. Used for vendor performance scorecards.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,teleradiology_case,study_datetime,study_datetime,Study Acquisition Datetime,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,The date and time at which the imaging study was acquired (scan performed) at the originating facility. Sourced from the DICOM Study Date/Time tags. Represents the principal real-world clinical event time for this case.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,teleradiology_case,subspecialty_required,subspecialty_required,Subspecialty Required,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"The radiology subspecialty expertise required for interpretation of this study (e.g., neuroradiology, musculoskeletal, pediatric radiology, interventional). Drives subspecialty routing logic and vendor capability matching.",
radiology,interpretation_reporting,teleradiology_case,transmission_datetime,transmission_datetime,Study Transmission Datetime,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,The date and time (ISO 8601 with timezone offset) at which the imaging study DICOM data was transmitted from the originating facilitys PACS to the teleradiology vendors receiving system. This is the TAT clock start event.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,teleradiology_case,transmission_method,transmission_method,Transmission Method,STRING,,,,dicom_push|dicom_pull|vpn_transfer|cloud_upload|hl7_mllp|other,transactional_data,The technical method used to transmit the imaging study to the teleradiology vendor. Used for transmission failure analysis and infrastructure performance monitoring.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,teleradiology_case,transmission_success,transmission_success,Transmission Success Indicator,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,Boolean flag indicating whether the DICOM study transmission to the teleradiology vendor was completed successfully without errors or data loss. False triggers retransmission workflows.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,teleradiology_case,updated_timestamp,updated_timestamp,Record Updated Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,The date and time at which this teleradiology case record was most recently modified. Used for incremental data pipeline processing and audit trail maintenance.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,teleradiology_case,vendor_accession_number,vendor_accession_number,Vendor Accession Number,STRING,,,"dbx_confidential,pii_phi,pii_pii,pii_sensitive",,transactional_data,The accession number assigned by the teleradiology vendors RIS upon receipt of the transmitted study. Used for cross-referencing vendor reports back to the originating order and for reconciliation workflows.,
radiology,interpretation_reporting,teleradiology_case,vendor_receipt_datetime,vendor_receipt_datetime,Vendor Receipt Datetime,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,The date and time at which the teleradiology vendor confirmed receipt and availability of the transmitted imaging study in their PACS/reading workstation. Used to measure transmission latency and adjust TAT calculations.,
radiology,order_management,imaging_order,imaging_order_id,imaging_order_id,Imaging Order ID,BIGINT,Y,,,,transactional_data,Unique surrogate primary key for each imaging order record in the radiology information system (RIS). Serves as the SSOT identifier for the imaging order lifecycle within the Databricks Silver layer.,
radiology,order_management,imaging_order,clinical_order_id,clinical_order_id,Clinical Order Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,order.clinical_order.clinical_order_id,,,transactional_data,Foreign key linking to order.clinical_order. Business justification: Imaging orders originate from clinical orders in CPOE workflows. Order reconciliation at care transitions requires linking imaging orders to parent clinical orders for complete medication and order hi,
radiology,order_management,imaging_order,contrast_drug_master_id,contrast_drug_master_id,Contrast Drug Master Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,pharmacy.drug_master.drug_master_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to pharmacy.drug_master. Business justification: Imaging orders specify contrast agents for CT/MRI studies. FK to drug_master enables formulary checking, allergy screening, inventory management, and standardized contrast protocol validation. Real bu",
radiology,order_management,imaging_order,contrast_material_master_id,contrast_material_master_id,Contrast Material Master Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,supply.material_master.material_master_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to supply.material_master. Business justification: Imaging orders requiring contrast agents must link to material master for inventory tracking, lot number traceability, and recall management. Standard radiology supply chain process tracks contrast co",
radiology,order_management,imaging_order,cost_center_id,cost_center_id,Cost Center Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,finance.cost_center.cost_center_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to finance.cost_center. Business justification: Radiology orders must be allocated to departmental cost centers for activity-based costing, P&L reporting by modality/service line, and operational expense tracking. Essential for financial management",
radiology,order_management,imaging_order,demographics_id,demographics_id,Patient ID,BIGINT,,patient.demographics.demographics_id,,,transactional_data,Reference to the patient for whom the imaging order was placed. Links to the master patient record in the MPI (Master Patient Index).,
radiology,order_management,imaging_order,employee_id,employee_id,Performing Technologist ID,BIGINT,,workforce.employee.employee_id,"dbx_confidential, dbx_pii",,transactional_data,"Reference to the radiologic technologist (RT) who performed the imaging examination. Used for technologist productivity reporting, competency tracking, and quality assurance audits.",
radiology,order_management,imaging_order,health_plan_id,health_plan_id,Insurance Plan ID,BIGINT,,insurance.health_plan.health_plan_id,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii",,transactional_data,"Reference to the patients active insurance coverage plan at the time the imaging order was placed. Used for eligibility verification, prior authorization routing, and claim submission to the correct payer.",
radiology,order_management,imaging_order,hie_query_id,hie_query_id,Hie Query Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,interoperability.hie_query.hie_query_id,,,transactional_data,Foreign key linking to interoperability.hie_query. Business justification: Radiology orders trigger HIE queries (XCA/XDS-I.b) to retrieve prior imaging studies and relevant clinical history from external facilities for radiologist comparison and clinical decision support. Li,
radiology,order_management,imaging_order,icd10_primary_diagnosis_icd_code_id,icd10_primary_diagnosis_icd_code_id,Icd10 Primary Diagnosis Icd Code Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,reference.icd_code.icd_code_id,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_health",,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to reference.icd_code. Business justification: Orders carry ICD-10 diagnosis codes to justify medical necessity for payer authorization, support clinical decision support, and enable quality reporting. Core requirement for radiology order manageme",
radiology,order_management,imaging_order,mpi_record_id,mpi_record_id,,BIGINT,,patient.mpi_record.mpi_record_id,,,transactional_data,description,
radiology,order_management,imaging_order,payer_id,payer_id,Payer Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,insurance.payer.payer_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to insurance.payer. Business justification: Imaging orders require payer identification for eligibility verification, prior authorization routing, and claim submission. Distinct from insurance_plan_id which captures member-specific coverage tie",
radiology,order_management,imaging_order,primary_imaging_care_site_id,primary_imaging_care_site_id,Facility ID,BIGINT,,facility.care_site.care_site_id,,,transactional_data,"Reference to the facility (hospital, outpatient imaging center, clinic) where the imaging procedure is to be performed. Supports multi-site radiology operations, facility-level utilization reporting, and CMS cost report allocation.",
radiology,order_management,imaging_order,primary_imaging_clinician_id,primary_imaging_clinician_id,Ordering Provider ID,BIGINT,,provider.clinician.clinician_id,,,transactional_data,"Reference to the clinician (physician, NP, PA) who placed the imaging order via CPOE (Computerized Physician Order Entry). Used for provider-level utilization reporting and MIPS quality measures.",
radiology,order_management,imaging_order,procedure_code_cpt_code_id,procedure_code_cpt_code_id,Procedure Code Cpt Code Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,reference.cpt_code.cpt_code_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to reference.cpt_code. Business justification: Imaging orders reference CPT codes to define billable procedures, support prior authorization, and enable revenue cycle management. Essential for claims submission and procedure standardization across",
radiology,order_management,imaging_order,radiology_study_id,radiology_study_id,,BIGINT,,radiology.radiology_study.radiology_study_id,,,transactional_data,study_id,
radiology,order_management,imaging_order,research_study_id,research_study_id,Research Study Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,research.research_study.research_study_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to research.research_study. Business justification: Clinical trials require protocol-specified imaging procedures. Research orders flow through standard radiology workflow, requiring linkage for protocol compliance tracking, research billing determinat",
radiology,order_management,imaging_order,scheduling_appointment_id,scheduling_appointment_id,,BIGINT,,scheduling.scheduling_appointment.scheduling_appointment_id,,,transactional_data,FK to scheduling.scheduling_appointment.scheduling_appointment_id,
radiology,order_management,imaging_order,treatment_consent_id,treatment_consent_id,Treatment Consent Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,consent.treatment_consent.treatment_consent_id,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii",,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to consent.treatment_consent. Business justification: Imaging orders require informed consent verification before exam performance, especially for procedures involving contrast, radiation, or interventional techniques. Links order to the consent authoriz",
radiology,order_management,imaging_order,visit_id,visit_id,Encounter ID,BIGINT,,encounter.visit.visit_id,,,transactional_data,"Reference to the clinical encounter (inpatient, outpatient, ED visit) during which the imaging order was placed. Supports encounter-level analytics and billing reconciliation.",
radiology,order_management,imaging_order,accession_number,accession_number,RIS Accession Number,STRING,,,"pii_phi,pii_pii,pii_sensitive",,transactional_data,"tags: pii_phi,pii_pii,pii_sensitive",
radiology,order_management,imaging_order,body_part,body_part,Body Part Examined,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"The anatomical body part or region targeted by the imaging order (e.g., CHEST, ABDOMEN, BRAIN, KNEE, SPINE). Uses SNOMED CT or DICOM body part examined codes. Supports procedure-level analytics, radiation dose tracking by anatomy, and ACR Dose Index Registry reporting.",
radiology,order_management,imaging_order,cancellation_reason,cancellation_reason,Cancellation Reason,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"The reason code or description for why the imaging order was cancelled (e.g., Patient Refused, Duplicate Order, Clinical Condition Changed, No Auth Obtained). Null if order was not cancelled. Used for cancellation root cause analysis and operational improvement.",
radiology,order_management,imaging_order,cancelled_timestamp,cancelled_timestamp,Order Cancelled Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,"The date and time when the imaging order was cancelled. Null if the order was not cancelled. Used for cancellation rate analytics, capacity recapture reporting, and revenue cycle reconciliation.",
radiology,order_management,imaging_order,clinical_indication,clinical_indication,Clinical Indication,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Free-text clinical reason or indication for the imaging order as entered by the ordering provider in CPOE. Supports CDI (Clinical Documentation Improvement) review, radiologist interpretation context, and ACR Appropriateness Criteria validation.",
radiology,order_management,imaging_order,contrast_required,contrast_required,Contrast Required Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,"Indicates whether intravenous or oral contrast agent is required for this imaging procedure. Drives pre-procedure screening workflows (renal function check, allergy screening), contrast preparation, and charge capture for contrast administration.",
radiology,order_management,imaging_order,created_timestamp,created_timestamp,Record Created Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,The date and time when this imaging order record was first created in the source RIS system (Epic Radiant / Cerner RadNet). Serves as the audit trail creation timestamp for data lineage and HIPAA audit log requirements.,
radiology,order_management,imaging_order,critical_finding_flag,critical_finding_flag,Critical Finding Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,Indicates whether the radiologist identified a critical or urgent finding requiring immediate communication to the ordering provider. Triggers the critical results notification workflow per Joint Commission NPSG.02.03.01 and ACR communication standards.,
radiology,order_management,imaging_order,exam_end_timestamp,exam_end_timestamp,Exam End Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,"The date and time when the imaging examination was completed (acquisition finished). Used to calculate exam duration, modality utilization, and throughput metrics.",
radiology,order_management,imaging_order,exam_start_timestamp,exam_start_timestamp,Exam Start Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,"The date and time when the imaging examination physically began (patient on table, acquisition started). Captured by the RIS/modality worklist. Used for TAT calculation from order to exam start and for radiation dose event timestamping.",
radiology,order_management,imaging_order,is_portable,is_portable,Portable Exam Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,"Indicates whether the imaging examination is to be performed as a portable/bedside study (e.g., portable chest X-ray in ICU). Drives equipment dispatch workflows, technologist assignment, and portable exam charge capture.",
radiology,order_management,imaging_order,is_stat_override,is_stat_override,STAT Override Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,"Indicates whether the STAT priority designation was applied as a manual override by a provider or charge nurse, bypassing standard priority assignment logic. Used for STAT utilization auditing and appropriate use compliance monitoring.",
radiology,order_management,imaging_order,laterality,laterality,Laterality,STRING,,,,left|right|bilateral|unspecified,transactional_data,"Specifies the side of the body for the imaging procedure where applicable (e.g., left knee MRI, right shoulder X-ray). Critical for patient safety (wrong-site imaging prevention), DICOM image tagging, and surgical/procedural correlation.",
radiology,order_management,imaging_order,modality_type,modality_type,Imaging Modality Type,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"The imaging modality requested for this order using DICOM modality codes. CT = Computed Tomography, MRI = Magnetic Resonance Imaging, XR/DX/CR = X-ray, US = Ultrasound, PET = Positron Emission Tomography, FL = Fluoroscopy, NM = Nuclear Medicine, MG = Mammography. Drives modality-specific scheduling, equipment assignment, and radiation dose tracking requirements. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: CT|MRI|XR|US|PET|FL|NM|MG|DX|CR — 10 candidates stripped; promote to reference product]",
radiology,order_management,imaging_order,mrn,mrn,Medical Record Number (MRN),STRING,,,"dbx_pii_identifier,dbx_restricted,pii_phi,pii_pii,pii_sensitive",,transactional_data,The patients Medical Record Number (MRN) as assigned by the facilitys Master Patient Index (MPI). Denormalized on the order for operational lookup and cross-system reconciliation with Epic Radiant and Cerner RadNet without requiring a join.,
radiology,order_management,imaging_order,order_priority,order_priority,Order Priority,STRING,,,,stat|urgent|routine|asap|elective,transactional_data,Clinical priority assigned to the imaging order at placement. STAT indicates immediate life-threatening urgency; urgent indicates same-day completion; routine indicates standard scheduling. Drives RIS scheduling queue prioritization and turnaround time (TAT) SLA measurement.,
radiology,order_management,imaging_order,order_source,order_source,Order Source Setting,STRING,,,,inpatient|outpatient|emergency|ambulatory|telehealth,transactional_data,"The care setting from which the imaging order originated. Drives billing rules (facility vs professional fee), payer contract application, and population health analytics by care setting.",
radiology,order_management,imaging_order,order_status,order_status,Imaging Order Status,STRING,,,,ordered|scheduled|in_progress|completed|cancelled|on_hold,transactional_data,Current workflow status of the imaging order within the RIS lifecycle. Transitions: ordered → scheduled → in_progress → completed; or ordered → cancelled / on_hold. Aligns with HL7 FHIR ServiceRequest.status and IHE SWF workflow states. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: ordered|scheduled|in_progress|completed|cancelled|on_hold|discontinued|pending_auth — promote to reference product if additional states are needed],
radiology,order_management,imaging_order,ordered_timestamp,ordered_timestamp,Order Placed Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,"The date and time when the imaging order was placed by the ordering provider in the CPOE system (Epic Orders / Cerner PowerChart). This is the principal business event timestamp for the order lifecycle. Used for TAT (Turnaround Time) measurement, STAT order compliance tracking, and regulatory reporting.",
radiology,order_management,imaging_order,ordering_provider_npi,ordering_provider_npi,Ordering Provider National Provider Identifier (NPI),STRING,,,"pii_phi,pii_pii,pii_sensitive",^[0-9]{10}$,transactional_data,"The 10-digit NPI (National Provider Identifier) of the ordering clinician. Denormalized on the order for direct use in CMS-1500 and UB-04 claim submission, payer prior authorization requests, and MIPS reporting without requiring a provider table join.",
radiology,order_management,imaging_order,prior_auth_number,prior_auth_number,Prior Authorization Number,STRING,,,"pii_phi,pii_pii,pii_sensitive",,transactional_data,"The prior authorization number issued by the payer for this imaging procedure. Required for high-cost modalities (MRI, CT, PET) under many payer contracts. Null if prior authorization is not required or not yet obtained. Used in claim submission and denial management.",
radiology,order_management,imaging_order,prior_auth_status,prior_auth_status,Prior Authorization Status,STRING,,,,approved|pending|denied|not_required|expired,transactional_data,Current status of the prior authorization request for this imaging order. Drives RCM (Revenue Cycle Management) workflows — orders with denied or pending auth may be held from scheduling. Critical for denial prevention and payer compliance.,
radiology,order_management,imaging_order,procedure_description,procedure_description,Procedure Description,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Human-readable description of the imaging procedure as defined in the CDM (Charge Description Master) or RIS procedure dictionary (e.g., CT Chest with Contrast, MRI Brain without and with Contrast). Used for clinical communication, scheduling display, and report headers.",
radiology,order_management,imaging_order,protocol_name,protocol_name,Imaging Protocol Name,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"The specific imaging acquisition protocol assigned to this order by the radiologist or technologist (e.g., CT Chest PE Protocol, MRI Brain Stroke Protocol). Drives scanner programming, contrast timing, and image reconstruction parameters. Sourced from the RIS protocol library.",
radiology,order_management,imaging_order,radiation_dose_ctdi,radiation_dose_ctdi,Radiation Dose CT Dose Index Volume (CTDIvol) mGy,"DECIMAL(10,4)",,,,,transactional_data,"The CT Dose Index Volume (CTDIvol) in mGy for CT examinations, representing the average radiation dose within the scan volume. Extracted from DICOM RDSR. Used alongside DLP for ACR Dose Index Registry benchmarking and radiation safety compliance.",
radiology,order_management,imaging_order,radiation_dose_dlp,radiation_dose_dlp,Radiation Dose Dose-Length Product (DLP) mGy·cm,"DECIMAL(10,4)",,,,,transactional_data,"The Dose-Length Product (DLP) in mGy·cm recorded for CT examinations, representing the total radiation dose delivered during the scan. Populated from DICOM Radiation Dose Structured Report (RDSR). Required for ACR Dose Index Registry (DIR) submission and CMS radiation dose reporting.",
radiology,order_management,imaging_order,referring_department,referring_department,Referring Department,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"The hospital department or clinical unit that originated the imaging order (e.g., Emergency Department, ICU, Cardiology, Orthopedics). Used for departmental utilization reporting, cost allocation, and radiology demand forecasting.",
radiology,order_management,imaging_order,report_finalized_timestamp,report_finalized_timestamp,Report Finalized Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,"The date and time when the radiologist finalized (signed/attested) the radiology report in the RIS. Critical for TAT measurement from exam completion to report delivery, ACR reporting benchmarks, and Joint Commission communication of critical findings requirements.",
radiology,order_management,imaging_order,report_status,report_status,Radiology Report Status,STRING,,,,not_started|preliminary|final|addendum|corrected,transactional_data,Current status of the radiology interpretation report associated with this order. Preliminary reports are available before final sign-off; addendum and corrected statuses indicate post-finalization changes. Drives critical result notification workflows and clinical decision support.,
radiology,order_management,imaging_order,requisition_number,requisition_number,Requisition Number,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,The requisition or placer order number generated by the CPOE system (Epic Orders / Cerner PowerChart) at the time the order is placed. Serves as the placer order identifier in HL7 ORM/ORU messaging and FHIR ServiceRequest.identifier.,
radiology,order_management,imaging_order,scheduled_timestamp,scheduled_timestamp,Scheduled Appointment Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,"The date and time when the imaging procedure is scheduled to be performed. Populated when the order transitions to scheduled status in the RIS. Used for modality capacity planning, patient notification, and scheduling analytics.",
radiology,order_management,imaging_order,source_system,source_system,Source System,STRING,,,,epic_radiant|cerner_radnet|meditech|manual,transactional_data,"Identifies the operational RIS/EHR system from which this imaging order record was sourced (e.g., Epic Radiant, Cerner RadNet, MEDITECH). Supports multi-system data lineage tracking in the Databricks Silver layer and ETL reconciliation.",
radiology,order_management,imaging_order,source_system_order_code,source_system_order_code,Source System Order ID,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"The native order identifier from the originating RIS/EHR system (Epic Radiant order ID, Cerner RadNet order ID). Preserved for cross-system reconciliation, ETL audit trails, and support escalation without requiring reverse lookup.",
radiology,order_management,imaging_order,updated_timestamp,updated_timestamp,Record Last Updated Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,"The date and time when this imaging order record was last modified in the source RIS system. Used for incremental ETL processing, change data capture, and audit trail compliance.",
radiology,order_management,radiology_appointment,radiology_appointment_id,radiology_appointment_id,Appointment Identifier,BIGINT,Y,,,,transactional_data,Primary key for appointment,
radiology,order_management,radiology_appointment,care_site_id,care_site_id,Facility ID,BIGINT,,facility.care_site.care_site_id,,,transactional_data,"Reference to the healthcare facility (hospital, outpatient imaging center, clinic) where the imaging appointment is scheduled to take place.",
radiology,order_management,radiology_appointment,clinical_order_id,clinical_order_id,Clinical Order Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,order.clinical_order.clinical_order_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to order.clinical_order. Business justification: Imaging appointments fulfill clinical orders. Scheduling workflows require linking appointments to orders for prep instruction delivery, authorization verification, and patient communication. Operatio",
radiology,order_management,radiology_appointment,employee_id,employee_id,Radiology Technologist ID,BIGINT,,workforce.employee.employee_id,"dbx_confidential, dbx_pii",,transactional_data,"Reference to the radiology technologist (RT) assigned to perform the imaging study for this appointment. Used for staffing, productivity tracking, and quality assurance.",
radiology,order_management,radiology_appointment,health_plan_id,health_plan_id,Insurance Plan ID,BIGINT,,insurance.health_plan.health_plan_id,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii",,transactional_data,"Reference to the patients active insurance plan at the time of the imaging appointment. Used for eligibility verification, pre-authorization, and revenue cycle management.",
radiology,order_management,radiology_appointment,icd10_diagnosis_icd_code_id,icd10_diagnosis_icd_code_id,Icd10 Diagnosis Icd Code Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,reference.icd_code.icd_code_id,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_health",,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to reference.icd_code. Business justification: Appointments carry diagnosis codes for prior authorization verification at scheduling time, support medical necessity screening, and enable diagnosis-based appointment prioritization for urgent condit",
radiology,order_management,radiology_appointment,imaging_order_id,imaging_order_id,Imaging Order ID,BIGINT,,radiology.imaging_order.imaging_order_id,,,transactional_data,Reference to the radiology order (CPOE) that initiated this appointment. Enables traceability from scheduling back to the clinical order.,
radiology,order_management,radiology_appointment,modality_room_id,modality_room_id,Modality Room ID,BIGINT,,facility.room.room_id,,,transactional_data,"Reference to the specific imaging room or scanner unit assigned for this appointment. Enables room-level utilization tracking, maintenance scheduling, and capacity management.",
radiology,order_management,radiology_appointment,mpi_record_id,mpi_record_id,Patient ID,BIGINT,,patient.mpi_record.mpi_record_id,,,transactional_data,"Reference to the patient receiving the imaging service. Serves as the PARTY_REFERENCE for this transaction, linking to the patient master record.",
radiology,order_management,radiology_appointment,primary_radiology_clinician_id,primary_radiology_clinician_id,Ordering Provider ID,BIGINT,,provider.clinician.clinician_id,,,transactional_data,"Reference to the clinician who placed the imaging order that generated this appointment. Used for referral tracking, utilization management, and RVU attribution.",
radiology,order_management,radiology_appointment,procedure_cpt_code_id,procedure_cpt_code_id,Procedure Cpt Code Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,reference.cpt_code.cpt_code_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to reference.cpt_code. Business justification: Appointments are scheduled for specific CPT-coded procedures to enable resource allocation, exam duration estimation, and scheduling template management. Links support capacity planning and utilizatio",
radiology,order_management,radiology_appointment,scheduling_appointment_id,scheduling_appointment_id,Enterprise Appointment ID,BIGINT,,scheduling.scheduling_appointment.scheduling_appointment_id,,,transactional_data,Reference to the parent enterprise scheduling appointment record. Links this radiology-specific scheduling record to the general enterprise scheduling infrastructure.,
radiology,order_management,radiology_appointment,subject_enrollment_id,subject_enrollment_id,Subject Enrollment Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,research.subject_enrollment.subject_enrollment_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to research.subject_enrollment. Business justification: Research imaging appointments are scheduled per protocol visit schedules. Direct linkage to subject enrollment enables protocol compliance tracking, visit window adherence monitoring, and research bil",
radiology,order_management,radiology_appointment,tertiary_radiology_referring_provider_clinician_id,tertiary_radiology_referring_provider_clinician_id,Referring Provider ID,BIGINT,,provider.clinician.clinician_id,,,transactional_data,"Reference to the provider who referred the patient for this imaging study, which may differ from the ordering provider. Used for referral analytics, network management, and payer reporting.",
radiology,order_management,radiology_appointment,visit_id,visit_id,Encounter ID,BIGINT,,encounter.visit.visit_id,,,transactional_data,Reference to the clinical encounter or visit associated with this imaging appointment. Connects the radiology scheduling event to the broader patient visit context.,
radiology,order_management,radiology_appointment,accession_number,accession_number,Radiology Accession Number,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Unique identifier assigned by the Radiology Information System (RIS) to this imaging study appointment. Used as the primary cross-system identifier linking the RIS, PACS, and EHR for this imaging event. Conforms to DICOM accession number format.",
radiology,order_management,radiology_appointment,actual_end_datetime,actual_end_datetime,Actual End Date and Time,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,The actual date and time the imaging procedure concluded. Combined with actual_start_datetime to compute actual procedure duration for throughput and capacity analytics.,
radiology,order_management,radiology_appointment,actual_start_datetime,actual_start_datetime,Actual Start Date and Time,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,"The actual date and time the imaging procedure began (patient on table / scan initiated). Used to measure schedule adherence, wait times, and operational efficiency.",
radiology,order_management,radiology_appointment,appointment_comment,appointment_comment,Appointment Comment,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Free-text clinical or operational notes associated with the imaging appointment (e.g., special patient needs, equipment requirements, interpreter needed, claustrophobia notes for MRI). Not intended for clinical documentation.",
radiology,order_management,radiology_appointment,appointment_status,appointment_status,Appointment Status,STRING,,,,scheduled|arrived|in_progress|completed|cancelled|no_show,transactional_data,Current workflow state of the radiology imaging appointment. Tracks the full lifecycle from initial scheduling through completion or cancellation. Aligns with IHE SWF appointment status codes.,
radiology,order_management,radiology_appointment,appointment_type,appointment_type,Appointment Type,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Clinical classification of the imaging appointment indicating the urgency and purpose of the study. Drives scheduling priority, slot allocation, and workflow routing. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: routine|urgent|stat|screening|follow_up|pre_op|research — promote to reference product if additional types are needed]",
radiology,order_management,radiology_appointment,auth_status,auth_status,Authorization Status,STRING,,,,approved|pending|denied|not_required|expired,transactional_data,"Current status of the insurance pre-authorization for this imaging appointment. Drives scheduling holds, revenue cycle workflows, and denial management processes.",
radiology,order_management,radiology_appointment,body_part,body_part,Body Part Examined,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"The anatomical region or body part targeted by the imaging study (e.g., CHEST, ABDOMEN, BRAIN, KNEE). Aligns with DICOM Body Part Examined attribute and SNOMED CT anatomical terminology.",
radiology,order_management,radiology_appointment,cancellation_reason,cancellation_reason,Cancellation Reason,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"The documented reason for appointment cancellation when appointment_status is cancelled. Used for operational analytics, capacity recovery, and patient access improvement initiatives.",
radiology,order_management,radiology_appointment,clinical_indication,clinical_indication,Clinical Indication,STRING,,,"dbx_pii_health,dbx_restricted,pii_phi,pii_pii,pii_sensitive",,transactional_data,"The clinical reason or indication for the imaging study as documented by the ordering provider. Contains PHI and is used for clinical decision support, ACR appropriateness criteria evaluation, and CDI.",
radiology,order_management,radiology_appointment,contrast_required,contrast_required,Contrast Required Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,"Indicates whether intravenous or oral contrast agent is required for this imaging study. Drives pre-appointment prep instructions, allergy screening, renal function checks, and contrast timing workflows.",
radiology,order_management,radiology_appointment,contrast_type,contrast_type,Contrast Administration Type,STRING,,,,IV|oral|intrathecal|intra_articular|not_applicable,transactional_data,"The route of contrast agent administration planned for this imaging study. Used for pre-procedure preparation, patient safety screening, and contrast administration documentation.",
radiology,order_management,radiology_appointment,created_timestamp,created_timestamp,Record Created Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,"The date and time when this imaging appointment record was first created in the system. Serves as the audit creation timestamp for data lineage, compliance, and change tracking.",
radiology,order_management,radiology_appointment,is_portable,is_portable,Portable Imaging Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,Indicates whether the imaging study is to be performed at the patients bedside or location (portable) rather than in a dedicated imaging room. Affects equipment assignment and technologist dispatch.,
radiology,order_management,radiology_appointment,is_stat,is_stat,STAT Order Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,"Indicates whether this imaging appointment was ordered as STAT (immediate/urgent priority), requiring expedited scheduling and turnaround. Drives workflow prioritization in the RIS and PACS.",
radiology,order_management,radiology_appointment,laterality,laterality,Laterality,STRING,,,,left|right|bilateral|not_applicable,transactional_data,"Specifies the side of the body for the imaging study when applicable (left, right, bilateral). Critical for patient safety, correct-site imaging compliance, and DICOM metadata accuracy.",
radiology,order_management,radiology_appointment,modality_type,modality_type,Imaging Modality Type,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"The type of imaging modality assigned for this appointment (e.g., CT, MRI, X-ray, Ultrasound, PET). Core radiology scheduling attribute that determines equipment, room, and technologist assignment. Uses DICOM modality codes. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: CT|MRI|XR|US|PET|NM|MG|FL|DXA|DEXA — promote to reference product]",
radiology,order_management,radiology_appointment,no_show_reason,no_show_reason,No-Show Reason,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"The documented reason the patient did not appear for the scheduled imaging appointment when appointment_status is no_show. Used for patient outreach, access analytics, and population health management.",
radiology,order_management,radiology_appointment,pacs_study_uid,pacs_study_uid,Picture Archiving and Communication System (PACS) Study Instance UID,STRING,,,"pii_phi,pii_pii,pii_sensitive",^[0-9]+(.[0-9]+)+$,transactional_data,The globally unique DICOM Study Instance UID assigned by the PACS for the imaging study associated with this appointment. Enables direct linkage between the scheduling record and the DICOM image archive.,
radiology,order_management,radiology_appointment,patient_location,patient_location,Patient Location at Time of Appointment,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"The patients physical location at the time of the imaging appointment (e.g., inpatient unit/bed, ED bay, outpatient clinic, external). Used for transport coordination and portable imaging dispatch.",
radiology,order_management,radiology_appointment,prep_instructions,prep_instructions,Patient Preparation Instructions,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Specific pre-appointment preparation instructions communicated to the patient (e.g., NPO after midnight, bowel prep, hydration requirements, medication holds). Critical for imaging quality and patient safety.",
radiology,order_management,radiology_appointment,prior_auth_number,prior_auth_number,Insurance Pre-Authorization Number,STRING,,,"pii_phi,pii_pii,pii_sensitive",,transactional_data,The pre-authorization or prior authorization reference number obtained from the patients insurance payer before the imaging study. Required for reimbursement and revenue cycle management. Null if authorization not required or not yet obtained.,
radiology,order_management,radiology_appointment,procedure_description,procedure_description,Procedure Description,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Human-readable description of the imaging procedure to be performed, corresponding to the CPT code. Used for patient communication, scheduling displays, and clinical documentation.",
radiology,order_management,radiology_appointment,radiation_dose_flag,radiation_dose_flag,Radiation Dose Tracking Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,"Indicates whether radiation dose tracking is required for this imaging appointment (applicable to CT, fluoroscopy, nuclear medicine, and other ionizing radiation modalities). Drives dose monitoring workflows per ACR and Joint Commission requirements.",
radiology,order_management,radiology_appointment,reschedule_count,reschedule_count,Reschedule Count,INT,,,,,transactional_data,"The number of times this imaging appointment has been rescheduled. Used to identify access barriers, patient compliance issues, and scheduling inefficiencies.",
radiology,order_management,radiology_appointment,ris_appointment_code,ris_appointment_code,Radiology Information System (RIS) Appointment ID,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,The native appointment identifier from the source Radiology Information System (RIS) such as Epic Radiant or Cerner RadNet. Used for cross-system reconciliation and ETL lineage tracking.,
radiology,order_management,radiology_appointment,scheduled_duration_minutes,scheduled_duration_minutes,Scheduled Duration (Minutes),INT,,,,,transactional_data,"The planned duration of the imaging appointment in minutes as defined at time of scheduling. Drives modality slot blocking, throughput analysis, and schedule optimization.",
radiology,order_management,radiology_appointment,scheduled_end_datetime,scheduled_end_datetime,Scheduled End Date and Time,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,The planned date and time the imaging appointment is expected to conclude. Used with scheduled_start_datetime to determine the reserved slot duration on the modality schedule.,
radiology,order_management,radiology_appointment,scheduled_start_datetime,scheduled_start_datetime,Scheduled Start Date and Time,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,"The planned date and time the imaging appointment is scheduled to begin. Serves as the principal business event timestamp for scheduling analytics, capacity planning, and patient communication.",
radiology,order_management,radiology_appointment,scheduling_source,scheduling_source,Scheduling Source,STRING,,,,provider_referral|patient_self|order_based|transfer|walk_in|portal,transactional_data,"The channel or source through which this imaging appointment was scheduled. Used for access analytics, referral management, and patient experience reporting.",
radiology,order_management,radiology_appointment,updated_timestamp,updated_timestamp,Record Updated Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,"The date and time when this imaging appointment record was most recently modified. Used for incremental ETL processing, audit trails, and change data capture in the lakehouse pipeline.",
radiology,order_management,radiology_order_status_history,radiology_order_status_history_id,radiology_order_status_history_id,,BIGINT,Y,,,,transactional_data,Self-referencing FK to the immediately preceding status history record for this order,
radiology,order_management,radiology_order_status_history,care_site_id,care_site_id,Facility ID,BIGINT,,facility.care_site.care_site_id,,,transactional_data,Reference to the healthcare facility or imaging center where the status change event occurred. Supports facility-level workflow benchmarking and multi-site operational reporting.,
radiology,order_management,radiology_order_status_history,clinician_id,clinician_id,Performing Radiologist ID,BIGINT,,provider.clinician.clinician_id,,,transactional_data,"Reference to the radiologist assigned to interpret the imaging study at the time of this status event. Relevant for read-phase status transitions (preliminary-read, final-read, report-signed) and radiologist productivity analytics.",
radiology,order_management,radiology_order_status_history,correcting_status_history_id,correcting_status_history_id,Corrected History ID,BIGINT,,claim.status_history.status_history_id,,,transactional_data,"Reference to the original imaging_order_status_history_id record that this entry corrects, populated only when is_corrective_entry is True. Enables a complete correction chain for audit and compliance review.",
radiology,order_management,radiology_order_status_history,demographics_id,demographics_id,Patient ID,BIGINT,,patient.demographics.demographics_id,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_identifier",,transactional_data,Reference to the patient associated with the imaging order at the time of this status event. Retained on the history record to support patient-level workflow analytics without requiring a join to the order.,
radiology,order_management,radiology_order_status_history,employee_id,employee_id,Changed By User ID,BIGINT,,workforce.employee.employee_id,"dbx_confidential, dbx_pii",,transactional_data,"Internal system user identifier of the individual who performed the status change action in the RIS. Complements the NPI for non-provider staff (technologists, schedulers, coordinators) who may not have an NPI.",
radiology,order_management,radiology_order_status_history,imaging_order_id,imaging_order_id,Imaging Order ID,BIGINT,,radiology.imaging_order.imaging_order_id,,,transactional_data,Reference to the parent imaging order whose status changed. Links this history record to the originating radiology order in the RIS workflow.,
radiology,order_management,radiology_order_status_history,message_log_id,message_log_id,Message Log Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,interoperability.message_log.message_log_id,,,transactional_data,Foreign key linking to interoperability.message_log. Business justification: Order status transitions (scheduled→in-progress→complete→cancelled) trigger HL7 ORM order messages to referring systems and EHRs for real-time status updates. Message_log tracks each status change mes,
radiology,order_management,radiology_order_status_history,org_unit_id,org_unit_id,Department ID,BIGINT,,workforce.org_unit.org_unit_id,,,transactional_data,"Reference to the radiology department or imaging unit where this status event occurred. Supports department-level workflow analytics, staffing analysis, and operational benchmarking across imaging service lines.",
radiology,order_management,radiology_order_status_history,radiology_study_id,radiology_study_id,,BIGINT,,radiology.radiology_study.radiology_study_id,,,transactional_data,description,
radiology,order_management,radiology_order_status_history,report_id,report_id,Radiology Report ID,BIGINT,,radiology.report.report_id,,,transactional_data,"Reference to the radiology report record associated with this status event, populated for read-phase transitions (preliminary-read, final-read, report-signed, report-delivered). Enables direct linkage between workflow events and the resulting diagnostic report.",
radiology,order_management,radiology_order_status_history,scheduling_appointment_id,scheduling_appointment_id,Imaging Appointment ID,BIGINT,,scheduling.scheduling_appointment.scheduling_appointment_id,,,transactional_data,"Reference to the imaging appointment associated with this status event, when applicable. Links scheduling events (scheduled, patient-arrived) to the corresponding appointment record for scheduling workflow analytics.",
radiology,order_management,radiology_order_status_history,visit_id,visit_id,Encounter ID,BIGINT,,encounter.visit.visit_id,,,transactional_data,Reference to the clinical encounter (visit) associated with the imaging order at the time of this status event. Supports encounter-level workflow analytics and integration with clinical documentation.,
radiology,order_management,radiology_order_status_history,accession_number,accession_number,Accession Number,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"RIS-assigned accession number for the imaging order at the time of this status event. Serves as the primary cross-system identifier linking RIS, PACS, and HL7 ADT/ORM messages for this imaging study.",
radiology,order_management,radiology_order_status_history,cancellation_category,cancellation_category,Cancellation Category,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,Structured category for the cancellation or on-hold reason when the new status is cancelled or on-hold. Enables standardized reporting on cancellation root causes for operational improvement. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: patient-no-show|patient-refused|duplicate-order|clinical-contraindication|equipment-failure|scheduling-error|prior-auth-denied|provider-order-change|other — promote to reference product],
radiology,order_management,radiology_order_status_history,changed_by_user_npi,changed_by_user_npi,Changed By User National Provider Identifier (NPI),STRING,,,,^[0-9]{10}$,transactional_data,"The 10-digit National Provider Identifier (NPI) of the clinician or staff member who triggered the status change. Used for accountability tracking, audit compliance, and provider-level workflow performance analysis.",
radiology,order_management,radiology_order_status_history,changed_by_user_role,changed_by_user_role,Changed By User Role,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"The functional role of the user who triggered the status change (e.g., radiologist, technologist, scheduler). Supports role-based workflow analytics and identification of process bottlenecks by staff category. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: radiologist|technologist|scheduler|nurse|physician|system|coordinator|other — 8 candidates stripped; promote to reference product]",
radiology,order_management,radiology_order_status_history,created_timestamp,created_timestamp,Record Created Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,"The date and time when this status history record was first written to the data platform. Represents the audit record creation time, distinct from the business event timestamp (status_change_timestamp). Used for data lineage and ETL reconciliation.",
radiology,order_management,radiology_order_status_history,hl7_message_reference,hl7_message_reference,Health Level Seven (HL7) Message ID,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"The unique message control identifier from the HL7 v2.x ORM/ORU/ADT message that triggered this status change, when applicable. Enables end-to-end HL7 message traceability and interface troubleshooting.",
radiology,order_management,radiology_order_status_history,hl7_message_type,hl7_message_type,Health Level Seven (HL7) Message Type,STRING,,,,ORM|ORU|ADT|SIU|ACK|other,transactional_data,"The HL7 message type (e.g., ORM, ORU, ADT) associated with the status change event. Supports interface-level audit trails and HL7 workflow integration diagnostics.",
radiology,order_management,radiology_order_status_history,ip_address,ip_address,IP Address,STRING,,,"dbx_confidential,dbx_pii_ip,pii_phi,pii_pii,pii_sensitive",,transactional_data,Network IP address of the workstation or system that submitted the status change event. Retained for HIPAA security audit trail compliance and forensic investigation of unauthorized access or workflow anomalies.,
radiology,order_management,radiology_order_status_history,is_corrective_entry,is_corrective_entry,Is Corrective Entry,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,Indicates whether this status change record was entered as a correction to a previously recorded erroneous status transition. Supports audit integrity and distinguishes legitimate workflow events from administrative corrections.,
radiology,order_management,radiology_order_status_history,is_sla_breach,is_sla_breach,Is Service Level Agreement (SLA) Breach,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,Indicates whether this status transition exceeded the defined SLA threshold for the given order priority and modality. True when transition_duration_seconds exceeds sla_threshold_seconds. Supports SLA compliance dashboards and regulatory reporting.,
radiology,order_management,radiology_order_status_history,is_system_generated,is_system_generated,Is System Generated,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,"Indicates whether this status change was automatically triggered by the RIS system (e.g., via HL7 interface, automated workflow rule, or PACS integration) rather than manually entered by a user. Supports differentiation of automated vs. manual workflow events in process analytics.",
radiology,order_management,radiology_order_status_history,modality_type,modality_type,Modality Type,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"The imaging modality associated with the order at the time of this status event (e.g., CT, MRI, X-ray, Ultrasound, PET). Retained on the history record to enable modality-specific workflow and SLA analytics without joining to the order. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: CT|MRI|XR|US|PET|NM|MG|FL|other — 9 candidates stripped; promote to reference product]",
radiology,order_management,radiology_order_status_history,new_status,new_status,New Order Status,STRING,,,,scheduled|patient-arrived|exam-started|exam-completed|images-available|preliminary-read,transactional_data,The workflow status assigned to the imaging order as a result of this transition event. Represents the current state after the change. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: ordered|scheduled|patient-arrived|exam-started|exam-completed|images-available|preliminary-read|final-read|report-signed|report-delivered|cancelled|on-hold — promote to reference product],
radiology,order_management,radiology_order_status_history,on_hold_reason,on_hold_reason,On-Hold Reason,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Free-text description of why the imaging order was placed on hold, populated when new_status is on-hold. Captures clinical or operational context such as pending prior authorization, patient preparation issues, or equipment unavailability.",
radiology,order_management,radiology_order_status_history,order_priority,order_priority,Order Priority,STRING,,,,STAT|URGENT|ROUTINE|ASAP|ELECTIVE,transactional_data,"The clinical priority level of the imaging order at the time of this status event. Used to assess whether SLA thresholds were met relative to the urgency of the order (e.g., STAT orders have tighter turnaround requirements).",
radiology,order_management,radiology_order_status_history,pacs_study_uid,pacs_study_uid,Picture Archiving and Communication System (PACS) Study UID,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"The DICOM Study Instance UID assigned by the PACS system, populated when the status transition involves image availability (images-available state). Links the RIS workflow event to the corresponding PACS study for cross-system traceability.",
radiology,order_management,radiology_order_status_history,prior_status,prior_status,Prior Order Status,STRING,,,,ordered|scheduled|patient-arrived|exam-started|exam-completed|images-available,transactional_data,The workflow status of the imaging order immediately before this transition event. Enables reconstruction of the full status progression sequence and detection of invalid or out-of-sequence transitions. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: ordered|scheduled|patient-arrived|exam-started|exam-completed|images-available|preliminary-read|final-read|report-signed|report-delivered|cancelled|on-hold — promote to reference product],
radiology,order_management,radiology_order_status_history,radiology_order_status_history_status,radiology_order_status_history_status,,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,description,
radiology,order_management,radiology_order_status_history,ris_order_status_code,ris_order_status_code,Radiology Information System (RIS) Order Status Code,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,The native status code as recorded in the source RIS system (Epic Radiant or Cerner RadNet) before normalization to the enterprise status vocabulary. Preserves source fidelity for reconciliation and interface troubleshooting.,
radiology,order_management,radiology_order_status_history,sequence_number,sequence_number,Status Sequence Number,INT,,,,,transactional_data,"Ordinal sequence number of this status transition within the lifecycle of the imaging order, starting at 1 for the first transition. Enables ordered reconstruction of the complete status history and detection of missing or duplicate events.",
radiology,order_management,radiology_order_status_history,sla_threshold_seconds,sla_threshold_seconds,Service Level Agreement (SLA) Threshold Seconds,INT,,,,,transactional_data,"The configured SLA time threshold in seconds for this specific status transition, based on order priority and modality type. Used to evaluate whether the transition met the defined Service Level Agreement (SLA) target.",
radiology,order_management,radiology_order_status_history,source_system,source_system,Source System,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"The originating system or interface that generated this status change event (e.g., Epic Radiant, Cerner RadNet, HL7 interface engine, manual entry). Critical for data lineage, reconciliation, and multi-system RIS environments. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: Epic-Radiant|Cerner-RadNet|MEDITECH|HL7-Interface|Manual|API|other — 7 candidates stripped; promote to reference product]",
radiology,order_management,radiology_order_status_history,source_system_event_code,source_system_event_code,Source System Event ID,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,The native event or transaction identifier assigned by the originating RIS or interface system for this status change. Enables traceability back to the source system record for reconciliation and audit purposes.,
radiology,order_management,radiology_order_status_history,status_change_reason,status_change_reason,Status Change Reason,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Free-text or coded reason explaining why the status transition occurred. Particularly important for cancellation, on-hold, and exception states. Supports root cause analysis and RIS process improvement initiatives.",
radiology,order_management,radiology_order_status_history,status_change_reason_code,status_change_reason_code,Status Change Reason Code,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Standardized coded value for the status change reason, drawn from the RIS reason code master. Enables structured analytics and reporting on transition causes without relying on free-text parsing.",
radiology,order_management,radiology_order_status_history,status_change_timestamp,status_change_timestamp,Status Change Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,"The precise date and time when the status transition occurred in the RIS system. This is the principal business event timestamp for this log record, used for SLA compliance measurement, workflow duration analytics, and turnaround time reporting.",
radiology,order_management,radiology_order_status_history,transition_duration_seconds,transition_duration_seconds,Transition Duration Seconds,INT,,,,,transactional_data,"The elapsed time in seconds between the prior status and this new status transition. Computed at ingestion time from consecutive status timestamps and stored to support SLA compliance measurement, bottleneck identification, and workflow efficiency analytics without requiring window function recalculation.",
radiology,order_management,radiology_order_status_history,updated_timestamp,updated_timestamp,Record Updated Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,"The date and time when this status history record was last modified in the data platform, typically populated only for corrective entries. Supports change data capture and audit trail completeness.",
radiology,order_management,radiology_order_status_history,workstation_code,workstation_code,Workstation ID,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,Identifier of the RIS or PACS workstation from which the status change was performed. Supports physical location tracking of workflow events and security audit requirements under HIPAA access controls.,
radiology,quality_operations,interventional_procedure,interventional_procedure_id,interventional_procedure_id,Interventional Procedure ID,BIGINT,Y,,,,transactional_data,Unique surrogate identifier for the interventional radiology (IR) procedure record in the lakehouse silver layer. Primary key for this entity.,
radiology,quality_operations,interventional_procedure,biopsy_specimen_id,biopsy_specimen_id,Biopsy Specimen Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,laboratory.specimen.specimen_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to laboratory.specimen. Business justification: Interventional radiology performs image-guided biopsies, aspirations, and tissue sampling that generate laboratory specimens requiring pathology or microbiology analysis. Chain of custody, specimen tr",
radiology,quality_operations,interventional_procedure,care_site_id,care_site_id,Facility ID,BIGINT,,facility.care_site.care_site_id,,,transactional_data,"Reference to the facility or suite (IR suite, hybrid OR, cath lab) where the procedure was performed.",
radiology,quality_operations,interventional_procedure,clinical_order_id,clinical_order_id,Clinical Order Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,order.clinical_order.clinical_order_id,,,transactional_data,Foreign key linking to order.clinical_order. Business justification: Interventional radiology procedures are ordered via clinical orders. Procedural documentation requires linking procedure reports to original order indication for clinical context. Charge capture valid,
radiology,quality_operations,interventional_procedure,contrast_drug_master_id,contrast_drug_master_id,Contrast Drug Master Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,pharmacy.drug_master.drug_master_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to pharmacy.drug_master. Business justification: Interventional procedures use contrast agents and may involve sedation/anesthesia medications. FK to drug_master enables medication reconciliation, adverse event tracking, billing accuracy, and regula",
radiology,quality_operations,interventional_procedure,cpt_code_id,cpt_code_id,Cpt Code Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,reference.cpt_code.cpt_code_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to reference.cpt_code. Business justification: Interventional procedures are billed using CPT codes for charge capture, RVU calculation, and procedural volume tracking. Essential for interventional radiology revenue cycle and productivity analytic",
radiology,quality_operations,interventional_procedure,demographics_id,demographics_id,Patient ID,BIGINT,,patient.demographics.demographics_id,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_identifier",,transactional_data,Reference to the patient who underwent the interventional procedure. Links to the master patient record.,
radiology,quality_operations,interventional_procedure,employee_id,employee_id,Scrub Technologist ID,BIGINT,,workforce.employee.employee_id,"dbx_confidential, dbx_pii",,transactional_data,"Reference to the radiology technologist or scrub tech who assisted with the procedure. Used for staffing analytics, competency tracking, and case documentation.",
radiology,quality_operations,interventional_procedure,icd10_primary_diagnosis_icd_code_id,icd10_primary_diagnosis_icd_code_id,Icd10 Primary Diagnosis Icd Code Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,reference.icd_code.icd_code_id,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_health",,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to reference.icd_code. Business justification: Interventional procedures document primary diagnosis for medical necessity validation, prior authorization, and outcomes tracking by indication. Supports interventional radiology quality and appropria",
radiology,quality_operations,interventional_procedure,imaging_order_id,imaging_order_id,Imaging Order ID,BIGINT,,radiology.imaging_order.imaging_order_id,,,transactional_data,Reference to the originating imaging order (from radiology.imaging_order) that triggered this interventional procedure.,
radiology,quality_operations,interventional_procedure,message_log_id,message_log_id,Message Log Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,interoperability.message_log.message_log_id,,,transactional_data,Foreign key linking to interoperability.message_log. Business justification: Interventional radiology procedures generate HL7 ORU result messages and DICOM structured reports (SR) for procedure documentation exchange with referring providers and EHR systems. Message_log tracks,
radiology,quality_operations,interventional_procedure,osha_exposure_incident_id,osha_exposure_incident_id,Osha Exposure Incident Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,compliance.osha_exposure_incident.osha_exposure_incident_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to compliance.osha_exposure_incident. Business justification: Interventional radiology procedures involve radiation and sharps exposure risks. OSHA tracks employee exposures (needlesticks, radiation overexposure) during IR procedures; incidents reference the spe",
radiology,quality_operations,interventional_procedure,preprocedure_lab_order_id,preprocedure_lab_order_id,Preprocedure Lab Order Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,laboratory.lab_order.lab_order_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to laboratory.lab_order. Business justification: Pre-procedure lab orders (PT/INR, platelet count, CBC) are standard of care for interventional procedures to assess bleeding risk and procedural safety. Regulatory and accreditation requirements manda",
radiology,quality_operations,interventional_procedure,primary_device_material_master_id,primary_device_material_master_id,Primary Device Material Master Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,supply.material_master.material_master_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to supply.material_master. Business justification: Interventional radiology procedures consume high-cost devices (stents, catheters, guidewires, embolization coils) tracked in material master. Essential for accurate procedure costing, charge capture, ",
radiology,quality_operations,interventional_procedure,primary_interventional_clinician_id,primary_interventional_clinician_id,Performing Provider ID,BIGINT,,provider.clinician.clinician_id,,,transactional_data,Reference to the interventional radiologist or proceduralist who performed the procedure. Maps to the provider master record.,
radiology,quality_operations,interventional_procedure,procedure_room_id,procedure_room_id,Procedure Room Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,facility.room.room_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to facility.room. Business justification: Interventional radiology procedures (biopsies, drainages, vascular interventions) occur in specific IR suites/procedure rooms. Tracking the exact room is essential for: (1) scheduling and room utiliza",
radiology,quality_operations,interventional_procedure,research_study_id,research_study_id,Research Study Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,research.research_study.research_study_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to research.research_study. Business justification: Interventional radiology procedures are often investigational (device trials, novel techniques) or protocol-specified interventions. Linkage required for IDE compliance, device accountability, procedu",
radiology,quality_operations,interventional_procedure,surgical_case_id,surgical_case_id,Surgical Case Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,scheduling.surgical_case.surgical_case_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to scheduling.surgical_case. Business justification: Interventional radiology procedures requiring OR time are scheduled through surgical scheduling system. Real workflow: IR cases booked as surgical cases, then tracked in radiologys interventional_pro",
radiology,quality_operations,interventional_procedure,treatment_consent_id,treatment_consent_id,Treatment Consent Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,consent.treatment_consent.treatment_consent_id,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii",,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to consent.treatment_consent. Business justification: Interventional radiology procedures (biopsies, drains, ablations, embolizations) require specific procedural informed consent documenting risks, benefits, alternatives. Critical regulatory requirement",
radiology,quality_operations,interventional_procedure,visit_id,visit_id,Encounter ID,BIGINT,,encounter.visit.visit_id,,,transactional_data,"Reference to the clinical encounter (inpatient, outpatient, or ED visit) during which the interventional procedure was performed.",
radiology,quality_operations,interventional_procedure,access_site,access_site,Vascular Access Site,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Anatomical location used for vascular or percutaneous access during the procedure (e.g., right common femoral artery, right internal jugular vein, left radial artery). Critical for complication tracking and access-site adverse event reporting.",
radiology,quality_operations,interventional_procedure,accession_number,accession_number,Accession Number,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Unique RIS-assigned accession number for this interventional procedure, used for PACS integration and DICOM image linkage. Serves as the primary business identifier within the Radiology Information System (RIS).",
radiology,quality_operations,interventional_procedure,anesthesia_type,anesthesia_type,Anesthesia Type,STRING,,,,none|local|moderate-sedation|general|MAC|spinal,transactional_data,"Type of anesthesia or sedation administered during the interventional procedure. Impacts OR scheduling, anesthesia billing, and patient safety monitoring requirements.",
radiology,quality_operations,interventional_procedure,asa_classification,asa_classification,American Society of Anesthesiologists (ASA) Physical Status Classification,STRING,,,,ASA-I|ASA-II|ASA-III|ASA-IV|ASA-V|ASA-VI,transactional_data,"ASA physical status classification assigned to the patient prior to the procedure, reflecting overall health and anesthetic risk. Required for anesthesia billing, risk-adjusted outcome reporting, and case complexity analysis.",
radiology,quality_operations,interventional_procedure,body_region,body_region,Body Region,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Anatomical body region or organ system targeted by the intervention (e.g., hepatic, renal, pulmonary, peripheral vascular, spine). Used for procedure classification, PACS routing, and quality reporting.",
radiology,quality_operations,interventional_procedure,cancellation_reason,cancellation_reason,Cancellation Reason,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Reason the procedure was cancelled (e.g., patient declined, clinical contraindication, equipment failure, scheduling conflict). Required for operational improvement and suite utilization reporting. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: patient-declined|clinical-contraindication|equipment-failure|scheduling-conflict|insurance-denial|patient-no-show|other — promote to reference product]",
radiology,quality_operations,interventional_procedure,cancelled_timestamp,cancelled_timestamp,Cancellation Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,"Date and time the procedure was cancelled, if applicable. Used for suite utilization analysis, cancellation rate reporting, and downstream order management.",
radiology,quality_operations,interventional_procedure,complication_occurred,complication_occurred,Complication Occurred Indicator,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,Indicates whether a procedural complication was documented during or immediately following the interventional procedure. Triggers complication detail capture and quality event reporting workflows.,
radiology,quality_operations,interventional_procedure,complication_severity,complication_severity,Complication Severity Grade,STRING,,,,minor|moderate|major|death,transactional_data,"SIR severity grade of the documented complication: minor (no therapy required), moderate (nominal therapy required), major (major therapy required or permanent adverse sequelae), or death. Used for quality benchmarking and regulatory reporting.",
radiology,quality_operations,interventional_procedure,complication_type,complication_type,Complication Type,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Standardized classification of the procedural complication using SIR severity grading (e.g., hemorrhage, vessel perforation, contrast reaction, infection, pneumothorax). Required for SIR quality benchmarking and adverse event reporting. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: hemorrhage|vessel-perforation|contrast-reaction|infection|pneumothorax|nerve-injury|device-malfunction|other — promote to reference product]",
radiology,quality_operations,interventional_procedure,contrast_agent_used,contrast_agent_used,Contrast Agent Used Indicator,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,"Indicates whether an iodinated or gadolinium-based contrast agent was administered during the interventional procedure. Drives contrast reaction monitoring, nephrotoxicity risk documentation, and billing for contrast administration.",
radiology,quality_operations,interventional_procedure,contrast_volume_ml,contrast_volume_ml,Contrast Volume Administered (mL),"DECIMAL(7,2)",,,,,transactional_data,"Total volume of contrast agent administered in milliliters during the procedure. Used for nephrotoxicity risk stratification (contrast-to-creatinine ratio), adverse event documentation, and quality benchmarking.",
radiology,quality_operations,interventional_procedure,created_timestamp,created_timestamp,Record Created Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,Date and time when the interventional procedure record was first created in the source system (RIS/EHR). Audit trail field for data lineage and HIPAA audit log compliance.,
radiology,quality_operations,interventional_procedure,device_name,device_name,Device Name,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Commercial or generic name of the primary medical device or implant used (e.g., Wallstent Endoprosthesis, Greenfield IVC Filter, Port-a-Cath). Supports supply chain reconciliation and device surveillance.",
radiology,quality_operations,interventional_procedure,device_udi,device_udi,Device Unique Device Identifier (UDI),STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"FDA-assigned Unique Device Identifier (UDI) for the primary implant or device placed during the procedure. Mandatory for device surveillance, recall management, and FDA GUDID registry compliance.",
radiology,quality_operations,interventional_procedure,fluoroscopy_time_minutes,fluoroscopy_time_minutes,Fluoroscopy Time (Minutes),"DECIMAL(8,2)",,,,,transactional_data,"Total cumulative fluoroscopy time in minutes recorded during the procedure. Mandatory for radiation dose documentation, ALARA compliance, and Joint Commission radiation safety reporting.",
radiology,quality_operations,interventional_procedure,icd10_post_procedure_diagnosis_code,icd10_post_procedure_diagnosis_code,International Classification of Diseases 10th Revision (ICD-10) Post-Procedure Diagnosis Code,STRING,,,"dbx_pii_health,dbx_restricted,pii_phi,pii_pii,pii_sensitive","^[A-Z][0-9]{2}(.[A-Z0-9]{1,4})?$",transactional_data,"ICD-10-CM diagnosis code assigned after the procedure, reflecting findings confirmed or revised during the intervention. May differ from pre-procedure diagnosis and is used for DRG grouping and CDI.",
radiology,quality_operations,interventional_procedure,imaging_guidance_modality,imaging_guidance_modality,Imaging Guidance Modality,STRING,,,,fluoroscopy|CT|ultrasound|MRI|PET-CT|combined,transactional_data,"Imaging modality used to guide the interventional procedure in real time (e.g., fluoroscopy for vascular interventions, CT for biopsies, ultrasound for drainage). Drives radiation dose tracking and CPT guidance code selection.",
radiology,quality_operations,interventional_procedure,implant_used,implant_used,Implant Used Indicator,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,"Indicates whether a medical device or implant (stent, coil, filter, catheter, port) was placed during the procedure. Triggers UDI capture requirements per FDA 21st Century Cures Act and device surveillance workflows.",
radiology,quality_operations,interventional_procedure,laterality,laterality,Procedure Laterality,STRING,,,,left|right|bilateral|midline|not-applicable,transactional_data,"Anatomical side of the body on which the interventional procedure was performed. Required for correct-site surgery compliance, ICD-10 coding, and wrong-site event prevention per Joint Commission Universal Protocol.",
radiology,quality_operations,interventional_procedure,performing_provider_npi,performing_provider_npi,Performing Provider National Provider Identifier (NPI),STRING,,,,^[0-9]{10}$,transactional_data,10-digit National Provider Identifier (NPI) of the interventional radiologist who performed the procedure. Required on professional claims (CMS-1500) and for provider credentialing verification.,
radiology,quality_operations,interventional_procedure,procedure_approach,procedure_approach,Procedure Approach,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Technique or approach used to access the target anatomy during the interventional procedure. Impacts CPT code selection, complication risk stratification, and case complexity scoring. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: percutaneous|endovascular|endoscopic|open-hybrid|transarterial|transvenous|transhepatic — promote to reference product]",
radiology,quality_operations,interventional_procedure,procedure_category,procedure_category,Interventional Radiology (IR) Procedure Category,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"High-level clinical category of the interventional radiology procedure. Supports case mix analysis, resource planning, and complication benchmarking. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: vascular|non-vascular|neuro-IR|oncologic|drainage|biopsy|embolization|other — promote to reference product]",
radiology,quality_operations,interventional_procedure,procedure_end_timestamp,procedure_end_timestamp,Procedure End Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,"Date and time when the interventional procedure was completed (dressing applied, catheter removed, or patient left the IR suite). Used with start timestamp to calculate procedure duration for suite utilization and staffing analytics.",
radiology,quality_operations,interventional_procedure,procedure_name,procedure_name,Procedure Name,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Full descriptive name of the interventional procedure as documented in the RIS/EHR (e.g., Percutaneous Transhepatic Cholangiography, TIPS Procedure, Uterine Fibroid Embolization).",
radiology,quality_operations,interventional_procedure,procedure_start_timestamp,procedure_start_timestamp,Procedure Start Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,"Date and time when the interventional procedure was initiated (first incision, needle insertion, or catheter placement). Principal business event timestamp for case duration calculation and OR/suite utilization reporting.",
radiology,quality_operations,interventional_procedure,procedure_status,procedure_status,Procedure Status,STRING,,,,scheduled|in-progress|completed|cancelled|on-hold,transactional_data,"Current lifecycle status of the interventional procedure, aligned with HL7 FHIR Procedure.status value set. Drives workflow routing in the RIS and case management dashboards.",
radiology,quality_operations,interventional_procedure,radiation_dose_dap_gycm2,radiation_dose_dap_gycm2,Radiation Dose Area Product (DAP) (Gy·cm²),"DECIMAL(10,3)",,,,,transactional_data,"Dose-area product (DAP) in Gy·cm² representing the total radiation energy delivered, accounting for field size. Complementary to RAK for stochastic risk estimation and dose registry reporting.",
radiology,quality_operations,interventional_procedure,radiation_dose_kerma_mgy,radiation_dose_kerma_mgy,Radiation Dose Reference Air Kerma (mGy),"DECIMAL(10,3)",,,,,transactional_data,Total reference air kerma (RAK) in milligrays (mGy) delivered to the patient during the procedure. Primary radiation dose metric for fluoroscopy-guided interventions per ACR and Joint Commission dose tracking requirements.,
radiology,quality_operations,interventional_procedure,report_finalized_timestamp,report_finalized_timestamp,Report Finalized Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,Date and time when the interventional radiology procedure report was finalized (signed) by the interpreting radiologist. Used for turnaround time (TAT) measurement and regulatory reporting on result communication.,
radiology,quality_operations,interventional_procedure,report_status,report_status,Radiology Report Status,STRING,,,,preliminary|final|addendum|amended|cancelled,transactional_data,"Current status of the interventional radiology procedure report in the RIS/PACS workflow. Drives report distribution, result notification, and HIM documentation completion tracking.",
radiology,quality_operations,interventional_procedure,secondary_cpt_codes,secondary_cpt_codes,Secondary Current Procedural Terminology (CPT) Codes,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Pipe-delimited list of additional CPT codes for add-on procedures, guidance codes, or concurrent services performed during the same IR session (e.g., imaging guidance CPT 77012 alongside a biopsy CPT).",
radiology,quality_operations,interventional_procedure,specimen_collected,specimen_collected,Specimen Collected Indicator,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,"Indicates whether a tissue or fluid specimen was collected during the procedure (e.g., biopsy core, aspirate, cytology). Triggers downstream laboratory order linkage and pathology workflow.",
radiology,quality_operations,interventional_procedure,specimen_type,specimen_type,Specimen Type,STRING,,,,core-biopsy|fine-needle-aspirate|fluid-aspirate|tissue-excision|cytology|not-applicable,transactional_data,"Type of specimen collected during the interventional procedure. Used for pathology order routing, LIS integration, and quality reporting on diagnostic yield.",
radiology,quality_operations,interventional_procedure,technical_success,technical_success,Technical Success Indicator,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,"Indicates whether the procedure achieved its intended technical endpoint as defined by the performing interventionalist (e.g., successful vessel recanalization, complete embolization, adequate drainage). Core quality metric for IR outcome reporting.",
radiology,quality_operations,interventional_procedure,updated_timestamp,updated_timestamp,Record Updated Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,"Date and time when the interventional procedure record was last modified in the source system. Supports incremental ETL processing, audit trail maintenance, and change data capture.",
radiology,quality_operations,network_modality_participation,network_modality_participation_id,network_modality_participation_id,Network Modality Participation Identifier,BIGINT,Y,,,,association_data,Unique surrogate identifier for this network modality participation record. Primary key.,
radiology,quality_operations,network_modality_participation,facility_contract_id,facility_contract_id,Network Contract Identifier,BIGINT,,facility.facility_contract.facility_contract_id,,,association_data,"Business identifier for the underlying contract or participation agreement governing this modalitys inclusion in the network. Links to contract management systems for terms, amendments, and renewal tracking.",
radiology,quality_operations,network_modality_participation,modality_id,modality_id,Network Modality Participation - Modality Id,BIGINT,,radiology.modality.modality_id,,,association_data,Foreign key linking to the imaging modality unit participating in this network,
radiology,quality_operations,network_modality_participation,provider_network_id,provider_network_id,Network Modality Participation - Provider Network Id,BIGINT,,insurance.provider_network.provider_network_id,,,association_data,Foreign key linking to the provider network in which this modality participates,
radiology,quality_operations,network_modality_participation,accepting_new_referrals_flag,accepting_new_referrals_flag,Accepting New Referrals Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,association_data,"Indicates whether this modality is currently accepting new patient referrals through this network. True allows scheduling, False blocks new appointments. May differ from overall modality operational status due to network-specific capacity management.",
radiology,quality_operations,network_modality_participation,authorization_required_flag,authorization_required_flag,Prior Authorization Required Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,association_data,"Indicates whether prior authorization or pre-certification is required for imaging services on this modality within this network. True requires authorization before service, False allows direct access. Drives utilization management workflows.",
radiology,quality_operations,network_modality_participation,authorization_threshold_amount,authorization_threshold_amount,Authorization Threshold Amount,"DECIMAL(10,2)",,,,,association_data,Dollar amount threshold above which prior authorization is required for services on this modality. Null if authorization_required_flag is False or if all services require authorization regardless of cost.,
radiology,quality_operations,network_modality_participation,contracted_rate,contracted_rate,Contracted Modality Rate,"DECIMAL(12,2)",,,dbx_pii-financial,,association_data,"Negotiated reimbursement rate for imaging services performed on this modality within this network. May be per-procedure, per-study, or bundled rate depending on contract terms. Used for claims adjudication and provider payment.",
radiology,quality_operations,network_modality_participation,created_timestamp,created_timestamp,Record Created Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,association_data,Timestamp when this network modality participation record was created in the system. Audit field for data lineage and compliance.,
radiology,quality_operations,network_modality_participation,credentialing_verified_date,credentialing_verified_date,Credentialing Verification Date,DATE,,,,,association_data,Date when the facility and modality credentials were verified for network participation. Required for CMS network adequacy and accreditation compliance. Typically reverified on recredentialing cycle.,
radiology,quality_operations,network_modality_participation,effective_date,effective_date,Participation Effective Date,DATE,,,,,association_data,Date when this modalitys participation in the provider network becomes active. Used for claims adjudication to determine in-network vs out-of-network status at service date.,
radiology,quality_operations,network_modality_participation,member_cost_share_tier,member_cost_share_tier,Member Cost Share Tier,STRING,,,,,association_data,"Cost-sharing tier assigned to this modality within this network, determining member copay, coinsurance, and deductible application. Aligns with network tier and modality quality/efficiency metrics.",
radiology,quality_operations,network_modality_participation,network_adequacy_counted_flag,network_adequacy_counted_flag,Network Adequacy Counted Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,association_data,"Indicates whether this modality is counted toward network adequacy metrics for CMS or state regulatory reporting. True if modality meets adequacy criteria (accepting patients, operational, credentialed). False if excluded from adequacy calculations.",
radiology,quality_operations,network_modality_participation,next_credentialing_due_date,next_credentialing_due_date,Next Credentialing Due Date,DATE,,,,,association_data,Scheduled date for next credentialing review of this modalitys network participation. Drives compliance workflows and network adequacy maintenance.,
radiology,quality_operations,network_modality_participation,participation_status,participation_status,Network Participation Status,STRING,,,,,association_data,Current lifecycle status of this modalitys participation in the provider network. Active indicates the modality is currently in-network and available for member utilization. Drives claims adjudication and member cost-sharing calculations.,
radiology,quality_operations,network_modality_participation,quality_tier_assignment,quality_tier_assignment,Quality Tier Assignment,STRING,,,,,association_data,"Quality performance tier assigned to this modality within this network based on quality metrics, patient outcomes, and efficiency measures. Used for tiered network design and member steering.",
radiology,quality_operations,network_modality_participation,rate_type,rate_type,Rate Type,STRING,,,,,association_data,"Classification of how the contracted rate is structured. Per-Procedure rates apply to individual CPT codes, Per-Study rates apply to complete imaging studies, Bundled rates cover multiple services, Fee-Schedule references a standard fee schedule, Percentage-of-Charges applies a discount to billed charges.",
radiology,quality_operations,network_modality_participation,termination_date,termination_date,Participation Termination Date,DATE,,,,,association_data,Date when this modalitys participation in the provider network ends. Null if participation is ongoing. Critical for claims processing and member notification of network changes.,
radiology,quality_operations,network_modality_participation,updated_timestamp,updated_timestamp,Record Updated Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,association_data,Timestamp when this network modality participation record was last updated. Audit field for change tracking and data quality monitoring.,
radiology,quality_operations,radiology_peer_review,radiology_peer_review_id,radiology_peer_review_id,Radiology Peer Review ID,BIGINT,Y,,,,transactional_data,Unique surrogate identifier for each radiology peer review event record in the silver layer lakehouse. Primary key for this entity.,
radiology,quality_operations,radiology_peer_review,audit_finding_id,audit_finding_id,Audit Finding Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,compliance.audit_finding.audit_finding_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to compliance.audit_finding. Business justification: Peer review programs are audited for OPPE/FPPE compliance, ACR RadPeer standards, and medical staff bylaws adherence. Compliance verifies peer review program effectiveness and regulatory compliance.",
radiology,quality_operations,radiology_peer_review,care_site_id,care_site_id,Facility ID,BIGINT,,facility.care_site.care_site_id,,,transactional_data,Reference to the facility or imaging center where the original study was performed and where the peer review is attributed for accreditation and quality reporting purposes.,
radiology,quality_operations,radiology_peer_review,corrective_action_plan_id,corrective_action_plan_id,Corrective Action Plan Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,compliance.corrective_action_plan.corrective_action_plan_id,,,transactional_data,Foreign key linking to compliance.corrective_action_plan. Business justification: Peer review discrepancies trigger corrective action plans for quality improvement and patient safety. Quality/compliance departments create CAPs to address systematic issues identified through peer re,
radiology,quality_operations,radiology_peer_review,cpt_code_id,cpt_code_id,Cpt Code Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,reference.cpt_code.cpt_code_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to reference.cpt_code. Business justification: Peer reviews reference procedure codes for case categorization, discrepancy rate analysis by exam type, and OPPE/FPPE reporting. Links enable quality improvement targeting by procedure complexity.",
radiology,quality_operations,radiology_peer_review,employee_id,employee_id,Coordinator Employee Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,workforce.employee.employee_id,"dbx_confidential, dbx_pii",,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to workforce.employee. Business justification: Peer review programs have administrative coordinators (QA nurses, radiology managers) who manage case selection, distribution, and follow-up. Required for OPPE/FPPE programs and accreditation.",
radiology,quality_operations,radiology_peer_review,org_unit_id,org_unit_id,Department ID,BIGINT,,workforce.org_unit.org_unit_id,,,transactional_data,"Reference to the radiology department or imaging section (e.g., Neuroradiology, Body Imaging, Emergency Radiology) within the facility where the peer review is attributed. Supports department-level quality metric stratification.",
radiology,quality_operations,radiology_peer_review,report_addendum_id,report_addendum_id,Addendum Report ID,BIGINT,,radiology.report_addendum.report_addendum_id,,,transactional_data,"Reference to the addendum or amended radiology report created as a result of this peer review, if applicable. Populated only when review_disposition is addendum_required or report_amended. Supports audit trail linking original and corrected reports.",
radiology,quality_operations,radiology_peer_review,report_id,report_id,Original Radiology Report ID,BIGINT,,radiology.report.report_id,,,transactional_data,Reference to the radiology report that was authored by the original interpreting radiologist and is being reviewed in this peer review event.,
radiology,quality_operations,radiology_peer_review,visit_id,visit_id,Encounter ID,BIGINT,,encounter.visit.visit_id,,,transactional_data,Reference to the patient encounter (visit) associated with the imaging study under review. Supports clinical context linkage for quality and population health analytics.,
radiology,quality_operations,radiology_peer_review,accession_number,accession_number,Accession Number,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,The RIS-assigned accession number of the original imaging study that is the subject of this peer review. Serves as the primary business identifier linking the review to the source imaging order and PACS study.,
radiology,quality_operations,radiology_peer_review,acr_accreditation_cycle,acr_accreditation_cycle,ACR Accreditation Cycle,STRING,,,,^[0-9]{4}-[0-9]{4}$,transactional_data,"The ACR accreditation cycle year range (e.g., 2023-2026) to which this peer review event is attributed. Used to aggregate peer review volumes and discrepancy rates for ACR accreditation submission and renewal reporting.",
radiology,quality_operations,radiology_peer_review,acr_radpeer_score,acr_radpeer_score,ACR RADPEER Concordance Score,INT,,,,,transactional_data,"The ACR RADPEER 2.0 concordance rating assigned by the reviewing radiologist on a 1–4 scale: 1 = Agree with interpretation; 2 = Disagree, but would not have changed management; 3 = Disagree, may have changed management; 4 = Disagree, would have changed management. Drives quality reporting and radiologist performance management.",
radiology,quality_operations,radiology_peer_review,blinded_review_flag,blinded_review_flag,Blinded Review Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,"Indicates whether the peer review was conducted in a blinded manner, meaning the reviewing radiologist did not have access to the original report at the time of review. True = blinded review (ACR RADPEER preferred methodology); False = non-blinded review.",
radiology,quality_operations,radiology_peer_review,body_part_examined,body_part_examined,Body Part Examined,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"The anatomical region or body part that was the primary subject of the imaging study under review, using SNOMED CT or DICOM body part terminology (e.g., CHEST, ABDOMEN, BRAIN, SPINE). Supports subspecialty-level peer review analytics.",
radiology,quality_operations,radiology_peer_review,case_conference_flag,case_conference_flag,Case Conference Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,Indicates whether this peer review case was referred to or discussed at a departmental case conference or quality committee meeting. True = case was presented at conference; False = not referred to conference. Supports TJC quality committee documentation requirements.,
radiology,quality_operations,radiology_peer_review,clinical_history_available_flag,clinical_history_available_flag,Clinical History Available Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,Indicates whether adequate clinical history was available to the original interpreting radiologist at the time of interpretation. Contextual factor used in assessing the fairness and validity of the peer review discrepancy rating.,
radiology,quality_operations,radiology_peer_review,created_timestamp,created_timestamp,Record Created Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,"The date and time this peer review record was first created in the data platform. Audit trail field supporting data lineage, compliance, and silver layer ingestion tracking.",
radiology,quality_operations,radiology_peer_review,discrepancy_category,discrepancy_category,Discrepancy Category,STRING,,,,none|minor|major,transactional_data,Classification of the interpretation discrepancy identified during peer review. none = no discrepancy found (RADPEER score 1); minor = discrepancy unlikely to change clinical management (RADPEER score 2); major = discrepancy that may or would change clinical management (RADPEER scores 3–4). Drives escalation and reporting workflows.,
radiology,quality_operations,radiology_peer_review,discrepancy_description,discrepancy_description,Discrepancy Description,STRING,,,"dbx_confidential,pii_phi,pii_pii,pii_sensitive",,transactional_data,"Free-text narrative describing the nature of the interpretation discrepancy identified by the reviewing radiologist. Captures the specific finding, anatomical location, and clinical significance. Protected under peer review privilege in most jurisdictions.",
radiology,quality_operations,radiology_peer_review,discrepancy_type,discrepancy_type,Discrepancy Type,STRING,,,,missed_finding|mischaracterization|incorrect_recommendation|incomplete_report|wrong_anatomy,transactional_data,Categorical classification of the type of interpretation error or discrepancy identified. missed_finding = finding present but not reported; mischaracterization = finding reported but incorrectly described; incorrect_recommendation = appropriate finding but wrong follow-up recommendation; incomplete_report = report lacks required elements; wrong_anatomy = finding attributed to incorrect anatomical location. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: missed_finding|mischaracterization|incorrect_recommendation|incomplete_report|wrong_anatomy — promote to reference product],
radiology,quality_operations,radiology_peer_review,educational_feedback_flag,educational_feedback_flag,Educational Feedback Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,Indicates whether the peer review event generated educational feedback to be communicated to the original interpreting radiologist. True = educational feedback was provided; False = no educational feedback generated. Supports CME tracking and radiologist performance improvement programs.,
radiology,quality_operations,radiology_peer_review,escalated_to_chair_flag,escalated_to_chair_flag,Escalated to Department Chair Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,Indicates whether this peer review case was escalated to the radiology department chair or medical director due to a major discrepancy or patient safety concern. True = escalated; False = not escalated. Triggers formal performance management workflow.,
radiology,quality_operations,radiology_peer_review,icd10_finding_code,icd10_finding_code,International Classification of Diseases 10th Revision (ICD-10) Finding Code,STRING,,,,"^[A-Z][0-9]{2}(.[A-Z0-9]{1,4})?$",transactional_data,"The ICD-10-CM diagnosis code corresponding to the primary imaging finding or discrepancy identified during peer review. Supports clinical coding alignment, quality reporting, and population health analytics.",
radiology,quality_operations,radiology_peer_review,modality_code,modality_code,Imaging Modality Code,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"DICOM-standard modality code identifying the imaging technology used for the study under review (e.g., CT = Computed Tomography, MR = Magnetic Resonance Imaging, XR = X-Ray, US = Ultrasound, PT = PET). Used for subspecialty-stratified peer review reporting and ACR accreditation compliance. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: CT|MR|XR|US|PT|NM|MG|FL|DX|CR — 10 candidates stripped; promote to reference product]",
radiology,quality_operations,radiology_peer_review,oppe_fppe_flag,oppe_fppe_flag,Ongoing/Focused Professional Practice Evaluation (OPPE/FPPE) Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,Indicates whether this peer review event is being counted toward the radiologists Ongoing Professional Practice Evaluation (OPPE) or Focused Professional Practice Evaluation (FPPE) for medical staff credentialing and privileging purposes. True = counts toward OPPE/FPPE; False = routine QA only.,
radiology,quality_operations,radiology_peer_review,original_radiologist_npi,original_radiologist_npi,Original Radiologist National Provider Identifier (NPI),STRING,,,"pii_phi,pii_pii,pii_sensitive",^[0-9]{10}$,transactional_data,The 10-digit National Provider Identifier (NPI) of the radiologist who authored the original interpretation being reviewed. Used for performance tracking and credentialing compliance.,
radiology,quality_operations,radiology_peer_review,original_radiologist_response,original_radiologist_response,Original Radiologist Response,STRING,,,"dbx_confidential,pii_phi,pii_pii,pii_sensitive",,transactional_data,Free-text response or rebuttal provided by the original interpreting radiologist in response to the peer review findings. Supports the formal peer review appeal and feedback loop process. Protected under peer review privilege.,
radiology,quality_operations,radiology_peer_review,original_report_finalized_datetime,original_report_finalized_datetime,Original Report Finalized Date and Time,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,"The date and time the original radiology report was finalized (signed/attested) by the interpreting radiologist. Used to calculate the lag between report finalization and peer review, and to assess timeliness of discrepancy identification.",
radiology,quality_operations,radiology_peer_review,patient_safety_event_flag,patient_safety_event_flag,Patient Safety Event Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,Indicates whether the discrepancy identified in this peer review was determined to constitute a patient safety event requiring reporting to the facilitys patient safety officer or risk management. True = patient safety event; False = not a patient safety event.,
radiology,quality_operations,radiology_peer_review,prior_study_available_flag,prior_study_available_flag,Prior Study Available Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,Indicates whether prior imaging studies were available to the original interpreting radiologist at the time of interpretation. Relevant context for assessing the reasonableness of the original interpretation and the severity of any discrepancy.,
radiology,quality_operations,radiology_peer_review,response_datetime,response_datetime,Original Radiologist Response Date and Time,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,The date and time the original interpreting radiologist submitted their response or acknowledgment of the peer review findings. Used to track completion of the feedback loop and compliance with departmental peer review policy timelines.,
radiology,quality_operations,radiology_peer_review,review_assigned_datetime,review_assigned_datetime,Peer Review Assigned Date and Time,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,The date and time the peer review case was assigned to the reviewing radiologist. Used to calculate turnaround time and compliance with departmental SLA targets for peer review completion.,
radiology,quality_operations,radiology_peer_review,review_datetime,review_datetime,Peer Review Date and Time,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,The date and time at which the peer review was performed and the concordance score was assigned by the reviewing radiologist. Principal business event timestamp for this transaction.,
radiology,quality_operations,radiology_peer_review,review_disposition,review_disposition,Peer Review Disposition,STRING,,,,no_action|feedback_provided|addendum_required|report_amended|escalated|referred_to_committee,transactional_data,"The final action or outcome disposition resulting from the peer review. no_action = review complete, no further action needed; feedback_provided = educational feedback sent to original radiologist; addendum_required = original report requires addendum; report_amended = original report was amended; escalated = referred to department leadership; referred_to_committee = referred to quality or peer review committee. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: no_action|feedback_provided|addendum_required|report_amended|escalated|referred_to_committee — promote to reference product]",
radiology,quality_operations,radiology_peer_review,review_program_type,review_program_type,Peer Review Program Type,STRING,,,,acr_radpeer|internal_qa|mips|vbp|tjc_required|focused_professional_practice_evaluation,transactional_data,Identifies the quality or regulatory program under which this peer review was conducted. acr_radpeer = ACR RADPEER program; internal_qa = internal departmental QA; mips = MIPS quality measure; vbp = Value-Based Purchasing; tjc_required = TJC-mandated review; focused_professional_practice_evaluation = FPPE for credentialing. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: acr_radpeer|internal_qa|mips|vbp|tjc_required|focused_professional_practice_evaluation — promote to reference product],
radiology,quality_operations,radiology_peer_review,review_status,review_status,Peer Review Status,STRING,,,,pending|in_progress|completed|cancelled|escalated,transactional_data,Current workflow lifecycle status of the peer review event. pending = assigned but not yet started; in_progress = reviewer has opened the case; completed = review scoring and disposition finalized; cancelled = review voided; escalated = referred to department chair or quality committee.,
radiology,quality_operations,radiology_peer_review,review_type,review_type,Peer Review Type,STRING,,,,random|targeted|discrepancy|prospective|retrospective|focused,transactional_data,"Classification of the peer review event indicating how the case was selected for review. random = randomly selected for routine QA; targeted = selected due to specific criteria (modality, subspecialty); discrepancy = triggered by a known or suspected interpretation discrepancy; prospective = review before report finalization; retrospective = review after report finalization; focused = directed review for performance improvement. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: random|targeted|discrepancy|prospective|retrospective|focused — promote to reference product]",
radiology,quality_operations,radiology_peer_review,reviewer_comments,reviewer_comments,Reviewer Comments,STRING,,,"dbx_confidential,pii_phi,pii_pii,pii_sensitive",,transactional_data,"Free-text comments entered by the reviewing radiologist providing additional context, clinical reasoning, or recommendations beyond the structured discrepancy description. Protected under peer review privilege statutes in most jurisdictions.",
radiology,quality_operations,radiology_peer_review,reviewer_radiologist_npi,reviewer_radiologist_npi,Reviewer Radiologist National Provider Identifier (NPI),STRING,,,"pii_phi,pii_pii,pii_sensitive",^[0-9]{10}$,transactional_data,The 10-digit National Provider Identifier (NPI) of the radiologist who performed the peer review. Must be a credentialed radiologist distinct from the original interpreter per ACR RADPEER blinding requirements.,
radiology,quality_operations,radiology_peer_review,source_system,source_system,Source System,STRING,,,,epic_radiant|cerner_radnet|meditech|manual_entry,transactional_data,"Identifies the operational system of record from which this peer review record was sourced (e.g., epic_radiant, cerner_radnet, meditech, manual_entry). Supports data lineage, ETL reconciliation, and multi-system integration governance.",
radiology,quality_operations,radiology_peer_review,study_datetime,study_datetime,Imaging Study Date and Time,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,The date and time the imaging study was performed (acquisition datetime from PACS/DICOM metadata). Provides temporal context for the study under review and supports lag-time analytics between study acquisition and peer review.,
radiology,quality_operations,radiology_peer_review,subspecialty,subspecialty,Radiology Subspecialty,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,The radiology subspecialty category of the study under review. Used to ensure subspecialty-matched peer review assignments and to generate subspecialty-stratified quality metrics for ACR accreditation and departmental performance reporting. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: neuroradiology|musculoskeletal|body|breast|cardiovascular|interventional|nuclear|pediatric|emergency — promote to reference product],
radiology,quality_operations,radiology_peer_review,subspecialty_matched_flag,subspecialty_matched_flag,Subspecialty Matched Review Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,Indicates whether the reviewing radiologists subspecialty matches the subspecialty of the imaging study under review. True = subspecialty-matched review; False = cross-subspecialty review. ACR RADPEER recommends subspecialty-matched reviews for complex studies.,
radiology,quality_operations,radiology_peer_review,updated_timestamp,updated_timestamp,Record Updated Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,"The date and time this peer review record was last modified in the data platform. Supports incremental ETL processing, audit trail, and change data capture for the silver layer.",
radiology,quality_operations,transmission,transmission_id,transmission_id,Transmission Identifier,BIGINT,Y,,,,association_data,Unique surrogate primary key for the study transmission record. Identifies a specific transmission event of one study to one trading partner.,
radiology,quality_operations,transmission,employee_id,employee_id,Initiated By User,BIGINT,,workforce.employee.employee_id,"dbx_confidential, dbx_pii",,association_data,"Reference to the employee or system user who initiated the manual transmission request, if applicable. Null for automated transmissions triggered by workflow rules.",
radiology,quality_operations,transmission,radiology_study_id,radiology_study_id,Transmission - Imaging Study Id,BIGINT,,radiology.radiology_study.radiology_study_id,,,association_data,Foreign key linking to the imaging study that was transmitted to the external partner.,
radiology,quality_operations,transmission,trading_partner_id,trading_partner_id,Transmission - Trading Partner Id,BIGINT,,interoperability.trading_partner.trading_partner_id,,,association_data,Foreign key linking to the external trading partner that received the imaging study.,
radiology,quality_operations,transmission,acknowledgment_timestamp,acknowledgment_timestamp,Acknowledgment Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,association_data,Date and time when the trading partner acknowledged successful receipt of the imaging study. Used to calculate transmission latency and confirm end-to-end delivery.,
radiology,quality_operations,transmission,created_timestamp,created_timestamp,Created Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,association_data,Date and time this transmission record was first created in the source system. Supports audit trails and data lineage tracking.,
radiology,quality_operations,transmission,error_message,error_message,Error Message,STRING,,,,,association_data,Detailed error message or rejection reason returned by the trading partner or interface engine when transmission fails. Supports operational troubleshooting and root cause analysis.,
radiology,quality_operations,transmission,purpose,purpose,Transmission Purpose,STRING,,,,,association_data,Business reason or clinical purpose for transmitting the imaging study to this specific trading partner. Supports audit trails and compliance with data sharing agreement terms.,
radiology,quality_operations,transmission,retry_count,retry_count,Retry Count,INT,,,,,association_data,Number of retry attempts made to transmit the study to the trading partner after initial transmission failures. Supports operational troubleshooting and partner reliability assessment.,
radiology,quality_operations,transmission,size_mb,size_mb,Transmission Size,"DECIMAL(12,3)",,,,,association_data,"Total size of the transmitted imaging study data in megabytes. Used for bandwidth monitoring, cost allocation, and transmission performance analysis.",
radiology,quality_operations,transmission,sla_met_flag,sla_met_flag,SLA Met Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,association_data,Indicates whether the transmission met the service level agreement (SLA) time commitment defined in the data sharing agreement with the trading partner. Used for partner performance reporting and contract compliance.,
radiology,quality_operations,transmission,transmission_method,transmission_method,Transmission Method,STRING,,,,,association_data,Technical protocol or method used to transmit the imaging study to the trading partner. Indicates the interoperability standard and transport mechanism employed for this specific transmission.,
radiology,quality_operations,transmission,transmission_status,transmission_status,Transmission Status,STRING,,,,,association_data,"Current status of the transmission workflow. Tracks whether the study was successfully delivered, is in transit, failed, or was acknowledged/rejected by the receiving partner. Drives operational monitoring and retry logic.",
radiology,quality_operations,transmission,transmission_timestamp,transmission_timestamp,Transmission Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,association_data,"Date and time when the imaging study was transmitted to the trading partner. Marks the initiation of the outbound transfer via DICOM C-STORE, XDS-I, or FHIR ImagingStudy exchange.",
radiology,quality_operations,transmission,updated_timestamp,updated_timestamp,Updated Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,association_data,"Date and time this transmission record was most recently modified in the source system. Tracks status updates, acknowledgment receipt, and retry attempts.",
radiology,study_acquisition,contrast_admin,contrast_admin_id,contrast_admin_id,Contrast Admin Identifier,BIGINT,Y,,,,transactional_data,Primary key for contrast_admin,
radiology,study_acquisition,contrast_admin,administering_clinician_id,administering_clinician_id,Administering Clinician ID,BIGINT,,provider.clinician.clinician_id,,,transactional_data,"Reference to the clinician (nurse, radiologic technologist, or radiologist) who administered the contrast agent. Used for accountability and adverse event tracking.",
radiology,study_acquisition,contrast_admin,clinical_order_id,clinical_order_id,Clinical Order Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,order.clinical_order.clinical_order_id,,,transactional_data,Foreign key linking to order.clinical_order. Business justification: Contrast administration must link to clinical orders for medication reconciliation workflows. Clinical decision support for contrast allergy screening requires full order context including patient all,
radiology,study_acquisition,contrast_admin,contrast_material_master_id,contrast_material_master_id,Contrast Material Master Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,supply.material_master.material_master_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to supply.material_master. Business justification: Contrast administration records must link to material master for non-pharmacy contrast agents, enabling lot tracking, expiration management, and FDA recall response. Critical for patient safety when c",
radiology,study_acquisition,contrast_admin,demographics_id,demographics_id,Patient ID,BIGINT,,patient.demographics.demographics_id,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_identifier",,transactional_data,Reference to the patient who received the contrast agent. Links to the Master Patient Index (MPI) record. Protected Health Information (PHI) under HIPAA.,
radiology,study_acquisition,contrast_admin,drug_master_id,drug_master_id,Drug Master Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,pharmacy.drug_master.drug_master_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to pharmacy.drug_master. Business justification: Contrast agents are medications managed in pharmacy formulary. Currently has agent_name and ndc_code as text. FK to drug_master normalizes contrast agent data, enables allergy checking, formulary mana",
radiology,study_acquisition,contrast_admin,equipment_asset_id,equipment_asset_id,Power Injector Device ID,BIGINT,,facility.equipment_asset.equipment_asset_id,,,transactional_data,"The asset or serial identifier of the power injector device used for contrast administration. Supports medical device tracking, maintenance scheduling, and adverse event investigation.",
radiology,study_acquisition,contrast_admin,imaging_order_id,imaging_order_id,Imaging Order ID,BIGINT,,radiology.imaging_order.imaging_order_id,,,transactional_data,Reference to the parent imaging order that triggered this contrast administration event. Links to the radiology order in Epic Radiant or Cerner RadNet.,
radiology,study_acquisition,contrast_admin,laboratory_test_result_id,laboratory_test_result_id,Egfr Lab Result Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,laboratory.laboratory_test_result.laboratory_test_result_id,,,transactional_data,Foreign key linking to laboratory.test_result. Business justification: Contrast administration protocols mandate recent eGFR/creatinine results to assess contrast-induced nephropathy risk. ACR guidelines require documented renal function within specific timeframes. Direc,
radiology,study_acquisition,contrast_admin,ndc_drug_id,ndc_drug_id,Ndc Drug Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,reference.ndc_drug.ndc_drug_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to reference.ndc_drug. Business justification: Contrast agents are pharmaceutical products identified by NDC for medication administration records, adverse event tracking, inventory management, and pharmacy billing. Essential for drug safety surve",
radiology,study_acquisition,contrast_admin,osha_exposure_incident_id,osha_exposure_incident_id,Osha Exposure Incident Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,compliance.osha_exposure_incident.osha_exposure_incident_id,,,transactional_data,Foreign key linking to compliance.osha_exposure_incident. Business justification: Contrast extravasation or allergic reactions involving employee exposure are OSHA-recordable incidents. Safety office tracks which contrast administrations resulted in employee injuries or exposures r,
radiology,study_acquisition,contrast_admin,radiology_study_id,radiology_study_id,Imaging Study ID,BIGINT,,radiology.radiology_study.radiology_study_id,,,transactional_data,Reference to the imaging study (DICOM study) with which this contrast administration is associated. Supports PACS integration and study-level traceability.,
radiology,study_acquisition,contrast_admin,subject_enrollment_id,subject_enrollment_id,Subject Enrollment Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,research.subject_enrollment.subject_enrollment_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to research.subject_enrollment. Business justification: Contrast administration to research subjects requires tracking for adverse event monitoring, safety reporting, and protocol compliance. Contrast reactions are reportable adverse events. Linkage enable",
radiology,study_acquisition,contrast_admin,treatment_consent_id,treatment_consent_id,Treatment Consent Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,consent.treatment_consent.treatment_consent_id,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii",,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to consent.treatment_consent. Business justification: Contrast agent administration requires specific informed consent due to allergy/anaphylaxis risks, renal function considerations, and potential adverse reactions. Standard of care requirement. Links c",
radiology,study_acquisition,contrast_admin,visit_id,visit_id,Encounter ID,BIGINT,,encounter.visit.visit_id,,,transactional_data,Reference to the clinical encounter (visit) during which the contrast was administered. Supports revenue cycle and clinical documentation linkage.,
radiology,study_acquisition,contrast_admin,accession_number,accession_number,Radiology Accession Number,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,The Radiology Information System (RIS) accession number assigned to the imaging order. Serves as the primary business identifier linking the contrast event to the RIS workflow in Epic Radiant and Cerner RadNet.,
radiology,study_acquisition,contrast_admin,administering_clinician_npi,administering_clinician_npi,Administering Clinician National Provider Identifier (NPI),STRING,,,,^d{10}$,transactional_data,"The 10-digit National Provider Identifier (NPI) of the clinician who administered the contrast agent. Required for regulatory reporting, billing, and provider accountability tracking.",
radiology,study_acquisition,contrast_admin,administration_datetime,administration_datetime,Contrast Administration Date and Time,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,"The precise date and time at which the contrast agent was administered to the patient. This is the principal real-world event timestamp for this transaction, distinct from record audit timestamps.",
radiology,study_acquisition,contrast_admin,administration_status,administration_status,Contrast Administration Status,STRING,,,,completed|in-progress|not-done|on-hold|stopped|entered-in-error,transactional_data,"Current lifecycle status of the contrast administration event, aligned with HL7 FHIR MedicationAdministration status codes. not-done indicates contrast was withheld after screening.",
radiology,study_acquisition,contrast_admin,adverse_reaction_datetime,adverse_reaction_datetime,Adverse Reaction Date and Time,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,The date and time at which the adverse reaction was first observed following contrast administration. Used to calculate time-to-reaction interval for safety analytics.,
radiology,study_acquisition,contrast_admin,adverse_reaction_description,adverse_reaction_description,Adverse Reaction Description,STRING,,,"dbx_pii_health,dbx_restricted,pii_phi,pii_pii,pii_sensitive",,transactional_data,"Detailed clinical description of the adverse reaction signs and symptoms observed following contrast administration (e.g., urticaria on trunk and arms, resolved with diphenhydramine). Required for FDA MedWatch and internal safety reporting.",
radiology,study_acquisition,contrast_admin,adverse_reaction_occurred,adverse_reaction_occurred,Adverse Reaction Occurred Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,"Indicates whether the patient experienced an adverse reaction following contrast administration (True = reaction occurred, False = no reaction). Triggers mandatory documentation and reporting workflows.",
radiology,study_acquisition,contrast_admin,adverse_reaction_severity,adverse_reaction_severity,Adverse Reaction Severity,STRING,,,"dbx_pii_health,dbx_restricted,pii_phi,pii_pii,pii_sensitive",mild|moderate|severe|life-threatening,transactional_data,"Severity classification of the adverse reaction experienced by the patient following contrast administration, per ACR grading criteria. Drives escalation protocols and mandatory reporting thresholds.",
radiology,study_acquisition,contrast_admin,adverse_reaction_treatment,adverse_reaction_treatment,Adverse Reaction Treatment,STRING,,,"dbx_pii_health,dbx_restricted,pii_phi,pii_pii,pii_sensitive",,transactional_data,"Description of the clinical interventions performed to treat the adverse contrast reaction (e.g., epinephrine 0.3mg IM, oxygen 4L/min via nasal cannula, IV fluid bolus). Supports quality review and safety reporting.",
radiology,study_acquisition,contrast_admin,agent_class,agent_class,Contrast Agent Class,STRING,,,,iodinated|gadolinium-based|barium|microbubble|manganese-based|iron-based,transactional_data,"Classification of the contrast agent by chemical class. Drives safety screening protocols (e.g., gadolinium retention monitoring, iodine allergy screening) and ACR guideline compliance.",
radiology,study_acquisition,contrast_admin,agent_osmolality_type,agent_osmolality_type,Contrast Agent Osmolality Type,STRING,,,,low-osmolality|iso-osmolality|high-osmolality,transactional_data,"Osmolality classification of the iodinated contrast agent (low, iso, or high osmolality). Relevant for patient safety risk stratification, particularly in patients with renal impairment.",
radiology,study_acquisition,contrast_admin,body_region,body_region,Imaging Body Region,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"The anatomical body region being imaged (e.g., abdomen/pelvis, brain, chest, spine). Used for contrast protocol selection and population health analytics.",
radiology,study_acquisition,contrast_admin,catheter_gauge,catheter_gauge,Intravenous Catheter Gauge,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"The gauge size of the intravenous catheter used for contrast injection (e.g., 18G, 20G, 22G). Relevant for power injector safety limits and extravasation risk assessment.",
radiology,study_acquisition,contrast_admin,concentration_mg_per_ml,concentration_mg_per_ml,Contrast Agent Concentration (mg/mL),"DECIMAL(8,3)",,,,,transactional_data,"The concentration of the contrast agent in the administered preparation, expressed in milligrams per milliliter (mg/mL). Used to verify dose calculations and product selection.",
radiology,study_acquisition,contrast_admin,consent_record_created_timestamp,consent_record_created_timestamp,Record Created Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,The date and time when this contrast administration record was first created in the source system or ingested into the lakehouse Silver layer. Supports audit trail and data lineage requirements.,
radiology,study_acquisition,contrast_admin,consent_record_updated_timestamp,consent_record_updated_timestamp,Record Updated Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,The date and time when this contrast administration record was last modified in the source system or updated in the lakehouse Silver layer. Supports change tracking and audit compliance.,
radiology,study_acquisition,contrast_admin,contrast_allergy_screening_result,contrast_allergy_screening_result,Contrast Allergy Screening Result,STRING,,,"dbx_pii_health,dbx_restricted,pii_phi,pii_pii,pii_sensitive",no-allergy|prior-reaction|allergy-confirmed|screening-not-done|contraindicated,transactional_data,"The result of the pre-administration contrast allergy screening assessment. Captures whether the patient has a documented prior contrast reaction, confirmed allergy, or no known allergy. Drives pre-medication decision.",
radiology,study_acquisition,contrast_admin,contrast_protocol_name,contrast_protocol_name,Contrast Protocol Name,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"The name of the institutional contrast administration protocol followed (e.g., CT Abdomen Pelvis with IV Contrast — Standard Adult). Supports protocol compliance auditing and quality improvement.",
radiology,study_acquisition,contrast_admin,dose_amount_mg,dose_amount_mg,Contrast Dose Amount (mg),"DECIMAL(10,3)",,,,,transactional_data,"The total mass of contrast agent administered, measured in milligrams (mg). Supports weight-based dosing verification and cumulative gadolinium/iodine exposure tracking.",
radiology,study_acquisition,contrast_admin,dose_volume_ml,dose_volume_ml,Contrast Dose Volume (mL),"DECIMAL(8,2)",,,,,transactional_data,"The total volume of contrast agent administered, measured in milliliters (mL). Used for dose tracking, pharmacy reconciliation, and radiation/contrast safety monitoring.",
radiology,study_acquisition,contrast_admin,extravasation_occurred,extravasation_occurred,Contrast Extravasation Occurred Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,"Indicates whether contrast agent extravasation (leakage into surrounding tissue) occurred during injection (True = extravasation, False = no extravasation). Triggers wound care and incident reporting protocols.",
radiology,study_acquisition,contrast_admin,extravasation_volume_ml,extravasation_volume_ml,Extravasation Volume (mL),"DECIMAL(6,2)",,,,,transactional_data,"Estimated volume of contrast agent that extravasated into surrounding tissue, in milliliters (mL). Used to guide clinical management and severity classification of the extravasation event.",
radiology,study_acquisition,contrast_admin,informed_consent_obtained,informed_consent_obtained,Informed Consent Obtained Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,"Indicates whether informed consent was obtained from the patient prior to contrast administration (True = consent obtained, False = consent not obtained or waived). Required for regulatory compliance and risk management.",
radiology,study_acquisition,contrast_admin,injection_rate_ml_per_sec,injection_rate_ml_per_sec,Injection Rate (mL/sec),"DECIMAL(6,2)",,,,,transactional_data,"The rate at which the contrast agent was injected, expressed in milliliters per second (mL/sec). Relevant for CT bolus timing, power injector programming, and adverse event analysis.",
radiology,study_acquisition,contrast_admin,injection_site,injection_site,Injection Site,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"The anatomical site of contrast injection (e.g., right antecubital vein, left hand dorsal vein, lumbar intrathecal space). Supports extravasation tracking and adverse event documentation.",
radiology,study_acquisition,contrast_admin,metformin_held,metformin_held,Metformin Held Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,"Indicates whether metformin was held prior to or following contrast administration per ACR guidelines for patients with renal impairment (True = metformin held, False = not held or not applicable).",
radiology,study_acquisition,contrast_admin,modality,modality,Imaging Modality,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"The imaging modality for which the contrast was administered (e.g., CT, MRI, Ultrasound, PET). Determines applicable ACR contrast guidelines and safety protocols. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: CT|MRI|XR|US|PET|NM|FLUORO|ANGIO — 8 candidates stripped; promote to reference product]",
radiology,study_acquisition,contrast_admin,patient_weight_kg,patient_weight_kg,Patient Weight at Administration (kg),"DECIMAL(6,2)",,,"dbx_pii_health,dbx_restricted,pii_phi,pii_pii,pii_sensitive",,transactional_data,The patients body weight in kilograms (kg) recorded at the time of contrast administration. Used for weight-based dose calculation verification and contrast safety risk stratification.,
radiology,study_acquisition,contrast_admin,power_injector_used,power_injector_used,Power Injector Used Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,Indicates whether a power injector device was used to administer the contrast agent (True) or manual hand injection was performed (False). Relevant for injection rate documentation and device safety tracking.,
radiology,study_acquisition,contrast_admin,pregnancy_status,pregnancy_status,Pregnancy Status at Administration,STRING,,,"dbx_pii_health,dbx_restricted,pii_phi,pii_pii,pii_sensitive",not-pregnant|pregnant|unknown|not-applicable,transactional_data,The patients pregnancy status at the time of contrast administration screening. Required for contrast safety risk assessment and informed consent documentation per ACR guidelines.,
radiology,study_acquisition,contrast_admin,premedication_details,premedication_details,Pre-Medication Details,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Free-text or structured description of the pre-medication regimen administered (e.g., Prednisone 50mg PO x3 doses + Diphenhydramine 50mg IV). Supports clinical documentation and pharmacy reconciliation.",
radiology,study_acquisition,contrast_admin,premedication_given,premedication_given,Pre-Medication Given Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,"Indicates whether pre-medication (e.g., corticosteroid prophylaxis) was administered prior to contrast injection to reduce the risk of allergic reaction (True = pre-medicated, False = not pre-medicated).",
radiology,study_acquisition,contrast_admin,prior_contrast_reaction_type,prior_contrast_reaction_type,Prior Contrast Reaction Type,STRING,,,"dbx_pii_health,dbx_restricted,pii_phi,pii_pii,pii_sensitive",,transactional_data,"Description of the type of prior contrast reaction documented in the patients allergy history (e.g., urticaria, bronchospasm, anaphylaxis). Informs pre-medication protocol selection.",
radiology,study_acquisition,contrast_admin,route_of_administration,route_of_administration,Route of Administration,STRING,,,,intravenous|oral|intrathecal|intra-arterial|intraperitoneal|rectal,transactional_data,"The anatomical route by which the contrast agent was delivered to the patient (e.g., intravenous, oral, intrathecal). Critical for adverse reaction risk assessment and clinical documentation.",
radiology,study_acquisition,contrast_admin,source_system,source_system,Source System,STRING,,,,Epic Radiant|Cerner RadNet|MEDITECH|Manual Entry|Interface,transactional_data,"The originating operational system from which this contrast administration record was sourced (e.g., Epic Radiant, Cerner RadNet). Supports data lineage, ETL audit, and multi-system reconciliation.",
radiology,study_acquisition,contrast_admin,source_system_record_code,source_system_record_code,Source System Record ID,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"The native record identifier from the originating operational system (e.g., Epic Radiant administration event ID, Cerner RadNet medication administration ID). Supports ETL traceability and cross-system reconciliation.",
radiology,study_acquisition,contrast_admin,thyroid_disease_flag,thyroid_disease_flag,Thyroid Disease Flag,BOOLEAN,,,"dbx_pii_health,dbx_restricted,pii_phi,pii_pii,pii_sensitive",,transactional_data,"Indicates whether the patient has a documented thyroid condition (e.g., hyperthyroidism, thyroid cancer) that may be relevant to iodinated contrast administration safety screening.",
radiology,study_acquisition,dicom_series,dicom_series_id,dicom_series_id,Digital Imaging and Communications in Medicine (DICOM) Series Identifier,BIGINT,Y,,,,master_data,Unique identifier for the DICOM series record within the lakehouse. Primary key for this table.,
radiology,study_acquisition,dicom_series,employee_id,employee_id,Performing Technologist Employee Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,workforce.employee.employee_id,"dbx_confidential, dbx_pii",,master_data,"Foreign key linking to workforce.employee. Business justification: Series-level technologist tracking needed for quality control, competency assessment, and protocol compliance. Study-level employee_id insufficient for multi-series studies with different operators pe",
radiology,study_acquisition,dicom_series,imaging_protocol_id,imaging_protocol_id,Imaging Protocol Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,radiology.protocol.protocol_id,,,master_data,Foreign key linking to radiology.protocol. Business justification: dicom_series currently has protocol_name: STRING (free-text field). Each DICOM series is acquired using a specific imaging protocol. Adding imaging_protocol_id FK normalizes this relationship to the p,
radiology,study_acquisition,dicom_series,radiology_study_id,radiology_study_id,Imaging Study Identifier,BIGINT,,radiology.radiology_study.radiology_study_id,,,master_data,Foreign key reference to the parent imaging study that contains this series. Links to the imaging_study product.,
radiology,study_acquisition,dicom_series,accession_number,accession_number,Radiology Accession Number,STRING,,,,,master_data,Unique identifier assigned by the RIS to the imaging order or examination. Links DICOM images to radiology orders and reports.,
radiology,study_acquisition,dicom_series,body_part_examined,body_part_examined,Body Part Examined,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Anatomical region or body part that was imaged in this series (e.g., CHEST, HEAD, ABDOMEN). May use SNOMED CT codes or free text.",
radiology,study_acquisition,dicom_series,contrast_bolus_agent,contrast_bolus_agent,Contrast Bolus Agent,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Name or description of the contrast agent administered for this series (e.g., Iohexol 300mg/mL, Gadolinium). Null if no contrast was used.",
radiology,study_acquisition,dicom_series,contrast_bolus_route,contrast_bolus_route,Contrast Bolus Administration Route,STRING,,,,IV|ORAL|RECTAL|INTRA_ARTERIAL|INTRATHECAL,master_data,"Route by which contrast agent was administered (e.g., intravenous, oral). Null if no contrast was used.",
radiology,study_acquisition,dicom_series,contrast_bolus_volume_ml,contrast_bolus_volume_ml,Contrast Bolus Volume in Milliliters (mL),"DECIMAL(10,2)",,,,,master_data,Total volume of contrast agent administered in milliliters. Null if no contrast was used or volume not recorded.,
radiology,study_acquisition,dicom_series,cpt_code,cpt_code,Current Procedural Terminology (CPT) Code,STRING,,,,^[0-9]{5}$,master_data,Five-digit CPT code representing the billable radiology procedure performed for this series. Used for revenue cycle management and claims processing.,
radiology,study_acquisition,dicom_series,created_timestamp,created_timestamp,Record Created Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,master_data,Timestamp when this series record was first created in the lakehouse. Audit trail for data lineage.,
radiology,study_acquisition,dicom_series,ctdi_vol_mgy,ctdi_vol_mgy,Computed Tomography (CT) Dose Index Volume in Milligray (mGy),"DECIMAL(12,4)",,,,,master_data,"CT Dose Index Volume, a standardized measure of radiation dose for CT examinations. Null for non-CT modalities.",
radiology,study_acquisition,dicom_series,dlp_mgy_cm,dlp_mgy_cm,Dose Length Product in Milligray-Centimeters (mGy·cm),"DECIMAL(12,4)",,,,,master_data,"Dose Length Product, representing the integrated radiation dose over the scan length for CT examinations. Null for non-CT modalities.",
radiology,study_acquisition,dicom_series,exposure_ma,exposure_ma,X-Ray Tube Current in Milliamperes (mA),"DECIMAL(10,2)",,,,,master_data,X-ray tube current in milliamperes during image acquisition. Used for radiation dose calculation. Null for non-radiation modalities.,
radiology,study_acquisition,dicom_series,exposure_time_ms,exposure_time_ms,Exposure Time in Milliseconds (ms),"DECIMAL(10,2)",,,,,master_data,Duration of X-ray exposure in milliseconds. Used for radiation dose calculation. Null for non-radiation modalities.,
radiology,study_acquisition,dicom_series,image_orientation_patient,image_orientation_patient,Image Orientation Patient,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Direction cosines of the first row and first column with respect to the patient coordinate system. Six-value array stored as string (e.g., 1␀␀␀1␀). Essential for 3D spatial registration.",
radiology,study_acquisition,dicom_series,kvp,kvp,Kilovoltage Peak (kVp),"DECIMAL(10,2)",,,,,master_data,Peak kilovoltage output of the X-ray generator used for CT or radiography acquisition. Null for non-radiation modalities.,
radiology,study_acquisition,dicom_series,laterality,laterality,Anatomical Laterality,STRING,,,,L|R|B|U,master_data,"Laterality of the body part examined: L (Left), R (Right), B (Bilateral), U (Unpaired/midline). Null if not applicable.",
radiology,study_acquisition,dicom_series,manufacturer,manufacturer,Equipment Manufacturer,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Manufacturer of the imaging equipment used to acquire this series (e.g., GE Healthcare, Siemens Healthineers, Philips Medical Systems).",
radiology,study_acquisition,dicom_series,manufacturer_model_name,manufacturer_model_name,Equipment Manufacturer Model Name,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Model name of the imaging equipment (e.g., Discovery CT750 HD, MAGNETOM Skyra, Ingenuity CT).",
radiology,study_acquisition,dicom_series,modality,modality,Imaging Modality,STRING,,,,,master_data,Type of imaging equipment or acquisition method used to create this series. Standard DICOM modality codes. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: CT|MR|XA|RF|US|MG|DX|CR|NM|PT|OT — 11 candidates stripped; promote to reference product],
radiology,study_acquisition,dicom_series,number_of_series_related_instances,number_of_series_related_instances,Number of Series Related Instances,INT,,,,,master_data,Total count of DICOM image instances (individual images or frames) contained within this series. Used for completeness validation and PACS retrieval.,
radiology,study_acquisition,dicom_series,pacs_archive_status,pacs_archive_status,Picture Archiving and Communication System (PACS) Archive Status,STRING,,,,online|nearline|offline|archived|pending_archive,master_data,"Current storage tier or availability status of the series within the PACS archive hierarchy (online cache, nearline storage, offline tape, etc.).",
radiology,study_acquisition,dicom_series,pacs_storage_path,pacs_storage_path,Picture Archiving and Communication System (PACS) Storage Path,STRING,,,"dbx_confidential,pii_phi,pii_pii,pii_sensitive",,master_data,File system path or object storage location where the DICOM series images are stored in the PACS archive. Used for image retrieval and system integration.,
radiology,study_acquisition,dicom_series,patient_position,patient_position,Patient Position,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Patient position during image acquisition using DICOM standard codes: HFS (Head First Supine), HFP (Head First Prone), FFS (Feet First Supine), etc. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: HFS|HFP|FFS|FFP|HFDR|HFDL|FFDR|FFDL — 8 candidates stripped; promote to reference product]",
radiology,study_acquisition,dicom_series,performing_physician_name,performing_physician_name,Performing Physician Name,STRING,,,"dbx_confidential,pii_phi,pii_pii,pii_sensitive",,master_data,Name of the physician or technologist who performed or supervised the image acquisition for this series.,
radiology,study_acquisition,dicom_series,pixel_spacing_mm,pixel_spacing_mm,Pixel Spacing in Millimeters (mm),STRING,,,,^[0-9]+.[0-9]+\[0-9]+.[0-9]+$,master_data,"Physical distance between pixel centers in millimeters, formatted as row_spacingcolumn_spacing (e.g., 0.625␀.625). Used for accurate measurement and calibration.",
radiology,study_acquisition,dicom_series,procedure_code_modifier,procedure_code_modifier,Procedure Code Modifier,STRING,,,,^[0-9A-Z]{2}$,master_data,"Two-character CPT or HCPCS modifier providing additional information about the procedure (e.g., laterality, professional/technical component). Null if no modifier applies.",
radiology,study_acquisition,dicom_series,quality_control_comments,quality_control_comments,Quality Control Comments,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Free-text comments from quality control review, documenting any issues, artifacts, or technical concerns identified during QC assessment.",
radiology,study_acquisition,dicom_series,quality_control_status,quality_control_status,Quality Control Status,STRING,,,,pending|passed|failed|not_required,master_data,Result of quality control review for this series. Indicates whether the series meets institutional quality standards for diagnostic interpretation.,
radiology,study_acquisition,dicom_series,radiation_dose_mgy,radiation_dose_mgy,Radiation Dose in Milligray (mGy),"DECIMAL(12,4)",,,,,master_data,Estimated or measured radiation dose delivered to the patient during this series in milligray. Critical for dose tracking and regulatory reporting. Null for non-radiation modalities.,
radiology,study_acquisition,dicom_series,referring_physician_npi,referring_physician_npi,Referring Physician National Provider Identifier (NPI),STRING,,,"pii_phi,pii_pii,pii_sensitive",^[0-9]{10}$,master_data,Ten-digit NPI of the referring physician. Used for provider attribution and claims processing.,
radiology,study_acquisition,dicom_series,requesting_physician_name,requesting_physician_name,Requesting Physician Name,STRING,,,"dbx_confidential,pii_phi,pii_pii,pii_sensitive",,master_data,Name of the physician who ordered the imaging study. Used for result routing and clinical communication.,
radiology,study_acquisition,dicom_series,series_completeness_flag,series_completeness_flag,Series Completeness Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,"Indicates whether all expected instances for this series have been received and stored in PACS. True if complete, False if incomplete or pending.",
radiology,study_acquisition,dicom_series,series_date,series_date,Series Acquisition Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,Date when the series was acquired or started. Represents the calendar day of image capture.,
radiology,study_acquisition,dicom_series,series_description,series_description,Series Description,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Human-readable description of the series content, typically including anatomical region, imaging protocol, and acquisition parameters (e.g., Chest CT with Contrast Axial 2.5mm).",
radiology,study_acquisition,dicom_series,series_instance_uid,series_instance_uid,Series Instance Unique Identifier (UID),STRING,,,"pii_phi,pii_pii,pii_sensitive",^[0-9.]+$,master_data,Globally unique DICOM Series Instance UID conforming to ISO 8824 UID format. This is the business identifier for the series across all systems and institutions.,
radiology,study_acquisition,dicom_series,series_number,series_number,Series Number,INT,,,,,master_data,Sequential number assigned to this series within the parent study. Used for ordering and display purposes in PACS and radiology workstations.,
radiology,study_acquisition,dicom_series,series_status,series_status,Series Lifecycle Status,STRING,,,,acquired|archived|quality_review|approved|rejected|deleted,master_data,Current lifecycle status of the series within the PACS and RIS workflow. Tracks progression from acquisition through archival and quality assurance.,
radiology,study_acquisition,dicom_series,series_time,series_time,Series Acquisition Time,TIMESTAMP,,,,,master_data,"Time when the series was acquired or started, in DICOM TM format (HHMMSS.FFFFFF). Combined with series_date provides precise acquisition timestamp.",
radiology,study_acquisition,dicom_series,slice_thickness_mm,slice_thickness_mm,Slice Thickness in Millimeters (mm),"DECIMAL(10,4)",,,,,master_data,Nominal thickness of each image slice in millimeters. Critical for 3D reconstruction and volumetric analysis.,
radiology,study_acquisition,dicom_series,software_version,software_version,Equipment Software Version,STRING,,,,,master_data,Software version of the imaging equipment at the time of acquisition. Important for image quality assessment and protocol standardization.,
radiology,study_acquisition,dicom_series,station_name,station_name,Acquisition Station Name,STRING,,,,,master_data,"User-defined name or identifier of the imaging station or device where the series was acquired (e.g., CT1_ER, MRI2_MAIN).",
radiology,study_acquisition,dicom_series,updated_timestamp,updated_timestamp,Record Updated Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,master_data,Timestamp when this series record was last modified in the lakehouse. Audit trail for data lineage and change tracking.,
radiology,study_acquisition,dose_record,dose_record_id,dose_record_id,Dose Record Identifier,BIGINT,Y,,,,transactional_data,Primary key for dose_record,
radiology,study_acquisition,dose_record,care_site_id,care_site_id,Facility ID,BIGINT,,facility.care_site.care_site_id,,,transactional_data,"Reference to the facility or imaging center where the study was performed. Supports facility-level dose benchmarking, ACR DIR site-level reporting, and Joint Commission accreditation tracking.",
radiology,study_acquisition,dose_record,clinical_order_id,clinical_order_id,Clinical Order Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,order.clinical_order.clinical_order_id,,,transactional_data,Foreign key linking to order.clinical_order. Business justification: Radiation dose records must be traceable to clinical orders for dose optimization programs and regulatory reporting to dose index registries. Quality assurance workflows validate appropriate imaging u,
radiology,study_acquisition,dose_record,employee_id,employee_id,Reviewing Physicist Employee Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,workforce.employee.employee_id,"dbx_confidential, dbx_pii",,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to workforce.employee. Business justification: Radiation dose records require medical physicist review for quality assurance and regulatory compliance (ACR, state regulations). Physicists may not have clinician_id if non-provider staff.",
radiology,study_acquisition,dose_record,imaging_order_id,imaging_order_id,Imaging Order ID,BIGINT,,radiology.imaging_order.imaging_order_id,,,transactional_data,Reference to the radiology order (CPOE) that initiated the imaging study. Links dose data to the clinical order for appropriateness review and order management workflows in Epic Radiant or Cerner RadNet.,
radiology,study_acquisition,dose_record,imaging_protocol_id,imaging_protocol_id,Imaging Protocol Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,radiology.protocol.protocol_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to radiology.protocol. Business justification: dose_record currently has imaging_protocol_name: STRING (free-text field). Radiation dose records are tied to the acquisition protocol used, which determines expected dose ranges and DRL comparisons. ",
radiology,study_acquisition,dose_record,message_log_id,message_log_id,Message Log Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,interoperability.message_log.message_log_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to interoperability.message_log. Business justification: Radiation dose structured reports (RDSR) are transmitted via HL7 ORU or DICOM to dose registries (ACR DIR, state registries) for regulatory reporting and dose optimization programs. Message_log tracks",
radiology,study_acquisition,dose_record,mpi_record_id,mpi_record_id,Patient ID,BIGINT,,patient.mpi_record.mpi_record_id,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_identifier",,transactional_data,Reference to the patient who received the radiation exposure. Links to the Master Patient Index (MPI) record for cumulative dose tracking and patient-level radiation safety monitoring per ALARA principle.,
radiology,study_acquisition,dose_record,osha_safety_program_id,osha_safety_program_id,Osha Safety Program Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,compliance.osha_safety_program.osha_safety_program_id,,,transactional_data,Foreign key linking to compliance.osha_safety_program. Business justification: Dose records support OSHA radiation safety programs by documenting employee and patient exposure levels. Safety programs monitor cumulative dose data to ensure compliance with occupational exposure li,
radiology,study_acquisition,dose_record,primary_dose_clinician_id,primary_dose_clinician_id,Ordering Provider ID,BIGINT,,provider.clinician.clinician_id,,,transactional_data,"Reference to the clinician who ordered the imaging study. Used for utilization management, appropriateness criteria reporting, and CMS quality program compliance.",
radiology,study_acquisition,dose_record,procedure_cpt_code_id,procedure_cpt_code_id,Procedure Cpt Code Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,reference.cpt_code.cpt_code_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to reference.cpt_code. Business justification: Radiation dose records link to CPT codes for dose-by-procedure benchmarking, ACR Dose Index Registry submissions, and radiation safety quality measures. Supports dose optimization program reporting.",
radiology,study_acquisition,dose_record,public_health_report_id,public_health_report_id,Public Health Report Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,interoperability.public_health_report.public_health_report_id,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii",,transactional_data,Foreign key linking to interoperability.public_health_report. Business justification: Radiation dose records are submitted to state dose registries and ACR Dose Index Registry for public health surveillance and dose optimization programs. Links dose record to its public health submissi,
radiology,study_acquisition,dose_record,research_study_id,research_study_id,Research Study Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,research.research_study.research_study_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to research.research_study. Business justification: Radiation dose tracking for research subjects is IRB-mandated for protocols involving imaging. Cumulative dose monitoring, safety reporting to IRBs and sponsors, and protocol-specified dose limits req",
radiology,study_acquisition,dose_record,visit_id,visit_id,Encounter ID,BIGINT,,encounter.visit.visit_id,,,transactional_data,Reference to the clinical encounter (visit) during which the imaging study and radiation exposure occurred. Supports revenue cycle linkage and clinical context for dose reporting.,
radiology,study_acquisition,dose_record,accession_number,accession_number,Accession Number,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,Radiology Information System (RIS) accession number uniquely identifying the imaging order/study to which this dose record belongs. Primary business identifier linking dose data to the imaging study in Epic Radiant or Cerner RadNet.,
radiology,study_acquisition,dose_record,body_part_examined,body_part_examined,Body Part Examined,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"DICOM-coded body part or anatomical region examined during the imaging study (e.g., CHEST, ABDOMEN, HEAD, PELVIS). Used for dose benchmarking by anatomy and ACR DIR stratification.",
radiology,study_acquisition,dose_record,contrast_administered,contrast_administered,Contrast Agent Administered Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,"Indicates whether iodinated or gadolinium-based contrast agent was administered during the imaging study. True = contrast used; False = non-contrast study. Relevant for dose context, adverse event tracking, and clinical protocol classification.",
radiology,study_acquisition,dose_record,contrast_agent_type,contrast_agent_type,Contrast Agent Type,STRING,,,,iodinated|gadolinium|barium|none,transactional_data,Type of contrast agent administered during the imaging study. iodinated=CT/X-ray contrast; gadolinium=MRI contrast (tracked for nephrogenic systemic fibrosis risk); barium=GI fluoroscopy; none=no contrast. Used for clinical safety monitoring and protocol classification.,
radiology,study_acquisition,dose_record,created_timestamp,created_timestamp,Record Created Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,"Date and time when this dose record was first created in the source system or ingested into the lakehouse Silver layer. Supports audit trail, data lineage, and regulatory record retention requirements.",
radiology,study_acquisition,dose_record,ctdivol_mgy,ctdivol_mgy,CT Dose Index Volume (CTDIvol) in Milligray (mGy),"DECIMAL(10,4)",,,,,transactional_data,Volume CT Dose Index (CTDIvol) in milligray (mGy) for CT studies. Represents the average radiation dose delivered within the scan volume for a single series or the entire study. Primary CT dose metric for ACR DIR benchmarking and dose alert thresholds per NCRP and FDA guidance.,
radiology,study_acquisition,dose_record,cumulative_dose_msv,cumulative_dose_msv,Cumulative Patient Radiation Dose (mSv),"DECIMAL(12,4)",,,"dbx_pii_health,dbx_restricted,pii_phi,pii_pii,pii_sensitive",,transactional_data,"Running cumulative effective dose in millisieverts (mSv) for this patient across all prior ionizing radiation imaging studies recorded in the system, including the current study. Supports ALARA principle compliance, radiation safety counseling, and identification of high-dose patients for clinical review.",
radiology,study_acquisition,dose_record,dap_gy_cm2,dap_gy_cm2,Dose Area Product (DAP) in Gray-Centimeter Squared (Gy·cm²),"DECIMAL(12,4)",,,,,transactional_data,"Dose Area Product (DAP) in Gy·cm² for fluoroscopy, X-ray angiography, and interventional radiology procedures. Measures total radiation energy delivered to the patient. Primary dose metric for fluoroscopic procedures per IEC 60601-2-43.",
radiology,study_acquisition,dose_record,dlp_mgy_cm,dlp_mgy_cm,Dose Length Product (DLP) in Milligray-Centimeter (mGy·cm),"DECIMAL(10,4)",,,,,transactional_data,Dose Length Product (DLP) in mGy·cm for CT studies. Represents the total radiation energy imparted along the scan length. Used with conversion coefficients to estimate effective dose and is the primary metric for ACR DIR CT dose reporting.,
radiology,study_acquisition,dose_record,dose_alert_flag,dose_alert_flag,Dose Alert Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,"Indicates whether this study triggered a radiation dose alert based on institutional or regulatory thresholds (e.g., CTDIvol > alert level, fluoroscopy time > 30 min, RAK > 3 Gy). True = alert triggered; False = within normal limits. Supports Joint Commission radiation safety event reporting.",
radiology,study_acquisition,dose_record,dose_alert_threshold_type,dose_alert_threshold_type,Dose Alert Threshold Type,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"The specific dose metric that triggered the dose alert, if applicable. Identifies which threshold was exceeded to support targeted clinical review and root cause analysis. not_triggered when dose_alert_flag is False. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: ctdivol|dlp|dap|fluoroscopy_time|rak|effective_dose|not_triggered — 7 candidates stripped; promote to reference product]",
radiology,study_acquisition,dose_record,dose_alert_value,dose_alert_value,Dose Alert Threshold Value,"DECIMAL(12,4)",,,,,transactional_data,"The numeric threshold value that was exceeded to trigger the dose alert, expressed in the unit of the triggering metric (mGy, mGy·cm, Gy·cm², seconds, or mSv). Supports audit trail for dose safety events.",
radiology,study_acquisition,dose_record,dose_record_status,dose_record_status,Dose Record Status,STRING,,,,preliminary|final|amended|corrected|cancelled,transactional_data,Current lifecycle status of the radiation dose record. preliminary = dose data received but not yet reviewed; final = reviewed and confirmed; amended = corrected after finalization; corrected = technical correction applied; cancelled = study voided.,
radiology,study_acquisition,dose_record,dose_registry_submission_status,dose_registry_submission_status,ACR Dose Index Registry (DIR) Submission Status,STRING,,,,pending|submitted|accepted|rejected|not_required,transactional_data,Status of submission of this dose record to the ACR Dose Index Registry (DIR). pending=queued for submission; submitted=transmitted to ACR DIR; accepted=confirmed by ACR DIR; rejected=rejected by ACR DIR (requires correction); not_required=procedure not in DIR scope.,
radiology,study_acquisition,dose_record,dose_registry_submission_timestamp,dose_registry_submission_timestamp,Dose Registry Submission Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,Date and time when this dose record was submitted to the ACR Dose Index Registry (DIR) or other regulatory dose registry. Supports audit trail for regulatory compliance and CMS quality program reporting.,
radiology,study_acquisition,dose_record,drl_comparison_result,drl_comparison_result,Diagnostic Reference Level (DRL) Comparison Result,STRING,,,,below_drl|at_drl|above_drl|not_applicable,transactional_data,Result of comparing the study dose against the applicable national or institutional Diagnostic Reference Level (DRL). below_drl=dose is below the reference level (optimal); at_drl=dose equals reference level; above_drl=dose exceeds reference level (requires review); not_applicable=no DRL defined for this procedure.,
radiology,study_acquisition,dose_record,effective_dose_msv,effective_dose_msv,Effective Dose Estimate in Millisievert (mSv),"DECIMAL(10,4)",,,,,transactional_data,"Estimated effective dose in millisieverts (mSv) representing the stochastic risk-weighted whole-body equivalent dose. Derived from DLP × conversion coefficient (k-factor) for CT, or from DAP for fluoroscopy. Used for patient communication, cumulative dose tracking, and ALARA compliance.",
radiology,study_acquisition,dose_record,entrance_skin_dose_mgy,entrance_skin_dose_mgy,Entrance Skin Dose (ESD) in Milligray (mGy),"DECIMAL(10,4)",,,,,transactional_data,Entrance skin dose (ESD) in milligray (mGy) for radiographic and fluoroscopic procedures. Represents the absorbed dose at the skin entry point. Critical for radiation injury risk assessment and Joint Commission threshold monitoring.,
radiology,study_acquisition,dose_record,fluoroscopy_time_sec,fluoroscopy_time_sec,Fluoroscopy Time in Seconds,"DECIMAL(10,2)",,,,,transactional_data,"Total fluoroscopy beam-on time in seconds for fluoroscopic and interventional procedures. Regulatory threshold monitoring metric; Joint Commission requires tracking and alerting when fluoroscopy time exceeds defined thresholds (e.g., 30 minutes cumulative).",
radiology,study_acquisition,dose_record,kvp,kvp,Peak Kilovoltage (kVp),"DECIMAL(8,2)",,,,,transactional_data,"Peak kilovoltage (kVp) applied to the X-ray tube during the study. Represents the energy of the X-ray beam. Used for dose optimization, protocol review, and physics quality assurance.",
radiology,study_acquisition,dose_record,modality_type,modality_type,Imaging Modality Type,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"DICOM modality code indicating the type of imaging equipment used. CT=Computed Tomography, FL=Fluoroscopy, NM=Nuclear Medicine, DX=Digital Radiography (X-ray), MG=Mammography, XA=X-Ray Angiography, RF=Radiofluoroscopy. Determines applicable dose metrics (CTDIvol/DLP for CT, DAP/fluoroscopy time for fluoroscopy). [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: CT|FL|NM|DX|MG|XA|RF|PT|SPECT — promote to reference product]",
radiology,study_acquisition,dose_record,number_of_exposures,number_of_exposures,Number of Exposures,INT,,,,,transactional_data,Total count of individual X-ray exposures (radiographic frames or pulses) delivered during the study. Used for dose optimization analysis and comparison against diagnostic reference levels (DRLs).,
radiology,study_acquisition,dose_record,patient_age_at_study,patient_age_at_study,Patient Age at Study (Years),INT,,,,,transactional_data,"Patient age in whole years at the time of the imaging study. Used for pediatric dose benchmarking (pediatric patients require lower dose protocols), age-stratified DRL comparisons, and ACR DIR age-group reporting. Derived at time of study to avoid recalculation.",
radiology,study_acquisition,dose_record,patient_size_cm,patient_size_cm,Patient Size (Effective Diameter) in Centimeters (cm),"DECIMAL(6,2)",,,"dbx_pii_health,dbx_restricted,pii_phi,pii_pii,pii_sensitive",,transactional_data,"Patient effective diameter or water-equivalent diameter in centimeters, used for Size-Specific Dose Estimate (SSDE) calculation in CT. Derived from scout/localizer images or patient measurements. Required for AAPM TG-204 SSDE methodology.",
radiology,study_acquisition,dose_record,patient_weight_kg,patient_weight_kg,Patient Weight in Kilograms (kg),"DECIMAL(6,2)",,,"dbx_pii_health,dbx_restricted,pii_phi,pii_pii,pii_sensitive",,transactional_data,"Patient body weight in kilograms at the time of the imaging study. Used for size-specific dose estimate (SSDE) calculations for CT, weight-based protocol selection, and dose normalization for benchmarking.",
radiology,study_acquisition,dose_record,physicist_review_flag,physicist_review_flag,Medical Physicist Review Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,"Indicates whether this dose record has been flagged for or completed a review by a qualified medical physicist. True = physicist review required or completed; False = no physicist review needed. Triggered by dose alerts, unusual protocol deviations, or regulatory requirements.",
radiology,study_acquisition,dose_record,physicist_review_timestamp,physicist_review_timestamp,Medical Physicist Review Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,Date and time when the medical physicist completed the review of this dose record. Null if physicist_review_flag is False or review is pending. Supports compliance audit trail for Joint Commission radiation safety requirements.,
radiology,study_acquisition,dose_record,procedure_description,procedure_description,Procedure Description,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Human-readable description of the imaging procedure performed (e.g., CT Chest with Contrast, Fluoroscopic Guidance for Biopsy). Sourced from the Charge Description Master (CDM) or RIS procedure catalog.",
radiology,study_acquisition,dose_record,rdsr_uid,rdsr_uid,Radiation Dose Structured Report (RDSR) Unique Identifier (UID),STRING,,,"pii_phi,pii_pii,pii_sensitive",,transactional_data,DICOM Radiation Dose Structured Report (RDSR) SOP Instance UID per IEC 61910 standard. Globally unique identifier for the structured dose report generated by the imaging modality. Used for PACS integration and ACR Dose Index Registry (DIR) submission.,
radiology,study_acquisition,dose_record,reference_air_kerma_mgy,reference_air_kerma_mgy,Reference Air Kerma (RAK) in Milligray (mGy),"DECIMAL(10,4)",,,,,transactional_data,Reference Air Kerma (RAK) in mGy for interventional fluoroscopy procedures. Measured at the interventional reference point (IRP) per IEC 60601-2-43. Used for radiation injury risk assessment and regulatory threshold compliance.,
radiology,study_acquisition,dose_record,scanner_manufacturer,scanner_manufacturer,Scanner Manufacturer,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Manufacturer of the imaging equipment used for the study (e.g., Siemens, GE Healthcare, Philips, Canon). Used for equipment-level dose benchmarking, physics QA, and ACR DIR equipment stratification.",
radiology,study_acquisition,dose_record,scanner_model,scanner_model,Scanner Model Name,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Model name of the imaging equipment used (e.g., SOMATOM Force, Revolution CT, Ingenuity Elite). Used for equipment-specific dose performance tracking and physics quality assurance.",
radiology,study_acquisition,dose_record,scanner_station_name,scanner_station_name,Scanner Station Name,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"DICOM station name or AE title of the imaging modality that generated the dose data. Used for equipment-level dose tracking, PACS routing, and physics QA within a multi-scanner facility.",
radiology,study_acquisition,dose_record,source_system,source_system,Source System,STRING,,,,epic_radiant|cerner_radnet|meditech|dose_management_system|other,transactional_data,"Operational system of record from which this dose record was sourced (e.g., Epic Radiant, Cerner RadNet, third-party dose management system). Used for data lineage, ETL audit, and multi-system reconciliation in the lakehouse Silver layer.",
radiology,study_acquisition,dose_record,ssde_mgy,ssde_mgy,Size-Specific Dose Estimate (SSDE) in Milligray (mGy),"DECIMAL(10,4)",,,,,transactional_data,"Size-Specific Dose Estimate (SSDE) in mGy for CT studies, calculated per AAPM TG-204 methodology by applying a size-based conversion factor to CTDIvol. Provides a more accurate patient-specific dose estimate than CTDIvol alone. Used for pediatric dose optimization and ACR DIR advanced reporting.",
radiology,study_acquisition,dose_record,study_date,study_date,Study Date,DATE,,,,,transactional_data,"Calendar date on which the imaging study was performed. Principal business event date for dose record. Used for trending, regulatory reporting, and cumulative dose period calculations.",
radiology,study_acquisition,dose_record,study_instance_uid,study_instance_uid,DICOM Study Instance Unique Identifier (UID),STRING,,,"pii_phi,pii_pii,pii_sensitive",,transactional_data,"tags: pii_phi,pii_pii,pii_sensitive",
radiology,study_acquisition,dose_record,study_timestamp,study_timestamp,Study Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,"Precise date and time the imaging study was performed, including timezone offset. Used for intraday workflow analysis, dose alert timing, and RDSR correlation.",
radiology,study_acquisition,dose_record,tube_current_mas,tube_current_mas,Tube Current-Time Product (mAs),"DECIMAL(10,2)",,,,,transactional_data,X-ray tube current-time product in milliampere-seconds (mAs) for the study. Directly influences radiation dose output. Used for protocol optimization and dose benchmarking.,
radiology,study_acquisition,dose_record,updated_timestamp,updated_timestamp,Record Updated Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,"Date and time when this dose record was last modified in the source system or Silver layer. Used for incremental ETL processing, change data capture, and audit trail maintenance.",
radiology,study_acquisition,modality,modality_id,modality_id,Modality ID,BIGINT,Y,,,,master_data,Unique surrogate identifier for the imaging modality unit within the enterprise data platform. Primary key for the modality master reference entity.,
radiology,study_acquisition,modality,care_site_id,care_site_id,Facility ID,BIGINT,,facility.care_site.care_site_id,,,master_data,"Reference to the enterprise facility (hospital, clinic, imaging center) where this modality unit is physically deployed. Supports multi-site utilization analytics, capacity planning, and regulatory reporting by location.",
radiology,study_acquisition,modality,employee_id,employee_id,Primary Operator Employee Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,workforce.employee.employee_id,"dbx_confidential, dbx_pii",,master_data,"Foreign key linking to workforce.employee. Business justification: Radiology equipment has assigned primary operators/technologists for accountability, competency tracking, and maintenance coordination. Required for quality assurance programs and regulatory complianc",
radiology,study_acquisition,modality,fixed_asset_id,fixed_asset_id,Fixed Asset Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,finance.fixed_asset.fixed_asset_id,,,master_data,"Foreign key linking to finance.fixed_asset. Business justification: Imaging equipment (CT, MRI, X-ray) are capital assets requiring linkage for depreciation calculation, asset lifecycle tracking, maintenance cost capitalization, and capital planning. Modality operatio",
radiology,study_acquisition,modality,interface_channel_id,interface_channel_id,Interface Channel Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,interoperability.interface_channel.interface_channel_id,,,master_data,"Foreign key linking to interoperability.interface_channel. Business justification: DICOM modalities connect to PACS/RIS via specific interface channels for modality worklist (MWL), MPPS, and image transmission. Links modality to its configured channel for troubleshooting connectivit",
radiology,study_acquisition,modality,osha_safety_program_id,osha_safety_program_id,Osha Safety Program Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,compliance.osha_safety_program.osha_safety_program_id,,,master_data,"Foreign key linking to compliance.osha_safety_program. Business justification: Imaging modalities, especially radiation-emitting equipment, are governed by OSHA safety programs. Safety programs define modality-specific protocols for employee protection, calibration, and hazard m",
radiology,study_acquisition,modality,acr_accreditation_expiration_date,acr_accreditation_expiration_date,ACR Accreditation Expiration Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,Date on which the current American College of Radiology (ACR) accreditation for this modality unit expires. Null if not accredited or not applicable. Critical for maintaining Medicare billing eligibility for advanced imaging services.,
radiology,study_acquisition,modality,acr_accreditation_status,acr_accreditation_status,American College of Radiology (ACR) Accreditation Status,STRING,,,,accredited|provisional|denied|expired|not_applicable,master_data,"Current American College of Radiology (ACR) accreditation status for this imaging modality unit. ACR accreditation is required for Medicare reimbursement for advanced imaging services (CT, MRI, PET, nuclear medicine) under CMS policy. Drives billing eligibility and quality reporting.",
radiology,study_acquisition,modality,ae_title,ae_title,DICOM Application Entity (AE) Title,STRING,,,,"^[A-Z0-9_-]{1,16}$",master_data,"DICOM Application Entity (AE) title assigned to this modality unit, used for DICOM network communication, PACS routing, and worklist queries. Must be unique across the enterprise DICOM network. Configured in PACS and RIS for image routing and storage commitment.",
radiology,study_acquisition,modality,bore_diameter_cm,bore_diameter_cm,Gantry Bore Diameter (cm),"DECIMAL(5,2)",,,,,master_data,"Inner diameter of the CT or MRI gantry bore in centimeters (e.g., 70 cm wide-bore MRI, 80 cm CT). Null for non-gantry equipment. Used for patient eligibility screening (claustrophobia, body habitus) and order routing to appropriate equipment.",
radiology,study_acquisition,modality,building_code,building_code,Building Code,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Facility building or wing code where the modality unit is located (e.g., MAIN, NORTH, MOB-A). Supports physical asset management, maintenance routing, and emergency response planning.",
radiology,study_acquisition,modality,contrast_capable,contrast_capable,Contrast Administration Capable Indicator,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,"Indicates whether this modality unit is equipped and approved for contrast-enhanced imaging procedures. Drives protocol assignment, contrast administration workflow routing, and safety checklist requirements in the RIS and EHR order management.",
radiology,study_acquisition,modality,created_timestamp,created_timestamp,Record Created Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,master_data,"Timestamp when this modality unit record was first created in the enterprise data platform. Supports data lineage, audit trail requirements, and HIPAA Security Rule audit controls.",
radiology,study_acquisition,modality,decommission_date,decommission_date,Decommission Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,"Date the imaging modality unit was permanently retired from clinical service. Null for active equipment. Used for asset lifecycle management, capital planning, and historical utilization analysis.",
radiology,study_acquisition,modality,department_name,department_name,Department Name,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Name of the clinical department or imaging section within the facility where this modality unit is assigned (e.g., Radiology, Emergency Radiology, Cardiac Imaging, Breast Imaging Center). Used for departmental cost allocation and operational reporting.",
radiology,study_acquisition,modality,detector_type,detector_type,Imaging Detector Type,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Type of image detector technology used in the modality unit (e.g., Flat Panel, Curved Array, Photon Counting, CCD, Amorphous Silicon, Scintillator). Relevant for image quality benchmarking, protocol optimization, and ACR phantom testing requirements.",
radiology,study_acquisition,modality,dicom_modality_code,dicom_modality_code,DICOM Modality Code,STRING,,,,"^[A-Z]{2,4}$",master_data,"Standardized DICOM modality code as defined in DICOM PS3.3 (e.g., CT, MR, US, DX, PT, NM, MG, RF, XA). Used for PACS routing, DICOM worklist matching, and interoperability with imaging systems. Critical for HL7 and FHIR image exchange.",
radiology,study_acquisition,modality,dose_tracking_enabled,dose_tracking_enabled,Radiation Dose Tracking Enabled Indicator,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,"Indicates whether automated radiation dose tracking and reporting is enabled for this modality unit, feeding the ACR Dose Index Registry (DIR) and enterprise dose management systems. Required for CMS quality reporting and MIPS measures related to radiation safety.",
radiology,study_acquisition,modality,equipment_type,equipment_type,Imaging Equipment Type,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Classification of the imaging modality by technology type, aligned with DICOM modality codes and ACR accreditation categories. Drives order routing rules, protocol assignment, and utilization reporting. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: CT|MRI|X-ray|Ultrasound|PET-CT|PET|Fluoroscopy|Mammography|Nuclear Medicine|DEXA|Angiography — promote to reference product]",
radiology,study_acquisition,modality,facility_service_contract_expiration_date,facility_service_contract_expiration_date,Service Contract Expiration Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,Date on which the current service and maintenance contract for this modality unit expires. Drives contract renewal alerts and procurement planning to ensure continuous coverage and Joint Commission compliance.,
radiology,study_acquisition,modality,facility_service_contract_number,facility_service_contract_number,Service Contract Number,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Identifier for the active service and maintenance contract covering this imaging modality unit. Links to the vendor service agreement in the procurement system. Used for service dispatch, cost tracking, and contract renewal management.",
radiology,study_acquisition,modality,fda_510k_number,fda_510k_number,FDA 510(k) Clearance Number,STRING,,,,^K[0-9]{6}$,master_data,"FDA 510(k) premarket notification clearance number for this imaging device model, confirming substantial equivalence to a predicate device. Supports regulatory compliance documentation and procurement validation.",
radiology,study_acquisition,modality,fda_registration_number,fda_registration_number,FDA Device Registration Number,STRING,,,,^[0-9]{7}$,master_data,U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA) device establishment registration number assigned to this imaging equipment unit under 21 CFR Part 807. Required for regulatory compliance tracking and FDA inspection readiness.,
radiology,study_acquisition,modality,installation_date,installation_date,Installation Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,"Date the imaging modality unit was physically installed and commissioned at the facility. Used to calculate equipment age, depreciation schedules, warranty expiration, and capital replacement planning.",
radiology,study_acquisition,modality,is_mobile,is_mobile,Mobile Equipment Indicator,BOOLEAN,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_phone",,master_data,"Indicates whether this modality unit is a portable or mobile imaging device (True) that can be transported to patient care areas (e.g., portable X-ray, mobile ultrasound, mobile CT), versus a fixed-installation unit (False). Affects scheduling logic, location tracking, and utilization reporting.",
radiology,study_acquisition,modality,last_calibration_date,last_calibration_date,Last Calibration Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,"Date of the most recent calibration or quality control (QC) performance of the imaging modality unit. Required for ACR accreditation, state radiation control compliance, and Joint Commission equipment maintenance standards.",
radiology,study_acquisition,modality,last_preventive_maintenance_date,last_preventive_maintenance_date,Last Preventive Maintenance Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,Date of the most recent scheduled preventive maintenance (PM) service performed on the modality unit by biomedical engineering or the manufacturers field service team. Supports Joint Commission equipment maintenance compliance and uptime tracking.,
radiology,study_acquisition,modality,manufacturer,manufacturer,Equipment Manufacturer,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Name of the original equipment manufacturer (OEM) of the imaging modality unit (e.g., Siemens Healthineers, GE Healthcare, Philips Healthcare, Canon Medical, Hologic). Used for vendor management, service contract tracking, and FDA device registration.",
radiology,study_acquisition,modality,max_patient_weight_kg,max_patient_weight_kg,Maximum Patient Weight Capacity (kg),"DECIMAL(6,2)",,,,,master_data,"Maximum patient weight in kilograms that the modality units table or gantry is rated to support. Critical for bariatric patient scheduling, safety screening, and order routing to appropriate equipment. Drives clinical decision support alerts in the RIS and EHR.",
radiology,study_acquisition,modality,model_name,model_name,Equipment Model Name,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Manufacturer-assigned model name or product line designation for the imaging equipment unit (e.g., SOMATOM Force, MAGNETOM Vida, Revolution CT, Ingenia Elition). Used for service contract management, software upgrade tracking, and ACR accreditation documentation.",
radiology,study_acquisition,modality,next_calibration_due_date,next_calibration_due_date,Next Calibration Due Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,Scheduled date by which the next calibration or quality control test must be completed to maintain regulatory compliance and accreditation status. Drives preventive maintenance scheduling and compliance alerts.,
radiology,study_acquisition,modality,next_preventive_maintenance_date,next_preventive_maintenance_date,Next Preventive Maintenance Due Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,Scheduled date for the next preventive maintenance service on the modality unit. Used by biomedical engineering and facilities management for maintenance scheduling and Joint Commission compliance.,
radiology,study_acquisition,modality,operational_status,operational_status,Operational Status,STRING,,,,active|inactive|under_maintenance|decommissioned|pending_installation,master_data,"Current operational lifecycle status of the imaging modality unit. Drives scheduling availability, order routing eligibility, and equipment utilization reporting. active = available for clinical use; under_maintenance = temporarily unavailable; decommissioned = permanently retired from service.",
radiology,study_acquisition,modality,pacs_node_name,pacs_node_name,PACS (Picture Archiving and Communication System) Node Name,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Name of the PACS (Picture Archiving and Communication System) storage node or archive destination configured for this modality unit. Defines the image routing path from the modality to the enterprise PACS for storage, retrieval, and radiologist interpretation.",
radiology,study_acquisition,modality,radiation_emitting,radiation_emitting,Radiation Emitting Indicator,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,"Indicates whether this imaging modality unit emits ionizing radiation (True = ionizing radiation, e.g., CT, X-ray, PET, fluoroscopy; False = non-ionizing, e.g., MRI, ultrasound). Drives radiation dose tracking requirements, state radiation control reporting, and ALARA compliance workflows.",
radiology,study_acquisition,modality,ris_resource_code,ris_resource_code,Radiology Information System (RIS) Resource ID,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Identifier for this modality unit as configured in the source Radiology Information System (RIS) — Epic Radiant or Cerner RadNet. Used for system-of-record traceability, ETL reconciliation, and cross-system integration with scheduling and order management.",
radiology,study_acquisition,modality,room_identifier,room_identifier,Room Identifier,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Physical room or suite identifier within the facility where the modality unit is installed (e.g., Room 3, Suite B-102, MRI Suite 1). Used for scheduling, patient wayfinding, and facility management.",
radiology,study_acquisition,modality,scheduled_hours_per_day,scheduled_hours_per_day,Scheduled Operating Hours Per Day,"DECIMAL(4,2)",,,,,master_data,"Standard number of hours per day this modality unit is scheduled for clinical operations. Used as the denominator for equipment utilization rate calculations, capacity planning, and staffing models in radiology operations analytics.",
radiology,study_acquisition,modality,serial_number,serial_number,Equipment Serial Number,STRING,,,"dbx_confidential,pii_phi,pii_pii,pii_sensitive",,master_data,"Manufacturer-assigned unique serial number for the physical imaging equipment unit. Required for FDA device registration, warranty tracking, service contract management, and ACR accreditation. Stored as confidential due to its role in device security and regulatory compliance.",
radiology,study_acquisition,modality,shared_service_indicator,shared_service_indicator,Shared Service Indicator,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,"Indicates whether this modality unit is shared across multiple departments, facilities, or service lines (True) versus dedicated to a single department (False). Relevant for cost allocation, scheduling priority rules, and utilization analytics in multi-entity health systems.",
radiology,study_acquisition,modality,slice_count,slice_count,CT Detector Slice Count,INT,,,,,master_data,"Number of detector rows or slices for CT modality units (e.g., 16, 64, 128, 256, 320). Null for non-CT equipment. Determines CT protocol capabilities, scan speed, and clinical application eligibility (e.g., cardiac CT requires ≥64 slices). Used in equipment utilization and capability reporting.",
radiology,study_acquisition,modality,software_version,software_version,Equipment Software Version,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Current installed software or firmware version on the imaging modality unit. Critical for cybersecurity patch management, FDA software as a medical device (SaMD) compliance, and protocol compatibility with PACS and RIS systems.",
radiology,study_acquisition,modality,tesla_field_strength,tesla_field_strength,MRI Magnetic Field Strength (Tesla),"DECIMAL(4,2)",,,,,master_data,"Magnetic field strength in Tesla (T) for MRI modality units (e.g., 1.5, 3.0, 7.0). Null for non-MRI equipment. Determines MRI safety zone classifications, implant screening requirements, and protocol capabilities. Required for ACR MRI accreditation documentation.",
radiology,study_acquisition,modality,unit_code,unit_code,Modality Unit Code,STRING,,,,"^[A-Z0-9_-]{2,30}$",master_data,"Facility-assigned alphanumeric code uniquely identifying this imaging equipment unit within the enterprise. Used as the operational business identifier in RIS scheduling, order routing, and PACS integration (e.g., CT01, MRI-3T-02). Corresponds to the equipment code in Epic Radiant and Cerner RadNet.",
radiology,study_acquisition,modality,unit_name,unit_name,Modality Unit Name,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Human-readable display name for the imaging modality unit as it appears in scheduling systems, worklists, and operational dashboards (e.g., Main Campus CT Scanner 1, North Wing 3T MRI). Used by technologists and schedulers to identify equipment.",
radiology,study_acquisition,modality,updated_timestamp,updated_timestamp,Record Updated Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,master_data,"Timestamp of the most recent update to this modality unit record in the enterprise data platform. Supports change data capture (CDC), ETL incremental load processing, and audit trail requirements under HIPAA Security Rule.",
radiology,study_acquisition,protocol,protocol_id,protocol_id,Protocol Identifier,BIGINT,Y,,,,reference_data,Primary key for protocol,
radiology,study_acquisition,protocol,approving_clinician_id,approving_clinician_id,Approving Clinician Id,BIGINT,,provider.clinician.clinician_id,dbx_internal,,reference_data,FK to provider.clinician,
radiology,study_acquisition,protocol,compliance_policy_id,compliance_policy_id,Policy Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,compliance.compliance_policy.compliance_policy_id,,,reference_data,"Foreign key linking to compliance.policy. Business justification: Imaging protocols operationalize compliance policies for radiation safety, contrast administration, and clinical appropriateness. Policies mandate protocol standards; protocols reference governing pol",
radiology,study_acquisition,protocol,contrast_drug_master_id,contrast_drug_master_id,Contrast Drug Master Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,pharmacy.drug_master.drug_master_id,,,reference_data,"Foreign key linking to pharmacy.drug_master. Business justification: Imaging protocols define standard contrast agents for specific exam types. FK to drug_master ensures protocol-formulary alignment, supports automated order validation, and enables protocol updates whe",
radiology,study_acquisition,protocol,cpt_code_id,cpt_code_id,Cpt Code Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,reference.cpt_code.cpt_code_id,,,reference_data,"Foreign key linking to reference.cpt_code. Business justification: Imaging protocols are mapped to CPT codes to standardize procedure ordering, support charge capture automation, and enable protocol-to-billing reconciliation. Essential for revenue cycle optimization ",
radiology,study_acquisition,protocol,employee_id,employee_id,Created By Employee Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,workforce.employee.employee_id,"dbx_confidential, dbx_pii",,reference_data,"Foreign key linking to workforce.employee. Business justification: Imaging protocols authored by radiologists or medical physicists require creator tracking for audit trail, version control, and regulatory compliance. Distinct from approving_clinician_id which captur",
radiology,study_acquisition,protocol,loinc_code_id,loinc_code_id,Loinc Code Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,reference.loinc_code.loinc_code_id,,,reference_data,"Foreign key linking to reference.loinc_code. Business justification: Protocols reference LOINC codes for interoperable procedure identification in HL7 messages, support standardized order entry, and enable cross-facility protocol comparison for quality benchmarking.",
radiology,study_acquisition,protocol,parent_protocol_id,parent_protocol_id,Parent Protocol ID,BIGINT,,radiology.protocol.protocol_id,,,reference_data,"Reference to the imaging_protocol_id of the parent protocol from which this protocol was derived or branched (e.g., a pediatric variant derived from an adult protocol). Supports protocol hierarchy and variant management within the Radiant protocol library.",
radiology,study_acquisition,protocol,primary_superseded_by_protocol_id,primary_superseded_by_protocol_id,Superseded By Protocol ID,BIGINT,,radiology.protocol.protocol_id,,,reference_data,Reference to the imaging_protocol_id of the newer protocol version that replaced this one upon retirement. Enables forward navigation through protocol version history and ensures continuity of care documentation.,
radiology,study_acquisition,protocol,acr_appropriateness_rating,acr_appropriateness_rating,ACR Appropriateness Criteria Rating,STRING,,,,usually_appropriate|may_be_appropriate|usually_not_appropriate,reference_data,"American College of Radiology (ACR) Appropriateness Criteria rating for this protocol-indication combination. Used for clinical decision support, prior authorization, and CMS Appropriate Use Criteria (AUC) compliance reporting under PAMA.",
radiology,study_acquisition,protocol,approval_date,approval_date,Protocol Approval Date,DATE,,,,,reference_data,Date on which the approving radiologist formally approved this protocol version for clinical use. Marks the transition from draft to active status and is used for audit trails and regulatory compliance documentation.,
radiology,study_acquisition,protocol,approving_radiologist_npi,approving_radiologist_npi,Approving Radiologist National Provider Identifier (NPI),STRING,,,,^d{10}$,reference_data,National Provider Identifier (NPI) of the radiologist who reviewed and approved this protocol version. Ensures accountability for clinical protocol governance and supports credentialing verification. Links to provider registry.,
radiology,study_acquisition,protocol,body_part,body_part,Body Part Examined,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"Anatomical region or body part targeted by this imaging protocol (e.g., Brain, Chest, Abdomen and Pelvis, Lumbar Spine). Corresponds to the DICOM Body Part Examined attribute and SNOMED CT anatomical site codes. Used for protocol selection and PACS routing.",
radiology,study_acquisition,protocol,clinical_indication,clinical_indication,Clinical Indication,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"The clinical reason or diagnostic question driving the imaging order for which this protocol is designed (e.g., Pulmonary Embolism Rule-Out, Abdominal Pain, Stroke Workup). Maps to ICD-10 diagnosis categories and supports appropriateness criteria evaluation.",
radiology,study_acquisition,protocol,contrast_dose_ml,contrast_dose_ml,Contrast Dose (mL),"DECIMAL(8,2)",,,,,reference_data,Standard contrast agent dose in milliliters specified for this protocol. May be weight-based (documented separately in patient preparation instructions) or fixed volume. Used for pharmacy preparation and contrast utilization tracking.,
radiology,study_acquisition,protocol,contrast_flow_rate_ml_per_sec,contrast_flow_rate_ml_per_sec,Contrast Flow Rate (mL/sec),"DECIMAL(5,2)",,,,,reference_data,Injection flow rate for intravenous contrast in milliliters per second as specified in the protocol. Critical for CT angiography and dynamic phase imaging to achieve optimal vascular enhancement. Null for non-IV contrast protocols.,
radiology,study_acquisition,protocol,contrast_required,contrast_required,Contrast Required Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,reference_data,"Indicates whether intravenous or oral contrast administration is required for this protocol. True = contrast is required; False = non-contrast study. Drives pre-procedure screening for contrast allergies, renal function checks, and pharmacy preparation.",
radiology,study_acquisition,protocol,contrast_route,contrast_route,Contrast Administration Route,STRING,,,,intravenous|oral|rectal|intrathecal|intra_articular|none,reference_data,"Route of administration for the contrast agent specified in this protocol (e.g., intravenous for CT angiography, oral for GI studies, intrathecal for myelography). Drives nursing preparation and patient consent requirements.",
radiology,study_acquisition,protocol,created_timestamp,created_timestamp,Record Created Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,reference_data,"Timestamp when this protocol record was first created in the radiology data platform. Used for audit trail, data lineage, and compliance with HIPAA record retention requirements.",
radiology,study_acquisition,protocol,dose_optimization_program,dose_optimization_program,Dose Optimization Program,STRING,,,,image_gently|image_wisely|acr_dir|none,reference_data,"Radiation dose optimization program under which this protocol was designed or benchmarked. image_gently for pediatric dose reduction, image_wisely for adult dose reduction, acr_dir for ACR Dose Index Registry benchmarking. Supports regulatory reporting and quality improvement programs.",
radiology,study_acquisition,protocol,effective_date,effective_date,Protocol Effective Date,DATE,,,,,reference_data,Date from which this protocol version becomes effective and available for clinical use in the RIS. May differ from approval_date if a future activation date is set. Used for version control and ensuring technologists use the current protocol.,
radiology,study_acquisition,protocol,fasting_duration_hours,fasting_duration_hours,Fasting Duration (hours),INT,,,,,reference_data,"Required fasting duration in hours prior to the examination when fasting_required is True (e.g., 4 hours for contrast CT, 6 hours for PET-CT). Null when fasting is not required.",
radiology,study_acquisition,protocol,fasting_required,fasting_required,Fasting Required Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,reference_data,Indicates whether the patient must fast (NPO) prior to this imaging examination. True = fasting required; False = no fasting required. Drives pre-procedure patient instructions and scheduling communication.,
radiology,study_acquisition,protocol,field_of_view_mm,field_of_view_mm,Field of View (FOV) (mm),"DECIMAL(8,2)",,,,,reference_data,Field of view in millimeters defining the anatomical coverage area for image reconstruction. Determines spatial resolution and the extent of anatomy captured in the image matrix. Applicable to CT and MRI protocols.,
radiology,study_acquisition,protocol,implant_screening_required,implant_screening_required,Implant Screening Required Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,reference_data,"Indicates whether MRI implant safety screening is required before performing this protocol. True = screening required (applicable to all MRI protocols); False = not required. Drives pre-procedure safety questionnaire workflows to identify contraindicated implants, pacemakers, or metallic foreign bodies.",
radiology,study_acquisition,protocol,kvp,kvp,Peak Kilovoltage (kVp),INT,,,,,reference_data,"Peak kilovoltage (kVp) setting for the X-ray tube as specified in this protocol. Determines X-ray beam energy and affects image contrast and patient radiation dose. Applicable to CT, X-ray, and fluoroscopy modalities. Null for MRI and ultrasound.",
radiology,study_acquisition,protocol,last_updated_timestamp,last_updated_timestamp,Record Last Updated Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,reference_data,"Timestamp when this protocol record was most recently modified in the radiology data platform. Used for change tracking, audit trails, and incremental data pipeline processing in the Databricks Silver layer.",
radiology,study_acquisition,protocol,magnetic_field_strength_tesla,magnetic_field_strength_tesla,Magnetic Field Strength (Tesla),"DECIMAL(4,2)",,,,,reference_data,"Magnetic field strength in Tesla for MRI protocols (e.g., 1.5T, 3.0T, 7.0T). Determines scanner compatibility, image quality characteristics, and specific absorption rate (SAR) limits. Null for non-MRI modalities.",
radiology,study_acquisition,protocol,mas,mas,Milliampere-Seconds (mAs),"DECIMAL(8,2)",,,,,reference_data,Milliampere-seconds (mAs) setting specifying the X-ray tube current-time product for this protocol. Directly influences image noise and patient radiation dose. Used in CT and radiography protocols. Null for MRI and ultrasound.,
radiology,study_acquisition,protocol,modality_type,modality_type,Modality Type,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"DICOM-standard imaging modality code for which this protocol is defined (e.g., CT = Computed Tomography, MRI = Magnetic Resonance Imaging, XR = X-Ray, US = Ultrasound, PET = Positron Emission Tomography, NM = Nuclear Medicine, MG = Mammography). Drives scheduling to the correct equipment and technologist skill set. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: CT|MRI|XR|US|PET|NM|MG|FL|DX|PT — 10 candidates stripped; promote to reference product]",
radiology,study_acquisition,protocol,pacs_routing_code,pacs_routing_code,PACS Routing Code,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"Code used to route completed images to the correct reading worklist, hanging protocol, and storage location within the Picture Archiving and Communication System (PACS). Ensures images are delivered to the appropriate radiologist subspecialty queue for interpretation.",
radiology,study_acquisition,protocol,patient_population,patient_population,Patient Population,STRING,,,,adult|pediatric|neonatal|geriatric|obstetric|all,reference_data,Target patient population for which this protocol is designed. Drives protocol selection logic in the RIS based on patient age and clinical context. Pediatric and neonatal protocols use weight-based dosing and modified acquisition parameters.,
radiology,study_acquisition,protocol,patient_prep_instructions,patient_prep_instructions,Patient Preparation Instructions,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"Standardized patient preparation instructions for this protocol, including fasting requirements (e.g., NPO 4 hours), hydration instructions, medication holds (e.g., hold Metformin for contrast studies), bowel preparation, and breath-hold coaching. Displayed to scheduling staff and communicated to patients prior to the exam.",
radiology,study_acquisition,protocol,pitch_factor,pitch_factor,CT Pitch Factor,"DECIMAL(5,3)",,,,,reference_data,"Helical pitch factor for CT protocols, defined as table feed per rotation divided by total collimation. Values less than 1.0 indicate overlapping acquisitions (higher dose, better quality); values greater than 1.0 indicate faster coverage with lower dose. Null for non-helical CT and other modalities.",
radiology,study_acquisition,protocol,protocol_category,protocol_category,Protocol Category,STRING,,,,diagnostic|screening|interventional|research|emergency|pediatric,reference_data,"Clinical category classifying the purpose of this imaging protocol. diagnostic for standard clinical workup, screening for population health programs (e.g., lung cancer screening), interventional for image-guided procedures, research for IRB-approved studies, emergency for ED/trauma protocols, pediatric for age-specific protocols.",
radiology,study_acquisition,protocol,protocol_code,protocol_code,Protocol Code,STRING,,,,"^[A-Z0-9_-]{2,30}$",reference_data,"Externally-known alphanumeric code uniquely identifying the protocol within the Radiology Information System (RIS), such as Epic Radiant or Cerner RadNet. Used for order mapping, PACS integration, and cross-system reference.",
radiology,study_acquisition,protocol,protocol_name,protocol_name,Protocol Name,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"Human-readable name of the imaging acquisition protocol as displayed in the RIS and PACS worklist (e.g., CT Abdomen Pelvis with Contrast, MRI Brain without Contrast). Used by technologists and radiologists to identify the correct acquisition procedure.",
radiology,study_acquisition,protocol,protocol_status,protocol_status,Protocol Status,STRING,,,,active|inactive|draft|retired|under_review,reference_data,Current lifecycle status of the imaging protocol. active indicates the protocol is approved and available for use; draft indicates pending approval; retired indicates superseded by a newer version; under_review indicates undergoing clinical review.,
radiology,study_acquisition,protocol,pulse_sequence_type,pulse_sequence_type,MRI Pulse Sequence Type,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"MRI pulse sequence type used in this protocol (e.g., T1 SE, T2 FSE, FLAIR, DWI, GRE, SSFP, EPI). Defines the fundamental MRI acquisition technique and determines tissue contrast characteristics. Null for non-MRI modalities.",
radiology,study_acquisition,protocol,radiation_dose_ctdi_vol_mgy,radiation_dose_ctdi_vol_mgy,Reference CT Dose Index Volume (CTDIvol) (mGy),"DECIMAL(10,3)",,,,,reference_data,Reference CT Dose Index Volume (CTDIvol) in milligray representing the average radiation dose within the scan volume for this CT protocol. Standardized metric for comparing dose across CT scanners and protocols. Reported to ACR Dose Index Registry and used for DRL benchmarking.,
radiology,study_acquisition,protocol,radiation_dose_dlp_mgy_cm,radiation_dose_dlp_mgy_cm,Reference Radiation Dose - Dose Length Product (DLP) (mGy·cm),"DECIMAL(10,3)",,,,,reference_data,"Reference Dose Length Product (DLP) in milligray-centimeters representing the expected radiation dose for this CT protocol under standard conditions. Used for radiation dose optimization programs, comparison against Diagnostic Reference Levels (DRLs), and regulatory reporting to CMS and ACR Dose Index Registry.",
radiology,study_acquisition,protocol,radlex_code,radlex_code,RSNA RadLex Code,STRING,,,,^RIDd+$,reference_data,"RSNA RadLex ontology code for the imaging procedure or anatomy associated with this protocol (e.g., RID10321 for CT of abdomen). Supports standardized terminology in radiology reporting, PACS integration, and research data aggregation.",
radiology,study_acquisition,protocol,reconstruction_algorithm,reconstruction_algorithm,Reconstruction Algorithm,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"Image reconstruction algorithm specified for this protocol (e.g., Filtered Back Projection, Iterative Reconstruction, Deep Learning Reconstruction, ASIR-V 40%). Affects image quality, noise characteristics, and radiation dose efficiency. Vendor-specific algorithm names are stored as-is.",
radiology,study_acquisition,protocol,renal_function_check_required,renal_function_check_required,Renal Function Check Required Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,reference_data,Indicates whether pre-procedure renal function assessment (eGFR/creatinine) is required before administering contrast for this protocol. True = renal check required (standard for iodinated and gadolinium contrast protocols); False = not required. Drives lab order triggers in Epic Radiant.,
radiology,study_acquisition,protocol,retirement_date,retirement_date,Protocol Retirement Date,DATE,,,,,reference_data,Date on which this protocol version was retired or superseded by a newer version. Null for currently active protocols. Used for version lifecycle management and historical audit trails.,
radiology,study_acquisition,protocol,ris_procedure_code,ris_procedure_code,Radiology Information System (RIS) Procedure Code,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"Internal procedure code assigned to this protocol within the Radiology Information System (RIS), such as Epic Radiant or Cerner RadNet. Used for order entry mapping, scheduling, and charge capture integration with the CDM.",
radiology,study_acquisition,protocol,scan_duration_estimate_sec,scan_duration_estimate_sec,Estimated Scan Duration (seconds),INT,,,,,reference_data,"Estimated acquisition time in seconds for this protocol under standard conditions. Used for scheduling slot allocation in the RIS, patient throughput planning, and breath-hold instruction timing for chest and abdominal studies.",
radiology,study_acquisition,protocol,sedation_required,sedation_required,Sedation Required Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,reference_data,"Indicates whether procedural sedation or anesthesia is required or commonly needed for this protocol (e.g., pediatric MRI, claustrophobic patients). True = sedation required; False = no sedation required. Triggers anesthesia scheduling and pre-sedation assessment workflows.",
radiology,study_acquisition,protocol,slice_thickness_mm,slice_thickness_mm,Slice Thickness (mm),"DECIMAL(6,2)",,,,,reference_data,"Nominal slice thickness in millimeters for cross-sectional imaging protocols (CT, MRI). Thinner slices provide higher spatial resolution for small structure evaluation; thicker slices reduce noise and radiation dose. Null for planar modalities.",
radiology,study_acquisition,protocol,total_exam_duration_min,total_exam_duration_min,Total Exam Duration Estimate (minutes),INT,,,,,reference_data,"Total estimated examination time in minutes including patient preparation, positioning, scanning, and post-processing. Used for scheduling block allocation in the RIS and patient appointment communication. Distinct from scan_duration_estimate_sec which covers acquisition only.",
radiology,study_acquisition,protocol,version,version,Protocol Version,STRING,,,,^d+.d+(.d+)?$,reference_data,"Version number of the protocol definition following semantic versioning (e.g., 1.0, 2.3, 3.1.2). Enables tracking of protocol revisions over time and ensures technologists are using the current approved version.",
radiology,study_acquisition,radiology_study,radiology_study_id,radiology_study_id,Imaging Study ID,BIGINT,Y,,,,master_data,"Unique surrogate primary key for the imaging study record in the lakehouse. Serves as the anchor for all downstream joins to series, reports, dose records, and contrast events.",
radiology,study_acquisition,radiology_study,audit_finding_id,audit_finding_id,Audit Finding Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,compliance.audit_finding.audit_finding_id,,,master_data,"Foreign key linking to compliance.audit_finding. Business justification: Imaging studies are primary audit targets for MQSA, ACR accreditation, state radiation control programs. Compliance audits sample studies to verify quality standards, dose optimization, and protocol c",
radiology,study_acquisition,radiology_study,care_site_id,care_site_id,Facility ID,BIGINT,,facility.care_site.care_site_id,,,master_data,Reference to the facility or imaging center where the study was performed. Supports multi-site reporting and capacity analytics.,
radiology,study_acquisition,radiology_study,claim_id,claim_id,Claim Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,claim.claim.claim_id,,,master_data,"Foreign key linking to claim.claim. Business justification: Completed imaging studies are the billable service event that triggers claim generation. Revenue cycle teams link studies to claims for payment posting, variance analysis, and reimbursement tracking. ",
radiology,study_acquisition,radiology_study,clinical_order_id,clinical_order_id,Clinical Order Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,order.clinical_order.clinical_order_id,,,master_data,"Foreign key linking to order.clinical_order. Business justification: Studies fulfill clinical orders. Direct linkage supports charge capture validation (matching performed study to ordered procedure), results reporting workflows where study context requires original or",
radiology,study_acquisition,radiology_study,clinician_id,clinician_id,Ordering Provider ID,BIGINT,,provider.clinician.clinician_id,,,master_data,"Reference to the clinician who placed the imaging order. Used for referral tracking, utilization management, and RVU attribution.",
radiology,study_acquisition,radiology_study,contrast_drug_master_id,contrast_drug_master_id,Contrast Drug Master Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,pharmacy.drug_master.drug_master_id,,,master_data,"Foreign key linking to pharmacy.drug_master. Business justification: Studies document actual contrast administered during imaging. FK to drug_master enables adverse event tracking, lot number traceability for recalls, billing reconciliation, and REMS compliance reporti",
radiology,study_acquisition,radiology_study,cost_center_id,cost_center_id,Cost Center Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,finance.cost_center.cost_center_id,,,master_data,"Foreign key linking to finance.cost_center. Business justification: Imaging studies drive departmental cost allocation for technical component expenses (equipment time, technologist labor, supplies). Required for profitability analysis by modality, cost-per-study metr",
radiology,study_acquisition,radiology_study,cpt_code_id,cpt_code_id,Cpt Code Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,reference.cpt_code.cpt_code_id,,,master_data,"Foreign key linking to reference.cpt_code. Business justification: Studies are billed using CPT codes for professional and technical components. Links enable RVU calculation, charge capture validation, and revenue integrity audits across PACS and billing systems.",
radiology,study_acquisition,radiology_study,demographics_id,demographics_id,Patient ID,BIGINT,,patient.demographics.demographics_id,,,master_data,Reference to the patient who is the subject of this imaging study. Core PARTY_REFERENCE linking the study to the Master Patient Index (MPI).,
radiology,study_acquisition,radiology_study,employee_id,employee_id,Performing Radiologist ID,BIGINT,,workforce.employee.employee_id,"dbx_confidential, dbx_pii",,master_data,Reference to the radiologist or reading physician who interpreted and signed the final radiology report for this study.,
radiology,study_acquisition,radiology_study,equipment_asset_id,equipment_asset_id,Scanner Device Identifier,BIGINT,,facility.equipment_asset.equipment_asset_id,,,master_data,"Identifier of the imaging device (scanner, modality unit) used to acquire this study. Corresponds to DICOM Station Name (0008,1010) or Device Serial Number. Used for equipment utilization, maintenance scheduling, and dose calibration tracking.",
radiology,study_acquisition,radiology_study,hie_query_id,hie_query_id,Hie Query Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,interoperability.hie_query.hie_query_id,,,master_data,"Foreign key linking to interoperability.hie_query. Business justification: DICOM studies imported from external facilities via HIE queries (XCA/XDS-I.b) for prior comparison require linkage to track query success, patient matching confidence, and external study retrieval for",
radiology,study_acquisition,radiology_study,icd10_primary_icd_code_id,icd10_primary_icd_code_id,Icd10 Primary Icd Code Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,reference.icd_code.icd_code_id,,,master_data,"Foreign key linking to reference.icd_code. Business justification: Studies document ICD-10 codes for medical necessity validation, claims adjudication, and clinical registry reporting. Essential for linking imaging findings to diagnosis codes in quality measures.",
radiology,study_acquisition,radiology_study,imaging_protocol_id,imaging_protocol_id,Imaging Protocol Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,radiology.protocol.protocol_id,,,master_data,Foreign key linking to radiology.protocol. Business justification: study currently has acquisition_protocol: STRING (free-text field). Adding imaging_protocol_id FK normalizes this relationship to the protocol master table. Studies are acquired using standardized pro,
radiology,study_acquisition,radiology_study,modality_id,modality_id,Modality Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,radiology.modality.modality_id,,,master_data,"Foreign key linking to radiology.modality. Business justification: study currently has modality_code: STRING (descriptive code like CT, MR, XR) and equipment_asset_id FK to facility.equipment_asset. Adding modality_id FK links to the radiology-specific equipment mast",
radiology,study_acquisition,radiology_study,research_study_id,research_study_id,Research Study Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,research.research_study.research_study_id,,,master_data,"Foreign key linking to research.research_study. Business justification: Imaging studies performed as research protocol assessments must link to study for endpoint adjudication, protocol compliance verification, research billing determination, and regulatory documentation.",
radiology,study_acquisition,radiology_study,treatment_consent_id,treatment_consent_id,Treatment Consent Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,consent.treatment_consent.treatment_consent_id,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii",,master_data,"Foreign key linking to consent.treatment_consent. Business justification: Completed imaging studies reference the consent obtained for the procedure. Essential for compliance documentation and medicolegal defense. Links the performed study to the consent that authorized it,",
radiology,study_acquisition,radiology_study,visit_id,visit_id,Encounter ID,BIGINT,,encounter.visit.visit_id,,,master_data,"Reference to the clinical encounter (inpatient, outpatient, or ED visit) during which this imaging study was ordered and performed.",
radiology,study_acquisition,radiology_study,accession_number,accession_number,Accession Number,STRING,,,"pii_phi,pii_pii,pii_sensitive",,master_data,"RIS-assigned accession number uniquely identifying this imaging study within the facilitys Radiology Information System (RIS). Used for order tracking, billing, and PACS worklist management. Corresponds to DICOM attribute (0008,0050).",
radiology,study_acquisition,radiology_study,body_part_examined,body_part_examined,Body Part Examined,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Anatomical body part or region imaged during the study. Corresponds to DICOM attribute (0018,0015). Used for clinical classification, protocol selection, and radiation dose benchmarking.",
radiology,study_acquisition,radiology_study,clinical_indication,clinical_indication,Clinical Indication,STRING,,,"dbx_pii_health,dbx_restricted,pii_phi,pii_pii,pii_sensitive",,master_data,"Clinical reason or indication for the imaging study as documented by the ordering provider (e.g., Rule out pulmonary embolism, Evaluate chest pain). Supports ACR Appropriateness Criteria compliance and CDI workflows.",
radiology,study_acquisition,radiology_study,contrast_administered,contrast_administered,Contrast Agent Administered Indicator,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,"Indicates whether a contrast agent (e.g., iodinated contrast for CT, gadolinium for MRI) was administered during this study. Drives contrast reaction monitoring, nephrotoxicity risk tracking, and CPT code selection.",
radiology,study_acquisition,radiology_study,created_timestamp,created_timestamp,Record Created Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,master_data,Date and time this imaging study record was first created in the source RIS/PACS system. Supports audit trail and data lineage requirements.,
radiology,study_acquisition,radiology_study,critical_finding_flag,critical_finding_flag,Critical Finding Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,Indicates whether the radiologist identified a critical or actionable finding requiring immediate communication to the ordering provider per ACR communication guidelines. Drives critical results notification workflows.,
radiology,study_acquisition,radiology_study,critical_finding_notified_timestamp,critical_finding_notified_timestamp,Critical Finding Notification Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,master_data,Date and time the radiologist or radiology staff notified the ordering provider of a critical imaging finding. Required for Joint Commission and ACR compliance documentation. Populated only when critical_finding_flag = True.,
radiology,study_acquisition,radiology_study,dicom_study_instance_uid,dicom_study_instance_uid,DICOM Study Instance Unique Identifier (UID),STRING,,,"pii_phi,pii_pii,pii_sensitive",^[0-9]+(.[0-9]+)+$,master_data,"Globally unique DICOM Study Instance UID assigned at acquisition. The primary DICOM identifier used by PACS for image retrieval, routing, and federation across imaging systems. Conforms to DICOM PS3.3 attribute (0020,000D).",
radiology,study_acquisition,radiology_study,image_count,image_count,Number of Images,INT,,,,,master_data,"Total number of DICOM image instances across all series in this study. Corresponds to DICOM attribute (0020,1208). Used for PACS storage sizing and study completeness checks.",
radiology,study_acquisition,radiology_study,import_method,import_method,External Study Import Method,STRING,,,,cd_dvd|direct_dicom|fax_scan|hie_exchange|vendor_neutral_archive|patient_portal,master_data,"Method by which an externally acquired study was imported into the local PACS (e.g., CD/DVD media, direct DICOM push, HIE exchange, Vendor Neutral Archive). Applicable only when is_external_import = True.",
radiology,study_acquisition,radiology_study,is_external_import,is_external_import,External Import Indicator,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,Indicates whether this study was imported from an external facility rather than acquired internally. True = externally sourced study; False = internally acquired. Drives provenance tracking and comparison read workflows.,
radiology,study_acquisition,radiology_study,is_stat_read_completed,is_stat_read_completed,STAT Read Completed Indicator,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,Indicates whether a STAT (immediate) read was completed within the required turnaround time SLA for urgent/STAT priority studies. Used for quality reporting and radiologist performance monitoring.,
radiology,study_acquisition,radiology_study,laterality,laterality,Laterality,STRING,,,,left|right|bilateral|unilateral|not_applicable,master_data,"Anatomical laterality of the body part examined (left, right, bilateral). Corresponds to DICOM attribute (0020,0060). Critical for patient safety, wrong-site prevention, and surgical correlation.",
radiology,study_acquisition,radiology_study,order_received_timestamp,order_received_timestamp,Order Received Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,master_data,Date and time the imaging order was received by the radiology department or RIS. Used to calculate order-to-scan turnaround time and measure scheduling efficiency.,
radiology,study_acquisition,radiology_study,pacs_archive_location,pacs_archive_location,PACS Archive Location,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Logical or physical storage location identifier within the PACS where this studys images are archived (e.g., tier name, storage node, cloud bucket path). Used for image retrieval routing and storage lifecycle management.",
radiology,study_acquisition,radiology_study,pacs_status,pacs_status,Picture Archiving and Communication System (PACS) Archive Status,STRING,,,,received|archived|retrieved|purged|error,master_data,"Current archival status of the study images within the PACS. Indicates whether images have been received, fully archived to long-term storage, retrieved for reading, or purged per retention policy.",
radiology,study_acquisition,radiology_study,patient_age_at_study,patient_age_at_study,Patient Age at Study (Years),INT,,,,,master_data,"Age of the patient in years at the time of the imaging study. Derived at acquisition time and stored for analytics, pediatric protocol selection, and dose benchmarking without requiring a join to patient demographics.",
radiology,study_acquisition,radiology_study,patient_sex,patient_sex,Patient Sex,STRING,,,"dbx_pii_health,dbx_restricted,pii_phi,pii_pii,pii_sensitive",M|F|O|U,master_data,"Biological sex of the patient as recorded at the time of the imaging study. Used for protocol selection (e.g., pelvic MRI), dose benchmarking, and population health analytics. Corresponds to DICOM attribute (0010,0040).",
radiology,study_acquisition,radiology_study,priority,priority,Study Priority,STRING,,,,stat|urgent|routine|elective,master_data,"Clinical priority level assigned to the imaging study at the time of ordering. Drives RIS worklist ordering, scheduling urgency, and turnaround time (TAT) SLA targets.",
radiology,study_acquisition,radiology_study,radiation_dose_ctdi_vol,radiation_dose_ctdi_vol,CT Dose Index Volume (CTDIvol) mGy,"DECIMAL(10,4)",,,,,master_data,"Volume CT Dose Index (CTDIvol) in mGy for CT studies, representing the average radiation dose within the scan volume. Used alongside DLP for dose benchmarking against ACR national dose reference levels.",
radiology,study_acquisition,radiology_study,radiation_dose_dlp,radiation_dose_dlp,Radiation Dose Dose-Length Product (DLP) mGy·cm,"DECIMAL(10,2)",,,,,master_data,"Dose-Length Product (DLP) in mGy·cm representing the total radiation dose delivered during this CT or fluoroscopy study. Key metric for radiation dose tracking, ACR Dose Index Registry (DIR) reporting, and patient safety compliance.",
radiology,study_acquisition,radiology_study,referring_department,referring_department,Referring Department,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Clinical department or service line that originated the imaging order (e.g., Emergency Department, Oncology, Orthopedics). Used for utilization analytics, volume reporting by department, and capacity planning.",
radiology,study_acquisition,radiology_study,report_finalized_timestamp,report_finalized_timestamp,Report Finalized Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,master_data,"Date and time the radiologist finalized (signed) the interpretation report. Used to calculate scan-to-report turnaround time (TAT), a key quality and operational KPI.",
radiology,study_acquisition,radiology_study,report_status,report_status,Radiology Report Status,STRING,,,,preliminary|final|addendum|corrected|cancelled,master_data,Current status of the radiologists interpretation report for this study. Preliminary reports are available before final sign-off; addendum and corrected statuses track post-signature changes.,
radiology,study_acquisition,radiology_study,ris_system_source,ris_system_source,Radiology Information System (RIS) Source System,STRING,,,,epic_radiant|cerner_radnet|meditech|other,master_data,"Identifies the source Radiology Information System (RIS) from which this study record was ingested. Supports multi-system data lineage, reconciliation, and provenance tracking in the lakehouse.",
radiology,study_acquisition,radiology_study,series_count,series_count,Number of Series,INT,,,,,master_data,"Total number of DICOM series contained within this imaging study. Corresponds to DICOM attribute (0020,1206). Used for PACS storage capacity planning and study completeness validation.",
radiology,study_acquisition,radiology_study,size_mb,size_mb,Study Size (Megabytes),"DECIMAL(12,3)",,,,,master_data,"Total storage size of all DICOM image files for this study, expressed in megabytes. Used for PACS storage capacity planning, archival cost allocation, and data lifecycle management.",
radiology,study_acquisition,radiology_study,source_facility_name,source_facility_name,Source Facility Name,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Name of the external facility from which this study was imported, when is_external_import = True. Supports outside study tracking, comparison read workflows, and HIE provenance.",
radiology,study_acquisition,radiology_study,start_timestamp,start_timestamp,Study Start Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,master_data,"Date and time when image acquisition began for this study. Corresponds to DICOM Study Time (0008,0030). Used for turnaround time (TAT) calculation and operational throughput analytics.",
radiology,study_acquisition,radiology_study,study_date,study_date,Study Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,"Calendar date on which the imaging study was performed. Corresponds to DICOM attribute (0008,0020). Used for scheduling analytics, turnaround time measurement, and regulatory reporting.",
radiology,study_acquisition,radiology_study,study_description,study_description,Study Description,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Human-readable description of the imaging study as defined in the RIS/PACS worklist (e.g., CT Chest with Contrast, MRI Brain without Contrast). Corresponds to DICOM attribute (0008,1030).",
radiology,study_acquisition,radiology_study,study_status,study_status,Imaging Study Status,STRING,,,,scheduled|arrived|in_progress|completed|cancelled|on_hold,master_data,"Current workflow status of the imaging study within the RIS/PACS lifecycle. Drives worklist management, reporting queues, and operational dashboards.",
radiology,study_acquisition,radiology_study,updated_timestamp,updated_timestamp,Record Last Updated Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,master_data,Date and time this imaging study record was most recently modified in the source system. Used for incremental ETL processing and change data capture.,
