reference,clinical_terminology,cpt_code,age_range_high,age_range_high,Age Range High,INT,,,,,reference_data,Maximum patient age (in years) for which the CPT code is clinically appropriate. Null if no upper age restriction applies. Used for claims editing and clinical decision support.,
reference,clinical_terminology,cpt_code,age_range_low,age_range_low,Age Range Low,INT,,,,,reference_data,Minimum patient age (in years) for which the CPT code is clinically appropriate. Null if no lower age restriction applies. Used for claims editing and clinical decision support.,
reference,clinical_terminology,cpt_code,anesthesia_base_units,anesthesia_base_units,Anesthesia Base Units,"DECIMAL(6,2)",,,,,reference_data,"Base unit value assigned to anesthesia CPT codes, representing the complexity and risk of the anesthesia service. Used in anesthesia billing formulas along with time units and modifying factors.",
reference,clinical_terminology,cpt_code,clinical_family,clinical_family,Clinical Family,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"Grouping of clinically related CPT codes, such as all codes for a specific type of surgery or diagnostic test. Used for clinical pathway design, order sets, and utilization management.",
reference,clinical_terminology,cpt_code,conversion_factor,conversion_factor,Conversion Factor,"DECIMAL(10,4)",,,,,reference_data,Dollar amount multiplied by total RVU to calculate Medicare payment. Updated annually by CMS. Used in revenue cycle forecasting and contract modeling.,
reference,clinical_terminology,cpt_code,cpt_code,cpt_code,CPT (Current Procedural Terminology) Code,STRING,,,,^[0-9]{5}$,reference_data,"Five-digit numeric code published by the American Medical Association (AMA) that identifies medical, surgical, and diagnostic services. This is the authoritative business identifier used on CMS-1500 claims, in CPOE systems, and for professional billing.",
reference,clinical_terminology,cpt_code,cpt_code_category,cpt_code_category,CPT (Current Procedural Terminology) Category,STRING,,,,Category I|Category II|Category III,reference_data,"Classification of the CPT code. Category I codes describe established procedures and services. Category II codes are supplemental tracking codes for performance measurement. Category III codes are temporary codes for emerging technology, services, and procedures.",
reference,clinical_terminology,cpt_code,cpt_code_status,cpt_code_status,CPT (Current Procedural Terminology) Code Status,STRING,,,,active|inactive|deleted|pending,reference_data,Current lifecycle status of the CPT code. Active codes are valid for billing. Inactive codes have been retired but retained for historical claims. Deleted codes are no longer recognized. Pending codes are scheduled for future activation.,
reference,clinical_terminology,cpt_code,created_timestamp,created_timestamp,Created Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,reference_data,Timestamp when this CPT code record was first created in the enterprise reference data system. Used for audit trail and data lineage.,
reference,clinical_terminology,cpt_code,effective_date,effective_date,CPT (Current Procedural Terminology) Code Effective Date,DATE,,,,,reference_data,Date on which the CPT code became valid for use in billing and clinical documentation. Typically January 1 of the release year for annual updates.,
reference,clinical_terminology,cpt_code,facility_indicator,facility_indicator,Facility Indicator,STRING,,,,facility|non-facility|both,reference_data,"Indicates whether the CPT code is typically performed in a facility setting (hospital, ASC) or non-facility setting (physician office). Affects practice expense RVU calculation.",
reference,clinical_terminology,cpt_code,full_descriptor,full_descriptor,CPT (Current Procedural Terminology) Full Descriptor,STRING,,,"pii_phi,pii_pii,pii_sensitive",,reference_data,"pii_phi,pii_pii,pii_sensitive",
reference,clinical_terminology,cpt_code,gender_specific,gender_specific,Gender Specific,STRING,,,"dbx_confidential, dbx_pii",male|female|both,reference_data,Indicates whether the procedure is anatomically or clinically specific to male or female patients. Used for claims editing and clinical decision support.,
reference,clinical_terminology,cpt_code,global_period,global_period,Global Period,STRING,,,,,reference_data,Number of days of post-operative care included in the procedure payment. 000 = endoscopic or minor procedure with 0-day follow-up. 010 = minor procedure with 10-day follow-up. 090 = major surgery with 90-day follow-up. XXX = global concept does not apply. YYY = carrier determines global period. ZZZ = add-on code. MMM = maternity codes with global period. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: 000|010|090|XXX|YYY|ZZZ|MMM — 7 candidates stripped; promote to reference product],
reference,clinical_terminology,cpt_code,malpractice_rvu,malpractice_rvu,Malpractice RVU (Relative Value Unit),"DECIMAL(10,4)",,,,,reference_data,Relative Value Unit representing the professional liability insurance component. Reflects the relative risk and cost of malpractice insurance for the service.,
reference,clinical_terminology,cpt_code,medically_unlikely_edit_value,medically_unlikely_edit_value,MUE (Medically Unlikely Edit) Value,INT,,,,,reference_data,Maximum number of units of service that CMS considers medically reasonable for a single patient on a single date of service. Used for claims editing and fraud detection.,
reference,clinical_terminology,cpt_code,modifier_indicator,modifier_indicator,Modifier Indicator,STRING,,,,0|1|2|3|9,reference_data,"Indicates whether bilateral surgery, assistant surgeon, or co-surgeon modifiers are applicable. 0 = not subject to modifier rules. 1 = bilateral surgery applies. 2 = assistant surgeon may not be paid. 3 = assistant surgeon and co-surgeon rules apply. 9 = concept does not apply.",
reference,clinical_terminology,cpt_code,multiple_procedure_indicator,multiple_procedure_indicator,Multiple Procedure Indicator,STRING,,,,,reference_data,Indicates payment adjustment rules when multiple procedures are performed in the same session. 0 = no payment adjustment. 1 = standard payment adjustment applies. 2 = bilateral adjustment applies. 3 = assistant surgeon adjustment. 4 = diagnostic imaging adjustment. 5 = therapy adjustment. 9 = concept does not apply. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: 0|1|2|3|4|5|9 — 7 candidates stripped; promote to reference product],
reference,clinical_terminology,cpt_code,national_payment_amount,national_payment_amount,National Payment Amount,"DECIMAL(12,2)",,,,,reference_data,"National average Medicare payment amount for the CPT code, calculated as total RVU multiplied by the conversion factor. Actual payment varies by geographic locality. Used for budgeting and benchmarking.",
reference,clinical_terminology,cpt_code,ncci_edit_indicator,ncci_edit_indicator,NCCI (National Correct Coding Initiative) Edit Indicator,BOOLEAN,,,,,reference_data,"Indicates whether this CPT code is subject to National Correct Coding Initiative edits, which prevent inappropriate code combinations from being billed together. Used for claims scrubbing and compliance.",
reference,clinical_terminology,cpt_code,physician_supervision_required,physician_supervision_required,Physician Supervision Required,STRING,,,,direct|general|personal|none,reference_data,Level of physician supervision required for the service to be billable. Direct = physician must be present in the room. General = physician must be immediately available. Personal = physician must perform the service. None = no supervision required.,
reference,clinical_terminology,cpt_code,place_of_service_restriction,place_of_service_restriction,Place of Service Restriction,STRING,,,,,reference_data,Comma-separated list of valid CMS Place of Service codes where this CPT code may be performed and billed. Used for claims editing and compliance validation.,
reference,clinical_terminology,cpt_code,practice_expense_rvu,practice_expense_rvu,Practice Expense RVU (Relative Value Unit),"DECIMAL(10,4)",,,,,reference_data,"Relative Value Unit representing the practice expense component, including clinical staff, medical supplies, and equipment costs. Varies by facility vs non-facility setting.",
reference,clinical_terminology,cpt_code,section,section,CPT (Current Procedural Terminology) Section,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"High-level section of the CPT code set to which this code belongs, such as Evaluation and Management, Anesthesia, Surgery, Radiology, Pathology and Laboratory, or Medicine. Used for reporting and analytics grouping.",
reference,clinical_terminology,cpt_code,short_descriptor,short_descriptor,CPT (Current Procedural Terminology) Short Descriptor,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"Abbreviated description of the procedure or service, typically 28 characters or fewer, used in billing systems and charge capture interfaces for space-constrained displays.",
reference,clinical_terminology,cpt_code,source_system,source_system,Source System,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"Name of the operational system or reference data vendor from which this CPT code record was sourced, such as AMA CPT Database, 3M Coding and Reimbursement, or Epic Resolute Professional Billing.",
reference,clinical_terminology,cpt_code,source_system_code,source_system_code,Source System ID,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"Unique identifier for this CPT code in the source system. Used for data lineage, reconciliation, and troubleshooting integration issues.",
reference,clinical_terminology,cpt_code,subsection,subsection,CPT (Current Procedural Terminology) Subsection,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"Subsection within the CPT section, providing more granular classification such as Digestive System, Cardiovascular System, or Office Visits. Used for clinical analytics and charge capture workflows.",
reference,clinical_terminology,cpt_code,telemedicine_eligible,telemedicine_eligible,Telemedicine Eligible,BOOLEAN,,,,,reference_data,Indicates whether the service can be delivered via telemedicine or telehealth platforms and remain eligible for reimbursement. Updated based on CMS and payer policies.,
reference,clinical_terminology,cpt_code,termination_date,termination_date,CPT (Current Procedural Terminology) Code Termination Date,DATE,,,,,reference_data,Date on which the CPT code was retired or deleted from the active code set. Null for currently active codes. Used to prevent billing of obsolete codes and support historical claims adjudication.,
reference,clinical_terminology,cpt_code,total_rvu,total_rvu,Total RVU (Relative Value Unit),"DECIMAL(10,4)",,,,,reference_data,"Sum of work RVU, practice expense RVU, and malpractice RVU. Used to calculate Medicare reimbursement and benchmark physician productivity.",
reference,clinical_terminology,cpt_code,updated_timestamp,updated_timestamp,Updated Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,reference_data,Timestamp when this CPT code record was last modified in the enterprise reference data system. Used for change tracking and data quality monitoring.,
reference,clinical_terminology,cpt_code,work_rvu,work_rvu,Work RVU (Relative Value Unit),"DECIMAL(10,4)",,,,,reference_data,"Relative Value Unit representing the physician work component, including time, technical skill, physical effort, mental effort, and judgment required to perform the service. Used in MIPS reporting and physician compensation models.",
reference,clinical_terminology,crosswalk,crosswalk_id,crosswalk_id,Crosswalk Identifier (ID),BIGINT,Y,,,,reference_data,Unique identifier for the terminology crosswalk mapping record.,
reference,clinical_terminology,crosswalk,crosswalk_code_set_version_id,crosswalk_code_set_version_id,Code Set Version Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,reference.code_set_version.code_set_version_id,,,reference_data,"Foreign key linking to reference.code_set_version. Business justification: Crosswalk mappings are version-specific - ICD-10-CM to SNOMED CT mappings change with each release of both terminologies. The crosswalk table has source_code_system_version (STRING), target_code_syste",
reference,clinical_terminology,crosswalk,source_code_set_version_id,source_code_set_version_id,,BIGINT,,reference.code_set_version.code_set_version_id,,,reference_data,FK to reference.code_set_version.code_set_version_id,
reference,clinical_terminology,crosswalk,approximate_flag,approximate_flag,Approximate Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,reference_data,"Indicates whether the mapping is an approximate or inexact match (True) requiring clinical review, or an exact semantic match (False).",
reference,clinical_terminology,crosswalk,choice_list_indicator,choice_list_indicator,Choice List Indicator,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"Indicates whether the target code is one of multiple valid choices for the source code, requiring clinical judgment to select the most appropriate target.",
reference,clinical_terminology,crosswalk,combination_flag,combination_flag,Combination Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,reference_data,Indicates whether this mapping requires multiple target codes to fully represent the source code (True) or is a single 1:1 or 1:0 mapping (False).,
reference,clinical_terminology,crosswalk,created_timestamp,created_timestamp,Created Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,reference_data,The date and time when this crosswalk mapping record was first created in the system.,
reference,clinical_terminology,crosswalk,directionality,directionality,Mapping Directionality,STRING,,,,forward|backward|bidirectional,reference_data,"Indicates whether the mapping is valid in one direction (forward: source to target only, backward: target to source only) or both directions (bidirectional).",
reference,clinical_terminology,crosswalk,effective_date,effective_date,Effective Date,DATE,,,,,reference_data,The date on which this crosswalk mapping becomes valid and available for use.,
reference,clinical_terminology,crosswalk,last_validated_date,last_validated_date,Last Validated Date,DATE,,,,,reference_data,The most recent date on which this mapping was reviewed and validated by clinical or coding subject matter experts.,
reference,clinical_terminology,crosswalk,map_group,map_group,Map Group,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"Grouping identifier for related mappings that should be considered together (e.g., all mappings for a specific clinical domain or use case).",
reference,clinical_terminology,crosswalk,map_priority,map_priority,Map Priority,INT,,,,,reference_data,Numeric ranking indicating the preferred order when multiple target codes are valid for a single source code (lower numbers indicate higher priority).,
reference,clinical_terminology,crosswalk,mapping_authority,mapping_authority,Mapping Authority,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"The authoritative source or organization that published or validated this mapping (e.g., CMS, NLM, SNOMED International, Regenstrief Institute, internal clinical terminology team).",
reference,clinical_terminology,crosswalk,mapping_purpose,mapping_purpose,Mapping Purpose,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"The intended use case or business purpose for this mapping (e.g., claims submission, clinical documentation, quality reporting, SDOH screening, interoperability, legacy system migration).",
reference,clinical_terminology,crosswalk,mapping_quality,mapping_quality,Mapping Quality,STRING,,,,exact|high|moderate|low,reference_data,"The confidence or precision level of the mapping: exact (perfect semantic match), high (strong clinical equivalence), moderate (acceptable with context), low (weak or conditional match).",
reference,clinical_terminology,crosswalk,mapping_rule,mapping_rule,Mapping Rule,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"Textual description of any conditional logic, clinical context, or business rules that govern when and how this mapping should be applied.",
reference,clinical_terminology,crosswalk,mapping_type,mapping_type,Mapping Type,STRING,,,,equivalent|broader|narrower|related|inexact|unmatched,reference_data,"The semantic relationship between source and target codes: equivalent (1:1 exact match), broader (source is more specific than target), narrower (source is more general than target), related (associated but not hierarchical), inexact (approximate match), unmatched (no suitable target).",
reference,clinical_terminology,crosswalk,no_map_flag,no_map_flag,No Map Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,reference_data,Indicates whether the source code has no suitable equivalent in the target code system (True) or a valid mapping exists (False).,
reference,clinical_terminology,crosswalk,notes,notes,Mapping Notes,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"Free-text field for additional context, clinical guidance, or special instructions related to this mapping.",
reference,clinical_terminology,crosswalk,scenario_flag,scenario_flag,Scenario Flag,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"Identifies specific clinical or billing scenarios where this mapping applies (e.g., inpatient vs outpatient, primary vs secondary diagnosis).",
reference,clinical_terminology,crosswalk,source_code,source_code,Source Code,STRING,,,,"^[A-Z0-9.-]{1,50}$",reference_data,"pii_phi,pii_pii,pii_sensitive",
reference,clinical_terminology,crosswalk,source_code_display,source_code_display,Source Code Display Name,STRING,,,,,reference_data,Human-readable display text or description for the source code.,
reference,clinical_terminology,crosswalk,source_code_system,source_code_system,Source Code System,STRING,,,,"^[A-Z0-9_-]{2,50}$",reference_data,"The originating terminology or code system from which the mapping is derived (e.g., ICD-10-CM, SNOMED CT, CPT, LOINC, NDC, RxNorm).",
reference,clinical_terminology,crosswalk,source_system,source_system,Source System,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"The operational system or data source from which this crosswalk mapping was originally loaded or derived (e.g., Epic Caboodle, 3M Encoder, NLM UMLS, internal terminology service).",
reference,clinical_terminology,crosswalk,target_code,target_code,Target Code,STRING,,,,"^[A-Z0-9.-]{1,50}$",reference_data,"The specific code value in the target code system being mapped to (e.g., 73211009 for SNOMED CT, 99213 for CPT).",
reference,clinical_terminology,crosswalk,target_code_display,target_code_display,Target Code Display Name,STRING,,,,,reference_data,Human-readable display text or description for the target code.,
reference,clinical_terminology,crosswalk,target_code_system,target_code_system,Target Code System,STRING,,,,"^[A-Z0-9_-]{2,50}$",reference_data,"The destination terminology or code system to which the mapping is made (e.g., ICD-10-CM, SNOMED CT, CPT, LOINC, NDC, RxNorm).",
reference,clinical_terminology,crosswalk,termination_date,termination_date,Termination Date,DATE,,,,,reference_data,The date on which this crosswalk mapping is no longer valid or has been superseded. Null indicates the mapping is still active.,
reference,clinical_terminology,crosswalk,updated_timestamp,updated_timestamp,Updated Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,reference_data,The date and time when this crosswalk mapping record was last modified.,
reference,clinical_terminology,crosswalk,usage_count,usage_count,Usage Count,BIGINT,,,,,reference_data,"The number of times this crosswalk mapping has been applied in production systems, used for mapping quality assessment and optimization.",
reference,clinical_terminology,crosswalk,validated_by,validated_by,Validated By,STRING,,,,,reference_data,The name or identifier of the clinical or coding expert who last validated this mapping.,
reference,clinical_terminology,drg,drg_id,drg_id,Diagnosis-Related Group (DRG) Identifier,BIGINT,Y,,,,reference_data,Unique identifier for the DRG record. Primary key.,
reference,clinical_terminology,drg,code_set_version_id,code_set_version_id,Code Set Version Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,reference.code_set_version.code_set_version_id,,,reference_data,"Foreign key linking to reference.code_set_version. Business justification: DRG grouper systems (MS-DRG, APR-DRG, AP-DRG) are versioned annually by CMS with fiscal-year-specific relative weights and payment rules. The drg table has grouper_version (STRING), fiscal_year (INT),",
reference,clinical_terminology,drg,major_diagnostic_category_id,major_diagnostic_category_id,Major Diagnostic Category (MDC) Identifier,BIGINT,,reference.major_diagnostic_category.major_diagnostic_category_id,,,reference_data,Foreign key reference to the parent Major Diagnostic Category under which this DRG is classified.,
reference,clinical_terminology,drg,arithmetic_mean_los,arithmetic_mean_los,Arithmetic Mean Length of Stay (LOS),"DECIMAL(6,2)",,,,,reference_data,The arithmetic mean (average) length of stay in days for cases in this DRG. Used for benchmarking and operational performance analysis.,
reference,clinical_terminology,drg,bundled_payment_flag,bundled_payment_flag,Bundled Payment Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,reference_data,Indicates whether this DRG is included in bundled payment initiatives such as the Bundled Payments for Care Improvement (BPCI) program or Comprehensive Care for Joint Replacement (CJR) model.,
reference,clinical_terminology,drg,clinical_family,clinical_family,Clinical Family,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"Grouping of related DRGs into clinical families for service line analysis (e.g., Cardiovascular, Orthopedic, Neurology). Facilitates portfolio management and strategic planning.",
reference,clinical_terminology,drg,complication_level,complication_level,Complication or Comorbidity (CC) / Major Complication or Comorbidity (MCC) Level,STRING,,,,without CC/MCC|with CC|with MCC,reference_data,"Indicates the severity level of complications or comorbidities included in this DRG definition: without CC/MCC, with CC (moderate complications), or with MCC (major complications). Drives relative weight differentiation.",
reference,clinical_terminology,drg,cost_outlier_threshold,cost_outlier_threshold,Cost Outlier Threshold,"DECIMAL(12,2)",,,,,reference_data,The dollar threshold above which a case qualifies for additional outlier payment. Calculated as: (DRG payment × fixed loss ratio) + fixed loss amount.,
reference,clinical_terminology,drg,created_timestamp,created_timestamp,Created Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,reference_data,The timestamp when this DRG record was first created in the reference data system. Used for data lineage and historical analysis.,
reference,clinical_terminology,drg,drg_code,drg_code,Diagnosis-Related Group (DRG) Code,STRING,,,,"^[0-9]{3,4}$",reference_data,"The official numeric code assigned to this DRG by the grouper system (e.g., 470, 871). Used as the business identifier for reimbursement and case mix reporting.",
reference,clinical_terminology,drg,drg_description,drg_description,Description,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"Extended narrative description of the DRG, including clinical context, typical procedures, and coding guidance. Used for clinical documentation improvement (CDI) and coder education.",
reference,clinical_terminology,drg,drg_type,drg_type,Diagnosis-Related Group (DRG) Type,STRING,,,,medical|surgical|procedure,reference_data,"Classification of the DRG as medical (non-surgical), surgical, or procedure-based. Used for service line segmentation and resource planning.",
reference,clinical_terminology,drg,effective_date,effective_date,Effective Date,DATE,,,,,reference_data,The date on which this DRG definition and relative weight became effective (typically October 1 of the fiscal year).,
reference,clinical_terminology,drg,expiration_date,expiration_date,Expiration Date,DATE,,,,,reference_data,The date on which this DRG definition and relative weight expire (typically September 30 of the fiscal year). Null for currently active DRGs.,
reference,clinical_terminology,drg,geometric_mean_los,geometric_mean_los,Geometric Mean Length of Stay (LOS),"DECIMAL(6,2)",,,,,reference_data,"The geometric mean length of stay in days for cases in this DRG, calculated from national claims data. Used as the threshold for identifying outlier cases and calculating outlier payments.",
reference,clinical_terminology,drg,grouper_system,grouper_system,Grouper System,STRING,,,,MS-DRG|AP-DRG|APR-DRG|IR-DRG,reference_data,"The DRG grouper classification system under which this DRG is defined: MS-DRG (Medicare Severity), AP-DRG (All Patient), APR-DRG (All Patient Refined), or IR-DRG (International Refined).",
reference,clinical_terminology,drg,last_updated_timestamp,last_updated_timestamp,Last Updated Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,reference_data,The timestamp when this DRG record was last modified in the reference data system. Used for change tracking and audit trails.,
reference,clinical_terminology,drg,national_average_charges,national_average_charges,National Average Charges,"DECIMAL(12,2)",,,,,reference_data,The national average total charges (not payments) for cases in this DRG. Used for charge benchmarking and cost-to-charge ratio analysis.,
reference,clinical_terminology,drg,national_average_payment,national_average_payment,National Average Payment,"DECIMAL(12,2)",,,,,reference_data,"The national average Medicare payment amount for this DRG, calculated as: national base rate × relative weight. Used for benchmarking and financial forecasting.",
reference,clinical_terminology,drg,national_case_volume,national_case_volume,National Case Volume,INT,,,,,reference_data,The total number of Medicare cases nationally that grouped to this DRG in the most recent fiscal year. Used for prevalence analysis and market sizing.,
reference,clinical_terminology,drg,operating_room_procedure_flag,operating_room_procedure_flag,Operating Room (OR) Procedure Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,reference_data,"Indicates whether this DRG is classified as an OR procedure DRG, which affects payment and resource allocation.",
reference,clinical_terminology,drg,post_acute_transfer_flag,post_acute_transfer_flag,Post-Acute Transfer Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,reference_data,"Indicates whether this DRG is subject to the post-acute care transfer policy, which adjusts payment when a patient is discharged to a post-acute care setting (SNF, IRF, LTCH, HHA) before the geometric mean LOS.",
reference,clinical_terminology,drg,principal_diagnosis_range_end,principal_diagnosis_range_end,Principal Diagnosis Range End,STRING,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_health",,reference_data,The ending ICD-10-CM diagnosis code in the range of principal diagnoses that can group to this DRG.,
reference,clinical_terminology,drg,principal_diagnosis_range_start,principal_diagnosis_range_start,Principal Diagnosis Range Start,STRING,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_health",,reference_data,The starting ICD-10-CM diagnosis code in the range of principal diagnoses that can group to this DRG. Used for grouper logic validation and clinical documentation improvement.,
reference,clinical_terminology,drg,procedure_requirement_flag,procedure_requirement_flag,Procedure Requirement Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,reference_data,"Indicates whether this DRG requires the presence of a specific ICD-10-PCS procedure code to group (true for surgical DRGs, false for medical DRGs).",
reference,clinical_terminology,drg,quality_measure_flag,quality_measure_flag,Quality Measure Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,reference_data,Indicates whether this DRG is associated with specific quality measures under the Hospital Value-Based Purchasing (VBP) or Hospital-Acquired Condition (HAC) Reduction Programs.,
reference,clinical_terminology,drg,readmission_penalty_flag,readmission_penalty_flag,Readmission Penalty Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,reference_data,Indicates whether this DRG is included in the Hospital Readmissions Reduction Program (HRRP) and subject to payment penalties for excess readmissions.,
reference,clinical_terminology,drg,relative_weight,relative_weight,Relative Weight,"DECIMAL(10,4)",,,,,reference_data,The DRG relative weight representing the average resource intensity for cases in this DRG compared to the national average (1.0000). Used to calculate expected reimbursement: base rate × relative weight.,
reference,clinical_terminology,drg,source_system,source_system,Source System,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"The system of record from which this DRG definition was sourced (e.g., 3M Grouper, Epic Resolute, Cerner Revenue Cycle). Used for data lineage and reconciliation.",
reference,clinical_terminology,drg,special_pay_flag,special_pay_flag,Special Payment Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,reference_data,"Indicates whether this DRG has special payment rules or adjustments (e.g., new technology add-on payments, device-intensive procedures).",
reference,clinical_terminology,drg,title,title,Diagnosis-Related Group (DRG) Title,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"The full descriptive title of the DRG (e.g., Major Hip and Knee Joint Replacement or Reattachment of Lower Extremity with MCC).",
reference,clinical_terminology,fhir_value_set,fhir_value_set_id,fhir_value_set_id,Fast Healthcare Interoperability Resources (FHIR) Value Set Identifier,BIGINT,Y,,,,reference_data,Unique identifier for the FHIR value set record. Primary key.,
reference,clinical_terminology,fhir_value_set,code_set_version_id,code_set_version_id,Code Set Version Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,reference.code_set_version.code_set_version_id,,,reference_data,Foreign key linking to reference.code_set_version. Business justification: FHIR value sets are versioned by HL7 with release-specific canonical URLs and expansion timestamps. The fhir_value_set table has version (STRING) and status attributes that should be normalized to cod,
reference,clinical_terminology,fhir_value_set,interoperability_exchange_standard_id,interoperability_exchange_standard_id,,BIGINT,,interoperability.exchange_standard.exchange_standard_id,,,reference_data,FK to interoperability.exchange_standard.exchange_standard_id,
reference,clinical_terminology,fhir_value_set,approval_date,approval_date,Approval Date,DATE,,,,,reference_data,Date when this value set was formally approved by the governance authority for production use. Required for regulatory compliance and change control.,
reference,clinical_terminology,fhir_value_set,binding_strength,binding_strength,Binding Strength,STRING,,,,required|extensible|preferred|example,reference_data,"Defines how strictly FHIR resources must conform to this value set. Required = must use codes from this set only, Extensible = should use but may extend, Preferred = recommended but not enforced, Example = illustrative only.",
reference,clinical_terminology,fhir_value_set,canonical_url,canonical_url,Canonical Uniform Resource Locator (URL),STRING,,,,"^https?://[a-zA-Z0-9.-]+(/[a-zA-Z0-9._~:/?#[]@!$&()*+,;=-]*)?$",reference_data,Globally unique canonical URL that permanently identifies this value set across all FHIR implementations. Used for terminology server lookups and resource references.,
reference,clinical_terminology,fhir_value_set,compose_exclude_count,compose_exclude_count,Compose Exclude Count,INT,,,,,reference_data,Number of exclude rules defined in the value set composition. Exclude rules remove specific concepts from the included set.,
reference,clinical_terminology,fhir_value_set,compose_include_count,compose_include_count,Compose Include Count,INT,,,,,reference_data,Number of include rules defined in the value set composition. Each include rule specifies a code system and filter criteria for selecting concepts.,
reference,clinical_terminology,fhir_value_set,contact_json,contact_json,Contact Information JavaScript Object Notation (JSON),STRING,,,,,reference_data,"JSON-encoded contact details for the publisher or steward of this value set, including name, email, phone, and URL. Used for support and governance inquiries.",
reference,clinical_terminology,fhir_value_set,copyright,copyright,Copyright Notice,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"Legal copyright and licensing terms governing the use of this value set. Critical for code systems like SNOMED CT, CPT, and ICD-10 that require licensing agreements.",
reference,clinical_terminology,fhir_value_set,created_timestamp,created_timestamp,Created Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,reference_data,Date and time when this value set record was first created in the enterprise terminology repository. Audit trail for data lineage.,
reference,clinical_terminology,fhir_value_set,effective_end_date,effective_end_date,Effective End Date,DATE,,,,,reference_data,Date when this value set version is retired and should no longer be used for new data entry. Null indicates the value set is currently active with no planned retirement.,
reference,clinical_terminology,fhir_value_set,effective_start_date,effective_start_date,Effective Start Date,DATE,,,,,reference_data,Date when this value set version becomes active and available for use in clinical systems. Part of the temporal validity window.,
reference,clinical_terminology,fhir_value_set,expansion_identifier,expansion_identifier,Expansion Identifier,STRING,,,,,reference_data,Unique identifier for the current expansion of this value set. Changes each time the value set is expanded by a terminology server to reflect the current set of member concepts.,
reference,clinical_terminology,fhir_value_set,expansion_offset,expansion_offset,Expansion Offset,INT,,,,,reference_data,Paging offset used when the expansion was generated. Supports large value sets that cannot be returned in a single response.,
reference,clinical_terminology,fhir_value_set,expansion_parameter_json,expansion_parameter_json,Expansion Parameter JavaScript Object Notation (JSON),STRING,,,,,reference_data,"JSON-encoded parameters used during the expansion operation, such as language, display variant, or active-only filters. Stored as text for auditability.",
reference,clinical_terminology,fhir_value_set,expansion_timestamp,expansion_timestamp,Expansion Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,reference_data,Date and time when the value set was last expanded by a terminology server to produce the current list of member concepts. Critical for cache invalidation and version control.,
reference,clinical_terminology,fhir_value_set,expansion_total_concepts,expansion_total_concepts,Expansion Total Concepts,INT,,,,,reference_data,Total number of coded concepts included in the current expansion of this value set. Used for validation and performance optimization.,
reference,clinical_terminology,fhir_value_set,experimental_flag,experimental_flag,Experimental Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,reference_data,Indicates whether this value set is for testing or experimental purposes and should not be used in production clinical systems. True means not approved for operational use.,
reference,clinical_terminology,fhir_value_set,fhir_element_path,fhir_element_path,Fast Healthcare Interoperability Resources (FHIR) Element Path,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"Specific element path within the FHIR resource where this value set binding applies, using dot notation. Example: Observation.code, Condition.clinicalStatus, Procedure.category.",
reference,clinical_terminology,fhir_value_set,fhir_resource_type,fhir_resource_type,Fast Healthcare Interoperability Resources (FHIR) Resource Type,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"The FHIR resource type that this value set is bound to, such as Observation, Condition, Procedure, MedicationRequest, or AllergyIntolerance. Indicates where this terminology is applied in clinical workflows.",
reference,clinical_terminology,fhir_value_set,fhir_value_set_description,fhir_value_set_description,Value Set Description,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"Detailed narrative description of the value set purpose, scope, and intended use cases. Provides clinical and business context for terminology consumers.",
reference,clinical_terminology,fhir_value_set,immutable_flag,immutable_flag,Immutable Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,reference_data,Indicates whether the value set definition is immutable and will never change once published. True means the expansion will always produce the same set of codes.,
reference,clinical_terminology,fhir_value_set,jurisdiction_codes,jurisdiction_codes,Jurisdiction Codes,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"Comma-separated list of ISO 3166 country codes or jurisdiction identifiers where this value set is intended for use. Examples: USA, CAN, GBR. Supports regional terminology requirements.",
reference,clinical_terminology,fhir_value_set,last_review_date,last_review_date,Last Review Date,DATE,,,,,reference_data,Date when this value set was last reviewed for clinical accuracy and relevance. Used to trigger periodic re-validation cycles per governance policy.,
reference,clinical_terminology,fhir_value_set,modified_timestamp,modified_timestamp,Modified Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,reference_data,Date and time when this value set record was last updated in the enterprise terminology repository. Supports change tracking and cache invalidation.,
reference,clinical_terminology,fhir_value_set,publisher,publisher,Publisher Organization,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"Name of the organization or individual responsible for publishing and maintaining this value set. Examples include HL7, SNOMED International, LOINC, or internal enterprise teams.",
reference,clinical_terminology,fhir_value_set,purpose,purpose,Value Set Purpose,STRING,,,,,reference_data,Explanation of why this value set was created and the specific clinical or administrative problem it addresses. Helps users understand appropriate usage scenarios.,
reference,clinical_terminology,fhir_value_set,title,title,Value Set Title,STRING,,,,,reference_data,Human-readable title for the value set displayed in user interfaces and documentation. May contain spaces and special characters.,
reference,clinical_terminology,fhir_value_set,use_context_json,use_context_json,Use Context JavaScript Object Notation (JSON),STRING,,,,,reference_data,"JSON-encoded array of usage contexts defining when and where this value set should be applied. Includes clinical specialty, care setting, patient demographics, and workflow phase.",
reference,clinical_terminology,fhir_value_set,value_set_name,value_set_name,Value Set Name,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"Computer-friendly name for the value set, typically used in code generation and system identifiers. Must be alphanumeric without spaces.",
reference,clinical_terminology,fhir_value_set,value_set_oid,value_set_oid,Object Identifier (OID),STRING,,,,^[0-2](.(0|[1-9][0-9]*))+$,reference_data,ISO object identifier uniquely identifying this value set in the global OID registry. Format follows ISO/IEC 8824 dotted decimal notation.,
reference,clinical_terminology,hcpcs_code,hcpcs_code_id,hcpcs_code_id,HCPCS (Healthcare Common Procedure Coding System) Code ID,BIGINT,Y,,,,reference_data,Unique identifier for the HCPCS code record. Primary key.,
reference,clinical_terminology,hcpcs_code,code_set_version_id,code_set_version_id,Code Set Version Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,reference.code_set_version.code_set_version_id,,,reference_data,Foreign key linking to reference.code_set_version. Business justification: HCPCS Level II codes are maintained by CMS with annual updates and quarterly releases. The hcpcs_code table has version_year (INT) and status attributes that should be normalized to code_set_version f,
reference,clinical_terminology,hcpcs_code,age_restriction,age_restriction,Age Restriction,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"Indicates any age-based coverage restrictions for this HCPCS code (e.g., pediatric only, adult only, age 65+). Defines patient age eligibility criteria.",
reference,clinical_terminology,hcpcs_code,anesthesia_base_units,anesthesia_base_units,Anesthesia Base Units,"DECIMAL(5,2)",,,,,reference_data,"The base unit value assigned to anesthesia-related HCPCS codes, used in calculating anesthesia reimbursement. Null for non-anesthesia codes.",
reference,clinical_terminology,hcpcs_code,asc_payment_indicator,asc_payment_indicator,ASC (Ambulatory Surgical Center) Payment Indicator,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"Indicates the payment methodology for this HCPCS code when performed in an Ambulatory Surgical Center setting. Defines whether the code is separately payable, bundled, or excluded from ASC payment.",
reference,clinical_terminology,hcpcs_code,assistant_surgeon_indicator,assistant_surgeon_indicator,Assistant Surgeon Indicator,STRING,,,,,reference_data,Indicates whether an assistant surgeon is allowed for this HCPCS code and the applicable payment percentage for assistant surgeon services.,
reference,clinical_terminology,hcpcs_code,bilateral_surgery_indicator,bilateral_surgery_indicator,Bilateral Surgery Indicator,STRING,,,,,reference_data,Indicates whether this HCPCS code is eligible for bilateral surgery payment adjustment when performed on both sides of the body during the same operative session.,
reference,clinical_terminology,hcpcs_code,co_surgeon_indicator,co_surgeon_indicator,Co-Surgeon Indicator,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"Indicates whether co-surgeons are allowed for this HCPCS code, where two surgeons perform distinct portions of a complex procedure.",
reference,clinical_terminology,hcpcs_code,code_type,code_type,HCPCS (Healthcare Common Procedure Coding System) Code Type,STRING,,,,permanent|temporary|deleted,reference_data,"Classification of the code lifecycle: permanent codes are established in the annual update, temporary codes are used for emerging technology or services, deleted codes are no longer valid.",
reference,clinical_terminology,hcpcs_code,coverage_indicator,coverage_indicator,Medicare Coverage Indicator,STRING,,,,covered|not_covered|carrier_discretion|bundled|conditional,reference_data,"Indicates whether the HCPCS code is covered by Medicare: covered codes are reimbursable, not_covered codes are excluded, carrier_discretion allows local Medicare Administrative Contractor (MAC) determination, bundled codes are included in other services, conditional codes require specific clinical criteria.",
reference,clinical_terminology,hcpcs_code,diagnosis_requirement_indicator,diagnosis_requirement_indicator,Diagnosis Requirement Indicator,BOOLEAN,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_health",,reference_data,"Indicates whether this HCPCS code requires specific ICD-10 diagnosis codes for coverage. True if diagnosis-based medical necessity criteria apply, false otherwise.",
reference,clinical_terminology,hcpcs_code,dme_indicator,dme_indicator,DME (Durable Medical Equipment) Indicator,BOOLEAN,,,,,reference_data,"Indicates whether this HCPCS code represents durable medical equipment as defined by Medicare. True for DME items (typically E-codes), false for other categories.",
reference,clinical_terminology,hcpcs_code,drug_indicator,drug_indicator,Drug Indicator,BOOLEAN,,,,,reference_data,"Indicates whether this HCPCS code represents a pharmaceutical drug or biological product (typically J-codes). True for drug codes, false for equipment, supplies, and services.",
reference,clinical_terminology,hcpcs_code,effective_date,effective_date,HCPCS (Healthcare Common Procedure Coding System) Effective Date,DATE,,,,,reference_data,The date on which this HCPCS code became valid and available for use in billing and claims submission.,
reference,clinical_terminology,hcpcs_code,frequency_limit,frequency_limit,Frequency Limit,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"The maximum frequency at which this HCPCS code can be billed (e.g., once per year, once per lifetime, twice per month). Defines time-based coverage restrictions.",
reference,clinical_terminology,hcpcs_code,gender_restriction,gender_restriction,Gender Restriction,STRING,,,"dbx_confidential, dbx_pii",male|female|none,reference_data,Indicates any gender-based restrictions for this HCPCS code. Some codes are specific to male or female anatomy; most have no restriction.,
reference,clinical_terminology,hcpcs_code,global_period,global_period,Global Period,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"The number of days of post-operative care included in the payment for this HCPCS code (e.g., 000, 010, 090, XXX, YYY, ZZZ). Defines the global surgical package period.",
reference,clinical_terminology,hcpcs_code,hcpcs_code_category,hcpcs_code_category,HCPCS (Healthcare Common Procedure Coding System) Category,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"The major category of the HCPCS code based on the first letter: A=Transportation/Medical Supplies, B=Enteral/Parenteral, C=Outpatient PPS, D=Dental, E=DME, G=Temporary Procedures, H=Alcohol/Drug, J=Drugs, K=Temporary Codes, L=Orthotics/Prosthetics, M=Medical Services, P=Pathology/Lab, Q=Temporary Codes, R=Diagnostic Radiology, S=Private Payer, T=State Medicaid, V=Vision/Hearing. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: A|B|C|D|E|G|H|J|K|L|M|P|Q|R|S|T|V — 17 candidates stripped; promote to reference product]",
reference,clinical_terminology,hcpcs_code,hcpcs_code_code,hcpcs_code_code,HCPCS (Healthcare Common Procedure Coding System) Code,STRING,,,,^[A-Z][0-9]{4}$,reference_data,"The five-character alphanumeric HCPCS Level II code (e.g., E0601, J1234). First character is always a letter (A-V), followed by four digits. Used to identify durable medical equipment, prosthetics, orthotics, supplies, drugs, and non-physician services.",
reference,clinical_terminology,hcpcs_code,intraoperative_percentage,intraoperative_percentage,Intraoperative Percentage,"DECIMAL(5,2)",,,,,reference_data,The percentage of the total payment allocated to intraoperative services for this HCPCS code within the global surgical package.,
reference,clinical_terminology,hcpcs_code,last_updated_date,last_updated_date,Last Updated Date,DATE,,,,,reference_data,"The date on which this HCPCS code record was last modified in the reference data system, reflecting the most recent change to code attributes, descriptions, or coverage indicators.",
reference,clinical_terminology,hcpcs_code,long_description,long_description,HCPCS (Healthcare Common Procedure Coding System) Long Description,STRING,,,"pii_phi,pii_pii,pii_sensitive",,reference_data,"pii_phi,pii_pii,pii_sensitive",
reference,clinical_terminology,hcpcs_code,modifier_required_indicator,modifier_required_indicator,Modifier Required Indicator,BOOLEAN,,,,,reference_data,"Indicates whether a modifier is required when billing this HCPCS code. True if a modifier is mandatory for proper claims adjudication, false otherwise.",
reference,clinical_terminology,hcpcs_code,multiple_procedure_indicator,multiple_procedure_indicator,Multiple Procedure Indicator,STRING,,,,,reference_data,Indicates whether and how payment adjustments apply when this HCPCS code is billed with other procedures on the same date of service. Defines reduction percentages for subsequent procedures.,
reference,clinical_terminology,hcpcs_code,ndc_crosswalk_indicator,ndc_crosswalk_indicator,NDC (National Drug Code) Crosswalk Indicator,BOOLEAN,,,,,reference_data,"Indicates whether this HCPCS code has an associated NDC crosswalk mapping. True for drug codes that map to specific NDC products, false otherwise.",
reference,clinical_terminology,hcpcs_code,opps_payment_indicator,opps_payment_indicator,OPPS (Outpatient Prospective Payment System) Payment Indicator,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"Indicates the payment status for this HCPCS code under the Hospital Outpatient Prospective Payment System. Defines whether the code is separately payable, packaged, or excluded from OPPS payment.",
reference,clinical_terminology,hcpcs_code,place_of_service_restriction,place_of_service_restriction,Place of Service Restriction,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"Indicates any restrictions on where this HCPCS code may be performed or billed (e.g., inpatient only, outpatient only, office only). Defines valid place of service codes.",
reference,clinical_terminology,hcpcs_code,postoperative_percentage,postoperative_percentage,Postoperative Percentage,"DECIMAL(5,2)",,,,,reference_data,The percentage of the total payment allocated to postoperative services for this HCPCS code within the global surgical package.,
reference,clinical_terminology,hcpcs_code,preoperative_percentage,preoperative_percentage,Preoperative Percentage,"DECIMAL(5,2)",,,,,reference_data,The percentage of the total payment allocated to preoperative services for this HCPCS code within the global surgical package.,
reference,clinical_terminology,hcpcs_code,pricing_indicator,pricing_indicator,HCPCS (Healthcare Common Procedure Coding System) Pricing Indicator,STRING,,,,fee_schedule|asc|reasonable_charge|not_priced|contractor_priced,reference_data,"Indicates the pricing methodology for the HCPCS code: fee_schedule uses CMS published rates, asc uses Ambulatory Surgical Center payment, reasonable_charge uses historical pricing, not_priced has no established rate, contractor_priced is determined by local MAC.",
reference,clinical_terminology,hcpcs_code,prior_authorization_indicator,prior_authorization_indicator,Prior Authorization Indicator,BOOLEAN,,,,,reference_data,"Indicates whether this HCPCS code requires prior authorization from the payer before services can be rendered. True if pre-approval is required, false otherwise.",
reference,clinical_terminology,hcpcs_code,professional_component_indicator,professional_component_indicator,Professional Component Indicator,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"Indicates whether this HCPCS code has separate professional and technical components (e.g., for radiology and pathology services). Defines billing options for split or global billing.",
reference,clinical_terminology,hcpcs_code,quantity_limit,quantity_limit,Quantity Limit,"DECIMAL(10,2)",,,,,reference_data,"The maximum allowable quantity of this HCPCS code that can be billed per claim, per day, or per time period as defined by coverage policy. Null if no limit applies.",
reference,clinical_terminology,hcpcs_code,short_description,short_description,HCPCS (Healthcare Common Procedure Coding System) Short Description,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"Abbreviated description of the HCPCS code, typically 28 characters or less, used for display on claims and billing screens.",
reference,clinical_terminology,hcpcs_code,source_system,source_system,Source System,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"The name of the source system or data feed from which this HCPCS code record was obtained (e.g., CMS HCPCS Annual Update, 3M Coding System, internal reference data management system).",
reference,clinical_terminology,hcpcs_code,superseded_by_code,superseded_by_code,Superseded By HCPCS (Healthcare Common Procedure Coding System) Code,STRING,,,,,reference_data,The HCPCS code that replaces this code if it has been superseded or deleted. Null for active codes that have not been replaced.,
reference,clinical_terminology,hcpcs_code,team_surgery_indicator,team_surgery_indicator,Team Surgery Indicator,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"Indicates whether team surgery is allowed for this HCPCS code, where multiple surgeons of different specialties are medically necessary.",
reference,clinical_terminology,hcpcs_code,technical_component_indicator,technical_component_indicator,Technical Component Indicator,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"Indicates whether this HCPCS code includes a technical component representing facility resources, equipment, and supplies.",
reference,clinical_terminology,hcpcs_code,termination_date,termination_date,HCPCS (Healthcare Common Procedure Coding System) Termination Date,DATE,,,,,reference_data,The date on which this HCPCS code was discontinued or replaced. Null for currently active codes.,
reference,clinical_terminology,hcpcs_code,unit_of_measure,unit_of_measure,Unit of Measure,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"The standard unit of measure for billing this HCPCS code (e.g., each, milligram, milliliter, hour, day, unit). Defines the quantity increment for claims submission.",
reference,clinical_terminology,icd_code,icd_code_id,icd_code_id,ICD (International Classification of Diseases) Code ID,BIGINT,Y,,,,reference_data,Unique identifier for the ICD code record. Primary key.,
reference,clinical_terminology,icd_code,code_set_version_id,code_set_version_id,Code Set Version Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,reference.code_set_version.code_set_version_id,,,reference_data,Foreign key linking to reference.code_set_version. Business justification: ICD-10-CM and ICD-10-PCS codes are published annually by CMS with version-specific effective/expiration dates. The icd_code table has version (STRING) and status attributes that should be normalized t,
reference,clinical_terminology,icd_code,age_high,age_high,Maximum Age,INT,,,,,reference_data,The maximum patient age (in years) for which this ICD code is clinically appropriate. Used for coding validation and quality checks. Null if no maximum age restriction applies.,
reference,clinical_terminology,icd_code,age_low,age_low,Minimum Age,INT,,,,,reference_data,The minimum patient age (in years) for which this ICD code is clinically appropriate. Used for coding validation and quality checks. Null if no minimum age restriction applies.,
reference,clinical_terminology,icd_code,billable_flag,billable_flag,Billable Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,reference_data,Indicates whether this ICD code is valid for billing and reimbursement purposes. Only billable codes may be submitted on claims to payers. Non-billable codes are typically higher-level category codes used for classification only.,
reference,clinical_terminology,icd_code,cc_flag,cc_flag,CC (Complication or Comorbidity) Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,reference_data,Indicates whether this diagnosis code is classified as a Complication or Comorbidity (CC) for DRG assignment and severity adjustment purposes.,
reference,clinical_terminology,icd_code,chapter,chapter,ICD (International Classification of Diseases) Chapter,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"The ICD-10 chapter to which this code belongs, representing the highest-level clinical category (e.g., Chapter 1: Certain infectious and parasitic diseases, Chapter 9: Diseases of the circulatory system).",
reference,clinical_terminology,icd_code,chapter_code,chapter_code,ICD (International Classification of Diseases) Chapter Code Range,STRING,,,,^[A-Z][0-9]{2}-[A-Z][0-9]{2}$,reference_data,"The alphanumeric range defining the chapter boundaries (e.g., A00-B99 for infectious diseases). Used for hierarchical grouping and reporting.",
reference,clinical_terminology,icd_code,code_type,code_type,ICD (International Classification of Diseases) Code Type,STRING,,,,diagnosis|procedure,reference_data,Indicates whether this code represents a diagnosis (ICD-10-CM) or a procedure (ICD-10-PCS).,
reference,clinical_terminology,icd_code,created_timestamp,created_timestamp,Record Created Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,reference_data,The date and time when this ICD code record was first created in the system. Used for audit trail and data lineage tracking.,
reference,clinical_terminology,icd_code,effective_date,effective_date,Effective Date,DATE,,,,,reference_data,"The date on which this ICD code became valid for use in clinical documentation, billing, and reporting. Aligns with annual CMS ICD-10 update cycles (typically October 1).",
reference,clinical_terminology,icd_code,etiology_code_flag,etiology_code_flag,Etiology Code Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,reference_data,Indicates whether this code represents the underlying etiology or cause of a condition and should be sequenced before manifestation codes per ICD-10-CM coding conventions.,
reference,clinical_terminology,icd_code,expiration_date,expiration_date,Expiration Date,DATE,,,,,reference_data,The date on which this ICD code was retired or replaced and is no longer valid for use. Null for currently active codes.,
reference,clinical_terminology,icd_code,gender_specific_flag,gender_specific_flag,Gender-Specific Flag,STRING,,,"dbx_confidential, dbx_pii",male|female|both|unknown,reference_data,"Indicates whether this ICD code is applicable only to male patients, only to female patients, or to both. Used for clinical validation and coding accuracy.",
reference,clinical_terminology,icd_code,hac_flag,hac_flag,HAC (Hospital-Acquired Condition) Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,reference_data,Indicates whether this diagnosis code represents a Hospital-Acquired Condition (HAC) as defined by CMS. HACs may result in payment penalties under the Hospital-Acquired Condition Reduction Program.,
reference,clinical_terminology,icd_code,icd_code_category,icd_code_category,ICD (International Classification of Diseases) Category,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"The three-character category code representing a group of related conditions or procedures within a chapter (e.g., A01 for typhoid and paratyphoid fevers).",
reference,clinical_terminology,icd_code,icd_code_code,icd_code_code,ICD (International Classification of Diseases) Code,STRING,,,,"^[A-Z][0-9]{2}(.[0-9A-Z]{1,4})?$",reference_data,"The full ICD-10-CM diagnosis code or ICD-10-PCS procedure code as published by WHO and maintained by CMS. Format follows alphanumeric pattern with optional decimal subdivision (e.g., A01.0, Z99.89).",
reference,clinical_terminology,icd_code,long_description,long_description,ICD (International Classification of Diseases) Code Long Description,STRING,,,"pii_phi,pii_pii,pii_sensitive",,reference_data,STRING,
reference,clinical_terminology,icd_code,manifestation_code_flag,manifestation_code_flag,Manifestation Code Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,reference_data,Indicates whether this code represents a manifestation of an underlying disease and must be sequenced after the underlying condition code per ICD-10-CM coding conventions.,
reference,clinical_terminology,icd_code,mcc_flag,mcc_flag,MCC (Major Complication or Comorbidity) Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,reference_data,Indicates whether this diagnosis code is classified as a Major Complication or Comorbidity (MCC) for DRG assignment and severity adjustment purposes. MCCs have greater impact on reimbursement than standard CCs.,
reference,clinical_terminology,icd_code,parent_code,parent_code,Parent ICD (International Classification of Diseases) Code,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"The immediate parent code in the ICD-10 hierarchy, enabling hierarchical rollup and drill-down navigation for reporting and analytics.",
reference,clinical_terminology,icd_code,poa_exempt_flag,poa_exempt_flag,POA (Present on Admission) Exempt Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,reference_data,Indicates whether this diagnosis code is exempt from the CMS Present on Admission (POA) reporting requirement for inpatient claims. POA-exempt codes do not require a POA indicator on UB-04 claims.,
reference,clinical_terminology,icd_code,replacement_code,replacement_code,Replacement ICD (International Classification of Diseases) Code,STRING,,,,,reference_data,The ICD code that replaces this code if the code has been retired or superseded. Used for code mapping and historical claims reprocessing.,
reference,clinical_terminology,icd_code,short_description,short_description,ICD (International Classification of Diseases) Code Short Description,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"Abbreviated clinical description of the diagnosis or procedure code, typically used in constrained display contexts such as billing forms and summary reports.",
reference,clinical_terminology,icd_code,snomed_ct_mapping,snomed_ct_mapping,SNOMED CT (Systematized Nomenclature of Medicine Clinical Terms) Mapping,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"The corresponding SNOMED CT concept identifier(s) mapped to this ICD code, enabling interoperability with clinical terminology systems and EHR platforms.",
reference,clinical_terminology,icd_code,subcategory,subcategory,ICD (International Classification of Diseases) Subcategory,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"The four-character subcategory code providing additional clinical specificity within a category (e.g., A01.0 for typhoid fever).",
reference,clinical_terminology,icd_code,unacceptable_principal_dx_flag,unacceptable_principal_dx_flag,Unacceptable Principal Diagnosis Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,reference_data,Indicates whether this diagnosis code is prohibited from being used as the principal diagnosis on an inpatient claim per CMS coding guidelines.,
reference,clinical_terminology,icd_code,updated_timestamp,updated_timestamp,Record Updated Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,reference_data,The date and time when this ICD code record was last modified in the system. Used for audit trail and change tracking.,
reference,clinical_terminology,icd_code,valid_for_coding_flag,valid_for_coding_flag,Valid for Coding Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,reference_data,"Indicates whether this code is valid for use in clinical documentation and coding. Codes may be invalid due to retirement, replacement, or administrative reasons.",
reference,clinical_terminology,loinc_code,loinc_code_id,loinc_code_id,LOINC (Logical Observation Identifiers Names and Codes) Code ID,BIGINT,Y,,,,reference_data,Unique identifier for the LOINC code record. Primary key.,
reference,clinical_terminology,loinc_code,code_set_version_id,code_set_version_id,Code Set Version Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,reference.code_set_version.code_set_version_id,,,reference_data,"Foreign key linking to reference.code_set_version. Business justification: LOINC codes are maintained by Regenstrief Institute with biannual releases. The loinc_code table has version_first_released (STRING), version_last_changed (STRING), and status attributes that should b",
reference,clinical_terminology,loinc_code,class,class,Class,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"The high-level category or domain of the observation (e.g., CHEM=Chemistry, HEM/BC=Hematology/Blood Count, MICRO=Microbiology, RAD=Radiology, VITALS=Vital Signs).",
reference,clinical_terminology,loinc_code,component,component,Component,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"The substance or entity being measured or observed (e.g., Glucose, Hemoglobin, Creatinine). This is the analyte, the target of the measurement.",
reference,clinical_terminology,loinc_code,consumer_name,consumer_name,Consumer Name,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"A patient-friendly, lay-language name for the observation or test, used in patient portals and consumer-facing applications.",
reference,clinical_terminology,loinc_code,created_timestamp,created_timestamp,Created Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,reference_data,The date and time when this LOINC code record was first created in the system. Audit trail field.,
reference,clinical_terminology,loinc_code,deprecated_date,deprecated_date,Deprecated Date,DATE,,,,,reference_data,The date when this LOINC code was deprecated or retired. Null if the code is still active.,
reference,clinical_terminology,loinc_code,display_name,display_name,Display Name,STRING,,,,,reference_data,The preferred display name for this LOINC code in the current implementation. May be customized by the organization while maintaining the standard LOINC number.,
reference,clinical_terminology,loinc_code,effective_date,effective_date,Effective Date,DATE,,,,,reference_data,The date when this LOINC code became active and available for use in clinical systems.,
reference,clinical_terminology,loinc_code,example_ucum_units,example_ucum_units,Example UCUM (Unified Code for Units of Measure) Units,STRING,,,,,reference_data,The standardized UCUM representation of the example units. Used for interoperability and unit conversion.,
reference,clinical_terminology,loinc_code,example_units,example_units,Example Units,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"Common units of measure for this observation (e.g., mg/dL, mmol/L, %). Provides guidance for result reporting.",
reference,clinical_terminology,loinc_code,external_copyright_notice,external_copyright_notice,External Copyright Notice,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"Copyright or licensing information for LOINC codes that incorporate third-party content (e.g., SNOMED CT, CPT). Required for compliance with external terminology licenses.",
reference,clinical_terminology,loinc_code,hl7_field_subfield_code,hl7_field_subfield_code,HL7 (Health Level Seven) Field Subfield ID,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"The HL7 v2.x message field identifier where this LOINC code is typically used (e.g., OBX-3 for observation identifier). Supports HL7 message mapping.",
reference,clinical_terminology,loinc_code,hl7_v3_code_system_oid,hl7_v3_code_system_oid,HL7 (Health Level Seven) Version 3 Code System OID (Object Identifier),STRING,,,,,reference_data,The HL7 v3 object identifier for the LOINC code system (typically 2.16.840.1.113883.6.1). Used in CDA documents and HL7 v3 messages.,
reference,clinical_terminology,loinc_code,is_active,is_active,Is Active,BOOLEAN,,,,,reference_data,"Boolean flag indicating whether this LOINC code is currently active and available for use in the organization. True=active, False=inactive or deprecated locally.",
reference,clinical_terminology,loinc_code,last_verified_date,last_verified_date,Last Verified Date,DATE,,,,,reference_data,The date when this LOINC code mapping was last reviewed and verified by clinical informatics or laboratory staff. Supports ongoing terminology governance.,
