reference,clinical_terminology,snomed_concept,cpt_map_target,cpt_map_target,CPT (Current Procedural Terminology) Map Target Code,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"The CPT code(s) to which this SNOMED CT procedure concept is mapped, if applicable. Supports billing and revenue cycle management by linking clinical procedures to reimbursable CPT codes.",
reference,clinical_terminology,snomed_concept,created_timestamp,created_timestamp,Created Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,reference_data,The timestamp when this concept record was first created in the enterprise data platform. Used for audit trail and data lineage tracking.,
reference,clinical_terminology,snomed_concept,definition_status,definition_status,Definition Status,STRING,,,,primitive|fully_defined,reference_data,Indicates whether the concept is primitive (defined only by its stated relationships) or fully defined (sufficient conditions provided for automated classification). Fully defined concepts can be automatically classified by description logic reasoners.,
reference,clinical_terminology,snomed_concept,effective_time,effective_time,Effective Time,DATE,,,,,reference_data,"The date on which this version of the concept became effective in the SNOMED CT release. Represents the snapshot date of the concept state in the release cycle (typically in YYYYMMDD format in source, stored as DATE).",
reference,clinical_terminology,snomed_concept,fhir_value_set_membership,fhir_value_set_membership,FHIR (Fast Healthcare Interoperability Resources) Value Set Membership,STRING,,,,,reference_data,Comma-separated list of FHIR value set identifiers (URIs) to which this concept belongs. Used to support FHIR-based interoperability and constrain coded elements in FHIR resources.,
reference,clinical_terminology,snomed_concept,fully_specified_name,fully_specified_name,Fully Specified Name (FSN),STRING,,,,,reference_data,"The complete, unambiguous name of the SNOMED CT concept including the semantic tag in parentheses (e.g., Pneumonia (disorder)). The FSN uniquely identifies the concept and includes the semantic category to distinguish homonyms.",
reference,clinical_terminology,snomed_concept,hierarchy_level,hierarchy_level,Hierarchy Level,INT,,,,,reference_data,"The depth of this concept in the SNOMED CT hierarchy, with the root concept at level 0. Used for hierarchy traversal, rollup queries, and determining concept granularity.",
reference,clinical_terminology,snomed_concept,icd10_map_correlation,icd10_map_correlation,ICD-10 Map Correlation,STRING,,,,exact|narrow_to_broad|broad_to_narrow|partial|not_mappable,reference_data,"The correlation type between the SNOMED CT concept and the ICD-10 map target, indicating the semantic equivalence of the mapping (e.g., exact match, SNOMED concept is narrower than ICD-10 code, SNOMED concept is broader, partial overlap, or not mappable).",
reference,clinical_terminology,snomed_concept,icd10_map_target,icd10_map_target,ICD-10 (International Classification of Diseases 10th Revision) Map Target Code,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"The ICD-10 code(s) to which this SNOMED CT concept is mapped, if applicable. Supports billing, reporting, and interoperability with systems that use ICD-10 for diagnosis coding. Multiple codes may be pipe-separated.",
reference,clinical_terminology,snomed_concept,is_ehr_preferred,is_ehr_preferred,Is EHR (Electronic Health Record) Preferred Concept Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,reference_data,Boolean flag indicating whether this concept is designated as a preferred term for use in the organizations EHR system. Preferred concepts are promoted in search results and pick lists to standardize documentation.,
reference,clinical_terminology,snomed_concept,is_leaf_concept,is_leaf_concept,Is Leaf Concept Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,reference_data,Boolean flag indicating whether this concept is a leaf node in the hierarchy (has no child concepts). Leaf concepts represent the most granular clinical terms available.,
reference,clinical_terminology,snomed_concept,is_primitive,is_primitive,Is Primitive Concept Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,reference_data,Boolean flag indicating whether the concept is primitive (true) or fully defined (false). Primitive concepts require manual classification; fully defined concepts can be automatically classified by reasoners.,
reference,clinical_terminology,snomed_concept,is_reportable,is_reportable,Is Reportable Condition Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,reference_data,"Boolean flag indicating whether this concept represents a condition that must be reported to public health authorities (e.g., notifiable diseases, healthcare-associated infections). Used to trigger automated reporting workflows.",
reference,clinical_terminology,snomed_concept,last_used_date,last_used_date,Last Used Date,DATE,,,,,reference_data,The most recent date on which this concept was used in clinical documentation within the organization. Used to identify obsolete or rarely used concepts for potential retirement or training needs.,
reference,clinical_terminology,snomed_concept,loinc_map_target,loinc_map_target,LOINC (Logical Observation Identifiers Names and Codes) Map Target Code,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"The LOINC code(s) to which this SNOMED CT concept is mapped, if applicable. Used for laboratory and clinical observations to support interoperability with laboratory information systems and FHIR resources.",
reference,clinical_terminology,snomed_concept,module_code,module_code,Module Identifier,BIGINT,,,,,reference_data,"Identifier of the SNOMED CT module (namespace) to which this concept belongs. Modules represent different editions or extensions (e.g., International Edition, US Edition, UK Edition) and control versioning and governance.",
reference,clinical_terminology,snomed_concept,patient_friendly_term,patient_friendly_term,Patient-Friendly Term,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"A simplified, patient-friendly description of the concept for use in patient portals, after-visit summaries, and patient education materials. Avoids medical jargon and uses plain language.",
reference,clinical_terminology,snomed_concept,preferred_term,preferred_term,Preferred Term (PT),STRING,,,,,reference_data,"The preferred human-readable term for the concept in the default language (typically English). This is the term most commonly used in clinical documentation and user interfaces, without the semantic tag.",
reference,clinical_terminology,snomed_concept,quality_measure_inclusion,quality_measure_inclusion,Quality Measure Inclusion,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"Comma-separated list of quality measure identifiers (e.g., HEDIS, CMS, MIPS) for which this concept is included in the numerator, denominator, or exclusion criteria. Supports automated quality reporting and value-based care programs.",
reference,clinical_terminology,snomed_concept,relationship_count,relationship_count,Relationship Count,INT,,,,,reference_data,The total number of active relationships (both stated and inferred) associated with this concept. Relationships define the concepts meaning and position in the ontology.,
reference,clinical_terminology,snomed_concept,rxnorm_map_target,rxnorm_map_target,RxNorm Map Target Code,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"The RxNorm code(s) to which this SNOMED CT pharmaceutical/biologic product concept is mapped, if applicable. Enables medication interoperability and e-prescribing by linking to the NLM RxNorm drug terminology.",
reference,clinical_terminology,snomed_concept,semantic_tag,semantic_tag,Semantic Tag,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"The high-level semantic category of the concept extracted from the FSN (e.g., disorder, procedure, finding, body structure, substance, organism). Used to classify concepts into broad clinical domains.",
reference,clinical_terminology,snomed_concept,source_system,source_system,Source System,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"The system or module from which this concept record was sourced (e.g., SNOMED International RF2, Epic Clarity, Cerner Millennium, NLM UMLS). Supports data lineage and troubleshooting.",
reference,clinical_terminology,snomed_concept,specialty_relevance,specialty_relevance,Specialty Relevance,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"Comma-separated list of medical specialties for which this concept is particularly relevant (e.g., Cardiology, Oncology, Pediatrics, Emergency Medicine). Used to customize pick lists and search results by provider specialty.",
reference,clinical_terminology,snomed_concept,synonym_count,synonym_count,Synonym Count,INT,,,,,reference_data,The number of active synonym descriptions associated with this concept. Synonyms provide alternative terms for the same concept to support varied clinical documentation styles and search.,
reference,clinical_terminology,snomed_concept,top_level_hierarchy,top_level_hierarchy,Top-Level Hierarchy,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"The top-level SNOMED CT hierarchy to which this concept belongs (e.g., Clinical Finding, Procedure, Body Structure, Pharmaceutical / Biologic Product, Organism, Substance, Physical Object, Qualifier Value, Observable Entity, Situation, Event, Environment, Social Context, Staging and Scales, Linkage Concept, Special Concept, Navigational Concept, Record Artifact). Derived from the root ancestor in the IS-A hierarchy.",
reference,clinical_terminology,snomed_concept,updated_timestamp,updated_timestamp,Updated Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,reference_data,The timestamp when this concept record was last updated in the enterprise data platform. Used for change tracking and incremental data processing.,
reference,clinical_terminology,snomed_concept,usage_frequency_rank,usage_frequency_rank,Usage Frequency Rank,INT,,,,,reference_data,Rank of this concept based on usage frequency in clinical documentation within the organization. Lower numbers indicate higher usage. Used to prioritize search results and optimize user interfaces.,
reference,platform_governance,reference_delta_tblproperties,reference_delta_tblproperties_id,reference_delta_tblproperties_id,reference_delta_tblproperties Identifier,BIGINT,Y,,,,,Primary key for reference_delta_tblproperties,
reference,platform_governance,reference_delta_tblproperties,retention,retention,,STRING - Delta TBLPROPERTIES for retention,,,,,,description,
reference,platform_governance,reference_hipaa_retention_annotations,reference_hipaa_retention_annotations_id,reference_hipaa_retention_annotations_id,reference_hipaa_retention_annotations Identifier,BIGINT,Y,,,,,Primary key for reference_hipaa_retention_annotations,
reference,platform_governance,reference_hipaa_retention_annotations,delta_reference_delta_tblproperties_id,delta_reference_delta_tblproperties_id,Delta Reference Delta Tblproperties Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,reference.reference_delta_tblproperties.reference_delta_tblproperties_id,,,,Foreign key linking to reference.reference_delta_tblproperties. Business justification: HIPAA retention annotations contain inline delta_tblproperty_key/value that reference Delta Lake table properties. Normalizing to a FK to reference_delta_tblproperties centralizes TBLPROPERTIES manage,Internal - LLM Generated Cross-Domain Link
reference,platform_governance,reference_hipaa_retention_annotations,rls_reference_rls_predicates_id,rls_reference_rls_predicates_id,Rls Reference Rls Predicates Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,reference.reference_rls_predicates.reference_rls_predicates_id,,,,Foreign key linking to reference.reference_rls_predicates. Business justification: HIPAA retention annotations contain an inline rls_predicate_expression that references a Row-Level Security predicate. Normalizing to a FK to reference_rls_predicates centralizes RLS predicate managem,Internal - LLM Generated Cross-Domain Link
reference,platform_governance,reference_hipaa_retention_annotations,uc_tag_reference_uc_tag_definitions_id,uc_tag_reference_uc_tag_definitions_id,Uc Tag Reference Uc Tag Definitions Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,reference.reference_uc_tag_definitions.reference_uc_tag_definitions_id,,,,Foreign key linking to reference.reference_uc_tag_definitions. Business justification: HIPAA retention annotations reference specific Unity Catalog tag definitions (unity_catalog_tag_key/value are inline). Normalizing to a FK to reference_uc_tag_definitions allows centralized management,Internal - LLM Generated Cross-Domain Link
reference,platform_governance,reference_hipaa_retention_annotations,annotation_code,annotation_code,,STRING,,,,,,"Unique business code identifying this retention annotation rule, used for programmatic reference in Delta Lake TBLPROPERTIES and Unity Catalog tag definitions.",
reference,platform_governance,reference_hipaa_retention_annotations,annotation_name,annotation_name,,STRING,,,,,,"Human-readable name describing the retention annotation rule, used in governance dashboards and compliance reports.",
reference,platform_governance,reference_hipaa_retention_annotations,annotation_status,annotation_status,,STRING,,,,,,Current lifecycle status of this retention annotation rule within the governance framework.,
reference,platform_governance,reference_hipaa_retention_annotations,applicable_record_type,applicable_record_type,,STRING,,,,,,"The type of healthcare record this annotation governs (e.g., medical_record, billing_record, consent_form, research_data, employment_record, insurance_claim). [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: medical_record|billing_record|consent_form|research_data|employment_record|insurance_claim|radiology_image|lab_result|prescription — promote to reference product]",
reference,platform_governance,reference_hipaa_retention_annotations,approved_by,approved_by,,STRING,,,,,,"Name or role of the compliance officer, privacy officer, or governance committee that approved this retention annotation.",
reference,platform_governance,reference_hipaa_retention_annotations,archive_storage_tier,archive_storage_tier,,STRING,,,,,,"The cloud storage tier to which data is moved during the retention lifecycle, enabling cost optimization while maintaining HIPAA-compliant accessibility.",
reference,platform_governance,reference_hipaa_retention_annotations,audit_access_logging_required,audit_access_logging_required,,BOOLEAN,,,,,,Indicates whether all access to data governed by this annotation must be logged for HIPAA audit trail compliance.,
reference,platform_governance,reference_hipaa_retention_annotations,breach_notification_required,breach_notification_required,,BOOLEAN,,,,,,Indicates whether unauthorized access to data governed by this annotation triggers HIPAA breach notification requirements under the Breach Notification Rule.,
reference,platform_governance,reference_hipaa_retention_annotations,data_classification_level,data_classification_level,,STRING,,,,,,"The sensitivity classification level of data governed by this retention annotation, aligned with organizational data governance tiers.",
reference,platform_governance,reference_hipaa_retention_annotations,data_domain,data_domain,,STRING,,,,,,"The healthcare data domain to which this retention annotation applies (e.g., patient, encounter, clinical, billing, claim, pharmacy, laboratory, radiology, scheduling, provider, facility, workforce, quality, research, reference, compliance, finance, insurance, consent, interoperability, supply, order). [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: patient|encounter|clinical|billing|claim|pharmacy|laboratory|radiology|scheduling|provider|facility|workforce|quality|research|reference|compliance|finance|insurance|consent|interoperability|supply|order — promote to reference product]",
reference,platform_governance,reference_hipaa_retention_annotations,de_identification_method,de_identification_method,,STRING,,,,,,The HIPAA-approved de-identification method applicable when data must be anonymized at retention expiry. Safe Harbor removes 18 identifiers; Expert Determination uses statistical methods.,
reference,platform_governance,reference_hipaa_retention_annotations,effective_date,effective_date,,DATE,,,,,,The date from which this retention annotation becomes enforceable in the data governance framework.,
reference,platform_governance,reference_hipaa_retention_annotations,encryption_at_rest_required,encryption_at_rest_required,,BOOLEAN,,,,,,Indicates whether data governed by this annotation must be encrypted at rest per HIPAA Security Rule technical safeguards.,
reference,platform_governance,reference_hipaa_retention_annotations,expiration_date,expiration_date,,DATE,,,,,,The date after which this retention annotation is no longer valid. NULL indicates no planned expiration.,
reference,platform_governance,reference_hipaa_retention_annotations,last_review_date,last_review_date,,DATE,,,,,,Date when this retention annotation was last reviewed by the compliance or privacy team for continued accuracy and regulatory alignment.,
reference,platform_governance,reference_hipaa_retention_annotations,legal_hold_eligible,legal_hold_eligible,,BOOLEAN,,,,,,"Indicates whether data governed by this annotation may be subject to legal hold, which suspends normal retention expiration during litigation or investigation.",
reference,platform_governance,reference_hipaa_retention_annotations,liquid_clustering_columns,liquid_clustering_columns,,STRING,,,,,,Comma-separated list of recommended clustering columns for Delta Lake liquid clustering on tables governed by this retention annotation.,
reference,platform_governance,reference_hipaa_retention_annotations,liquid_clustering_enabled,liquid_clustering_enabled,,BOOLEAN,,,,,,Indicates whether Delta Lake liquid clustering is recommended for tables governed by this annotation to optimize query performance on retention-managed datasets.,
reference,platform_governance,reference_hipaa_retention_annotations,minor_patient_extension_years,minor_patient_extension_years,,INT,,,,,,Additional years of retention required when records pertain to minor patients. Many states require retention until the minor reaches age of majority plus standard retention period.,
reference,platform_governance,reference_hipaa_retention_annotations,next_review_date,next_review_date,,DATE,,,,,,Scheduled date for the next periodic review of this retention annotation to ensure ongoing regulatory compliance.,
reference,platform_governance,reference_hipaa_retention_annotations,notes,notes,,STRING,,,,,,"Free-text notes providing additional context, exceptions, or implementation guidance for this retention annotation.",
reference,platform_governance,reference_hipaa_retention_annotations,phi_indicator,phi_indicator,,BOOLEAN,,,,,,Indicates whether the data governed by this annotation contains Protected Health Information subject to HIPAA Privacy Rule requirements.,
reference,platform_governance,reference_hipaa_retention_annotations,pii_indicator,pii_indicator,,BOOLEAN,,,,,,Indicates whether the data governed by this annotation contains Personally Identifiable Information requiring enhanced protection controls.,
reference,platform_governance,reference_hipaa_retention_annotations,policy_document_reference,policy_document_reference,,STRING,,,,,,Reference identifier or URL to the organizational retention policy document that this annotation implements.,
reference,platform_governance,reference_hipaa_retention_annotations,purge_method,purge_method,,STRING,,,,,,The method used to dispose of data after the retention period expires. HIPAA requires secure destruction; method selection depends on data sensitivity and operational needs.,
reference,platform_governance,reference_hipaa_retention_annotations,regulatory_authority,regulatory_authority,,STRING,,,,,,"The governing body or regulation mandating this retention requirement (e.g., HIPAA, CMS, state DOH, The Joint Commission, FDA, DEA).",
reference,platform_governance,reference_hipaa_retention_annotations,regulatory_citation,regulatory_citation,,STRING,,,,,,"Specific regulatory citation or CFR reference mandating the retention period (e.g., 45 CFR §164.530(j), 42 CFR §482.24).",
reference,platform_governance,reference_hipaa_retention_annotations,retention_period_days,retention_period_days,,INT,,,,,,Granular retention period expressed in days for precise Delta Lake lifecycle management and automated purge scheduling.,
reference,platform_governance,reference_hipaa_retention_annotations,retention_period_years,retention_period_years,,INT,,,,,,The minimum number of years that data must be retained under HIPAA and applicable state regulations. HIPAA mandates 6 years from creation or last effective date; state laws may require longer.,
reference,platform_governance,reference_hipaa_retention_annotations,retention_start_event,retention_start_event,,STRING,,,,,,"The business event that triggers the start of the retention clock (e.g., record_creation, last_encounter_date, patient_discharge, contract_termination, last_access_date). [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: record_creation|last_encounter_date|patient_discharge|contract_termination|last_access_date|coverage_end_date|claim_adjudication_date — promote to reference product]",
reference,platform_governance,reference_hipaa_retention_annotations,scd_type,scd_type,,STRING,,,,,,The SCD strategy recommended for tables governed by this retention annotation. Type 2 is standard for PHI to maintain full audit history required by HIPAA.,
reference,platform_governance,reference_hipaa_retention_annotations,state_jurisdiction,state_jurisdiction,,STRING,,,,,,Two-letter US state code where additional state-specific retention requirements apply. NULL indicates federal-level requirement only. State medical record retention laws often exceed HIPAA minimums.,
reference,platform_governance,reference_hipaa_retention_annotations,table_name_pattern,table_name_pattern,,STRING,,,,,,Regex or glob pattern matching Delta Lake table names to which this retention annotation applies. Supports wildcard matching for bulk policy assignment across catalog schemas.,
reference,platform_governance,reference_hipaa_retention_annotations,version_number,version_number,,INT,,,,,,"Version number of this retention annotation, incremented when retention rules are updated due to regulatory changes.",
reference,platform_governance,reference_rls_predicates,reference_rls_predicates_id,reference_rls_predicates_id,reference_rls_predicates Identifier,BIGINT,Y,,,,,Primary key for reference_rls_predicates,
reference,platform_governance,reference_rls_predicates,phi_predicate,phi_predicate,,STRING - RLS predicate example for PHI,,,,,,description,
reference,platform_governance,reference_uc_tag_definitions,reference_uc_tag_definitions_id,reference_uc_tag_definitions_id,reference_uc_tag_definitions Identifier,BIGINT,Y,,,,,Primary key for reference_uc_tag_definitions,
reference,platform_governance,reference_uc_tag_definitions,uc_tags,uc_tags,,STRING - UC tag definitions for Unity Catalog,,,,,,UC tag definitions for Unity Catalog,
reference,provider_registry,geographic_region,geographic_region_id,geographic_region_id,Geographic Region Identifier (ID),BIGINT,Y,,,,reference_data,Unique identifier for the geographic region entity. Primary key.,
reference,provider_registry,geographic_region,parent_region_geographic_region_id,parent_region_geographic_region_id,Parent Region Identifier (ID),BIGINT,,reference.geographic_region.geographic_region_id,,,reference_data,"Reference to the parent geographic region in the hierarchy (e.g., a ZIP codes parent county, a countys parent state). Null for top-level regions (e.g., country).",
reference,provider_registry,geographic_region,aco_service_area_flag,aco_service_area_flag,Accountable Care Organization (ACO) Service Area Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,reference_data,Indicates whether this region is part of an ACO service area. True if the region is included in one or more ACO service territories; false otherwise. Used for value-based care program eligibility and population attribution.,
reference,provider_registry,geographic_region,cbsa_code,cbsa_code,Core-Based Statistical Area (CBSA) Code,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"The U.S. Census Bureau Core-Based Statistical Area code. Used for metropolitan and micropolitan statistical area analysis, market segmentation, and payer contracting territories.",
reference,provider_registry,geographic_region,cbsa_name,cbsa_name,Core-Based Statistical Area (CBSA) Name,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"The human-readable name of the CBSA (e.g., New York-Newark-Jersey City, NY-NJ-PA). Null for non-CBSA region types.",
reference,provider_registry,geographic_region,census_division,census_division,Census Division,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"The U.S. Census Bureau division classification, a finer granularity than census_region. Values: new_england, middle_atlantic, east_north_central, west_north_central, south_atlantic, east_south_central, west_south_central, mountain, pacific. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: new_england|middle_atlantic|east_north_central|west_north_central|south_atlantic|east_south_central|west_south_central|mountain|pacific — 9 candidates stripped; promote to reference product]",
reference,provider_registry,geographic_region,census_region,census_region,Census Region,STRING,,,,northeast|midwest|south|west,reference_data,"The U.S. Census Bureau region classification: northeast, midwest, south, west. Used for demographic and statistical analysis.",
reference,provider_registry,geographic_region,cms_region_number,cms_region_number,Centers for Medicare and Medicaid Services (CMS) Region Number,INT,,,,,reference_data,"The CMS administrative region number (1-10). Used for regulatory reporting, Quality Payment Program (QPP) reporting, and CMS regional office alignment.",
reference,provider_registry,geographic_region,country_code,country_code,Country Code,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"The ISO 3166-1 alpha-3 country code (e.g., USA, CAN, MEX). Used for international patient populations and cross-border care coordination.",
reference,provider_registry,geographic_region,effective_end_date,effective_end_date,Effective End Date,DATE,,,,,reference_data,The date through which this geographic region record is effective. Null for currently active regions. Used for temporal validity and historical analysis of region definitions.,
reference,provider_registry,geographic_region,effective_start_date,effective_start_date,Effective Start Date,DATE,,,,,reference_data,"The date from which this geographic region record is effective. Used for temporal validity and historical analysis of region definitions (e.g., ZIP code boundary changes, CBSA redefinitions).",
reference,provider_registry,geographic_region,fips_code,fips_code,Federal Information Processing Standards (FIPS) Code,STRING,,,,,reference_data,The Federal Information Processing Standards code for this region. Used for counties (5-digit) and states (2-digit). Null for non-FIPS region types.,
reference,provider_registry,geographic_region,hrr_code,hrr_code,Hospital Referral Region (HRR) Code,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"The CMS Hospital Referral Region code representing a regional health care market for tertiary medical care. Used for population health management, quality benchmarking, and regional variation analysis.",
reference,provider_registry,geographic_region,hsa_code,hsa_code,Hospital Service Area (HSA) Code,STRING,,,,,reference_data,The CMS Hospital Service Area code representing a collection of ZIP codes whose residents receive most of their hospitalizations from the hospitals in that area. Used for facility service area definitions and market share analysis.,
reference,provider_registry,geographic_region,is_active,is_active,Active Status Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,reference_data,Indicates whether this geographic region record is currently active and valid for use. True if active; false if retired or superseded. Used for address validation and operational reporting.,
reference,provider_registry,geographic_region,last_updated_timestamp,last_updated_timestamp,Last Updated Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,reference_data,"The timestamp when this geographic region record was last updated in the data platform. Used for data lineage, change tracking, and audit purposes.",
reference,provider_registry,geographic_region,latitude,latitude,Latitude,"DECIMAL(10,7)",,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_address",,reference_data,"The geographic latitude coordinate (decimal degrees) representing the centroid or representative point of the region. Used for mapping, distance calculations, and geospatial analysis.",
reference,provider_registry,geographic_region,longitude,longitude,Longitude,"DECIMAL(10,7)",,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_address",,reference_data,"The geographic longitude coordinate (decimal degrees) representing the centroid or representative point of the region. Used for mapping, distance calculations, and geospatial analysis.",
reference,provider_registry,geographic_region,median_household_income,median_household_income,Median Household Income,"DECIMAL(12,2)",,,,,reference_data,"The median household income (in USD) for this region, sourced from U.S. Census or American Community Survey data. Used for Social Determinants of Health (SDOH) analysis, financial assistance program eligibility, and health equity reporting.",
reference,provider_registry,geographic_region,population_estimate,population_estimate,Population Estimate,BIGINT,,,,,reference_data,"The estimated total population residing in this geographic region, sourced from the most recent U.S. Census or American Community Survey data. Used for population health stratification, capacity planning, and per-capita rate calculations.",
reference,provider_registry,geographic_region,poverty_rate_percent,poverty_rate_percent,Poverty Rate Percentage,"DECIMAL(5,2)",,,,,reference_data,"The percentage of the population living below the federal poverty line in this region. Used for SDOH analysis, charity care program targeting, and community health needs assessments.",
reference,provider_registry,geographic_region,region_code,region_code,Region Code,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"The standardized code representing this geographic region (e.g., ZIP code, FIPS code, CBSA code, HSA code, HRR code, state abbreviation). Format and length vary by region_type.",
reference,provider_registry,geographic_region,region_name,region_name,Region Name,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"The human-readable name of the geographic region (e.g., city name for ZIP, county name, CBSA name, state name).",
reference,provider_registry,geographic_region,region_type,region_type,Region Type,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"Discriminator indicating the type of geographic region: zip_code (5-digit ZIP), county, state, cbsa (Core-Based Statistical Area), hsa (Hospital Service Area), hrr (Hospital Referral Region), cms_region (CMS administrative region), aco_service_area (Accountable Care Organization service area), zcta (ZIP Code Tabulation Area), country. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: zip_code|county|state|cbsa|hsa|hrr|cms_region|aco_service_area|zcta|country — 10 candidates stripped; promote to reference product]",
reference,provider_registry,geographic_region,ruca_code,ruca_code,Rural-Urban Commuting Area (RUCA) Code,STRING,,,,,reference_data,The Rural-Urban Commuting Area code classifying the region by urbanization and commuting patterns. Used for population health stratification and Social Determinants of Health (SDOH) analysis.,
reference,provider_registry,geographic_region,source_system,source_system,Source System,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"The name of the source system or data provider from which this geographic region record was sourced (e.g., USPS, U.S. Census Bureau, CMS, Dartmouth Atlas, commercial geocoding vendor).",
reference,provider_registry,geographic_region,state_abbreviation,state_abbreviation,State Abbreviation,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"The two-letter U.S. state abbreviation (e.g., CA, NY, TX). Populated for U.S. regions; null for non-U.S. or non-state region types.",
reference,provider_registry,geographic_region,time_zone,time_zone,Time Zone,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"The IANA time zone identifier for this region (e.g., America/New_York, America/Chicago). Used for scheduling, appointment management, and operational reporting across multiple facilities.",
reference,provider_registry,geographic_region,uninsured_rate_percent,uninsured_rate_percent,Uninsured Rate Percentage,"DECIMAL(5,2)",,,,,reference_data,"The percentage of the population without health insurance coverage in this region. Used for access-to-care analysis, payer mix forecasting, and community benefit program planning.",
reference,provider_registry,geographic_region,urban_rural_classification,urban_rural_classification,Urban-Rural Classification,STRING,,,,urban|suburban|rural|frontier,reference_data,"High-level classification of the region as urban, suburban, rural, or frontier. Derived from RUCA codes or other urbanization metrics. Used for access-to-care analysis and health equity reporting.",
