reference,provider_registry,npi_registry,authorized_official_title,authorized_official_title,Authorized Official Title or Position,STRING,,,,,master_data,"The job title or position of the authorized official within the organization (e.g., CEO, CFO, Administrator, President, Medical Director). Used to verify organizational authority and credentialing compliance.",
reference,provider_registry,npi_registry,deactivation_date,deactivation_date,NPI Deactivation Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,"The date the NPI was deactivated by the provider or CMS. Indicates the provider is no longer actively using this identifier. Used for claims validation, credentialing status checks, and provider directory management.",
reference,provider_registry,npi_registry,employer_identification_number,employer_identification_number,Employer Identification Number (EIN),STRING,,,dbx_confidential,^[0-9]{9}$,master_data,The IRS Employer Identification Number (EIN) for organizational providers (Type 2 only). Used for tax reporting and organizational identification. Also known as Federal Tax ID.,
reference,provider_registry,npi_registry,entity_type_code,entity_type_code,Entity Type Code,STRING,,,,1|2,master_data,"Indicates whether the NPI is assigned to an individual provider (Type 1) or an organization (Type 2). Type 1 = Individual healthcare provider (physician, nurse, therapist). Type 2 = Healthcare organization (hospital, clinic, group practice, pharmacy).",
