reference,provider_registry,npi_registry,mailing_address_line_2,mailing_address_line_2,Mailing Address Line 2,STRING,,,"dbx_confidential, dbx_pii_address",,master_data,"The second line of the providers mailing address (apartment, suite, building, floor). Optional field for additional address detail.",
reference,provider_registry,npi_registry,mailing_address_postal_code,mailing_address_postal_code,Mailing Address Postal Code,STRING,,,"dbx_confidential, dbx_pii_address",^[0-9]{5}(-[0-9]{4})?$,master_data,"The ZIP code or ZIP+4 code for the providers mailing address. Used for mail delivery, geographic analysis, and service area determination.",
reference,provider_registry,npi_registry,mailing_address_state,mailing_address_state,Mailing Address State,STRING,,,"dbx_confidential, dbx_pii_address",,master_data,"The two-letter state or territory code for the providers mailing address (e.g., CA, NY, TX). Used for state-level reporting and regulatory compliance.",
reference,provider_registry,npi_registry,mailing_address_telephone_number,mailing_address_telephone_number,Mailing Address Telephone Number,STRING,,,"dbx_confidential, dbx_pii_phone",,master_data,The telephone number associated with the providers mailing address. Used for provider contact and verification during credentialing and claims inquiries.,
reference,provider_registry,npi_registry,npi,npi,National Provider Identifier (NPI),STRING,,,,^[0-9]{10}$,master_data,"The 10-digit National Provider Identifier assigned by CMS NPPES. Unique identifier for healthcare providers in the United States. This is the authoritative business identifier for provider lookup across claims, credentialing, and directory systems.",
