reference,provider_registry,npi_registry,practice_location_address_line_1,practice_location_address_line_1,Practice Location Address Line 1,STRING,,,"dbx_confidential, dbx_pii_address",,master_data,"The first line of the providers primary practice location address (street address, suite number). This is the physical location where the provider sees patients or delivers services. Used for provider directories, patient navigation, and service area mapping.",
reference,provider_registry,npi_registry,practice_location_address_line_2,practice_location_address_line_2,Practice Location Address Line 2,STRING,,,"dbx_confidential, dbx_pii_address",,master_data,"The second line of the providers practice location address (apartment, suite, building, floor). Optional field for additional address detail.",
reference,provider_registry,npi_registry,practice_location_fax_number,practice_location_fax_number,Practice Location Fax Number,STRING,,,"dbx_confidential, dbx_pii_phone",,master_data,"The fax number for the providers practice location. Used for medical records transmission, referral coordination, and prior authorization requests.",
reference,provider_registry,npi_registry,practice_location_telephone_number,practice_location_telephone_number,Practice Location Telephone Number,STRING,,,"dbx_confidential, dbx_pii_phone",,master_data,"The telephone number for the providers practice location. Used for patient appointment scheduling, provider directory listings, and referral coordination.",
reference,provider_registry,npi_registry,primary_taxonomy_code,primary_taxonomy_code,Primary Healthcare Provider Taxonomy Code,STRING,,,,^[0-9]{10}[A-Z]$,master_data,"The primary NUCC Health Care Provider Taxonomy code assigned to this NPI. A 10-digit alphanumeric code that classifies the providers type, classification, and specialization (e.g., 207Q00000X = Family Medicine, 208D00000X = General Practice). This is the providers main specialty for claims submission and network assignment.",
