scheduling,operative_scheduling,surgical_case,visit_id,visit_id,Visit Identifier (ID),BIGINT,,encounter.visit.visit_id,,,transactional_data,Reference to the encounter or visit during which this surgical case occurs. Links to the inpatient admission or outpatient encounter record.,
scheduling,operative_scheduling,surgical_case,actual_duration_minutes,actual_duration_minutes,Actual Duration in Minutes,INT,,,,,transactional_data,Actual length of the surgical procedure in minutes. Calculated from actual start and end times. Used for performance benchmarking and future duration estimation refinement.,
scheduling,operative_scheduling,surgical_case,actual_end_time,actual_end_time,Actual End Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,Actual date and time when the surgical procedure concluded. Captured when the patient exits the OR or when closure is complete. Used for duration variance analysis and turnover time calculation.,
scheduling,operative_scheduling,surgical_case,actual_start_time,actual_start_time,Actual Start Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,"Actual date and time when the surgical procedure began. Captured when the patient enters the operating room or when incision occurs, depending on institutional policy. Used for on-time start performance measurement.",
scheduling,operative_scheduling,surgical_case,add_on_case_indicator,add_on_case_indicator,Add-On Case Indicator,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,Indicates whether this case was added to the schedule after the initial scheduling deadline. Add-on cases may indicate urgent needs or scheduling inefficiencies.,
scheduling,operative_scheduling,surgical_case,anesthesia_type,anesthesia_type,Anesthesia Type,STRING,,,,general|regional|local|monitored_anesthesia_care|sedation|none,transactional_data,"Type of anesthesia planned or administered for the surgical case. Determines anesthesia staffing requirements, billing codes, and patient preparation protocols.",
scheduling,operative_scheduling,surgical_case,asa_classification,asa_classification,American Society of Anesthesiologists (ASA) Physical Status Classification,STRING,,,,I|II|III|IV|V|VI,transactional_data,ASA physical status classification representing the patients pre-anesthesia medical condition. Ranges from I (healthy) to VI (brain-dead organ donor). Used for risk stratification and anesthesia planning.,
scheduling,operative_scheduling,surgical_case,block_owner_npi,block_owner_npi,Block Owner National Provider Identifier (NPI),STRING,,,,^[0-9]{10}$,transactional_data,National Provider Identifier of the surgeon or service that owns the block time during which this case is scheduled. Used for block utilization and release tracking.,
scheduling,operative_scheduling,surgical_case,block_time_indicator,block_time_indicator,Block Time Indicator,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,Indicates whether this case is scheduled within a surgeons allocated block time. Block time is pre-reserved OR time assigned to specific surgeons or services. Used for block utilization reporting.,
scheduling,operative_scheduling,surgical_case,cancellation_reason,cancellation_reason,Cancellation Reason,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Reason for case cancellation if status is cancelled. Categorized into patient-related, physician-related, facility-related, or administrative reasons. Used for quality improvement and scheduling optimization.",
scheduling,operative_scheduling,surgical_case,cancellation_timestamp,cancellation_timestamp,Cancellation Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,Date and time when the surgical case was cancelled. Used to measure cancellation lead time and assess impact on OR utilization.,
scheduling,operative_scheduling,surgical_case,case_number,case_number,Surgical Case Number,STRING,,,,"^[A-Z0-9]{8,20}$",transactional_data,Business identifier for the surgical case. Human-readable case number assigned by the surgical scheduling system. Used for operational tracking and communication between surgical staff.,
scheduling,operative_scheduling,surgical_case,case_status,case_status,Surgical Case Status,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,Current lifecycle status of the surgical case. Tracks progression from initial request through completion or cancellation. Critical for operational dashboards and capacity planning. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: requested|scheduled|confirmed|in_progress|completed|cancelled|postponed|on_hold — 8 candidates stripped; promote to reference product],
scheduling,operative_scheduling,surgical_case,case_type,case_type,Surgical Case Type,STRING,,,,inpatient|outpatient|ambulatory|emergency|trauma|transplant,transactional_data,"Classification of the surgical case based on patient status and urgency. Determines scheduling priority, resource allocation, and billing rules.",
scheduling,operative_scheduling,surgical_case,consent_obtained_indicator,consent_obtained_indicator,Informed Consent Obtained Indicator,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,Indicates whether informed consent has been obtained from the patient or legal representative. Required before proceeding with surgery. Used for compliance verification.,
scheduling,operative_scheduling,surgical_case,consent_timestamp,consent_timestamp,Consent Obtained Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,Date and time when informed consent was obtained. Used for regulatory compliance documentation and pre-operative checklist verification.,
scheduling,operative_scheduling,surgical_case,created_timestamp,created_timestamp,Record Created Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,Date and time when the surgical case record was first created in the system. Used for audit trail and data lineage tracking.,
scheduling,operative_scheduling,surgical_case,equipment_requirements,equipment_requirements,Equipment Requirements,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,Special equipment or instrumentation required for the surgical case. Free-text or structured list of equipment codes. Used for equipment scheduling and availability verification.,
scheduling,operative_scheduling,surgical_case,estimated_duration_minutes,estimated_duration_minutes,Estimated Duration in Minutes,INT,,,,,transactional_data,"Estimated length of the surgical procedure in minutes. Based on historical averages for the procedure type, surgeon, and patient complexity. Used for block time allocation and scheduling optimization.",
scheduling,operative_scheduling,surgical_case,facility_code,facility_code,Facility Code,STRING,,,,"^[A-Z0-9]{3,10}$",transactional_data,Code identifying the hospital or surgical facility where the case is performed. Used for multi-site health systems to track case volume and resource utilization by location.,
scheduling,operative_scheduling,surgical_case,facility_service_line,facility_service_line,Surgical Service Line,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Clinical service line or specialty department responsible for the surgical case (e.g., Orthopedics, Cardiothoracic, General Surgery, Neurosurgery). Used for departmental reporting and resource allocation.",
scheduling,operative_scheduling,surgical_case,implant_required,implant_required,Implant Required Indicator,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,Indicates whether the surgical case requires implantable devices or hardware. Triggers supply chain coordination and implant tracking requirements.,
scheduling,operative_scheduling,surgical_case,last_modified_timestamp,last_modified_timestamp,Record Last Modified Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,"Date and time when the surgical case record was last updated. Used for audit trail, change tracking, and data quality monitoring.",
scheduling,operative_scheduling,surgical_case,laterality,laterality,Surgical Laterality,STRING,,,,left|right|bilateral|not_applicable,transactional_data,Anatomical side on which the procedure is performed. Critical for surgical site verification and wrong-site surgery prevention. Part of the Universal Protocol.,
scheduling,operative_scheduling,surgical_case,mrn,mrn,Medical Record Number (MRN),STRING,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_identifier","^[A-Z0-9]{6,12}$",transactional_data,Patient medical record number. Unique identifier for the patient undergoing the surgical procedure. Links to the patient master index.,
scheduling,operative_scheduling,surgical_case,patient_class,patient_class,Patient Class,STRING,,,,inpatient|outpatient|observation|same_day_surgery|extended_recovery,transactional_data,"Patient classification for the surgical encounter. Determines billing rules, bed assignment requirements, and post-operative care pathways.",
scheduling,operative_scheduling,surgical_case,post_op_diagnosis,post_op_diagnosis,Post-Operative Diagnosis,STRING,,,dbx_confidential,,transactional_data,Final clinical diagnosis documented after the surgical procedure. May differ from pre-operative diagnosis based on intra-operative findings. Used for billing and clinical documentation.,
scheduling,operative_scheduling,surgical_case,requires_blood_products,requires_blood_products,Requires Blood Products Indicator,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,Indicates whether the surgical case requires blood products to be available. Triggers blood bank coordination and type-and-screen orders.,
scheduling,operative_scheduling,surgical_case,requires_icu_bed,requires_icu_bed,Requires Intensive Care Unit (ICU) Bed Indicator,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,Indicates whether the patient will require an ICU bed post-operatively. Used for bed management and capacity planning coordination between OR and ICU.,
scheduling,operative_scheduling,surgical_case,scheduled_date,scheduled_date,Scheduled Surgery Date,DATE,,,,,transactional_data,Date on which the surgical procedure is scheduled to occur. Used for day-level capacity planning and patient preparation scheduling.,
scheduling,operative_scheduling,surgical_case,scheduled_end_time,scheduled_end_time,Scheduled End Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,Anticipated date and time when the surgical case is expected to conclude. Calculated from scheduled start time plus estimated duration. Used for downstream resource planning.,
scheduling,operative_scheduling,surgical_case,scheduled_start_time,scheduled_start_time,Scheduled Start Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,"Precise date and time when the surgical case is scheduled to begin. Used for minute-level OR scheduling, staff coordination, and patient arrival instructions.",
scheduling,operative_scheduling,surgical_case,secondary_procedure_codes,secondary_procedure_codes,Secondary Procedure Codes,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,Additional procedure codes performed during the same surgical case. Comma-separated list of CPT or ICD-10-PCS codes. Used for comprehensive billing and case complexity assessment.,
scheduling,operative_scheduling,surgical_case,site_marked_indicator,site_marked_indicator,Surgical Site Marked Indicator,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,Indicates whether the surgical site has been marked by the surgeon. Required by the Universal Protocol for procedures involving laterality or multiple structures. Used for pre-operative safety checklist.,
scheduling,operative_scheduling,surgical_case,specialty,specialty,Surgical Specialty,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,Medical specialty of the primary surgeon or the procedure type. More granular than service line. Used for surgeon credentialing and case mix analysis.,
scheduling,operative_scheduling,surgical_case,timeout_completed_indicator,timeout_completed_indicator,Surgical Timeout Completed Indicator,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,"Indicates whether the surgical team completed the mandatory pre-incision timeout. Timeout verifies patient identity, procedure, site, and team readiness. Required by The Joint Commission.",
scheduling,operative_scheduling,surgical_case,urgency_level,urgency_level,Case Urgency Level,STRING,,,,elective|urgent|emergent|trauma,transactional_data,Clinical urgency classification of the surgical case. Determines scheduling priority and resource allocation. Emergent cases may displace elective cases.,
scheduling,operative_scheduling,surgical_case_team,surgical_case_team_id,surgical_case_team_id,Surgical Case Team ID,BIGINT,Y,,,,association_data,Unique identifier for the surgical case team assignment record. Primary key for this entity.,
scheduling,operative_scheduling,surgical_case_team,surgical_case_id,surgical_case_id,Surgical Case ID,BIGINT,,scheduling.surgical_case.surgical_case_id,,,association_data,Reference to the surgical case for which this team member is assigned. Links to the surgical_case product.,
scheduling,operative_scheduling,surgical_case_team,surgical_employee_id,surgical_employee_id,Credentialing Verified By User ID,BIGINT,,workforce.employee.employee_id,"dbx_confidential, dbx_pii",,association_data,System user identifier of the person who verified the team members credentials and privileges for this case.,
scheduling,operative_scheduling,surgical_case_team,tertiary_employee_id,tertiary_employee_id,Cancelled By User ID,BIGINT,,workforce.employee.employee_id,"dbx_confidential, dbx_pii",,association_data,System user identifier of the person who cancelled this team member assignment.,
scheduling,operative_scheduling,surgical_case_team,training_completion_id,training_completion_id,Training Completion Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,compliance.training_completion.training_completion_id,,,association_data,"Foreign key linking to compliance.training_completion. Business justification: Surgical team members require procedure-specific training verification including scrub technique, equipment operation, and specialty certifications. Joint Commission and medical staff bylaws requireme",
scheduling,operative_scheduling,surgical_case_team,actual_end_datetime,actual_end_datetime,Actual End Date Time,TIMESTAMP,,,,,association_data,The actual date and time when the team member completed their participation in the surgical case. Used for time tracking and billing.,
scheduling,operative_scheduling,surgical_case_team,actual_start_datetime,actual_start_datetime,Actual Start Date Time,TIMESTAMP,,,,,association_data,The actual date and time when the team member began their participation in the surgical case. Used for time tracking and billing.,
scheduling,operative_scheduling,surgical_case_team,anesthesiologist_npi,anesthesiologist_npi,Anesthesiologist National Provider Identifier (NPI),STRING,,,,^[0-9]{10}$,association_data,"National Provider Identifier of the anesthesiologist or CRNA (Certified Registered Nurse Anesthetist) assigned to the case. Used for anesthesia billing and quality tracking. [Moved from surgical_case: This attribute represents the anesthesiologist clinician-case relationship. In the M:N model, this becomes a record in surgical_case_team with team_role_code=ANESTHESIOLOGIST or CRNA. The current model cannot represent cases with multiple anesthesia providers or CRNA+anesthesiologist teams.]",
scheduling,operative_scheduling,surgical_case_team,assisting_surgeon_npi,assisting_surgeon_npi,Assisting Surgeon National Provider Identifier (NPI),STRING,,,,^[0-9]{10}$,association_data,"National Provider Identifier of the assisting surgeon, if applicable. Used for billing assistant surgeon charges and documenting surgical team composition. [Moved from surgical_case: This attribute represents another specific clinician-case relationship (the assisting surgeon role). In the M:N model, this becomes a record in surgical_case_team with team_role_code=ASSISTING_SURGEON. The current model artificially limits cases to one assisting surgeon.]",
scheduling,operative_scheduling,surgical_case_team,billable_flag,billable_flag,Billable Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,association_data,"Indicates whether this team members participation is billable to the patient or payer. True if billable, False if non-billable (e.g., resident supervision, observation).",
scheduling,operative_scheduling,surgical_case_team,billing_modifier_code,billing_modifier_code,Billing Modifier Code,STRING,,,,,association_data,"CPT or HCPCS modifier code applied to this team members billing for the surgical case. Used to indicate special circumstances (e.g., assistant surgeon, co-surgeon, teaching physician).",
scheduling,operative_scheduling,surgical_case_team,board_certification_status,board_certification_status,Board Certification Status,STRING,,,,certified|not_certified|expired|pending,association_data,Current status of the team members board certification in their specialty. Used for quality reporting and credentialing.,
scheduling,operative_scheduling,surgical_case_team,call_status,call_status,Call Status,STRING,,,,scheduled|on_call|backup|emergency,association_data,"Indicates whether the team member is scheduled, on-call, backup, or responding to an emergency for this case. Used for staffing and scheduling analytics.",
scheduling,operative_scheduling,surgical_case_team,cancellation_datetime,cancellation_datetime,Cancellation Date Time,TIMESTAMP,,,,,association_data,The date and time when this team member assignment was cancelled. Null if assignment was not cancelled.,
scheduling,operative_scheduling,surgical_case_team,cancellation_reason,cancellation_reason,Cancellation Reason,STRING,,,,,association_data,"Reason why this team member assignment was cancelled. May include provider unavailability, case cancellation, or scheduling changes.",
scheduling,operative_scheduling,surgical_case_team,confirmation_datetime,confirmation_datetime,Confirmation Date Time,TIMESTAMP,,,,,association_data,The date and time when the team member confirmed their participation in the surgical case.,
scheduling,operative_scheduling,surgical_case_team,confirmation_status,confirmation_status,Confirmation Status,STRING,,,,pending|confirmed|declined|tentative,association_data,Status indicating whether the team member has confirmed their availability and commitment to participate in this surgical case.,
scheduling,operative_scheduling,surgical_case_team,conflict_description,conflict_description,Conflict Description,STRING,,,,,association_data,Detailed description of any scheduling conflict identified for this team member assignment. Includes conflicting case number or appointment details.,
scheduling,operative_scheduling,surgical_case_team,conflict_flag,conflict_flag,Scheduling Conflict Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,association_data,"Indicates whether this team member assignment has a scheduling conflict with another commitment. True if conflict exists, False otherwise.",
scheduling,operative_scheduling,surgical_case_team,created_timestamp,created_timestamp,Record Created Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,association_data,The date and time when this team member assignment record was first created in the system. Used for audit trail and data lineage.,
scheduling,operative_scheduling,surgical_case_team,credentialing_verification_datetime,credentialing_verification_datetime,Credentialing Verification Date Time,TIMESTAMP,,,,,association_data,The date and time when the team members credentials and privileges were verified for this surgical case.,
scheduling,operative_scheduling,surgical_case_team,credentialing_verified_flag,credentialing_verified_flag,Credentialing Verified Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,association_data,"Indicates whether the team members credentials and privileges have been verified for this specific surgical case. True if verified, False if not verified or pending.",
scheduling,operative_scheduling,surgical_case_team,last_modified_timestamp,last_modified_timestamp,Record Last Modified Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,association_data,The date and time when this team member assignment record was last modified. Used for audit trail and change tracking.,
scheduling,operative_scheduling,surgical_case_team,license_number,license_number,Professional License Number,STRING,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_identifier",,association_data,The professional license number of the team member. Required for regulatory compliance and credentialing verification.,
scheduling,operative_scheduling,surgical_case_team,license_state,license_state,License State Code,STRING,,,,^[A-Z]{2}$,association_data,Two-letter state code where the team members professional license was issued. Must match the facilitys state or have reciprocity agreement.,
scheduling,operative_scheduling,surgical_case_team,participation_duration_minutes,participation_duration_minutes,Participation Duration Minutes,INT,,,,,association_data,Total duration in minutes of the team members actual participation in the surgical case. Calculated from actual start and end times.,
scheduling,operative_scheduling,surgical_case_team,primary_role_flag,primary_role_flag,Primary Role Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,association_data,"Indicates whether this team member holds the primary responsibility for their role category (e.g., primary surgeon vs. assisting surgeon). True if primary, False if secondary or assisting.",
scheduling,operative_scheduling,surgical_case_team,primary_surgeon_name,primary_surgeon_name,Primary Surgeon Name,STRING,,,,,association_data,"Full name of the primary surgeon. Used for operational communication, patient information, and surgical schedule displays. [Moved from surgical_case: Denormalized display attribute derived from the primary surgeon relationship. Should be removed as it can be derived from the surgical_case_team association joined to clinician.]",
scheduling,operative_scheduling,surgical_case_team,primary_surgeon_npi,primary_surgeon_npi,Primary Surgeon National Provider Identifier (NPI),STRING,,,,^[0-9]{10}$,association_data,"National Provider Identifier of the primary surgeon responsible for the surgical case. Ten-digit unique identifier assigned by CMS. Used for credentialing, billing, and quality reporting. [Moved from surgical_case: This attribute represents one specific clinician-case relationship (the primary surgeon role). In the M:N model, this becomes a record in surgical_case_team with team_role_code=PRIMARY_SURGEON. Storing it as a single attribute on surgical_case violates normalization and prevents tracking multiple surgeons or role changes.]",
scheduling,operative_scheduling,surgical_case_team,privilege_code,privilege_code,Clinical Privilege Code,STRING,,,,,association_data,Code representing the specific clinical privilege that authorizes this team member to perform their role in this surgical case. Links to the providers credentialing and privileging records.,
scheduling,operative_scheduling,surgical_case_team,provider_assignment_notes,provider_assignment_notes,Assignment Notes,STRING,,,,,association_data,"Free-text notes regarding this team member assignment. May include special requirements, preferences, or coordination details.",
scheduling,operative_scheduling,surgical_case_team,provider_assignment_priority,provider_assignment_priority,Assignment Priority Rank,INT,,,,,association_data,Numeric priority ranking of this team member assignment relative to other assignments for the same case. Lower numbers indicate higher priority. Used for scheduling conflict resolution.,
scheduling,operative_scheduling,surgical_case_team,provider_assignment_status,provider_assignment_status,Assignment Status,STRING,,,,scheduled|confirmed|in_progress|completed|cancelled|no_show,association_data,Current status of the team member assignment. Tracks the lifecycle from scheduling through completion or cancellation.,
scheduling,operative_scheduling,surgical_case_team,quality_measure_applicable_flag,quality_measure_applicable_flag,Quality Measure Applicable Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,association_data,"Indicates whether this team member assignment is subject to quality measurement or reporting requirements. True if applicable, False otherwise.",
scheduling,operative_scheduling,surgical_case_team,replacement_team_member_npi,replacement_team_member_npi,Replacement Team Member National Provider Identifier (NPI),STRING,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_identifier",^[0-9]{10}$,association_data,The NPI of the replacement team member if this assignment was substituted. Used to track last-minute staffing changes.,
scheduling,operative_scheduling,surgical_case_team,requested_datetime,requested_datetime,Requested Date Time,TIMESTAMP,,,,,association_data,The date and time when this team member was requested for assignment to the surgical case.,
scheduling,operative_scheduling,surgical_case_team,scheduled_end_datetime,scheduled_end_datetime,Scheduled End Date Time,TIMESTAMP,,,,,association_data,The date and time when the team member is scheduled to complete their participation in the surgical case.,
scheduling,operative_scheduling,surgical_case_team,scheduled_start_datetime,scheduled_start_datetime,Scheduled Start Date Time,TIMESTAMP,,,,,association_data,The date and time when the team member is scheduled to begin their participation in the surgical case.,
scheduling,operative_scheduling,surgical_case_team,scrub_time_minutes,scrub_time_minutes,Scrub Time Minutes,INT,,,,,association_data,"Time in minutes spent by the team member in surgical scrub preparation. Applicable to scrubbed team members (surgeons, scrub techs).",
scheduling,operative_scheduling,surgical_case_team,source_system,source_system,Source System Name,STRING,,,,,association_data,"Name of the source system from which this team member assignment record originated (e.g., Epic OpTime, Cerner SurgiNet).",
scheduling,operative_scheduling,surgical_case_team,source_system_identifier,source_system_identifier,Source System Identifier,STRING,,,,,association_data,Unique identifier for this team member assignment in the source system. Used for data lineage and reconciliation.,
scheduling,operative_scheduling,surgical_case_team,specialty_code,specialty_code,Medical Specialty Code,STRING,,,,,association_data,"Code representing the medical specialty or clinical discipline of the team member (e.g., orthopedic surgery, cardiothoracic surgery, anesthesiology).",
scheduling,operative_scheduling,surgical_case_team,supervising_provider_npi,supervising_provider_npi,Supervising Provider National Provider Identifier (NPI),STRING,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_identifier",^[0-9]{10}$,association_data,"The NPI of the attending physician or supervising provider if this team member is a resident, fellow, or student. Required for teaching case billing compliance.",
scheduling,operative_scheduling,surgical_case_team,teaching_case_flag,teaching_case_flag,Teaching Case Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,association_data,"Indicates whether this is a teaching case with resident or student participation under supervision. True if teaching case, False otherwise. Impacts billing and documentation requirements.",
scheduling,operative_scheduling,surgical_case_team,team_member_name,team_member_name,Team Member Full Name,STRING,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_name",,association_data,Full legal name of the care team member assigned to this surgical case. Used for case documentation and credentialing verification.,
scheduling,operative_scheduling,surgical_case_team,team_member_npi,team_member_npi,National Provider Identifier (NPI),STRING,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_identifier",^[0-9]{10}$,association_data,The 10-digit National Provider Identifier for the team member assigned to this surgical case. Required for billing and credentialing verification.,
scheduling,operative_scheduling,surgical_case_team,team_role_code,team_role_code,Team Role Code,STRING,,,,SURGEON|CO_SURGEON|ANESTHESIOLOGIST|CRNA|SCRUB_TECH|CIRCULATING_NURSE,association_data,"Standardized code representing the role of the team member in the surgical case. Values: SURGEON (primary surgeon), CO_SURGEON (assisting surgeon), ANESTHESIOLOGIST (physician anesthesiologist), CRNA (Certified Registered Nurse Anesthetist), SCRUB_TECH (scrub technician), CIRCULATING_NURSE (circulating nurse). [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: SURGEON|CO_SURGEON|ANESTHESIOLOGIST|CRNA|SCRUB_TECH|CIRCULATING_NURSE|PERFUSIONIST|FIRST_ASSIST|SURGICAL_RESIDENT|ANESTHESIA_RESIDENT|STUDENT_NURSE — promote to reference product]",
scheduling,operative_scheduling,surgical_case_team,team_role_description,team_role_description,Team Role Description,STRING,,,,,association_data,Human-readable description of the team members role and responsibilities during the surgical case.,
scheduling,operative_scheduling,surgical_case_team,time_in_room_minutes,time_in_room_minutes,Time In Operating Room (OR) Minutes,INT,,,,,association_data,Total time in minutes that the team member spent in the operating room for this case. Used for efficiency and utilization analysis.,
scheduling,resource_capacity,capacity_utilization,capacity_utilization_id,capacity_utilization_id,Capacity Utilization Identifier,BIGINT,Y,,,,master_data,Primary key for capacity_utilization,
