billing,account_management,payment_plan,payment_employee_id,payment_employee_id,Approved By User Identifier (ID),BIGINT,,workforce.employee.employee_id,"dbx_confidential,dbx_pii,pii_pii,pii_sensitive",,master_data,"Reference to the user or staff member who approved the payment plan, typically a financial counselor, billing manager, or revenue cycle specialist.",
billing,account_management,payment_plan,tertiary_employee_id,tertiary_employee_id,Last Modified By User Identifier (ID),BIGINT,,workforce.employee.employee_id,"dbx_confidential,dbx_pii,pii_pii,pii_sensitive",,master_data,Reference to the user or system process that most recently modified the payment plan record.,
billing,account_management,payment_plan,actual_completion_date,actual_completion_date,Actual Completion Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,"Actual date when the payment plan was completed, either through full payment or early payoff. Null if plan is still active or was cancelled/defaulted.",
billing,account_management,payment_plan,agreement_signed_date,agreement_signed_date,Agreement Signed Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,Date when the payment plan agreement was signed by the patient or guarantor.,
billing,account_management,payment_plan,agreement_signed_flag,agreement_signed_flag,Agreement Signed Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,"Indicates whether the patient or guarantor has signed the payment plan agreement. True means a signed agreement is on file, false means signature is pending or not required.",
billing,account_management,payment_plan,approval_date,approval_date,Approval Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,Date when the payment plan was reviewed and approved by authorized staff.,
billing,account_management,payment_plan,auto_pay_flag,auto_pay_flag,Auto Pay Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,"Indicates whether automatic recurring payments are enabled for this payment plan. True means installments are automatically charged to the stored payment method on the due date, false means manual payment is required.",
billing,account_management,payment_plan,cancellation_date,cancellation_date,Cancellation Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,Date when the payment plan was cancelled by either the patient or the healthcare organization.,
billing,account_management,payment_plan,cancellation_reason,cancellation_reason,Cancellation Reason,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Free-text explanation of why the payment plan was cancelled, including patient request, non-compliance, account paid in full, or administrative reasons.",
billing,account_management,payment_plan,created_timestamp,created_timestamp,Created Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,master_data,Timestamp when the payment plan record was first created in the system. Represents the audit trail for record creation.,
billing,account_management,payment_plan,default_date,default_date,Default Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,Date when the payment plan was declared in default due to missed payments exceeding the grace period.,
billing,account_management,payment_plan,default_reason,default_reason,Default Reason,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Explanation of why the payment plan defaulted, such as consecutive missed payments, insufficient funds, or patient non-response.",
billing,account_management,payment_plan,down_payment_amount,down_payment_amount,Down Payment Amount,"DECIMAL(18,2)",,,,,master_data,"Initial payment made at the time of plan enrollment, if required. This amount is applied to the balance before installments begin. Expressed in USD.",
billing,account_management,payment_plan,effective_end_date,effective_end_date,Effective End Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,Scheduled date when the payment plan is expected to be completed based on the original terms. Nullable for open-ended plans.,
billing,account_management,payment_plan,effective_start_date,effective_start_date,Effective Start Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,Date when the payment plan becomes active and the first installment is due. This is the binding start date of the agreement.,
billing,account_management,payment_plan,enrollment_channel,enrollment_channel,Enrollment Channel,STRING,,,,patient_portal|phone|in_person|mail|email|mobile_app,master_data,"Channel through which the patient or guarantor enrolled in the payment plan. Patient portal indicates online self-service enrollment, phone indicates enrollment via call center, in-person indicates enrollment at a facility registration or billing desk, mail indicates paper application, email indicates enrollment via email correspondence, and mobile app indicates enrollment through a mobile application.",
billing,account_management,payment_plan,enrollment_date,enrollment_date,Enrollment Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,Date when the patient or guarantor enrolled in the payment plan.,
billing,account_management,payment_plan,finance_charge_amount,finance_charge_amount,Finance Charge Amount,"DECIMAL(18,2)",,,,,master_data,Total finance charges or interest applied to the payment plan over its lifetime. Zero for interest-free plans. Expressed in USD.,
billing,account_management,payment_plan,financial_assistance_program_code,financial_assistance_program_code,Financial Assistance Program Code,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Code identifying the financial assistance or charity care program under which this payment plan was approved, if applicable. Links to the organizations financial assistance policy and eligibility criteria.",
billing,account_management,payment_plan,grace_period_days,grace_period_days,Grace Period Days,INT,,,,,master_data,Number of days after the installment due date during which a late payment can be made without penalty or default.,
billing,account_management,payment_plan,installment_amount,installment_amount,Installment Amount,"DECIMAL(18,2)",,,,,master_data,Fixed amount due for each scheduled installment payment. Expressed in USD.,
billing,account_management,payment_plan,installment_frequency,installment_frequency,Installment Frequency,STRING,,,,weekly|biweekly|monthly|quarterly|custom,master_data,"Frequency at which installment payments are scheduled. Weekly indicates every 7 days, biweekly every 14 days, monthly on the same day each month, quarterly every 3 months, and custom indicates a non-standard schedule.",
billing,account_management,payment_plan,installments_paid,installments_paid,Installments Paid,INT,,,,,master_data,Count of installment payments that have been successfully received and posted to date.,
billing,account_management,payment_plan,installments_remaining,installments_remaining,Installments Remaining,INT,,,,,master_data,Count of installment payments still outstanding to complete the payment plan.,
billing,account_management,payment_plan,interest_rate_percentage,interest_rate_percentage,Interest Rate Percentage,"DECIMAL(5,2)",,,,,master_data,"Annual percentage rate (APR) applied to the payment plan balance, if applicable. Zero for interest-free plans. Expressed as a percentage (e.g., 5.00 for 5%).",
billing,account_management,payment_plan,last_modified_timestamp,last_modified_timestamp,Last Modified Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,master_data,Timestamp when the payment plan record was most recently updated. Represents the audit trail for record modification.,
billing,account_management,payment_plan,last_payment_amount,last_payment_amount,Last Payment Amount,"DECIMAL(18,2)",,,,,master_data,Amount of the most recent installment payment received. Expressed in USD.,
billing,account_management,payment_plan,last_payment_date,last_payment_date,Last Payment Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,Date when the most recent installment payment was received and posted.,
billing,account_management,payment_plan,late_fee_amount,late_fee_amount,Late Fee Amount,"DECIMAL(18,2)",,,,,master_data,"Standard late fee charged for each missed or late installment payment, as defined in the payment plan agreement. Expressed in USD.",
billing,account_management,payment_plan,missed_payments_count,missed_payments_count,Missed Payments Count,INT,,,,,master_data,Total number of installment payments that were missed or not received by the due date during the life of the payment plan.,
billing,account_management,payment_plan,next_payment_due_date,next_payment_due_date,Next Payment Due Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,"Date when the next scheduled installment payment is due. Null if plan is completed, cancelled, or defaulted.",
billing,account_management,payment_plan,notes,notes,Payment Plan Notes,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Free-text notes and comments related to the payment plan, including special arrangements, patient circumstances, or administrative instructions.",
billing,account_management,payment_plan,number_of_installments,number_of_installments,Number of Installments,INT,,,,,master_data,Total number of scheduled installment payments required to complete the payment plan.,
billing,account_management,payment_plan,original_balance_amount,original_balance_amount,Original Balance Amount,"DECIMAL(18,2)",,,,,master_data,Total outstanding patient balance at the time the payment plan was established. This is the starting principal amount before any plan payments are applied. Expressed in USD.,
billing,account_management,payment_plan,payment_method,payment_method,Payment Method,STRING,,,,credit_card|debit_card|ach|check|cash|money_order,master_data,"Primary payment instrument used for installment payments. Credit card and debit card indicate card-based payments, ACH (Automated Clearing House) indicates electronic bank transfer, check indicates paper check, cash indicates in-person cash payment, and money order indicates certified payment instrument.",
billing,account_management,payment_plan,plan_number,plan_number,Payment Plan Number,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Externally visible unique business identifier for the payment plan, used in patient communications and statements.",
billing,account_management,payment_plan,plan_status,plan_status,Payment Plan Status,STRING,,,,pending|active|completed|defaulted|cancelled|suspended,master_data,"Current lifecycle status of the payment plan. Pending indicates awaiting approval or first payment, active indicates plan is in good standing with payments being made, completed indicates all installments paid in full, defaulted indicates missed payments beyond grace period, cancelled indicates plan was terminated by patient or organization, suspended indicates temporarily paused by mutual agreement.",
billing,account_management,payment_plan,plan_type,plan_type,Payment Plan Type,STRING,,,,standard|interest_free|hardship|extended|short_term|custom,master_data,"Classification of the payment plan based on terms and eligibility criteria. Standard plans follow default terms, interest-free plans waive interest charges, hardship plans are for patients with demonstrated financial need, extended plans have longer durations, short-term plans are for smaller balances, and custom plans have negotiated terms.",
billing,account_management,payment_plan,remaining_balance_amount,remaining_balance_amount,Remaining Balance Amount,"DECIMAL(18,2)",,,,,master_data,Current outstanding balance on the payment plan after all payments to date have been applied. Expressed in USD.,
billing,account_management,payment_plan,total_paid_amount,total_paid_amount,Total Paid Amount,"DECIMAL(18,2)",,,,,master_data,"Cumulative sum of all payments received and applied to this payment plan to date, including down payment and all installments. Expressed in USD.",
billing,account_management,payment_plan,total_plan_amount,total_plan_amount,Total Payment Plan Amount,"DECIMAL(18,2)",,,,,master_data,"Total amount to be paid under the payment plan, including any interest, fees, or finance charges. May equal original balance for interest-free plans. Expressed in USD.",
billing,account_management,rac_audit,rac_audit_id,rac_audit_id,Recovery Audit Contractor (RAC) Audit ID,BIGINT,Y,,,,transactional_data,Unique identifier for the RAC audit record. Primary key for the rac_audit product.,
billing,account_management,rac_audit,care_site_id,care_site_id,Care Site Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,facility.care_site.care_site_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to facility.care_site. Business justification: RAC audits target specific Medicare provider numbers (facilities). Tracking the facility is essential for audit response coordination, corrective action plan implementation, and monitoring facility-sp",
billing,account_management,rac_audit,compliance_audit_id,compliance_audit_id,Compliance Audit Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,compliance.audit.audit_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to compliance.audit. Business justification: RAC audits are compliance audits conducted by Recovery Audit Contractors. Linking to compliance.audit enables unified audit finding tracking, corrective action plan management, and regulatory reportin",
billing,account_management,rac_audit,invoice_id,invoice_id,Invoice ID,BIGINT,,billing.invoice.invoice_id,,,transactional_data,Foreign key reference to the invoice or claim that was subject to audit review.,
billing,account_management,rac_audit,mpi_record_id,mpi_record_id,Patient ID,BIGINT,,patient.mpi_record.mpi_record_id,"pii_phi,pii_pii,pii_sensitive",,transactional_data,Foreign key reference to the patient whose care or billing was audited.,
billing,account_management,rac_audit,payer_id,payer_id,Payer ID,BIGINT,,insurance.payer.payer_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key reference to the insurance payer or government program that initiated or sponsored the audit (e.g., Medicare, Medicaid, commercial payer).",
billing,account_management,rac_audit,rac_employee_id,rac_employee_id,Assigned Reviewer User ID,BIGINT,,workforce.employee.employee_id,"dbx_confidential,dbx_pii,pii_pii,pii_sensitive",,transactional_data,"Internal user ID of the compliance officer, revenue cycle analyst, or HIM professional assigned to manage the audit response and resolution.",
billing,account_management,rac_audit,response_cda_document_id,response_cda_document_id,Response Cda Document Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,interoperability.cda_document.cda_document_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to interoperability.cda_document. Business justification: RAC audit response workflow: audits request clinical documentation, which is submitted as CDA documents. Tracking which CDA document was submitted in response to each audit enables audit management, r",
billing,account_management,rac_audit,tertiary_employee_id,tertiary_employee_id,Last Modified By User ID,BIGINT,,workforce.employee.employee_id,"dbx_confidential,dbx_pii,pii_pii,pii_sensitive",,transactional_data,User ID of the individual who last modified this audit record.,
billing,account_management,rac_audit,visit_id,visit_id,Visit ID,BIGINT,,encounter.visit.visit_id,,,transactional_data,Foreign key reference to the patient visit or encounter associated with the audited claim or billing record.,
billing,account_management,rac_audit,audit_notes,audit_notes,Audit Notes,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Free-text notes documenting audit details, correspondence with auditor, internal review findings, and resolution activities.",
billing,account_management,rac_audit,audit_number,audit_number,Audit Number,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,External audit reference number assigned by the auditing contractor or agency. Business identifier for tracking and correspondence.,
billing,account_management,rac_audit,audit_period_end_date,audit_period_end_date,Audit Period End Date,DATE,,,,,transactional_data,Ending date of the service period under audit review. Defines the temporal scope of claims and billing records subject to audit.,
billing,account_management,rac_audit,audit_period_start_date,audit_period_start_date,Audit Period Start Date,DATE,,,,,transactional_data,Beginning date of the service period under audit review. Defines the temporal scope of claims and billing records subject to audit.,
billing,account_management,rac_audit,audit_request_date,audit_request_date,Audit Request Date,DATE,,,,,transactional_data,Date the audit request or Additional Documentation Request (ADR) was received by the organization. Principal business event timestamp for the audit lifecycle.,
billing,account_management,rac_audit,audit_status,audit_status,Audit Status,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,Current lifecycle status of the audit. Tracks progression from initial request through resolution and closure. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: requested|in_progress|findings_issued|appeal_filed|appeal_pending|resolved|closed — 7 candidates stripped; promote to reference product],
billing,account_management,rac_audit,audit_type,audit_type,Audit Type,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Classification of the audit program. RAC (Recovery Audit Contractor), MAC (Medicare Administrative Contractor), OIG (Office of Inspector General), ZPIC (Zone Program Integrity Contractor), UPIC (Unified Program Integrity Contractor), internal compliance, payer audit, state Medicaid, or quality review. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: rac|mac|oig|zpic|upic|internal_compliance|payer_audit|state_medicaid|quality_review — 9 candidates stripped; promote to reference product]",
billing,account_management,rac_audit,claim_appeal_decision_date,claim_appeal_decision_date,Appeal Decision Date,DATE,,,,,transactional_data,"Date the appeal decision was issued by the reviewing authority (MAC, QIC, ALJ, Appeals Council, or Federal Court).",
billing,account_management,rac_audit,claim_appeal_filed_date,claim_appeal_filed_date,Appeal Filed Date,DATE,,,,,transactional_data,Date the organization filed an appeal of the audit findings. Typically must be within 120 days of determination letter for Medicare RAC audits.,
billing,account_management,rac_audit,claim_appeal_filed_flag,claim_appeal_filed_flag,Appeal Filed Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,"Indicates whether the organization filed an appeal of the audit findings. True if appeal was filed, False if no appeal.",
billing,account_management,rac_audit,claim_appeal_level,claim_appeal_level,Appeal Level,STRING,,,,redetermination|reconsideration|alj_hearing|mac_review|federal_court,transactional_data,"Current level in the Medicare appeals process. Redetermination (Level 1), Reconsideration by QIC (Level 2), ALJ Hearing (Level 3), Medicare Appeals Council Review (Level 4), Federal Court (Level 5).",
billing,account_management,rac_audit,claim_appeal_outcome_amount,claim_appeal_outcome_amount,Appeal Outcome Amount,"DECIMAL(18,2)",,,,,transactional_data,Final monetary amount after appeal resolution. May differ from original finding_amount if appeal was partially or fully favorable.,
billing,account_management,rac_audit,claim_appeal_status,claim_appeal_status,Appeal Status,STRING,,,,pending|upheld|overturned|partially_favorable|withdrawn|dismissed,transactional_data,"Current status or outcome of the appeal. Pending (under review), upheld (original finding affirmed), overturned (finding reversed), partially favorable (partial reversal), withdrawn, or dismissed.",
billing,account_management,rac_audit,compliance_resolution_status,compliance_resolution_status,Compliance Resolution Status,STRING,,,,open|corrective_action_plan_submitted|corrective_action_implemented|validated|closed,transactional_data,"Status of internal compliance remediation activities in response to audit findings. Tracks corrective action plan development, implementation, and validation.",
billing,account_management,rac_audit,contractor_jurisdiction,contractor_jurisdiction,Contractor Jurisdiction,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Geographic or organizational jurisdiction of the auditing contractor (e.g., Region A, Region B, statewide, national).",
billing,account_management,rac_audit,contractor_name,contractor_name,Audit Contractor Name,STRING,,,"dbx_pii_identifier,dbx_restricted,pii_pii,pii_sensitive",,transactional_data,"Name of the auditing organization or contractor conducting the audit (e.g., Cotiviti, Performant, HMS, or internal compliance department).",
billing,account_management,rac_audit,corrective_action_description,corrective_action_description,Corrective Action Description,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Narrative description of corrective actions taken to remediate audit findings and prevent recurrence (e.g., staff training, policy updates, system enhancements, coding review process changes).",
billing,account_management,rac_audit,corrective_action_plan_date,corrective_action_plan_date,Corrective Action Plan Date,DATE,,,,,transactional_data,Date the organization submitted or finalized a corrective action plan to address systemic issues identified in the audit.,
billing,account_management,rac_audit,created_timestamp,created_timestamp,Created Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,Timestamp when this audit record was first created in the system. Audit trail for record creation.,
billing,account_management,rac_audit,extrapolation_flag,extrapolation_flag,Extrapolation Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,"Indicates whether the auditor applied statistical extrapolation to project findings from a sample to a larger population of claims. True if extrapolation was used, False otherwise.",
billing,account_management,rac_audit,extrapolation_sample_size,extrapolation_sample_size,Extrapolation Sample Size,INT,,,,,transactional_data,"Number of claims in the statistical sample used for extrapolation, if extrapolation_flag is True.",
billing,account_management,rac_audit,extrapolation_universe_size,extrapolation_universe_size,Extrapolation Universe Size,INT,,,,,transactional_data,"Total number of claims in the population to which sample findings were extrapolated, if extrapolation_flag is True.",
billing,account_management,rac_audit,finding_amount,finding_amount,Finding Amount,"DECIMAL(18,2)",,,,,transactional_data,"Total monetary amount identified in the audit finding. Positive for overpayments (amounts owed to payer), negative for underpayments (amounts owed to provider).",
billing,account_management,rac_audit,finding_type,finding_type,Finding Type,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Classification of the audit finding. Overpayment (provider must refund), underpayment (provider owed additional payment), no finding (claim upheld), documentation deficiency, coding error, medical necessity denial, or coverage denial. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: overpayment|underpayment|no_finding|documentation_deficiency|coding_error|medical_necessity|coverage_denial — 7 candidates stripped; promote to reference product]",
billing,account_management,rac_audit,findings_issued_date,findings_issued_date,Findings Issued Date,DATE,,,,,transactional_data,"Date the auditor issued formal findings, determination letter, or demand letter communicating audit results.",
billing,account_management,rac_audit,interest_amount,interest_amount,Interest Amount,"DECIMAL(18,2)",,,,,transactional_data,Interest charges applied to overpayment amounts per statutory requirements. Calculated from date of overpayment to date of recoupment.,
billing,account_management,rac_audit,last_modified_timestamp,last_modified_timestamp,Last Modified Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,Timestamp when this audit record was last updated. Audit trail for record modification.,
billing,account_management,rac_audit,overpayment_amount,overpayment_amount,Overpayment Amount,"DECIMAL(18,2)",,,,,transactional_data,Amount determined to have been overpaid to the provider and subject to recoupment. Subset of finding_amount when finding_type is overpayment.,
billing,account_management,rac_audit,records_requested_count,records_requested_count,Records Requested Count,INT,,,,,transactional_data,"Number of medical records, claims, or billing documents requested by the auditor for review.",
billing,account_management,rac_audit,records_submitted_count,records_submitted_count,Records Submitted Count,INT,,,,,transactional_data,"Number of medical records, claims, or billing documents actually submitted to the auditor in response to the request.",
billing,account_management,rac_audit,recoupment_amount,recoupment_amount,Recoupment Amount,"DECIMAL(18,2)",,,,,transactional_data,"Actual amount recouped or offset from future payments by the payer. May differ from overpayment_amount if partial recoupment, payment plan, or appeal adjustments occurred.",
billing,account_management,rac_audit,recoupment_date,recoupment_date,Recoupment Date,DATE,,,,,transactional_data,Date the payer initiated recoupment or offset of the overpayment amount from provider payments.,
billing,account_management,rac_audit,recoupment_method,recoupment_method,Recoupment Method,STRING,,,,offset|direct_payment|installment_plan|settlement|waived,transactional_data,"Method by which the overpayment was recovered. Offset (deducted from future payments), direct payment (check or EFT), installment plan (extended payment agreement), settlement (negotiated amount), or waived.",
billing,account_management,rac_audit,response_due_date,response_due_date,Response Due Date,DATE,,,,,transactional_data,Deadline by which the organization must submit requested documentation to the auditor. Typically 45 days from ADR receipt for RAC audits.,
billing,account_management,rac_audit,response_submitted_date,response_submitted_date,Response Submitted Date,DATE,,,,,transactional_data,Date the organization submitted the requested documentation to the auditor.,
billing,account_management,rac_audit,underpayment_amount,underpayment_amount,Underpayment Amount,"DECIMAL(18,2)",,,,,transactional_data,Amount determined to have been underpaid to the provider and subject to additional reimbursement. Subset of finding_amount when finding_type is underpayment.,
