billing,revenue_cycle,billing_coverage,active_flag,active_flag,Coverage Active Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,Indicates whether this coverage is currently active and eligible for claims submission. Derived from coverage_status and verification results. True if coverage is active.,
billing,revenue_cycle,billing_coverage,authorization_required_flag,authorization_required_flag,Prior Authorization Required Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,Indicates whether this coverage requires prior authorization for certain services. True if authorization workflows must be followed.,
billing,revenue_cycle,billing_coverage,bin_number,bin_number,Bank Identification Number (BIN),STRING,,,,,master_data,Bank Identification Number used for pharmacy benefit claims routing. Six-digit number identifying the pharmacy benefit manager or payer for prescription drug coverage.,
billing,revenue_cycle,billing_coverage,coinsurance_percentage,coinsurance_percentage,Coinsurance Percentage,"DECIMAL(5,2)",,,,,master_data,"Percentage of covered service costs the patient is responsible for after the deductible is met. Expressed as a percentage (e.g., 20.00 for 20% coinsurance).",
billing,revenue_cycle,billing_coverage,consent_verification_source_system,consent_verification_source_system,Verification Source System,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Name of the system or clearinghouse used to perform the most recent eligibility verification (e.g., Change Healthcare, Availity, Epic Resolute, Cerner Revenue Cycle).",
billing,revenue_cycle,billing_coverage,coordination_of_benefits_order,coordination_of_benefits_order,Coordination of Benefits (COB) Order,STRING,,,,Primary|Secondary|Tertiary,master_data,"Priority order for this coverage when patient has multiple insurance plans. Primary coverage is billed first, secondary and tertiary follow COB rules.",
billing,revenue_cycle,billing_coverage,copay_amount,copay_amount,Copayment Amount,"DECIMAL(10,2)",,,,,master_data,Fixed dollar amount the patient must pay at the time of service for covered services under this plan. Varies by service type.,
billing,revenue_cycle,billing_coverage,coverage_status,coverage_status,Coverage Status,STRING,,,,Active|Inactive|Suspended|Terminated|Pending,master_data,Current lifecycle status of the insurance coverage record. Active indicates coverage is in force and eligible for claims.,
billing,revenue_cycle,billing_coverage,coverage_type,coverage_type,Coverage Type,STRING,,,,Medical|Dental|Vision|Pharmacy|Behavioral Health|Long-Term Care,master_data,Category of healthcare services covered by this insurance plan. A patient may have multiple coverage records for different service types.,
billing,revenue_cycle,billing_coverage,created_timestamp,created_timestamp,Record Created Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,master_data,Timestamp when this coverage record was first created in the system. Represents the initial capture of this coverage information.,
billing,revenue_cycle,billing_coverage,deductible_amount,deductible_amount,Deductible Amount,"DECIMAL(10,2)",,,,,master_data,Total annual deductible amount the patient must pay out-of-pocket before insurance begins covering costs under this plan.,
billing,revenue_cycle,billing_coverage,deductible_met_amount,deductible_met_amount,Deductible Met Amount,"DECIMAL(10,2)",,,,,master_data,Amount of the annual deductible that has been satisfied by the patient as of the most recent eligibility verification. Updated through real-time and batch eligibility checks.,
billing,revenue_cycle,billing_coverage,effective_date,effective_date,Coverage Effective Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,Date when the insurance coverage becomes active and benefits are available. Start of the benefit period.,
billing,revenue_cycle,billing_coverage,eligibility_verification_count,eligibility_verification_count,Eligibility Verification Count,INT,,,,,master_data,"Total number of eligibility verification transactions performed for this coverage record. Includes real-time, batch, and manual verifications.",
billing,revenue_cycle,billing_coverage,employer_name,employer_name,Employer Name,STRING,,,,,master_data,Name of the employer or organization sponsoring this insurance coverage. Applicable for employer-sponsored group health plans.,
billing,revenue_cycle,billing_coverage,last_modified_timestamp,last_modified_timestamp,Record Last Modified Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,master_data,Timestamp when this coverage record was most recently updated. Tracks the latest change to any field in the record.,
billing,revenue_cycle,billing_coverage,last_verification_date,last_verification_date,Last Eligibility Verification Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,"Date when eligibility for this coverage was most recently verified with the payer. Updated through real-time 270/271 transactions, manual verification, or batch processes.",
billing,revenue_cycle,billing_coverage,last_verification_method,last_verification_method,Last Eligibility Verification Method,STRING,,,,Real-Time 270/271|Manual|Batch|Portal,master_data,"Method used for the most recent eligibility verification. Real-Time 270/271 indicates automated EDI transaction, Manual indicates phone or fax verification, Batch indicates scheduled bulk verification, Portal indicates payer web portal lookup.",
billing,revenue_cycle,billing_coverage,last_verification_status,last_verification_status,Last Eligibility Verification Status,STRING,,,,Verified Active|Verified Inactive|Verification Failed|Pending,master_data,Result status of the most recent eligibility verification attempt. Verified Active indicates coverage is confirmed and active. Verification Failed indicates payer did not confirm coverage.,
billing,revenue_cycle,billing_coverage,network_status,network_status,Network Status,STRING,,,,In-Network|Out-of-Network|Both,master_data,"Indicates whether this coverage applies to in-network providers, out-of-network providers, or both. Affects reimbursement rates and patient cost-sharing.",
billing,revenue_cycle,billing_coverage,out_of_pocket_maximum,out_of_pocket_maximum,Out-of-Pocket Maximum Amount,"DECIMAL(10,2)",,,,,master_data,Maximum total amount the patient must pay out-of-pocket in a benefit period before insurance covers 100% of covered services.,
billing,revenue_cycle,billing_coverage,out_of_pocket_met_amount,out_of_pocket_met_amount,Out-of-Pocket Met Amount,"DECIMAL(10,2)",,,,,master_data,Amount of the out-of-pocket maximum that has been satisfied by the patient as of the most recent eligibility verification. Updated through real-time and batch eligibility checks.,
billing,revenue_cycle,billing_coverage,payer_response_code,payer_response_code,Payer Response Code,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Response code returned by the payer during the most recent eligibility verification. Indicates coverage status, limitations, or error conditions per HIPAA 271 transaction standards.",
billing,revenue_cycle,billing_coverage,payer_response_message,payer_response_message,Payer Response Message,STRING,,,,,master_data,Human-readable message returned by the payer during the most recent eligibility verification. Provides additional context for the response code.,
billing,revenue_cycle,billing_coverage,pcn_number,pcn_number,Processor Control Number (PCN),STRING,,,,,master_data,Processor Control Number used in conjunction with BIN for pharmacy claims routing. Identifies specific benefit plan or processing rules within the payer system.,
billing,revenue_cycle,billing_coverage,plan_year_end_date,plan_year_end_date,Plan Year End Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,End date of the plan year for this coverage. Marks the end of the benefit period before deductibles and out-of-pocket maximums reset.,
billing,revenue_cycle,billing_coverage,plan_year_start_date,plan_year_start_date,Plan Year Start Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,Start date of the plan year for this coverage. Deductibles and out-of-pocket maximums typically reset on this date annually.,
billing,revenue_cycle,billing_coverage,policy_number,policy_number,Policy Number,STRING,,,,,master_data,Unique policy identifier assigned by the insurance payer. May be the same as member_id or a separate contract identifier.,
billing,revenue_cycle,billing_coverage,referral_required_flag,referral_required_flag,Referral Required Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,Indicates whether this coverage requires a referral from a Primary Care Physician (PCP) for specialist visits. Common in HMO plans.,
billing,revenue_cycle,billing_coverage,rx_group_number,rx_group_number,Pharmacy Benefit Group Number,STRING,,,,,master_data,Group number specific to pharmacy benefits. May differ from the medical group_number for plans with separate pharmacy benefit managers.,
billing,revenue_cycle,billing_coverage,source_system,source_system,Source System,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Name of the operational system from which this coverage record originated (e.g., Epic Resolute, Cerner Revenue Cycle, MEDITECH Expanse).",
billing,revenue_cycle,billing_coverage,source_system_code,source_system_code,Source System ID,STRING,,,,,master_data,Unique identifier for this coverage record in the source operational system. Used for data lineage and reconciliation.,
billing,revenue_cycle,billing_coverage,subscriber_relationship,subscriber_relationship,Subscriber Relationship,STRING,,,,Self|Spouse|Child|Other,master_data,Relationship of the patient to the primary subscriber (policyholder). Determines dependent status and coverage rules.,
billing,revenue_cycle,billing_coverage,termination_date,termination_date,Coverage Termination Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,Date when the insurance coverage ends and benefits are no longer available. Null for open-ended active coverage.,
billing,revenue_cycle,invoice,invoice_id,invoice_id,Invoice Identifier,BIGINT,Y,,,,transactional_data,Unique identifier for the invoice record. Primary key for the invoice entity representing a professional or facility bill generated for a patient encounter or episode of care.,
billing,revenue_cycle,invoice,ar_account_id,ar_account_id,Ar Account Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,finance.ar_account.ar_account_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to finance.ar_account. Business justification: Patient invoices create AR accounts in the general ledger. Required for aging analysis, collection tracking, cash application, allowance for doubtful accounts, and GAAP-compliant revenue recognition i",
billing,revenue_cycle,invoice,billing_provider_clinician_id,billing_provider_clinician_id,,BIGINT,,provider.clinician.clinician_id,,,transactional_data,FK to provider.clinician.clinician_id,
billing,revenue_cycle,invoice,claim_id,claim_id,Claim Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,claim.claim.claim_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to claim.claim. Business justification: Invoices are billing-side representations of claims submitted to payers. Revenue cycle reconciliation, claim-to-cash tracking, and payment variance analysis require linking invoices to their correspon",
billing,revenue_cycle,invoice,clinical_order_id,clinical_order_id,,BIGINT,,order.clinical_order.clinical_order_id,,,transactional_data,foreign_key_to,
billing,revenue_cycle,invoice,compliance_audit_id,compliance_audit_id,Compliance Audit Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,compliance.audit.audit_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to compliance.audit. Business justification: Invoices selected for compliance audit sampling (RAC, MAC, internal billing audits, accreditation surveys) must link to the audit record for documentation, sample frame tracking, extrapolation calcula",
billing,revenue_cycle,invoice,cost_center_id,cost_center_id,Cost Center Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,finance.cost_center.cost_center_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to finance.cost_center. Business justification: Invoices should track responsible cost center for revenue attribution, departmental performance measurement, cost-to-collect analysis, and profitability reporting by service line or department. Requir",
billing,revenue_cycle,invoice,guarantor_id,guarantor_id,Guarantor Identifier,BIGINT,,patient.guarantor.guarantor_id,,,transactional_data,"pii_phi,pii_pii,pii_sensitive",
billing,revenue_cycle,invoice,health_plan_id,health_plan_id,Health Plan Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,insurance.health_plan.health_plan_id,"dbx_pii,dbx_restricted,pii_phi,pii_pii,pii_sensitive",,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to insurance.health_plan. Business justification: Invoices are adjudicated against specific health plan benefits, fee schedules, and coverage rules. Real-world claims processing requires plan-level detail for benefit determination, allowed amount cal",
billing,revenue_cycle,invoice,invoice_clinician_id,invoice_clinician_id,Billing Provider Identifier,BIGINT,,provider.clinician.clinician_id,,,transactional_data,Reference to the provider or organization submitting the bill. Holds the National Provider Identifier (NPI) for the billing entity on the claim form.,
billing,revenue_cycle,invoice,invoice_mpi_record_id,invoice_mpi_record_id,Patient Identifier,BIGINT,,patient.mpi_record.mpi_record_id,"pii_phi,pii_pii,pii_sensitive",,transactional_data,Reference to the patient who received services and is responsible for or associated with this invoice. Primary party for billing purposes.,
billing,revenue_cycle,invoice,mpi_record_id,mpi_record_id,,BIGINT,,patient.mpi_record.mpi_record_id,,,transactional_data,description,
billing,revenue_cycle,invoice,org_provider_id,org_provider_id,Org Provider Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,provider.org_provider.org_provider_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to provider.org_provider. Business justification: Institutional claims (UB-04 forms) are billed by organizational providers. Invoice must reference org_provider_id to identify the billing facility for hospital inpatient/outpatient claims, validate NP",
billing,revenue_cycle,invoice,post_acute_episode_id,post_acute_episode_id,Post Acute Episode Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,post_acute_care.post_acute_episode.post_acute_episode_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to post_acute_care.post_acute_episode. Business justification: Post-acute institutional claims (UB-04) are generated per episode/stay. Invoice must reference the episode for correct bill type, covered days calculation, and PDPM/PDGM grouper-based reimbursement.",Internal - LLM Generated Cross-Domain Link
billing,revenue_cycle,invoice,primary_payer_id,primary_payer_id,Primary Payer Identifier,BIGINT,,insurance.payer.payer_id,,,transactional_data,Reference to the primary insurance payer for this invoice. The first payer in the coordination of benefits sequence responsible for adjudicating the claim.,
billing,revenue_cycle,invoice,provider_location_id,provider_location_id,Provider Location Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,provider.provider_location.provider_location_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to provider.provider_location. Business justification: Place of service on claims must reference specific provider location for accurate reimbursement (facility vs non-facility rates differ significantly), network validation (location-specific contracts),",
billing,revenue_cycle,invoice,referral_order_id,referral_order_id,Referral Order Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,order.referral_order.referral_order_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to order.referral_order. Business justification: Referral orders generate separate professional service invoices; billing departments track referral-specific revenue, authorization compliance, and payer-specific referral billing rules by linking inv",
billing,revenue_cycle,invoice,tertiary_payer_id,tertiary_payer_id,Tertiary Payer Identifier,BIGINT,,insurance.payer.payer_id,,,transactional_data,"Reference to the tertiary insurance payer for this invoice. The third payer in the coordination of benefits sequence, billed after secondary payer adjudication.",
billing,revenue_cycle,invoice,visit_id,visit_id,Visit Identifier,BIGINT,,encounter.visit.visit_id,,,transactional_data,Reference to the patient visit or encounter for which this invoice was generated. Links the invoice to the clinical encounter that generated the charges.,
billing,revenue_cycle,invoice,admission_source_code,admission_source_code,Admission Source Code,STRING,,,,"^[0-9A-Z]{1,2}$",transactional_data,"Code indicating the source of the admission for facility claims. Examples: 1=Non-Healthcare Facility, 2=Clinic, 4=Transfer from Hospital, 5=Transfer from SNF, 7=Emergency Room.",
billing,revenue_cycle,invoice,admission_type_code,admission_type_code,Admission Type Code,STRING,,,,1|2|3|4|5|9,transactional_data,"Single-digit code indicating the priority of the admission for facility claims. 1=Emergency, 2=Urgent, 3=Elective, 4=Newborn, 5=Trauma, 9=Information Not Available.",
billing,revenue_cycle,invoice,allowed_amount,allowed_amount,Allowed Amount,"DECIMAL(15,2)",,,,,transactional_data,The maximum amount the payer will reimburse for the services on this invoice based on the contracted rate or fee schedule. Total charges minus contractual adjustment.,
billing,revenue_cycle,invoice,bad_debt_amount,bad_debt_amount,Bad Debt Write-Off Amount,"DECIMAL(15,2)",,,,,transactional_data,The dollar amount written off as bad debt. Represents uncollectible patient responsibility that is removed from accounts receivable and recorded as bad debt expense.,
billing,revenue_cycle,invoice,bad_debt_date,bad_debt_date,Bad Debt Write-Off Date,DATE,,,,,transactional_data,The date the outstanding balance was written off as bad debt after exhausting collection efforts. Represents the date the account was deemed uncollectible.,
billing,revenue_cycle,invoice,bill_type_code,bill_type_code,Bill Type Code,STRING,,,,^[0-9]{3}$,transactional_data,"Three-digit code on UB-04 facility claims indicating the type of facility, type of care, and billing sequence. First digit = facility type, second digit = care type, third digit = billing sequence.",
billing,revenue_cycle,invoice,claim_appeal_date,claim_appeal_date,Appeal Submission Date,DATE,,,,,transactional_data,The date an appeal was submitted to the payer for a denied or underpaid claim. Tracks the start of the appeals process in denial management workflow.,
billing,revenue_cycle,invoice,claim_appeal_status,claim_appeal_status,Appeal Status,STRING,,,,not_appealed|appeal_pending|appeal_approved|appeal_denied|appeal_partially_approved,transactional_data,Current status of the appeal process for a denied claim. Tracks whether an appeal has been filed and the outcome of the appeal.,
billing,revenue_cycle,invoice,claim_control_number,claim_control_number,Claim Control Number (CCN),STRING,,,,,transactional_data,Unique identifier assigned by the payer to track the claim through adjudication. Also known as Document Control Number (DCN) or Internal Control Number (ICN). Returned on ERA/EOB.,
billing,revenue_cycle,invoice,claim_denial_reason_code,claim_denial_reason_code,Claim Denial Reason Code,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Standardized code indicating the reason the claim was denied or rejected by the payer. Used for denial management and appeals. Examples: CO-16=Claim lacks information, PR-1=Deductible.",
billing,revenue_cycle,invoice,claim_denial_reason_description,claim_denial_reason_description,Claim Denial Reason Description,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,Human-readable description of the denial reason provided by the payer. Provides additional context beyond the denial reason code for revenue cycle staff.,
billing,revenue_cycle,invoice,clearinghouse_name,clearinghouse_name,Clearinghouse Name,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"The name of the claims clearinghouse used to transmit the claim to the payer, if applicable. Clearinghouses validate, format, and route claims to multiple payers.",
billing,revenue_cycle,invoice,collection_status,collection_status,Collection Status,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,Current status of collection efforts for outstanding patient balances. Tracks aging and escalation of unpaid patient responsibility amounts. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: current|past_due_30|past_due_60|past_due_90|past_due_120|in_collections|bad_debt|write_off — 8 candidates stripped; promote to reference product],
billing,revenue_cycle,invoice,contractual_adjustment,contractual_adjustment,Contractual Adjustment Amount,"DECIMAL(15,2)",,,,,transactional_data,The write-off amount representing the difference between billed charges and the contracted reimbursement rate with the payer. Reflects negotiated discounts per payer contracts.,
billing,revenue_cycle,invoice,covered_charges,covered_charges,Covered Charges Amount,"DECIMAL(15,2)",,,,,transactional_data,The portion of total charges that are covered by the patients insurance plan. Represents charges eligible for payer reimbursement under the coverage terms.,
billing,revenue_cycle,invoice,created_timestamp,created_timestamp,Record Created Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,The date and time this invoice record was first created in the revenue cycle system. Audit trail for record creation.,
billing,revenue_cycle,invoice,discharge_status_code,discharge_status_code,Discharge Status Code,STRING,,,,^[0-9]{2}$,transactional_data,"Two-digit code indicating the patient status at discharge for facility claims. Examples: 01=Home, 02=Transfer to Short-Term Hospital, 03=SNF, 07=Left AMA, 20=Expired, 30=Still Patient.",
billing,revenue_cycle,invoice,drg_code,drg_code,Diagnosis-Related Group (DRG) Code,STRING,,,,^[0-9]{3}$,transactional_data,Three-digit code representing the DRG assignment for facility inpatient claims. Used by Medicare and other payers for prospective payment system reimbursement. Assigned by 3M grouper software.,
billing,revenue_cycle,invoice,drg_weight,drg_weight,Diagnosis-Related Group (DRG) Weight,"DECIMAL(6,4)",,,,,transactional_data,Relative weight assigned to the DRG code reflecting the expected resource consumption for this case. Used to calculate Medicare reimbursement by multiplying the base rate by the DRG weight.,
billing,revenue_cycle,invoice,facility_service_from_date,facility_service_from_date,Service From Date,DATE,,,,,transactional_data,"The start date of the service period covered by this invoice. For single-day encounters, equals service_through_date. For multi-day stays, represents admission or first service date.",
billing,revenue_cycle,invoice,facility_service_through_date,facility_service_through_date,Service Through Date,DATE,,,,,transactional_data,"The end date of the service period covered by this invoice. For single-day encounters, equals service_from_date. For multi-day stays, represents discharge or last service date.",
billing,revenue_cycle,invoice,form_type,form_type,Claim Form Type,STRING,,,,CMS-1500|UB-04|ADA-2012|NCPDP,transactional_data,"The standardized claim form type used for this invoice. CMS-1500 for professional billing, UB-04 for facility billing, ADA-2012 for dental, NCPDP for pharmacy.",
billing,revenue_cycle,invoice,insurance_payment,insurance_payment,Insurance Payment Amount,"DECIMAL(15,2)",,,,,transactional_data,The total amount paid by the insurance payer(s) toward this invoice. Sum of all insurance payments posted from Electronic Remittance Advice (ERA) or manual payment posting.,
billing,revenue_cycle,invoice,invoice_date,invoice_date,Invoice Date,DATE,,,,,transactional_data,The date the invoice was generated and finalized for submission. Represents the formal billing document creation date.,
billing,revenue_cycle,invoice,invoice_number,invoice_number,Invoice Number,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Externally-known unique business identifier for the invoice. Used for patient communication, payer correspondence, and revenue cycle tracking. Human-readable invoice reference number.",
billing,revenue_cycle,invoice,invoice_status,invoice_status,Invoice Status,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,Current lifecycle status of the invoice in the revenue cycle management workflow. Tracks the invoice from creation through final disposition. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: draft|ready_to_bill|submitted|accepted|rejected|paid|partially_paid|denied|appealed|voided|cancelled — 11 candidates stripped; promote to reference product],
billing,revenue_cycle,invoice,invoice_type,invoice_type,Invoice Type,STRING,,,,professional|facility|institutional|ancillary|durable_medical_equipment|home_health,transactional_data,Classification of the invoice based on the type of services billed. Professional invoices use CMS-1500 form for physician services; facility invoices use UB-04 form for hospital services.,
billing,revenue_cycle,invoice,modified_timestamp,modified_timestamp,Record Modified Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,The date and time this invoice record was last modified. Audit trail for tracking changes to the invoice throughout its lifecycle.,
billing,revenue_cycle,invoice,non_covered_charges,non_covered_charges,Non-Covered Charges Amount,"DECIMAL(15,2)",,,,,transactional_data,The portion of total charges that are not covered by the patients insurance plan. Represents charges that are patient responsibility or not eligible for payer reimbursement.,
billing,revenue_cycle,invoice,outstanding_balance,outstanding_balance,Outstanding Balance Amount,"DECIMAL(15,2)",,,,,transactional_data,The remaining unpaid balance on this invoice after all payments and adjustments. Represents the current amount due from all responsible parties.,
billing,revenue_cycle,invoice,patient_payment,patient_payment,Patient Payment Amount,"DECIMAL(15,2)",,,,,transactional_data,The total amount paid by the patient toward this invoice. Sum of all patient payments including copays collected at time of service and subsequent patient payments.,
billing,revenue_cycle,invoice,patient_responsibility,patient_responsibility,Patient Responsibility Amount,"DECIMAL(15,2)",,,,,transactional_data,"The total amount the patient is responsible to pay, including deductibles, copayments, coinsurance, and non-covered charges. Calculated after insurance adjudication.",
billing,revenue_cycle,invoice,place_of_service_code,place_of_service_code,Place of Service (POS) Code,STRING,,,,^[0-9]{2}$,transactional_data,"Two-digit code on CMS-1500 professional claims identifying the location where services were rendered. Examples: 11=Office, 21=Inpatient Hospital, 22=Outpatient Hospital, 23=Emergency Room.",
billing,revenue_cycle,invoice,revenue_code,revenue_code,Revenue Code,STRING,,,,^[0-9]{4}$,transactional_data,"Four-digit code on UB-04 facility claims identifying the specific accommodation, ancillary service, or billing calculation related to the charge. Examples: 0110=Room & Board Private, 0450=Emergency Room, 0636=Drugs.",
billing,revenue_cycle,invoice,statement_date,statement_date,Patient Statement Date,DATE,,,,,transactional_data,The date a patient statement was generated and sent for this invoice. Tracks patient billing communication in the revenue cycle.,
billing,revenue_cycle,invoice,submission_date,submission_date,Claim Submission Date,DATE,,,,,transactional_data,The date the invoice was submitted to the payer as a claim. Represents when the billing document was transmitted electronically or mailed to the insurance company.,
billing,revenue_cycle,invoice,submission_method,submission_method,Claim Submission Method,STRING,,,,electronic_837|paper_mail|clearinghouse|direct_payer_portal,transactional_data,The method used to submit the claim to the payer. Electronic 837 transactions are the standard for HIPAA-compliant electronic claims submission.,
billing,revenue_cycle,invoice,total_charges,total_charges,Total Charges Amount,"DECIMAL(15,2)",,,,,transactional_data,"The total gross charges for all services on this invoice before any adjustments, discounts, or payments. Sum of all charge line items from the Charge Description Master (CDM).",
billing,revenue_cycle,invoice_coverage_billing,invoice_coverage_billing_id,invoice_coverage_billing_id,Invoice Coverage Billing - Invoice Coverage Billing Id,BIGINT,Y,,,,association_data,Primary key for the invoice_coverage_billing association,
billing,revenue_cycle,invoice_coverage_billing,billing_coverage_id,billing_coverage_id,Invoice Coverage Billing - Coverage Id,BIGINT,,billing.billing_coverage.billing_coverage_id,,,association_data,Foreign key linking to the insurance coverage to which this invoice is being billed,
billing,revenue_cycle,invoice_coverage_billing,invoice_id,invoice_id,Invoice Coverage Billing - Invoice Id,BIGINT,,billing.invoice.invoice_id,,,association_data,Foreign key linking to the invoice being submitted for payment,
billing,revenue_cycle,invoice_coverage_billing,adjudication_date,adjudication_date,Claim Adjudication Date,DATE,,,,,association_data,The date this payer completed adjudication and issued payment or denial for this invoice. Received from remittance advice (835).,
billing,revenue_cycle,invoice_coverage_billing,allowed_amount,allowed_amount,Allowed Amount,"DECIMAL(15,2)",,,,,association_data,The amount this specific payer determined as allowable for this invoice based on their contract or fee schedule. Returned in the remittance advice (835).,
billing,revenue_cycle,invoice_coverage_billing,check_eft_number,check_eft_number,Check or EFT Number,STRING,,,,,association_data,The check number or electronic funds transfer trace number for the payment received from this payer for this invoice.,
billing,revenue_cycle,invoice_coverage_billing,claim_denial_reason_code,claim_denial_reason_code,Claim Denial Reason Code,STRING,,,,,association_data,The reason code provided by this payer if the claim was denied or partially denied. Used for denial management and appeal workflows.,
billing,revenue_cycle,invoice_coverage_billing,claim_denial_reason_description,claim_denial_reason_description,Claim Denial Reason Description,STRING,,,,,association_data,Human-readable description of why this payer denied or partially denied this claim. Supports denial management and staff training.,
