claim,adjudication_resolution,claim_appeal,claim_appeal_type,claim_appeal_type,Appeal Type,STRING,,,,clinical|administrative|expedited|standard,transactional_data,Classification of the appeal based on the nature of the dispute. Clinical appeals challenge medical necessity or appropriateness of care decisions. Administrative appeals address procedural or billing errors. Expedited appeals are fast-tracked for urgent situations. Standard appeals follow normal timelines.,
claim,adjudication_resolution,claim_appeal,claim_denial_reason_code,claim_denial_reason_code,Denial Reason Code,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,The standardized code provided by the payer indicating why the claim was denied or underpaid. This is the basis for the appeal and drives the appeal strategy.,
