insurance,network_contracting,payer_contract,facility_contract_document_location,facility_contract_document_location,Contract Document Location,STRING,,,dbx_confidential,,master_data,"File path, URL, or document management system reference to the signed contract document for audit and reference purposes.",
insurance,network_contracting,payer_contract,facility_contract_name,facility_contract_name,Contract Name,STRING,,,,,master_data,Human-readable name or title of the payer contract for identification and reporting purposes.,
insurance,network_contracting,payer_contract,facility_contract_number,facility_contract_number,Contract Number,STRING,,,,,master_data,"The externally-known unique business identifier for this payer contract, used in communications with the payer and internal revenue cycle operations.",
insurance,network_contracting,payer_contract,facility_contract_status,facility_contract_status,Contract Status,STRING,,,,draft|pending_approval|active|suspended|terminated|expired,master_data,Current lifecycle status of the payer contract. Draft indicates contract under negotiation; pending approval awaiting internal or payer sign-off; active means contract is in force; suspended indicates temporary hold; terminated means contract ended before expiration; expired means contract reached its end date.,
insurance,network_contracting,payer_contract,facility_contract_type,facility_contract_type,Contract Type,STRING,,,,fee_for_service|capitation|bundled_payment|shared_savings|pay_for_performance|value_based,master_data,Classification of the reimbursement model governing this contract. Fee-for-service pays per service rendered; capitation pays a fixed amount per member per month; bundled payment covers an episode of care; shared savings rewards cost reduction; pay-for-performance (P4P) ties payment to quality metrics; value-based combines quality and cost outcomes.,
insurance,network_contracting,payer_contract,fee_schedule_reference,fee_schedule_reference,Fee Schedule Reference,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Reference identifier to the base fee schedule or rate table that governs reimbursement rates for services under this contract (e.g., Medicare Fee Schedule, custom negotiated rates).",
insurance,network_contracting,payer_contract,geographic_coverage,geographic_coverage,Geographic Coverage,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Description of the geographic region or service area covered by this contract (e.g., statewide, multi-state, specific counties).",
insurance,network_contracting,payer_contract,last_amendment_date,last_amendment_date,Last Amendment Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,Date of the most recent amendment or modification to this contract.,
insurance,network_contracting,payer_contract,network_tier,network_tier,Network Tier,STRING,,,,tier_1|tier_2|tier_3|preferred|standard|out_of_network,master_data,"The tier or level of this provider within the payers network, affecting member cost-sharing and reimbursement rates. Tier 1 typically offers lowest member cost-sharing; out-of-network highest.",
insurance,network_contracting,payer_contract,notes,notes,Contract Notes,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Free-text field for additional notes, special provisions, or operational guidance related to this payer contract.",
insurance,network_contracting,payer_contract,payment_terms_days,payment_terms_days,Payment Terms Days,INT,,,,,master_data,Number of days within which the payer is contractually obligated to remit payment after claim adjudication.,
insurance,network_contracting,payer_contract,prior_authorization_required,prior_authorization_required,Prior Authorization Required Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,Indicates whether prior authorization is required for certain services under this contract before services are rendered.,
insurance,network_contracting,payer_contract,quality_bonus_eligible,quality_bonus_eligible,Quality Bonus Eligible Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,Indicates whether this contract includes provisions for quality-based bonus payments tied to performance metrics such as Healthcare Effectiveness Data and Information Set (HEDIS) scores or Merit-based Incentive Payment System (MIPS) performance.,
insurance,network_contracting,payer_contract,quality_measure_set,quality_measure_set,Quality Measure Set,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Identifier or name of the quality measure set or program used to evaluate performance under this contract (e.g., HEDIS, MIPS, hospital-acquired infection rates).",
insurance,network_contracting,payer_contract,quality_penalty_eligible,quality_penalty_eligible,Quality Penalty Eligible Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,Indicates whether this contract includes provisions for quality-based penalties or payment reductions for failure to meet performance thresholds.,
insurance,network_contracting,payer_contract,reconciliation_frequency,reconciliation_frequency,Reconciliation Frequency,STRING,,,,monthly|quarterly|semi_annually|annually|none,master_data,"The frequency at which financial reconciliation and settlement occurs between provider and payer for shared savings, risk adjustments, or quality bonuses.",
insurance,network_contracting,payer_contract,regulatory_filing_reference,regulatory_filing_reference,Regulatory Filing Reference Number,STRING,,,,,master_data,Reference number or identifier assigned by the regulatory body for this contracts filing or approval.,
insurance,network_contracting,payer_contract,regulatory_filing_required,regulatory_filing_required,Regulatory Filing Required Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,Indicates whether this contract must be filed with state insurance departments or other regulatory bodies for approval or compliance purposes.,
insurance,network_contracting,payer_contract,reimbursement_method,reimbursement_method,Reimbursement Method,STRING,,,,,master_data,The calculation method used to determine payment amounts. Percent of charges pays a percentage of billed charges; percent of Medicare pays a percentage of Medicare rates; flat rate is a fixed amount per service; per diem is a daily rate; case rate is a fixed amount per case; DRG-based uses Diagnosis-Related Group rates; capitation is a fixed per-member-per-month amount. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: percent_of_charges|percent_of_medicare|flat_rate|per_diem|case_rate|drg_based|capitation — 7 candidates stripped; promote to reference product],
insurance,network_contracting,payer_contract,renewal_notice_days,renewal_notice_days,Renewal Notice Days,INT,,,,,master_data,Number of days advance notice required to terminate or renegotiate the contract before auto-renewal occurs.,
insurance,network_contracting,payer_contract,risk_arrangement_type,risk_arrangement_type,Risk Arrangement Type,STRING,,,,no_risk|upside_only|downside_only|two_sided_risk|full_risk,master_data,Defines the financial risk-sharing model between provider and payer. No risk means traditional fee-for-service; upside only allows provider to share in savings; downside only exposes provider to penalties; two-sided risk includes both savings and penalties; full risk transfers all financial risk to provider.,
insurance,network_contracting,payer_contract,source_system,source_system,Source System,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Identifier of the source system from which this payer contract record originated (e.g., Epic Resolute, Cerner Revenue Cycle, contract management system).",
insurance,network_contracting,payer_contract,state_code,state_code,State Code,STRING,,,,,master_data,Two-letter state code indicating the primary state jurisdiction for this contract.,
insurance,network_contracting,payer_contract,stop_loss_threshold_amount,stop_loss_threshold_amount,Stop-Loss Threshold Amount,"DECIMAL(15,2)",,,,,master_data,"The dollar amount threshold above which stop-loss or reinsurance provisions apply, protecting the provider or payer from catastrophic claims costs. Null if no stop-loss provision exists.",
insurance,network_contracting,payer_contract,termination_date,termination_date,Contract Termination Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,The date on which this payer contract ends or is scheduled to end. Null for open-ended contracts or contracts with auto-renewal.,
insurance,network_contracting,payer_contract,timely_filing_limit_days,timely_filing_limit_days,Timely Filing Limit Days,INT,,,,,master_data,Number of days from date of service within which claims must be submitted to the payer to be considered timely filed and eligible for reimbursement.,
insurance,network_contracting,payer_contract,updated_by,updated_by,Record Updated By User,STRING,,,,,master_data,User identifier or name of the person who last updated this payer contract record.,
insurance,network_contracting,payer_contract,updated_timestamp,updated_timestamp,Record Updated Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,master_data,Timestamp when this payer contract record was last modified in the system.,
insurance,network_contracting,plan_network,plan_network_id,plan_network_id,Plan Network ID,BIGINT,Y,,,,association_data,Unique identifier for the plan-network association record. Primary key.,
insurance,network_contracting,plan_network,health_plan_id,health_plan_id,Health Plan ID,BIGINT,,insurance.health_plan.health_plan_id,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii",,association_data,Identifier of the health plan participating in this network association. Links to the health plan master record.,
insurance,network_contracting,plan_network,provider_network_id,provider_network_id,Provider Network ID,BIGINT,,insurance.provider_network.provider_network_id,,,association_data,Identifier of the provider network associated with this plan. Links to the provider network master record.,
insurance,network_contracting,plan_network,superseded_plan_network_id,superseded_plan_network_id,Superseded Plan Network Id,BIGINT,,insurance.plan_network.plan_network_id,dbx_self_ref_fk,,association_data,Self-referencing FK on plan_network (superseded_plan_network_id),
insurance,network_contracting,plan_network,auto_assignment_eligible,auto_assignment_eligible,Auto Assignment Eligible Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,association_data,Indicates whether members can be automatically assigned to providers within this network when no explicit selection is made. Used in HMO (Health Maintenance Organization) and POS (Point of Service) plan configurations.,
insurance,network_contracting,plan_network,claims_processing_priority,claims_processing_priority,Claims Processing Priority,INT,,,,,association_data,Priority level for processing claims from this network within the plan. Lower numbers indicate higher priority for adjudication workflows.,
insurance,network_contracting,plan_network,coinsurance_percentage,coinsurance_percentage,Coinsurance Percentage,"DECIMAL(5,2)",,,,,association_data,"Default coinsurance percentage that members pay for services within this network under the plan. Expressed as a percentage (e.g., 20.00 for 20% member responsibility).",
insurance,network_contracting,plan_network,copay_tier_code,copay_tier_code,Copay Tier Code,STRING,,,,,association_data,Code identifying the copayment tier structure applicable to this network within the plan. Links to benefit copay schedules for member cost-sharing calculations.,
insurance,network_contracting,plan_network,county_code,county_code,County Code,STRING,,,,^[0-9]{5}$,association_data,Five-digit FIPS county code for granular geographic applicability of the plan-network association.,
insurance,network_contracting,plan_network,created_timestamp,created_timestamp,Created Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,association_data,Timestamp when this plan-network association record was first created in the system. Used for audit trails and data lineage tracking.,
insurance,network_contracting,plan_network,deductible_applies,deductible_applies,Deductible Applies Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,association_data,Indicates whether the plan deductible applies to services rendered within this network. Some plan designs waive deductibles for preferred network tiers.,
insurance,network_contracting,plan_network,effective_date,effective_date,Effective Date,DATE,,,,,association_data,Date when this plan-network association becomes active and available to plan members for benefit determination.,
insurance,network_contracting,plan_network,facility_contract_number,facility_contract_number,Network Contract Number,STRING,,,dbx_confidential,,association_data,Contract or agreement number governing the relationship between the health plan and the provider network. Used for contract management and financial reconciliation.,
insurance,network_contracting,plan_network,filing_reference_number,filing_reference_number,Regulatory Filing Reference Number,STRING,,,,,association_data,Reference number assigned by the regulatory authority for the filing of this plan-network association. Used for compliance tracking and audit trails.,
insurance,network_contracting,plan_network,geographic_region,geographic_region,Geographic Region,STRING,,,,,association_data,"Geographic region or service area where this network is applicable for the plan. May include state, county, or custom region codes.",
insurance,network_contracting,plan_network,member_communication_required,member_communication_required,Member Communication Required Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,association_data,Indicates whether plan members must be notified about this network association or changes to it. Used for regulatory compliance with member notification requirements.,
insurance,network_contracting,plan_network,network_adequacy_certification_date,network_adequacy_certification_date,Network Adequacy Certification Date,DATE,,,,,association_data,Date when network adequacy certification was granted for this plan-network association. Used for regulatory reporting and compliance tracking.,
insurance,network_contracting,plan_network,network_adequacy_certified,network_adequacy_certified,Network Adequacy Certified Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,association_data,Indicates whether this network has been certified as meeting network adequacy standards for the plan service area. Required for CMS (Centers for Medicare and Medicaid Services) and state regulatory compliance.,
insurance,network_contracting,plan_network,network_priority,network_priority,Network Priority Rank,INT,,,,,association_data,Numeric priority ranking of this network within the plan when multiple networks are available. Lower numbers indicate higher priority for benefit determination.,
insurance,network_contracting,plan_network,network_role,network_role,Network Role,STRING,,,,primary|secondary|tertiary|out_of_area|specialty|behavioral_health,association_data,"Role or function of this network within the plan structure. Indicates whether the network serves as the primary, secondary, or specialized network for plan members.",
insurance,network_contracting,plan_network,network_tier,network_tier,Network Tier Designation,STRING,,,,tier_1|tier_2|tier_3|preferred|standard|out_of_network,association_data,Tier designation of the network within the plan benefit structure. Determines member cost-sharing levels and benefit coverage percentages.,
insurance,network_contracting,plan_network,network_type,network_type,Network Type,STRING,,,,,association_data,"Type of network model used in this plan-network association. HMO (Health Maintenance Organization), PPO (Preferred Provider Organization), EPO (Exclusive Provider Organization), POS (Point of Service), HDHP (High Deductible Health Plan). [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: hmo|ppo|epo|pos|hdhp|medicare_advantage|medicaid_managed_care — 7 candidates stripped; promote to reference product]",
insurance,network_contracting,plan_network,notes,notes,Association Notes,STRING,,,,,association_data,"Free-text notes or comments about this plan-network association. Used for documenting special configurations, exceptions, or business context.",
insurance,network_contracting,plan_network,out_of_network_coverage,out_of_network_coverage,Out of Network Coverage Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,association_data,Indicates whether the plan provides any coverage for services rendered by providers outside this network. Supports PPO (Preferred Provider Organization) and POS (Point of Service) plan designs.,
insurance,network_contracting,plan_network,out_of_pocket_max_applies,out_of_pocket_max_applies,Out of Pocket Maximum Applies Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,association_data,Indicates whether member cost-sharing for services in this network counts toward the plan out-of-pocket maximum. Critical for Affordable Care Act (ACA) compliance.,
insurance,network_contracting,plan_network,pcp_selection_required,pcp_selection_required,Primary Care Physician (PCP) Selection Required Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,association_data,Indicates whether members enrolled in this plan-network combination must select a Primary Care Physician (PCP) from the network.,
insurance,network_contracting,plan_network,plan_network_status,plan_network_status,Association Status,STRING,,,,active|inactive|pending|suspended|terminated,association_data,Current lifecycle status of the plan-network association. Indicates whether the association is currently in effect for benefit determination and claim adjudication.,
insurance,network_contracting,plan_network,referral_required,referral_required,Referral Required Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,association_data,Indicates whether specialist referrals are required for members using this network under the plan. Common in HMO (Health Maintenance Organization) configurations.,
insurance,network_contracting,plan_network,regulatory_filing_required,regulatory_filing_required,Regulatory Filing Required Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,association_data,Indicates whether this plan-network association requires filing with state insurance departments or CMS (Centers for Medicare and Medicaid Services) for approval.,
insurance,network_contracting,plan_network,reimbursement_method,reimbursement_method,Reimbursement Method,STRING,,,,fee_for_service|capitation|bundled_payment|value_based|drg|per_diem,association_data,"Primary reimbursement methodology used for providers in this network under the plan. DRG (Diagnosis-Related Group) for inpatient, fee-for-service, capitation, or value-based arrangements.",
insurance,network_contracting,plan_network,source_system,source_system,Source System,STRING,,,,,association_data,Name or code of the source system from which this plan-network association was ingested. Supports data lineage and reconciliation processes.,
insurance,network_contracting,plan_network,state_code,state_code,State Code,STRING,,,,^[A-Z]{2}$,association_data,Two-letter state code where this plan-network association is active. Supports multi-state plan configurations.,
insurance,network_contracting,plan_network,termination_date,termination_date,Termination Date,DATE,,,,,association_data,Date when this plan-network association ends. Null indicates an open-ended association with no planned termination.,
insurance,network_contracting,plan_network,updated_by,updated_by,Updated By User,STRING,,,,,association_data,Identifier of the user or system process that last updated this record. Supports audit trail requirements and change management.,
insurance,network_contracting,plan_network,updated_timestamp,updated_timestamp,Updated Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,association_data,Timestamp when this plan-network association record was last modified. Used for change tracking and audit compliance.,
insurance,network_contracting,provider_network,provider_network_id,provider_network_id,Provider Network ID,BIGINT,Y,,,,master_data,Unique identifier for the provider network. Primary key.,
insurance,network_contracting,provider_network,parent_provider_network_id,parent_provider_network_id,Parent Provider Network Id,BIGINT,,insurance.provider_network.provider_network_id,dbx_self_ref_fk,,master_data,Self-referencing FK on provider_network (parent_provider_network_id),
insurance,network_contracting,provider_network,payer_id,payer_id,Payer ID,BIGINT,,insurance.payer.payer_id,,,master_data,Identifier of the payer or health plan that owns and manages this provider network.,
insurance,network_contracting,provider_network,accepting_new_patients_flag,accepting_new_patients_flag,Accepting New Patients Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,Indicates whether the network as a whole has capacity to accept new members. True if sufficient providers are accepting new patients. False if network is at capacity. Used for enrollment management.,
insurance,network_contracting,provider_network,adequacy_review_date,adequacy_review_date,Network Adequacy Review Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,Date of the most recent network adequacy assessment by CMS or state regulators. Networks must be reviewed annually or when material changes occur.,
insurance,network_contracting,provider_network,behavioral_health_included_flag,behavioral_health_included_flag,Behavioral Health Included Flag,BOOLEAN,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii",,master_data,Indicates whether this network includes behavioral health and mental health providers. True if behavioral health services are covered. False if behavioral health is carved out to a separate network.,
insurance,network_contracting,provider_network,cms_approval_date,cms_approval_date,CMS (Centers for Medicare and Medicaid Services) Approval Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,Date when CMS approved the network adequacy filing. Null if not yet approved or not required.,
insurance,network_contracting,provider_network,cms_filing_date,cms_filing_date,CMS (Centers for Medicare and Medicaid Services) Filing Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,Date when the network adequacy filing was submitted to CMS. Required for Medicare Advantage and Marketplace plans.,
insurance,network_contracting,provider_network,cms_filing_status,cms_filing_status,CMS (Centers for Medicare and Medicaid Services) Filing Status,STRING,,,,filed|approved|rejected|pending|not_required,master_data,Status of the network adequacy filing with CMS for Medicare Advantage or Marketplace plans. Filed indicates submission. Approved indicates CMS acceptance. Rejected indicates CMS denial. Pending indicates under CMS review. Not required for non-CMS regulated plans.,
insurance,network_contracting,provider_network,created_timestamp,created_timestamp,Created Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,master_data,Date and time when this provider network record was first created in the system. Used for audit trail and data lineage.,
insurance,network_contracting,provider_network,credentialing_standard,credentialing_standard,Credentialing Standard,STRING,,,,NCQA|URAC|AAAHC|TJC|state_specific|internal,master_data,Accreditation or regulatory standard used for provider credentialing in this network. NCQA (National Committee for Quality Assurance) is most common. URAC is utilization review accreditation. AAAHC (Accreditation Association for Ambulatory Health Care) for ambulatory settings. TJC (The Joint Commission) for hospitals. State-specific for state-mandated standards. Internal for payer-defined standards.,
insurance,network_contracting,provider_network,dental_network_included_flag,dental_network_included_flag,Dental Network Included Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,Indicates whether this network includes dental providers or if dental benefits are managed separately. True if dental is included. False if dental is carved out.,
insurance,network_contracting,provider_network,directory_last_updated_date,directory_last_updated_date,Directory Last Updated Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,Date when the provider directory was last updated with current network participation information. CMS requires directories to be updated at least monthly.,
insurance,network_contracting,provider_network,effective_date,effective_date,Network Effective Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,Date when the provider network becomes active and available for member enrollment and claim adjudication. Must align with plan year or regulatory approval dates.,
insurance,network_contracting,provider_network,facility_contract_type,facility_contract_type,Contract Type,STRING,,,,fee_for_service|capitation|shared_savings|bundled_payment|value_based|hybrid,master_data,Payment model used for provider contracts in this network. Fee-for-service pays per service. Capitation pays per member per month. Shared savings shares cost savings with providers. Bundled payment pays fixed amount for episode of care. Value-based ties payment to quality and outcomes. Hybrid combines multiple models.,
insurance,network_contracting,provider_network,facility_count,facility_count,Facility Count,INT,,,,,master_data,"Total number of facilities (hospitals, clinics, surgery centers, imaging centers) participating in this network. Used for network adequacy assessment and member communications.",
insurance,network_contracting,provider_network,facility_service_area_type,facility_service_area_type,Service Area Type,STRING,,,,statewide|regional|county|zip_code|msa|national,master_data,Classification of the geographic service area scope. Statewide covers entire state. Regional covers multiple counties or regions. County covers specific counties. ZIP code covers specific ZIP codes. MSA (Metropolitan Statistical Area) covers census-defined metro areas. National covers multiple states or entire country.,
insurance,network_contracting,provider_network,geographic_service_area,geographic_service_area,Geographic Service Area,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Geographic region where the provider network operates, defined by state, county, ZIP code, or metropolitan statistical area. Used for network adequacy assessment and member eligibility determination.",
insurance,network_contracting,provider_network,legacy_parent_network_code,legacy_parent_network_code,Parent Network ID,BIGINT,,,,,master_data,Identifier of the parent or umbrella network if this network is a subset or regional variant. Used for hierarchical network structures where a national network has regional sub-networks. Null for top-level networks.,
insurance,network_contracting,provider_network,network_adequacy_status,network_adequacy_status,Network Adequacy Status,STRING,,,,adequate|inadequate|pending_review|conditionally_adequate|exempt,master_data,"Assessment of whether the provider network meets regulatory standards for provider availability, geographic access, and appointment wait times. Adequate networks meet all standards. Inadequate networks require corrective action. Conditionally adequate networks meet standards with exceptions.",
insurance,network_contracting,provider_network,network_description,network_description,Network Description,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Detailed description of the provider network, including key features, geographic coverage, specialty availability, and member benefits. Used in plan marketing materials and member communications.",
insurance,network_contracting,provider_network,network_directory_url,network_directory_url,Network Directory URL (Uniform Resource Locator),STRING,,,,,master_data,Web address of the online provider directory for this network. Members use this to search for in-network providers. Required by CMS for Medicare Advantage and Marketplace plans.,
insurance,network_contracting,provider_network,network_identifier_code,network_identifier_code,Network Identifier,STRING,,,network_id=network_id,,master_data,Unique business code identifying this provider network for cross-system reference and plan-network linkage.,
insurance,network_contracting,provider_network,network_model,network_model,Network Model,STRING,,,,staff_model|group_model|network_model|IPA|direct_contract|rental_network,master_data,Organizational structure of the provider network. Staff model employs providers directly. Group model contracts with multi-specialty groups. Network model contracts with multiple IPAs. IPA (Independent Practice Association) is a physician-owned network. Direct contract is payer-to-provider agreements. Rental network leases access to another payers network.,
insurance,network_contracting,provider_network,network_name,network_name,Network Name,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Human-readable name of the provider network, used in member communications, plan documents, and provider directories.",
insurance,network_contracting,provider_network,network_status,network_status,Network Status,STRING,,,,active|inactive|pending|suspended|terminated,master_data,Current lifecycle status of the provider network. Active networks are available for member enrollment and claim adjudication. Pending networks are under development or regulatory review. Suspended networks are temporarily unavailable. Terminated networks are closed and no longer accepting new members.,
insurance,network_contracting,provider_network,network_tier,network_tier,Network Tier,STRING,,,,preferred|standard|out_of_network|tier_1|tier_2|tier_3,master_data,Tier classification of the network for cost-sharing purposes. Preferred or Tier 1 networks offer lowest member cost-sharing. Standard or Tier 2 networks have moderate cost-sharing. Out-of-network or Tier 3 have highest cost-sharing. Used in tiered network benefit designs.,
insurance,network_contracting,provider_network,network_type,network_type,Network Type,STRING,,,,,master_data,Classification of the provider network structure. HMO (Health Maintenance Organization) requires PCP referrals and in-network care. PPO (Preferred Provider Organization) allows out-of-network care at higher cost. EPO (Exclusive Provider Organization) requires in-network care except emergencies. POS (Point of Service) combines HMO and PPO features. ACO (Accountable Care Organization) is a value-based network. Narrow network limits provider choice for lower premiums. Tiered network assigns cost-sharing levels by provider performance. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: HMO|PPO|EPO|POS|ACO|narrow_network|tiered_network|exclusive_network|open_network — 9 candidates stripped; promote to reference product],
insurance,network_contracting,provider_network,pcp_count,pcp_count,Primary Care Physician (PCP) Count,INT,,,,,master_data,Total number of primary care physicians in this network. Critical metric for HMO and POS networks that require PCP selection. Used for network adequacy assessment.,
insurance,network_contracting,provider_network,pharmacy_network_included_flag,pharmacy_network_included_flag,Pharmacy Network Included Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,Indicates whether this network includes pharmacy providers or if pharmacy benefits are managed separately. True if pharmacy is included. False if pharmacy is carved out.,
insurance,network_contracting,provider_network,provider_count,provider_count,Provider Count,INT,,,,,master_data,"Total number of individual providers (physicians, specialists, allied health professionals) participating in this network. Used for network adequacy assessment and member communications.",
insurance,network_contracting,provider_network,quality_tier_methodology,quality_tier_methodology,Quality Tier Methodology,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Description of the methodology used to assign providers to quality or performance tiers within this network. May reference HEDIS measures, patient satisfaction scores, cost efficiency, or clinical outcomes. Used in tiered network designs.",
insurance,network_contracting,provider_network,recredentialing_cycle_months,recredentialing_cycle_months,Recredentialing Cycle Months,INT,,,,,master_data,Number of months between provider recredentialing reviews. Typically 24 or 36 months per NCQA standards. Used to schedule provider credential verification and quality reviews.,
insurance,network_contracting,provider_network,risk_arrangement,risk_arrangement,Risk Arrangement,STRING,,,,full_risk|shared_risk|upside_only|downside_risk|no_risk,master_data,Financial risk-sharing arrangement between payer and network providers. Full risk transfers all financial risk to providers. Shared risk splits risk between payer and providers. Upside only allows providers to share savings but not losses. Downside risk requires providers to cover losses. No risk is traditional fee-for-service.,
insurance,network_contracting,provider_network,source_system,source_system,Source System,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Name of the operational system that is the source of record for this provider network. May be Epic, Cerner, proprietary payer system, or network management platform.",
insurance,network_contracting,provider_network,specialist_count,specialist_count,Specialist Count,INT,,,,,master_data,Total number of specialist physicians in this network. Used for network adequacy assessment and member communications.,
insurance,network_contracting,provider_network,telehealth_enabled_flag,telehealth_enabled_flag,Telehealth Enabled Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,Indicates whether this network includes telehealth or virtual care providers. True if telehealth services are available. False if only in-person care is covered.,
insurance,network_contracting,provider_network,termination_date,termination_date,Network Termination Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,Date when the provider network is terminated and no longer available for new member enrollment. Existing members may have a transition period. Null for open-ended networks.,
