insurance,plan_management,benefit,coinsurance_percentage,coinsurance_percentage,Coinsurance Percentage,"DECIMAL(5,2)",,,,,master_data,"Percentage of allowed amount the member pays after deductible is met. Expressed as percentage (e.g., 20.00 for 20%). Null if benefit uses copay instead of coinsurance.",
insurance,plan_management,benefit,copay_amount,copay_amount,Copayment (Copay) Amount,"DECIMAL(10,2)",,,,,master_data,Fixed dollar amount the member pays per service or visit as defined by the benefit. Null if benefit uses coinsurance instead of copay.,
insurance,plan_management,benefit,cost_sharing_tier,cost_sharing_tier,Cost Sharing Tier,STRING,,,,bronze|silver|gold|platinum,master_data,Actuarial value tier of the benefit indicating the percentage of costs the plan covers on average. Used for ACA marketplace plans.,
insurance,plan_management,benefit,coverage_percentage,coverage_percentage,Coverage Percentage,"DECIMAL(5,2)",,,,,master_data,"Percentage of allowed amount the plan pays for this benefit. Expressed as percentage (e.g., 80.00 for 80% plan payment). Inverse of coinsurance_percentage.",
insurance,plan_management,benefit,created_timestamp,created_timestamp,Benefit Record Created Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,master_data,Timestamp when this benefit record was first created in the system. Used for audit trail and data lineage tracking.,
insurance,plan_management,benefit,day_limit_count,day_limit_count,Day Limit Count,INT,,,,,master_data,"Maximum number of days covered per benefit period for services measured in days (e.g., 90 days skilled nursing facility per benefit period). Null if no day limit applies.",
insurance,plan_management,benefit,day_limit_period,day_limit_period,Day Limit Period,STRING,,,,per_admission|per_year|per_lifetime,master_data,"Time period over which the day limit count applies. Example: per_admission for inpatient stays, per_year for annual day limits.",
insurance,plan_management,benefit,days_supply_limit,days_supply_limit,Days Supply Limit,INT,,,,,master_data,"Maximum number of days supply allowed per prescription fill for pharmacy benefits. Common limits are 30, 60, or 90 days. Null if not applicable.",
insurance,plan_management,benefit,deductible_applies_flag,deductible_applies_flag,Deductible Applies Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,"Indicates whether the plan deductible must be met before this benefit pays. True if deductible applies, False if benefit is not subject to deductible (e.g., preventive services).",
insurance,plan_management,benefit,diagnosis_code_type,diagnosis_code_type,Diagnosis Code Type,STRING,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_health",ICD10CM|ICD9CM,master_data,Type of diagnosis coding system used for medical necessity determination and benefit eligibility. ICD-10-CM is current standard in US; ICD-9-CM is legacy.,
insurance,plan_management,benefit,dollar_limit_amount,dollar_limit_amount,Dollar Limit Amount,"DECIMAL(12,2)",,,,,master_data,Maximum dollar amount the plan will pay for this benefit per limit period. Null if no dollar limit applies. Note: ACA prohibits lifetime and annual dollar limits on essential health benefits.,
insurance,plan_management,benefit,dollar_limit_period,dollar_limit_period,Dollar Limit Period,STRING,,,,per_visit|per_day|per_year|per_lifetime,master_data,Time period over which the dollar limit amount applies. Used for non-essential benefits where dollar limits are permitted.,
insurance,plan_management,benefit,effective_date,effective_date,Benefit Effective Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,Date when this benefit component becomes active and available for coverage. Must align with plan year or mid-year plan changes.,
