provider,workforce_identity,org_provider,accreditation_body,accreditation_body,Accreditation Body,STRING,,,,,master_data,"The accrediting organization that granted the current accreditation status (e.g., The Joint Commission (TJC), DNV GL Healthcare, Healthcare Facilities Accreditation Program (HFAP), Accreditation Association for Ambulatory Health Care (AAAHC)). [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: TJC|DNV_GL|HFAP|AAAHC|ACHC|CARF|URAC|none — 8 candidates stripped; promote to reference product]",
provider,workforce_identity,org_provider,accreditation_expiration_date,accreditation_expiration_date,Accreditation Expiration Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,The date on which the current accreditation certificate expires. Used to trigger renewal workflows and monitor compliance with accreditation maintenance requirements.,
provider,workforce_identity,org_provider,accreditation_status,accreditation_status,Accreditation Status,STRING,,,,accredited|provisional|not_accredited|under_review|revoked,master_data,"Current accreditation status of the organizational provider as granted by a recognized accrediting body (e.g., The Joint Commission, DNV GL, HFAP, AAAHC). Accreditation is required for Medicare deemed status and quality program participation.",
provider,workforce_identity,org_provider,address_line1,address_line1,Primary Service Address Line 1,STRING,,,"dbx_confidential, dbx_pii_address",,master_data,"The primary street address of the organizational providers physical service location. Used for claims billing, provider directory, and regulatory correspondence.",
provider,workforce_identity,org_provider,address_line2,address_line2,Primary Service Address Line 2,STRING,,,"dbx_confidential, dbx_pii_address",,master_data,"Secondary address information (suite, floor, building) for the organizational providers physical service location.",
provider,workforce_identity,org_provider,bed_count,bed_count,Licensed Bed Count,INT,,,,,master_data,"The total number of licensed inpatient beds at the facility as reported to the state Department of Health and CMS. Used for capacity planning, DRG-based reimbursement analysis, and regulatory reporting. Applicable to inpatient facilities; null for outpatient-only organizations.",
provider,workforce_identity,org_provider,city,city,Service Location City,STRING,,,"dbx_confidential, dbx_pii_address",,master_data,"City of the organizational providers primary service location. Used for geographic network analysis, provider directory, and regulatory reporting.",
provider,workforce_identity,org_provider,cms_certification_number,cms_certification_number,CMS Certification Number (CCN),STRING,,,dbx_confidential,^[0-9]{6}$,master_data,The 6-digit CMS Certification Number (formerly Medicare Provider Number) assigned to certified healthcare facilities by CMS. Required for Medicare and Medicaid participation and cost reporting.,
provider,workforce_identity,org_provider,county,county,Service Location County,STRING,,,,,master_data,"County of the organizational providers primary service location. Used for population health management, HRSA Health Professional Shortage Area (HPSA) designation, and rural health program eligibility.",
provider,workforce_identity,org_provider,created_timestamp,created_timestamp,Record Created Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,master_data,"The timestamp when the organizational provider record was first created in the system of record. Supports audit trail, data lineage, and HIPAA audit log requirements.",
provider,workforce_identity,org_provider,credentialing_expiration_date,credentialing_expiration_date,Credentialing Expiration Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,The date on which the organizational providers current credentialing cycle expires. Triggers re-credentialing workflows in Symplr to maintain uninterrupted network participation and claims payment eligibility.,
provider,workforce_identity,org_provider,credentialing_status,credentialing_status,Organizational Credentialing Status,STRING,,,,credentialed|pending|expired|revoked|not_applicable,master_data,Current credentialing status of the organizational provider as maintained in the credentialing system (Symplr). Tracks whether the organization has completed payer and network credentialing requirements for participation.,
provider,workforce_identity,org_provider,critical_access_hospital_flag,critical_access_hospital_flag,Critical Access Hospital (CAH) Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,"Indicates whether the facility holds Critical Access Hospital (CAH) designation from CMS, qualifying it for cost-based Medicare reimbursement. CAH designation requires rural location, 25 or fewer acute care beds, and 24/7 emergency services.",
provider,workforce_identity,org_provider,disproportionate_share_flag,disproportionate_share_flag,Disproportionate Share Hospital (DSH) Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,"Indicates whether the facility qualifies for CMS Disproportionate Share Hospital (DSH) payment adjustments, which compensate hospitals serving a high proportion of low-income and Medicaid patients.",
provider,workforce_identity,org_provider,doing_business_as_name,doing_business_as_name,Doing Business As (DBA) Name,STRING,,,,,master_data,The trade or operating name under which the organization conducts business if different from the legal name. Commonly used in patient-facing communications and signage.,
provider,workforce_identity,org_provider,effective_date,effective_date,Provider Effective Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,The date on which the organizational provider record became effective and the organization was authorized to participate in applicable programs and networks. Used for enrollment tracking and retroactive claims adjudication.,
provider,workforce_identity,org_provider,ehr_system,ehr_system,Electronic Health Record (EHR) System,STRING,,,,,master_data,"The primary Electronic Health Record (EHR) or Electronic Medical Record (EMR) system deployed at the organizational provider. Used for HIE connectivity planning, HL7/FHIR interface configuration, and interoperability assessments. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: epic|cerner|meditech|allscripts|athenahealth|other|none — 7 candidates stripped; promote to reference product]",
provider,workforce_identity,org_provider,enrollment_status,enrollment_status,Medicare/Medicaid Enrollment Status,STRING,,,,enrolled|not_enrolled|pending|revoked|opt_out,master_data,Current CMS enrollment status of the organizational provider in Medicare and/or Medicaid programs. Distinct from general provider_status; specifically tracks payer program participation eligibility.,
provider,workforce_identity,org_provider,facility_type,facility_type,Facility Type,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Classification of the organizational provider by facility type (e.g., acute care hospital, critical access hospital, ambulatory surgery center, federally qualified health center, skilled nursing facility, outpatient clinic, group practice). Drives billing rules, regulatory requirements, and reimbursement methodology. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: acute_care_hospital|critical_access_hospital|ambulatory_surgery_center|federally_qualified_health_center|skilled_nursing_facility|outpatient_clinic|group_practice|long_term_care|behavioral_health|home_health|hospice|urgent_care — promote to reference product]",
provider,workforce_identity,org_provider,fax,fax,Primary Fax Number,STRING,,,"dbx_confidential, dbx_pii_phone","^+?[0-9-()s]{7,20}$",master_data,"Primary fax number for the organizational provider. Used for clinical document transmission, referral communications, and payer correspondence in compliance with HIPAA secure transmission requirements.",
provider,workforce_identity,org_provider,fhir_endpoint_url,fhir_endpoint_url,Fast Healthcare Interoperability Resources (FHIR) Endpoint URL,STRING,,,,,master_data,The base URL of the organizational providers HL7 FHIR R4 API endpoint for electronic health information exchange. Required under the CMS Interoperability and Patient Access Rule for payer-to-provider data exchange.,
provider,workforce_identity,org_provider,legal_name,legal_name,Legal Organization Name,STRING,,,dbx_confidential,,master_data,"The full legal name of the organizational provider as registered with state licensing authorities, CMS, and the IRS. Used for billing, contracting, and regulatory submissions.",
provider,workforce_identity,org_provider,license_state,license_state,Facility License State,STRING,,,,^[A-Z]{2}$,master_data,The two-letter US state code where the facility operating license was issued. Determines applicable state regulatory requirements and Medicaid program participation rules.,
provider,workforce_identity,org_provider,medicaid_provider_number,medicaid_provider_number,Medicaid Provider Number,STRING,,,dbx_confidential,,master_data,State-assigned Medicaid provider identification number for the organizational provider. Required for Medicaid claims submission and program participation. Format varies by state Medicaid Management Information System (MMIS).,
provider,workforce_identity,org_provider,medicare_participation_flag,medicare_participation_flag,Medicare Participation Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,"Indicates whether the organizational provider has an active Medicare participation agreement with CMS, authorizing it to bill Medicare for covered services at the Medicare-approved rate.",
provider,workforce_identity,org_provider,network_participation_status,network_participation_status,Payer Network Participation Status,STRING,,,,in_network|out_of_network|pending|terminated,master_data,"Current status of the organizational providers participation in contracted payer networks. Drives claims adjudication, patient cost-sharing calculations, and network adequacy reporting to state and federal regulators.",
provider,workforce_identity,org_provider,oig_exclusion_flag,oig_exclusion_flag,Office of Inspector General (OIG) Exclusion Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,Indicates whether the organizational provider is currently listed on the OIG List of Excluded Individuals/Entities (LEIE). Excluded providers are prohibited from participating in federal healthcare programs. Must be checked prior to contracting and claims payment.,
provider,workforce_identity,org_provider,organization_type,organization_type,Organization Type,STRING,,,,,master_data,"High-level classification of the organizational providers structural type (e.g., hospital, clinic, group practice, Accountable Care Organization (ACO), Integrated Delivery Organization (IDO), health system, outpatient center). Distinct from facility_type which captures the CMS/regulatory classification. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: hospital|clinic|group_practice|aco|ido|health_system|outpatient_center — 7 candidates stripped; promote to reference product]",
provider,workforce_identity,org_provider,ownership_type,ownership_type,Ownership Type,STRING,,,,non_profit|for_profit|government|tribal|faith_based,master_data,"The ownership classification of the organizational provider indicating whether it is non-profit, for-profit, government-owned, tribal, or faith-based. Affects tax status, CMS cost reporting requirements, and regulatory obligations.",
provider,workforce_identity,org_provider,phone,phone,Primary Contact Phone Number,STRING,,,"dbx_confidential, dbx_pii_phone","^+?[0-9-()s]{7,20}$",master_data,"Primary telephone number for the organizational providers main administrative or clinical contact line. Used for referral coordination, payer communications, and provider directory.",
provider,workforce_identity,org_provider,primary_specialty,primary_specialty,Primary Organizational Specialty,STRING,,,,,master_data,"The primary clinical specialty or service line of the organizational provider as designated in NPPES and CMS enrollment records (e.g., General Acute Care Hospital, Multispecialty Group Practice, Radiology Center). Used for network directory, referral routing, and quality reporting.",
provider,workforce_identity,org_provider,provider_status,provider_status,Organizational Provider Status,STRING,,,,active|inactive|pending|suspended|terminated,master_data,"Current lifecycle status of the organizational provider record. Drives eligibility for claims submission, referral routing, and network directory inclusion. Active indicates the organization is currently enrolled and operational; pending indicates enrollment or credentialing in progress.",
provider,workforce_identity,org_provider,sam_exclusion_flag,sam_exclusion_flag,System for Award Management (SAM) Exclusion Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,"Indicates whether the organizational provider is listed in the federal SAM.gov exclusions database, which prohibits participation in federal contracts and assistance programs including CMS programs.",
provider,workforce_identity,org_provider,source_system,source_system,Source System of Record,STRING,,,,,master_data,"The operational system of record from which this organizational provider record was sourced (e.g., Epic, Cerner Millennium, Symplr, NPPES, CMS PECOS). Used for data lineage tracking and master data management reconciliation. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: epic|cerner|meditech|symplr|nppes|pecos|manual|other — 8 candidates stripped; promote to reference product]",
provider,workforce_identity,org_provider,state,state,Service Location State,STRING,,,,^[A-Z]{2}$,master_data,"Two-letter US state code of the organizational providers primary service location. Determines applicable state regulations, Medicaid program rules, and network adequacy requirements.",
provider,workforce_identity,org_provider,state_license_expiration_date,state_license_expiration_date,State Facility License Expiration Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,The expiration date of the state-issued facility operating license. Triggers license renewal workflows and compliance monitoring to prevent lapse in operating authority.,
provider,workforce_identity,org_provider,state_license_number,state_license_number,State Facility License Number,STRING,,,dbx_confidential,,master_data,The facility license number issued by the state Department of Health authorizing the organization to operate as a healthcare facility. Required for state regulatory compliance and CMS certification.,
provider,workforce_identity,org_provider,tax_identification_number,tax_identification_number,Tax Identification Number (TIN) / Employer Identification Number (EIN),STRING,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_identifier",^[0-9]{2}-[0-9]{7}$,master_data,"The federal Employer Identification Number (EIN) or Tax Identification Number (TIN) assigned by the IRS to the organizational provider. Required for claims billing, 1099 reporting, and payer contracting.",
provider,workforce_identity,org_provider,teaching_status,teaching_status,Teaching Hospital Status,STRING,,,,major_teaching|minor_teaching|non_teaching,master_data,Designation of the facilitys teaching status as recognized by CMS for Indirect Medical Education (IME) and Direct Graduate Medical Education (DGME) payment adjustments. Major teaching hospitals have a resident-to-bed ratio above CMS thresholds.,
provider,workforce_identity,org_provider,termination_date,termination_date,Provider Termination Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,"The date on which the organizational providers participation or enrollment was terminated. Null for active providers. Used for claims adjudication, network directory management, and regulatory reporting.",
provider,workforce_identity,org_provider,trauma_level,trauma_level,Trauma Center Designation Level,STRING,,,,I|II|III|IV|V|not_designated,master_data,"The American College of Surgeons (ACS) or state-designated trauma center level (I through V) indicating the facilitys trauma care capability. Level I provides the highest level of comprehensive trauma care. Used for ED routing, transfer protocols, and quality reporting.",
provider,workforce_identity,org_provider,updated_timestamp,updated_timestamp,Record Last Updated Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,master_data,"The timestamp when the organizational provider record was most recently modified. Used for change data capture (CDC), ETL incremental loads, and audit trail compliance.",
provider,workforce_identity,org_provider,website_url,website_url,Organization Website URL,STRING,,,,,master_data,"The public-facing website URL of the organizational provider. Used in provider directory, patient portal, and Salesforce Health Cloud patient relationship management.",
