provider,workforce_identity,provider_location,after_hours_phone,after_hours_phone,After Hours Phone Number,STRING,,,"dbx_confidential, dbx_pii_phone","^+?[0-9-() ]{7,20}$",master_data,Telephone number for reaching the practice location or on-call provider outside of regular business hours. Required for continuity of care and NCQA medical home standards.,
provider,workforce_identity,provider_location,appointment_scheduling_url,appointment_scheduling_url,Appointment Scheduling URL,STRING,,,,,master_data,Direct URL for online patient appointment scheduling at this location. Published in provider directories and patient portals to support patient self-scheduling and access.,
provider,workforce_identity,provider_location,city,city,City,STRING,,,"dbx_confidential, dbx_pii_address",,master_data,City or municipality where the practice location is physically situated. Used for geographic network adequacy analysis and provider directory search.,
provider,workforce_identity,provider_location,cms_enrollment_number,cms_enrollment_number,Centers for Medicare and Medicaid Services (CMS) Enrollment ID,STRING,,,,,master_data,CMS-assigned enrollment identifier (PTAN — Provider Transaction Access Number) for this practice location. Required for Medicare claims submission and CMS enrollment validation.,
provider,workforce_identity,provider_location,cms_place_of_service_code,cms_place_of_service_code,Centers for Medicare and Medicaid Services (CMS) Place of Service (POS) Code,STRING,,,,^[0-9]{2}$,master_data,"Two-digit CMS Place of Service code identifying the setting where healthcare services are rendered (e.g., 11=Office, 21=Inpatient Hospital, 02=Telehealth). Required on CMS-1500 professional claims and drives reimbursement rate determination.",
provider,workforce_identity,provider_location,country_code,country_code,Country Code,STRING,,,,^[A-Z]{3}$,master_data,"ISO 3166-1 alpha-3 three-letter country code for the practice location (e.g., USA). Supports international provider networks and cross-border care coordination.",
