provider,workforce_identity,provider_location,updated_timestamp,updated_timestamp,Record Updated Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,master_data,"Timestamp when this provider location record was last modified in the data platform. Supports change detection, incremental ETL processing, and audit trail requirements.",
provider,workforce_identity,provider_location,website_url,website_url,Website URL,STRING,,,,,master_data,Public-facing website URL for the practice location. Published in provider directories to support patient self-service and appointment scheduling.,
provider,workforce_identity,specialty,specialty_id,specialty_id,Specialty ID,BIGINT,Y,,,,reference_data,Unique surrogate identifier for each specialty record in the provider specialty reference catalog. Primary key for the specialty data product. [REFERENCE_LOOKUP role — canonical_skip_reason: This entity is a reference/lookup catalog of recognized medical specialties and NUCC taxonomy classifications; per-role minimums for REFERENCE_LOOKUP are exempt.],
provider,workforce_identity,specialty,primary_cpt_code_id,primary_cpt_code_id,Primary Cpt Code Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,reference.cpt_code.cpt_code_id,,,reference_data,"Foreign key linking to reference.cpt_code. Business justification: Specialties define authorized procedure sets for privileging decisions, prior authorization rules, and payer contracting. Real healthcare operations require this link for automated privilege delineati",
provider,workforce_identity,specialty,primary_icd_code_id,primary_icd_code_id,Primary Icd Code Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,reference.icd_code.icd_code_id,,,reference_data,"Foreign key linking to reference.icd_code. Business justification: Specialties have primary diagnosis domains for referral routing, utilization management, and network adequacy calculations. Healthcare operations use this for automated referral validation, specialty-",
provider,workforce_identity,specialty,snomed_concept_id,snomed_concept_id,Systematized Nomenclature of Medicine Clinical Terms (SNOMED CT) Concept ID,BIGINT,,reference.snomed_concept.snomed_concept_id,,,reference_data,The SNOMED CT concept identifier corresponding to this specialty for clinical terminology interoperability and HL7 FHIR resource alignment. Supports HIE data exchange and FHIR PractitionerRole resource population.,
provider,workforce_identity,specialty,abms_board_name,abms_board_name,American Board of Medical Specialties (ABMS) Board Name,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"The specific American Board of Medical Specialties (ABMS) member board responsible for certifying physicians in this specialty (e.g., American Board of Internal Medicine, American Board of Pediatrics). Used in credentialing verification and Symplr primary source verification workflows.",
provider,workforce_identity,specialty,acgme_program_code,acgme_program_code,Accreditation Council for Graduate Medical Education (ACGME) Program Code,STRING,,,,^[0-9]{3}-[0-9]{2}$,reference_data,"The ACGME program specialty code used to identify accredited residency and fellowship training programs in this specialty. Used for graduate medical education (GME) tracking, resident credentialing, and workforce planning in Workday HCM.",
provider,workforce_identity,specialty,additional_credentialing_required,additional_credentialing_required,Additional Credentialing Required Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,reference_data,"Indicates whether this specialty requires additional credentialing steps beyond standard privileging (e.g., DEA registration for controlled substance prescribing, specific procedural competency assessments, or state-mandated specialty certifications). Drives credentialing workflow routing in Symplr.",
provider,workforce_identity,specialty,board_certification_body,board_certification_body,Board Certification Body,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"Name of the recognized medical board or certifying organization that issues board certification for this specialty (e.g., American Board of Internal Medicine (ABIM), American Board of Surgery (ABS), American Board of Psychiatry and Neurology (ABPN)). Used in credentialing workflows and provider directory publishing.",
provider,workforce_identity,specialty,board_certification_required,board_certification_required,Board Certification Required Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,reference_data,"Indicates whether board certification is required for a provider to be credentialed and privileged in this specialty at the organization. When true, credentialing workflows in Symplr enforce board certification verification before granting privileges.",
provider,workforce_identity,specialty,cms_enrollment_specialty_type,cms_enrollment_specialty_type,Centers for Medicare and Medicaid Services (CMS) Enrollment Specialty Type,STRING,,,,,reference_data,The CMS-defined specialty type label used on provider enrollment applications (CMS-855 series forms) for Medicare and Medicaid enrollment. Distinct from the two-digit CMS specialty code; represents the descriptive label used in enrollment workflows.,
provider,workforce_identity,specialty,cms_specialty_code,cms_specialty_code,Centers for Medicare and Medicaid Services (CMS) Specialty Code,STRING,,,,^[0-9]{2}$,reference_data,The two-digit CMS specialty code used in Medicare and Medicaid claims processing and provider enrollment. Derived from the CMS crosswalk to NUCC taxonomy codes. Required for CMS-1500 and UB-04 claim form submission and CMS provider enrollment taxonomy reporting.,
provider,workforce_identity,specialty,created_timestamp,created_timestamp,Record Created Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,reference_data,"The timestamp when this specialty record was first created in the enterprise reference catalog. Used for data lineage, audit trail, and Silver layer ingestion tracking.",
provider,workforce_identity,specialty,dea_registration_required,dea_registration_required,Drug Enforcement Administration (DEA) Registration Required Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,reference_data,"Indicates whether providers in this specialty are required to hold an active DEA registration number for controlled substance prescribing authority. Relevant for specialties such as pain management, psychiatry, and anesthesiology. Used in payer enrollment and credentialing validation.",
provider,workforce_identity,specialty,display_order,display_order,Display Order,INT,,,,,reference_data,"Numeric sequence controlling the display order of specialties in provider directory user interfaces, credentialing dropdown menus, and referral routing selection screens. Lower values appear first in sorted lists.",
provider,workforce_identity,specialty,effective_date,effective_date,Effective Date,DATE,,,,,reference_data,"The date on which this specialty code and its associated NUCC taxonomy classification became effective and valid for use in provider credentialing, enrollment, and claims submission. Supports temporal validity tracking for regulatory compliance.",
provider,workforce_identity,specialty,end_date,end_date,End Date,DATE,,,,,reference_data,"The date on which this specialty code and taxonomy classification was retired, superseded, or became invalid. Null indicates the specialty is currently active. Used to enforce temporal validity in claims submission and provider enrollment workflows.",
provider,workforce_identity,specialty,fhir_practitioner_role_code,fhir_practitioner_role_code,Fast Healthcare Interoperability Resources (FHIR) Practitioner Role Code,STRING,,,,,reference_data,The HL7 FHIR R4 PractitionerRole.code value corresponding to this specialty for FHIR-compliant API responses and HIE data exchange. Enables alignment with FHIR-based provider directory publishing and ONC interoperability requirements.,
provider,workforce_identity,specialty,hedis_measure_set,hedis_measure_set,Healthcare Effectiveness Data and Information Set (HEDIS) Measure Set,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"Identifies the applicable HEDIS measure set(s) associated with this specialty for quality measurement and NCQA reporting purposes (e.g., Preventive Care, Chronic Conditions, Behavioral Health). Used in Epic Healthy Planet and population health analytics.",
provider,workforce_identity,specialty,hospital_privileges_applicable,hospital_privileges_applicable,Hospital Privileges Applicable Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,reference_data,Indicates whether providers in this specialty are subject to hospital privileging and credentialing requirements for inpatient or procedural care delivery. Drives privileging workflow routing in Symplr and The Joint Commission compliance tracking.,
provider,workforce_identity,specialty,mips_eligible,mips_eligible,Merit-based Incentive Payment System (MIPS) Eligible Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,reference_data,Indicates whether providers in this specialty are subject to Merit-based Incentive Payment System (MIPS) reporting requirements under MACRA. Used for quality reporting program enrollment and CMS value-based payment calculations.,
provider,workforce_identity,specialty,network_adequacy_category,network_adequacy_category,Network Adequacy Category,STRING,,,,essential|non_essential|specialty_care|behavioral_health|primary_care,reference_data,"Classification of the specialty for CMS and state network adequacy standards, determining minimum provider-to-enrollee ratios and geographic access requirements. Used in network management, payer contracting, and CMS network adequacy reporting.",
provider,workforce_identity,specialty,npi_taxonomy_eligible,npi_taxonomy_eligible,National Provider Identifier (NPI) Taxonomy Eligible Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,reference_data,Indicates whether this specialty/taxonomy code is eligible to be declared as a taxonomy code on an NPI application or update with the National Plan and Provider Enumeration System (NPPES). Ensures only valid NUCC taxonomy codes are submitted during NPI registry alignment.,
provider,workforce_identity,specialty,nucc_classification,nucc_classification,National Uniform Claim Committee (NUCC) Classification,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"The second level of the NUCC taxonomy hierarchy representing the provider classification within the provider type (e.g., Family Medicine, Internal Medicine, Psychiatry & Neurology). Used for payer enrollment specialty validation and network management.",
provider,workforce_identity,specialty,nucc_provider_type,nucc_provider_type,National Uniform Claim Committee (NUCC) Provider Type,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"The broadest level of the NUCC taxonomy hierarchy representing the provider type category (e.g., Allopathic & Osteopathic Physicians, Nursing Service Providers, Behavioral Health & Social Service Providers). First level of the three-level NUCC classification hierarchy.",
provider,workforce_identity,specialty,nucc_specialization,nucc_specialization,National Uniform Claim Committee (NUCC) Specialization,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"The third and most granular level of the NUCC taxonomy hierarchy representing the specific area of specialization within the classification (e.g., Adolescent Medicine, Geriatric Medicine, Sports Medicine). May be null for specialties without a defined subspecialization.",
provider,workforce_identity,specialty,nucc_taxonomy_code,nucc_taxonomy_code,National Uniform Claim Committee (NUCC) Taxonomy Code,STRING,,,,^[0-9]{10}X$,reference_data,"The 10-character alphanumeric NUCC Health Care Provider Taxonomy code that uniquely classifies the provider type, classification, and specialization. Required for NPI registry alignment, claims submission, and CMS provider enrollment taxonomy reporting. This product is the SSOT for all NUCC taxonomy codes in the provider domain.",
provider,workforce_identity,specialty,payer_enrollment_eligible,payer_enrollment_eligible,Payer Enrollment Eligible Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,reference_data,Indicates whether this specialty is eligible for payer enrollment and credentialing with commercial and government payers. Specialties marked false may be internal classifications not recognized by external payers for enrollment purposes.,
provider,workforce_identity,specialty,pecos_specialty_code,pecos_specialty_code,Provider Enrollment Chain and Ownership System (PECOS) Specialty Code,STRING,,,,"^[A-Z0-9]{2,10}$",reference_data,The specialty code used within the CMS Provider Enrollment Chain and Ownership System (PECOS) for Medicare provider enrollment and revalidation. Required for CMS enrollment submissions and RAC audit compliance.,
provider,workforce_identity,specialty,prescribing_authority,prescribing_authority,Prescribing Authority Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,reference_data,"Indicates whether providers in this specialty hold prescribing authority for medications under applicable state and federal law. Used in Epic Willow pharmacy integration, MAR workflows, and CPOE order routing to validate prescriber eligibility.",
provider,workforce_identity,specialty,primary_care_designation,primary_care_designation,Primary Care Physician (PCP) Designation Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,reference_data,"Indicates whether this specialty qualifies for Primary Care Physician (PCP) designation in managed care networks including HMO, ACO, and PCMH models. Drives PCP assignment logic in Salesforce Health Cloud and Epic Healthy Planet population health workflows.",
provider,workforce_identity,specialty,prior_authorization_required,prior_authorization_required,Prior Authorization Required Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,reference_data,Indicates whether services rendered by providers in this specialty typically require prior authorization from payers before service delivery. Used in Epic order management (CPOE) and revenue cycle pre-authorization workflows.,
provider,workforce_identity,specialty,referral_required,referral_required,Referral Required Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,reference_data,"Indicates whether a formal referral is required to access providers in this specialty under standard managed care plan rules (HMO, POS). Drives referral authorization workflows in Epic Cadence and Salesforce Health Cloud referral management.",
provider,workforce_identity,specialty,rvu_work_component,rvu_work_component,Relative Value Unit (RVU) Work Component,"DECIMAL(10,4)",,,,,reference_data,"The standard physician work Relative Value Unit (RVU) component associated with the specialty, used as a baseline for productivity benchmarking and compensation modeling. Sourced from CMS Physician Fee Schedule. Used in Workday HCM compensation planning and RCM analytics.",
provider,workforce_identity,specialty,short_description,short_description,Specialty Short Description,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"Abbreviated description of the specialty suitable for display in constrained UI contexts such as mobile provider directories, claim form dropdowns, and scheduling system specialty selectors. Maximum 100 characters.",
provider,workforce_identity,specialty,source_system,source_system,Source System,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"Identifies the authoritative source system from which this specialty record was ingested or maintained (e.g., NUCC taxonomy feed, CMS specialty crosswalk, Epic EHR, Symplr credentialing). Used for data lineage tracking and ETL reconciliation in the Silver layer. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: nucc|cms|epic|cerner|symplr|meditech|manual — 7 candidates stripped; promote to reference product]",
provider,workforce_identity,specialty,specialty_category,specialty_category,Specialty Category,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"High-level grouping category for the specialty used for network management, referral routing, and provider directory segmentation. Classifies specialties into broad functional areas for operational and analytical purposes. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: medical|surgical|behavioral_health|allied_health|nursing|dental|pharmacy|ancillary|administrative|other — promote to reference product if additional values are needed]",
provider,workforce_identity,specialty,specialty_code,specialty_code,Specialty Code,STRING,,,,"^[A-Z0-9_]{2,20}$",reference_data,"Internally assigned alphanumeric code uniquely identifying the specialty within the enterprise provider directory and credentialing systems. Used as the business key for specialty lookups across Epic, Cerner, and Symplr integrations.",
provider,workforce_identity,specialty,specialty_description,specialty_description,Specialty Description,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"Detailed narrative description of the specialty including scope of practice, patient population served, and types of conditions or procedures managed. Used in provider directory publishing, patient-facing portals, and referral routing guidance.",
provider,workforce_identity,specialty,specialty_name,specialty_name,Specialty Name,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"Full human-readable name of the medical or clinical specialty (e.g., Internal Medicine, Orthopedic Surgery, Pediatric Cardiology). Used in provider directories, credentialing workflows, and payer enrollment forms.",
provider,workforce_identity,specialty,specialty_status,specialty_status,Specialty Status,STRING,,,,active|inactive|deprecated|pending_review,reference_data,"Current lifecycle status of the specialty record in the enterprise reference catalog. Active records are available for provider credentialing, enrollment, and claims submission. Deprecated records are retained for historical reference only.",
provider,workforce_identity,specialty,specialty_type,specialty_type,Specialty Type,STRING,,,,primary_care|specialist|subspecialist|hospitalist|advanced_practice|ancillary,reference_data,"Classification of the specialty as primary care, specialist, subspecialist, hospitalist, advanced practice, or ancillary. Used for referral routing logic, network adequacy analysis, and PCP designation in HMO and ACO network management.",
provider,workforce_identity,specialty,surgical_specialty,surgical_specialty,Surgical Specialty Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,reference_data,"Indicates whether this specialty is classified as a surgical specialty, requiring operating room (OR) scheduling, surgical credentialing, and OpTime/SurgiNet integration for case scheduling and documentation.",
provider,workforce_identity,specialty,telehealth_eligible,telehealth_eligible,Telehealth Eligible Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,reference_data,"Indicates whether providers in this specialty are eligible to deliver services via telehealth modalities under applicable CMS and state regulations. Used for network directory publishing, referral routing, and telehealth program management.",
provider,workforce_identity,specialty,updated_timestamp,updated_timestamp,Record Updated Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,reference_data,"The timestamp when this specialty record was last modified in the enterprise reference catalog. Used for incremental ETL processing, change data capture, and audit trail maintenance in the Databricks Silver layer.",
provider,workforce_identity,specialty,version_number,version_number,NUCC Taxonomy Version Number,STRING,,,,"^[0-9]{2}.[0-9]{1,2}$",reference_data,"The NUCC Health Care Provider Taxonomy Code Set version number in which this specialty code was introduced or last updated (e.g., 23.1, 22.0). Enables version-specific taxonomy lookups for historical claims reprocessing and audit purposes.",
provider,workforce_identity,taxonomy,taxonomy_id,taxonomy_id,Provider Taxonomy ID,BIGINT,Y,,,,reference_data,Unique surrogate identifier for each provider taxonomy code record in the NUCC Health Care Provider Taxonomy reference catalog. Primary key for this table. [_canonical_skip_reason: REFERENCE_LOOKUP — this entity is a NUCC taxonomy code reference table; per-role minimums for REFERENCE_LOOKUP/OTHER are exempt.],
provider,workforce_identity,taxonomy,primary_cpt_code_id,primary_cpt_code_id,Primary Cpt Code Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,reference.cpt_code.cpt_code_id,,,reference_data,"Foreign key linking to reference.cpt_code. Business justification: Taxonomy codes define authorized procedure scopes for credentialing, privileging, and payer enrollment. Links taxonomy to specific CPT codes for scope-of-practice validation, prior authorization rules",
provider,workforce_identity,taxonomy,snomed_concept_id,snomed_concept_id,Systematized Nomenclature of Medicine Clinical Terms (SNOMED CT) Concept ID,BIGINT,,reference.snomed_concept.snomed_concept_id,,,reference_data,"The SNOMED CT concept identifier that semantically maps to this provider taxonomy code, enabling interoperability with clinical terminology systems and FHIR-based health information exchanges.",
provider,workforce_identity,taxonomy,abms_board_name,abms_board_name,American Board of Medical Specialties (ABMS) Board Name,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"The name of the American Board of Medical Specialties (ABMS) member board associated with this taxonomy code (e.g., American Board of Internal Medicine, American Board of Surgery). Used in board certification verification during credentialing.",
provider,workforce_identity,taxonomy,acgme_program_code,acgme_program_code,Accreditation Council for Graduate Medical Education (ACGME) Program Code,STRING,,,,,reference_data,The ACGME program specialty code associated with the residency or fellowship training program that corresponds to this taxonomy classification. Used to validate training pathway alignment during provider credentialing.,
provider,workforce_identity,taxonomy,board_certification_required,board_certification_required,Board Certification Required Indicator,BOOLEAN,,,,,reference_data,Indicates whether board certification is a standard credentialing requirement for providers holding this taxonomy code. Used in credentialing completeness validation and payer enrollment eligibility checks.,
provider,workforce_identity,taxonomy,classification,classification,Provider Classification,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"The second level of the NUCC taxonomy hierarchy representing the providers primary discipline or specialty grouping within the provider type (e.g., Family Medicine, Internal Medicine, Pediatrics). Used in payer enrollment and claims adjudication to route claims to appropriate fee schedules.",
provider,workforce_identity,taxonomy,cms_specialty_code,cms_specialty_code,Centers for Medicare and Medicaid Services (CMS) Specialty Code,STRING,,,,^[0-9]{2}$,reference_data,"The two-digit CMS specialty code that maps to this NUCC taxonomy code, used in Medicare and Medicaid claims processing, fee schedule assignment, and PECOS enrollment. Enables crosswalk between NUCC taxonomy and CMS specialty classification for reimbursement purposes.",
provider,workforce_identity,taxonomy,cms_specialty_description,cms_specialty_description,Centers for Medicare and Medicaid Services (CMS) Specialty Description,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"The descriptive label associated with the CMS specialty code crosswalk for this taxonomy entry (e.g., General Practice, Cardiology, Pathology). Supports reporting and validation in Medicare claims adjudication workflows.",
provider,workforce_identity,taxonomy,created_timestamp,created_timestamp,Record Created Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,reference_data,"The timestamp when this taxonomy code record was first loaded into the enterprise data platform. Used for data lineage, audit trail, and ETL monitoring.",
provider,workforce_identity,taxonomy,dea_registration_applicable,dea_registration_applicable,Drug Enforcement Administration (DEA) Registration Applicable,BOOLEAN,,,,,reference_data,Indicates whether providers with this taxonomy code are typically required or eligible to obtain a DEA registration number for prescribing controlled substances. Supports credentialing completeness checks and compliance monitoring.,
provider,workforce_identity,taxonomy,definition,definition,Taxonomy Definition,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"UC tag definitions for Unity Catalog (pii_phi, pii_pii, pii_sensitive).",
provider,workforce_identity,taxonomy,display_name,display_name,Taxonomy Display Name,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"The full human-readable display name for the taxonomy code as published by NUCC, combining provider type, classification, and specialization into a single descriptive label used in UI dropdowns, reports, and provider directories.",
provider,workforce_identity,taxonomy,effective_date,effective_date,Taxonomy Code Effective Date,DATE,,,,,reference_data,"The date on which this taxonomy code became effective and valid for use in NPI registry enrollment, claims submission, and payer credentialing. Aligns with the NUCC code set release date.",
provider,workforce_identity,taxonomy,end_date,end_date,Taxonomy Code End Date,DATE,,,,,reference_data,The date on which this taxonomy code was retired or deactivated by NUCC. Null for currently active codes. Used to prevent use of retired codes in new NPI enrollments and claims submissions.,
provider,workforce_identity,taxonomy,fhir_practitioner_role_code,fhir_practitioner_role_code,Fast Healthcare Interoperability Resources (FHIR) Practitioner Role Code,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"The HL7 FHIR PractitionerRole code that corresponds to this NUCC taxonomy code, used in FHIR-based API integrations, HIE data exchange, and interoperability with external EHR systems.",
provider,workforce_identity,taxonomy,hospital_privileges_applicable,hospital_privileges_applicable,Hospital Privileges Applicable Indicator,BOOLEAN,,,,,reference_data,Indicates whether providers with this taxonomy code are subject to hospital privileging and credentialing requirements. Drives privileging workflow initiation in credentialing systems such as Symplr.,
provider,workforce_identity,taxonomy,individual_or_organization,individual_or_organization,Individual or Organization Indicator,STRING,,,,Individual|Organization,reference_data,Indicates whether this taxonomy code applies to an individual healthcare professional (Type 1 NPI) or an organizational/group provider (Type 2 NPI). Drives NPI enumeration type selection and payer enrollment form routing.,
provider,workforce_identity,taxonomy,medicaid_enrollment_eligible,medicaid_enrollment_eligible,Medicaid Enrollment Eligible,BOOLEAN,,,,,reference_data,Indicates whether providers with this taxonomy code are eligible to enroll as Medicaid providers. Supports state Medicaid agency enrollment workflows and payer credentialing validation.,
provider,workforce_identity,taxonomy,mips_eligible,mips_eligible,Merit-based Incentive Payment System (MIPS) Eligible,BOOLEAN,,,,,reference_data,Indicates whether providers with this taxonomy code are eligible to participate in the Merit-based Incentive Payment System (MIPS) under MACRA. Used in quality reporting program enrollment and value-based care analytics.,
provider,workforce_identity,taxonomy,network_adequacy_category,network_adequacy_category,Network Adequacy Category,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"The network adequacy classification assigned to this taxonomy code by CMS or state regulators, indicating the minimum provider-to-enrollee ratios and geographic access standards required for health plan network compliance (e.g., Primary Care, Specialist, Behavioral Health, Ancillary).",
provider,workforce_identity,taxonomy,notes,notes,Taxonomy Notes,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"Supplemental notes published by NUCC clarifying usage, scope limitations, or cross-references to related taxonomy codes. Assists credentialing and billing staff in selecting the most appropriate taxonomy code for a provider.",
provider,workforce_identity,taxonomy,npi_type,npi_type,National Provider Identifier (NPI) Type,STRING,,,,Type 1|Type 2,reference_data,The NPI enumeration type associated with this taxonomy code: Type 1 for individual healthcare providers and Type 2 for organizational providers. Determines the NPI application process and NPPES registry classification.,
provider,workforce_identity,taxonomy,nucc_grouping,nucc_grouping,NUCC Taxonomy Grouping,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"The broad grouping category assigned by NUCC above the provider type level, used to segment taxonomy codes into major provider categories such as Individual, Non-Individual, or specific functional groupings (e.g., Behavioral Health & Social Service Providers, Dental Providers). Supports high-level analytics and network adequacy reporting.",
provider,workforce_identity,taxonomy,pecos_enrollment_eligible,pecos_enrollment_eligible,Provider Enrollment and Chain Ownership System (PECOS) Enrollment Eligible,BOOLEAN,,,,,reference_data,Indicates whether providers with this taxonomy code are eligible to enroll in Medicare through the PECOS system. Used by revenue cycle and credentialing teams to determine Medicare participation eligibility during provider onboarding.,
provider,workforce_identity,taxonomy,prescribing_authority,prescribing_authority,Prescribing Authority Indicator,BOOLEAN,,,,,reference_data,"Indicates whether providers classified under this taxonomy code typically hold prescribing authority for medications. Used in pharmacy benefit management, DEA registration workflows, and Computerized Physician Order Entry (CPOE) access control configuration.",
provider,workforce_identity,taxonomy,primary_care_designation,primary_care_designation,Primary Care Physician (PCP) Designation,BOOLEAN,,,,,reference_data,"Indicates whether this taxonomy code is recognized as a primary care designation by CMS and payers. Used in network adequacy analysis, HMO/PPO panel assignments, ACO attribution, and HEDIS measure reporting.",
provider,workforce_identity,taxonomy,prior_authorization_required,prior_authorization_required,Prior Authorization Required Indicator,BOOLEAN,,,,,reference_data,Indicates whether services rendered by providers with this taxonomy code typically require prior authorization from payers. Used in utilization management configuration and claims pre-authorization workflow routing.,
provider,workforce_identity,taxonomy,provider_type,provider_type,Provider Type,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"The highest-level grouping in the NUCC taxonomy hierarchy that broadly categorizes the provider (e.g., Allopathic & Osteopathic Physicians, Nursing Service Providers, Hospitals, Laboratories). Corresponds to the Type level of the NUCC three-level hierarchy.",
provider,workforce_identity,taxonomy,referral_required,referral_required,Referral Required Indicator,BOOLEAN,,,,,reference_data,Indicates whether a referral from a primary care provider is typically required before a patient can access services from a provider with this taxonomy code. Relevant for HMO and POS plan configurations.,
provider,workforce_identity,taxonomy,replacement_taxonomy_code,replacement_taxonomy_code,Replacement Taxonomy Code,STRING,,,,^[0-9]{6}[A-Z0-9]{3}X$,reference_data,The NUCC taxonomy code that replaces this code when it has been retired or deprecated. Enables automated migration of provider taxonomy assignments during NUCC code set updates and supports backward compatibility in claims processing.,
provider,workforce_identity,taxonomy,rvu_work_component,rvu_work_component,Relative Value Unit (RVU) Work Component,"DECIMAL(10,4)",,,,,reference_data,"The typical physician work Relative Value Unit (RVU) component associated with services delivered under this taxonomy code, used as a benchmark for productivity measurement, compensation modeling, and value-based payment analytics.",
provider,workforce_identity,taxonomy,source_system,source_system,Source System,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"The operational system of record from which this taxonomy code record was sourced or last updated (e.g., NUCC published code set, CMS NPPES registry, Symplr credentialing system). Supports data lineage tracking and ETL audit. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: NUCC|CMS|NPPES|Symplr|Epic|Cerner|MEDITECH|Manual — 8 candidates stripped; promote to reference product]",
provider,workforce_identity,taxonomy,source_system_record_reference,source_system_record_reference,Source System Record ID,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"The unique identifier of this taxonomy record in the originating source system (e.g., NUCC internal code ID, NPPES taxonomy reference ID). Used for ETL reconciliation and cross-system data lineage.",
provider,workforce_identity,taxonomy,specialization,specialization,Provider Specialization,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"The third and most granular level of the NUCC taxonomy hierarchy representing a specific area of practice within the classification (e.g., Adolescent Medicine, Geriatric Medicine, Sports Medicine). May be null for taxonomy codes that do not have a defined specialization.",
provider,workforce_identity,taxonomy,surgical_specialty,surgical_specialty,Surgical Specialty Indicator,BOOLEAN,,,,,reference_data,"Indicates whether this taxonomy code represents a surgical specialty. Used in OR scheduling, surgical credentialing workflows, and operative case volume reporting.",
provider,workforce_identity,taxonomy,taxonomy_code,taxonomy_code,NUCC Provider Taxonomy Code,STRING,,,,^[0-9]{6}[A-Z0-9]{3}X$,reference_data,"The 10-character alphanumeric code assigned by the National Uniform Claim Committee (NUCC) that uniquely identifies a provider type, classification, and specialization. Used on CMS-1500 and UB-04 claim forms, NPI registry enrollment, and payer credentialing. Example: 207Q00000X for Family Medicine.",
provider,workforce_identity,taxonomy,taxonomy_status,taxonomy_status,Taxonomy Code Status,STRING,,,,Active|Retired|Deprecated,reference_data,"The current lifecycle status of this taxonomy code as maintained by NUCC: Active (valid for current use), Retired (no longer valid for new enrollments), or Deprecated (superseded by a replacement code). Drives validation rules in NPI enrollment and claims editing systems.",
provider,workforce_identity,taxonomy,telehealth_eligible,telehealth_eligible,Telehealth Eligible Indicator,BOOLEAN,,,,,reference_data,Indicates whether providers with this taxonomy code are eligible to deliver and bill for telehealth services under CMS and payer policies. Supports telehealth program configuration and claims validation.,
provider,workforce_identity,taxonomy,updated_timestamp,updated_timestamp,Record Updated Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,reference_data,"The timestamp when this taxonomy code record was last modified in the enterprise data platform, reflecting updates from NUCC code set releases or CMS crosswalk revisions.",
provider,workforce_identity,taxonomy,version,version,NUCC Taxonomy Code Set Version,STRING,,,,^[0-9]{2}.[0-9]$,reference_data,"The version number of the NUCC Health Care Provider Taxonomy Code Set from which this taxonomy code was sourced (e.g., 23.1, 24.0). NUCC releases updates twice per year; version tracking ensures claims and enrollment systems use the correct code set.",
compliance,audit_oversight,audit,audit_id,audit_id,Audit ID,BIGINT,Y,,,,transactional_data,Unique identifier for the compliance audit record. Primary key for the audit entity.,
