finance,capital_assets,fixed_asset,care_site_id,care_site_id,Facility ID,BIGINT,,facility.care_site.care_site_id,,,master_data,Identifier of the healthcare facility where the fixed asset is physically located and assigned for operational use.,
finance,capital_assets,fixed_asset,chart_of_accounts_id,chart_of_accounts_id,Chart Of Accounts Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,finance.chart_of_accounts.chart_of_accounts_id,,,master_data,Foreign key linking to finance.chart_of_accounts. Business justification: fixed_asset has gl_account_code (STRING) which should be normalized to FK to chart_of_accounts. Enables joining to get the GL asset account for the fixed asset.,
finance,capital_assets,fixed_asset,cost_center_id,cost_center_id,Cost Center ID,BIGINT,,finance.cost_center.cost_center_id,,,master_data,Identifier of the cost center or department responsible for the fixed asset and to which depreciation expense is allocated for financial reporting and budgeting.,
finance,capital_assets,fixed_asset,parent_fixed_asset_id,parent_fixed_asset_id,Parent Fixed Asset Id,BIGINT,,finance.fixed_asset.fixed_asset_id,dbx_self_ref_fk,,master_data,Self-referencing FK on fixed_asset (parent_fixed_asset_id),
finance,capital_assets,fixed_asset,accumulated_depreciation,accumulated_depreciation,Accumulated Depreciation,"DECIMAL(18,2)",,,,,master_data,Total depreciation expense recognized to date since the asset was placed in service. Contra-asset account that reduces the gross book value. Recorded in USD.,
finance,capital_assets,fixed_asset,acquisition_cost,acquisition_cost,Acquisition Cost,"DECIMAL(18,2)",,,,,master_data,"Total capitalized cost of acquiring the fixed asset including purchase price, installation costs, freight, and other costs necessary to prepare the asset for its intended use. Recorded in USD.",
finance,capital_assets,fixed_asset,acquisition_date,acquisition_date,Acquisition Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,"Date on which the healthcare organization legally acquired ownership or control of the fixed asset through purchase, donation, or construction completion.",
finance,capital_assets,fixed_asset,asset_category,asset_category,Asset Category,STRING,,,,medical_equipment|building|land|leasehold_improvement|it_equipment|vehicle,master_data,Primary classification of the fixed asset type. Medical equipment includes diagnostic and treatment devices; buildings include owned structures; land includes real property; leasehold improvements include tenant modifications; IT equipment includes servers and network infrastructure; vehicles include ambulances and transport.,
finance,capital_assets,fixed_asset,asset_description,asset_description,Asset Description,STRING,,,,,master_data,Clean boilerplate phrase from description,
finance,capital_assets,fixed_asset,asset_name,asset_name,Asset Name,STRING,,,,,master_data,"pii_phi,pii_pii,pii_sensitive",
finance,capital_assets,fixed_asset,asset_status,asset_status,Asset Status,STRING,,,,active|disposed|transferred|fully_depreciated|under_construction|retired,master_data,Current lifecycle status of the fixed asset. Active indicates in-service use; disposed indicates sold or scrapped; transferred indicates moved to another entity; fully depreciated indicates zero net book value but still in use; under construction indicates not yet placed in service; retired indicates removed from service.,
finance,capital_assets,fixed_asset,asset_subcategory,asset_subcategory,Asset Subcategory,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Secondary classification providing additional granularity within the asset category (e.g., MRI scanner, CT scanner, ultrasound machine for medical equipment category).",
finance,capital_assets,fixed_asset,asset_tag_number,asset_tag_number,Asset Tag Number,STRING,,,,"^[A-Z0-9]{6,20}$",master_data,Unique physical identifier affixed to the asset for tracking and inventory purposes. Externally visible barcode or RFID tag number used in physical audits.,
finance,capital_assets,fixed_asset,capitalization_threshold_met,capitalization_threshold_met,Capitalization Threshold Met,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,Flag indicating whether the asset acquisition cost met or exceeded the organizations capitalization threshold policy. True indicates the asset was properly capitalized; False would indicate an expense treatment.,
finance,capital_assets,fixed_asset,created_timestamp,created_timestamp,Created Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,master_data,Date and time when the fixed asset record was first created in the system. Used for audit trail and data lineage tracking.,
finance,capital_assets,fixed_asset,depreciation_method,depreciation_method,Depreciation Method,STRING,,,,straight_line|declining_balance|macrs|units_of_production|sum_of_years_digits,master_data,Accounting method used to systematically allocate the cost of the fixed asset over its useful life. Straight-line allocates evenly; declining balance accelerates early depreciation; MACRS (Modified Accelerated Cost Recovery System) follows IRS tax rules; units of production bases depreciation on usage; sum of years digits accelerates depreciation.,
finance,capital_assets,fixed_asset,disposal_date,disposal_date,Disposal Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,"Date on which the fixed asset was disposed of through sale, donation, scrapping, or other removal from service. Null for active assets.",
finance,capital_assets,fixed_asset,disposal_method,disposal_method,Disposal Method,STRING,,,,sold|donated|scrapped|traded_in|returned_to_lessor|transferred,master_data,Method by which the fixed asset was disposed. Sold indicates sale to third party; donated indicates charitable contribution; scrapped indicates destruction; traded in indicates exchange for new asset; returned to lessor indicates lease termination; transferred indicates internal move to another entity.,
finance,capital_assets,fixed_asset,disposal_proceeds,disposal_proceeds,Disposal Proceeds,"DECIMAL(18,2)",,,,,master_data,Cash or fair value of consideration received from disposal of the fixed asset. Used to calculate gain or loss on disposal. Recorded in USD.,
finance,capital_assets,fixed_asset,fda_device_class,fda_device_class,FDA (Food and Drug Administration) Device Class,STRING,,,,class_i|class_ii|class_iii|not_applicable,master_data,FDA classification of the medical device based on risk level. Class I is low risk; Class II is moderate risk; Class III is high risk. Not applicable for non-medical equipment.,
finance,capital_assets,fixed_asset,fda_regulated_indicator,fda_regulated_indicator,FDA (Food and Drug Administration) Regulated Indicator,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,Flag indicating whether the fixed asset is a medical device or equipment subject to FDA regulatory oversight and compliance requirements. True for FDA-regulated medical equipment.,
finance,capital_assets,fixed_asset,insurance_coverage_amount,insurance_coverage_amount,Insurance Coverage Amount,"DECIMAL(18,2)",,,,,master_data,Maximum insured value or coverage limit for the fixed asset under the insurance policy. Recorded in USD.,
finance,capital_assets,fixed_asset,insurance_policy_number,insurance_policy_number,Insurance Policy Number,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Policy number of the insurance coverage protecting the fixed asset against loss, damage, or theft. Used for risk management and claims processing.",
finance,capital_assets,fixed_asset,last_maintenance_date,last_maintenance_date,Last Maintenance Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,Date of the most recent preventive or corrective maintenance service performed on the fixed asset. Used to track maintenance compliance and schedule next service.,
finance,capital_assets,fixed_asset,last_physical_inventory_date,last_physical_inventory_date,Last Physical Inventory Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,Date of the most recent physical inventory audit or verification confirming the existence and condition of the fixed asset.,
finance,capital_assets,fixed_asset,lease_end_date,lease_end_date,Lease End Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,Date on which the lease agreement for the fixed asset expires. Null for owned assets. Used for lease renewal planning and return logistics.,
finance,capital_assets,fixed_asset,lease_indicator,lease_indicator,Lease Indicator,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,Flag indicating whether the fixed asset is leased (True) or owned (False). Determines accounting treatment under ASC 842 lease accounting standards.,
finance,capital_assets,fixed_asset,lease_type,lease_type,Lease Type,STRING,,,,operating_lease|finance_lease|capital_lease|not_applicable,master_data,Classification of the lease agreement if the asset is leased. Operating lease transfers use rights; finance/capital lease transfers substantially all risks and rewards of ownership. Not applicable for owned assets.,
finance,capital_assets,fixed_asset,maintenance_schedule,maintenance_schedule,Maintenance Schedule,STRING,,,,,master_data,Frequency of scheduled preventive maintenance required for the fixed asset to ensure safe operation and regulatory compliance. Critical for medical equipment and life safety systems. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: daily|weekly|monthly|quarterly|semi_annual|annual|as_needed — 7 candidates stripped; promote to reference product],
finance,capital_assets,fixed_asset,manufacturer_name,manufacturer_name,Manufacturer Name,STRING,,,,,master_data,Name of the original equipment manufacturer (OEM) who produced the fixed asset. May differ from vendor if purchased through a distributor.,
finance,capital_assets,fixed_asset,model_number,model_number,Model Number,STRING,,,,,master_data,Manufacturer-assigned model number or designation that identifies the specific product configuration and specifications of the fixed asset.,
finance,capital_assets,fixed_asset,modified_timestamp,modified_timestamp,Modified Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,master_data,Date and time when the fixed asset record was last updated in the system. Used for audit trail and change tracking.,
finance,capital_assets,fixed_asset,net_book_value,net_book_value,Net Book Value (NBV),"DECIMAL(18,2)",,,,,master_data,Current carrying value of the fixed asset calculated as acquisition cost minus accumulated depreciation. Represents the undepreciated balance on the balance sheet. Recorded in USD.,
finance,capital_assets,fixed_asset,next_maintenance_due_date,next_maintenance_due_date,Next Maintenance Due Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,Scheduled date for the next preventive maintenance service based on the maintenance schedule and last service date. Used for maintenance planning and compliance tracking.,
finance,capital_assets,fixed_asset,physical_location,physical_location,Physical Location,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Current physical location of the fixed asset including facility name, building, floor, room number, or department where the asset is deployed and in use.",
finance,capital_assets,fixed_asset,placed_in_service_date,placed_in_service_date,Placed in Service Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,Date on which the fixed asset was ready and available for its intended use and depreciation began. May differ from acquisition date for assets requiring installation or construction.,
finance,capital_assets,fixed_asset,purchase_order_number,purchase_order_number,Purchase Order (PO) Number,STRING,,,,,master_data,Purchase order number under which the fixed asset was procured. Links the asset to the original procurement transaction and vendor contract.,
finance,capital_assets,fixed_asset,responsible_party_name,responsible_party_name,Responsible Party Name,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Name of the individual or role responsible for the custody, maintenance, and proper use of the fixed asset. Typically a department manager or equipment coordinator.",
finance,capital_assets,fixed_asset,salvage_value,salvage_value,Salvage Value,"DECIMAL(18,2)",,,,,master_data,Estimated residual value of the fixed asset at the end of its useful life. Amount expected to be recovered through sale or disposal. Recorded in USD.,
finance,capital_assets,fixed_asset,serial_number,serial_number,Serial Number,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Manufacturer-assigned unique serial number that identifies the individual unit of the fixed asset for warranty, service, and tracking purposes.",
finance,capital_assets,fixed_asset,useful_life_years,useful_life_years,Useful Life Years,"DECIMAL(5,2)",,,,,master_data,Estimated number of years the fixed asset is expected to provide economic benefit to the healthcare organization. Used to calculate depreciation expense.,
finance,capital_assets,fixed_asset,vendor_name,vendor_name,Vendor Name,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Name of the vendor, supplier, or manufacturer from whom the fixed asset was purchased or leased.",
finance,capital_assets,fixed_asset,warranty_expiration_date,warranty_expiration_date,Warranty Expiration Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,Date on which the manufacturer or vendor warranty coverage for the fixed asset expires. Used for maintenance planning and service contract decisions.,
finance,cost_management,allocation_method,allocation_method_id,allocation_method_id,Allocation Method Identifier (ID),BIGINT,Y,,,,reference_data,Unique identifier for the cost allocation method. Primary key for the allocation method reference master.,
finance,cost_management,allocation_method,allocation_employee_id,allocation_employee_id,Created By Identifier (ID),BIGINT,,workforce.employee.employee_id,"confidential,pii",,reference_data,Identifier of the user who created this allocation method record. Links to workforce or user management system for accountability.,
finance,cost_management,allocation_method,owner_employee_id,owner_employee_id,Method Owner Identifier (ID),BIGINT,,workforce.employee.employee_id,"dbx_confidential, dbx_pii",,reference_data,Identifier of the cost accounting analyst or finance manager responsible for maintaining and updating this allocation method. Links to workforce or user management system.,
finance,cost_management,allocation_method,primary_employee_id,primary_employee_id,Approved By Identifier (ID),BIGINT,,workforce.employee.employee_id,"dbx_confidential, dbx_pii",,reference_data,Identifier of the finance executive or cost accounting manager who approved this allocation method. Links to workforce or user management system for accountability and audit trail.,
finance,cost_management,allocation_method,superseded_allocation_method_id,superseded_allocation_method_id,Superseded Method Identifier (ID),BIGINT,,finance.allocation_method.allocation_method_id,,,reference_data,Identifier of the previous allocation method that this method replaces. Creates a lineage chain for tracking method evolution and supporting historical cost report reconstruction.,
finance,cost_management,allocation_method,activity_driver_description,activity_driver_description,Activity Driver Description,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"For activity-based costing (ABC) methods, describes the specific activity or cost driver that causes costs to be incurred. Examples include number of purchase orders processed, number of patient admissions, number of surgical procedures performed. Provides transparency into ABC methodology.",
finance,cost_management,allocation_method,allocation_basis_type,allocation_basis_type,Allocation Basis Type,STRING,,,,,reference_data,The statistical or financial measure used as the basis for distributing costs. Square footage for facility costs; FTE (Full-Time Equivalent) count for HR costs; revenue for administrative overhead; RVU (Relative Value Unit) for physician services; patient days for nursing; procedures for surgical services; direct cost for proportional allocation; labor hours for labor-intensive departments; visits for outpatient services; discharges for inpatient services. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: square_footage|fte_count|revenue|rvu|patient_days|procedures|direct_cost|labor_hours|visits|discharges — 10 candidates stripped; promote to reference product],
finance,cost_management,allocation_method,allocation_frequency,allocation_frequency,Allocation Frequency,STRING,,,,monthly|quarterly|annually|as_needed|real_time,reference_data,How often this allocation method is executed. Monthly for routine cost accounting; quarterly for less frequent allocations; annually for year-end adjustments; as needed for special allocations; real-time for continuous allocation in advanced systems.,
finance,cost_management,allocation_method,allocation_percentage_cap,allocation_percentage_cap,Allocation Percentage Cap,"DECIMAL(5,2)",,,,,reference_data,"Maximum percentage of source cost that can be allocated to any single target cost center. Used to prevent disproportionate allocation and ensure equitable distribution. Expressed as a percentage (e.g., 25.00 for 25%).",
finance,cost_management,allocation_method,allocation_sequence,allocation_sequence,Allocation Sequence Number,INT,,,,,reference_data,The order in which this allocation method is applied in step-down or sequential allocation processes. Lower numbers are allocated first. Critical for step-down methodology where allocation order affects final cost distribution.,
finance,cost_management,allocation_method,approval_date,approval_date,Method Approval Date,DATE,,,,,reference_data,The date on which this allocation method was formally approved by finance leadership or the cost accounting committee. Required for audit trail and regulatory compliance documentation.,
finance,cost_management,allocation_method,audit_trail_required_flag,audit_trail_required_flag,Audit Trail Required Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,reference_data,Indicates whether detailed audit trail logging is required for allocations using this method. True for regulatory or high-value allocations requiring full traceability; false for routine internal allocations.,
finance,cost_management,allocation_method,basis_data_source,basis_data_source,Allocation Basis Data Source,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"The system, report, or data source from which the allocation basis statistics are obtained. Examples include facility management system for square footage, HR system for FTE counts, general ledger for revenue, clinical system for RVUs and patient days.",
finance,cost_management,allocation_method,calculation_formula,calculation_formula,Allocation Calculation Formula,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"The mathematical formula or algorithm used to calculate allocation amounts. May reference basis statistics, weighting factors, and cost pools. Provides transparency and reproducibility for cost accounting calculations.",
finance,cost_management,allocation_method,cms_cost_report_schedule,cms_cost_report_schedule,Centers for Medicare and Medicaid Services (CMS) Cost Report Schedule,STRING,,,,"^[A-Z]-[0-9]{1,2}(-[A-Z0-9]{1,3})?$",reference_data,"The specific Medicare Cost Report worksheet or schedule to which this allocation method applies. Examples include Worksheet A (Reclassification and Adjustment of Trial Balance), Worksheet B (Cost Allocation), Worksheet C (Departmental Cost Allocation). Critical for regulatory compliance and reimbursement.",
finance,cost_management,allocation_method,created_timestamp,created_timestamp,Record Created Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,reference_data,The date and time when this allocation method record was first created in the system. Supports audit trail and data lineage tracking.,
finance,cost_management,allocation_method,decimal_precision,decimal_precision,Allocation Decimal Precision,INT,,,,,reference_data,"Number of decimal places to which allocation amounts are calculated and stored. Typically 2 for dollar amounts, but may be higher for statistical allocations or percentage calculations.",
finance,cost_management,allocation_method,effective_end_date,effective_end_date,Effective End Date,DATE,,,,,reference_data,The date on which this allocation method ceases to be active. Null indicates the method is currently in use. Used for historical tracking and audit compliance.,
finance,cost_management,allocation_method,effective_start_date,effective_start_date,Effective Start Date,DATE,,,,,reference_data,The date from which this allocation method becomes active and applicable for cost accounting calculations. Aligns with fiscal period boundaries and Medicare Cost Report periods.,
finance,cost_management,allocation_method,gaap_compliant_flag,gaap_compliant_flag,Generally Accepted Accounting Principles (GAAP) Compliant Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,reference_data,Indicates whether this allocation method complies with Generally Accepted Accounting Principles (GAAP) for financial statement preparation. True for methods acceptable under GAAP; false for methods used only for internal or regulatory purposes.,
finance,cost_management,allocation_method,last_review_date,last_review_date,Last Review Date,DATE,,,,,reference_data,"The date on which this allocation method was last reviewed for accuracy, relevance, and compliance. Used to ensure methods are periodically validated and updated as business needs evolve.",
finance,cost_management,allocation_method,method_code,method_code,Allocation Method Code,STRING,,,,"^[A-Z0-9_]{2,20}$",reference_data,Short alphanumeric code uniquely identifying the allocation method for system processing and reporting. Used in cost accounting transactions and Medicare Cost Report preparation.,
finance,cost_management,allocation_method,method_description,method_description,Allocation Method Description,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"Detailed narrative description of the allocation method, including business rationale, calculation approach, and any special considerations. Used for documentation, training, and audit support.",
finance,cost_management,allocation_method,method_name,method_name,Allocation Method Name,STRING,,,,,reference_data,Full descriptive name of the cost allocation method. Human-readable label used in financial reports and cost accounting documentation.,
finance,cost_management,allocation_method,method_status,method_status,Allocation Method Status,STRING,,,,active|inactive|pending_approval|deprecated|under_review,reference_data,Current lifecycle status of the allocation method. Active methods are in use; inactive methods are retired; pending approval methods await finance leadership sign-off; deprecated methods are being phased out; under review methods are being evaluated for changes.,
finance,cost_management,allocation_method,method_type,method_type,Allocation Method Type,STRING,,,,step_down|direct|reciprocal|activity_based_costing|simultaneous|double_distribution,reference_data,Classification of the cost allocation methodology. Step-down allocates overhead sequentially; direct allocates without intermediate steps; reciprocal accounts for mutual service exchanges; activity-based costing (ABC) allocates based on cost drivers; simultaneous solves all allocations concurrently; double distribution performs two-pass allocation.,
finance,cost_management,allocation_method,modified_timestamp,modified_timestamp,Record Modified Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,reference_data,The date and time when this allocation method record was last modified. Supports change tracking and audit compliance.,
finance,cost_management,allocation_method,next_review_date,next_review_date,Next Review Date,DATE,,,,,reference_data,The scheduled date for the next periodic review of this allocation method. Supports proactive governance and ensures methods remain current with regulatory and business requirements.,
finance,cost_management,allocation_method,prior_period_adjustment_flag,prior_period_adjustment_flag,Prior Period Adjustment Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,reference_data,Indicates whether this allocation method supports retroactive adjustments to prior accounting periods. True for methods that allow historical corrections; false for methods that only allocate current period costs.,
finance,cost_management,allocation_method,reciprocal_allocation_flag,reciprocal_allocation_flag,Reciprocal Allocation Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,reference_data,Indicates whether this method supports reciprocal allocation where departments can allocate costs to each other. True for methods that handle mutual service exchanges; false for unidirectional allocation methods.,
finance,cost_management,allocation_method,regulatory_compliance_flag,regulatory_compliance_flag,Regulatory Compliance Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,reference_data,"Indicates whether this allocation method is required for regulatory reporting compliance (CMS Medicare Cost Report, state Medicaid cost reports, or other regulatory filings). True for methods mandated by regulation; false for internal management accounting methods.",
finance,cost_management,allocation_method,rounding_rule,rounding_rule,Allocation Rounding Rule,STRING,,,,round_half_up|round_half_down|round_up|round_down|truncate|no_rounding,reference_data,Specifies how calculated allocation amounts are rounded. Round half up rounds 0.5 and above up; round half down rounds 0.5 and below down; round up always rounds up; round down always rounds down; truncate drops decimals; no rounding preserves full precision. Critical for ensuring allocation totals reconcile to source costs.,
finance,cost_management,allocation_method,source_cost_center_category,source_cost_center_category,Source Cost Center Category,STRING,,,,,reference_data,Classification of the cost centers from which costs are allocated using this method. Overhead includes facilities and utilities; administrative includes finance and HR; support services includes IT and housekeeping; ancillary includes lab and radiology; clinical includes nursing and therapy; revenue-producing vs non-revenue-producing distinguishes direct patient care from support functions. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: overhead|administrative|support_services|ancillary|clinical|revenue_producing|non_revenue_producing — 7 candidates stripped; promote to reference product],
finance,cost_management,allocation_method,target_cost_center_category,target_cost_center_category,Target Cost Center Category,STRING,,,,clinical|ancillary|revenue_producing|all_departments|patient_care_only,reference_data,Classification of the cost centers to which costs are allocated using this method. Defines the recipient departments for overhead distribution. Patient care only excludes further allocation to administrative departments.,
finance,cost_management,allocation_method,usage_notes,usage_notes,Method Usage Notes,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"Free-text field for cost accounting analysts to document special instructions, exceptions, or considerations when applying this allocation method. Supports knowledge transfer and operational continuity.",
finance,cost_management,allocation_method,version_number,version_number,Method Version Number,STRING,,,,^[0-9]+.[0-9]+$,reference_data,"Version identifier for this allocation method configuration. Incremented when method parameters, formulas, or basis types are changed. Supports change tracking and historical analysis.",
finance,cost_management,allocation_method,weighting_factor,weighting_factor,Allocation Weighting Factor,"DECIMAL(10,4)",,,,,reference_data,"Numeric multiplier applied to the allocation basis to adjust for intensity, complexity, or other factors. Used to refine allocation precision when raw statistics do not fully reflect cost consumption patterns.",
finance,cost_management,allocation_run,allocation_run_id,allocation_run_id,Allocation Run Identifier,BIGINT,Y,,,,master_data,Primary key for allocation_run,
finance,cost_management,allocation_run,allocation_employee_id,allocation_employee_id,Approved By User Employee Id,BIGINT,,workforce.employee.employee_id,"confidential,pii",,master_data,Reference to the user who approved this allocation run for posting to the general ledger.,
finance,cost_management,allocation_run,allocation_method_id,allocation_method_id,Allocation Method Id,BIGINT,,finance.allocation_method.allocation_method_id,,,master_data,"Reference to the allocation methodology applied in this run (e.g., direct, step-down, reciprocal, activity-based costing).",
finance,cost_management,allocation_run,cost_center_id,cost_center_id,Cost Center Id,BIGINT,,finance.cost_center.cost_center_id,,,master_data,Reference to the primary cost center or cost pool from which costs are being allocated in this run.,
finance,cost_management,allocation_run,fiscal_period_id,fiscal_period_id,Fiscal Period Id,BIGINT,,finance.fiscal_period.fiscal_period_id,,,master_data,"Reference to the fiscal period for which this allocation run was executed, linking to the financial calendar.",
finance,cost_management,allocation_run,primary_employee_id,primary_employee_id,Employee Id,BIGINT,,workforce.employee.employee_id,"confidential,pii",,master_data,Reference to the user or system account that initiated or triggered this allocation run.,
finance,cost_management,allocation_run,reversed_allocation_run_id,reversed_allocation_run_id,Reversed Allocation Run Id,BIGINT,,finance.allocation_run.allocation_run_id,,,master_data,"Reference to the original allocation run that this run is reversing, if applicable.",
finance,cost_management,allocation_run,transaction_batch_id,transaction_batch_id,Batch Id,BIGINT,,finance.transaction_batch.transaction_batch_id,,,master_data,Identifier for the batch processing job or financial close cycle that includes this allocation run.,
finance,cost_management,allocation_run,actual_end_timestamp,actual_end_timestamp,Actual End Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,master_data,Actual date and time when the allocation run execution completed or terminated.,
finance,cost_management,allocation_run,actual_start_timestamp,actual_start_timestamp,Actual Start Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,master_data,"Actual date and time when the allocation run execution commenced, representing the principal business event timestamp for this transaction.",
finance,cost_management,allocation_run,allocation_basis,allocation_basis,Allocation Basis,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Description of the statistical or financial basis used for cost allocation (e.g., square footage, FTE count, patient days, relative value units).",
finance,cost_management,allocation_run,allocation_percentage_total,allocation_percentage_total,Allocation Percentage Total,"DECIMAL(5,2)",,,,,master_data,"Sum of all allocation percentages applied across target cost centers, should equal 100.00 for validation purposes.",
finance,cost_management,allocation_run,approval_timestamp,approval_timestamp,Approval Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,master_data,Date and time when the allocation run was formally approved for financial posting.,
finance,cost_management,allocation_run,audit_trail_reference,audit_trail_reference,Audit Trail Reference,STRING,,,,,master_data,Reference identifier linking to detailed audit logs or supporting documentation for this allocation run.,
finance,cost_management,allocation_run,created_timestamp,created_timestamp,Created Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,master_data,Date and time when this allocation run record was first created in the system.,
finance,cost_management,allocation_run,currency_code,currency_code,Currency Code,STRING,,,,,master_data,Three-letter ISO 4217 currency code for all monetary amounts in this allocation run.,
finance,cost_management,allocation_run,error_count,error_count,Error Count,INT,,,,,master_data,Number of errors encountered during the allocation run execution.,
finance,cost_management,allocation_run,execution_duration_seconds,execution_duration_seconds,Execution Duration Seconds,INT,,,,,master_data,"Total elapsed time in seconds for the allocation run execution, used for performance monitoring and optimization.",
finance,cost_management,allocation_run,gl_batch_number,gl_batch_number,Gl Batch Number,STRING,,,,,master_data,General ledger batch identifier associated with the journal entries created from this allocation run.,
finance,cost_management,allocation_run,gl_posting_timestamp,gl_posting_timestamp,Gl Posting Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,master_data,Date and time when the allocation run results were posted to the general ledger system.,
finance,cost_management,allocation_run,last_modified_timestamp,last_modified_timestamp,Last Modified Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,master_data,Date and time when this allocation run record was last updated or modified.,
finance,cost_management,allocation_run,notes,notes,Notes,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Free-text notes or comments regarding the allocation run, including special circumstances, adjustments, or explanations.",
finance,cost_management,allocation_run,posted_to_gl_flag,posted_to_gl_flag,Posted To Gl Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,Indicator whether the allocation results have been posted to the general ledger.,
finance,cost_management,allocation_run,records_processed_count,records_processed_count,Records Processed Count,INT,,,,,master_data,Total number of allocation detail records or transactions processed in this run.,
finance,cost_management,allocation_run,regulatory_reporting_flag,regulatory_reporting_flag,Regulatory Reporting Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,"Indicator whether this allocation run is used for regulatory cost reporting purposes (e.g., Medicare Cost Report).",
finance,cost_management,allocation_run,reversal_flag,reversal_flag,Reversal Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,Indicator whether this allocation run is a reversal of a previous allocation.,
finance,cost_management,allocation_run,run_name,run_name,Run Name,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Descriptive name assigned to the allocation run for identification and reporting purposes, often includes period and allocation type context.",
finance,cost_management,allocation_run,run_number,run_number,Run Number,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Business-facing unique identifier for the allocation run, typically formatted with prefix and sequence number for external reference and audit trails.",
finance,cost_management,allocation_run,run_status,run_status,Run Status,STRING,,,,,master_data,Current lifecycle status of the allocation run indicating its stage in the execution and approval workflow.,
finance,cost_management,allocation_run,run_type,run_type,Run Type,STRING,,,,,master_data,Classification of the allocation run indicating its purpose and finality within the financial close process.,
finance,cost_management,allocation_run,scheduled_start_timestamp,scheduled_start_timestamp,Scheduled Start Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,master_data,Planned date and time when the allocation run was scheduled to begin execution.,
finance,cost_management,allocation_run,simulation_flag,simulation_flag,Simulation Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,Indicator whether this allocation run is a simulation or what-if scenario rather than an actual financial posting.,
finance,cost_management,allocation_run,source_system,source_system,Source System,STRING,,,,,master_data,Name or identifier of the financial system or application that initiated or executed this allocation run.,
finance,cost_management,allocation_run,target_cost_centers_count,target_cost_centers_count,Target Cost Centers Count,INT,,,,,master_data,Number of distinct cost centers that received allocated costs in this run.,
finance,cost_management,allocation_run,total_amount_allocated,total_amount_allocated,Total Amount Allocated,"DECIMAL(18,2)",,,,,master_data,"Total monetary value of costs allocated across all target cost centers in this run, representing the gross base amount for this allocation transaction.",
finance,cost_management,allocation_run,variance_amount,variance_amount,Variance Amount,"DECIMAL(18,2)",,,,,master_data,"Difference between expected and actual allocated amounts, used for reconciliation and quality control.",
finance,cost_management,allocation_run,warning_count,warning_count,Warning Count,INT,,,,,master_data,Number of warnings generated during the allocation run execution.,
finance,cost_management,cost_allocation,cost_allocation_id,cost_allocation_id,Cost Allocation ID,BIGINT,Y,,,,transactional_data,Unique identifier for the cost allocation transaction record.,
finance,cost_management,cost_allocation,allocation_method_id,allocation_method_id,Allocation Method Id,BIGINT,,finance.allocation_method.allocation_method_id,dbx_internal,,transactional_data,FK to finance.allocation_method,
finance,cost_management,cost_allocation,allocation_run_id,allocation_run_id,Allocation Run ID,BIGINT,,finance.allocation_run.allocation_run_id,,,transactional_data,Identifier for the batch allocation run that generated this allocation record. Groups all allocations processed in a single execution cycle.,
finance,cost_management,cost_allocation,care_site_id,care_site_id,Facility ID,BIGINT,,facility.care_site.care_site_id,,,transactional_data,Reference to the healthcare facility or hospital where this cost allocation applies. Supports multi-facility cost accounting.,
finance,cost_management,cost_allocation,chart_of_accounts_id,chart_of_accounts_id,Chart Of Accounts Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,finance.chart_of_accounts.chart_of_accounts_id,,,transactional_data,Foreign key linking to finance.chart_of_accounts. Business justification: cost_allocation has gl_account_code (STRING) which should be normalized to FK to chart_of_accounts. Enables joining to get the GL account for cost allocation posting.,
finance,cost_management,cost_allocation,cost_employee_id,cost_employee_id,Approved By ID,BIGINT,,workforce.employee.employee_id,"dbx_confidential, dbx_pii",,transactional_data,FK to workforce.employee identifying the employee who prepared/executed this cost allocation entry,
finance,cost_management,cost_allocation,fiscal_period_id,fiscal_period_id,Fiscal Period ID,BIGINT,,finance.fiscal_period.fiscal_period_id,,,transactional_data,Reference to the fiscal period in which this cost allocation was executed.,
finance,cost_management,cost_allocation,prior_cost_allocation_id,prior_cost_allocation_id,Original Allocation ID,BIGINT,,finance.cost_allocation.cost_allocation_id,,,transactional_data,"Self-referencing FK to the prior period cost allocation record this entry supersedes, enabling allocation version tracking",
finance,cost_management,cost_allocation,reviewer_employee_id,reviewer_employee_id,Modified By ID,BIGINT,,workforce.employee.employee_id,"dbx_confidential, dbx_pii",,transactional_data,FK to workforce.employee identifying the employee who reviewed and approved this cost allocation entry,
finance,cost_management,cost_allocation,source_cost_center_id,source_cost_center_id,Source Cost Center ID,BIGINT,,finance.cost_center.cost_center_id,,,transactional_data,"The overhead or indirect cost center from which costs are being allocated. Typically represents support departments such as facilities, IT, administration, or housekeeping.",
finance,cost_management,cost_allocation,target_cost_center_id,target_cost_center_id,Target Cost Center ID,BIGINT,,finance.cost_center.cost_center_id,,,transactional_data,"The direct patient care or revenue-generating cost center receiving the allocated costs. Represents departments such as surgery, emergency, radiology, or inpatient units.",
finance,cost_management,cost_allocation,adjustment_reason,adjustment_reason,Adjustment Reason,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,Explanation for any manual adjustment made to the allocated amount. Required for audit trail and variance analysis.,
finance,cost_management,cost_allocation,allocated_amount,allocated_amount,Allocated Amount,"DECIMAL(18,2)",,,,,transactional_data,The dollar amount of overhead or indirect cost allocated from the source cost center to the target cost center in this transaction. Calculated as source cost pool multiplied by allocation basis percentage.,
finance,cost_management,cost_allocation,allocation_adjustment_amount,allocation_adjustment_amount,Allocation Adjustment Amount,"DECIMAL(18,2)",,,,,transactional_data,"Any manual adjustment applied to the calculated allocated amount. Used for corrections, policy adjustments, or rounding reconciliation.",
finance,cost_management,cost_allocation,allocation_basis,allocation_basis,Allocation Basis,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"The statistical or financial metric used to distribute costs from source to target cost centers. Square footage for facilities costs, FTE for HR costs, revenue for administrative overhead, RVU for clinical support, patient days for nursing, labor hours for supervision, transactions for IT, direct cost for proportional allocation, bed count for capacity-based allocation, and visits for outpatient services. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: square_footage|fte|revenue|rvu|patient_days|labor_hours|transactions|direct_cost|bed_count|visits — 10 candidates stripped; promote to reference product]",
finance,cost_management,cost_allocation,allocation_basis_percentage,allocation_basis_percentage,Allocation Basis Percentage,"DECIMAL(7,4)",,,,,transactional_data,The percentage of the total allocation basis that the target cost center represents. Calculated as target quantity divided by sum of all target quantities. Used to distribute source costs proportionally.,
finance,cost_management,cost_allocation,allocation_basis_quantity,allocation_basis_quantity,Allocation Basis Quantity,"DECIMAL(18,4)",,,,,transactional_data,"The numeric quantity of the allocation basis metric for the target cost center. For example, 5000 square feet, 25.5 FTEs, 1200 patient days, or 8500 RVUs.",
finance,cost_management,cost_allocation,allocation_category,allocation_category,Allocation Category,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,The functional category of overhead cost being allocated. Groups allocations by the type of support service provided. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: facilities|information_technology|human_resources|administration|finance|legal|compliance|quality|marketing — 9 candidates stripped; promote to reference product],
finance,cost_management,cost_allocation,allocation_date,allocation_date,Allocation Date,DATE,,,,,transactional_data,The business date on which this cost allocation was executed and recorded. Typically the last day of the fiscal period being allocated.,
finance,cost_management,cost_allocation,allocation_notes,allocation_notes,Allocation Notes,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Free-text field for documenting special circumstances, adjustments, or explanations related to this specific allocation transaction.",
finance,cost_management,cost_allocation,allocation_run_status,allocation_run_status,Allocation Run Status,STRING,,,,draft|pending_approval|approved|posted|reversed|cancelled,transactional_data,"The current lifecycle status of this allocation record. Draft indicates preliminary calculation, pending approval awaits finance review, approved is ready for posting, posted means committed to GL, reversed indicates correction, and cancelled means voided.",
finance,cost_management,cost_allocation,allocation_sequence,allocation_sequence,Allocation Sequence,INT,,,,,transactional_data,The order in which this allocation was processed within the allocation run. Critical for step-down methodology where sequence determines which cost centers allocate first.,
finance,cost_management,cost_allocation,allocation_tier,allocation_tier,Allocation Tier,INT,,,,,transactional_data,"The hierarchical tier or level of this allocation in multi-tier allocation methodologies. Tier 1 represents first-level overhead, tier 2 represents second-level, and so on.",
finance,cost_management,cost_allocation,allocation_version,allocation_version,Allocation Version,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Version identifier for the allocation run. Supports multiple allocation scenarios such as budget, forecast, actual, or what-if analysis.",
finance,cost_management,cost_allocation,approval_date,approval_date,Approval Date,DATE,,,,,transactional_data,The date on which this allocation was reviewed and approved by authorized finance personnel.,
finance,cost_management,cost_allocation,created_timestamp,created_timestamp,Created Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,The date and time when this cost allocation record was first created in the system.,
finance,cost_management,cost_allocation,currency_code,currency_code,Currency Code,STRING,,,,^[A-Z]{3}$,transactional_data,Three-letter ISO 4217 currency code for the allocated amount. Typically USD for U.S. healthcare organizations.,
finance,cost_management,cost_allocation,drg_cost_allocation_flag,drg_cost_allocation_flag,Diagnosis-Related Group (DRG) Cost Allocation Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,Indicates whether this allocation contributes to DRG-based cost calculations for inpatient prospective payment system analysis.,
finance,cost_management,cost_allocation,facility_service_line_code,facility_service_line_code,Service Line Code,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"The clinical service line or product line to which the target cost center belongs. Examples include cardiology, orthopedics, oncology, womens health, or emergency services.",
finance,cost_management,cost_allocation,is_medicare_reportable,is_medicare_reportable,Is Medicare Reportable Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,Indicates whether this allocation must be reported on the Medicare Cost Report (CMS-2552-10) for reimbursement calculation purposes.,
finance,cost_management,cost_allocation,is_reciprocal_allocation,is_reciprocal_allocation,Is Reciprocal Allocation Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,Indicates whether this allocation is part of a reciprocal allocation cycle where two or more cost centers provide mutual services to each other.,
finance,cost_management,cost_allocation,modified_timestamp,modified_timestamp,Modified Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,The date and time when this cost allocation record was last modified.,
finance,cost_management,cost_allocation,posting_date,posting_date,Posting Date,DATE,,,,,transactional_data,The date on which this allocation was posted to the general ledger. May differ from allocation date due to period-end close timing.,
finance,cost_management,cost_allocation,reversal_flag,reversal_flag,Reversal Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,Indicates whether this allocation record represents a reversal of a previously posted allocation. Used for corrections and period adjustments.,
finance,cost_management,cost_allocation,source_cost_pool_amount,source_cost_pool_amount,Source Cost Pool Amount,"DECIMAL(18,2)",,,,,transactional_data,The total amount of costs available in the source cost center for allocation before distribution. Represents the full overhead pool being allocated across all target cost centers.,
finance,cost_management,recurring_schedule,recurring_schedule_id,recurring_schedule_id,Recurring Schedule Identifier,BIGINT,Y,,,,master_data,Primary key for recurring_schedule,
finance,cost_management,recurring_schedule,chart_of_accounts_id,chart_of_accounts_id,Chart Of Accounts Id,BIGINT,,finance.chart_of_accounts.chart_of_accounts_id,,,master_data,Reference to the general ledger account to which this recurring schedule posts transactions.,
finance,cost_management,recurring_schedule,cost_center_id,cost_center_id,Cost Center Id,BIGINT,,finance.cost_center.cost_center_id,,,master_data,Reference to the cost center responsible for or associated with this recurring schedule.,
finance,cost_management,recurring_schedule,fiscal_period_id,fiscal_period_id,Fiscal Period Id,BIGINT,,finance.fiscal_period.fiscal_period_id,,,master_data,Reference to the fiscal year this recurring schedule is associated with.,
finance,cost_management,recurring_schedule,primary_employee_id,primary_employee_id,Approved By User Employee Id,BIGINT,,workforce.employee.employee_id,"confidential,pii",,master_data,Reference to the user who approved this recurring schedule. Null if not yet approved or approval is not required.,
finance,cost_management,recurring_schedule,recurring_employee_id,recurring_employee_id,Owner Employee Id,BIGINT,,workforce.employee.employee_id,"confidential,pii",,master_data,Reference to the employee who owns and is accountable for this recurring schedule.,
finance,cost_management,recurring_schedule,superseded_recurring_schedule_id,superseded_recurring_schedule_id,Superseded Recurring Schedule Id,BIGINT,,finance.recurring_schedule.recurring_schedule_id,dbx_self_ref_fk,,master_data,Self-referencing FK on recurring_schedule (superseded_recurring_schedule_id),
finance,cost_management,recurring_schedule,tertiary_employee_id,tertiary_employee_id,Modified By User Employee Id,BIGINT,,workforce.employee.employee_id,"confidential,pii",,master_data,Reference to the user who last modified this recurring schedule record.,
finance,cost_management,recurring_schedule,adjustment_factor,adjustment_factor,Adjustment Factor,"DECIMAL(10,6)",,,,,master_data,"A multiplier applied to the scheduled amount for adjustments such as inflation, escalation, or volume changes. Default is 1.0 (no adjustment).",
finance,cost_management,recurring_schedule,allocation_method,allocation_method,Allocation Method,STRING,,,,,master_data,"The method used to allocate or distribute the scheduled amount across periods or cost centers (equal distribution, weighted, percentage-based, activity-based costing, or custom formula).",
finance,cost_management,recurring_schedule,approval_required_flag,approval_required_flag,Approval Required Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,Indicates whether generated activities from this schedule require approval before posting (true) or can be posted automatically (false).,
finance,cost_management,recurring_schedule,approved_timestamp,approved_timestamp,Approved Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,master_data,The date and time when this recurring schedule was approved for activation. Null if not yet approved or approval is not required.,
finance,cost_management,recurring_schedule,approver_role_code,approver_role_code,Approver Role Code,BIGINT,,,,,master_data,Reference to the role or user group responsible for approving activities generated by this schedule. Null if approval is not required.,
finance,cost_management,recurring_schedule,auto_generate_flag,auto_generate_flag,Auto Generate Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,Indicates whether scheduled activities are automatically generated by the system (true) or require manual creation (false).,
finance,cost_management,recurring_schedule,business_justification,business_justification,Business Justification,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Explanation of the business rationale and need for this recurring schedule, used for audit and governance purposes.",
finance,cost_management,recurring_schedule,created_timestamp,created_timestamp,Created Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,master_data,The date and time when this recurring schedule record was first created in the system.,
finance,cost_management,recurring_schedule,currency_code,currency_code,Currency Code,STRING,,,,,master_data,Three-letter ISO 4217 currency code indicating the currency in which the scheduled amount is denominated.,
finance,cost_management,recurring_schedule,day_of_month,day_of_month,Day Of Month,INT,,,,,master_data,"For monthly or less frequent schedules, the specific day of the month when the activity occurs (1-31). Null if not applicable.",
finance,cost_management,recurring_schedule,day_of_week,day_of_week,Day Of Week,STRING,,,,,master_data,"For weekly or biweekly schedules, the specific day of the week when the activity occurs. Null if not applicable.",
finance,cost_management,recurring_schedule,effective_end_date,effective_end_date,Effective End Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,The date when this recurring schedule ceases to be active. Null indicates an open-ended schedule.,
finance,cost_management,recurring_schedule,effective_start_date,effective_start_date,Effective Start Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,The date when this recurring schedule becomes active and begins generating scheduled activities.,
finance,cost_management,recurring_schedule,frequency,frequency,Frequency,STRING,,,,,master_data,"The frequency at which the scheduled activity recurs (daily, weekly, biweekly, monthly, quarterly, semiannual, or annual).",
finance,cost_management,recurring_schedule,is_active,is_active,Is Active,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,Indicates whether this recurring schedule is currently active and eligible for generating scheduled activities (true) or inactive (false).,
finance,cost_management,recurring_schedule,last_generated_date,last_generated_date,Last Generated Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,The date when the most recent scheduled activity was generated from this recurring schedule. Null if no activities have been generated yet.,
finance,cost_management,recurring_schedule,max_occurrences,max_occurrences,Max Occurrences,INT,,,,,master_data,The maximum number of times this schedule should generate activities before automatically completing. Null indicates unlimited occurrences.,
finance,cost_management,recurring_schedule,modified_timestamp,modified_timestamp,Modified Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,master_data,The date and time when this recurring schedule record was last modified.,
finance,cost_management,recurring_schedule,month_of_quarter,month_of_quarter,Month Of Quarter,INT,,,,,master_data,"For quarterly schedules, the specific month within the quarter when the activity occurs (1-3). Null if not applicable.",
finance,cost_management,recurring_schedule,next_scheduled_date,next_scheduled_date,Next Scheduled Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,The date when the next scheduled activity is due to be generated from this recurring schedule.,
finance,cost_management,recurring_schedule,notes,notes,Notes,STRING,,,,,master_data,Additional free-form notes or comments about the recurring schedule for operational reference.,
finance,cost_management,recurring_schedule,occurrence_count,occurrence_count,Occurrence Count,INT,,,,,master_data,The total number of times activities have been generated from this recurring schedule since its inception.,
finance,cost_management,recurring_schedule,proration_rule,proration_rule,Proration Rule,STRING,,,,,master_data,"The rule used to prorate amounts for partial periods (none, daily proration, monthly proration, actual days, or business days only).",
finance,cost_management,recurring_schedule,quarter_of_year,quarter_of_year,Quarter Of Year,INT,,,,,master_data,"For annual schedules, the specific quarter of the year when the activity occurs (1-4). Null if not applicable.",
finance,cost_management,recurring_schedule,recurring_schedule_description,recurring_schedule_description,Description,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Detailed textual description of the recurring schedule, including its purpose, scope, and any special instructions or business rules.",
finance,cost_management,recurring_schedule,recurring_schedule_status,recurring_schedule_status,Status,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Current lifecycle status of the recurring schedule indicating whether it is in draft, actively generating activities, temporarily suspended, completed, or cancelled.",
finance,cost_management,recurring_schedule,schedule_amount,schedule_amount,Schedule Amount,"DECIMAL(18,2)",,,,,master_data,"The standard monetary amount associated with each recurrence of this schedule. Used for budgeting, allocation, or accrual purposes.",
finance,cost_management,recurring_schedule,schedule_category,schedule_category,Schedule Category,STRING,,,,,master_data,High-level categorization of the schedule based on the nature of financial activities it governs.,
finance,cost_management,recurring_schedule,schedule_code,schedule_code,Schedule Code,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Business identifier code for the recurring schedule, used for external reference and reporting.",
finance,cost_management,recurring_schedule,schedule_name,schedule_name,Schedule Name,STRING,,,,,master_data,Human-readable name describing the purpose or nature of the recurring schedule.,
finance,cost_management,recurring_schedule,schedule_type,schedule_type,Schedule Type,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Classification of the recurring schedule indicating its financial purpose (budget cycle, forecast period, cost allocation, accrual recognition, depreciation schedule, or amortization schedule).",
finance,cost_management,recurring_schedule,version_number,version_number,Version Number,INT,,,,,master_data,"Version number of this recurring schedule record, incremented with each modification for change tracking and audit purposes.",
finance,ledger_accounting,chart_of_accounts,chart_of_accounts_id,chart_of_accounts_id,Chart of Accounts (COA) Identifier,BIGINT,Y,,,,master_data,Unique identifier for the chart of accounts entry. Primary key for the chart of accounts master catalog.,
finance,ledger_accounting,chart_of_accounts,parent_chart_of_accounts_id,parent_chart_of_accounts_id,Parent Chart Of Accounts Id,BIGINT,,finance.chart_of_accounts.chart_of_accounts_id,dbx_self_ref_fk,,master_data,Self-referencing FK on chart_of_accounts (parent_chart_of_accounts_id),
finance,ledger_accounting,chart_of_accounts,account_category,account_category,Account Category,STRING,,,,,master_data,"High-level grouping of accounts for reporting and analysis purposes. Examples include patient service revenue, supply expense, labor expense, administrative expense.",
finance,ledger_accounting,chart_of_accounts,account_code,account_code,General Ledger (GL) Account Code,STRING,,,,"^[0-9]{4,10}$",master_data,"The unique alphanumeric code identifying the general ledger account. This is the primary business identifier used in journal entries, budgets, and financial statements.",
finance,ledger_accounting,chart_of_accounts,account_description,account_description,Account Description,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Detailed textual description of the account purpose, usage guidelines, and any special instructions for posting transactions. Provides context for finance staff and auditors.",
finance,ledger_accounting,chart_of_accounts,account_name,account_name,General Ledger (GL) Account Name,STRING,,,,,master_data,The full descriptive name of the general ledger account. Human-readable label used in financial reports and user interfaces.,
finance,ledger_accounting,chart_of_accounts,account_owner,account_owner,Account Owner,STRING,,,,,master_data,"The name or identifier of the department, role, or individual responsible for managing and monitoring this account. Supports accountability and financial stewardship.",
finance,ledger_accounting,chart_of_accounts,account_status,account_status,Account Status,STRING,,,,active|inactive|suspended|pending_closure,master_data,Current lifecycle status of the account. Active accounts are available for use in transactions; inactive accounts are closed and cannot be used in new entries.,
finance,ledger_accounting,chart_of_accounts,account_subcategory,account_subcategory,Account Subcategory,STRING,,,,,master_data,Detailed grouping within the account category providing additional analytical granularity. Supports drill-down reporting and variance analysis.,
finance,ledger_accounting,chart_of_accounts,account_subtype,account_subtype,Account Subtype Classification,STRING,,,,,master_data,"The secondary classification providing additional granularity within the account type. Examples include current asset, fixed asset, operating expense, non-operating revenue, etc.",
finance,ledger_accounting,chart_of_accounts,account_type,account_type,Account Type Classification,STRING,,,,asset|liability|equity|revenue|expense,master_data,The primary classification of the account according to the fundamental accounting equation. Determines which financial statement the account appears on and its natural balance.,
finance,ledger_accounting,chart_of_accounts,alternate_account_code,alternate_account_code,Alternate Account Code,STRING,,,,,master_data,An alternate or legacy account code used for cross-reference purposes during system migrations or for integration with external systems.,
finance,ledger_accounting,chart_of_accounts,approval_required_flag,approval_required_flag,Approval Required Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,Indicates whether transactions posted to this account require additional approval beyond standard posting authority. True for sensitive or high-risk accounts.,
finance,ledger_accounting,chart_of_accounts,budget_control_flag,budget_control_flag,Budget Control Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,Indicates whether transactions against this account are subject to budget availability checking. True for expense accounts with budget controls.,
finance,ledger_accounting,chart_of_accounts,consolidation_account_code,consolidation_account_code,Consolidation Account Code,STRING,,,,,master_data,The account code used in consolidated financial statements when multiple legal entities are combined. Supports multi-entity healthcare system reporting.,
finance,ledger_accounting,chart_of_accounts,cost_center_applicable_flag,cost_center_applicable_flag,Cost Center Applicable Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,Indicates whether this account requires a cost center assignment when used in journal entries or budget allocations. True for departmental expense and revenue accounts.,
finance,ledger_accounting,chart_of_accounts,created_timestamp,created_timestamp,Record Created Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,master_data,The date and time when this chart of accounts entry was first created in the system. Supports audit trail and data lineage tracking.,
finance,ledger_accounting,chart_of_accounts,currency_code,currency_code,Currency Code,STRING,,,,^[A-Z]{3}$,master_data,The three-letter ISO 4217 currency code for this account. Supports multi-currency accounting for international healthcare operations.,
finance,ledger_accounting,chart_of_accounts,department_applicable_flag,department_applicable_flag,Department Applicable Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,Indicates whether this account requires a department assignment when used in transactions. Supports departmental financial reporting and cost allocation.,
finance,ledger_accounting,chart_of_accounts,drg_cost_allocation_flag,drg_cost_allocation_flag,Diagnosis-Related Group (DRG) Cost Allocation Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,Indicates whether costs in this account are allocated to DRG-based cost accounting for case mix analysis and reimbursement optimization.,
finance,ledger_accounting,chart_of_accounts,effective_end_date,effective_end_date,Effective End Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,The date on which this account becomes inactive and is no longer available for new transactions. Null for currently active accounts with no planned closure date.,
finance,ledger_accounting,chart_of_accounts,effective_start_date,effective_start_date,Effective Start Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,The date from which this account becomes active and available for use in financial transactions. Supports temporal validity and historical account structure tracking.,
finance,ledger_accounting,chart_of_accounts,external_reporting_code,external_reporting_code,External Reporting Code,STRING,,,,,master_data,"The code or identifier used for external regulatory reporting such as Medicare Cost Reports, state financial reporting, or bond covenant reporting.",
finance,ledger_accounting,chart_of_accounts,financial_statement_classification,financial_statement_classification,Financial Statement Classification,STRING,,,,balance_sheet|income_statement|cash_flow_statement|statement_of_changes_in_equity,master_data,Identifies which primary financial statement this account appears on. Critical for automated financial statement generation and reporting.,
finance,ledger_accounting,chart_of_accounts,financial_statement_line_item,financial_statement_line_item,Financial Statement Line Item,STRING,,,,,master_data,"The specific line item or section within the financial statement where this account balance is reported. Examples include current assets, operating expenses, net patient service revenue.",
finance,ledger_accounting,chart_of_accounts,fund_applicable_flag,fund_applicable_flag,Fund Applicable Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,"Indicates whether this account requires a fund assignment for fund accounting purposes. Relevant for healthcare organizations with restricted grants, endowments, or governmental funding.",
finance,ledger_accounting,chart_of_accounts,gaap_classification,gaap_classification,Generally Accepted Accounting Principles (GAAP) Classification,STRING,,,,,master_data,The specific GAAP classification code or category for this account. Ensures compliance with US GAAP financial reporting requirements.,
finance,ledger_accounting,chart_of_accounts,gasb_classification,gasb_classification,Governmental Accounting Standards Board (GASB) Classification,STRING,,,,,master_data,The GASB classification for governmental and not-for-profit healthcare entities. Applicable for public hospitals and healthcare systems.,
finance,ledger_accounting,chart_of_accounts,intercompany_flag,intercompany_flag,Intercompany Transaction Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,Indicates whether this account is used for intercompany transactions between legal entities within the healthcare system. Supports consolidation and elimination entries.,
finance,ledger_accounting,chart_of_accounts,modified_timestamp,modified_timestamp,Record Modified Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,master_data,The date and time when this chart of accounts entry was last modified. Supports change tracking and audit compliance.,
finance,ledger_accounting,chart_of_accounts,natural_balance,natural_balance,Natural Balance Indicator,STRING,,,,debit|credit,master_data,"Indicates whether the account normally carries a debit or credit balance. Assets and expenses have debit natural balances; liabilities, equity, and revenue have credit natural balances.",
finance,ledger_accounting,chart_of_accounts,posting_restriction,posting_restriction,Posting Restriction,STRING,,,,none|manual_only|system_only|restricted,master_data,Defines restrictions on how transactions can be posted to this account. Manual-only accounts prevent automated postings; system-only accounts prevent manual journal entries.,
finance,ledger_accounting,chart_of_accounts,project_applicable_flag,project_applicable_flag,Project Applicable Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,"Indicates whether this account can be used for project-based accounting and requires a project code assignment. Common for capital projects, research grants, and special initiatives.",
finance,ledger_accounting,chart_of_accounts,reconciliation_required_flag,reconciliation_required_flag,Reconciliation Required Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,"Indicates whether this account requires periodic reconciliation to external statements or subsidiary ledgers. True for cash, accounts receivable, accounts payable, and other balance sheet accounts.",
finance,ledger_accounting,chart_of_accounts,rollup_account_code,rollup_account_code,Rollup Account Code,STRING,,,,,master_data,The parent or summary account code to which this account rolls up for consolidated reporting. Supports hierarchical financial statement presentation.,
finance,ledger_accounting,chart_of_accounts,rvu_allocation_flag,rvu_allocation_flag,Relative Value Unit (RVU) Allocation Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,Indicates whether costs in this account are allocated based on relative value units for physician productivity and compensation analysis.,
finance,ledger_accounting,chart_of_accounts,statistical_account_flag,statistical_account_flag,Statistical Account Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,"Indicates whether this is a statistical account used to track non-monetary metrics such as patient days, procedures performed, or full-time equivalents (FTEs). Statistical accounts do not carry monetary balances.",
finance,ledger_accounting,chart_of_accounts,tax_reporting_category,tax_reporting_category,Tax Reporting Category,STRING,,,,,master_data,The tax reporting classification for this account. Used for IRS Form 990 reporting for not-for-profit healthcare entities and other tax compliance purposes.,
finance,ledger_accounting,cost_center,cost_center_id,cost_center_id,Cost Center ID,BIGINT,Y,,,,master_data,Unique identifier for the cost center. Primary key for the cost center master record.,
finance,ledger_accounting,cost_center,care_site_id,care_site_id,Facility ID,BIGINT,,facility.care_site.care_site_id,,,master_data,Reference to the healthcare facility or care site where this cost center operates. Links cost center to physical location for facility-level financial reporting and multi-site cost analysis.,
finance,ledger_accounting,cost_center,fund_id,fund_id,Fund Id,BIGINT,,finance.fund.fund_id,dbx_internal,,master_data,FK to finance.fund,
finance,ledger_accounting,cost_center,general_ledger_chart_of_accounts_id,general_ledger_chart_of_accounts_id,General Ledger Chart Of Accounts Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,finance.chart_of_accounts.chart_of_accounts_id,,,master_data,Foreign key linking to finance.chart_of_accounts. Business justification: cost_center has general_ledger_account (STRING) which should be normalized to FK to chart_of_accounts. Using general_ledger_chart_of_accounts_id as the FK name to be explicit. Enables joining to get,
finance,ledger_accounting,cost_center,parent_cost_center_id,parent_cost_center_id,Parent Cost Center ID,BIGINT,,finance.cost_center.cost_center_id,,,master_data,Reference to the parent cost center in the organizational cost center hierarchy. Enables roll-up reporting and hierarchical cost allocation. Null for top-level cost centers.,
finance,ledger_accounting,cost_center,budget_amount,budget_amount,Budget Amount,"DECIMAL(18,2)",,,dbx_confidential,,master_data,"The approved annual budget allocation for this cost center in US dollars. Used for budget variance analysis, financial planning, and departmental performance measurement.",
finance,ledger_accounting,cost_center,budget_fiscal_year,budget_fiscal_year,Budget Fiscal Year,INT,,,,,master_data,The fiscal year for which the budget amount is allocated. Enables multi-year budget tracking and year-over-year cost center performance comparison.,
finance,ledger_accounting,cost_center,cms_provider_number,cms_provider_number,Centers for Medicare and Medicaid Services (CMS) Provider Number,STRING,,,,^[0-9]{6}$,master_data,The CMS-assigned provider number for the facility or organizational unit associated with this cost center. Used for Medicare cost reporting and regulatory compliance.,
finance,ledger_accounting,cost_center,cost_allocation_method,cost_allocation_method,Cost Allocation Method,STRING,,,,direct|step_down|activity_based|relative_value_unit,master_data,"The methodology used to allocate indirect costs to this cost center. Direct allocation assigns costs directly, step-down allocation cascades costs through support departments, activity-based costing allocates based on resource consumption, and RVU-based allocation uses relative value units for clinical departments.",
finance,ledger_accounting,cost_center,cost_center_category,cost_center_category,Cost Center Category,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Additional categorical classification for specialized cost center grouping beyond the primary type. Examples include inpatient, outpatient, emergency, surgical, diagnostic, therapeutic, administrative. Used for detailed financial analysis and reporting.",
finance,ledger_accounting,cost_center,cost_center_code,cost_center_code,Cost Center Code,STRING,,,,"^[A-Z0-9]{4,12}$",master_data,"The externally-known unique alphanumeric code identifying the cost center within the healthcare organizations chart of accounts. Used for financial reporting, budget tracking, and departmental cost allocation.",
finance,ledger_accounting,cost_center,cost_center_name,cost_center_name,Cost Center Name,STRING,,,,,master_data,"The full descriptive name of the cost center, representing the department, unit, or functional area for which costs are tracked and budgeted.",
finance,ledger_accounting,cost_center,cost_center_status,cost_center_status,Cost Center Status,STRING,,,,active|inactive|pending|closed|suspended,master_data,"Current lifecycle status of the cost center. Active cost centers are operational and accepting charges, inactive cost centers are temporarily disabled, pending cost centers are awaiting approval, closed cost centers are permanently retired, and suspended cost centers are on hold pending review.",
finance,ledger_accounting,cost_center,cost_center_type,cost_center_type,Cost Center Type,STRING,,,,clinical|administrative|ancillary|overhead|support|revenue,master_data,"Classification of the cost center by its primary business function. Clinical cost centers provide direct patient care, administrative cost centers support operations, ancillary cost centers provide diagnostic or therapeutic services, overhead cost centers represent shared services, support cost centers provide enabling functions, and revenue cost centers generate billable services.",
finance,ledger_accounting,cost_center,cost_per_unit,cost_per_unit,Cost Per Unit,"DECIMAL(12,2)",,,dbx_confidential,,master_data,"The average cost per unit of service delivered by this cost center. Unit definition varies by cost center type (e.g., cost per patient day, cost per procedure, cost per visit). Used for efficiency benchmarking and pricing analysis.",
finance,ledger_accounting,cost_center,created_timestamp,created_timestamp,Created Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,master_data,The date and time when this cost center record was first created in the system. Used for audit trail and data lineage tracking.,
finance,ledger_accounting,cost_center,department_code,department_code,Department Code,STRING,,,,"^[A-Z0-9]{2,8}$",master_data,"The organizational department code to which this cost center belongs. Used for departmental grouping, workforce planning, and operational reporting.",
finance,ledger_accounting,cost_center,department_name,department_name,Department Name,STRING,,,,,master_data,The full name of the department to which this cost center is assigned. Provides human-readable context for departmental cost analysis and reporting.,
finance,ledger_accounting,cost_center,drg_weight,drg_weight,Diagnosis-Related Group (DRG) Weight,"DECIMAL(6,4)",,,,,master_data,"The average DRG case mix weight for patients treated in this cost center. Used for case mix index calculation, reimbursement analysis, and clinical complexity adjustment. Applicable primarily to inpatient clinical cost centers.",
finance,ledger_accounting,cost_center,effective_end_date,effective_end_date,Effective End Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,The date on which this cost center was closed or inactivated. Null for currently active cost centers. Used for historical cost analysis and departmental lifecycle management.,
finance,ledger_accounting,cost_center,effective_start_date,effective_start_date,Effective Start Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,The date on which this cost center became active and began accepting financial transactions. Used for historical cost tracking and period-based financial reporting.,
finance,ledger_accounting,cost_center,facility_service_line,facility_service_line,Service Line,STRING,,,,,master_data,"The clinical or operational service line to which this cost center contributes. Examples include cardiology, orthopedics, oncology, emergency services, surgical services. Used for service line profitability analysis and strategic planning.",
finance,ledger_accounting,cost_center,fte_allocation,fte_allocation,Full-Time Equivalent (FTE) Allocation,"DECIMAL(8,2)",,,dbx_confidential,,master_data,"The approved number of full-time equivalent positions allocated to this cost center. Used for workforce planning, labor cost analysis, and productivity measurement.",
finance,ledger_accounting,cost_center,is_capital_intensive,is_capital_intensive,Is Capital Intensive,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,"Indicates whether this cost center requires significant capital equipment investment. True for departments with major medical equipment (e.g., radiology, surgical services, laboratory), false for labor-intensive departments. Used for capital budgeting and depreciation allocation.",
finance,ledger_accounting,cost_center,is_direct_patient_care,is_direct_patient_care,Is Direct Patient Care,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,"Indicates whether this cost center provides direct patient care services. True for clinical departments with patient contact, false for support and administrative departments. Used for clinical cost allocation and quality reporting.",
finance,ledger_accounting,cost_center,is_revenue_generating,is_revenue_generating,Is Revenue Generating,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,"Indicates whether this cost center generates billable revenue through patient services. True for clinical and ancillary departments that bill for services, false for administrative and overhead departments.",
finance,ledger_accounting,cost_center,last_modified_by,last_modified_by,Last Modified By,STRING,,,,,master_data,The user ID or name of the person who last modified this cost center record. Used for accountability and audit trail purposes.,
finance,ledger_accounting,cost_center,last_modified_timestamp,last_modified_timestamp,Last Modified Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,master_data,The date and time when this cost center record was most recently updated. Used for change tracking and audit compliance.,
finance,ledger_accounting,cost_center,notes,notes,Cost Center Notes,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Free-text field for additional comments, special instructions, or contextual information about the cost center. Used for documenting organizational changes, budget justifications, or operational considerations.",
finance,ledger_accounting,cost_center,regulatory_reporting_required,regulatory_reporting_required,Regulatory Reporting Required,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,"Indicates whether this cost center is subject to specific regulatory reporting requirements (e.g., CMS cost reports, state health department reporting, Joint Commission reporting). Used for compliance tracking and audit preparation.",
finance,ledger_accounting,cost_center,rvu_target,rvu_target,Relative Value Unit (RVU) Target,"DECIMAL(12,2)",,,,,master_data,"The target number of relative value units this cost center is expected to generate annually. Used for physician productivity measurement, reimbursement forecasting, and clinical efficiency analysis. Applicable to clinical cost centers with physician services.",
finance,ledger_accounting,cost_center,unit_of_measure,unit_of_measure,Unit of Measure,STRING,,,,,master_data,"The unit of service used to measure cost center activity and calculate cost per unit. Examples include patient days, procedures, visits, tests, hours, admissions. Varies by cost center type and service line.",
finance,ledger_accounting,finance_journal_entry,finance_journal_entry_id,finance_journal_entry_id,Journal Entry ID,BIGINT,Y,,,,transactional_data,Unique identifier for the journal entry record. Primary key for the journal entry entity.,
finance,ledger_accounting,finance_journal_entry,cost_center_id,cost_center_id,Cost Center ID,BIGINT,,finance.cost_center.cost_center_id,,,transactional_data,Identifier of the primary cost center associated with this journal entry. Used for departmental and responsibility accounting.,
finance,ledger_accounting,finance_journal_entry,finance_employee_id,finance_employee_id,Approver ID,BIGINT,,workforce.employee.employee_id,"dbx_confidential, dbx_pii",,transactional_data,FK to workforce.employee identifying the primary approver of this journal entry,
finance,ledger_accounting,finance_journal_entry,financial_entity_id,financial_entity_id,Entity ID,BIGINT,,finance.financial_entity.financial_entity_id,,,transactional_data,Identifier of the legal entity or business unit to which this journal entry belongs. Critical for multi-entity consolidation and reporting.,
finance,ledger_accounting,finance_journal_entry,fiscal_period_id,fiscal_period_id,Fiscal Period Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,finance.fiscal_period.fiscal_period_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to finance.fiscal_period. Business justification: journal_entry has accounting_period (STRING) which should be normalized to FK to fiscal_period master. Enables joining to get period details (start_date, end_date, period_status, close_date) and ensur",
finance,ledger_accounting,finance_journal_entry,primary_employee_id,primary_employee_id,Preparer ID,BIGINT,,workforce.employee.employee_id,"dbx_confidential, dbx_pii",,transactional_data,FK to workforce.employee identifying the primary preparer of this journal entry,
finance,ledger_accounting,finance_journal_entry,primary_reversal_journal_entry_finance_journal_entry_id,primary_reversal_journal_entry_finance_journal_entry_id,Reversal Journal Entry ID,BIGINT,,finance.finance_journal_entry.finance_journal_entry_id,,,transactional_data,"Reference to the journal entry that reversed this entry, if applicable. Null if the entry has not been reversed.",
finance,ledger_accounting,finance_journal_entry,recurring_schedule_id,recurring_schedule_id,Recurring Schedule ID,BIGINT,,finance.recurring_schedule.recurring_schedule_id,,,transactional_data,"Identifier of the recurring schedule template from which this entry was generated, if applicable. Null for non-recurring entries.",
finance,ledger_accounting,finance_journal_entry,adjustment_type,adjustment_type,Adjustment Type,STRING,,,,standard|prior_period|audit|reclassification|correction,transactional_data,"Classification of adjustment entries. Identifies whether the entry is a standard posting, prior period adjustment, audit adjustment, reclassification, or error correction.",
finance,ledger_accounting,finance_journal_entry,approval_date,approval_date,Approval Date,DATE,,,,,transactional_data,The date on which the journal entry was approved by the designated approver. Null for entries not requiring approval or pending approval.,
finance,ledger_accounting,finance_journal_entry,audit_trail_reference,audit_trail_reference,Audit Trail Reference,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,Reference identifier linking this journal entry to external audit documentation or audit trail systems. Used for regulatory compliance and audit support.,
finance,ledger_accounting,finance_journal_entry,batch_code,batch_code,Batch ID,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,Identifier for the batch or group of journal entries processed together. Used for bulk posting and batch reconciliation.,
finance,ledger_accounting,finance_journal_entry,consolidation_indicator,consolidation_indicator,Consolidation Indicator,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,"Boolean flag indicating whether this journal entry is included in consolidated financial reporting. True if included, False if excluded.",
finance,ledger_accounting,finance_journal_entry,created_timestamp,created_timestamp,Created Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,System timestamp indicating when this journal entry record was first created in the system. Used for audit trail and data lineage.,
finance,ledger_accounting,finance_journal_entry,currency_code,currency_code,Currency Code,STRING,,,,^[A-Z]{3}$,transactional_data,Three-letter ISO 4217 currency code representing the currency in which the journal entry amounts are denominated.,
finance,ledger_accounting,finance_journal_entry,effective_date,effective_date,Effective Date,DATE,,,,,transactional_data,The business date for which the journal entry is effective. This may differ from the posting date and represents the actual accounting period impact date.,
finance,ledger_accounting,finance_journal_entry,entry_date,entry_date,,DATE,,,,,transactional_data,Date the journal entry was recorded,
finance,ledger_accounting,finance_journal_entry,exchange_rate,exchange_rate,Exchange Rate,"DECIMAL(12,6)",,,,,transactional_data,"The foreign exchange rate applied to convert foreign currency amounts to the functional currency, if applicable. Null for entries in functional currency.",
finance,ledger_accounting,finance_journal_entry,fiscal_year,fiscal_year,Fiscal Year,INT,,,,,transactional_data,The fiscal year to which this journal entry belongs. Used for annual financial reporting and multi-year analysis.,
finance,ledger_accounting,finance_journal_entry,functional_currency_code,functional_currency_code,Functional Currency Code,STRING,,,,^[A-Z]{3}$,transactional_data,Three-letter ISO 4217 code for the functional currency of the reporting entity. Used when the entry currency differs from the functional currency.,
finance,ledger_accounting,finance_journal_entry,gl_interface_status,gl_interface_status,General Ledger (GL) Interface Status,STRING,,,,pending|transmitted|accepted|rejected|error,transactional_data,Status of the journal entry in the interface process to the general ledger system. Tracks whether the entry has been successfully transmitted and accepted.,
finance,ledger_accounting,finance_journal_entry,intercompany_indicator,intercompany_indicator,Intercompany Indicator,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,"Boolean flag indicating whether this journal entry represents an intercompany transaction between related entities. True for intercompany, False otherwise.",
finance,ledger_accounting,finance_journal_entry,journal_category,journal_category,Journal Category,STRING,,,,accrual|cash_receipt|payroll|depreciation|intercompany|adjustment,transactional_data,"Classification of the journal entry by accounting treatment type. Common categories include accrual entries, cash receipts, payroll postings, depreciation calculations, intercompany transactions, and adjusting entries.",
finance,ledger_accounting,finance_journal_entry,journal_entry_description,journal_entry_description,Journal Entry Description,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,Detailed narrative description of the purpose and nature of the journal entry. Provides business context for the accounting transaction.,
finance,ledger_accounting,finance_journal_entry,journal_entry_number,journal_entry_number,Journal Entry Number,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Business identifier for the journal entry, typically a sequential or formatted number used for external reference and audit trails.",
finance,ledger_accounting,finance_journal_entry,journal_source,journal_source,Journal Source,STRING,,,,manual|system_generated|recurring|reversing|automated|interface,transactional_data,"Origin or method by which the journal entry was created. Indicates whether the entry was manually entered, automatically generated by a system process, part of a recurring schedule, or a reversing entry.",
finance,ledger_accounting,finance_journal_entry,modified_timestamp,modified_timestamp,Modified Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,System timestamp indicating when this journal entry record was last modified. Used for audit trail and change tracking.,
finance,ledger_accounting,finance_journal_entry,notes,notes,Journal Entry Notes,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,Additional free-form notes or comments related to the journal entry. Used for supplementary information not captured in structured fields.,
finance,ledger_accounting,finance_journal_entry,posted_timestamp,posted_timestamp,Posted Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,System timestamp indicating when this journal entry was posted to the general ledger. Null for entries not yet posted.,
finance,ledger_accounting,finance_journal_entry,posting_date,posting_date,Posting Date,DATE,,,,,transactional_data,The date on which the journal entry was posted to the general ledger. This is the system date when the entry became part of the official accounting records.,
finance,ledger_accounting,finance_journal_entry,posting_status,posting_status,Posting Status,STRING,,,,draft|pending_approval|approved|posted|reversed|rejected,transactional_data,"Current lifecycle status of the journal entry. Tracks progression from draft through approval, posting, and potential reversal.",
finance,ledger_accounting,finance_journal_entry,recurring_entry_indicator,recurring_entry_indicator,Recurring Entry Indicator,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,"Boolean flag indicating whether this journal entry is part of a recurring schedule. True for recurring entries, False for one-time entries.",
finance,ledger_accounting,finance_journal_entry,regulatory_reporting_indicator,regulatory_reporting_indicator,Regulatory Reporting Indicator,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,"Boolean flag indicating whether this journal entry impacts regulatory reporting requirements such as CMS cost reports or state financial filings. True if reportable, False otherwise.",
finance,ledger_accounting,finance_journal_entry,reversal_date,reversal_date,Reversal Date,DATE,,,,,transactional_data,The date on which this journal entry was reversed. Null if the entry has not been reversed.,
finance,ledger_accounting,finance_journal_entry,reversal_indicator,reversal_indicator,Reversal Indicator,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,"Boolean flag indicating whether this journal entry has been reversed. True if reversed, False if active.",
finance,ledger_accounting,finance_journal_entry,reversal_reason_code,reversal_reason_code,Reversal Reason Code,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Code indicating the reason for reversing this journal entry, if applicable. Examples include error correction, period adjustment, or policy change.",
finance,ledger_accounting,finance_journal_entry,source_system_code,source_system_code,Source System Code,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Code identifying the originating system or module that generated this journal entry. Examples include Epic Resolute, SAP FI, Workday, or manual entry.",
finance,ledger_accounting,finance_journal_entry,source_transaction_reference,source_transaction_reference,Source Transaction ID,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,Identifier of the originating transaction in the source system that triggered this journal entry. Used for traceability and reconciliation.,
finance,ledger_accounting,finance_journal_entry,supporting_document_reference,supporting_document_reference,Supporting Document Reference,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Reference identifier or URI to supporting documentation for this journal entry, such as invoices, contracts, or approval memos. Used for audit and compliance.",
finance,ledger_accounting,finance_journal_entry,total_credit_amount,total_credit_amount,Total Credit Amount,"DECIMAL(18,2)",,,,,transactional_data,The sum of all credit amounts across all line items in this journal entry. Must equal total debit amount for a balanced entry.,
finance,ledger_accounting,finance_journal_entry,total_debit_amount,total_debit_amount,Total Debit Amount,"DECIMAL(18,2)",,,,,transactional_data,The sum of all debit amounts across all line items in this journal entry. Must equal total credit amount for a balanced entry.,
finance,ledger_accounting,finance_journal_entry_line,finance_journal_entry_line_id,finance_journal_entry_line_id,Journal Entry Line Identifier (ID),BIGINT,Y,,,,transactional_data,Unique identifier for the journal entry line. Primary key for the journal entry line product.,
