finance,ledger_accounting,finance_journal_entry_line,fund_id,fund_id,Fund Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,finance.fund.fund_id,,,transactional_data,Foreign key linking to finance.fund. Business justification: journal_entry_line has fund_code (STRING) which should be normalized to FK to fund master. Enables joining to get fund details for fund accounting at the journal entry line level.,
finance,ledger_accounting,finance_journal_entry_line,primary_employee_id,primary_employee_id,Approved By User Identifier (ID),BIGINT,,workforce.employee.employee_id,"dbx_confidential, dbx_pii",,transactional_data,FK to workforce.employee identifying the employee who approved this individual journal entry line,
finance,ledger_accounting,finance_journal_entry_line,prior_journal_entry_line_finance_journal_entry_line_id,prior_journal_entry_line_finance_journal_entry_line_id,Reversed Journal Entry Line Identifier (ID),BIGINT,,finance.finance_journal_entry_line.finance_journal_entry_line_id,,,transactional_data,Reference to the original journal entry line that this line reverses. Null if this is not a reversal entry. Provides audit trail for corrections.,
finance,ledger_accounting,finance_journal_entry_line,approved_timestamp,approved_timestamp,Approved Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,The date and time when this journal entry line was approved for posting. Format: yyyy-MM-ddTHH:mm:ss.SSSXXX. Null if not yet approved. Used for audit trail.,
finance,ledger_accounting,finance_journal_entry_line,created_timestamp,created_timestamp,Created Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,The date and time when this journal entry line record was first created in the system. Format: yyyy-MM-ddTHH:mm:ss.SSSXXX. Used for audit trail.,
finance,ledger_accounting,finance_journal_entry_line,credit_amount,credit_amount,Credit Amount,"DECIMAL(18,2)",,,,,transactional_data,"The credit amount for this journal entry line in functional currency. Zero or null if this is a debit line. Credits increase liability, equity, and revenue accounts.",
finance,ledger_accounting,finance_journal_entry_line,debit_amount,debit_amount,Debit Amount,"DECIMAL(18,2)",,,,,transactional_data,The debit amount for this journal entry line in functional currency. Zero or null if this is a credit line. Debits increase asset and expense accounts.,
finance,ledger_accounting,finance_journal_entry_line,department_code,department_code,Department Code,STRING,,,,"^[A-Z0-9]{3,10}$",transactional_data,Department segment code for detailed organizational reporting. Provides finer granularity than cost center for departmental analysis.,
finance,ledger_accounting,finance_journal_entry_line,exchange_rate,exchange_rate,Exchange Rate,"DECIMAL(12,6)",,,,,transactional_data,The exchange rate used to convert transaction currency to functional currency. Expressed as functional currency per unit of transaction currency.,
finance,ledger_accounting,finance_journal_entry_line,fiscal_year,fiscal_year,Fiscal Year,INT,,,,,transactional_data,The fiscal year to which this journal entry line belongs. Used for annual financial reporting and multi-year analysis.,
finance,ledger_accounting,finance_journal_entry_line,functional_currency_code,functional_currency_code,Functional Currency Code,STRING,,,,^[A-Z]{3}$,transactional_data,The functional currency of the organization in which the debit and credit amounts are recorded. Three-letter ISO 4217 currency code.,
finance,ledger_accounting,finance_journal_entry_line,intercompany_entity_code,intercompany_entity_code,Intercompany Entity Code,STRING,,,,"^[A-Z0-9]{2,10}$",transactional_data,The code of the counterparty legal entity for intercompany transactions. Used for intercompany reconciliation and elimination entries during consolidation.,
