finance,ledger_accounting,general_ledger,general_ledger_id,general_ledger_id,General Ledger (GL) Identifier,BIGINT,Y,,,,master_data,Unique identifier for the general ledger. Primary key for the general ledger data product.,
finance,ledger_accounting,general_ledger,chart_of_accounts_id,chart_of_accounts_id,Chart of Accounts (COA) Identifier,BIGINT,,finance.chart_of_accounts.chart_of_accounts_id,,,master_data,Foreign key reference to the chart of accounts structure that defines the account hierarchy and classification framework for this ledger. Determines the available GL accounts for journal entry postings.,
finance,ledger_accounting,general_ledger,financial_entity_id,financial_entity_id,Legal Entity Identifier,BIGINT,,finance.financial_entity.financial_entity_id,,,master_data,Foreign key reference to the legal entity that owns and operates this general ledger. Establishes the organizational boundary for financial reporting and regulatory compliance.,
finance,ledger_accounting,general_ledger,parent_general_ledger_id,parent_general_ledger_id,Parent General Ledger Id,BIGINT,,finance.general_ledger.general_ledger_id,dbx_self_ref_fk,,master_data,Self-referencing FK on general_ledger (parent_general_ledger_id),
finance,ledger_accounting,general_ledger,accounting_basis,accounting_basis,Accounting Basis,STRING,,,,accrual|cash|modified_accrual,master_data,"The fundamental accounting method applied to this ledger. Accrual basis recognizes revenue when earned and expenses when incurred, cash basis recognizes transactions when cash changes hands, and modified accrual is a hybrid approach used primarily in governmental accounting.",
finance,ledger_accounting,general_ledger,audit_trail_level,audit_trail_level,Audit Trail Level,STRING,,,,none|summary|detailed|comprehensive,master_data,"The level of audit trail detail maintained for this ledger. None indicates no audit logging, summary captures high-level changes, detailed tracks all field-level modifications, and comprehensive includes full before/after values and user context.",
finance,ledger_accounting,general_ledger,budget_control_enabled_flag,budget_control_enabled_flag,Budget Control Enabled Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,"Indicates whether budget control and funds management is enabled for this ledger. When true, transactions are validated against available budget before posting to prevent overspending.",
finance,ledger_accounting,general_ledger,consolidation_group_code,consolidation_group_code,Consolidation Group Code,STRING,,,,"^[A-Z0-9]{2,10}$",master_data,The code identifying the consolidation group to which this ledger belongs. Used to aggregate financial results across multiple legal entities or business units for enterprise-wide reporting.,
finance,ledger_accounting,general_ledger,cost_center_enabled_flag,cost_center_enabled_flag,Cost Center Enabled Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,"Indicates whether cost center accounting is enabled for this ledger. When true, all journal entries must include cost center assignments for departmental expense tracking and allocation.",
finance,ledger_accounting,general_ledger,created_timestamp,created_timestamp,Created Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,master_data,The date and time when this general ledger record was first created in the system. Supports audit trail and data lineage tracking.,
finance,ledger_accounting,general_ledger,effective_end_date,effective_end_date,Effective End Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,The date on which this general ledger was closed or deactivated. Null for currently active ledgers. Used to manage ledger lifecycle transitions and historical reporting boundaries.,
finance,ledger_accounting,general_ledger,effective_start_date,effective_start_date,Effective Start Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,The date on which this general ledger became active and began accepting journal entry postings. Establishes the beginning of the ledgers operational lifecycle.,
finance,ledger_accounting,general_ledger,fiscal_year_start_month,fiscal_year_start_month,Fiscal Year Start Month,INT,,,,,master_data,The calendar month (1-12) in which the fiscal year begins for this ledger. Used to align financial periods with organizational planning cycles and regulatory reporting requirements.,
finance,ledger_accounting,general_ledger,fiscal_year_variant,fiscal_year_variant,Fiscal Year Variant,STRING,,,,"^[A-Z0-9]{2,4}$",master_data,"The fiscal calendar configuration code defining the number of periods, period lengths, and special period rules for this ledger. Aligns with enterprise resource planning system fiscal calendar structures.",
finance,ledger_accounting,general_ledger,functional_currency_code,functional_currency_code,Functional Currency Code,STRING,,,,^[A-Z]{3}$,master_data,The three-letter ISO 4217 currency code representing the primary currency in which this ledger operates and reports financial results. All transactions are translated to this currency for consolidation and reporting.,
finance,ledger_accounting,general_ledger,general_ledger_description,general_ledger_description,General Ledger (GL) Description,STRING,,,,,master_data,"A detailed narrative description of the general ledgers purpose, scope, and usage within the healthcare organizations financial management framework. Provides context for financial analysts and auditors.",
finance,ledger_accounting,general_ledger,intercompany_enabled_flag,intercompany_enabled_flag,Intercompany Enabled Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,"Indicates whether intercompany transaction tracking is enabled for this ledger. When true, transactions between legal entities are identified and reconciled for consolidated financial reporting.",
finance,ledger_accounting,general_ledger,last_closed_period,last_closed_period,Last Closed Period,STRING,,,,^[0-9]{4}-(0[1-9]|1[0-2])$,master_data,The most recent fiscal period (YYYY-MM format) that has been closed for this ledger. Closed periods are locked from further posting to ensure financial statement integrity.,
finance,ledger_accounting,general_ledger,last_posting_date,last_posting_date,Last Posting Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,The date of the most recent journal entry posted to this ledger. Used to monitor ledger activity and identify dormant or inactive ledgers.,
finance,ledger_accounting,general_ledger,leading_ledger_flag,leading_ledger_flag,Leading Ledger Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,Indicates whether this is the leading (primary) ledger for the organization. The leading ledger serves as the authoritative source for financial reporting and drives consolidation processes.,
finance,ledger_accounting,general_ledger,ledger_code,ledger_code,General Ledger (GL) Code,STRING,,,,"^[A-Z0-9]{2,10}$",master_data,The unique alphanumeric code identifying this general ledger within the enterprise chart of accounts structure. Used as the business identifier for journal entry postings and financial reporting.,
finance,ledger_accounting,general_ledger,ledger_name,ledger_name,General Ledger (GL) Name,STRING,,,,,master_data,"The full descriptive name of the general ledger, providing human-readable identification for financial reporting and analysis.",
finance,ledger_accounting,general_ledger,ledger_status,ledger_status,General Ledger (GL) Status,STRING,,,,active|inactive|closed|suspended|archived,master_data,"Current operational state of the general ledger. Active ledgers accept new postings, inactive ledgers are temporarily disabled, closed ledgers are finalized for a fiscal period, suspended ledgers are under review or audit, and archived ledgers are retained for historical reference only.",
finance,ledger_accounting,general_ledger,ledger_type,ledger_type,General Ledger (GL) Type,STRING,,,,corporate|management|statutory|consolidation|budget|forecast,master_data,"Classification of the general ledger by its primary purpose. Corporate ledgers support consolidated financial statements, management ledgers support internal decision-making, statutory ledgers meet regulatory reporting requirements, consolidation ledgers aggregate multi-entity financials, budget ledgers track planned allocations, and forecast ledgers project future performance.",
finance,ledger_accounting,general_ledger,modified_timestamp,modified_timestamp,Modified Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,master_data,The date and time when this general ledger record was last modified. Tracks the most recent update to any attribute for change management and audit purposes.,
finance,ledger_accounting,general_ledger,parallel_accounting_enabled_flag,parallel_accounting_enabled_flag,Parallel Accounting Enabled Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,"Indicates whether parallel accounting is enabled, allowing simultaneous posting to multiple ledgers with different accounting principles (e.g., GAAP and IFRS). Supports organizations with multi-jurisdictional reporting requirements.",
finance,ledger_accounting,general_ledger,profit_center_enabled_flag,profit_center_enabled_flag,Profit Center Enabled Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,"Indicates whether profit center accounting is enabled for this ledger. When true, revenue and expense transactions are tracked by profit center for segment profitability analysis.",
finance,ledger_accounting,general_ledger,project_accounting_enabled_flag,project_accounting_enabled_flag,Project Accounting Enabled Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,"Indicates whether project-based accounting is enabled for this ledger. When true, costs and revenues can be tracked at the project level for capital budgeting and grant management.",
finance,ledger_accounting,general_ledger,reporting_entity_code,reporting_entity_code,Reporting Entity Code,STRING,,,,"^[A-Z0-9]{2,10}$",master_data,The code identifying the reporting entity for external financial statement preparation. Maps this ledger to the appropriate regulatory and stakeholder reporting requirements.,
finance,ledger_accounting,general_ledger,retention_period_years,retention_period_years,Retention Period Years,INT,,,,,master_data,"The number of years that ledger data must be retained to meet regulatory, legal, and business requirements. Drives archival and purge policies for historical financial records.",
finance,ledger_accounting,general_ledger,segment_reporting_enabled_flag,segment_reporting_enabled_flag,Segment Reporting Enabled Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,"Indicates whether segment reporting dimensions are enabled for this ledger. When true, financial results can be analyzed by business segment for FASB ASC 280 segment disclosure requirements.",
