finance,payable_receivable,ap_payment,payment_terms,payment_terms,Payment Terms,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Payment terms applicable to this payment (e.g., Net 30, 2/10 Net 30). Reflects the terms under which the vendor invoices were paid.",
finance,payable_receivable,ap_payment,payment_type,payment_type,Payment Type,STRING,,,,invoice_payment|prepayment|refund|expense_reimbursement,transactional_data,"Classification of the payment transaction type. Values: invoice_payment (standard vendor invoice payment), prepayment (advance payment), refund (return of funds), expense_reimbursement (employee expense reimbursement).",
finance,payable_receivable,ap_payment,reconciled_date,reconciled_date,Reconciled Date,DATE,,,,,transactional_data,Date on which the payment was reconciled against the bank statement. Null if not yet reconciled.,
finance,payable_receivable,ap_payment,remittance_advice_reference,remittance_advice_reference,Remittance Advice Reference,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,Reference number or identifier for the remittance advice document sent to the vendor detailing which invoices this payment settles.,
finance,payable_receivable,ap_payment,void_date,void_date,Void Date,DATE,,,,,transactional_data,Date on which the payment was voided or cancelled. Null if payment has not been voided.,
finance,payable_receivable,ap_payment,void_reason,void_reason,Void Reason,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,Business reason or explanation for why the payment was voided. Null if payment has not been voided.,
finance,payable_receivable,ap_payment,wire_confirmation_number,wire_confirmation_number,Wire Confirmation Number,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,Bank confirmation or reference number for wire transfer payments. Null for non-wire payment methods.,
finance,payable_receivable,ar_account,ar_account_id,ar_account_id,Accounts Receivable (AR) Account Identifier,BIGINT,Y,,,,master_data,"Unique identifier for the accounts receivable account. Primary key for non-patient-billing receivables including grants, rental income, intercompany receivables, and physician practice management fees.",
finance,payable_receivable,ar_account,ar_employee_id,ar_employee_id,Assigned Collector Identifier,BIGINT,,workforce.employee.employee_id,"dbx_confidential, dbx_pii",,master_data,"Identifier of the internal staff member or external collection agency assigned to manage collection activities for this account. Used for workload distribution, performance tracking, and accountability.",
finance,payable_receivable,ar_account,chart_of_accounts_id,chart_of_accounts_id,Chart Of Accounts Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,finance.chart_of_accounts.chart_of_accounts_id,,,master_data,Foreign key linking to finance.chart_of_accounts. Business justification: ar_account has gl_account_code (STRING) which should be normalized to FK to chart_of_accounts. Enables joining to get account metadata for the receivable GL account.,
finance,payable_receivable,ar_account,cost_center_id,cost_center_id,Cost Center Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,finance.cost_center.cost_center_id,,,master_data,Foreign key linking to finance.cost_center. Business justification: ar_account has cost_center_code (STRING) which should be normalized to FK to cost_center master. Enables joining to get cost center details for receivable tracking by department/service line.,
finance,payable_receivable,ar_account,parent_ar_account_id,parent_ar_account_id,Parent Ar Account Id,BIGINT,,finance.ar_account.ar_account_id,dbx_self_ref_fk,,master_data,Self-referencing FK on ar_account (parent_ar_account_id),
finance,payable_receivable,ar_account,tertiary_employee_id,tertiary_employee_id,Last Modified By User Identifier,BIGINT,,workforce.employee.employee_id,"dbx_confidential, dbx_pii",,master_data,"The system user identifier of the person or process that most recently modified this AR account record. Used for accountability, audit trail, and change management.",
finance,payable_receivable,ar_account,account_number,account_number,Account Number,STRING,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii_financial",,master_data,"pii_phi,pii_pii,pii_sensitive",
finance,payable_receivable,ar_account,account_status,account_status,Account Status,STRING,,,,,master_data,Current lifecycle status of the receivable account. Open indicates active receivable with expected payment; closed indicates fully paid or resolved; written_off indicates uncollectible and removed from active AR; in_collections indicates transferred to internal or external collections; disputed indicates debtor has contested the amount; on_hold indicates temporarily suspended collection activity; pending_resolution indicates awaiting internal review or decision. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: open|closed|written_off|in_collections|disputed|on_hold|pending_resolution — 7 candidates stripped; promote to reference product],
finance,payable_receivable,ar_account,account_type,account_type,Account Type,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Classification of the receivable account indicating the nature of the financial relationship. Distinguishes between payer receivables, self-pay patient receivables, intercompany transactions, grant funding, physician practice management fees, rental income, and other non-RCM receivables. Note: This is for non-patient-billing AR; patient billing AR is managed in billing.patient_account. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: payer|self_pay|intercompany|grant|physician_practice_management|rental_income|other — 7 candidates stripped; promote to reference product]",
finance,payable_receivable,ar_account,aging_bucket,aging_bucket,Aging Bucket,STRING,,,,current|1_30_days|31_60_days|61_90_days|91_120_days|over_120_days,master_data,"Categorization of the receivable based on the number of days outstanding since the original invoice or billing date. Used for aging analysis, collection prioritization, and allowance for doubtful accounts estimation. Current indicates not yet due; subsequent buckets indicate days past due.",
finance,payable_receivable,ar_account,collection_agency_name,collection_agency_name,Collection Agency Name,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Name of the external third-party collection agency to which this account has been referred, if applicable. Null if account is managed internally or not yet in collections.",
finance,payable_receivable,ar_account,created_timestamp,created_timestamp,Record Created Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,master_data,"The date and time when this AR account record was first created in the system. Used for audit trail, data lineage, and account lifecycle tracking.",
finance,payable_receivable,ar_account,currency_code,currency_code,Currency Code,STRING,,,,^[A-Z]{3}$,master_data,Three-letter ISO 4217 currency code indicating the currency denomination of all monetary amounts on this account. Defaults to USD for domestic operations; supports multi-currency for international grants or intercompany receivables.,
finance,payable_receivable,ar_account,current_balance,current_balance,Current Balance Amount,"DECIMAL(18,2)",,,,,master_data,"The outstanding receivable balance as of the current date. Reflects original balance minus payments received, plus any adjustments, interest, or fees. This is the amount currently owed. Denominated in USD unless otherwise specified in currency_code.",
finance,payable_receivable,ar_account,days_outstanding,days_outstanding,Days Outstanding,INT,,,,,master_data,The number of calendar days that have elapsed since the original invoice or billing date. Used to calculate aging bucket and assess collection risk. Key metric for Days Sales Outstanding (DSO) reporting.,
finance,payable_receivable,ar_account,debtor_name,debtor_name,Debtor Name,STRING,,,dbx_confidential,,master_data,"The legal or business name of the entity or individual that owes payment on this receivable account. May be a payer organization, self-pay patient, affiliated entity, grantor, or other debtor.",
finance,payable_receivable,ar_account,debtor_type,debtor_type,Debtor Type,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Categorical classification of the debtor entity. Segments debtors into commercial insurance payers, government payers (Medicare, Medicaid), self-pay individuals, affiliated healthcare entities, grant-making organizations, corporate tenants, and other categories for reporting and collection strategy purposes. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: commercial_payer|government_payer|self_pay_individual|affiliated_entity|grant_organization|corporate_tenant|other — 7 candidates stripped; promote to reference product]",
finance,payable_receivable,ar_account,dispute_date,dispute_date,Dispute Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,The date on which the debtor formally notified the organization of the dispute. Used to track dispute aging and ensure timely resolution per regulatory requirements.,
finance,payable_receivable,ar_account,dispute_flag,dispute_flag,Dispute Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,Boolean indicator of whether the debtor has formally disputed the receivable amount or validity. True indicates an active dispute; false indicates no dispute. Disputed accounts typically require special handling and may be placed on hold pending resolution.,
finance,payable_receivable,ar_account,dispute_reason,dispute_reason,Dispute Reason,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Description of the reason provided by the debtor for disputing the receivable, such as services not rendered, incorrect billing amount, duplicate invoice, or contractual disagreement. Used to guide dispute resolution process.",
finance,payable_receivable,ar_account,due_date,due_date,Payment Due Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,The date by which payment is contractually due per the invoice terms or agreement. Used to determine whether the account is current or past due and to calculate late fees or interest if applicable.,
finance,payable_receivable,ar_account,interest_rate,interest_rate,Interest Rate,"DECIMAL(5,4)",,,,,master_data,"The annual interest rate applied to overdue balances on this account, expressed as a decimal (e.g., 0.0500 for 5%). Null if no interest is charged. Used to calculate interest charges on past-due amounts per contractual terms or state regulations.",
finance,payable_receivable,ar_account,invoice_date,invoice_date,Invoice Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,The date on which the original invoice or billing statement was issued to the debtor. Serves as the starting point for aging calculations and payment term enforcement.,
finance,payable_receivable,ar_account,last_activity_date,last_activity_date,Last Activity Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,"The most recent date on which any activity occurred on this account, including payments received, adjustments posted, collection calls made, correspondence sent, or status changes. Used to identify dormant accounts and prioritize follow-up.",
finance,payable_receivable,ar_account,last_modified_timestamp,last_modified_timestamp,Record Last Modified Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,master_data,"The date and time when this AR account record was most recently updated. Used for audit trail, change tracking, and data synchronization.",
finance,payable_receivable,ar_account,last_payment_amount,last_payment_amount,Last Payment Amount,"DECIMAL(18,2)",,,,,master_data,The monetary amount of the most recent payment received on this account. Denominated in the accounts currency_code. Used for payment trend analysis and debtor behavior assessment.,
finance,payable_receivable,ar_account,last_payment_date,last_payment_date,Last Payment Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,The date on which the most recent payment was received and posted to this account. Used to assess payment patterns and predict future payment likelihood.,
finance,payable_receivable,ar_account,legal_action_date,legal_action_date,Legal Action Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,The date on which legal action was initiated for collection of this receivable. Null if no legal action has been taken. Used for legal case tracking and statute of limitations monitoring.,
finance,payable_receivable,ar_account,legal_action_flag,legal_action_flag,Legal Action Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,"Boolean indicator of whether legal action (lawsuit, lien, garnishment) has been initiated to collect this receivable. True indicates active legal proceedings; false indicates no legal action. Used for legal department coordination and risk management.",
finance,payable_receivable,ar_account,notes,notes,Account Notes,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Free-text field for recording important notes, comments, or special instructions related to this account. May include collection history, debtor communication summaries, special handling requirements, or internal coordination notes.",
finance,payable_receivable,ar_account,original_balance,original_balance,Original Balance Amount,"DECIMAL(18,2)",,,,,master_data,"The initial receivable amount established when the account was opened. Represents the total amount originally owed before any payments, adjustments, or write-offs. Denominated in USD unless otherwise specified in currency_code.",
finance,payable_receivable,ar_account,payment_terms,payment_terms,Payment Terms,STRING,,,,,master_data,"The contractual payment terms agreed upon with the debtor, typically expressed as net days (e.g., Net 30, Net 60) or other terms such as due on receipt, installment plan, or custom terms. Defines the expected payment timeline.",
finance,payable_receivable,ar_account,settlement_accepted_flag,settlement_accepted_flag,Settlement Accepted Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,Boolean indicator of whether the debtor has accepted a settlement offer. True indicates acceptance; false indicates no acceptance or no offer made. Used to track settlement negotiations and finalize account closure.,
finance,payable_receivable,ar_account,settlement_offer_amount,settlement_offer_amount,Settlement Offer Amount,"DECIMAL(18,2)",,,,,master_data,"The reduced amount offered to the debtor as a settlement to close the account, if applicable. Typically less than current_balance. Null if no settlement has been offered. Denominated in the accounts currency_code.",
finance,payable_receivable,ar_account,total_adjustments,total_adjustments,Total Adjustments Amount,"DECIMAL(18,2)",,,,,master_data,"The cumulative sum of all adjustments (positive or negative) applied to this account, including billing corrections, contractual allowances, courtesy adjustments, and dispute resolutions. Denominated in the accounts currency_code.",
finance,payable_receivable,ar_account,total_fees_assessed,total_fees_assessed,Total Fees Assessed Amount,"DECIMAL(18,2)",,,,,master_data,"The cumulative amount of late fees, collection fees, administrative fees, or other charges assessed on this account. Included in the current_balance. Denominated in the accounts currency_code.",
finance,payable_receivable,ar_account,total_interest_accrued,total_interest_accrued,Total Interest Accrued Amount,"DECIMAL(18,2)",,,,,master_data,The cumulative amount of interest that has accrued on this account due to late payment. Included in the current_balance. Denominated in the accounts currency_code.,
finance,payable_receivable,ar_account,total_payments_received,total_payments_received,Total Payments Received Amount,"DECIMAL(18,2)",,,,,master_data,The cumulative sum of all payments received on this account since inception. Used to calculate current_balance and assess payment history. Denominated in the accounts currency_code.,
finance,payable_receivable,ar_account,write_off_amount,write_off_amount,Write-Off Amount,"DECIMAL(18,2)",,,,,master_data,The amount written off as uncollectible bad debt. Populated when account_status is written_off. Represents the portion of the receivable removed from active AR and recognized as a loss. Denominated in the accounts currency_code.,
finance,payable_receivable,ar_account,write_off_date,write_off_date,Write-Off Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,The date on which the receivable was written off as uncollectible. Null if the account has not been written off. Used for bad debt reporting and financial statement preparation.,
finance,payable_receivable,ar_account,write_off_reason,write_off_reason,Write-Off Reason,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Explanation or categorization of why the receivable was written off, such as debtor bankruptcy, inability to locate debtor, cost of collection exceeds balance, statute of limitations expired, or management decision. Used for root cause analysis and process improvement.",
finance,payable_receivable,finance_ar_transaction,finance_ar_transaction_id,finance_ar_transaction_id,Accounts Receivable (AR) Transaction ID,BIGINT,Y,,ar_transaction_id=ar_transaction_parent_id,,transactional_data,ar_transaction_parent_id,
finance,payable_receivable,finance_ar_transaction,ar_account_id,ar_account_id,Accounts Receivable (AR) Account ID,BIGINT,,finance.ar_account.ar_account_id,,,transactional_data,Reference to the AR account (non-RCM receivable account) associated with this transaction. Links to the AR account master for customer or entity billing relationships outside of revenue cycle management.,
finance,payable_receivable,finance_ar_transaction,chart_of_accounts_id,chart_of_accounts_id,Chart Of Accounts Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,finance.chart_of_accounts.chart_of_accounts_id,,,transactional_data,Foreign key linking to finance.chart_of_accounts. Business justification: ar_transaction has gl_account_code (STRING) which should be normalized to FK to chart_of_accounts. Enables joining to get account metadata for the GL account affected by the AR transaction.,
finance,payable_receivable,finance_ar_transaction,cost_center_id,cost_center_id,Cost Center Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,finance.cost_center.cost_center_id,,,transactional_data,Foreign key linking to finance.cost_center. Business justification: ar_transaction has cost_center_code (STRING) which should be normalized to FK to cost_center master. Enables joining to get cost center details for AR transaction allocation.,
finance,payable_receivable,finance_ar_transaction,employee_id,employee_id,Entered By User ID,BIGINT,,workforce.employee.employee_id,"dbx_confidential, dbx_pii",,transactional_data,User identifier of the person who created or entered this AR transaction into the system. Used for audit trail and accountability.,
finance,payable_receivable,finance_ar_transaction,finance_applied_to_ar_transaction_id,finance_applied_to_ar_transaction_id,,BIGINT,,finance.finance_ar_transaction.finance_ar_transaction_id,dbx_self_ref_fk,,transactional_data,"FK to the AR transaction this payment or credit memo is applied against (e.g., the invoice being paid). References finance.finance_ar_transaction.ar_transaction_id.",
finance,payable_receivable,finance_ar_transaction,finance_prior_ar_transaction_id,finance_prior_ar_transaction_id,,BIGINT,,finance.finance_ar_transaction.finance_ar_transaction_id,dbx_self_ref_fk,,transactional_data,"FK to the chronologically preceding AR transaction in a sequence (e.g., the previous payment application). References finance.finance_ar_transaction.ar_transaction_id.",
finance,payable_receivable,finance_ar_transaction,finance_reversed_by_ar_transaction_id,finance_reversed_by_ar_transaction_id,,BIGINT,,finance.finance_ar_transaction.finance_ar_transaction_id,dbx_self_ref_fk,,transactional_data,FK to the AR transaction that reverses/voids this transaction. References finance.finance_ar_transaction.ar_transaction_id.,
finance,payable_receivable,finance_ar_transaction,fiscal_period_id,fiscal_period_id,Fiscal Period Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,finance.fiscal_period.fiscal_period_id,,,transactional_data,Foreign key linking to finance.fiscal_period. Business justification: ar_transaction has posting_period (STRING) which should be normalized to FK to fiscal_period master. Enables joining to get period details and ensures AR transactions reference valid fiscal periods.,
finance,payable_receivable,finance_ar_transaction,parent_ar_transaction_finance_ar_transaction_id,parent_ar_transaction_finance_ar_transaction_id,,BIGINT,,finance.finance_ar_transaction.finance_ar_transaction_id,dbx_self_ref_fk,,transactional_data,"FK to the parent AR transaction in a hierarchy (e.g., original invoice that spawned this adjustment). References finance.finance_ar_transaction.ar_transaction_id.",
finance,payable_receivable,finance_ar_transaction,transaction_batch_id,transaction_batch_id,Batch ID,BIGINT,,finance.transaction_batch.transaction_batch_id,,,transactional_data,Identifier for the batch or group of transactions processed together. Used for batch reconciliation and control totals validation.,
finance,payable_receivable,finance_ar_transaction,adjustment_reason_code,adjustment_reason_code,Adjustment Reason Code,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Standardized code indicating the business reason for adjustment transactions: billing error, pricing correction, contractual adjustment, goodwill credit. Null for non-adjustment transactions.",
finance,payable_receivable,finance_ar_transaction,aging_bucket,aging_bucket,Aging Bucket,STRING,,,,current|1_30_days|31_60_days|61_90_days|over_90_days,transactional_data,"Calculated aging category based on days outstanding from transaction date to current date: current (0 days), 1-30 days, 31-60 days, 61-90 days, or over 90 days. Used for AR aging analysis and collection prioritization.",
finance,payable_receivable,finance_ar_transaction,approval_date,approval_date,Approval Date,DATE,,,,,transactional_data,The date when this AR transaction was approved for posting. Null for transactions not requiring approval or still pending approval.,
finance,payable_receivable,finance_ar_transaction,created_timestamp,created_timestamp,Created Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,System timestamp when this AR transaction record was first created in the database. Used for audit trail and data lineage tracking.,
finance,payable_receivable,finance_ar_transaction,currency_code,currency_code,Currency Code,STRING,,,,USD|EUR|GBP|CAD|AUD|JPY,transactional_data,Three-letter ISO 4217 currency code for the transaction amount. Supports multi-currency AR management and foreign exchange reconciliation.,
finance,payable_receivable,finance_ar_transaction,due_date,due_date,Due Date,DATE,,,,,transactional_data,The date by which payment is expected or required for charge transactions. Used to calculate days outstanding and aging. Null for payment and adjustment transactions.,
finance,payable_receivable,finance_ar_transaction,exchange_rate,exchange_rate,Exchange Rate,"DECIMAL(12,6)",,,,,transactional_data,The foreign exchange rate applied to convert transaction currency to functional currency. Null for transactions in functional currency.,
finance,payable_receivable,finance_ar_transaction,functional_amount,functional_amount,Functional Amount,"DECIMAL(18,2)",,,,,transactional_data,The transaction amount converted to the organizations functional reporting currency (typically USD) using the exchange rate at transaction date. Used for consolidated financial reporting.,
finance,payable_receivable,finance_ar_transaction,modified_timestamp,modified_timestamp,Modified Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,System timestamp when this AR transaction record was last modified. Used for audit trail and change tracking.,
finance,payable_receivable,finance_ar_transaction,notes,notes,Notes,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Additional free-text notes or comments about the transaction providing supplementary context for accounting staff, auditors, or management review.",
finance,payable_receivable,finance_ar_transaction,payment_method,payment_method,Payment Method,STRING,,,,check|wire_transfer|ach|credit_card|cash|electronic_funds_transfer,transactional_data,"The payment instrument or method used for payment transactions: check, wire transfer, ACH, credit card, cash, or electronic funds transfer. Null for non-payment transaction types.",
finance,payable_receivable,finance_ar_transaction,payment_reference_number,payment_reference_number,Payment Reference Number,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"External payment reference number such as check number, wire confirmation, or ACH trace number. Used for payment reconciliation and audit trail.",
finance,payable_receivable,finance_ar_transaction,posting_date,posting_date,Posting Date,DATE,,,,,transactional_data,The date when the transaction was posted to the general ledger and became part of the official financial record.,
finance,payable_receivable,finance_ar_transaction,posting_status,posting_status,Posting Status,STRING,,,,draft|posted|reversed|voided|pending_approval,transactional_data,"Current posting status of the AR transaction: draft (not yet posted), posted (finalized in GL), reversed (cancelled with offsetting entry), voided (cancelled before posting), or pending_approval (awaiting authorization).",
finance,payable_receivable,finance_ar_transaction,reconciliation_date,reconciliation_date,Reconciliation Date,DATE,,,,,transactional_data,The date when this transaction was reconciled and cleared. Null for unreconciled transactions.,
finance,payable_receivable,finance_ar_transaction,reconciliation_status,reconciliation_status,Reconciliation Status,STRING,,,,unreconciled|reconciled|disputed|under_review,transactional_data,"Status of the transaction in the AR reconciliation process: unreconciled (not yet matched), reconciled (matched and cleared), disputed (discrepancy identified), or under_review (being investigated).",
finance,payable_receivable,finance_ar_transaction,reference_document_number,reference_document_number,Reference Document Number,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"External reference number linking this AR transaction to source documents such as invoices, payment receipts, credit memos, or adjustment authorizations.",
finance,payable_receivable,finance_ar_transaction,reversal_flag,reversal_flag,Reversal Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,"Boolean indicator whether this transaction is a reversal entry that offsets a previously posted transaction. True for reversal entries, False otherwise.",
finance,payable_receivable,finance_ar_transaction,source_system_code,source_system_code,Source System Code,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Code identifying the originating system or module that created this AR transaction: SAP FI, Workday Financials, manual entry, interface from external system.",
finance,payable_receivable,finance_ar_transaction,source_system_transaction_reference,source_system_transaction_reference,Source System Transaction ID,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,The unique transaction identifier from the source system. Used for data lineage tracking and reconciliation back to operational systems.,
finance,payable_receivable,finance_ar_transaction,tax_amount,tax_amount,Tax Amount,"DECIMAL(18,2)",,,,,transactional_data,The tax component of the transaction amount for charge transactions. Used for tax reporting and reconciliation. Null for non-taxable transactions.,
finance,payable_receivable,finance_ar_transaction,tax_code,tax_code,Tax Code,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,Tax jurisdiction or tax type code applied to this transaction. Used for tax reporting and compliance with state and federal tax regulations.,
finance,payable_receivable,finance_ar_transaction,transaction_amount,transaction_amount,Transaction Amount,"DECIMAL(18,2)",,,,,transactional_data,"The monetary value of the AR transaction in the transaction currency. Positive for charges and debits, negative for payments and credits.",
finance,payable_receivable,finance_ar_transaction,transaction_date,transaction_date,Transaction Date,DATE,,,,,transactional_data,The business date when the AR transaction event occurred. This is the principal event timestamp for aging analysis and financial period assignment.,
finance,payable_receivable,finance_ar_transaction,transaction_description,transaction_description,Transaction Description,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"pii_phi,pii_pii,pii_sensitive",
finance,payable_receivable,finance_ar_transaction,transaction_number,transaction_number,Transaction Number,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,Business-facing unique transaction number or document reference assigned to this AR transaction for external communication and reconciliation purposes.,
finance,payable_receivable,finance_ar_transaction,transaction_type,transaction_type,Transaction Type,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Classification of the AR transaction event: charge (new receivable), payment (cash received), credit_memo (reduction), debit_memo (increase), adjustment (correction), write_off (uncollectible), or refund (payment reversal). [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: charge|payment|credit_memo|debit_memo|adjustment|write_off|refund — 7 candidates stripped; promote to reference product]",
finance,payable_receivable,finance_ar_transaction,write_off_reason_code,write_off_reason_code,Write-Off Reason Code,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Standardized code indicating the business reason for write-off transactions: bad debt, small balance, bankruptcy, deceased, statute of limitations. Null for non-write-off transactions.",
finance,payable_receivable,invoice_payment_application,invoice_payment_application_id,invoice_payment_application_id,Invoice Payment Application ID,BIGINT,Y,,,,association_data,Unique identifier for this payment application record. Primary key.,
finance,payable_receivable,invoice_payment_application,ap_invoice_id,ap_invoice_id,Invoice Payment Application - Ap Invoice Id,BIGINT,,finance.ap_invoice.ap_invoice_id,,,association_data,Foreign key linking to the accounts payable invoice being paid or settled by this payment application.,
finance,payable_receivable,invoice_payment_application,ap_payment_id,ap_payment_id,Invoice Payment Application - Ap Payment Id,BIGINT,,finance.ap_payment.ap_payment_id,,,association_data,Foreign key linking to the accounts payable payment being applied to settle the invoice.,
finance,payable_receivable,invoice_payment_application,employee_id,employee_id,Created By Employee ID,BIGINT,,workforce.employee.employee_id,"dbx_confidential, dbx_pii",,association_data,Identifier of the employee or system user who created this payment application record.,
finance,payable_receivable,invoice_payment_application,amount_applied,amount_applied,Payment Amount Applied,"DECIMAL(18,2)",,,,,association_data,"The monetary amount of this payment that was applied to settle this specific invoice. For partial payments, this will be less than the total payment amount. For split payments across multiple invoices, the sum of amount_applied across all applications equals the total payment amount.",
finance,payable_receivable,invoice_payment_application,amount_paid,amount_paid,Amount Paid,"DECIMAL(18,2)",,,,,association_data,"The total amount that has been paid against this invoice to date. May be less than total_amount for partial payments. [Moved from ap_invoice: This attribute represents the total amount paid against an invoice, which is actually the SUM of amount_applied across all payment applications for this invoice. It is a derived/calculated value that belongs in the association layer, not as a standalone attribute on the invoice.]",
finance,payable_receivable,invoice_payment_application,amount_remaining,amount_remaining,Amount Remaining,"DECIMAL(18,2)",,,,,association_data,"The outstanding balance remaining to be paid on this invoice, calculated as total_amount - amount_paid. [Moved from ap_invoice: This attribute represents the outstanding balance on an invoice, which is calculated as total_amount minus the sum of amount_applied from all payment applications. It is a derived value that should be calculated from the association data, not stored redundantly on the invoice.]",
finance,payable_receivable,invoice_payment_application,application_date,application_date,Application Date,DATE,,,,,association_data,The date on which this payment was applied to this invoice in the accounts payable system. This is the business event date for the payment allocation and may differ from the payment_date if payments are applied retroactively or in batch processes.,
finance,payable_receivable,invoice_payment_application,application_sequence,application_sequence,Application Sequence,INT,,,,,association_data,"The sequence number of this application when a single payment is applied to multiple invoices. Used to track the order in which payment funds were allocated across invoices, which is important for cash application rules and aging calculations.",
finance,payable_receivable,invoice_payment_application,application_status,application_status,Application Status,STRING,,,,,association_data,"The current status of this payment application. Values: applied (payment successfully applied to invoice), reversed (application was reversed due to payment void or correction), pending (application awaiting approval or clearing), cleared (application confirmed and reconciled).",
finance,payable_receivable,invoice_payment_application,created_timestamp,created_timestamp,Created Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,association_data,System timestamp when this payment application record was created.,
finance,payable_receivable,invoice_payment_application,discount_taken,discount_taken,Discount Taken,"DECIMAL(18,2)",,,,,association_data,"The early payment discount amount taken on this specific invoice as part of this payment application. If a payment covers multiple invoices, each invoice may have a different discount amount based on its payment terms and timing.",
finance,payable_receivable,invoice_payment_application,payment_date,payment_date,Payment Date,DATE,,,,,association_data,"The date the payment was issued to the vendor. [Moved from ap_invoice: An invoice can be paid by multiple payments on different dates. The payment_date belongs to the payment entity (ap_payment), and the relationship between invoice and payment is captured through the application_date in the association. This attribute on the invoice is ambiguous when multiple payments exist.]",
finance,payable_receivable,invoice_payment_application,reversal_date,reversal_date,Reversal Date,DATE,,,,,association_data,The date on which this payment application was reversed or voided. Null if the application has not been reversed.,
finance,payable_receivable,invoice_payment_application,reversal_reason,reversal_reason,Reversal Reason,STRING,,,,,association_data,Business reason or explanation for why this payment application was reversed. Null if not reversed.,
