workforce,credential_privileging,competency_assessment,employee_id,employee_id,Worker ID,BIGINT,,workforce.employee.employee_id,"dbx_confidential, dbx_pii",,transactional_data,"Reference to the employee, physician, or contract staff member who is the subject of this competency assessment or occupational health record. Links to the workforce worker entity.",
workforce,credential_privileging,competency_assessment,position_id,position_id,Position Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,workforce.position.position_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to workforce.position. Business justification: Competency assessments are often position-specific requirements (e.g., clinical competencies for RN positions, safety training for specific roles). Linking to position enables tracking which assessmen",
workforce,credential_privileging,competency_assessment,procedure_cpt_code_id,procedure_cpt_code_id,Procedure Cpt Code Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,reference.cpt_code.cpt_code_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to reference.cpt_code. Business justification: Procedural competency assessments tied to specific CPT codes (e.g., central line insertion CPT 36556 competency validation). Real-world: skills checklists for invasive procedures, annual competency ve",
workforce,credential_privileging,competency_assessment,administration_route,administration_route,Administration Route,STRING,,,,intramuscular|subcutaneous|intradermal|oral|intranasal,transactional_data,"Route by which the vaccine was administered (e.g., intramuscular, subcutaneous, intradermal, oral, intranasal). Required for immunization documentation and adverse event reporting.",
workforce,credential_privileging,competency_assessment,administration_site,administration_site,Administration Site,STRING,,,,left_deltoid|right_deltoid|left_thigh|right_thigh|left_arm|right_arm,transactional_data,"Anatomical site on the body where the vaccine was injected (e.g., left deltoid, right deltoid). Required for immunization documentation per CDC and ACIP standards.",
workforce,credential_privileging,competency_assessment,assessment_category,assessment_category,Assessment Category,STRING,,,,competency|immunization|health_screening,transactional_data,"Top-level category distinguishing whether this record represents a clinical or non-clinical competency evaluation, an occupational immunization, or an occupational health screening (e.g., TB test, N95 fit test).",
workforce,credential_privileging,competency_assessment,assessment_date,assessment_date,Assessment Date,DATE,,,,,transactional_data,"The actual date on which the competency was evaluated, the immunization was administered, or the health screening was performed. This is the principal real-world event date for this record.",
workforce,credential_privileging,competency_assessment,assessment_method,assessment_method,Assessment Method,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Method used to evaluate or document the competency or health record. For competency: observation, written_exam, simulation, return_demonstration, peer_review. For immunization: administration. For screening: record_review. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: observation|written_exam|simulation|return_demonstration|administration|record_review|peer_review — promote to reference product]",
workforce,credential_privileging,competency_assessment,assessment_number,assessment_number,Assessment Number,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Externally visible, human-readable identifier for this assessment record, used in compliance reports, audit trails, and occupational health documentation (e.g., CA-2024-00123).",
workforce,credential_privileging,competency_assessment,assessment_status,assessment_status,Assessment Status,STRING,,,,scheduled|in_progress|completed|overdue|waived|declined,transactional_data,"Current lifecycle status of this assessment record, indicating whether it has been completed, is pending, overdue, formally waived, or declined by the worker.",
workforce,credential_privileging,competency_assessment,assessment_type,assessment_type,Assessment Type,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Specific type of assessment within the category. For competency: orientation, annual, role-specific, post-incident. For immunization: influenza, hepatitis_B, MMR, varicella, Tdap, COVID-19. For health screening: PPD, IGRA, N95_fit_test, blood_borne_pathogen. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: orientation|annual|role_specific|post_incident|influenza|hepatitis_B|MMR|varicella|Tdap|COVID_19|PPD|IGRA|N95_fit_test — promote to reference product]",
workforce,credential_privileging,competency_assessment,attempt_number,attempt_number,Attempt Number,INT,,,,,transactional_data,"Sequential attempt number for this competency assessment, tracking how many times the worker has been evaluated for this specific competency (1 = initial, 2+ = re-attempts after remediation).",
workforce,credential_privileging,competency_assessment,cme_credit_hours,cme_credit_hours,Continuing Medical Education (CME) Credit Hours,"DECIMAL(5,2)",,,,,transactional_data,"Number of Continuing Medical Education (CME) or Continuing Education (CE) credit hours awarded upon successful completion of this competency assessment, if applicable.",
workforce,credential_privileging,competency_assessment,competency_domain,competency_domain,Competency Domain,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Clinical or operational domain to which this competency belongs (e.g., medication administration, infection control, patient safety, critical care, age-specific care, equipment operation). Null for immunization and health screening records.",
workforce,credential_privileging,competency_assessment,competency_name,competency_name,Competency Name,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Descriptive name of the specific competency, skill, vaccine, or screening test being assessed or administered (e.g., IV Catheter Insertion, Influenza Vaccine 2024-2025, Annual TB Screening).",
workforce,credential_privileging,competency_assessment,compliance_status,compliance_status,Compliance Status,STRING,,,,compliant|non_compliant|exempt|pending,transactional_data,"Regulatory compliance status of this assessment record, indicating whether the worker is currently compliant, non-compliant, formally exempt, or pending completion for TJC, CMS, or OSHA requirements.",
workforce,credential_privileging,competency_assessment,created_timestamp,created_timestamp,Record Created Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,"Timestamp when this competency assessment record was first created in the system, used for audit trail and data lineage tracking.",
workforce,credential_privileging,competency_assessment,declination_reason,declination_reason,Declination Reason,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Documented reason provided by the worker for declining an immunization or health screening (e.g., religious exemption, medical contraindication, prior immunity documented). Required for OSHA and TJC compliance when immunization is declined.",
workforce,credential_privileging,competency_assessment,department_name,department_name,Department Name,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Name of the clinical or operational department where the worker is assigned at the time of this assessment, used for department-level compliance reporting.",
workforce,credential_privileging,competency_assessment,due_date,due_date,Due Date,DATE,,,,,transactional_data,"Date by which this assessment, immunization, or health screening must be completed to remain in compliance with TJC, CMS, or OSHA requirements.",
workforce,credential_privileging,competency_assessment,fit_test_protocol,fit_test_protocol,Fit Test Protocol,STRING,,,,qualitative|quantitative,transactional_data,Protocol used for N95 respirator fit testing: qualitative (pass/fail based on taste/smell detection) or quantitative (numerical fit factor measurement). Required for OSHA 29 CFR 1910.134 compliance.,
workforce,credential_privileging,competency_assessment,job_role_applicability,job_role_applicability,Job Role Applicability,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Job role, position, or worker classification for which this competency or health requirement applies (e.g., RN, LPN, Surgical Tech, Environmental Services). Supports role-based compliance tracking.",
workforce,credential_privileging,competency_assessment,medical_contraindication,medical_contraindication,Medical Contraindication Flag,BOOLEAN,,,"dbx_pii,dbx_restricted,pii_phi,pii_sensitive",,transactional_data,Indicates whether a documented medical contraindication exists that exempts the worker from a required immunization or health screening. True when a physician-documented contraindication is on file.,
workforce,credential_privileging,competency_assessment,n95_respirator_model,n95_respirator_model,N95 Respirator Model,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,Make and model of the N95 respirator for which the worker was fit-tested. Required for OSHA respiratory protection program documentation.,
workforce,credential_privileging,competency_assessment,next_due_date,next_due_date,Next Due Date,DATE,,,,,transactional_data,"Date when the next recurring assessment, immunization booster, or health screening is due, used for proactive compliance tracking and workforce scheduling.",
workforce,credential_privileging,competency_assessment,notes,notes,Assessment Notes,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Free-text field for assessor or occupational health clinician notes, observations, or additional context related to this assessment, immunization, or health screening record.",
workforce,credential_privileging,competency_assessment,outcome,outcome,Assessment Outcome,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,Final result of the assessment or immunization event. For competency: pass or fail. For observation-based: satisfactory or unsatisfactory. For immunization: administered or declined. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: pass|fail|satisfactory|unsatisfactory|administered|declined|deferred — promote to reference product],
workforce,credential_privileging,competency_assessment,passing_score,passing_score,Passing Score,"DECIMAL(5,2)",,,,,transactional_data,Minimum score required to pass this competency assessment. Used to determine pass/fail outcome and trigger remediation workflows when the workers score falls below this threshold.,
workforce,credential_privileging,competency_assessment,prior_immunity_documented,prior_immunity_documented,Prior Immunity Documented Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,"Indicates whether the worker has documented evidence of prior immunity (e.g., positive titer for MMR or varicella), exempting them from the corresponding immunization requirement.",
workforce,credential_privileging,competency_assessment,reassessment_date,reassessment_date,Reassessment Date,DATE,,,,,transactional_data,Date on which the worker was re-evaluated following completion of a remediation plan after an initial competency assessment failure.,
workforce,credential_privileging,competency_assessment,regulatory_requirement,regulatory_requirement,Regulatory Requirement,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Specific regulatory standard or accreditation requirement that mandates this assessment (e.g., TJC HR.01.06.01, CMS CoP §482.42, OSHA 29 CFR 1910.1030, NCQA HEDIS). Used for compliance reporting and audit evidence.",
workforce,credential_privileging,competency_assessment,remediation_due_date,remediation_due_date,Remediation Due Date,DATE,,,,,transactional_data,Date by which the worker must complete the assigned remediation plan and be re-assessed for the failed competency.,
workforce,credential_privileging,competency_assessment,remediation_plan,remediation_plan,Remediation Plan,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Description of the corrective education, supervised practice, or training plan assigned to the worker following a failed competency assessment, including required activities and timeline.",
workforce,credential_privileging,competency_assessment,remediation_required,remediation_required,Remediation Required Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,Indicates whether the worker failed this competency assessment and requires a remediation plan before re-assessment. Drives remediation workflow in Workday HCM Learning.,
workforce,credential_privileging,competency_assessment,result_interpretation,result_interpretation,Result Interpretation,STRING,,,,positive|negative|indeterminate|reactive|non_reactive,transactional_data,"Clinical interpretation of the health screening result (e.g., positive, negative, indeterminate for TB tests; reactive/non-reactive for hepatitis B serology). Null for competency assessments.",
workforce,credential_privileging,competency_assessment,result_value,result_value,Result Value,"DECIMAL(18,2)",,,,,transactional_data,"Qualitative or quantitative result for health screening tests. For PPD: induration measurement in mm (e.g., 10mm). For IGRA: positive/negative/indeterminate. For N95 fit test: pass/fail with fit factor. Null for competency and immunization records.",
workforce,credential_privileging,competency_assessment,score,score,Assessment Score,"DECIMAL(5,2)",,,,,transactional_data,"Numeric score achieved by the worker on a written exam or simulation-based competency assessment (e.g., 85.00 out of 100). Null for immunization and health screening records.",
workforce,credential_privileging,competency_assessment,source_record_reference,source_record_reference,Source Record ID,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Native identifier of this record in the originating source system (e.g., Workday learning activity ID, Symplr compliance record ID). Supports reconciliation and ETL audit.",
workforce,credential_privileging,competency_assessment,source_system,source_system,Source System,STRING,,,,Workday|Symplr|Epic|Cerner|MEDITECH|Manual,transactional_data,"Operational system of record from which this assessment record originated (e.g., Workday HCM Learning, Symplr Credentialing, Epic, manual entry). Supports data lineage and ETL traceability.",
workforce,credential_privileging,competency_assessment,titer_result,titer_result,Titer Result,STRING,,,,immune|non_immune|indeterminate,transactional_data,"Result of a serological titer test confirming immunity status for vaccines such as MMR, varicella, or hepatitis B (immune, non_immune, indeterminate). Used to determine whether immunization is required.",
workforce,credential_privileging,competency_assessment,updated_timestamp,updated_timestamp,Record Updated Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,"Timestamp of the most recent modification to this competency assessment record, supporting audit trail requirements and change tracking.",
workforce,credential_privileging,competency_assessment,vaccine_dose_number,vaccine_dose_number,Vaccine Dose Number,INT,,,,,transactional_data,"Sequence number of the vaccine dose in a multi-dose series (e.g., dose 1, 2, or 3 of hepatitis B series; primary or booster for COVID-19). Null for single-dose vaccines.",
workforce,credential_privileging,competency_assessment,vaccine_lot_number,vaccine_lot_number,Vaccine Lot Number,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"pii_phi,pii_pii,pii_sensitive",
workforce,credential_privileging,competency_assessment,vaccine_manufacturer,vaccine_manufacturer,Vaccine Manufacturer,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,"Name of the pharmaceutical manufacturer of the vaccine administered (e.g., Pfizer, Moderna, Sanofi Pasteur). Required for adverse event reporting and immunization registry submissions.",
workforce,credential_privileging,competency_assessment,vaccine_ndc,vaccine_ndc,Vaccine National Drug Code (NDC),STRING,,,,^[0-9]{5}-[0-9]{4}-[0-9]{2}$,transactional_data,"National Drug Code (NDC) identifying the specific vaccine product administered. Used for immunization registry reporting, billing, and adverse event tracking.",
workforce,credential_privileging,employment_competency,employment_competency_id,employment_competency_id,Employment Competency ID,BIGINT,Y,,,,master_data,"Unique surrogate identifier for each employment competency record, covering credentials, privileges, and credentialing application lifecycle entries for healthcare workforce members.",
workforce,credential_privileging,employment_competency,care_site_id,care_site_id,Facility ID,BIGINT,,facility.care_site.care_site_id,,,master_data,"Reference to the healthcare facility (hospital, clinic, outpatient center) at which this privilege or credential is applicable. Null for credentials that are not facility-specific.",
workforce,credential_privileging,employment_competency,clinician_id,clinician_id,Clinician Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,provider.clinician.clinician_id,,,master_data,"Foreign key linking to provider.clinician. Business justification: Workforce competency records for clinicians. Real business need: unified competency tracking across HR and medical staff systems, credentialing integration, privileging coordination, regulatory compli",
workforce,credential_privileging,employment_competency,employee_id,employee_id,Worker ID,BIGINT,,workforce.employee.employee_id,"dbx_confidential, dbx_pii",,master_data,"Reference to the workforce member (employee, physician, contract staff, or allied health professional) to whom this competency record belongs.",
workforce,credential_privileging,employment_competency,privilege_cpt_code_id,privilege_cpt_code_id,Privilege Cpt Code Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,reference.cpt_code.cpt_code_id,,,master_data,"Foreign key linking to reference.cpt_code. Business justification: Clinical privileges granted for specific procedures identified by CPT codes. Real-world: privilege cards list CPT ranges (e.g., 33510-33536 for CABG), credentialing applications require procedure-spec",
workforce,credential_privileging,employment_competency,privilege_hcpcs_code_id,privilege_hcpcs_code_id,Privilege Hcpcs Code Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,reference.hcpcs_code.hcpcs_code_id,,,master_data,"Foreign key linking to reference.hcpcs_code. Business justification: Privileges for device/drug administration procedures using HCPCS (e.g., J-codes for chemotherapy, E-codes for DME ordering authority). Real-world: oncology nurse privileges for specific chemotherapy a",
workforce,credential_privileging,employment_competency,privilege_icd_code_id,privilege_icd_code_id,Privilege Icd Code Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,reference.icd_code.icd_code_id,,,master_data,"Foreign key linking to reference.icd_code. Business justification: Medical staff privilege delineation links procedures to diagnosis codes (e.g., cardiac surgeon privileges for ICD-10 I21.* acute MI). Real-world: privilege dictionaries in medical staff bylaws, creden",
workforce,credential_privileging,employment_competency,application_complete_date,application_complete_date,Application Complete Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,The date on which the credentialing application was deemed complete with all required documentation and verifications received by the Medical Staff Office.,
workforce,credential_privileging,employment_competency,application_decision,application_decision,Credentialing Application Decision,STRING,,,,approved|denied|deferred|withdrawn|pending,master_data,Final decision rendered by the Medical Staff committee on the credentialing or reappointment application.,
workforce,credential_privileging,employment_competency,application_decision_date,application_decision_date,Application Decision Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,"The date on which the formal credentialing decision (approval, denial, deferral) was rendered by the Medical Staff committee.",
workforce,credential_privileging,employment_competency,application_submission_date,application_submission_date,Application Submission Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,The date on which the credentialing or reappointment application was formally submitted by the practitioner to the Medical Staff Office.,
workforce,credential_privileging,employment_competency,application_type,application_type,Credentialing Application Type,STRING,,,,initial|reappointment|reinstatement|modification|temporary,master_data,Type of credentialing or privileging application submitted by the practitioner. Initial applications are for new Medical Staff members; reappointment applications occur on the standard cycle (typically every 2 years).,
workforce,credential_privileging,employment_competency,appointment_effective_date,appointment_effective_date,Medical Staff Appointment Effective Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,"The date from which the Medical Staff appointment or reappointment becomes effective, authorizing the practitioner to practice at the facility.",
workforce,credential_privileging,employment_competency,appointment_expiration_date,appointment_expiration_date,Medical Staff Appointment Expiration Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,"The date on which the Medical Staff appointment expires, triggering the reappointment process. Typically every 24 months per TJC standards.",
workforce,credential_privileging,employment_competency,claim_denial_reason,claim_denial_reason,Application Denial Reason,STRING,,,dbx_confidential,,master_data,Documented reason for denial or deferral of a credentialing application or privilege request by the Medical Staff committee. Classified as confidential per peer review protection statutes.,
workforce,credential_privileging,employment_competency,cme_credit_hours,cme_credit_hours,Continuing Medical Education (CME) Credit Hours,"DECIMAL(6,2)",,,,,master_data,Number of Continuing Medical Education (CME) credit hours earned by the workforce member relevant to this credential or privilege cycle. Used to verify CME requirements for license renewal and reappointment.,
workforce,credential_privileging,employment_competency,cme_requirement_hours,cme_requirement_hours,Continuing Medical Education (CME) Requirement Hours,"DECIMAL(6,2)",,,,,master_data,Total number of CME credit hours required for the current credentialing or license renewal cycle as mandated by the issuing authority or Medical Staff bylaws.,
workforce,credential_privileging,employment_competency,competency_assessment_date,competency_assessment_date,Competency Assessment Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,The date on which the formal competency assessment or skills validation was conducted for the workforce member.,
workforce,credential_privileging,employment_competency,competency_assessment_score,competency_assessment_score,Competency Assessment Score,"DECIMAL(5,2)",,,,,master_data,"Numeric score from a formal competency assessment, skills validation, or simulation evaluation conducted to verify the practitioners proficiency for a specific privilege or clinical activity.",
workforce,credential_privileging,employment_competency,competency_type,competency_type,Competency Record Type,STRING,,,,credential|privilege|credentialing_application,master_data,"Discriminator indicating whether this record represents a professional credential, a clinical privilege, or a credentialing/re-credentialing application.",
workforce,credential_privileging,employment_competency,created_timestamp,created_timestamp,Record Created Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,master_data,"The timestamp when this employment competency record was first created in the system, supporting audit trail and data lineage requirements.",
workforce,credential_privileging,employment_competency,department_name,department_name,Medical Staff Department Name,STRING,,,,,master_data,"The clinical department within the Medical Staff organization to which the practitioner is assigned (e.g., Department of Medicine, Department of Surgery, Department of Radiology).",
workforce,credential_privileging,employment_competency,expiration_date,expiration_date,Credential Expiration Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,"The date on which the credential, license, or certification expires and must be renewed. Null for credentials with no expiration (e.g., certain board certifications).",
workforce,credential_privileging,employment_competency,issue_date,issue_date,Credential Issue Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,"The date on which the credential, license, or certification was originally issued by the issuing authority.",
workforce,credential_privileging,employment_competency,issuing_authority,issuing_authority,Issuing Authority,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Name of the organization, board, or government body that issued the credential (e.g., State Medical Board, Drug Enforcement Administration, American Board of Internal Medicine, State Board of Nursing).",
workforce,credential_privileging,employment_competency,issuing_country,issuing_country,Issuing Country Code,STRING,,,,^[A-Z]{3}$,master_data,ISO 3166-1 alpha-3 country code of the jurisdiction that issued the credential. Supports international medical graduates and foreign-trained clinicians.,
workforce,credential_privileging,employment_competency,issuing_state,issuing_state,Issuing State Code,STRING,,,,^[A-Z]{2}$,master_data,"Two-letter US state code of the jurisdiction that issued the credential. Applicable for state-issued licenses (medical, nursing, pharmacy). Null for federal or national credentials.",
workforce,credential_privileging,employment_competency,malpractice_coverage_verified,malpractice_coverage_verified,Malpractice Coverage Verification Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,Indicates whether the practitioners professional liability (malpractice) insurance coverage has been verified as meeting the facilitys minimum coverage requirements during the credentialing process.,
workforce,credential_privileging,employment_competency,medical_staff_category,medical_staff_category,Medical Staff Category,STRING,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii",,master_data,"The Medical Staff membership category assigned to the practitioner, defining their rights, responsibilities, and voting privileges within the Medical Staff organization. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: active|associate|courtesy|consulting|honorary|provisional|affiliate — 7 candidates stripped; promote to reference product]",
workforce,credential_privileging,employment_competency,medical_staff_committee,medical_staff_committee,Medical Staff Committee,STRING,,,"dbx_restricted, dbx_pii",,master_data,"Name of the Medical Staff committee responsible for reviewing and approving the clinical privilege (e.g., Credentials Committee, Executive Committee of the Medical Staff, Department of Surgery Peer Review Committee).",
workforce,credential_privileging,employment_competency,npdb_query_date,npdb_query_date,National Practitioner Data Bank (NPDB) Query Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,"The date on which the National Practitioner Data Bank (NPDB) was queried for adverse action reports, malpractice payments, and licensure actions related to this practitioner as part of the credentialing process.",
workforce,credential_privileging,employment_competency,npdb_query_result,npdb_query_result,National Practitioner Data Bank (NPDB) Query Result,STRING,,,dbx_confidential,no_report|report_found|pending,master_data,Result of the NPDB query indicating whether adverse action reports or malpractice payment reports were found for the practitioner. Classified as confidential per NPDB disclosure restrictions.,
workforce,credential_privileging,employment_competency,oig_exclusion_check_date,oig_exclusion_check_date,Office of Inspector General (OIG) Exclusion Check Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,The most recent date on which the practitioner was screened against the OIG List of Excluded Individuals and Entities (LEIE). Monthly screening is recommended by OIG.,
workforce,credential_privileging,employment_competency,oig_exclusion_checked,oig_exclusion_checked,Office of Inspector General (OIG) Exclusion Check Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,Indicates whether the practitioner has been screened against the OIG List of Excluded Individuals and Entities (LEIE) as required for participation in Medicare and Medicaid programs.,
workforce,credential_privileging,employment_competency,primary_source_verified,primary_source_verified,Primary Source Verification (PSV) Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,Indicates whether the credential has been verified directly with the issuing authority (primary source verification) as required by NCQA and The Joint Commission credentialing standards.,
workforce,credential_privileging,employment_competency,privilege_category,privilege_category,Clinical Privilege Category,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Classification of the clinical privilege granted by the Medical Staff (e.g., core privileges, special privileges, temporary privileges, telemedicine privileges, surgical privileges). [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: core|special|temporary|provisional|telemedicine|surgical|procedural|admitting|consulting — promote to reference product]",
workforce,credential_privileging,employment_competency,privilege_effective_date,privilege_effective_date,Privilege Effective Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,The date from which the clinical privilege becomes operationally effective and the practitioner is authorized to perform the privileged activity at the facility.,
workforce,credential_privileging,employment_competency,privilege_expiration_date,privilege_expiration_date,Privilege Expiration Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,The date on which the clinical privilege expires and must be reappointed through the Medical Staff reappointment process. Typically aligned with the Medical Staff appointment cycle (every 2 years per TJC).,
workforce,credential_privileging,employment_competency,privilege_grant_date,privilege_grant_date,Privilege Grant Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,The date on which the Medical Staff committee formally approved and granted the clinical privilege to the practitioner.,
workforce,credential_privileging,employment_competency,privilege_procedure_code,privilege_procedure_code,Privilege Procedure/Service Code,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Standardized code identifying the specific procedure, service, or clinical activity for which the privilege is granted. May reference CPT, HCPCS, or facility-defined procedure codes from the Delineation of Privileges form.",
workforce,credential_privileging,employment_competency,privilege_procedure_name,privilege_procedure_name,Privilege Procedure/Service Name,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Human-readable name of the specific procedure, service, or clinical activity for which the privilege is granted (e.g., laparoscopic cholecystectomy, cardiac catheterization, endotracheal intubation).",
workforce,credential_privileging,employment_competency,privilege_status,privilege_status,Clinical Privilege Status,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Current status of the clinical privilege as granted by the Medical Staff committee. Tracks the full privilege lifecycle from provisional grant through active, suspension, or revocation. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: active|provisional|suspended|revoked|expired|pending|voluntary_relinquishment — 7 candidates stripped; promote to reference product]",
workforce,credential_privileging,employment_competency,provider_committee_review_date,provider_committee_review_date,Committee Review Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,The date on which the Credentials Committee or Medical Staff Executive Committee formally reviewed the credentialing application.,
workforce,credential_privileging,employment_competency,provider_credential_category,provider_credential_category,Credential Category,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Classification of the professional credential type held by the workforce member. Examples include medical license, DEA registration, board certification, nursing license, allied health certification, advanced practice credential. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: medical_license|dea_registration|board_certification|nursing_license|allied_health_certification|advanced_practice_credential|cme_certificate|other — promote to reference product]",
workforce,credential_privileging,employment_competency,provider_credential_number,provider_credential_number,Credential License Number,STRING,,,"dbx_pii_identifier,dbx_restricted,pii_pii,pii_sensitive",,master_data,"The official license, registration, or certification number issued by the credentialing authority (e.g., state medical license number, DEA registration number, board certification number). Constitutes PHI/PII as it directly identifies a licensed individual.",
workforce,credential_privileging,employment_competency,provider_credential_status,provider_credential_status,Credential Status,STRING,,,,active|expired|suspended|revoked|pending_renewal|surrendered,master_data,Current lifecycle status of the professional credential as reported by the issuing authority or verified through primary source verification.,
workforce,credential_privileging,employment_competency,psv_date,psv_date,Primary Source Verification (PSV) Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,The date on which primary source verification of the credential was completed. Required for NCQA and TJC credentialing compliance tracking.,
workforce,credential_privileging,employment_competency,psv_method,psv_method,Primary Source Verification (PSV) Method,STRING,,,,online_portal|written_confirmation|telephone|third_party_service|automated_feed,master_data,"Method used to perform primary source verification of the credential (e.g., online portal query, written confirmation from issuing authority, third-party verification service such as CAQH ProView).",
workforce,credential_privileging,employment_competency,renewal_date,renewal_date,Credential Renewal Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,The date on which the credential was most recently renewed. Tracks the renewal cycle for ongoing compliance monitoring.,
workforce,credential_privileging,employment_competency,sam_exclusion_checked,sam_exclusion_checked,System for Award Management (SAM) Exclusion Check Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,"Indicates whether the practitioner has been screened against the federal SAM.gov exclusions database, required for federally funded programs and research activities.",
workforce,credential_privileging,employment_competency,updated_timestamp,updated_timestamp,Record Updated Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,master_data,"The timestamp when this employment competency record was most recently modified, supporting audit trail and change tracking requirements.",
workforce,credential_privileging,position_procedure_authorization,position_procedure_authorization_id,position_procedure_authorization_id,Position Procedure Authorization Identifier,BIGINT,Y,,,,association_data,Unique surrogate identifier for this position-procedure authorization record. Primary key.,
workforce,credential_privileging,position_procedure_authorization,cpt_code_id,cpt_code_id,Position Procedure Authorization - Cpt Code Id,BIGINT,,reference.cpt_code.cpt_code_id,,,association_data,Foreign key linking to the CPT procedure code,
workforce,credential_privileging,position_procedure_authorization,position_id,position_id,Position Procedure Authorization - Position Id,BIGINT,,workforce.position.position_id,,,association_data,Foreign key linking to the authorized organizational position,
workforce,credential_privileging,position_procedure_authorization,authorization_level,authorization_level,Authorization Level,STRING,,,,,association_data,Level of authorization granted to this position for performing this procedure. INDEPENDENT = can perform without supervision; SUPERVISED = requires attending oversight; ASSIST_ONLY = can assist but not perform as primary; RESTRICTED = special conditions apply.,
workforce,credential_privileging,position_procedure_authorization,authorization_status,authorization_status,Authorization Status,STRING,,,,,association_data,Current lifecycle status of this authorization. ACTIVE = currently valid; SUSPENDED = temporarily on hold; EXPIRED = past expiration date; REVOKED = permanently removed; PENDING = awaiting approval.,
workforce,credential_privileging,position_procedure_authorization,competency_validation_frequency,competency_validation_frequency,Competency Validation Frequency,STRING,,,,,association_data,"How often competency must be revalidated for this position-procedure authorization (e.g., ANNUAL, BIENNIAL, ONE_TIME). Drives credentialing and privileging cycles.",
workforce,credential_privileging,position_procedure_authorization,created_date,created_date,Record Created Date,TIMESTAMP,,,,,association_data,Timestamp when this authorization record was created in the system.,
workforce,credential_privileging,position_procedure_authorization,credentialing_committee_approval_date,credentialing_committee_approval_date,Credentialing Committee Approval Date,DATE,,,,,association_data,Date on which the medical staff credentialing committee approved this position-procedure authorization. Null if committee approval not required. Supports regulatory compliance and audit trails.,
workforce,credential_privileging,position_procedure_authorization,effective_date,effective_date,Authorization Effective Date,DATE,,,,,association_data,Date on which this position became authorized to perform this procedure. Tracks when credentialing or privilege granting occurred.,
workforce,credential_privileging,position_procedure_authorization,expiration_date,expiration_date,Authorization Expiration Date,DATE,,,,,association_data,Date on which this authorization expires and must be renewed. Null if authorization does not expire. Supports credentialing cycle management.,
workforce,credential_privileging,position_procedure_authorization,minimum_cases_required,minimum_cases_required,Minimum Cases Required,INT,,,,,association_data,Minimum number of observed or supervised cases required before independent authorization is granted for this position-procedure combination. Null if not applicable. Used in fellowship and residency competency tracking.,
workforce,credential_privileging,position_procedure_authorization,notes,notes,Authorization Notes,STRING,,,,,association_data,"Free-text notes regarding special conditions, restrictions, or context for this authorization (e.g., Limited to outpatient setting only, Requires peer review after first 5 cases). Null if no special notes.",
workforce,credential_privileging,position_procedure_authorization,supervision_requirement,supervision_requirement,Supervision Requirement,STRING,,,,,association_data,"Specific supervision requirements for this position when performing this procedure (e.g., Attending physician must be present, Indirect supervision acceptable, No supervision required). Drives scheduling and staffing rules.",
workforce,credential_privileging,position_procedure_authorization,training_description,training_description,Training Description,STRING,,,,,association_data,"Description of specific training, certification, or competency validation required for this position-procedure combination (e.g., ACLS certification, Observed cases: 10, Manufacturer device training). Null if no specific training required.",
workforce,credential_privileging,position_procedure_authorization,training_required,training_required,Training Required Indicator,BOOLEAN,,,,,association_data,Indicates whether specific training or certification is required before this position can perform this procedure. True = training prerequisite exists; False = no additional training beyond position requirements.,
workforce,credential_privileging,position_procedure_authorization,updated_date,updated_date,Record Updated Date,TIMESTAMP,,,,,association_data,Timestamp when this authorization record was last updated.,
workforce,credential_privileging,position_procedure_authorization,volume_expectation,volume_expectation,Volume Expectation,STRING,,,,,association_data,"Expected annual or monthly volume of this procedure for this position type (e.g., 50-100 per year, Core competency - frequent, Rare - maintain competency only). Used for competency maintenance planning and workload forecasting.",
workforce,credential_privileging,position_procedure_authorization,created_by,created_by,Record Created By,STRING,,,,,association_data,User or system identifier that created this authorization record.,
workforce,credential_privileging,workforce_provider_network_participation,workforce_provider_network_participation_id,workforce_provider_network_participation_id,Provider Network Participation - Provider Network Participation Id,BIGINT,Y,,,,association_data,Primary key for the provider_network_participation association,
workforce,credential_privileging,workforce_provider_network_participation,employee_id,employee_id,Provider Network Participation - Employee Id,BIGINT,,workforce.employee.employee_id,"dbx_confidential, dbx_pii,employee_id=workforce_provider_network_participation_employee_id",,association_data,"Foreign key linking to the clinical workforce member participating in the payer network. Only clinical employees with NPI numbers (physicians, nurses, allied health) participate in payer networks.",
workforce,credential_privileging,workforce_provider_network_participation,payer_id,payer_id,Provider Network Participation - Payer Id,BIGINT,,insurance.payer.payer_id,,,association_data,Foreign key linking to the insurance payer whose network the provider is participating in.,
workforce,credential_privileging,workforce_provider_network_participation,accepting_new_patients_flag,accepting_new_patients_flag,Accepting New Patients Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,association_data,Indicates whether this provider is currently accepting new patients covered by this payer. Used for payer provider directories and patient access management. Can vary by payer even for the same provider.,
workforce,credential_privileging,workforce_provider_network_participation,credentialing_expiration_date,credentialing_expiration_date,Credentialing Expiration Date,DATE,,,,,association_data,The date on which the providers credentialing with this payer expires and must be renewed. Payers typically require re-credentialing every 2-3 years. Used for proactive renewal tracking.,
workforce,credential_privileging,workforce_provider_network_participation,credentialing_status,credentialing_status,Credentialing Status,STRING,,,,,association_data,"Current status of the providers credentialing with this payer. Determines whether the provider can submit claims to this payer. Values: pending, approved, denied, suspended, expired, in_review.",
workforce,credential_privileging,workforce_provider_network_participation,effective_date,effective_date,Participation Effective Date,DATE,,,,,association_data,The date on which this providers participation in this payers network became or will become effective. Claims submitted for services on or after this date can be billed to this payer under this participation agreement.,
workforce,credential_privileging,workforce_provider_network_participation,enrollment_date,enrollment_date,Enrollment Date,DATE,,,,,association_data,The date on which the provider enrollment application was submitted to this payer. Used for tracking credentialing timelines and regulatory compliance with enrollment processing requirements.,
workforce,credential_privileging,workforce_provider_network_participation,facility_contract_reference_number,facility_contract_reference_number,Contract Reference Number,STRING,,,,,association_data,Reference number or identifier for the underlying participation contract or agreement between the healthcare organization and this payer that governs this providers participation terms.,
workforce,credential_privileging,workforce_provider_network_participation,network_participation_status,network_participation_status,Network Participation Status,STRING,,,,,association_data,"Current status of the providers active participation in this payers network. Values: active, inactive, terminated, pending_activation. Distinct from credentialing_status which tracks approval; this tracks operational participation.",
workforce,credential_privileging,workforce_provider_network_participation,network_tier,network_tier,Network Tier Assignment,STRING,,,,,association_data,"The tier or level of network participation assigned by the payer (e.g., Tier 1, Preferred, Standard, Out-of-Network). Affects reimbursement rates and patient cost-sharing. Varies by payer and provider.",
workforce,credential_privileging,workforce_provider_network_participation,payer_provider_number,payer_provider_number,Payer-Specific Provider Number,STRING,,,,,association_data,"The unique provider identifier assigned by this specific payer to this provider for claims submission. Distinct from NPI, this is the payers internal provider ID used in claim transactions and remittance advice.",
workforce,credential_privileging,workforce_provider_network_participation,reimbursement_rate_schedule,reimbursement_rate_schedule,Reimbursement Rate Schedule,STRING,,,,,association_data,Identifier or code for the fee schedule or reimbursement rate table that applies to this provider-payer participation. Different providers may have different negotiated rates with the same payer based on contract terms.,
workforce,credential_privileging,workforce_provider_network_participation,termination_date,termination_date,Participation Termination Date,DATE,,,,,association_data,The date on which this providers participation in this payers network ended or will end. Null for active ongoing participations. Claims for services after this date cannot be submitted under this participation.,
workforce,schedule_operations,channel_support_assignment,channel_support_assignment_id,channel_support_assignment_id,Channel Support Assignment Identifier,BIGINT,Y,,,,association_data,Unique surrogate identifier for each support assignment record. Primary key for the association.,
workforce,schedule_operations,channel_support_assignment,employee_id,employee_id,Channel Support Assignment - Employee Id,BIGINT,,workforce.employee.employee_id,"dbx_confidential, dbx_pii,employee_id=channel_support_assignment_employee_id",,association_data,Rename employee_id to channel_support_employee_id for clarity,
workforce,schedule_operations,channel_support_assignment,interface_channel_id,interface_channel_id,Channel Support Assignment - Interface Channel Id,BIGINT,,interoperability.interface_channel.interface_channel_id,,,association_data,Foreign key linking to the interface channel being supported by this workforce member,
workforce,schedule_operations,channel_support_assignment,created_timestamp,created_timestamp,Record Creation Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,association_data,System timestamp when this support assignment record was created in the data warehouse.,
workforce,schedule_operations,channel_support_assignment,escalation_tier,escalation_tier,Escalation Tier Level,INT,,,,,association_data,"Numeric tier level (1-3) indicating the escalation hierarchy for incident management. Tier 1 is first responder, Tier 2 is technical specialist, Tier 3 is senior architect or vendor escalation.",
workforce,schedule_operations,channel_support_assignment,notification_preference,notification_preference,Incident Notification Preference,STRING,,,,,association_data,The preferred communication channel for notifying this workforce member about incidents or alerts related to this interface channel. Used by incident management and alerting systems.,
workforce,schedule_operations,channel_support_assignment,on_call_rotation,on_call_rotation,On-Call Rotation Schedule,STRING,,,,,association_data,"The on-call rotation schedule identifier or pattern assigned to this support assignment (e.g., Week 1-2, Weekday Primary, Weekend Backup). Used for workforce scheduling and incident routing.",
workforce,schedule_operations,channel_support_assignment,provider_assignment_end_date,provider_assignment_end_date,Assignment End Date,DATE,,,,,association_data,The date on which this support assignment ended or is scheduled to end. Null indicates an active ongoing assignment. Used for rotation management and historical analysis.,
workforce,schedule_operations,channel_support_assignment,provider_assignment_start_date,provider_assignment_start_date,Assignment Start Date,DATE,,,,,association_data,The date on which this support assignment became effective. Used for historical tracking of support responsibility and workforce planning.,
workforce,schedule_operations,channel_support_assignment,provider_assignment_status,provider_assignment_status,Assignment Status,STRING,,,,,association_data,"Current lifecycle status of the support assignment. Active indicates current operational assignment, Inactive indicates ended assignment, Suspended indicates temporarily paused (e.g., employee on leave), Pending indicates future scheduled assignment.",
workforce,schedule_operations,channel_support_assignment,support_role,support_role,Support Role Type,STRING,,,,,association_data,"The tiered support role assigned to this workforce member for this specific interface channel. Primary indicates first-line support, Backup indicates secondary coverage, Escalation indicates senior technical escalation point, On-Call indicates rotation-based availability.",
workforce,schedule_operations,channel_support_assignment,updated_timestamp,updated_timestamp,Record Update Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,association_data,System timestamp when this support assignment record was last updated in the data warehouse.,
workforce,schedule_operations,fte_budget,fte_budget_id,fte_budget_id,Full-Time Equivalent (FTE) Budget ID,BIGINT,Y,,,,master_data,Unique surrogate identifier for each authorized FTE budget allocation record in the workforce financial planning system.,
workforce,schedule_operations,fte_budget,care_site_id,care_site_id,Facility ID,BIGINT,,facility.care_site.care_site_id,,,master_data,"Reference to the physical facility (hospital, clinic, outpatient center) where this FTE budget is authorized. Supports multi-site workforce planning and staffing ratio compliance.",
workforce,schedule_operations,fte_budget,fiscal_period_id,fiscal_period_id,Fiscal Period Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,finance.fiscal_period.fiscal_period_id,,,master_data,"Foreign key linking to finance.fiscal_period. Business justification: FTE budgets are tracked by fiscal period for monthly/quarterly workforce planning. Enables period-over-period FTE variance analysis, budget phasing, and alignment of workforce budget cycles with finan",
workforce,schedule_operations,fte_budget,position_id,position_id,Position ID,BIGINT,,workforce.position.position_id,,,master_data,Reference to the authorized position in Workday HCM to which this FTE budget line is tied. Enables position-level budget tracking and vacancy analysis.,
workforce,schedule_operations,fte_budget,workforce_org_unit_id,workforce_org_unit_id,Workforce Org Unit Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,workforce.org_unit.org_unit_id,,,master_data,Foreign key linking to workforce.org_unit. Business justification: FTE budget is allocated by organizational unit. fte_budget currently has department_id (BIGINT with no FK target) and department_name (denormalized string). Adding workforce_org_unit_id links to the a,
workforce,schedule_operations,fte_budget,actual_fte,actual_fte,Actual Full-Time Equivalent (FTE) Utilized,"DECIMAL(10,4)",,,,,master_data,"The actual FTE count consumed during the fiscal period, sourced from Workday HCM time and attendance data. Used for variance analysis against budgeted FTE.",
workforce,schedule_operations,fte_budget,actual_hours,actual_hours,Actual Hours Worked,"DECIMAL(14,2)",,,,,master_data,Actual hours worked recorded in Workday HCM time and attendance for this budget line during the fiscal period. Used for FTE conversion and productivity benchmarking.,
workforce,schedule_operations,fte_budget,actual_labor_cost,actual_labor_cost,Actual Labor Cost (USD),"DECIMAL(18,2)",,,dbx_confidential,,master_data,"Actual labor cost incurred in USD for this budget line during the fiscal period, sourced from SAP S/4HANA payroll postings. Compared against budgeted_labor_cost for variance analysis.",
workforce,schedule_operations,fte_budget,agency_fte,agency_fte,Agency/Contract Full-Time Equivalent (FTE),"DECIMAL(10,4)",,,,,master_data,The FTE equivalent of agency or contract labor utilized within this budget line during the fiscal period. Tracked separately from employed FTE for labor cost benchmarking and workforce mix analysis.,
workforce,schedule_operations,fte_budget,approval_date,approval_date,Budget Approval Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,The date on which this FTE budget allocation was formally approved by the authorized budget authority. Marks the transition from pending to approved status.,
workforce,schedule_operations,fte_budget,approved_by,approved_by,Approved By,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Name or employee identifier of the budget authority (e.g., CFO, VP of Finance, Department Director) who approved this FTE budget allocation. Supports audit trail and governance requirements.",
workforce,schedule_operations,fte_budget,benefits_burden_pct,benefits_burden_pct,Benefits Burden Percentage,"DECIMAL(6,2)",,,dbx_confidential,,master_data,"The percentage applied to base wages to account for employer-paid benefits costs (health insurance, retirement, FICA, workers compensation) for this FTE budget line. Used to calculate total labor cost including benefits.",
workforce,schedule_operations,fte_budget,budget_code,budget_code,FTE Budget Code,STRING,,,,"^[A-Z0-9-]{4,20}$",master_data,"pii_phi,pii_pii,pii_sensitive",
workforce,schedule_operations,fte_budget,budget_status,budget_status,Budget Approval Status,STRING,,,,draft|pending_approval|approved|rejected|superseded,master_data,"Current workflow status of this FTE budget allocation record: draft (in preparation), pending_approval (submitted for review), approved (authorized), rejected (denied), or superseded (replaced by a revised version).",
workforce,schedule_operations,fte_budget,budget_version,budget_version,Budget Version,STRING,,,,original|revised|final|forecast,master_data,"Identifies the version of the FTE budget record: original (initial approved budget), revised (mid-year amendment), final (year-end actuals reconciliation), or forecast (rolling forecast update). Supports budget cycle management.",
workforce,schedule_operations,fte_budget,budgeted_avg_hourly_rate,budgeted_avg_hourly_rate,Budgeted Average Hourly Rate (USD),"DECIMAL(10,4)",,,dbx_confidential,,master_data,"The budgeted average hourly wage rate in USD for positions covered by this FTE budget line, inclusive of base pay and applicable differentials. Used for labor cost projection and variance analysis.",
workforce,schedule_operations,fte_budget,budgeted_fte,budgeted_fte,Budgeted Full-Time Equivalent (FTE) Count,"DECIMAL(10,4)",,,,,master_data,"The authorized number of Full-Time Equivalent (FTE) positions approved for this department, cost center, job family, and fiscal period. Expressed as a decimal (e.g., 2.5 FTE). The principal quantitative fact of this budget record.",
workforce,schedule_operations,fte_budget,budgeted_hours,budgeted_hours,Budgeted Hours,"DECIMAL(14,2)",,,,,master_data,Total authorized worked hours budgeted for this FTE line in the fiscal period. Derived from budgeted FTE and standard hours per period; stored for direct comparison with actual hours from time and attendance.,
workforce,schedule_operations,fte_budget,budgeted_labor_cost,budgeted_labor_cost,Budgeted Labor Cost (USD),"DECIMAL(18,2)",,,dbx_confidential,,master_data,"Total authorized labor cost in USD for this FTE budget line for the fiscal period, including base wages, differentials, and benefits burden. Used for workforce financial planning and labor cost management.",
workforce,schedule_operations,fte_budget,budgeted_nonproductive_fte,budgeted_nonproductive_fte,Budgeted Non-Productive Full-Time Equivalent (FTE),"DECIMAL(10,4)",,,,,master_data,"The portion of the total budgeted FTE allocated to non-productive hours including paid time off (PTO), orientation, education, and leave. Supports total labor cost planning.",
workforce,schedule_operations,fte_budget,budgeted_overtime_fte,budgeted_overtime_fte,Budgeted Overtime Full-Time Equivalent (FTE),"DECIMAL(10,4)",,,,,master_data,The FTE equivalent of overtime hours budgeted for this department and fiscal period. Supports overtime cost management and FLSA compliance monitoring.,
workforce,schedule_operations,fte_budget,budgeted_productive_fte,budgeted_productive_fte,Budgeted Productive Full-Time Equivalent (FTE),"DECIMAL(10,4)",,,,,master_data,The portion of the total budgeted FTE allocated specifically to productive (direct patient care) hours. Used to calculate staffing ratios and productivity benchmarks per adjusted patient day.,
workforce,schedule_operations,fte_budget,cost_center_code,cost_center_code,Cost Center Code,STRING,,,,"^[A-Z0-9-]{3,15}$",master_data,SAP S/4HANA CO cost center code to which this FTE budget is financially assigned. Enables labor cost allocation and variance reporting at the cost center level.,
workforce,schedule_operations,fte_budget,created_timestamp,created_timestamp,Record Created Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,master_data,"The timestamp when this FTE budget record was first created in the system, in ISO 8601 format (yyyy-MM-ddTHH:mm:ss.SSSXXX). Supports audit trail and data lineage requirements.",
workforce,schedule_operations,fte_budget,effective_date,effective_date,Budget Effective Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,The date from which this FTE budget allocation becomes effective and binding for workforce planning and financial reporting purposes.,
workforce,schedule_operations,fte_budget,employment_type,employment_type,Employment Type,STRING,,,,full_time|part_time|per_diem|contract|agency,master_data,"Classification of the workforce category for this FTE budget line: full-time, part-time, per diem, contract, or agency staff. Supports workforce mix planning and FTE conversion calculations.",
workforce,schedule_operations,fte_budget,end_date,end_date,Budget End Date,DATE,,,,,master_data,The date on which this FTE budget allocation expires or is superseded. Null for open-ended or current-period budgets. Supports temporal budget management and historical reporting.,
workforce,schedule_operations,fte_budget,fiscal_period,fiscal_period,Fiscal Period,STRING,,,,^(Q[1-4]|P(0[1-9]|1[0-2]))$,master_data,The fiscal period (quarter Q1–Q4 or accounting period P01–P12) within the fiscal year for which this FTE budget is authorized. Supports monthly and quarterly workforce financial planning cycles.,
workforce,schedule_operations,fte_budget,fiscal_year,fiscal_year,Fiscal Year,INT,,,,,master_data,"The four-digit fiscal year to which this FTE budget allocation applies, aligned with the organizations financial planning calendar (e.g., 2024).",
workforce,schedule_operations,fte_budget,flsa_classification,flsa_classification,Fair Labor Standards Act (FLSA) Classification,STRING,,,,exempt|non_exempt,master_data,"FLSA classification of the positions covered by this FTE budget line: exempt (salaried, not eligible for overtime) or non-exempt (hourly, eligible for overtime pay). Drives overtime budget calculations.",
workforce,schedule_operations,fte_budget,fte_variance,fte_variance,FTE Variance,"DECIMAL(10,4)",,,,,master_data,The difference between budgeted FTE and actual FTE (budgeted_fte minus actual_fte) for the fiscal period. Positive value indicates under-utilization; negative value indicates over-budget staffing. Supports labor cost variance reporting.,
workforce,schedule_operations,fte_budget,is_union_position,is_union_position,Is Union Position Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,"Indicates whether this FTE budget line covers union-represented positions (True) or non-union positions (False). Affects labor cost modeling, scheduling constraints, and collective bargaining agreement compliance.",
workforce,schedule_operations,fte_budget,job_code,job_code,Job Code,STRING,,,,"^[A-Z0-9-]{3,15}$",master_data,Workday HCM job profile code identifying the specific job classification for this FTE budget line. Aligns with pay grade structures and staffing ratio standards.,
workforce,schedule_operations,fte_budget,job_family,job_family,Job Family,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Workday HCM job family classification grouping positions by functional role (e.g., Nursing, Physician, Allied Health, Administrative, Support Services). Used for workforce mix analysis and productivity benchmarking. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: Nursing|Physician|Allied Health|Administrative|Support Services|Pharmacy|Laboratory|Radiology|Therapy — promote to reference product]",
workforce,schedule_operations,fte_budget,labor_cost_per_apd,labor_cost_per_apd,Labor Cost per Adjusted Patient Day (APD),"DECIMAL(14,4)",,,dbx_confidential,,master_data,Budgeted labor cost divided by adjusted patient days (APD) for the fiscal period. A key productivity benchmark metric used in healthcare workforce financial planning and CMS value-based purchasing (VBP) reporting.,
workforce,schedule_operations,fte_budget,labor_cost_variance,labor_cost_variance,Labor Cost Variance (USD),"DECIMAL(18,2)",,,dbx_confidential,,master_data,The difference between budgeted and actual labor cost (budgeted_labor_cost minus actual_labor_cost) in USD. Positive value indicates favorable variance (under budget); negative indicates unfavorable (over budget).,
workforce,schedule_operations,fte_budget,notes,notes,Budget Notes,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Free-text field for budget analysts to document justifications, assumptions, mid-year amendments, or special circumstances associated with this FTE budget allocation (e.g., new service line launch, regulatory mandate, census-driven adjustment).",
workforce,schedule_operations,fte_budget,pay_grade,pay_grade,Pay Grade,STRING,,,dbx_confidential,"^[A-Z0-9-]{1,10}$",master_data,Workday HCM pay grade assigned to the positions in this FTE budget line. Determines the salary band used for labor cost budgeting and compensation planning.,
workforce,schedule_operations,fte_budget,pay_type,pay_type,Pay Type,STRING,,,,productive|non_productive|overtime|on_call|agency,master_data,"Classification of the FTE budget by labor pay category: productive (direct patient care hours), non-productive (PTO, education, orientation), overtime, on-call, or agency/contract labor. Critical for labor cost management and productivity benchmarking.",
workforce,schedule_operations,fte_budget,productivity_target_pct,productivity_target_pct,Productivity Target Percentage,"DECIMAL(6,2)",,,,,master_data,"The target productive hours as a percentage of total paid hours for this department and job family (e.g., 85.00%). Used for productivity benchmarking and workforce efficiency reporting.",
workforce,schedule_operations,fte_budget,source_system,source_system,Source System,STRING,,,,Workday|SAP_S4HANA|MEDITECH|Manual,master_data,"Identifies the operational system of record from which this FTE budget record originated (e.g., Workday HCM, SAP S/4HANA CO, MEDITECH, or Manual entry). Supports data lineage and ETL reconciliation.",
workforce,schedule_operations,fte_budget,staffing_ratio_target,staffing_ratio_target,Staffing Ratio Target,"DECIMAL(8,4)",,,,,master_data,"The target nurse-to-patient or staff-to-patient ratio for this department and job family as defined by regulatory or organizational standards (e.g., 1:4 for ICU nursing). Supports staffing ratio compliance monitoring.",
workforce,schedule_operations,fte_budget,standard_hours_per_fte,standard_hours_per_fte,Standard Hours per Full-Time Equivalent (FTE),"DECIMAL(8,2)",,,,,master_data,"The number of hours per fiscal period that constitutes one FTE for this job family and employment type (e.g., 2080 hours annually, 173.33 hours monthly). Used as the FTE conversion denominator.",
workforce,schedule_operations,fte_budget,union_code,union_code,Union Code,STRING,,,,"^[A-Z0-9-]{2,10}$",master_data,"Code identifying the labor union or collective bargaining unit associated with this FTE budget line (e.g., SEIU, CNA, AFSCME). Impacts wage rates, scheduling rules, and staffing ratio requirements.",
workforce,schedule_operations,fte_budget,updated_timestamp,updated_timestamp,Record Last Updated Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,master_data,"The timestamp when this FTE budget record was most recently modified, in ISO 8601 format (yyyy-MM-ddTHH:mm:ss.SSSXXX). Supports change tracking and audit compliance.",
workforce,schedule_operations,fte_budget,vacancy_fte,vacancy_fte,Vacancy Full-Time Equivalent (FTE),"DECIMAL(10,4)",,,,,master_data,"The number of FTE positions that are budgeted but currently unfilled (budgeted_fte minus filled FTE). Supports vacancy rate reporting, recruitment planning, and agency/contract labor justification.",
workforce,schedule_operations,staffing_assignment,staffing_assignment_id,staffing_assignment_id,Staffing Assignment ID,BIGINT,Y,,,,association_data,System-generated surrogate primary key for the staffing assignment record.,
workforce,schedule_operations,staffing_assignment,employee_id,employee_id,Staffing Assignment - Employee Id,BIGINT,,workforce.employee.employee_id,"confidential,pii",,association_data,Foreign key linking to the workforce employee who is assigned to the post-acute location,Internal - M:N Association FK
workforce,schedule_operations,staffing_assignment,post_acute_location_id,post_acute_location_id,Staffing Assignment - Post Acute Location Id,BIGINT,,post_acute_care.post_acute_location.post_acute_location_id,,,association_data,Foreign key linking to the post-acute care location where the employee is assigned to work,Internal - M:N Association FK
workforce,schedule_operations,staffing_assignment,assignment_role,assignment_role,Assignment Role,STRING,,,,,association_data,The specific clinical or administrative role the employee fills at this post-acute location. An employee may hold different roles at different locations.,
workforce,schedule_operations,staffing_assignment,credentialing_status,credentialing_status,Location Credentialing Status,STRING,,,,,association_data,Status of the employee's credential verification specific to this post-acute location. CMS requires facility-level credentialing verification for post-acute care settings. Status is per-location because different facilities may have different credentialing requirements.,
workforce,schedule_operations,staffing_assignment,effective_from,effective_from,Assignment Effective From Date,DATE,,,,,association_data,Date when the employee's assignment to this post-acute location becomes active. Required for tracking assignment history and compliance reporting.,
workforce,schedule_operations,staffing_assignment,effective_until,effective_until,Assignment Effective Until Date,DATE,,,,,association_data,Date when the employee's assignment to this post-acute location ends. Null indicates an open-ended/current assignment. Used for contract expiration tracking and renewal workflows.,
workforce,schedule_operations,staffing_assignment,fte_allocation,fte_allocation,FTE Allocation,"DECIMAL(5,4)",,,,,association_data,"Proportion of the employee's full-time equivalent allocated to this specific post-acute location. Enables tracking of split assignments across multiple locations (e.g., 0.6 FTE at Location A, 0.4 FTE at Location B).",
workforce,schedule_operations,time_attendance,time_attendance_id,time_attendance_id,Time and Attendance Record ID,BIGINT,Y,,,,transactional_data,Unique surrogate identifier for each time and attendance / payroll record in the Workday HCM Time Tracking and Payroll system. Primary key for the time_attendance data product.,
workforce,schedule_operations,time_attendance,care_site_id,care_site_id,Facility ID,BIGINT,,facility.care_site.care_site_id,,,transactional_data,"Reference to the healthcare facility (hospital, clinic, outpatient center) where the worker performed their shift or work assignment.",
workforce,schedule_operations,time_attendance,chart_of_accounts_id,chart_of_accounts_id,Chart Of Accounts Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,finance.chart_of_accounts.chart_of_accounts_id,,,transactional_data,Foreign key linking to finance.chart_of_accounts. Business justification: Time and attendance records must post labor costs to specific GL accounts for payroll expense recognition. Currently has gl_account_code as text. FK to chart_of_accounts enables proper labor cost acco,
workforce,schedule_operations,time_attendance,cost_center_id,cost_center_id,Cost Center ID,BIGINT,,finance.cost_center.cost_center_id,,,transactional_data,Reference to the General Ledger (GL) cost center to which labor costs for this record are allocated. Supports labor cost allocation by department and cost center for financial reporting.,
workforce,schedule_operations,time_attendance,employee_id,employee_id,Worker ID,BIGINT,,workforce.employee.employee_id,"dbx_confidential, dbx_pii",,transactional_data,Reference to the employee or contract worker whose time and attendance record this row represents. Links to the workforce worker/employee master.,
workforce,schedule_operations,time_attendance,fiscal_period_id,fiscal_period_id,Fiscal Period Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,finance.fiscal_period.fiscal_period_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to finance.fiscal_period. Business justification: Payroll accruals and labor costs must align with fiscal period close. Links time/attendance to fiscal period for payroll accrual accuracy, period-end labor cost cutoff, and reconciliation of payroll e",
workforce,schedule_operations,time_attendance,payroll_run_id,payroll_run_id,Payroll Run ID,BIGINT,,workforce.payroll_run.payroll_run_id,,,transactional_data,"The identifier of the Workday HCM payroll run batch in which this record was processed. Used for payroll reconciliation, audit, and reprocessing of failed payroll runs.",
workforce,schedule_operations,time_attendance,position_id,position_id,Position ID,BIGINT,,workforce.position.position_id,,,transactional_data,"Reference to the specific position or job assignment held by the worker during this pay period, supporting multi-position employees common in healthcare settings.",
workforce,schedule_operations,time_attendance,workforce_org_unit_id,workforce_org_unit_id,Workforce Org Unit Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,workforce.org_unit.org_unit_id,,,transactional_data,"Foreign key linking to workforce.org_unit. Business justification: Time and attendance records must be linked to organizational unit for labor cost allocation, payroll processing by org unit, and workforce analytics. time_attendance currently has department_code (den",
workforce,schedule_operations,time_attendance,approval_status,approval_status,Time Record Approval Status,STRING,,,,pending|approved|rejected|corrected|submitted,transactional_data,Current workflow state of the time and attendance record in the approval lifecycle. Pending indicates awaiting manager review; approved indicates manager-confirmed; corrected indicates timekeeper adjustment applied.,
workforce,schedule_operations,time_attendance,approval_timestamp,approval_timestamp,Approval Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,Date and time when the manager or timekeeper approved this time record. Distinct from payroll processing timestamp; used for SLA monitoring of approval workflows.,
workforce,schedule_operations,time_attendance,base_pay_rate,base_pay_rate,Base Pay Rate,"DECIMAL(12,4)",,,dbx_confidential,,transactional_data,"The employees base hourly rate or annualized salary rate used for payroll calculation. For hourly employees, expressed as dollars per hour; for salaried employees, expressed as annual salary divided by pay periods.",
workforce,schedule_operations,time_attendance,benefits_deduction,benefits_deduction,Benefits Deduction Amount,"DECIMAL(10,2)",,,dbx_confidential,,transactional_data,"Total amount deducted for employee benefits including health insurance premiums, dental, vision, life insurance, and retirement plan contributions (e.g., 401k) during this pay period.",
workforce,schedule_operations,time_attendance,bonus_amount,bonus_amount,Bonus Pay Amount,"DECIMAL(10,2)",,,dbx_confidential,,transactional_data,"Any bonus, incentive, or supplemental pay included in this payroll record, such as retention bonuses, sign-on bonuses, or performance incentives. Zero if no bonus applies.",
workforce,schedule_operations,time_attendance,clock_in_timestamp,clock_in_timestamp,Clock-In Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,"The date and time the worker clocked in to begin their shift, as recorded by Workday HCM Time Tracking. Represents the principal real-world business event time for shift start.",
workforce,schedule_operations,time_attendance,clock_out_timestamp,clock_out_timestamp,Clock-Out Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,The date and time the worker clocked out to end their shift. Null if the worker has not yet clocked out or if a missed punch was recorded.,
workforce,schedule_operations,time_attendance,correction_reason,correction_reason,Timekeeper Correction Reason,STRING,,,,missed_punch|system_error|schedule_change|manager_adjustment|employee_request|other,transactional_data,Reason code explaining why a timekeeper correction was applied to this record. Required when timekeeper_corrected is True for audit and compliance purposes.,
workforce,schedule_operations,time_attendance,created_timestamp,created_timestamp,Record Created Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,The date and time when this time and attendance record was first created in Workday HCM. Serves as the audit record creation timestamp for data lineage and compliance purposes.,
workforce,schedule_operations,time_attendance,flsa_compliance_flag,flsa_compliance_flag,FLSA (Fair Labor Standards Act) Compliance Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,"System-generated flag indicating whether this time record is compliant with FLSA requirements (e.g., overtime thresholds met, minimum wage satisfied). False triggers a compliance review workflow.",
workforce,schedule_operations,time_attendance,flsa_exempt,flsa_exempt,FLSA (Fair Labor Standards Act) Exempt Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,Indicates whether the employee is classified as exempt from FLSA overtime requirements (True = exempt salaried; False = non-exempt hourly). Critical for overtime eligibility determination and FLSA compliance audits.,
workforce,schedule_operations,time_attendance,fte_percentage,fte_percentage,Full-Time Equivalent (FTE) Percentage,"DECIMAL(5,2)",,,,,transactional_data,"The Full-Time Equivalent (FTE) percentage associated with this workers position for this pay period, expressed as a decimal (e.g., 1.00 = full-time, 0.50 = half-time). Used for workforce FTE tracking and labor cost allocation.",
workforce,schedule_operations,time_attendance,garnishment_deduction,garnishment_deduction,Garnishment Deduction Amount,"DECIMAL(10,2)",,,dbx_confidential,,transactional_data,"Total amount withheld for court-ordered wage garnishments (child support, creditor garnishments, tax levies) during this pay period. Zero if no garnishment applies.",
workforce,schedule_operations,time_attendance,gl_account_code,gl_account_code,General Ledger (GL) Account Code,STRING,,,,,transactional_data,The General Ledger (GL) account code used to post labor costs for this time record in SAP S/4HANA. Supports financial reporting and labor cost allocation by GL account.,
workforce,schedule_operations,time_attendance,gross_pay_amount,gross_pay_amount,Gross Pay Amount,"DECIMAL(12,2)",,,dbx_confidential,,transactional_data,"Total gross compensation earned by the employee for the pay period before any deductions, including base pay, shift differentials, overtime pay, and bonuses. Expressed in USD.",
workforce,schedule_operations,time_attendance,last_updated_timestamp,last_updated_timestamp,Record Last Updated Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,transactional_data,"The date and time when this time and attendance record was most recently modified in Workday HCM, including timekeeper corrections, approval status changes, or payroll adjustments.",
workforce,schedule_operations,time_attendance,leave_type,leave_type,Leave Type,STRING,,,,none|pto|fmla|sick|bereavement|jury_duty,transactional_data,Identifies the type of leave applied to this time record if the worker was absent. None indicates no leave; FMLA indicates Family and Medical Leave Act protected leave. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: none|pto|fmla|sick|bereavement|jury_duty|military|unpaid — promote to reference product if additional values needed],
workforce,schedule_operations,time_attendance,meal_break_minutes,meal_break_minutes,Meal Break Deduction Minutes,INT,,,,,transactional_data,Total minutes deducted for meal breaks during the shift or pay period. Applied per facility meal break policy and state labor law requirements to compute compensable hours.,
workforce,schedule_operations,time_attendance,missed_punch_count,missed_punch_count,Missed Punch Count,INT,,,,,transactional_data,Number of missed clock-in or clock-out punch events recorded for this worker during the pay period. Used for attendance compliance monitoring and timekeeper correction workflows.,
workforce,schedule_operations,time_attendance,net_pay_amount,net_pay_amount,Net Pay Amount,"DECIMAL(12,2)",,,dbx_confidential,,transactional_data,"Total net compensation paid to the employee after all deductions (taxes, benefits, garnishments) have been subtracted from gross pay. Represents the actual take-home amount.",
workforce,schedule_operations,time_attendance,on_call_hours,on_call_hours,On-Call Hours,"DECIMAL(8,2)",,,,,transactional_data,Total hours the employee was designated as on-call during the pay period. Tracked separately for on-call differential pay calculations and staffing analytics.,
workforce,schedule_operations,time_attendance,osha_incident_related,osha_incident_related,OSHA Incident Related Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,"Indicates whether this time record is associated with an OSHA-reportable workplace incident (e.g., injury, illness resulting in lost time). True triggers linkage to OSHA incident reporting workflows.",
workforce,schedule_operations,time_attendance,overtime_hours,overtime_hours,Overtime Hours,"DECIMAL(8,2)",,,,,transactional_data,"Total overtime hours worked during the pay period, as defined by FLSA thresholds (hours exceeding 40 per workweek for non-exempt employees). Used for overtime pay calculation and FLSA compliance reporting.",
workforce,schedule_operations,time_attendance,overtime_pay_amount,overtime_pay_amount,Overtime Pay Amount,"DECIMAL(10,2)",,,dbx_confidential,,transactional_data,"Total overtime compensation earned during the pay period, calculated at the applicable overtime rate (typically 1.5x base rate per FLSA) applied to overtime_hours.",
workforce,schedule_operations,time_attendance,pay_period_end_date,pay_period_end_date,Pay Period End Date,DATE,,,,,transactional_data,The last calendar date of the pay period covered by this time and attendance record. Together with pay_period_start_date defines the payroll processing window.,
workforce,schedule_operations,time_attendance,pay_period_start_date,pay_period_start_date,Pay Period Start Date,DATE,,,,,transactional_data,The first calendar date of the pay period covered by this time and attendance record. Used to group time entries into payroll processing cycles.,
workforce,schedule_operations,time_attendance,pay_type,pay_type,Pay Type,STRING,,,,hourly|salary|per_diem|contract,transactional_data,"Indicates whether the employee is compensated on an hourly, salaried, per diem, or contract basis. Drives payroll calculation logic and FLSA exemption status determination.",
workforce,schedule_operations,time_attendance,payment_method,payment_method,Payment Method,STRING,,,,direct_deposit|check|pay_card,transactional_data,The method by which net pay is disbursed to the employee. Direct deposit is the standard method; check and pay card are alternatives for employees without bank accounts.,
workforce,schedule_operations,time_attendance,payroll_run_date,payroll_run_date,Payroll Run Date,DATE,,,,,transactional_data,The date on which the payroll run that processed this record was executed. Distinct from pay_period_end_date; used for payroll processing SLA monitoring.,
workforce,schedule_operations,time_attendance,payroll_run_status,payroll_run_status,Payroll Run Status,STRING,,,,not_processed|processing|processed|on_hold|reversed,transactional_data,Indicates the current payroll processing state for this time record. Processed means the record has been included in a completed payroll run; reversed indicates a payroll correction was applied.,
workforce,schedule_operations,time_attendance,regular_hours_worked,regular_hours_worked,Regular Hours Worked,"DECIMAL(8,2)",,,,,transactional_data,"Total number of regular (non-overtime) hours worked by the employee during the pay period or shift, as calculated by Workday HCM Time Tracking after meal break deductions.",
workforce,schedule_operations,time_attendance,shift_date,shift_date,Shift Date,DATE,,,,,transactional_data,"The calendar date on which the work shift occurred. For overnight shifts, this is the date the shift started. Used for daily labor reporting and scheduling reconciliation.",
workforce,schedule_operations,time_attendance,shift_differential_amount,shift_differential_amount,Shift Differential Pay Amount,"DECIMAL(10,2)",,,dbx_confidential,,transactional_data,"Additional compensation earned for working evening, night, weekend, or holiday shifts. Calculated based on shift_type and applicable differential rate per the collective bargaining agreement or HR policy.",
workforce,schedule_operations,time_attendance,shift_type,shift_type,Shift Type,STRING,,,,day|evening|night|on_call|weekend|holiday,transactional_data,Classification of the work shift for differential pay and scheduling purposes. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: day|evening|night|on_call|weekend|holiday|rotating — promote to reference product if additional values needed],
workforce,schedule_operations,time_attendance,time_entry_type,time_entry_type,Time Entry Type,STRING,,,,regular|overtime|on_call|callback|charge|training,transactional_data,Categorizes the nature of the time entry for payroll calculation and labor cost reporting. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: regular|overtime|on_call|callback|charge|training|orientation|meeting — promote to reference product if additional values needed],
workforce,schedule_operations,time_attendance,timekeeper_corrected,timekeeper_corrected,Timekeeper Correction Applied Flag,BOOLEAN,,,,,transactional_data,Indicates whether a timekeeper or payroll administrator applied a manual correction to this time record. True when a correction has been made; supports audit trail and compliance review.,
workforce,schedule_operations,time_attendance,total_tax_deduction,total_tax_deduction,Total Tax Deduction Amount,"DECIMAL(10,2)",,,dbx_confidential,,transactional_data,"Total amount withheld for all applicable taxes (federal income tax, state income tax, FICA/Social Security, Medicare) during this pay period. Supports W-2 preparation and tax compliance reporting.",
workforce,schedule_operations,workforce_shift_schedule,workforce_shift_schedule_id,workforce_shift_schedule_id,Shift Schedule ID,BIGINT,Y,,shift_schedule_id=shift_schedule_parent_id,,master_data,shift_schedule_id,
workforce,schedule_operations,workforce_shift_schedule,care_site_id,care_site_id,Facility ID,BIGINT,,facility.care_site.care_site_id,,,master_data,"Identifier of the facility (hospital, clinic, outpatient center) where the shift is scheduled.",
workforce,schedule_operations,workforce_shift_schedule,clinician_id,clinician_id,Clinician Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,provider.clinician.clinician_id,,,master_data,"Foreign key linking to provider.clinician. Business justification: Clinical schedules for credentialed providers. Real business need: provider scheduling, on-call management, clinical coverage planning, productivity tracking, RVU capture, patient access management fo",
workforce,schedule_operations,workforce_shift_schedule,cost_center_id,cost_center_id,Cost Center Id,BIGINT,,finance.cost_center.cost_center_id,dbx_internal,,master_data,FK to finance.cost_center,
workforce,schedule_operations,workforce_shift_schedule,position_id,position_id,Position Id (Foreign Key),BIGINT,,workforce.position.position_id,,,master_data,"Foreign key linking to workforce.position. Business justification: Shift schedules are created for specific positions (the authorized headcount slots), not just employees. Linking to position enables position-based scheduling, FTE coverage analysis, and ensures shift",
workforce,schedule_operations,workforce_shift_schedule,primary_employee_id,primary_employee_id,,BIGINT,,workforce.employee.employee_id,,,master_data,Employee ID for shift schedule (role: scheduler),
workforce,schedule_operations,workforce_shift_schedule,primary_workforce_shift_schedule_id,primary_workforce_shift_schedule_id,,BIGINT,,workforce.workforce_shift_schedule.workforce_shift_schedule_id,dbx_self_ref_fk,,master_data,description,
workforce,schedule_operations,workforce_shift_schedule,room_id,room_id,,BIGINT,,facility.room.room_id,,,master_data,FK to facility.room.room_id,
workforce,schedule_operations,workforce_shift_schedule,swap_source_schedule_id,swap_source_schedule_id,Swap Source Schedule ID,BIGINT,,workforce.workforce_shift_schedule.workforce_shift_schedule_id,,,master_data,Reference to the original shift_schedule record from which this shift was swapped. Populated when assignment_status is swapped to maintain the audit trail of shift exchanges.,
workforce,schedule_operations,workforce_shift_schedule,unit_id,unit_id,Unit Id,BIGINT,,facility.unit.unit_id,dbx_internal,,master_data,FK to facility.unit,
workforce,schedule_operations,workforce_shift_schedule,workforce_employee_id,workforce_employee_id,Employee ID,BIGINT,,workforce.employee.employee_id,"dbx_confidential, dbx_pii",,master_data,Identifier of the employee assigned to this shift. References the workforce employee master record.,
workforce,schedule_operations,workforce_shift_schedule,workforce_org_unit_id,workforce_org_unit_id,Department ID,BIGINT,,workforce.org_unit.org_unit_id,,,master_data,"Identifier of the clinical or non-clinical department/unit (e.g., ICU, ED, OR, outpatient clinic) for which the shift is scheduled.",
workforce,schedule_operations,workforce_shift_schedule,actual_end_datetime,actual_end_datetime,Actual End Date and Time,TIMESTAMP,,,,,master_data,The actual date and time the employee clocked out or ended the shift. Used for actual hours worked calculation and overtime determination.,
workforce,schedule_operations,workforce_shift_schedule,actual_hours_worked,actual_hours_worked,Actual Hours Worked,"DECIMAL(5,2)",,,,,master_data,"Total number of hours the employee actually worked during this shift, based on actual clock-in and clock-out times. Used for payroll processing and overtime variance analysis.",
workforce,schedule_operations,workforce_shift_schedule,actual_start_datetime,actual_start_datetime,Actual Start Date and Time,TIMESTAMP,,,,,master_data,The actual date and time the employee clocked in or began the shift. Compared against scheduled_start_datetime for variance analysis and late-arrival tracking.,
workforce,schedule_operations,workforce_shift_schedule,agency_name,agency_name,Agency Name,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Name of the staffing agency or contract labor vendor supplying the worker for this shift, when is_agency_staff is true. Used for vendor performance tracking and agency spend management.",
workforce,schedule_operations,workforce_shift_schedule,approval_datetime,approval_datetime,Approval Date and Time,TIMESTAMP,,,,,master_data,Date and time when the shift schedule assignment was approved by the responsible manager or charge nurse.,
workforce,schedule_operations,workforce_shift_schedule,break_minutes,break_minutes,Break Minutes,INT,,,,,master_data,Total scheduled break time in minutes for this shift (meal and rest breaks). Used for net hours worked calculation and OSHA (Occupational Safety and Health Administration) compliance.,
workforce,schedule_operations,workforce_shift_schedule,cancellation_reason,cancellation_reason,Cancellation Reason,STRING,,,,,master_data,Reason code for shift cancellation when assignment_status is cancelled. Supports workforce analytics on cancellation patterns and FMLA (Family and Medical Leave Act) tracking. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: employee_request|low_census|call_out|fmla|bereavement|administrative|other — promote to reference product],
workforce,schedule_operations,workforce_shift_schedule,care_setting,care_setting,Care Setting,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Classification of the care environment where the shift takes place (e.g., inpatient, ED (Emergency Department), ICU (Intensive Care Unit), OR (Operating Room), outpatient, ambulatory, telehealth). Drives staffing ratio requirements and regulatory reporting. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: inpatient|ed|icu|or|outpatient|ambulatory|telehealth — 7 candidates stripped; promote to reference product]",
workforce,schedule_operations,workforce_shift_schedule,created_datetime,created_datetime,Record Created Date and Time,TIMESTAMP,,,,,master_data,Date and time when this shift schedule record was first created in the system. Supports audit trail and data lineage requirements.,
workforce,schedule_operations,workforce_shift_schedule,fte_value,fte_value,Full-Time Equivalent (FTE) Value,"DECIMAL(5,4)",,,,,master_data,"FTE (Full-Time Equivalent) contribution of this shift assignment, calculated as scheduled hours divided by standard full-time hours. Used for workforce capacity planning and regulatory staffing ratio reporting.",
workforce,schedule_operations,workforce_shift_schedule,is_agency_staff,is_agency_staff,Agency Staff Indicator,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,"Indicates whether the shift is filled by agency or contract (traveler) staff rather than direct-hire employees. Used for labor cost analysis, agency spend tracking, and staffing mix reporting.",
workforce,schedule_operations,workforce_shift_schedule,is_charge_role,is_charge_role,Charge Role Indicator,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,"Indicates whether the employee is serving in a charge nurse or charge clinician capacity during this shift, carrying supervisory and unit management responsibilities.",
workforce,schedule_operations,workforce_shift_schedule,is_float_assignment,is_float_assignment,Float Assignment Indicator,BOOLEAN,,,,,master_data,"Indicates whether the employee is assigned as a float pool staff member, meaning they are not permanently assigned to this unit and may be deployed across multiple departments as needed.",
workforce,schedule_operations,workforce_shift_schedule,last_updated_datetime,last_updated_datetime,Record Last Updated Date and Time,TIMESTAMP,,,,,master_data,"Date and time when this shift schedule record was most recently modified. Used for change tracking, incremental ETL (Extract Transform Load) processing, and audit compliance.",
workforce,schedule_operations,workforce_shift_schedule,nurse_to_patient_ratio,nurse_to_patient_ratio,Nurse-to-Patient Ratio,"DECIMAL(5,2)",,,,,master_data,"Actual nurse-to-patient ratio achieved during this shift, calculated as the number of nurses on duty divided by patient census. Used for regulatory compliance reporting and quality benchmarking.",
workforce,schedule_operations,workforce_shift_schedule,on_call_response_minutes,on_call_response_minutes,On-Call Response Time (Minutes),INT,,,,,master_data,Required response time in minutes for on-call staff to report to the facility when called in. Applicable when shift_type is on_call. Used for operational readiness and SLA (Service Level Agreement) compliance.,
workforce,schedule_operations,workforce_shift_schedule,overtime_hours,overtime_hours,Overtime Hours,"DECIMAL(5,2)",,,,,master_data,Number of hours worked beyond the standard shift threshold (typically 8 hours/day or 40 hours/week) that qualify as overtime under FLSA. Used for payroll and labor cost management.,
workforce,schedule_operations,workforce_shift_schedule,patient_census,patient_census,Patient Census,INT,,,,,master_data,Number of patients in the unit/department at the time of the shift. Used to validate nurse-to-patient ratio compliance and assess staffing adequacy relative to patient volume.,
workforce,schedule_operations,workforce_shift_schedule,pay_code,pay_code,Pay Code,STRING,,,,,master_data,"Payroll pay code associated with this shift assignment (e.g., REG for regular, OT for overtime, HOL for holiday, DIFF for differential). Drives payroll processing in Workday HCM.",
workforce,schedule_operations,workforce_shift_schedule,provider_assignment_status,provider_assignment_status,Assignment Status,STRING,,,,scheduled|confirmed|swapped|cancelled|no_show|completed,master_data,"Current lifecycle status of the individual shift assignment (e.g., scheduled, confirmed, swapped, cancelled, no_show, completed). Tracks the workflow state of the shift from planning through execution.",
workforce,schedule_operations,workforce_shift_schedule,published_datetime,published_datetime,Published Date and Time,TIMESTAMP,,,,,master_data,Date and time when the schedule was published and made visible to staff. Marks the transition from draft to published schedule status.,
