workforce,staff_administration,job_profile,competency_framework_code,competency_framework_code,Competency Framework Code,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"Reference code linking this job profile to the applicable competency framework or assessment model in Workday HCM Learning (e.g., clinical competency sets, leadership competency models). Drives annual competency assessment assignments.",
workforce,staff_administration,job_profile,created_timestamp,created_timestamp,Record Created Timestamp,TIMESTAMP,,,,,reference_data,"Timestamp when the job profile record was first created in the workforce data platform. Supports audit trail, data lineage, and compliance with HIPAA and HITRUST record-keeping requirements.",
workforce,staff_administration,job_profile,dea_registration_required,dea_registration_required,DEA Registration Required Indicator,BOOLEAN,,,,,reference_data,"Indicates whether a DEA (Drug Enforcement Administration) registration number is required for this job profile to prescribe or administer controlled substances. Applicable to physicians, advanced practice nurses, and pharmacists.",
workforce,staff_administration,job_profile,drug_screen_required,drug_screen_required,Drug Screen Required Indicator,BOOLEAN,,,,,reference_data,Indicates whether pre-employment and/or random drug screening is required for this job profile. Particularly relevant for roles with access to controlled substances. Aligns with DEA and OSHA requirements.,
workforce,staff_administration,job_profile,effective_date,effective_date,Effective Date,DATE,,,,,reference_data,Date on which the job profile definition becomes effective and available for use in position and employee assignments. Supports point-in-time workforce reporting.,
workforce,staff_administration,job_profile,employment_type,employment_type,Employment Type,STRING,,,,Full-Time|Part-Time|Per Diem|Contract|Temporary|Intern,reference_data,"Defines the standard employment arrangement associated with this job profile (e.g., Full-Time, Part-Time, Per Diem, Contract). Drives benefits eligibility, FTE (Full-Time Equivalent) calculation, and scheduling rules.",
workforce,staff_administration,job_profile,end_date,end_date,End Date,DATE,,,,,reference_data,Date on which the job profile is retired or superseded. Null indicates the profile is currently active and open-ended. Used to enforce temporal validity in workforce analytics.,
workforce,staff_administration,job_profile,flsa_status,flsa_status,Fair Labor Standards Act (FLSA) Exemption Status,STRING,,,,Exempt|Non-Exempt|Highly Compensated|Computer Employee,reference_data,Indicates whether the job profile is classified as Exempt or Non-Exempt under the Fair Labor Standards Act (FLSA). Non-Exempt employees are entitled to overtime pay. Critical for payroll compliance and labor law adherence.,
workforce,staff_administration,job_profile,fte_equivalent,fte_equivalent,Full-Time Equivalent (FTE) Value,"DECIMAL(5,2)",,,,,reference_data,"Standard FTE (Full-Time Equivalent) value associated with this job profile, representing the proportion of a full-time workload (e.g., 1.0 for full-time, 0.5 for half-time). Used in workforce capacity planning and CMS staffing ratio reporting.",
workforce,staff_administration,job_profile,hipaa_access_level,hipaa_access_level,HIPAA PHI Access Level,STRING,,,,No Access|Limited|Standard|Extended|Full,reference_data,Defines the level of access to PHI (Protected Health Information) authorized for this job profile under HIPAA minimum necessary standards. Drives role-based access control (RBAC) provisioning in EHR systems such as Epic and Cerner.,
workforce,staff_administration,job_profile,job_category,job_category,Job Category,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"EEO-1 (Equal Employment Opportunity) job category classification required for federal workforce reporting (e.g., Officials and Managers, Professionals, Technicians, Service Workers). Supports EEOC compliance reporting. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: Officials and Managers|Professionals|Technicians|Sales Workers|Administrative Support|Craft Workers|Operatives|Laborers|Service Workers — promote to reference product]",
workforce,staff_administration,job_profile,job_code,job_code,Job Code,STRING,,,,"^[A-Z0-9]{2,20}$",reference_data,"Externally-known alphanumeric code that uniquely identifies the job profile across the organization. Used in payroll, scheduling, and HR reporting systems. Sourced from Workday HCM.",
workforce,staff_administration,job_profile,job_description,job_description,Job Description,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"Full narrative description of the job profile including primary responsibilities, scope of practice, reporting relationships, and essential functions. Used in recruitment, performance management, ADA (Americans with Disabilities Act) compliance, and regulatory filings.",
workforce,staff_administration,job_profile,job_family,job_family,Job Family,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"Grouping of related job profiles that share common skills, knowledge, and career paths (e.g., Nursing, Pharmacy, Radiology, Administrative, Information Technology). Supports workforce planning and compensation benchmarking.",
workforce,staff_administration,job_profile,job_family_group,job_family_group,Job Family Group,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"Broader organizational grouping above job family that clusters related job families (e.g., Clinical, Non-Clinical, Administrative, Technical). Enables enterprise-level workforce analytics and reporting.",
workforce,staff_administration,job_profile,job_level,job_level,Job Level,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"Hierarchical level designation within the job family indicating seniority and scope of responsibility (e.g., Entry, Intermediate, Senior, Lead, Principal, Expert). Drives compensation grade assignment and career progression. [ENUM-REF-CANDIDATE: Entry|Intermediate|Senior|Lead|Principal|Expert|Director|Executive — promote to reference product]",
workforce,staff_administration,job_profile,job_title,job_title,Job Title,STRING,,,,,reference_data,"Official human-readable title of the job profile as defined in Workday HCM (e.g., Registered Nurse, Clinical Pharmacist, Radiologic Technologist). Used on offer letters, org charts, and regulatory filings.",
workforce,staff_administration,job_profile,last_reviewed_date,last_reviewed_date,Last Reviewed Date,DATE,,,,,reference_data,Date on which the job profile was last formally reviewed and validated by HR and/or the relevant department leadership. Supports compliance with The Joint Commission requirement for periodic job description review.,
workforce,staff_administration,job_profile,licensure_required,licensure_required,Licensure Required Indicator,BOOLEAN,,,,,reference_data,"Indicates whether active professional licensure (e.g., RN, MD, PharmD, RT) is a mandatory requirement for this job profile. When True, triggers licensure verification workflows in Symplr and compliance tracking.",
workforce,staff_administration,job_profile,management_level,management_level,Management Level,STRING,,,,Individual Contributor|Manager|Senior Manager|Director|Vice President|Executive,reference_data,"Indicates whether the job profile is an individual contributor or a people-management role, and at what tier of management. Used for span-of-control analysis, leadership development, and FTE (Full-Time Equivalent) reporting.",
workforce,staff_administration,job_profile,minimum_education_level,minimum_education_level,Minimum Education Level,STRING,,,,High School Diploma|Associate Degree|Bachelors Degree|Masters Degree|Doctoral Degree|Professional Degree,reference_data,"Minimum educational attainment required for this job profile (e.g., Bachelors Degree in Nursing, Doctor of Medicine). Used in applicant screening, credentialing verification, and regulatory compliance.",
workforce,staff_administration,job_profile,minimum_experience_years,minimum_experience_years,Minimum Experience Years,"DECIMAL(4,1)",,,,,reference_data,"Minimum number of years of relevant professional experience required for this job profile. Used in applicant screening, internal mobility decisions, and workforce planning.",
workforce,staff_administration,job_profile,npi_required,npi_required,National Provider Identifier (NPI) Required Indicator,BOOLEAN,,,,,reference_data,Indicates whether employees in this job profile are required to hold an individual NPI (National Provider Identifier) for billing and claims submission purposes. Applicable to licensed independent practitioners and certain allied health professionals.,
workforce,staff_administration,job_profile,on_call_required,on_call_required,On-Call Required Indicator,BOOLEAN,,,,,reference_data,"Indicates whether employees in this job profile are required to participate in on-call scheduling rotations. Relevant for clinical roles in ED (Emergency Department), OR (Operating Room), ICU (Intensive Care Unit), and other 24/7 care settings.",
